(993165,34,38,14,3,'Then the'),
(993166,34,38,14,4,'On that day his feet will stand on the Mount of Olives, (which is opposite Jerusalem, on the east). The Mount of Olives will be split into halves, from east to west, by an exceedingly great valley; and half of the mountain will slide northwards and half southwards.'),
(993167,34,38,14,5,'You will escape through my valley – the valley between the hills will extend as far as Azel, and you will flee as you fled from before the earthquake, in the days of Uzziah king of Judah. But the'),
(993168,34,38,14,6,'And in that day, there will be no heat nor cold nor frost,'),
(993169,34,38,14,7,'but it will be constant day – it is known to the'),
(993170,34,38,14,8,'And on that day living waters will flow from Jerusalem, half of them to the eastern sea and half of them to the western sea; in both summer and winter.'),
(993171,34,38,14,9,'The'),
(993172,34,38,14,10,'The land will be changed to plain, from Geba to Rimmon, south of Jerusalem, but Jerusalem will be high and inhabited as it stands, from the Benjamin Gate up to the place of the first gate, and from the Tower of Hananel to the Corner Gate, and as far as the king’s winepresses.'),
(993173,34,38,14,11,'Jerusalem will be inhabited, for never again will it be doomed to destruction, and its people will abide in security.'),
(993174,34,38,14,12,'This is the plague with which the'),
(993175,34,38,14,13,'On that day a great panic sent by the Lord will fall on them. Everyone will seize their neighbours and attack them.'),
(993176,34,38,14,14,'Even Judah will fight at Jerusalem, and the wealth of the surrounding nations will be gathered up – gold and silver and piles of clothing.'),
(993177,34,38,14,15,'Plague will fall upon the horses, mules, camels, and asses, and on all the animals in all those camps.'),
(993178,34,38,14,16,'All who are left of all the nations which fought against Jerusalem will come up from year to year to worship the King, the'),
(993179,34,38,14,17,'Whoever of all the peoples of the earth will not come up to Jerusalem to worship the King, the'),
(993180,34,38,14,18,'If the family of Egypt does not go up nor enter in, on them also will come the plague with which the'),
(993181,34,38,14,19,'This will be the punishment for the sin of Egypt and the punishment for the sin of all nations which do not come up to keep the feast of the tabernacles.'),
(993182,34,38,14,20,'On that day there will be inscribed upon the bells of the horses, “Holy to the'),
(993183,34,38,14,21,'Every pot in Jerusalem and in Judah will be holy to the'),
(993184,34,39,1,1,'An oracle. The message of the'),
(993185,34,39,1,2,'‘I have loved you,’ says the'),
(993186,34,39,1,3,'but hated Esau, and made his mountains a desolation, and transformed his ancestral land into a wilderness.'),
(993187,34,39,1,4,'When Edom says, “We are beaten down, but we will return and rebuild the ruined places”’ the'),
(993188,34,39,1,5,'Your own eyes will see this, and you will say, “the'),
(993189,34,39,1,7,'You offer on my altar bread that is polluted. You ask, “How have we polluted it?” Because you say, “The table of the'),
(993190,34,39,1,8,'When you offer the blind animal for sacrifice, “It doesn’t matter!” And when you offer the lame and the sick “It doesn’t matter!” Give an animal like that to your governor; will he be pleased with it? Will he receive you favourably?’ says the'),
(993191,34,39,1,9,'Now, plead for the favour of God with such an offering, so that he may be gracious to us. ‘Would I receive any of you favourably?’ says the'),
(993192,34,39,1,10,'‘If only one of you would shut the temple doors, so that you could not kindle useless fires on my altar! I have no pleasure in you,’ says the'),
(993193,34,39,1,11,'For from the rising of the sun to its setting my name is great among the nations, and in every place they offer to my name a pure offering. For my name is great among the nations,’ says the'),
(993194,34,39,1,12,'‘But you profane me when you say, “The table of the'),
(993195,34,39,1,13,'You say also, “How tired we are of all this!” and you sniff contemptuously at it. You have brought the blind, the lame and the sick as offerings. Should I accept this from your hand?’ says the'),
(993196,34,39,1,14,'‘Cursed be the cheat, who has in his flock a valuable male, but vows and sacrifices to the Lord a blemished animal! For I am a great king,’ says the'),
(993197,34,39,2,1,'‘Now, you priests, this command is for you.'),
(993198,34,39,2,2,'If you will not hear, and if you do not take it to heart, to give glory to my name,’ says the'),
(993199,34,39,2,3,'I will punish your descendants! I will spread offal upon your faces, even the offal of your pilgrim feasts, you will be discarded.'),
(993200,34,39,2,4,'You will then know that I have sent this command to you, so that my covenant with Levi may be preserved,’ says the'),
(993201,34,39,2,5,'‘My covenant with him was to give life and peace. I gave them to him so that he might revere me. He revered me, and stood in awe of my name.'),
(993202,34,39,2,6,'The true instruction was in his mouth, and injustice was not found in his lips; He walked with me in peace and uprightness, and turned many away from iniquity.'),
(993203,34,39,2,7,'For the priest’s lips should keep knowledge, and people should seek the law from his mouth, because he is the messenger of the'),
(993204,34,39,2,8,'‘But you have turned aside from that way. You have caused many to stumble in the law. You have corrupted the covenant of Levi,’ says the'),
(993205,34,39,2,9,'‘So I have I made you contemptible and degraded before all the people, because you have not kept my ways, and have had no respect for me in imparting the law.’'),
(993206,34,39,2,11,'Judah is treacherous, and abominations are committed in Israel and in Jerusalem because Judah has profaned the holy things loved by the'),
(993207,34,39,2,12,'May the'),
(993208,34,39,2,13,'And you also do this: You cover the altar of the'),
(993209,34,39,2,14,'Yet you ask, ‘Why?’ Because the'),
(993210,34,39,2,15,'Did not the one God make everyone, so that all both flesh and spirit is his? And what does that one God seek but godly children? Therefore keep watch over your spirit, and let none of you deal faithlessly with the wife of your youth.'),
(993211,34,39,2,16,'‘A man who divorces or puts away his wife,’ says'),
(993212,34,39,2,17,'You have wearied the'),
(993213,34,39,3,1,'‘I am about to send my messenger and he will clear a path before me: And the'),
(993214,34,39,3,2,'But who can endure the day of his coming? And who will stand firm when he appears? He is like a refiner’s fire, and like a launderer’s soap,'),
(993215,34,39,3,3,'and he will sit as a refiner and purifier. He will purify the descendants of Levi, and refine them like gold and silver, until they are fit to bring offerings to the'),
(993216,34,39,3,4,'Then will the offerings of Judah and Jerusalem be pleasant to the'),
(993217,34,39,3,5,'‘I will come to you in judgment. I will be quick to testify against the sorcerers, adulterers, perjurers, those who cheat workers, or widows, or orphans, deny justice to immigrants, and do not fear me,’ says the'),
(993218,34,39,3,6,'‘For I, the'),
(993219,34,39,3,7,'‘From the days of your ancestors, you have turned aside from my statutes, and you have not kept them. Turn to me and I will turn to you,’ says the'),
(993220,34,39,3,8,'Can a human rob God? Yet you robbed me. You ask, “How have we robbed you?” In tithes and gifts!'),
(993221,34,39,3,9,'You – your entire nation – are all cursed, because you rob me.'),
(993222,34,39,3,10,'‘Bring the whole tithe into the storehouse, so that there is food in my house. Test me in this way. See if I will not open to you the windows of the sky, and pour you out a blessing, until there is more than enough.'),
(993223,34,39,3,11,'I will rebuke for your sakes the devouring locust and he will not destroy your crops, nor will the vine fail to ripen its fruit in the field, says the'),
(993224,34,39,3,12,'and all nations will call you happy, for you will be a delightful land,’ says the'),
(993225,34,39,3,14,'You have said, “It is useless to serve God, and what do we gain from the'),
(993226,34,39,3,15,'So now we call the proud happy, evildoers thrive: they dare God and escape unharmed.”’'),
(993227,34,39,3,16,'Such things those who revered the'),
(993228,34,39,3,17,'‘They will be mine,’ says the'),
(993229,34,39,3,18,'Once again my people will see the difference between the righteous and the wicked, between the person who serves God and the person who does not.’'),
(993230,34,39,4,1,'‘The day is coming that will burn like a furnace, and all the proud and all evildoers will be stubble, and the day that is coming will burn them up,’ says the'),
(993231,34,39,4,2,'But to you who revere my name there will arise the sun of righteousness with healing in its wings, and you will run free like calves let out from their stall.'),
(993232,34,39,4,3,'In the day when I act you will tread down the wicked, they will be as ashes under the soles of your feet,’ says the'),
(993233,34,39,4,4,'‘Remember the law of Moses my servant, statutes and judgments which I gave him at Horeb for all Israel.'),
(993234,34,39,4,5,'I am about to send to you Elijah the prophet, before the great and terrible day of the'),
(993235,34,39,4,6,'He will turn fathers’ hearts to their sons and sons’ hearts to their fathers, so that I will not come and strike the earth with judgement.’'),
(993236,34,40,1,1,'A genealogy of Jesus Christ, a descendant of David and Abraham.'),
(993237,34,40,1,2,'Abraham was the father of Isaac, Isaac of Jacob, Jacob of Judah and his brothers,'),
(993238,34,40,1,3,'Judah of Perez and Zerah, whose mother was Tamar, Perez of Hezron, Hezron of Aram,'),
(993239,34,40,1,4,'Aram of Aminadab, Aminadab of Nahshon, Nahshon of Salmon,'),
(993240,34,40,1,5,'Salmon of Boaz, whose mother was Rahab, Boaz of Obed, whose mother was Ruth, Obed of Jesse,'),
(993241,34,40,1,6,'Jesse of David the King. David was the father of Solomon, whose mother was Uriah’s widow,'),
(993242,34,40,1,7,'Solomon of Rehoboam, Rehoboam of Abijah, Abijah of Asa,'),
(993243,34,40,1,8,'Asa of Jehoshaphat, Jehoshaphat of Joram, Joram of Uzziah,'),
(993244,34,40,1,9,'Uzziah of Jotham, Jotham of Ahaz, Ahaz of Hezekiah,'),
(993245,34,40,1,10,'Hezekiah of Manasseh, Manasseh of Amon, Amon of Josiah,'),
(993246,34,40,1,11,'Josiah of Jechoniah and his brothers, at the time of the Exile to Babylon.'),
(993247,34,40,1,12,'After the Exile to Babylon – Jechoniah was the father of Salathiel, Salathiel of Zerubbabel,'),
(993248,34,40,1,13,'Zerubbabel of Abiud, Abiud of Eliakim, Eliakim of Azor,'),
(993249,34,40,1,14,'Azor of Zadok, Zadok of Achim, Achim of Eliud,'),
(993250,34,40,1,15,'Eliud of Eleazar, Eleazar of Matthan, Matthan of Jacob,'),
(993251,34,40,1,16,'Jacob of Joseph, the husband of Mary, who was the mother of Jesus, who is called “Christ”.'),
(993252,34,40,1,17,'So the whole number of generations from Abraham to David is fourteen; from David to the Exile to Babylon fourteen; and from the Exile to Babylon to the Christ fourteen.'),
(993253,34,40,1,18,'This is how Jesus Christ was born:'),
(993254,34,40,1,19,'Her husband, Joseph, was a just man and, since he did not want to disgrace her publicly, he resolved to put an end to their engagement privately.'),
(993255,34,40,1,20,'He had been thinking this over, when an angel of the Lord appeared to him in a dream.'),
(993256,34,40,1,21,'She will give birth to a son; name him Jesus, for he will save his people from their sins.’'),
(993257,34,40,1,22,'All this happened in fulfilment of these words of the Lord through the prophet, where he says –'),
(993258,34,40,1,23,'“The virgin will conceive and will give birth to a son, and they will give him the name Immanuel”'),
(993259,34,40,1,24,'When Joseph woke up, he did as the angel of the Lord had directed him.'),
(993260,34,40,1,25,'He made Mary his wife, but they did not sleep together before the birth of her son; and to this son he gave the name Jesus.'),
(993261,34,40,2,1,'After the birth of Jesus at Bethlehem in Judea, in the reign of King Herod, some astrologers from the East arrived in Jerusalem, asking,'),
(993262,34,40,2,2,'‘Where is the newborn king of the Jews? For we saw his star in the east, and have come to worship him.’'),
(993263,34,40,2,3,'When King Herod heard of this, he was much troubled, and so too was all Jerusalem.'),
(993264,34,40,2,4,'He called together all the chief priests and teachers of the Law in the nation, and questioned them as to where the Christ was to be born.'),
(993265,34,40,2,5,'‘At Bethlehem in Judea,’ was their answer, ‘for it is said in the prophet –'),
(993266,34,40,2,6,'“And you, Bethlehem in Judah’s land,'),
(993267,34,40,2,7,'Then Herod secretly sent for the astrologers. He found out from them the time of the appearance of the star.'),
(993268,34,40,2,8,'Sending them to Bethlehem he said, ‘Go and make a careful search for the child. When you have found him, bring word back to me, so that I, too, can go and worship him.’'),
(993269,34,40,2,9,'The astrologers heard what the king had to say, and then continued their journey. The star which they had seen in the east led them on, until it reached and stood over the place where the child was.'),
(993270,34,40,2,10,'At the sight of the star they were filled with joy.'),
(993271,34,40,2,11,'Entering the house, they saw the child with his mother, Mary, and fell at his feet and worshipped him. Then they opened their treasure chests, and offered to the child presents of gold, frankincense, and myrrh.'),
(993272,34,40,2,12,'But afterwards, having been warned in a dream not to go back to Herod, they returned to their own country by another road.'),
(993273,34,40,2,13,'After they had left, an angel of the Lord appeared to Joseph in a dream, and said, ‘Get up, take the child and his mother, and seek refuge in Egypt; and stay there until I tell you to return, for Herod is about to search for the child, to put him to death.’'),
(993274,34,40,2,14,'Joseph woke up, and taking the child and his mother by night, went into Egypt,'),
(993275,34,40,2,15,'and there he stayed until Herod’s death; in fulfilment of these words of the Lord in the prophet, where he says –'),
(993276,34,40,2,16,'When Herod found out that the astrologers had tricked him, he flew into a rage. He sent and put to death all the boys in Bethlehem and the whole of that region, who were two years old or under, guided by the time which he had learned from the astrologers.'),
(993277,34,40,2,17,'Then were fulfilled these words spoken in the prophet Jeremiah, where he says –'),
(993278,34,40,2,18,'“A voice was heard in Ramah,'),
(993279,34,40,2,19,'But, on the death of Herod, an angel of the Lord appeared in a dream to Joseph in Egypt, and said,'),
(993280,34,40,2,20,'‘Get up, take the child and his mother, and go into the Land of Israel, for those who sought to take the child’s life are dead.’'),
(993281,34,40,2,21,'He woke up, and taking the child and his mother, went into the Land of Israel.'),
(993282,34,40,2,22,'But, hearing that Archelaus had succeeded his father Herod as king of Judea, he was afraid to go back there; and having been warned in a dream, he went into the part of the country called Galilee.'),
(993283,34,40,2,23,'There he settled in the town of Nazareth, in fulfilment of these words in the prophets – “He will be called a Nazarene.”'),
(993284,34,40,3,1,'About that time John the Baptist first appeared, proclaiming in the wilderness of Judea:'),
(993285,34,40,3,2,'‘Repent, for the kingdom of heaven is at hand.’'),
(993286,34,40,3,3,'John was the one who was spoken of in the prophet Isaiah, where he says –'),
(993287,34,40,3,4,'John’s clothes were made of camels’ hair, with a leather strap round his waist, and his food was locusts and wild honey.'),
(993288,34,40,3,5,'At that time Jerusalem, and all Judea, as well as the whole district of the Jordan, went out to him'),
(993289,34,40,3,6,'and were baptized by him in the Jordan River, confessing their sins.'),
(993290,34,40,3,7,'But when John saw many of the Pharisees and Sadducees coming to receive his baptism, he said to them, ‘You children of snakes! Who has prompted you to seek refuge from the coming judgment?'),
(993291,34,40,3,8,'Let your life, then, prove your repentance;'),
(993292,34,40,3,9,'and do not think that you can say among yourselves “Abraham is our ancestor,” for I tell you that out of these stones God is able to raise descendants for Abraham!'),
(993293,34,40,3,10,'Already the axe is lying at the root of the trees. Therefore every tree that fails to bear good fruit will be cut down and thrown into the fire.'),
(993294,34,40,3,11,'I, indeed, baptize you with water to teach repentance; but he who is coming after me is more powerful than I, and I am not fit even to carry his sandals. He will baptize you with the Holy Spirit and with fire.'),
(993295,34,40,3,12,'His winnowing-fan is in his hand, and he will clear his threshing-floor, and store his grain in the barn, but the chaff he will burn with a fire that cannot be put out.’'),
(993296,34,40,3,13,'Then Jesus came from Galilee to the Jordan, to John, to be baptized by him.'),
(993297,34,40,3,14,'But John tried to prevent him.'),
(993298,34,40,3,16,'After the baptism of Jesus, and just as he came up from the water, the heavens opened, and he saw the Spirit of God coming down like a dove and resting on him,'),
(993299,34,40,3,17,'and from the heavens there came a voice which said, ‘This is my dearly loved son, who brings me great joy.’'),
(993300,34,40,4,1,'Then Jesus was led up into the wilderness by the Spirit to be tempted by the devil.'),
(993301,34,40,4,2,'And, after he had fasted for forty days and forty nights, he became hungry.'),
(993302,34,40,4,3,'The Tempter came to him, and said:'),
(993303,34,40,4,4,'But Jesus answered,'),
(993304,34,40,4,5,'Then the devil took him to the Holy City, and, placing him on the parapet of the temple, said to him,'),
(993305,34,40,4,6,'‘If you are God’s Son, throw yourself down, for scripture says –'),
(993306,34,40,4,8,'The third time, the devil took Jesus to a very high mountain, and, showing him all the kingdoms of the world and their splendour, said to him:'),
(993307,34,40,4,9,'‘All these I will give you, if you will fall at my feet and worship me.’'),
(993308,34,40,4,10,'Then Jesus said to him,'),
(993309,34,40,4,11,'Then the devil left him alone, and angels came and helped him.'),
(993310,34,40,4,12,'When Jesus heard that John had been arrested, he returned to Galilee.'),
(993311,34,40,4,13,'Afterwards, leaving Nazareth, he went and settled at Capernaum, which is by the side of the sea, within the borders of Zebulun and Naphtali;'),
(993312,34,40,4,14,'in fulfilment of these words in the prophet Isaiah –'),
(993313,34,40,4,15,'“The land of Zebulun and the land of Naphtali,'),
(993314,34,40,4,16,'The people who were living in darkness'),
(993315,34,40,4,17,'At that time Jesus began to proclaim –'),
(993316,34,40,4,18,'As Jesus was walking along the shore of the Sea of Galilee, he saw two brothers – Simon, also known as Peter, and his brother Andrew – casting a net into the sea; for they were fishermen.'),
(993317,34,40,4,20,'The two men left their nets at once and followed him.'),
(993318,34,40,4,21,'Going further on, he saw two other men who were also brothers, James, Zebedee’s son, and his brother John, in their boat with their father, mending their nets. Jesus called them,'),
(993319,34,40,4,22,'and they at once left their boat and their father, and followed him.'),
(993320,34,40,4,23,'Jesus went all through Galilee, teaching in their synagogues, proclaiming the good news of the kingdom, and curing every kind of disease and every kind of sickness among the people;'),
(993321,34,40,4,24,'and his fame spread all through Syria. They brought to him all who were ill with any form of disease, or who were suffering pain – any who were either possessed by demons, or were lunatic, or paralysed; and he cured them.'),
(993322,34,40,4,25,'He was followed by large crowds from Galilee, the district of the Ten Towns, Jerusalem, Judea, and from beyond the Jordan.'),
(993323,34,40,5,1,'On seeing the crowds of people, Jesus went up the hill; and, when he had taken his seat, his disciples came up to him;'),
(993324,34,40,5,2,'and he began to teach them, saying:'),
(993325,34,40,7,28,'By the time that Jesus had finished speaking, the crowd was filled with amazement at his teaching.'),
(993326,34,40,7,29,'For he taught them like one who had authority, and not like their teachers of the Law.'),
(993327,34,40,8,1,'When Jesus had come down from the hill, great crowds followed him.'),
(993328,34,40,8,2,'He saw a leper who came up, and bowed to the ground before him, and said, ‘Master, if only you are willing, you are able to make me clean.’'),
(993329,34,40,8,3,'Stretching out his hand, Jesus touched him, saying as he did so,'),
(993330,34,40,8,4,'and then Jesus said to him,'),
(993331,34,40,8,5,'After Jesus had entered Capernaum, a captain in the Roman army came up to him, entreating his help.'),
(993332,34,40,8,6,'‘Sir,’ he said, ‘my manservant is lying ill at my house with a stroke of paralysis, and is suffering terribly.’'),
(993333,34,40,8,8,'‘Sir,’ the captain went on, ‘I am unworthy to receive you under my roof; but only speak, and my manservant will be cured.'),
(993334,34,40,8,9,'For I myself am a man under the orders of others, with soldiers under me; and, if I say to one of them “Go,” he goes, and to another “Come,” he comes, and to my slave “Do this,” he does it.’'),
(993335,34,40,8,10,'Jesus was surprised to hear this, and said to those who were following him,'),
(993336,34,40,8,13,'Then Jesus said to the captain,'),
(993337,34,40,8,14,'When Jesus went into Peter’s house, he saw Peter’s mother-in-law prostrated with fever.'),
(993338,34,40,8,15,'On his taking her hand, the fever left her, and she rose and began to take care of him.'),
(993339,34,40,8,16,'In the evening the people brought to Jesus many who were possessed by demons; and he drove out the spirits with a word, and cured all who were ill,'),
(993340,34,40,8,17,'in fulfilment of these words in the prophet Isaiah – “He took our infirmities on himself, and bore the burden of our diseases.”'),
(993341,34,40,8,18,'Seeing a crowd round him, Jesus gave orders to go across.'),
(993342,34,40,8,19,'A teacher of the Law came up to him, and said, ‘Teacher, I will follow you wherever you go.’'),
(993343,34,40,8,21,'‘Master,’ said another, who was a disciple, ‘let me first go and bury my father.’'),
(993344,34,40,8,22,'But Jesus answered,'),
(993345,34,40,8,23,'Then he got into the boat, followed by his disciples.'),
(993346,34,40,8,24,'Suddenly so great a storm came up on the sea, that the waves broke right over the boat. But Jesus was asleep;'),
(993347,34,40,8,25,'and the disciples came and roused him. ‘Master,’ they cried, ‘save us; we are lost!’'),
(993348,34,40,8,27,'The men were amazed, and exclaimed, ‘What kind of man is this, that even the winds and the sea obey him!’'),
(993349,34,40,8,28,'On getting to the other side – the region of the Gadarenes – Jesus met two men who were possessed by demons, coming out of the tombs. They were so violent that no one was able to pass that way.'),
(993350,34,40,8,29,'Suddenly they shrieked out, ‘What do you want with us, Son of God? Have you come here to torment us before our time?’'),
(993351,34,40,8,30,'A long way off, there was a drove of many pigs, feeding;'),
(993352,34,40,8,31,'and the foul spirits began begging Jesus, ‘If you drive us out, send us into the drove of pigs.’'),
(993353,34,40,8,33,'At this the men who tended them ran away and went to the town, carrying the news of all that had occurred, and of what had happened to the possessed men.'),
(993354,34,40,8,34,'At the news the whole town went out to meet Jesus, and, when they saw him, they entreated him to go away from their region.'),
(993355,34,40,9,1,'Afterwards Jesus got into a boat, and, crossing over, came to his own city.'),
(993356,34,40,9,2,'There some people brought to him a paralysed man on a bed. When Jesus saw their faith, he said to the man,'),
(993357,34,40,9,3,'Then some of the teachers of the Law said to themselves, ‘This man is blaspheming!’'),
(993358,34,40,9,4,'Knowing their thoughts, Jesus exclaimed,'),
(993359,34,40,9,7,'The man got up and went to his home.'),
(993360,34,40,9,8,'When the crowd saw this, they were awe-struck, and praised God for giving such power to human beings.'),
(993361,34,40,9,9,'As Jesus went along, he saw a man, called Matthew, sitting in the tax office, and said to him,'),
(993362,34,40,9,10,'And, later on, when he was having dinner in the house, a number of tax-gatherers and outcasts came in and took their places at the table with Jesus and his disciples.'),
(993363,34,40,9,11,'When the Pharisees saw this, they said to his disciples, ‘Why does your teacher eat in the company of tax-gatherers and outcasts?’'),
(993364,34,40,9,12,'On hearing this, Jesus said,'),
(993365,34,40,9,14,'Then John’s disciples came to Jesus, and asked, ‘Why do we and the Pharisees fast while your disciples do not?’'),
(993366,34,40,9,15,'Jesus answered,'),
(993367,34,40,9,18,'While Jesus was saying this, a synagogue leader came up and bowed to the ground before him. ‘My daughter,’ he said, ‘has just died; but come and place your hand on her, and she will be restored to life.’'),
(993368,34,40,9,19,'So Jesus rose and followed him, and his disciples went also.'),
(993369,34,40,9,20,'But meanwhile a woman, who had been suffering from haemorrhage for twelve years, came up behind and touched the tassel of his cloak.'),
(993370,34,40,9,21,'‘If I only touch his cloak,’ she said to herself, ‘I will get well.’'),
(993371,34,40,9,22,'Turning and seeing her, Jesus said,'),
(993372,34,40,9,23,'When Jesus reached the leader’s house, seeing the flute players, and a number of people all in confusion,'),
(993373,34,40,9,24,'he said,'),
(993374,34,40,9,25,'but, when the people had been sent out, Jesus went in, and took the little girl’s hand, and she rose.'),
(993375,34,40,9,26,'The report of this spread through all that part of the country.'),
(993376,34,40,9,27,'As Jesus was passing on from there, he was followed by two blind men, who kept calling out, ‘Take pity on us, Son of David!’'),
(993377,34,40,9,28,'When he had gone indoors, the blind men came up to him; and Jesus asked them,'),
(993378,34,40,9,29,'Then he touched their eyes, and said,'),
(993379,34,40,9,30,'Then their eyes were opened. Jesus sternly cautioned them.'),
(993380,34,40,9,31,'But the men went out, and spread the news about him through all that part of the country.'),
(993381,34,40,9,32,'Just as they were going out, some people brought up to Jesus a dumb man who was possessed by a demon;'),
(993382,34,40,9,33,'and, as soon as the demon had been driven out, the dumb man spoke. The people were astonished at this, and exclaimed, ‘Nothing like this has ever been seen in Israel!’'),
(993383,34,40,9,34,'But the Pharisees said, ‘He drives out the demons by the help of the chief of the demons.’'),
(993384,34,40,9,35,'Jesus went round all the towns and the villages, teaching in their synagogues, proclaiming the good news of the kingdom, and curing every kind of disease and every kind of sickness.'),
(993385,34,40,9,36,'But, when he saw the crowds, his heart was moved with compassion for them, because they were distressed and harassed, like sheep without a shepherd;'),
(993386,34,40,9,37,'and he said to his disciples,'),
(993387,34,40,10,1,'Calling his twelve Disciples to him, Jesus gave them authority over foul spirits, so that they could drive them out, as well as the power of curing every kind of disease and every kind of sickness.'),
(993388,34,40,10,2,'The names of the twelve apostles are these, First Simon, also known as Peter, and his brother Andrew; James the son of Zebedee, and his brother John;'),
(993389,34,40,10,3,'Philip and Bartholomew; Thomas and Matthew the tax-gather; James the son of Alphaeus, and Thaddaeus;'),
(993390,34,40,10,4,'Simon the Zealot, and Judas Iscariot – the apostle who betrayed him.'),
(993391,34,40,10,5,'These twelve Jesus sent out as his messengers, after giving them these instructions –'),
(993392,34,40,11,1,'After Jesus had finished giving directions to his twelve Disciples, he left that place in order to teach and preach in their towns.'),
(993393,34,40,11,2,'Now John had heard in prison what the Christ was doing, and he sent a message by his disciples,'),
(993394,34,40,11,3,'and asked – ‘Are you “the coming one,” or are we to look for someone else?’'),
(993395,34,40,11,4,'The answer of Jesus to the question was –'),
(993396,34,40,11,7,'While John’s disciples were going back, Jesus began to say to the crowds with reference to John,'),
(993397,34,40,11,20,'Then Jesus began to reproach the towns in which most of his miracles had been done, because they had not repented,'),
(993398,34,40,11,25,'At that same time Jesus uttered the words,'),
(993399,34,40,12,1,'About the same time Jesus walked through the cornfields one Sabbath. His disciples were hungry, and began to pick some ears of wheat and eat them.'),
(993400,34,40,12,2,'But, when the Pharisees saw this, they said, ‘Look! Your disciples are doing what it is not allowable to do on a Sabbath!’'),
(993401,34,40,12,9,'Passing on, Jesus went into their synagogue,'),
(993402,34,40,12,10,'and there he saw a man with a withered hand. Some people asked Jesus whether it was allowable to work a cure on the Sabbath – so that they might have a charge to bring against him.'),
(993403,34,40,12,11,'But Jesus said to them,'),
(993404,34,40,12,13,'Then he said to the man.'),
(993405,34,40,12,14,'On coming out, the Pharisees plotted against Jesus, to put him to death.'),
(993406,34,40,12,15,'Jesus, however, became aware of it, and went away from that place. A number of people followed him, and he cured them all;'),
(993407,34,40,12,16,'but he warned them not to make him known,'),
(993408,34,40,12,17,'in fulfilment of these words in the prophet Isaiah –'),
(993409,34,40,12,18,'“Here is my chosen servant, who I love and who pleases me! I will breathe my spirit on him, and he will announce a time of judgment to the Gentiles.'),
(993410,34,40,12,19,'He will not contend, nor cry aloud, Neither will anyone hear his voice in the streets;'),
(993411,34,40,12,20,'a bruised reed he will not break, and a smouldering wick he will not quench, until he has brought the judgment to a victorious issue,'),
(993412,34,40,12,21,'and on his name will the Gentiles rest their hopes.”'),
(993413,34,40,12,22,'Then some people brought to Jesus a possessed man, who was blind and dumb; and he cured him, so that the man who had been dumb both talked and saw.'),
(993414,34,40,12,23,'At this all the people were astounded. ‘Is it possible that this is the son of David?’ they exclaimed.'),
(993415,34,40,12,24,'But the Pharisees heard of it and said, ‘He drives out demons only by the help of Beelzebul the chief of the demons.’'),
(993416,34,40,12,25,'Jesus, however, was aware of what was passing in their minds, and said to them,'),
(993417,34,40,12,38,'At this point, some teachers of the Law and Pharisees spoke up. ‘Teacher,’ they said, ‘we want to see some sign from you.’'),
(993418,34,40,12,46,'While he was still speaking to the crowds, his mother and brothers were standing outside, asking to speak to him.'),
(993419,34,40,12,47,'Someone told him this, and Jesus replied,'),
(993420,34,40,12,49,'Then, stretching out his hands towards his disciples, he said,'),
(993421,34,40,13,1,'That same day, when Jesus had left the house and was sitting by the sea,'),
(993422,34,40,13,2,'such great crowds gathered round him, that he got into a boat, and sat in it, while all the people stood on the beach.'),
(993423,34,40,13,3,'Then he told them many truths in parables.'),
(993424,34,40,13,10,'Afterwards his disciples came to him, and said, ‘Why do you speak to them in parables?’'),
(993425,34,40,13,24,'Another parable which Jesus told them was this –'),
(993426,34,40,13,31,'Another parable which he told them was this –'),
(993427,34,40,13,33,'This was another parable which Jesus related –'),
(993428,34,40,13,34,'Of all this Jesus spoke to the crowd in parables; indeed to them he used never to speak at all except in parables,'),
(993429,34,40,13,35,'in fulfilment of these words in the prophet – “I will speak to them in parables; I will utter things kept secret since the foundation of the world.”'),
(993430,34,40,13,36,'Then Jesus left the crowd, and went into the house. Presently his disciples came to him, and said, ‘Explain to us the parable of the weeds in the field.’'),
(993431,34,40,13,37,'He answered,'),
(993432,34,40,13,52,'Then he added,'),
(993433,34,40,13,53,'When Jesus had finished these parables, he withdrew from that place.'),
(993434,34,40,13,54,'Going to his own part of the country, he taught the people in their synagogue in such a manner that they were deeply impressed. ‘Where did he get this wisdom?’ they said, ‘and the miracles?'),
(993435,34,40,13,55,'Isn’t he the carpenter’s son? Isn’t his mother called Mary, and his brothers James, and Joseph, and Simon, and Judas?'),
(993436,34,40,13,56,'And his sisters, too – are not they all living among us? Where, then did he get all this?’'),
(993437,34,40,13,57,'These things proved a hindrance to their believing in him. But Jesus said,'),
(993438,34,40,13,58,'He did not work many miracles there, because of their want of faith.'),
(993439,34,40,14,1,'At that time Prince Herod heard of the fame of Jesus,'),
(993440,34,40,14,2,'and said to his attendants, ‘This must be John the Baptist; he must be risen from the dead, and that is why these miraculous powers are active in him.’'),
(993441,34,40,14,3,'For Herod had arrested John, put him in chains, and shut him up in prison, to please Herodias, the wife of Herod’s brother Philip.'),
(993442,34,40,14,4,'For John had said to him “You have no right to be living with her.”'),
(993443,34,40,14,5,'Yet, though Herod wanted to put him to death, he was afraid of the people, because they looked on John as a prophet.'),
(993444,34,40,14,6,'But, when Herod’s birthday came, the daughter of Herodias danced before his guests, and so pleased Herod,'),
(993445,34,40,14,7,'that he promised with an oath to give her whatever she asked.'),
(993446,34,40,14,8,'Prompted by her mother, the girl said “Give me here, on a dish, the head of John the Baptist.”'),
(993447,34,40,14,9,'The king was distressed at this; yet, because of his oath and of the guests at his table, he ordered it to be given her.'),
(993448,34,40,14,10,'He had John beheaded in the prison'),
(993449,34,40,14,11,'and his head was brought on a dish and given to the girl, and she took it to her mother.'),
(993450,34,40,14,12,'Then John’s disciples came, and took the body away, and buried it; and went and told Jesus.'),
(993451,34,40,14,13,'When Jesus heard of it, he left privately in a boat to a lonely spot. The people, however, heard of his going, and followed him in crowds from the towns on foot.'),
(993452,34,40,14,14,'On getting out of the boat, Jesus saw a great crowd, and his heart was moved at the sight of them; and he cured all the sick among them.'),
(993453,34,40,14,15,'In the evening the disciples came up to him, and said, ‘This is a lonely spot, and the day is now far advanced; send the crowds away so that they can to the villages, and buy themselves food.’'),
(993454,34,40,14,16,'But Jesus said,'),
(993455,34,40,14,17,'‘We have nothing here,’ they said, ‘except five loaves and two fish.’'),
(993456,34,40,14,19,'Jesus ordered the people to take their seats on the grass; and, taking the five loaves and the two fish, he looked up to heaven, and said the blessing, and, after he had broken the loaves, gave them to his disciples; and they gave them to the crowds.'),
(993457,34,40,14,20,'Everyone had sufficient to eat, and they picked up enough of the broken pieces that were left to fill twelve baskets.'),
(993458,34,40,14,21,'The men who ate were about five thousand in number, without counting women and children.'),
(993459,34,40,14,22,'Immediately afterwards Jesus made the disciples get into a boat and cross over in advance of him, while he dismissed the crowds.'),
(993460,34,40,14,23,'After dismissing the crowds, he went up the hill by himself to pray; and, when evening fell, he was there alone.'),
(993461,34,40,14,24,'The boat was by this time some miles from shore, labouring in the waves, for the wind was against her.'),
(993462,34,40,14,25,'Three hours after midnight, however, Jesus came towards the disciples, walking on the water.'),
(993463,34,40,14,26,'But, when they saw him walking on the water, they were terrified. ‘It is a ghost,’ they exclaimed, and cried out in fear.'),
(993464,34,40,14,27,'But Jesus at once spoke to them.'),
(993465,34,40,14,28,'‘Master,’ Peter exclaimed, ‘if it is you, tell me to come to you on the water.’'),
(993466,34,40,14,29,'Jesus said,'),
(993467,34,40,14,30,'but, when he felt the wind, he was frightened, and, beginning to sink, cried out, ‘Master! Save me!’'),
(993468,34,40,14,31,'Instantly Jesus stretched out his hand, and caught hold of him.'),
(993469,34,40,14,32,'When they had got into the boat, the wind dropped.'),
(993470,34,40,14,33,'But the men in the boat threw themselves on their faces before him, and said, ‘You are indeed God’s Son.’'),
(993471,34,40,14,34,'When they had crossed over, they landed at Gennesaret.'),
(993472,34,40,14,35,'But the people of that place, recognising Jesus, sent out to the whole country round, and brought to him all who were ill,'),
(993473,34,40,14,36,'begging him merely to let them touch the tassel of his cloak; and all who touched were made perfectly well.'),
(993474,34,40,15,1,'Then some Pharisees and teachers of the Law came to Jesus, and said,'),
(993475,34,40,15,2,'‘How is it that your disciples break the traditions of our ancestors? For they do not wash their hands when they eat food.’'),
(993476,34,40,15,3,'His reply was,'),
(993477,34,40,15,10,'Then Jesus called the people to him, and said,'),
(993478,34,40,15,12,'His disciples came up to him, and said, ‘Do you know that the Pharisees were shocked on hearing what you said?’'),
(993479,34,40,15,15,'Peter spoke up, ‘Explain this saying to us.’'),
(993480,34,40,15,21,'On going away from that place, Jesus went to the country round Tyre and Sidon.'),
(993481,34,40,15,22,'There, a Canaanite woman of that district came out and began calling to Jesus, ‘Take pity on me, Master, Son of David; my daughter is grievously possessed by a demon.’'),
(993482,34,40,15,23,'But Jesus did not answer her a word; and his disciples came up and begged him to send her away. ‘She keeps calling out after us,’ they said.'),
(993483,34,40,15,25,'But the woman came, and, bowing to the ground before him, said, ‘Master, help me.’'),
(993484,34,40,15,27,'‘Yes, Master,’ she said, ‘for even dogs do feed on the scraps that fall from their owners’ table.’'),
(993485,34,40,15,29,'On leaving that place, Jesus went to the shore of the Sea of Galilee; and then went up the hill, and sat down.'),
(993486,34,40,15,30,'Great crowds of people came to him, bringing with them those who were lame, crippled, blind, or dumb, and many others. They put them down at his feet, and he cured them;'),
(993487,34,40,15,31,'and the crowds were astonished, when they saw the dumb talking, the cripples made sound, the lame walking about, and the blind with their sight restored; and they praised the God of Israel.'),
(993488,34,40,15,32,'Afterwards Jesus called his disciples to him, and said,'),
(993489,34,40,15,33,'‘Where can we,’ his disciples asked, ‘in a lonely place find enough bread for such a crowd as this?’'),
(993490,34,40,15,35,'Telling the crowd to sit down on the ground,'),
(993491,34,40,15,36,'Jesus took the seven loaves and the fish, and, after saying the thanksgiving, broke them, and gave them to the disciples; and the disciples gave them to the crowds.'),
(993492,34,40,15,37,'Everyone had sufficient to eat, and they picked up seven baskets full of the broken pieces left.'),
(993493,34,40,15,38,'The men who ate were four thousand in number without counting women and children.'),
(993494,34,40,15,39,'Then, after dismissing the crowds, Jesus got into the boat, and went to the region of Magadan.'),
(993495,34,40,16,1,'Here the Pharisees and Sadducees came up, and, to test Jesus, requested him to show them some sign from the heavens.'),
(993496,34,40,16,2,'But Jesus answered,'),
(993497,34,40,16,5,'Now the disciples had crossed to the opposite shore, and had forgotten to take any bread.'),
(993498,34,40,16,6,'Presently Jesus said to them, ‘Take care and be on your guard against the leaven of the Pharisees and Sadducees.’'),
(993499,34,40,16,7,'But the disciples began talking among themselves about their having brought no bread.'),
(993500,34,40,16,8,'On noticing this, Jesus said,');
INSERT INTO verses (id, version_id, book_id, chapter, verse, text) VALUES
(993501,34,40,16,12,'Then they understood that he had told them to be on their guard, not against the leaven of bread, but against the teaching of the Pharisees and Sadducees.'),
(993502,34,40,16,13,'On coming into the region of Caesarea Philippi, Jesus asked his disciples this question –'),
(993503,34,40,16,14,'‘Some say John the Baptist,’ they answered, ‘Others, however, say that he is Elijah, while others again say Jeremiah, or one of the prophets.’'),
(993504,34,40,16,16,'To this Simon Peter answered, ‘You are the Christ, the Son of the living God.’'),
(993505,34,40,16,20,'Then he charged his disciples not to tell anyone that he was the Christ.'),
(993506,34,40,16,21,'At that time Jesus Christ began to explain to his disciples that he must go to Jerusalem, and undergo much suffering at the hands of the elders, and chief priests, and teachers of the Law, and be put to death, and rise on the third day.'),
(993507,34,40,16,22,'But Peter took Jesus aside, and began to rebuke him. ‘Master,’ he said, ‘please God that will never be your fate!’'),
(993508,34,40,16,23,'Jesus, however, turning to Peter, said,'),
(993509,34,40,16,24,'Then Jesus said to his disciples,'),
(993510,34,40,17,1,'Six days later, Jesus took with him Peter, and the brothers James and John, and led them up a high mountain alone.'),
(993511,34,40,17,2,'There his appearance was transformed before their eyes; his face shown like the sun, and his clothes became as white as the light.'),
(993512,34,40,17,3,'All at once Moses and Elijah appeared to them, talking with Jesus.'),
(993513,34,40,17,4,'‘Master,’ exclaimed Peter, interposing, ‘it is good to be here; if you wish, I will make three tents here, one for you, one for Moses, and one for Elijah.’'),
(993514,34,40,17,5,'While he was still speaking, a bright cloud enveloped them, and there was a voice from the cloud that said – ‘This is my dearly loved son, who brings me great joy; listen to him.’'),
(993515,34,40,17,6,'The disciples, on hearing this, fell on their faces, greatly afraid.'),
(993516,34,40,17,7,'But Jesus came and touched them, saying as he did so,'),
(993517,34,40,17,8,'When they raised their eyes, they saw no one but Jesus himself alone.'),
(993518,34,40,17,9,'As they were going down the mountain side, Jesus gave them this warning –'),
(993519,34,40,17,10,'‘How is it,’ his disciples asked, ‘that our teachers of the Law say that Elijah has to come first?’'),
(993520,34,40,17,13,'Then the disciples understood that it was of John the Baptist that he had spoken to them.'),
(993521,34,40,17,14,'When they came to the crowd, a man came up to Jesus, and, kneeling down before him, said,'),
(993522,34,40,17,15,'‘Master, take pity on my son, for he is epileptic and suffers terribly; indeed, he often falls into the fire and into the water;'),
(993523,34,40,17,16,'I brought him to your disciples, but they could not cure him.’'),
(993524,34,40,17,18,'Then Jesus rebuked the demon, and it came out of the boy; and he was cured from that very hour.'),
(993525,34,40,17,19,'Afterwards the disciples came up to Jesus, and asked him privately, ‘Why was it that we could not drive it out?’'),
(993526,34,40,17,22,'While Jesus and his disciples were together in Galilee, he said to them,'),
(993527,34,40,17,24,'After they had reached Capernaum, the collectors of the Temple-rate came up to Peter, and said, ‘Does not your Master pay the Temple-rate?’'),
(993528,34,40,17,25,'‘Yes,’ answered Peter. But, on going into the house, before he could speak, Jesus said,'),
(993529,34,40,17,26,'‘From others,’ answered Peter.'),
(993530,34,40,18,1,'On the same occasion the disciples came to Jesus, and asked him, ‘Who is really the greatest in the kingdom of heaven?’'),
(993531,34,40,18,2,'Jesus called a little child to him, and placed it in the middle of them, and then said,'),
(993532,34,40,18,21,'Then Peter came up, and said to Jesus, ‘Master, how often am I to forgive someone who wrongs me? As many as seven times?’'),
(993533,34,40,18,22,'But Jesus answered,'),
(993534,34,40,19,1,'At the conclusion of this teaching, Jesus withdrew from Galilee, and went into that district of Judea which is on the other side of the Jordan.'),
(993535,34,40,19,2,'Great crowds followed him, and he cured them there.'),
(993536,34,40,19,3,'Presently some Pharisees came up to him, and, to test him, said, ‘Has a man the right to divorce his wife for every cause?’'),
(993537,34,40,19,7,'‘Why, then,’ they said, ‘did Moses direct that a man should serve his wife with a notice of separation and divorce her?’'),
(993538,34,40,19,10,'‘If that,’ said the disciples, ‘is the position of a man with regard to his wife, it is better not to marry.’'),
(993539,34,40,19,13,'Then some little children were brought to Jesus, for him to place his hands on them, and pray; but the disciples found fault with those who had brought them.'),
(993540,34,40,19,14,'Jesus, however, said,'),
(993541,34,40,19,15,'So he placed his hands on them, and then went on his way.'),
(993542,34,40,19,16,'A man came up to Jesus, and said, ‘Teacher, what good thing must I do to obtain eternal life?’'),
(993543,34,40,19,18,'‘What commandments?’ asked the man.'),
(993544,34,40,19,20,'‘I have observed all these,’ said the young man. ‘What is still wanting in me?’'),
(993545,34,40,19,22,'On hearing these words, the young man went away distressed, for he had great possessions.'),
(993546,34,40,19,23,'At this, Jesus said to his disciples,'),
(993547,34,40,19,25,'On hearing this, the disciples exclaimed in great astonishment, ‘Who then can possibly be saved?’'),
(993548,34,40,19,26,'But Jesus looked at them, and said,'),
(993549,34,40,19,27,'‘But we – we left everything, and followed you; what, then, will we have?’'),
(993550,34,40,20,17,'When Jesus was on the point of going up to Jerusalem, he gathered the twelve disciples round him by themselves, and said to them as they were on their way,'),
(993551,34,40,20,20,'Then the mother of Zebedee’s sons came to him with her sons, bowing to the ground, and begging a favour.'),
(993552,34,40,20,24,'On hearing of this, the ten others were very indignant about the two brothers.'),
(993553,34,40,20,25,'Jesus, however, called the ten to him, and said,'),
(993554,34,40,20,29,'As they were going out of Jericho, a great crowd followed him.'),
(993555,34,40,20,30,'Two blind men who were sitting by the roadside, hearing that Jesus was passing, called out, ‘Take pity on us, Master, Son of David!’'),
(993556,34,40,20,31,'The crowd told them to be quiet; but the men only called out the louder, ‘Take pity on us, Master, Son of David!’'),
(993557,34,40,20,32,'Then Jesus stopped and called them.'),
(993558,34,40,20,33,'‘Master,’ they replied, ‘we want our eyes to be opened.’'),
(993559,34,40,20,34,'So Jesus, moved with compassion, touched their eyes, and immediately they recovered their sight, and followed him.'),
(993560,34,40,21,1,'When they had almost reached Jerusalem, having come as far as Bethphage, on the Mount of Olives, Jesus sent on two disciples.'),
(993561,34,40,21,4,'This happened in fulfilment of these words in the prophet –'),
(993562,34,40,21,5,'“Say to the people of Zion – ‘Your King is coming to you, gentle, and riding on an ass, and on the foal of a beast of burden.’”'),
(993563,34,40,21,6,'So the disciples went and did as Jesus had directed them.'),
(993564,34,40,21,7,'They led the ass and the foal back, and, when they had put their cloaks on them, he seated himself on them.'),
(993565,34,40,21,8,'The immense crowd of people spread their cloaks in the road, while some cut branches off the trees, and spread them on the road.'),
(993566,34,40,21,9,'The crowds that led the way, as well as those that followed behind, kept shouting, ‘God save the Son of David! Blessed is he who comes in the name of the Lord! God save him from on high!’'),
(993567,34,40,21,10,'When he had entered Jerusalem, the whole city was stirred, and asked –'),
(993568,34,40,21,11,'‘Who is this?’, to which the crowd replied – ‘This is the prophet Jesus from Nazareth in Galilee.’'),
(993569,34,40,21,12,'Jesus went into the Temple Courts, and drove out all those who were buying and selling there. He overturned the tables of the money changers, and the seats of the pigeon-dealers,'),
(993570,34,40,21,13,'and said to them,'),
(993571,34,40,21,14,'While he was still in the Temple Courts, some blind and some lame people came up to him, and he cured them.'),
(993572,34,40,21,15,'But, when the chief priests and the teachers of the Law saw the wonderful things that Jesus did, and the boys who were calling out in the Temple Courts ‘God save the Son of David!’, they were indignant,'),
(993573,34,40,21,16,'and said to him, ‘Do you hear what these boys are saying?’'),
(993574,34,40,21,17,'Then he left them, and went out of the city to Bethany, and spent the night there.'),
(993575,34,40,21,18,'The next morning, in returning to the city, Jesus became hungry;'),
(993576,34,40,21,19,'and, noticing a solitary fig tree by the roadside, he went up to it, but found nothing on it but leaves. So he said to it,'),
(993577,34,40,21,20,'When the disciples saw this, they exclaimed in astonishment, ‘How suddenly the fig tree withered up!’'),
(993578,34,40,21,23,'After Jesus had come into the Temple Courts, the chief priests and the elders of the people came up to him as he was teaching, and said, ‘What authority have you to do these things? Who gave you this authority?’'),
(993579,34,40,21,26,'But if we say “human,” we are afraid of the people, for everyone regards John as a prophet.’'),
(993580,34,40,21,27,'So the answer they gave Jesus was – ‘We do not know.’'),
(993581,34,40,21,41,'‘Miserable wretches!’ they exclaimed, ‘he will put them to a miserable death, and he will let out the vineyard to other tenants, who will pay him his share of the produce at the proper times.’'),
(993582,34,40,21,42,'Then Jesus added,'),
(993583,34,40,21,45,'After listening to these parables, the chief priests and the Pharisees saw that it was about them that he was speaking;'),
(993584,34,40,21,46,'yet, although eager to arrest him, they were afraid of the crowds, who regarded him as a prophet.'),
(993585,34,40,22,1,'Once more Jesus spoke to them in parables.'),
(993586,34,40,22,15,'Then the Pharisees went away and conferred together as to how they might lay a trap for Jesus in the course of conversation.'),
(993587,34,40,22,16,'They sent their disciples, with the Herodians, to say to him, ‘Teacher, we know that you are an honest person, and that you teach the way of God honestly, and are not afraid of anyone; for you pay no regard to a person’s position.'),
(993588,34,40,22,17,'Tell us, then, what you think. Are we right in paying taxes to the Emperor, or not?’'),
(993589,34,40,22,18,'Perceiving their malice, Jesus answered,'),
(993590,34,40,22,20,'he asked,'),
(993591,34,40,22,21,'‘The Emperor’s,’ they answered, at which he said to them,'),
(993592,34,40,22,22,'They wondered at his answer, and left him alone and went away.'),
(993593,34,40,22,23,'That same day some Sadducees came up to Jesus, maintaining that there is no resurrection. Their question was this, –'),
(993594,34,40,22,24,'‘Teacher, Moses said – “should a man die without children, the man’s brother will become the husband of the widow, and raise a family for his brother.”'),
(993595,34,40,22,25,'Now we had living among us seven brothers; of whom the eldest married and died, and, as he had no family, left his wife for his brother.'),
(993596,34,40,22,26,'The same thing happened to the second and the third brothers, and indeed to all the seven.'),
(993597,34,40,22,27,'The woman herself died last of all.'),
(993598,34,40,22,28,'At the resurrection, then, whose wife will she be out of the seven, all of them having been married to her?’'),
(993599,34,40,22,33,'The crowds, who had been listening to him, were greatly struck with his teaching.'),
(993600,34,40,22,34,'When the Pharisees heard that Jesus had silenced the Sadducees, they collected together.'),
(993601,34,40,22,35,'Then one of them, a Student of the Law, to test him, asked this question –'),
(993602,34,40,22,36,'‘Teacher, what is the greatest commandment in the Law?’'),
(993603,34,40,22,37,'His answer was,'),
(993604,34,40,22,41,'Before the Pharisees separated, Jesus put this question to them –'),
(993605,34,40,22,46,'No one could say a word in answer; nor did anyone after that day venture to question him further.'),
(993606,34,40,23,1,'Then Jesus speaking to the crowds and to his disciples, said,'),
(993607,34,40,24,1,'Leaving the Temple Courts, Jesus was walking away, when his disciples came up to draw his attention to the Temple buildings.'),
(993608,34,40,24,3,'so, while Jesus was sitting on the Mount of Olives, his disciples came up to him privately and said, ‘Tell us when this will be, and what will be the sign of your coming, and of the close of the age.’'),
(993609,34,40,24,4,'Jesus replied to them,'),
(993610,34,40,26,1,'When Jesus had finished teaching all of that, he said to his disciples,'),
(993611,34,40,26,3,'Then the chief priests and the elders of the people met in the house of the high priest, who was called Caiaphas,'),
(993612,34,40,26,4,'and plotted together to arrest Jesus by stealth and put him to death;'),
(993613,34,40,26,5,'but they said, ‘Not during the Festival, or the people may riot.’'),
(993614,34,40,26,6,'After Jesus had reached Bethany, and while he was in the house of Simon the leper,'),
(993615,34,40,26,7,'a woman came up to him with an alabaster jar of very costly perfume, and poured the perfume on his head as he sat at the table.'),
(993616,34,40,26,8,'The disciples were indignant at seeing this. ‘What is this waste for?’ they exclaimed.'),
(993617,34,40,26,9,'‘It could have been sold for a large sum, and the money given to poor people.’'),
(993618,34,40,26,14,'It was then that one of the Twelve, named Judas Iscariot, made his way to the chief priests,'),
(993619,34,40,26,15,'and said ‘What are you willing to give me, if I betray Jesus to you?’ The Priests weighed him out thirty pieces of silver as payment.'),
(993620,34,40,26,16,'So from that time Judas looked for an opportunity to betray Jesus.'),
(993621,34,40,26,17,'On the first day of the Festival of the unleavened bread, the disciples came up to Jesus, and said, ‘Where do you wish us to make preparations for you to eat the Passover?’'),
(993622,34,40,26,19,'The disciples did as Jesus directed them, and prepared the Passover.'),
(993623,34,40,26,20,'In the evening Jesus took his place with the twelve disciples,'),
(993624,34,40,26,21,'and, while they were eating, he said,'),
(993625,34,40,26,22,'In great grief they began to say to him, one by one, ‘Can it be I, Master?’'),
(993626,34,40,26,25,'Judas, who was betraying him, turned to him and said, ‘Can it be I, Rabbi?’'),
(993627,34,40,26,26,'While they were eating, Jesus took some bread, and, after saying the blessing, broke it and, as he gave it to his disciples, said,'),
(993628,34,40,26,27,'Then he took a cup, and, after saying the thanksgiving, gave it to them, with the words,'),
(993629,34,40,26,30,'They then sang a hymn, and went out to the Mount of Olives.'),
(993630,34,40,26,31,'Then Jesus said to them,'),
(993631,34,40,26,33,'‘If everyone else falls away from you,’ Peter answered, ‘I will never fall away!’'),
(993632,34,40,26,35,'‘Even if I must die with you,’ Peter exclaimed, ‘I will never disown you!’ All the disciples spoke in the same way.'),
(993633,34,40,26,36,'Then Jesus came with them to a garden called Gethsemane, and he said to his disciples,'),
(993634,34,40,26,37,'Taking with him Peter and the two sons of Zebedee, he began to show signs of sadness and deep distress of mind.'),
(993635,34,40,26,39,'Going on a little further, he threw himself on his face in prayer.'),
(993636,34,40,26,40,'Then he came to his disciples, and found them asleep.'),
(993637,34,40,26,42,'Again, a second time, he went away, and prayed.'),
(993638,34,40,26,43,'And coming back again he found them asleep, for their eyes were heavy.'),
(993639,34,40,26,44,'So he left them, and went away again, and prayed a third time, again saying the same words.'),
(993640,34,40,26,45,'Then he came to the disciples, and said,'),
(993641,34,40,26,47,'And, while he was still speaking, Judas, who was one of the Twelve, came in sight; and with him was a great crowd of people, with swords and clubs, sent from the chief priests and elders of the people.'),
(993642,34,40,26,48,'Now the betrayer had arranged a signal with them. ‘The man whom I kiss,’ he had said, ‘will be the one; arrest him.’'),
(993643,34,40,26,49,'So he went up to Jesus at once, and exclaimed, ‘Welcome, Rabbi!’ and kissed him;'),
(993644,34,40,26,50,'at which Jesus said to him,'),
(993645,34,40,26,51,'Suddenly one of those who were with Jesus stretched out his hand, and drew his sword, and striking the high priest’s servant, cut off his ear.'),
(993646,34,40,26,55,'Jesus at the same time said to the crowds,'),
(993647,34,40,26,56,'The whole of this occurred in fulfilment of the Prophetic scriptures. Then the disciples all forsook him and fled.'),
(993648,34,40,26,57,'Those who had arrested Jesus took him to Caiaphas, the high priest, where the teachers of the Law and elders had assembled.'),
(993649,34,40,26,58,'Peter followed him at a distance as far as the courtyard of the offices, to see the end.'),
(993650,34,40,26,59,'Meanwhile the chief priests and the whole of the High Council were trying to get such false evidence against Jesus, as would warrant putting him to death,'),
(993651,34,40,26,60,'but they did not find any, although many came forward with false evidence. Later on, however, two men came forward and said,'),
(993652,34,40,26,61,'‘This man said “I am able to destroy the Temple of God, and to build it in three days.”’'),
(993653,34,40,26,62,'Then the high priest stood up, and said to Jesus, ‘Have you no answer? What is this evidence which these men are giving against you?’'),
(993654,34,40,26,63,'But Jesus remained silent. The high priest said to him, ‘I order you, by the living God, to tell us whether you are the Christ, the Son of God.’'),
(993655,34,40,26,65,'Then the high priest tore his robes. ‘This is blasphemy!’ he exclaimed. ‘Why do we want any more witnesses? You have just heard his blasphemy!'),
(993656,34,40,26,66,'What is your decision?’ They answered, ‘He deserves death.’'),
(993657,34,40,26,67,'Then they spat in his face, and struck him, while others dealt blows at him, saying as they did so,'),
(993658,34,40,26,68,'‘Now play the prophet for us, you Christ! Who was it that struck you?’'),
(993659,34,40,26,69,'Peter, meanwhile, was sitting outside in the courtyard; and a maidservant came up to him, and exclaimed, ‘Why, you were with Jesus the Galilean!’'),
(993660,34,40,26,70,'But Peter denied it before them all. ‘I do not know what you mean,’ he replied.'),
(993661,34,40,26,71,'When he had gone out into the gateway, another maid saw him, and said to those who were there, ‘This man was with Jesus of Nazareth!’'),
(993662,34,40,26,72,'Again he denied it with an oath, ‘I do not know the man!’'),
(993663,34,40,26,73,'But soon afterwards those who were standing by came up and said to Peter, ‘You also are certainly one of them; why, even your way of speaking proves it!’'),
(993664,34,40,26,74,'Then Peter said, ‘I swear that I do not know the man! May God punish me if I am lying!’ At that moment a cock crowed;'),
(993665,34,40,26,75,'and Peter remembered the words which Jesus had said –'),
(993666,34,40,27,1,'At daybreak all the chief priests and the elders of the people consulted together against Jesus, to bring about his death.'),
(993667,34,40,27,2,'They put him in chains and led him away, and gave him up to the Roman Governor, Pilate.'),
(993668,34,40,27,3,'Then Judas, who betrayed him, seeing that Jesus was condemned, repented of what he had done, and returned the thirty pieces of silver to the chief priests and elders.'),
(993669,34,40,27,4,'‘I did wrong in betraying a good man to his death,’ he said. ‘What has that to do with us?’ they replied. ‘You must see to that yourself.’'),
(993670,34,40,27,5,'Judas flung down the pieces of silver in the Temple, and left; and went away and hanged himself.'),
(993671,34,40,27,6,'The chief priests took the pieces of silver, but they said, ‘We must not put them into the Temple treasury, because they are blood-money.’'),
(993672,34,40,27,7,'So, after consultation, they bought with them the “Potter’s Field” for a burial-ground for foreigners;'),
(993673,34,40,27,8,'and that is why that field is called the “Field of Blood” to this very day.'),
(993674,34,40,27,9,'Then it was that these words spoken by the prophet Jeremiah were fulfilled – “They took the thirty pieces of silver, the price of him who was valued, whom some of the people of Israel valued,'),
(993675,34,40,27,10,'and gave them for the Potter’s field, as the Lord commanded me.”'),
(993676,34,40,27,11,'Meanwhile Jesus was brought before the Roman Governor. ‘Are you the king of the Jews?’ asked the Governor.'),
(993677,34,40,27,12,'While charges were being brought against him by the chief priests and elders, Jesus made no reply.'),
(993678,34,40,27,13,'Then Pilate said to him, ‘Don’t you hear how many accusations they are making against you?’'),
(993679,34,40,27,14,'Yet Jesus made no reply – not even a single word; at which the Governor was greatly astonished.'),
(993680,34,40,27,15,'Now, at the feast, the Governor was accustomed to grant the people the release of any one prisoner whom they might choose.'),
(993681,34,40,27,16,'At that time they had a notorious prisoner called Barabbas.'),
(993682,34,40,27,17,'So, when the people had collected, Pilate said to them, ‘Which do you wish me to release for you? Barabbas? Or Jesus who is called “Christ”?’'),
(993683,34,40,27,18,'For he knew that it was out of jealousy that they had given Jesus up to him.'),
(993684,34,40,27,19,'While he was still on the Bench, his wife sent this message to him – ‘Do not have anything to do with that good man, for I have been very unhappy today in a dream because of him.’'),
(993685,34,40,27,20,'But the chief priests and elders persuaded the crowds to ask for Barabbas, and to kill Jesus.'),
(993686,34,40,27,21,'The Governor, however, said to them, ‘Which of these two do you wish me to release for you?’'),
(993687,34,40,27,22,'‘What then,’ Pilate asked, ‘should I do with Jesus who is called “Christ?”’ ‘Crucify him,’ they all replied.'),
(993688,34,40,27,23,'‘Why, what harm has he done?’ he asked. But they kept shouting furiously, ‘Crucify him!’'),
(993689,34,40,27,24,'When Pilate saw that his efforts were unavailing, but that, on the contrary, a riot was beginning, he took some water, and washed his hands in the sight of the crowd, saying as he did so, ‘I am not answerable for this bloodshed; you must see to it yourselves.’'),
(993690,34,40,27,25,'And all the people answered, ‘His blood be on our heads and on our children’s!’'),
(993691,34,40,27,26,'The Pilate released Barabbas to them; but Jesus he scourged, and gave him up to be crucified.'),
(993692,34,40,27,27,'After that, the Governor’s soldiers took Jesus with them into the Government house, and gathered the whole garrison round him.'),
(993693,34,40,27,28,'They stripped him, and put on him a red military cloak,'),
(993694,34,40,27,29,'and having twisted some thorns into a crown, put it on his head, and a rod in his right hand, and then, going down on their knees before him, they mocked him. ‘Long life to you, king of the Jews!’ they said.'),
(993695,34,40,27,30,'They spat at him and, taking the rod, kept striking him on the head;'),
(993696,34,40,27,31,'and, when they had left off mocking him, they took off the military cloak, and put his own clothes on him, and led him away to be crucified.'),
(993697,34,40,27,32,'As they were on their way out, they came upon a man from Cyrene of the name of Simon; and they compelled him to go with them to carry the cross.'),
(993698,34,40,27,33,'On reaching a place named Golgotha (a place named from its likeness to a skull),'),
(993699,34,40,27,34,'they gave him some wine to drink which had been mixed with gall; but after tasting it, Jesus refused to drink it.'),
(993700,34,40,27,35,'When they had crucified him, they divided his clothes among them by casting lots.'),
(993701,34,40,27,36,'Then they sat down, and kept watch over him there.'),
(993702,34,40,27,37,'Above his head they fixed the accusation against him written out – “THIS IS JESUS THE KING OF THE JEWS.”'),
(993703,34,40,27,38,'At the same time two robbers were crucified with him, one on the right, the other on the left.'),
(993704,34,40,27,39,'The passers-by railed at him, shaking their heads as they said,'),
(993705,34,40,27,40,'‘You who “destroy the Temple and build one in three days,” save yourself! If you are God’s Son, come down from the cross!’'),
(993706,34,40,27,41,'In the same way the chief priests, with the Teaches of the Law and elders, said in mockery,'),
(993707,34,40,27,42,'‘He saved others, but he cannot save himself! He is the “king of Israel”! Why doesn’t he come down from the cross now, then we will believe in him.'),
(993708,34,40,27,43,'He has trusted in God; if God wants him, let him deliver him now; for he said “I am God’s Son.”’'),
(993709,34,40,27,44,'Even the robbers, who were crucified with him, insulted him in the same way.'),
(993710,34,40,27,45,'After midday a darkness came over all the country, lasting until three in the afternoon.'),
(993711,34,40,27,46,'About three Jesus called out loudly,'),
(993712,34,40,27,47,'Some of those standing by heard this, and said, ‘The man is calling for Elijah!’'),
(993713,34,40,27,48,'One of them immediately ran and took a sponge, and, filling it with common wine, put it on the end of a rod, and offered it to him to drink.'),
(993714,34,40,27,49,'But the rest said, ‘Wait and let us see if Elijah is coming to save him.’'),
(993715,34,40,27,50,'But Jesus, uttering another loud cry, gave up his spirit.'),
(993716,34,40,27,51,'Suddenly the Temple curtain was torn in two from top to bottom, the earth shook, the rocks were torn asunder,'),
(993717,34,40,27,52,'the tombs opened, and the bodies of many of God’s people who had fallen asleep rose,'),
(993718,34,40,27,53,'and they, leaving their tombs, went, after the resurrection of Jesus, into the Holy City, and appeared to many people.'),
(993719,34,40,27,54,'The Roman captain, and the men with him who were watching Jesus, on seeing the earthquake and all that was happening, became greatly frightened and exclaimed, ‘This must indeed have been God’s Son!’'),
(993720,34,40,27,55,'There were many women there, watching from a distance, who had accompanied Jesus from Galilee and had been attending on him.'),
(993721,34,40,27,56,'Among them were Mary of Magdala, Mary the mother of James and Joseph, and the mother of Zebedee’s sons.'),
(993722,34,40,27,57,'When evening had fallen, there came a rich man belonging to Ramah, named Joseph, who had himself become a disciple of Jesus.'),
(993723,34,40,27,58,'He went to see Pilate, and asked for the body of Jesus. Pilate ordered it to be given him.'),
(993724,34,40,27,59,'So Joseph took the body, and wrapped it in a clean linen sheet,'),
(993725,34,40,27,60,'and laid it in his newly made tomb which he had cut in the rock; and, before he left, he rolled a great stone against the entrance of the tomb.'),
(993726,34,40,27,61,'Mary of Magdala and the other Mary remained behind, sitting in front of the grave.'),
(993727,34,40,27,62,'The next day – that is, the day following the Preparation-day – the chief priests and Pharisees came in a body to Pilate, and said,'),
(993728,34,40,27,63,'‘Sir, we remember that, during his lifetime, that impostor said'),
(993729,34,40,27,64,'So order the tomb to be made secure until the third day. Otherwise his disciples may come and steal him, and then say to the people “He has risen from the dead,” when the latest imposture will be worse than the first.’'),
(993730,34,40,27,65,'‘You may have a guard,’ was Pilate’s reply. ‘Go and make the tomb as secure as you can.’'),
(993731,34,40,27,66,'So they went and made the tomb secure, by sealing the stone, in presence of the guard.'),
(993732,34,40,28,1,'After the Sabbath, as the first day of the week began to dawn, Mary of Magdala and the other Mary had gone to look at the grave,'),
(993733,34,40,28,2,'when suddenly a great earthquake occurred. For an angel of the Lord descended from heaven, and came and rolled away the stone, and seated himself on it.'),
(993734,34,40,28,3,'His appearance was as dazzling as lightning, and his clothing was as white as snow;'),
(993735,34,40,28,4,'and, in their terror of him, the men on guard trembled violently and became like dead men.'),
(993736,34,40,28,5,'But the angel, addressing the women, said, ‘You need not be afraid. I know that it is Jesus, who was crucified, for whom you are looking.'),
(993737,34,40,28,6,'He is not here; for he has risen, as he said he would. Come, and see the place where he was lying;'),
(993738,34,40,28,7,'and then go quickly and say to his disciples “He has risen from the dead, and is going before you into Galilee; there you will see him.” Remember, I have told you.’'),
(993739,34,40,28,8,'They left the tomb quickly, in awe and great joy, and ran to tell the news to the disciples.'),
(993740,34,40,28,9,'Suddenly Jesus met them.'),
(993741,34,40,28,11,'While they were still on their way, some of the guard came into the city, and reported to the chief priests everything that had happened.'),
(993742,34,40,28,12,'So they and the elders met and, after holding a consultation, gave a large sum of money to the soldiers,'),
(993743,34,40,28,13,'and told them to say that his disciples came in the night, and stole him while they were asleep;'),
(993744,34,40,28,14,'‘And should this matter come before the Governor,’ they added, ‘we will satisfy him, and see that you have nothing to fear.’'),
(993745,34,40,28,15,'So the soldiers took the money, and did as they were instructed. This story spread widely; the people of Judea still tell it today.'),
(993746,34,40,28,16,'The eleven disciples went to Galilee, to the mountain where Jesus told them to meet him;'),
(993747,34,40,28,17,'and, when they saw him, they bowed to the ground before him; although some felt doubtful.'),
(993748,34,40,28,18,'Then Jesus came up, and spoke to them, saying,'),
(993749,34,41,1,1,'The beginning of the good news about Jesus Christ.'),
(993750,34,41,1,2,'It is said in the prophet Isaiah –'),
(993751,34,41,1,3,'The voice of one crying aloud in the wilderness:'),
(993752,34,41,1,4,'John the Baptizer appeared in the wilderness, proclaiming a baptism on repentance, for the forgiveness of sins.'),
(993753,34,41,1,5,'The whole of Judea, as well as all the inhabitants of Jerusalem, went out to him; and they were baptized by him in the Jordan River, confessing their sins.'),
(993754,34,41,1,6,'John wore clothes made of camels’ hair, with a leather strap round his waist, and lived on locusts and wild honey;'),
(993755,34,41,1,7,'and he proclaimed – ‘After me is coming someone more powerful than I am, and I am not fit even to stoop down and unfasten his sandals.'),
(993756,34,41,1,8,'I have baptized you with water, but he will baptize you with the Holy Spirit.’'),
(993757,34,41,1,9,'Now about that time Jesus came from Nazareth in Galilee, and was baptized by John in the Jordan.'),
(993758,34,41,1,10,'Just as he was coming up out of the water, he saw the heavens split open and the Spirit coming down to him like a dove,'),
(993759,34,41,1,11,'and from the heavens came a voice – ‘You are my dearly loved son; you bring me great joy.’'),
(993760,34,41,1,12,'Immediately afterwards the Spirit drove Jesus out into the wilderness;'),
(993761,34,41,1,13,'and he was there in the wilderness forty days, tempted by Satan, and among the wild beasts, while the angels helped him.'),
(993762,34,41,1,14,'After John had been arrested, Jesus went to Galilee, proclaiming the good news of God –'),
(993763,34,41,1,16,'As Jesus was going along the shore of the Sea of Galilee, he saw Simon and his brother Andrew casting a net in the sea, for they were fishermen.'),
(993764,34,41,1,18,'They left their nets at once, and followed him.'),
(993765,34,41,1,19,'Going on a little further, he saw James, Zebedee’s son, and his brother John, who were in their boat mending the nets.'),
(993766,34,41,1,20,'Jesus called them at once, and they left their father Zebedee in the boat with the crew, and went after him.'),
(993767,34,41,1,21,'They walked to Capernaum. On the next Sabbath Jesus went into the synagogue and began to teach.'),
(993768,34,41,1,22,'The people were amazed at his teaching, for he taught them like one who had authority, and not like the teachers of the Law.'),
(993769,34,41,1,23,'Now there was in their synagogue at the time a man under the power of a foul spirit, who called out,'),
(993770,34,41,1,24,'‘What do you want with us, Jesus the Nazarene? Have you come to destroy us? I know who you are – the Holy One of God!’'),
(993771,34,41,1,25,'But Jesus rebuked the spirit,'),
(993772,34,41,1,26,'The foul spirit threw the man into a fit, and with a loud cry came out from him.'),
(993773,34,41,1,27,'They were all so amazed that they kept asking each other, ‘What is this? What is this, a new kind of teaching? He gives his commands with authority even to the foul spirits, and they obey him!’'),
(993774,34,41,1,28,'His fame spread at once in all directions, through the whole region of Galilee.'),
(993775,34,41,1,29,'As soon as they had left the synagogue, they went to the house of Simon and Andrew, along with James and John.'),
(993776,34,41,1,30,'Now Simon’s mother-in-law was lying ill with a fever, and they at once told Jesus about her.'),
(993777,34,41,1,31,'Jesus went up to her and, grasping her hand, raised her up; the fever left her, and she began to take care of them.'),
(993778,34,41,1,32,'In the evening, after sunset, the people brought to Jesus all who were ill or possessed by demons;'),
(993779,34,41,1,33,'and the whole city was gathered round the door.'),
(993780,34,41,1,34,'Jesus cured many who were ill with various diseases, and drove out many demons, and would not permit them to speak, because they knew him to be the Christ.'),
(993781,34,41,1,35,'In the morning, long before daylight, Jesus got up and went out to a lonely spot, and there he began to pray.'),
(993782,34,41,1,36,'But Simon and his companions went out searching for him;'),
(993783,34,41,1,37,'and, when they found him, they exclaimed, ‘Everyone is looking for you!’'),
(993784,34,41,1,38,'But Jesus said to them,'),
(993785,34,41,1,39,'And he went about making his proclamation in their synagogues all through Galilee, and driving out the demons.'),
(993786,34,41,1,40,'One day a leper came to Jesus and, falling on his knees, begged him for help. ‘If only you are willing,’ he said, ‘you are able to make me clean.’'),
(993787,34,41,1,41,'Moved with compassion, Jesus stretched out his hand and touched him, saying as he did so,'),
(993788,34,41,1,42,'Instantly the leprosy left the man, and he became clean;'),
(993789,34,41,1,43,'and then Jesus, after sternly warning him, immediately sent him away, and said to him,'),
(993790,34,41,1,45,'The man, however, went away, and began to speak about it publicly, and to spread the story so widely, that Jesus could no longer go openly into a town, but stayed outside in lonely places; and people came to him from every direction.'),
(993791,34,41,2,1,'Some days later, when Jesus came back to Capernaum, the news spread that he was in a house there;'),
(993792,34,41,2,2,'and so many people collected together, that after a while there was no room for them even round the door; and he began to tell them his message.'),
(993793,34,41,2,3,'Some people came, bringing to him a paralysed man, who was being carried by four of them.'),
(993794,34,41,2,4,'Being, however, unable to get him near to Jesus, owing to the crowd, they removed the roofing above Jesus; and, when they had made an opening, they let down the mat on which the paralysed man was lying.'),
(993795,34,41,2,5,'When Jesus saw their faith, he said to the man,'),
(993796,34,41,2,6,'But some of the teachers of the Law who were sitting there were debating in their minds,'),
(993797,34,41,2,7,'‘Why does this man speak like this? He is blaspheming! Who can forgive sins except God?’'),
(993798,34,41,2,8,'Jesus, at once intuitively aware that they were debating with themselves in this way, said to them,'),
(993799,34,41,2,12,'The man got up, and immediately took up his mat, and went out before them all; at which they were amazed, and, as they praised God, they said, ‘We have never seen anything like this!’'),
(993800,34,41,2,13,'Jesus went out again to the sea; and all the people came to him, and he taught them.'),
(993801,34,41,2,14,'As he went along, he saw Levi, the son of Alphaeus, sitting in the tax office, and said to him,'),
(993802,34,41,2,15,'Later on he was in his house having dinner, and a number of tax-gatherers and outcasts took their places at the table with Jesus and his disciples; for many of them were following him.'),
(993803,34,41,2,16,'When the teachers of the Law belonging to the party of the Pharisees saw that he was eating in the company of such people, they said to his disciples, ‘Why does he eat with the tax-gatherers and outcasts?’'),
(993804,34,41,2,17,'Hearing this, Jesus said,'),
(993805,34,41,2,18,'Now John’s disciples and the Pharisees were fasting, and people came and asked Jesus, ‘Why is it that John’s disciples and the disciples of the Pharisees fast, while yours do not?’'),
(993806,34,41,2,19,'Jesus answered,'),
(993807,34,41,2,23,'One Sabbath, as Jesus was walking through the cornfields, his disciples began to pick the ears of wheat as they went along.'),
(993808,34,41,2,24,'‘Look!’ the Pharisees said to him, ‘why are they doing what is not allowed on the Sabbath?’'),
(993809,34,41,2,27,'Then Jesus added,'),
(993810,34,41,3,1,'On another occasion Jesus went in to a synagogue, where there was a man whose hand was withered.'),
(993811,34,41,3,2,'And they watched Jesus closely, to see if he would cure the man on the Sabbath, so that they might have a charge to bring against him.'),
(993812,34,41,3,4,'and to the people he said,'),
(993813,34,41,3,5,'As they remained silent, Jesus looked round at them in anger, grieving at the hardness of their hearts, and said to the man,'),
(993814,34,41,3,6,'Immediately on leaving the synagogue, the Pharisees and the Herodians united in laying a plot against Jesus, to put him to death.'),
(993815,34,41,3,7,'Then Jesus went away with his disciples to the sea, followed by a great number of people from Galilee.'),
(993816,34,41,3,8,'A great number, hearing of all that he was doing, came to him from Judea, from Jerusalem, from Edom, from beyond the Jordan, and from the country round Tyre and Sidon.'),
(993817,34,41,3,9,'So Jesus told his disciples to keep a small boat close by, so that the crowd would not crush him.'),
(993818,34,41,3,10,'For he had cured many of them, and so people kept crowding around him, so all who were sick might touch him.'),
(993819,34,41,3,11,'The foul spirits, too, whenever they caught sight of him, flung themselves down before him, and screamed out, ‘You are the Son of God’!'),
(993820,34,41,3,12,'But he repeatedly warned them not to make him known.'),
(993821,34,41,3,13,'Jesus made his way up the hill, and called those whom he wished; and they went to him.'),
(993822,34,41,3,14,'He appointed twelve – whom he also named “apostles” – so that they might be with him, and that he might send them out as his messengers, to preach,'),
(993823,34,41,3,15,'and with power to drive out demons.'),
(993824,34,41,3,16,'So he appointed the Twelve – Peter (which was the name that Jesus gave to Simon),'),
(993825,34,41,3,17,'James, the son of Zebedee, and his brother John (to whom he gave the name of Boanerges, which means the Thunderers),'),
(993826,34,41,3,18,'Andrew, Philip, Bartholomew, Matthew, Thomas, James the son of Alphaeus, Thaddaeus, Simon the Zealot,'),
(993827,34,41,3,19,'and Judas Iscariot, the man who betrayed him.'),
(993828,34,41,3,20,'Jesus went into a house; and again a crowd collected, so that they were not even able to eat their food.'),
(993829,34,41,3,21,'When his relatives heard of it, they went to take charge of him, for they said that he was out of his mind.'),
(993830,34,41,3,22,'The teachers of the Law, who had come down from Jerusalem, said, ‘He has Beelzebul in him! He drives the demons out by the help of their chief.’'),
(993831,34,41,3,23,'So Jesus called them to him, and answered them in parables,'),
(993832,34,41,3,30,'This was said in reply to the charge that he had a foul spirit in him.'),
(993833,34,41,3,31,'His mother and his brothers came, and stood outside, and sent to ask him to come to them.'),
(993834,34,41,3,32,'There was a crowd sitting round Jesus, and some of them said to him, ‘Look, your mother and your brothers are outside, asking for you.’'),
(993835,34,41,3,34,'Then he looked around on the people sitting in a circle round him, and said,'),
(993836,34,41,4,1,'Jesus again began to teach by the sea; and, as an immense crowd was gathering round him, he got into a boat, and sat in it on the sea, while all the people were on the shore at the water’s edge.'),
(993837,34,41,4,2,'Then he taught them many truths in parables; and in the course of his teaching he said to them:'),
(993838,34,41,4,9,'And Jesus said,'),
(993839,34,41,4,10,'Afterwards, when he was alone, his followers and the Twelve asked him about his parables;'),
(993840,34,41,4,11,'and he said,'),
(993841,34,41,4,21,'Jesus said to them,'),
(993842,34,41,4,26,'Jesus also said,'),
(993843,34,41,4,30,'Jesus also said,'),
(993844,34,41,4,33,'With many such parables Jesus used to speak to the people of his message, as far as they were able to receive it;'),
(993845,34,41,4,34,'and to them he never used to speak except in parables; but in private to his own disciples he explained everything.'),
(993846,34,41,4,35,'In the evening of the same day, Jesus said to them,'),
(993847,34,41,4,36,'So, leaving the crowd behind, they took him with them, just as he was, in the boat; and there were other boats with him.'),
(993848,34,41,4,37,'A violent squall came on, and the waves kept dashing into the boat, so that the boat was actually filling.'),
(993849,34,41,4,38,'Jesus was in the stern asleep on the cushion; and the disciples roused him and cried, ‘Teacher! Is it nothing to you that we are lost?’'),
(993850,34,41,4,39,'Jesus rose and rebuked the wind, and said to the sea,'),
(993851,34,41,4,41,'But they were struck with great awe, and said to one another, ‘Who can this be that even the wind and the sea obey him?’'),
(993852,34,41,5,1,'They came to the other side of the sea – the region of the Gerasenes;'),
(993853,34,41,5,2,'and, as soon as Jesus had got out of the boat, he met a man coming out of the tombs, who was under the power of a foul spirit,'),
(993854,34,41,5,3,'and who made his home in the tombs. No one had ever been able to secure him, even with a chain;'),
(993855,34,41,5,4,'for, though he had many times been left secured with fetters and chains, he had snapped the chains and broken the fetters to pieces, and no one could master him.'),
(993856,34,41,5,5,'Night and day alike, he was continually shrieking in the tombs and among the hills, and cutting himself with stones.'),
(993857,34,41,5,6,'Catching sight of Jesus from a distance, he ran and bowed to the ground before him,'),
(993858,34,41,5,7,'shrieking out in a loud voice, ‘What do you want with me, Jesus, Son of the Most High God? For God’s sake do not torment me!’'),
(993859,34,41,5,8,'For Jesus had said,'),
(993860,34,41,5,9,'And he asked him,'),
(993861,34,41,5,10,'and he begged Jesus again and again not to send them away out of that country.'),
(993862,34,41,5,11,'There was a large drove of pigs close by, feeding on the hillside;'),
(993863,34,41,5,12,'and the spirits begged Jesus, ‘Send us into the pigs so that we can take possession of them.’'),
(993864,34,41,5,13,'Jesus gave them leave. They came out, and entered into the pigs; and the drove – about two thousand in number – rushed down the steep slope into the sea and were drowned in the sea.'),
(993865,34,41,5,14,'Then the men who tended them ran away, and carried the news to the town, and to the country round; and the people went to see what had happened.'),
(993866,34,41,5,15,'When they came to Jesus, they found the possessed man sitting there, clothed and in his right mind – the man who had had the “Legion” in him – and they were awe-struck.'),
(993867,34,41,5,16,'Then those who had seen it related to them all that had happened to the possessed man, as well as about the pigs;'),
(993868,34,41,5,17,'so they began to beg Jesus to leave their region.'),
(993869,34,41,5,18,'As Jesus was getting into the boat, the possessed man begged him to let him stay with him.'),
(993870,34,41,5,19,'But Jesus refused.'),
(993871,34,41,5,20,'So the man went, and began to proclaim in the district of the Ten Towns all that Jesus had done for him; and everyone was amazed.'),
(993872,34,41,5,21,'By the time Jesus had recrossed in the boat to the opposite shore, a great number of people had gathered to meet him, and were standing by the sea.'),
(993873,34,41,5,22,'One of the leaders of the synagogue, whose name was Jairus, came and, as soon as he saw Jesus, threw himself at his feet and begged him repeatedly,'),
(993874,34,41,5,23,'saying, ‘My little daughter is at death’s door. Please come and place your hands on her so that she may recover and live.’'),
(993875,34,41,5,24,'So Jesus went with him. A great number of people followed Jesus, and kept pressing round him.'),
(993876,34,41,5,25,'Meanwhile a woman who for twelve years had suffered from haemorrhage,'),
(993877,34,41,5,26,'and undergone much at the hands of many doctors, (spending all she had without obtaining any relief, but, on the contrary, growing worse),'),
(993878,34,41,5,27,'heard about Jesus, came behind in the crowd, and touched his cloak.'),
(993879,34,41,5,28,'‘If I can only touch his clothes,’ she said, ‘I will get well!’'),
(993880,34,41,5,29,'At once her bleeding stopped, and she felt in herself that she was cured of her affliction.'),
(993881,34,41,5,30,'Jesus at once became aware of the power that had gone out from him, and, turning round in the crowd, he said,'),
(993882,34,41,5,31,'‘You see the people pressing round you,’ exclaimed his disciples, ‘and yet you say'),
(993883,34,41,5,32,'But Jesus looked about to see who had done it.'),
(993884,34,41,5,33,'Then the woman, in fear and trembling, knowing what had happened to her, came and threw herself down before him, and told him the whole truth.'),
(993885,34,41,5,35,'Before he had finished speaking, some people from the house of the synagogue leader came and said, ‘Your daughter is dead! Why should you trouble the teacher further?’'),
(993886,34,41,5,36,'But Jesus, overhearing what they were saying, said to the synagogue leader,'),
(993887,34,41,5,37,'And he allowed no one to accompany him, except Peter, James, and John, the brother of James.'),
(993888,34,41,5,38,'Presently they reached the leader’s house, where Jesus saw a scene of confusion – people weeping and wailing incessantly.'),
(993889,34,41,5,40,'They began to laugh at him; but he sent them all out, and then, with the child’s father and mother and his companions, went into the room where she was lying.'),
(993890,34,41,5,41,'Taking her hand, Jesus said to her,'),
(993891,34,41,5,42,'The little girl stood up at once, and began to walk about; for she was twelve years old. And, as soon as they saw it, they were overwhelmed with amazement;'),
(993892,34,41,5,43,'but Jesus repeatedly cautioned them not to let anyone know of it, and told them to give her something to eat.'),
(993893,34,41,6,1,'On leaving that place, Jesus, followed by his disciples, went to his own part of the country.'),
(993894,34,41,6,2,'When the Sabbath came, he began to teach in the synagogue; and the people, as they listened, were deeply impressed. ‘Where did he get this?’ they said, ‘and what is this wisdom that has been given him? And these miracles which he is doing?'),
(993895,34,41,6,3,'Isn’t he the carpenter, the son of Mary, and the brother of James, and Joses, and Judas, and Simon? And aren’t his sisters, too, living here among us?’ This proved a hindrance to their believing in him;'),
(993896,34,41,6,4,'at which Jesus said,'),
(993897,34,41,6,5,'And he could not work any miracle there, beyond placing his hands on a few infirm persons, and curing them;'),
(993898,34,41,6,6,'and he wondered at the want of faith shown by the people. Jesus went round the villages, one after another, teaching.'),
(993899,34,41,6,7,'He called the Twelve to him, and began to send them out as his messengers, two and two, and gave them authority over foul spirits.'),
(993900,34,41,6,8,'He instructed them to take nothing but a staff for the journey – not even bread, or a bag, or coins in their purse;'),
(993901,34,41,6,9,'but they were to wear sandals, and not to put on a second coat.'),
(993902,34,41,6,12,'So they set out, and proclaimed the need of repentance.'),
(993903,34,41,6,13,'They drove out many demons, and anointed with oil many who were infirm, and cured them.'),
(993904,34,41,6,14,'Now King Herod heard of Jesus; for his name had become well known. People were saying – ‘John the Baptizer must have risen from the dead, and that is why these miraculous powers are active in him.’'),
(993905,34,41,6,15,'Others again said – ‘He is Elijah,’ and others – ‘He is a prophet, like one of the great prophets.’'),
(993906,34,41,6,16,'But when Herod heard of him, he said – ‘The man whom I beheaded – John – he must be risen!’'),
(993907,34,41,6,17,'For Herod himself had sent and arrested John, and put him in prison, in chains, to please Herodias, the wife of his brother Philip, because Herod had married her.'),
(993908,34,41,6,18,'For John had said to Herod – ‘You have no right to be living with your brother’s wife.’'),
(993909,34,41,6,19,'So Herodias was incensed against John, and wanted to put him to death, but was unable to do so,'),
(993910,34,41,6,20,'because Herod stood in fear of John, knowing him to be an upright and holy man, and protected him. He had listened to John, but still remained much perplexed, and yet he found pleasure in listening to him.'),
(993911,34,41,6,21,'A suitable opportunity, however, occurred when Herod, on his birthday, gave a dinner to his high officials, and his generals, and the foremost men in Galilee.'),
(993912,34,41,6,22,'When his daughter – that is, the daughter of Herodias – came in and danced, she delighted Herod and those who were dining with him. ‘Ask me for whatever you like,’ the king said to the girl, ‘and I will give it to you’;'),
(993913,34,41,6,23,'and he swore to her that he would give her whatever she asked him – up to half his kingdom.'),
(993914,34,41,6,24,'The girl went out, and said to her mother ‘What must I ask for?’'),
(993915,34,41,6,25,'So she went in as quickly as possible to the king, and made her request. ‘I want you,’ she said, ‘to give me at once, on a dish, the head of John the Baptist.’'),
(993916,34,41,6,26,'The king was much distressed; yet, because of his oath and of the guests at his table, he did not like to refuse her.'),
(993917,34,41,6,27,'He immediately dispatched one of his bodyguard, with orders to bring John’s head. The man went and beheaded John in the prison,'),
(993918,34,41,6,28,'and, bringing his head on a dish, gave it to the girl, and the girl gave it to her mother.'),
(993919,34,41,6,29,'When John’s disciples heard of it, they came and took his body away, and laid it in a tomb.'),
(993920,34,41,6,30,'When the apostles came back to Jesus, they told him all that they had done and all that they had taught.'),
(993921,34,41,6,32,'So they set off privately in their boat for a lonely spot.'),
(993922,34,41,6,33,'Many people saw them going, and recognised them, and from all the towns they flocked together to the place on foot, and got there before them.'),
(993923,34,41,6,34,'On getting out of the boat, Jesus saw a great crowd, and his heart was moved at the sight of them, because they were like sheep without a shepherd; and he began to teach them many things.'),
(993924,34,41,6,35,'When it grew late, his disciples came up to him, and said, ‘This is a lonely spot, and it is already late.'),
(993925,34,41,6,36,'Send the people away, so that they may go to the farms and villages around and buy themselves something to eat.’'),
(993926,34,41,6,37,'But Jesus answered,'),
(993927,34,41,6,39,'Jesus directed them to make all the people take their seats on the green grass, in parties;'),
(993928,34,41,6,40,'and they sat down in groups – in hundreds, and in fifties.'),
(993929,34,41,6,41,'Taking the five loaves and the two fish, Jesus looked up to heaven, and said the blessing; he broke the loaves into pieces, and gave them to his disciples for them to serve out to the people, and he divided the two fish also among them all.'),
(993930,34,41,6,42,'Everyone had sufficient to eat;'),
(993931,34,41,6,43,'and they picked up enough broken pieces to fill twelve baskets, as well as some of the fish.'),
(993932,34,41,6,44,'The people who ate the bread were five thousand in number.'),
(993933,34,41,6,45,'Immediately afterwards Jesus made his disciples get into the boat, and cross over in advance, in the direction of Bethsaida, while he himself was dismissing the crowd.'),
(993934,34,41,6,46,'After he had taken leave of the people, he went away up the hill to pray.'),
(993935,34,41,6,47,'When evening fell, the boat was out in the middle of the sea, and Jesus on the shore alone.'),
(993936,34,41,6,48,'Seeing them labouring at the oars – for the wind was against them – about three hours after midnight Jesus came towards them, walking on the water, intending to join them.'),
(993937,34,41,6,49,'But, when they saw him walking on the water, they thought it was a ghost, and cried out;'),
(993938,34,41,6,50,'for all of them saw him, and were terrified. But Jesus at once spoke to them.'),
(993939,34,41,6,51,'Then he got into the boat with them, and the wind dropped. The disciples were utterly amazed,'),
(993940,34,41,6,52,'for they had not understood about the loaves, their minds being slow to learn.'),
(993941,34,41,6,53,'When they had crossed over, they landed at Gennesaret, and moored the boat.'),
(993942,34,41,6,54,'But they had no sooner left her than the people, recognising Jesus,'),
(993943,34,41,6,55,'hurried over the whole country-side, and began to carry about on mats those who were ill, wherever they heard he was.'),
(993944,34,41,6,56,'So wherever he went – to villages, or towns, or farms – they would lay their sick in the market-places, begging him to let them touch only the tassel of his cloak; and all who touched were made well.'),
(993945,34,41,7,1,'One day the Pharisees and some of the teachers of the Law who had come from Jerusalem gathered round Jesus.'),
(993946,34,41,7,2,'They had noticed that some of his disciples ate their food with their hands “defiled,” by which they meant unwashed.'),
(993947,34,41,7,3,'(For the Pharisees, and indeed all strict Jews, will not eat without first scrupulously washing their hands, holding in this to the traditions of their ancestors.'),
(993948,34,41,7,4,'When they come from market, they will not eat without first sprinkling themselves; and there are many other customs which they have inherited and hold to, such as the ceremonial washing of cups, and jugs, and copper pans).'),
(993949,34,41,7,5,'So the Pharisees and the teachers of the Law asked Jesus this question – ‘How is it that your disciples do not follow the traditions of our ancestors, but eat their food with defiled hands?’'),
(993950,34,41,7,6,'His answer was,'),
(993951,34,41,7,14,'Then Jesus called the people to him again, and said,'),
(993952,34,41,7,17,'When Jesus went indoors, away from the crowd, his disciples began questioning him about this saying.'),
(993953,34,41,7,24,'On leaving that place, Jesus went to the district of Tyre and Sidon. He went into a house, and did not wish anyone to know it, but could not escape notice.'),
(993954,34,41,7,25,'For a woman, whose little daughter had a foul spirit in her, heard of him immediately, and came and threw herself at his feet –'),
(993955,34,41,7,26,'the woman was a foreigner, from Syrian Phoenicia – and she begged him to drive the demon out of her daughter.'),
(993956,34,41,7,28,'‘Yes, Master,’ she replied. ‘Even the dogs under the table do feed on the children’s crumbs.’'),
(993957,34,41,7,30,'The woman went home, and found the child lying on her bed, and the demon gone.'),
(993958,34,41,7,31,'On returning from the district of Tyre, Jesus went, by way of Sidon, to the Sea of Galilee, across the district of the Ten Towns.'),
(993959,34,41,7,32,'Some people brought to him a man who was deaf and almost dumb, and they begged Jesus to place his hand on him.'),
(993960,34,41,7,33,'Jesus took him aside from the crowd quietly, put his fingers into the man’s ears, and touched his tongue with saliva.'),
(993961,34,41,7,34,'Then, looking up to heaven, he sighed, and said to the man,'),
(993962,34,41,7,35,'The man’s ears were opened, the string of his tongue was freed, and he began to talk plainly.'),
(993963,34,41,7,36,'Jesus insisted on their not telling anyone; but the more he insisted, the more perseveringly they made it known,'),
(993964,34,41,7,37,'and a profound impression was made on the people. ‘He has done everything well!’ they exclaimed. ‘He makes even the deaf hear and the dumb speak!’'),
(993965,34,41,8,1,'About that time, when there was again a great crowd of people who had nothing to eat, Jesus called his disciples to him, and said,'),
(993966,34,41,8,4,'‘Where will it be possible,’ his disciples answered, ‘to get sufficient bread for these people in this lonely place?’'),
(993967,34,41,8,6,'Jesus told the crowd to sit down on the ground. Then he took the seven loaves, and, after saying the thanksgiving, broke them, and gave them to his disciples to serve out; and they served them out to the crowd.'),
(993968,34,41,8,7,'They had also a few small fish; and, after he had said the blessing, he told the disciples to serve out these as well.'),
(993969,34,41,8,8,'The people had sufficient to eat, and they picked up seven baskets full of the broken pieces that were left.'),
(993970,34,41,8,9,'There were about four thousand people. Then Jesus dismissed them.'),
(993971,34,41,8,10,'Immediately afterwards, getting into the boat with his disciples, Jesus went to the district of Dalmanutha.'),
(993972,34,41,8,11,'Here the Pharisees came out, and began to argue with Jesus, asking him for some sign from the heavens, to test him.'),
(993973,34,41,8,12,'Sighing deeply, Jesus said,'),
(993974,34,41,8,13,'So he left them to themselves, and, getting into the boat again, went away to the opposite shore.'),
(993975,34,41,8,14,'Now the disciples had forgotten to take any bread with them, one loaf being all that they had in the boat.'),
(993976,34,41,8,15,'So Jesus gave them this warning.'),
(993977,34,41,8,16,'They began talking to one another about their being short of bread;'),
(993978,34,41,8,17,'and, noticing this, Jesus said to them,'),
(993979,34,41,8,22,'They came to Bethsaida. There some people brought a blind man to Jesus, and begged him to touch him.'),
(993980,34,41,8,23,'Taking the blind man’s hand, Jesus led him to the outskirts of the village, and, when he had put saliva on the man’s eyes, he placed his hands on him, and asked him,'),
(993981,34,41,8,24,'The man looked up, and said, ‘I see the people, for, as they walk about, they look to me like trees.’'),
(993982,34,41,8,25,'Then Jesus again placed his hands on the man’s eyes; and the man saw clearly, his sight was restored, and he saw everything with perfect distinctness.'),
(993983,34,41,8,26,'Jesus sent him to his home, and said,'),
(993984,34,41,8,27,'Afterwards Jesus and his disciples went into the villages round Caesarea Philippi; and on the way he asked his disciples this question –'),
(993985,34,41,8,28,'‘John the Baptist,’ they answered, ‘but others say Elijah, while others say one of the prophets.’'),
(993986,34,41,8,30,'At which Jesus charged them not to say this about him to anyone.'),
(993987,34,41,8,31,'Then he began to teach them that the Son of Man must undergo much suffering, and that he must be rejected by the elders, and the chief priests, and the teachers of the Law, and be put to death, and rise again after three days.'),
(993988,34,41,8,32,'He said all this quite openly. But Peter took Jesus aside, and began to rebuke him.'),
(993989,34,41,8,33,'Jesus, however, turning round and seeing his disciples, rebuked Peter.'),
(993990,34,41,8,34,'Calling the people and his disciples to him, Jesus said,'),
(993991,34,41,9,2,'Six days later, Jesus took with him Peter, James, and John, and led them up a high mountain alone by themselves. There his appearance was transformed before their eyes,'),
(993992,34,41,9,3,'and his clothes became whiter than any launderer in the whole world could bleach them.'),
(993993,34,41,9,4,'And Elijah appeared to them, in company with Moses; and they were talking with Jesus.'),
(993994,34,41,9,5,'‘Rabbi,’ said Peter, interposing, ‘it is good to be here; let us make three tents, one for you, one for Moses, and one for Elijah.’'),
(993995,34,41,9,6,'For he did not know what to say, because they were much afraid.'),
(993996,34,41,9,7,'Then a cloud came down and enveloped them; and from the cloud there came a voice – ‘This is my dearly loved son; listen to him.’'),
(993997,34,41,9,8,'And suddenly, on looking round, they saw that there was now no one with them but Jesus alone.'),
(993998,34,41,9,9,'As they were going down the mountainside, Jesus cautioned them not to relate what they had seen to anyone, until after the Son of Man had risen from the dead.'),
(993999,34,41,9,10,'They seized on these words and discussed with one another what this “rising from the dead” meant.'),
(994000,34,41,9,11,'‘How is it,’ they asked Jesus, ‘that our teachers of the Law say that Elijah has to come first?’'),
(994001,34,41,9,14,'When they came to the other disciples, they saw a great crowd round them, and some teachers of the Law arguing with them.'),
(994002,34,41,9,15,'But, as soon as they saw Jesus, all the people, in great astonishment, ran up and greeted him.'),
(994003,34,41,9,17,'‘Teacher,’ answered a man in the crowd, ‘I brought my son to see you, as he has a spirit in him that makes him mute;'),
(994004,34,41,9,18,'and, wherever it seizes him, it dashes him down; he foams at the mouth and grinds his teeth, and he is pining away. I asked your disciples to drive the spirit out, but they failed.’'),
(994005,34,41,9,20,'They brought him to Jesus; but no sooner did the boy see him than the spirit threw him into convulsions; and he fell on the ground, and rolled about, foaming at the mouth.'),
(994006,34,41,9,22,'‘From his childhood,’ he answered. ‘It has often thrown him into fire and into water to put an end to his life; but, if you can possibly do anything, take pity on us, and help us!’'),
(994007,34,41,9,24,'The boy’s father immediately cried out, ‘I have faith; help my want of faith!’'),
(994008,34,41,9,25,'But, when Jesus saw that a crowd was quickly collecting, he rebuked the foul spirit,'),
(994009,34,41,9,26,'With a loud cry the spirit threw the boy into repeated convulsions, and then came out from him. The boy looked like a corpse, so that most of them said that he was dead.'),
(994010,34,41,9,27,'But Jesus took his hand, and lifted him; and he stood up.'),
(994011,34,41,9,28,'When Jesus had gone indoors, his disciples asked him privately, ‘Why couldn’t we drive it out?’'),
(994012,34,41,9,30,'Leaving that place, Jesus and his disciples went on their way through Galilee; but he did not wish anyone to know it,'),
(994013,34,41,9,31,'for he was instructing his disciples, and telling them –'),
(994014,34,41,9,32,'But the disciples did not understand his meaning and were afraid to question him.'),
(994015,34,41,9,33,'They came to Capernaum. When Jesus had gone into the house, he asked them,'),
(994016,34,41,9,34,'But they were silent; for on the way they had been arguing with one another which was the greatest.'),
(994017,34,41,9,35,'Sitting down, Jesus called the Twelve and said,'),
(994018,34,41,9,36,'Then Jesus took a little child, and placed it in the middle of them. Taking it in his arms, he said to them,'),
(994019,34,41,9,38,'‘Teacher,’ said John, ‘we saw a man driving out demons by using your name, and we tried to prevent him, because he did not follow us.’'),
(994020,34,41,10,1,'On leaving that place, Jesus went into the district of Judea on the other side of the Jordan. Crowds gathered about him again; and again, as usual, he began teaching them.'),
(994021,34,41,10,2,'Presently some Pharisees came up and, to test him, asked, ‘Has a husband the right to divorce his wife?’'),
(994022,34,41,10,4,'‘Moses,’ they said, ‘permitted a man to draw up in writing a notice of separation and divorce his wife.’'),
(994023,34,41,10,10,'When they were indoors, the disciples asked him again about this,'),
(994024,34,41,10,11,'and he said,'),
(994025,34,41,10,13,'Some of the people were bringing little children to Jesus, for him to touch them; but the disciples rebuked those who had brought them.'),
(994026,34,41,10,14,'When, however, Jesus saw this, he was indignant.'),
(994027,34,41,10,16,'Then he embraced the children, and, placing his hands on them, gave them his blessing.'),
(994028,34,41,10,17,'As Jesus was resuming his journey, a man came running up to him, and threw himself on his knees before him. ‘Good teacher,’ he asked, ‘what must I do to gain eternal life?’'),
(994029,34,41,10,20,'‘Teacher,’ he replied, ‘I have observed all these from my childhood.’'),
(994030,34,41,10,21,'Jesus looked at the man, and his heart went out to him, and he said,'),
(994031,34,41,10,22,'But the man’s face clouded at these words, and he went away distressed, for he had great possessions.'),
(994032,34,41,10,23,'Then Jesus looked round, and said to his disciples,'),
(994033,34,41,10,24,'The disciples were amazed at his words. But Jesus said again,'),
(994034,34,41,10,26,'‘Then who can be saved?’ they exclaimed in the greatest astonishment.'),
(994035,34,41,10,27,'Jesus looked at them, and answered,'),
(994036,34,41,10,28,'‘But we,’ began Peter, ‘we left everything and have followed you.’'),
(994037,34,41,10,32,'They were on the road going up to Jerusalem, with Jesus walking in front of them. The disciples were filled with awe, while those who were following behind were overwhelmed with fear. Gathering the Twelve round him once more, Jesus began to tell them what was about to happen to him.'),
(994038,34,41,10,35,'James and John, the two sons of Zebedee, went to Jesus, and said, ‘Teacher, we want you to do for us whatever we ask.’'),
(994039,34,41,10,37,'‘Grant us this,’ they answered, ‘to sit, one on your right, and the other on your left, when you come in glory.’'),
(994040,34,41,10,39,'‘Yes,’ they answered, ‘we can.’'),
(994041,34,41,10,41,'On hearing of this, the ten others were at first very indignant about James and John.'),
(994042,34,41,10,42,'But Jesus called the ten to him, and said,'),
(994043,34,41,10,46,'They came to Jericho. When Jesus was going out of the town with his disciples and a large crowd, Bartimaeus, the son of Timaeus, a blind beggar, was sitting by the roadside.'),
(994044,34,41,10,47,'Hearing that it was Jesus the Nazarene, he began to call out, ‘Jesus, Son of David, take pity on me.’'),
(994045,34,41,10,48,'Many of the people kept telling him to be quiet; but the man continued to call out all the louder, ‘Son of David, take pity on me.’'),
(994046,34,41,10,49,'Then Jesus stopped.'),
(994047,34,41,10,50,'The man threw off his cloak, sprang up, and came to Jesus.'),
(994048,34,41,11,1,'When they had almost reached Jerusalem, as far as Bethphage and Bethany, near the Mount of Olives, Jesus sent on two of his disciples.'),
(994049,34,41,11,4,'The two disciples went, and, finding a foal tethered outside a door in the street, they untied it.'),
(994050,34,41,11,5,'Some of the bystanders said to them, ‘What are you doing, untying the foal?’'),
(994051,34,41,11,6,'And the two disciples answered as Jesus had told them; and they allowed them to go.'),
(994052,34,41,11,7,'Then they brought the foal to Jesus, and, when they had laid their cloaks on it, he seated himself on it.'),
(994053,34,41,11,8,'Many of the people spread their cloaks on the road, while some strewed boughs which they had cut from the fields;'),
(994054,34,41,11,9,'and those who led the way, as well as those who followed, kept shouting, ‘God save him! Blessed is He who comes in the name of the Lord!'),
(994055,34,41,11,10,'Blessed is the coming kingdom of our father David! God save him from on high!’'),
(994056,34,41,11,11,'Jesus entered Jerusalem, and went into the Temple Courts; and, after looking round at everything, as it was already late, he went out to Bethany with the Twelve.'),
(994057,34,41,11,12,'The next day, after they had left Bethany, Jesus became hungry;'),
(994058,34,41,11,13,'and, noticing a fig-tree at a distance in leaf, he went to it to see if by any chance he could find something on it; but, on coming up to it, he found nothing but leaves, for it was not the season for figs.'),
(994059,34,41,11,14,'So, addressing the tree, he exclaimed,'),
(994060,34,41,11,15,'They came to Jerusalem. Jesus went into the Temple Courts, and began to drive out those who were buying and selling there. He overturned the tables of the money changers, and the seats of the pigeon-dealers,'),
(994061,34,41,11,16,'and would not allow anyone to carry anything across the Temple Courts.'),
(994062,34,41,11,17,'Then he began to teach.'),
(994063,34,41,11,18,'Now the chief priests and the teachers of the Law heard this and began to look for some way of putting Jesus to death; for they were afraid of him, since all the people were greatly impressed by his teaching.'),
(994064,34,41,11,19,'As soon as evening fell, Jesus and his disciples went out of the city.'),
(994065,34,41,11,20,'As they passed by early in the morning, they noticed that the fig-tree was withered up from the roots.'),
(994066,34,41,11,21,'Then Peter recalled what had occurred. ‘Look, Rabbi,’ he exclaimed, ‘the fig-tree which you doomed is withered up!’'),
(994067,34,41,11,27,'They came to Jerusalem again. While Jesus was walking about in the Temple Courts, the chief priests, the teachers of the Law, and the elders came up to him.'),
(994068,34,41,11,28,'‘What authority have you to do these things?’ they said. ‘Who gave you the authority to do them?’'),
(994069,34,41,11,31,'They began arguing together. ‘If we say “divine,” he will say “Why then didn’t you believe him?”'),
(994070,34,41,11,32,'Yet can we say “human”?’ They were afraid of the people, for everyone regarded John as undoubtedly a prophet.'),
(994071,34,41,11,33,'So their answer to Jesus was – ‘We do not know.’'),
(994072,34,41,12,1,'Jesus began to speak to them in parables,'),
(994073,34,41,12,12,'After this his enemies were eager to arrest him, but they were afraid of the crowd; for they saw that it was at them that he had aimed the parable. So they left him alone, and went away.'),
(994074,34,41,12,13,'Afterwards they sent to Jesus some of the Pharisees and Herodians, to set a trap for him in the course of conversation.'),
(994075,34,41,12,14,'These men came to him and said, ‘Teacher, we know that you are an honest man, and are not afraid of anyone, for you pay no regard to a person’s position, but teach the way of God honestly; are we right in paying taxes to the Emperor, or not?'),
(994076,34,41,12,15,'Should we pay, or should we not pay?’ Knowing their hypocrisy, Jesus said to them,'),
(994077,34,41,12,16,'And, when they had brought it, he asked,'),
(994078,34,41,12,17,'and Jesus replied,'),
(994079,34,41,12,18,'Next came some Sadducees – the men who maintain that there is no resurrection. Their question was this –'),
(994080,34,41,12,19,'‘Teacher, in our scriptures Moses decreed that, should a man’s brother die, leaving a widow but no child, the man should take the widow as his wife, and raise up a family for his brother.'),
(994081,34,41,12,20,'There were once seven brothers. The eldest married, but died and left no family;'),
(994082,34,41,12,21,'and the second married his widow, and died without family; and so did the third.'),
(994083,34,41,12,22,'All the seven died and left no family. The woman herself died last of all.'),
(994084,34,41,12,23,'At the resurrection whose wife will she be, all seven brothers having had her as their wife?’'),
(994085,34,41,12,28,'Then came up one of the teachers of the Law who had heard their discussions. Knowing that Jesus had answered them wisely, he asked him this question, ‘Which commandment is the most important of all?’'),
(994086,34,41,12,32,'‘Wisely answered, teacher!’ exclaimed the teacher of the Law. ‘It is true, as you say, that there is one God, and that there is no other besides him;'),
(994087,34,41,12,33,'and to love him with all one’s heart, and with all one’s understanding, and with all one’s strength, and to love one’s neighbour as one loves oneself is far beyond all burnt offerings and sacrifices.’'),
(994088,34,41,12,34,'Seeing that he had answered with discernment, Jesus said to him,'),
(994089,34,41,12,35,'While Jesus was teaching in the Temple Courts, he asked,'),
(994090,34,41,12,38,'In the course of his teaching, Jesus said,'),
(994091,34,41,12,41,'Then Jesus sat down opposite the chests for the Temple offerings, and watched how the people put money into them. Many rich people were putting in large sums;'),
(994092,34,41,12,42,'but one poor widow came and put in two small coins, worth very little.'),
(994093,34,41,12,43,'Then, calling his disciples to him, Jesus said,'),
(994094,34,41,13,1,'As Jesus was walking out of the Temple Courts, one of his disciples said to him, ‘Teacher, look what fine stones and buildings these are!’'),
(994095,34,41,13,3,'When Jesus had sat down on the Mount of Olives, facing the Temple, Peter, James, John and Andrew questioned him privately,'),
(994096,34,41,13,4,'‘Tell us when this will be, and what will be the sign when all this is drawing to its close.’'),
(994097,34,41,13,5,'Then Jesus began,'),
(994098,34,41,14,1,'It was now two days before the Festival of the Passover and the unleavened bread. The chief priests and the teachers of the Law were looking for an opportunity to arrest Jesus by stealth, and to put him to death;'),
(994099,34,41,14,2,'for they said, ‘Not during the Festival, or the people may riot.’'),
(994100,34,41,14,3,'When Jesus was still at Bethany, in the house of Simon the leper, while he was sitting at the table, a woman came with an alabaster jar of choice spikenard perfume of great value. She broke the jar, and poured the perfume on his head.'),
(994101,34,41,14,4,'Some of those who were present said to one another indignantly, ‘Why has the perfume been wasted like this?'),
(994102,34,41,14,5,'This perfume could have been sold for more than a year’s wages, and the money given to the poor.’'),
(994103,34,41,14,10,'After this, Judas Iscariot, one of the Twelve, went to the chief priests, to betray Jesus to them.'),
(994104,34,41,14,11,'They were glad to hear what he said, and promised to pay him. So he began looking for a good opportunity to betray Jesus.'),
(994105,34,41,14,12,'On the first day of the Festival of the unleavened bread, when it was customary to kill the Passover lambs, his disciples said to Jesus, ‘Where do you wish us to go and make preparations for your eating the Passover?’'),
(994106,34,41,14,13,'Jesus sent forward two of his disciples and said to them,'),
(994107,34,41,14,16,'So the disciples set out and went into the city, and found everything just as Jesus had told them; and they prepared the Passover.'),
(994108,34,41,14,17,'In the evening he went there with the Twelve,'),
(994109,34,41,14,18,'and when they had taken their places and were eating, Jesus said,'),
(994110,34,41,14,19,'They were grieved at this, and began to say to him, one after another, ‘Can it be I?’'),
(994111,34,41,14,22,'While they were eating, Jesus took some bread, and, after saying the blessing, broke it, and gave it to them, and said,'),
(994112,34,41,14,23,'Then he took a cup, and, after saying the thanksgiving, gave it to them, and they all drank from it.'),
(994113,34,41,14,26,'They then sang a hymn, and went out up the Mount of Olives,'),
(994114,34,41,14,27,'presently Jesus said to them,'),
(994115,34,41,14,29,'‘Even if everyone else falls away,’ said Peter, ‘I will not.’'),
(994116,34,41,14,31,'But Peter vehemently protested, ‘Even if I must die with you, I will never disown you!’ And they all said the same.'),
(994117,34,41,14,32,'Presently they came to a garden known as Gethsemane, and Jesus said to his disciples'),
(994118,34,41,14,33,'He took with him Peter, James, and John; and began to show signs of great dismay and deep distress of mind.'),
(994119,34,41,14,35,'Going on a little further, he threw himself on the ground, and began to pray that, if it were possible, he might be spared that hour.'),
(994120,34,41,14,37,'Then he came and found the three apostles asleep.'),
(994121,34,41,14,39,'Again he went away, and prayed in the same words;'),
(994122,34,41,14,40,'and coming back again he found them asleep, for their eyes were heavy; and they did not know what to say to him.'),
(994123,34,41,14,41,'A third time he came, and said to them,'),
(994124,34,41,14,43,'And just then, while he was still speaking, Judas, who was one of the Twelve, came up; and with him a crowd of people, with swords and clubs, sent by the chief priests, the teachers of the Law, and the elders.'),
(994125,34,41,14,44,'Now the betrayer had arranged a signal with them. ‘The man whom I kiss,’ he had said, ‘will be the one; arrest him and take him away safely.’'),
(994126,34,41,14,45,'As soon as Judas came, he went up to Jesus at once, and said, ‘Rabbi!’ and kissed him.'),
(994127,34,41,14,46,'Then the men seized Jesus, and arrested him.'),
(994128,34,41,14,47,'One of those who were standing by drew his sword, and struck at the high priest’s servant, and cut off his ear.'),
(994129,34,41,14,48,'But Jesus spoke up, and said to the men,'),
(994130,34,41,14,50,'And all the apostles deserted him and fled.'),
(994131,34,41,14,51,'One young man did indeed follow him, wrapped only in a linen sheet. They tried to arrest him;'),
(994132,34,41,14,52,'but he left the sheet in their hands, and fled naked.'),
(994133,34,41,14,53,'Then they took Jesus to the high priest; and all the chief priests, elders, and the teachers of the Law assembled.'),
(994134,34,41,14,54,'Peter, who had followed Jesus at a distance into the courtyard of the high priest, was sitting there among the police officers, warming himself at the blaze of the fire.'),
(994135,34,41,14,55,'Meanwhile the chief priest and the whole of the High Council were trying to get such evidence against Jesus as would warrant his being put to death, but they could not find any;'),
(994136,34,41,14,56,'for, though there were many who gave false evidence against him, yet their evidence did not agree.'),
(994137,34,41,14,57,'Presently some men stood up, and gave this false evidence against him –'),
(994138,34,41,14,58,'‘We ourselves heard him say “I will destroy this Temple made with hands, and in three days build another made without hands.”’'),
(994139,34,41,14,59,'Yet not even on that point did their evidence agree.'),
(994140,34,41,14,60,'Then the high priest stood forward, and questioned Jesus. ‘Have you no answer to make?’ he asked. ‘What is this evidence which these men are giving against you?’'),
(994141,34,41,14,61,'But Jesus remained silent, and made no answer.'),
(994142,34,41,14,63,'At this the high priest tore his vestments. ‘Why do we want any more witnesses?’ he exclaimed.'),
(994143,34,41,14,64,'‘You heard his blasphemy? What is your verdict?’ They all condemned him, declaring that he deserved death.'),
(994144,34,41,14,65,'Some of those present began to spit at him, and to blindfold his eyes, and strike him, saying, as they did so, ‘Now play the prophet!’ and even the police officers received him with blows.'),
(994145,34,41,14,66,'While Peter was in the courtyard down below, one of the high priest’s maidservants came up;'),
(994146,34,41,14,67,'and, seeing Peter warming himself, she looked closely at him, and exclaimed, ‘Why, you were with Jesus, the Nazarene!’'),
(994147,34,41,14,68,'But Peter denied it. ‘I do not know or understand what you mean,’ he replied. Then he went out into the porch;'),
(994148,34,41,14,69,'and there the maidservant, on seeing him, began to say again to the bystanders, ‘This is one of them!’'),
(994149,34,41,14,70,'But Peter again denied it.'),
(994150,34,41,14,71,'But he said to them, ‘I swear that I do not know the man you are talking about! May God punish me if I am lying!’'),
(994151,34,41,14,72,'At that moment, for the second time, a cock crowed; and Peter remembered the words that Jesus had said to him –'),
(994152,34,41,15,1,'As soon as it was daylight, the chief priests, after holding a consultation with elders and teachers of the Law – that is to say, the whole High Council – put Jesus in chains, and took him away, and gave him up to Pilate.'),
(994153,34,41,15,2,'‘Are you the king of the Jews?’ asked Pilate.'),
(994154,34,41,15,3,'Then the chief priests brought a number of charges against him.'),
(994155,34,41,15,4,'So Pilate questioned Jesus again. ‘Have you no reply to make?’ he asked. ‘Listen, how many charges they are bringing against you.’'),
(994156,34,41,15,5,'But Jesus still made no reply whatever; at which Pilate was astonished.'),
(994157,34,41,15,6,'Now, at the feast, Pilate used to grant the people the release of any one prisoner whom they might ask for.'),
(994158,34,41,15,7,'A man called Barabbas was in prison, with the rioters who had committed murder during a riot.'),
(994159,34,41,15,8,'So, when the crowd went up and began to ask Pilate to follow his usual custom,'),
(994160,34,41,15,9,'he answered, ‘Do you want me to release the “king of the Jews” for you?’'),
(994161,34,41,15,10,'For he was aware that it was out of jealousy that the chief priests had given Jesus up to him.'),
(994162,34,41,15,11,'But the chief priests incited the crowd to get Barabbas released instead.'),
(994163,34,41,15,12,'Pilate, however, spoke to them again, ‘What should I do then with the man whom you call the “king of the Jews”?’'),
(994164,34,41,15,13,'Again they shouted, ‘Crucify him!’'),
(994165,34,41,15,14,'‘Why, what harm has he done?’ Pilate kept saying to them. But they shouted furiously, ‘Crucify him!’'),
(994166,34,41,15,15,'And Pilate, wishing to satisfy the crowd, released Barabbas to them, and, after scourging Jesus, gave him up to be crucified.'),
(994167,34,41,15,16,'The soldiers then took Jesus away into the courtyard – that is the Government house – and they called the whole garrison together.'),
(994168,34,41,15,17,'They dressed him in a purple robe, and, having twisted a crown of thorns, put it on him,'),
(994169,34,41,15,18,'and then began to salute him. ‘Long life to you, king of the Jews!’ they said.'),
(994170,34,41,15,19,'And they kept striking him on the head with a rod, spitting at him, and bowing to the ground before him – going down on their knees;'),
(994171,34,41,15,20,'and, when they had left off mocking him, they took off the purple robe, and put his own clothes on him.'),
(994172,34,41,15,21,'They led Jesus out to crucify him; and they compelled a passer-by, Simon from Cyrene, who was on his way in from the country, the father of Alexander and Rufus, to go with them to carry his cross.'),
(994173,34,41,15,22,'They brought Jesus to the place which was known as Golgotha – a name which means “place of a Skull.”'),
(994174,34,41,15,23,'There they offered him drugged wine; but Jesus refused it.'),
(994175,34,41,15,24,'Then they crucified him, and divided his clothes among them, casting lots for them, to settle what each should take.'),
(994176,34,41,15,25,'It was nine in the morning when they crucified him.'),
(994177,34,41,15,26,'The words of the charge against him, written up over his head, read – “THE KING OF THE JEWS.”'),
(994178,34,41,15,27,'And with him they crucified two robbers, one on the right, and the other on the left.'),
(994179,34,41,15,29,'The passers-by railed at him, shaking their heads, as they said, ‘Ah! You who would destroy the Temple and build one in three days,'),
(994180,34,41,15,30,'come down from the cross and save yourself!’'),
(994181,34,41,15,31,'In the same way the chief priests, with the teachers of the Law, said to one another in mockery,'),
(994182,34,41,15,32,'‘He saved others, but he cannot save himself! Let the Christ, the “king of Israel,” come down from the cross now so that we can see it and believe.’ Even the men who had been crucified with Jesus insulted him.'),
(994183,34,41,15,33,'At midday, a darkness came over the whole country, lasting until three in the afternoon.'),
(994184,34,41,15,34,'And, at three, Jesus called out loudly,'),
(994185,34,41,15,35,'Some of those standing round heard this, and said, ‘Listen! He is calling for Elijah!’'),
(994186,34,41,15,36,'And a man ran, and, soaking a sponge in common wine, put it on the end of a rod, and offered it to him to drink, saying as he did so, ‘Wait and let us see if Elijah is coming to take him down.’'),
(994187,34,41,15,37,'But Jesus, giving a loud cry, breathed his last.'),
(994188,34,41,15,38,'The Temple curtain was torn in two from top to bottom.'),
(994189,34,41,15,39,'The Roman officer, who was standing facing Jesus, on seeing the way in which he breathed his last, exclaimed, ‘This man must indeed have been God’s son!’'),
(994190,34,41,15,40,'There were some women also watching from a distance, among them being Mary of Magdala, Mary the mother of James the Little and of Joseph, and Salome –'),
(994191,34,41,15,41,'all of whom used to accompany Jesus when he was in Galilee, and give him support – besides many other women who had come up with him to Jerusalem.'),
(994192,34,41,15,42,'The evening had already fallen, when, as it was the Preparation day – the day before the Sabbath –'),
(994193,34,41,15,43,'Joseph from Ramah, a councillor of good position, who was himself living in expectation of the kingdom of God, came and ventured to go in to see Pilate, and to ask for the body of Jesus.'),
(994194,34,41,15,44,'But Pilate was surprised to hear that he had already died. So he sent for the officer, and asked if he were already dead;'),
(994195,34,41,15,45,'and, on learning from the officer that it was so, he gave the corpse to Joseph.'),
(994196,34,41,15,46,'Joseph, having bought a linen sheet, took Jesus down, and wound the sheet round him, and laid him in a tomb which had been cut out of the rock; and then rolled a stone up against the entrance of the tomb.'),
(994197,34,41,15,47,'Mary of Magdala and Mary, the mother of Joseph, were watching to see where he was laid.'),
(994198,34,41,16,1,'When the Sabbath was over, Mary of Magdala, Mary the mother of James, and Salome bought some spices, so that they might go and anoint the body of Jesus.'),
(994199,34,41,16,2,'Very early on the first day of the week they went to the tomb, after sunrise.'),
(994200,34,41,16,3,'They were saying to one another, ‘Who will roll away the stone for us from the entrance of the tomb?’'),
(994201,34,41,16,4,'But, on looking up, they saw that the stone had already been rolled back; it was a very large one.'),
(994202,34,41,16,5,'Going into the tomb, they saw a young man sitting on their right, in a white robe, and they were dismayed; but he said to them,'),
(994203,34,41,16,6,'‘Do not be dismayed; you are looking for Jesus, the Nazarene, who has been crucified; he has risen, he is not here! Look! Here is the place where they laid him.'),
(994204,34,41,16,7,'But go, and say to his disciples and to Peter “He is going before you into Galilee; there you will see him, as he told you.”’'),
(994205,34,41,16,8,'They went out, and fled from the tomb, for they were trembling and bewildered; and they did not say a word to anyone, for they were frightened.'),
(994206,34,41,16,9,'After his rising again, early on the first day of the week, Jesus appeared first of all to Mary of Magdala, from whom he had driven out seven demons.'),
(994207,34,41,16,10,'She went and told the news to those who had been with him and who were now in sorrow and tears;'),
(994208,34,41,16,11,'yet even they, when they heard that he was alive and had been seen by her, did not believe it.'),
(994209,34,41,16,12,'Afterwards, altered in appearance, he made himself known to two of them, as they were walking, on their way into the country.'),
(994210,34,41,16,13,'They also went and told the rest, but they did not believe even them.'),
(994211,34,41,16,14,'Later on, he made himself known to the Eleven themselves as they were at a meal, and reproached them with their want of faith and their stubbornness, because they did not believe those who had seen him after he had risen from the dead.'),
(994212,34,41,16,15,'Then he said to them,'),
(994213,34,41,16,19,'So the Lord Jesus, after he had spoken to them, was taken up into heaven, and sat at the right hand of God.'),
(994214,34,41,16,20,'But they set out, and made the proclamation everywhere, the Lord working with them, and confirming the message by the signs which attended it.'),
(994215,34,42,1,1,'To his Excellency, Theophilus.'),
(994216,34,42,1,2,'just as they were reported to us by those who from the beginning were eye-witnesses, and afterwards became bearers of the message.'),
(994217,34,42,1,3,'And, therefore, I also, since I have investigated all these events with great care from their very beginning, have resolved to write a connected history of them for you,'),
(994218,34,42,1,4,'in order that you may be able to satisfy yourself of the accuracy of the story which you have heard from the lips of others.'),
(994219,34,42,1,5,'In the reign of Herod, king of Judea, there was a priest named Zechariah, who belonged to the division called after Abijah. His wife, whose name was Elizabeth, was also a descendant of Aaron.'),
(994220,34,42,1,6,'They were both righteous people, who lived blameless lives, guiding their steps by all the commandments and ordinances of the Lord.'),
(994221,34,42,1,7,'But they had no child, Elizabeth being barren; and both of them were advanced in years.'),
(994222,34,42,1,8,'One day, when Zechariah was officiating as priest before God, during the turn of his division,'),
(994223,34,42,1,9,'it fell to him by lot, in accordance with the practice among the priests, to go into the Temple of the Lord and burn incense;'),
(994224,34,42,1,10,'and, as it was the Hour of Incense, the people were all praying outside.'),
(994225,34,42,1,11,'And an angel of the Lord appeared to him, standing on the right of the Altar of Incense.'),
(994226,34,42,1,12,'Zechariah was startled at the sight and was awe-struck.'),
(994227,34,42,1,13,'But the angel said to him, ‘Do not be afraid, Zechariah; your prayer has been heard, and your wife Elizabeth will bear you a son, whom you will call by the name John.'),
(994228,34,42,1,14,'He will be to you a joy and a delight; and many will rejoice over his birth.'),
(994229,34,42,1,15,'For he will be great in the sight of the Lord; he will not drink any wine or strong drink, and he will be filled with the Holy Spirit from the very hour of his birth,'),
(994230,34,42,1,16,'and will reconcile many of the Israelites to the Lord their God.'),
(994231,34,42,1,17,'He will go before him in the spirit and with the power of Elijah, to reconcile fathers to their children and the disobedient to the wisdom of the righteous, and so make ready for the Lord a people prepared for him.’'),
(994232,34,42,1,18,'‘How can I be sure of this?’ Zechariah asked the angel. ‘For I am an old man and my wife is advanced in years.’'),
(994233,34,42,1,19,'‘I am Gabriel,’ the angel answered, ‘who stand in the presence of God, and I have been sent to speak to you and to bring you this good news.'),
(994234,34,42,1,20,'And now you will be silent and unable to speak until the day when this takes place, because you did not believe what I said, though my words will be fulfilled in due course.’'),
(994235,34,42,1,21,'Meanwhile the people were watching for Zechariah, wondering at his remaining so long in the Temple.'),
(994236,34,42,1,22,'When he came out, he was unable to speak to them, and they perceived that he had seen a vision there. But Zechariah kept making signs to them, and remained dumb.'),
(994237,34,42,1,23,'And, as soon as his term of service was finished, he returned home.'),
(994238,34,42,1,24,'After this his wife, Elizabeth, became pregnant and lived in seclusion for five months.'),
(994239,34,42,1,25,'‘The Lord has done this for me,’ she said, ‘he has shown me kindness and taken away the public disgrace of childlessness under which I have been living.’'),
(994240,34,42,1,26,'Six months later the angel Gabriel was sent from God to a town in Galilee called Nazareth,'),
(994241,34,42,1,27,'to a maiden there who was engaged to a man named Joseph, a descendant of David. Her name was Mary.'),
(994242,34,42,1,28,'Gabriel came into her presence and greeted her, saying, ‘You have been shown great favour – the Lord is with you.’'),
(994243,34,42,1,29,'Mary was much disturbed at his words, and was wondering to herself what such a greeting could mean,'),
(994244,34,42,1,30,'when the angel spoke again, ‘Do not be afraid, Mary, for you have found favour with God.'),
(994245,34,42,1,31,'And now, you will conceive and give birth to a son, and you will give him the name Jesus.'),
(994246,34,42,1,32,'The child will be great and will be called “Son of the Most High,” and the Lord God will give him the throne of his ancestor David,'),
(994247,34,42,1,33,'and he will reign over the descendants of Jacob for ever; And to his kingdom there will be no end.’'),
(994248,34,42,1,34,'‘How can this be?’ Mary asked the angel. ‘For I have no husband.’'),
(994249,34,42,1,35,'‘The Holy Spirit will descend on you,’ answered the angel, ‘and the Power of the Most High will overshadow you; and therefore the child will be called “holy,” and “Son of God.”'),
(994250,34,42,1,36,'And Elizabeth, your cousin, is herself also expecting a son in her old age; and it is now the sixth month with her, though she is called barren;'),
(994251,34,42,1,37,'for no promise from God will fail to be fulfilled.’'),
(994252,34,42,1,38,'‘I am the servant of the Lord,’ exclaimed Mary. ‘Let it be with me as you have said.’ Then the angel left her.'),
(994253,34,42,1,39,'Soon after this Mary set out, and made her way quickly into the hill-country, to a town in Judah;'),
(994254,34,42,1,40,'and there she went into Zechariah’s house and greeted Elizabeth.'),
(994255,34,42,1,41,'When Elizabeth heard Mary’s greeting, the child moved within her, and Elizabeth herself was filled with the Holy Spirit,'),
(994256,34,42,1,42,'and cried aloud, ‘Blessed are you among women, and blessed is your unborn child!'),
(994257,34,42,1,43,'But how have I this honour, that the mother of my Lord should come to me?'),
(994258,34,42,1,44,'For, as soon as your greeting reached my ears, the child moved within me with delight!'),
(994259,34,42,1,45,'Happy indeed is she who believed that the promise which she received from the Lord would be fulfilled.’'),
(994260,34,42,1,46,'And Mary said:'),
(994261,34,42,1,47,'and my spirit delights in God my Saviour,'),
(994262,34,42,1,48,'for he has looked with favour on his humble servant girl.'),
(994263,34,42,1,49,'‘For the Almighty has done great things for me,'),
(994264,34,42,1,50,'He has mercy on those who revere him'),
(994265,34,42,1,51,'‘Mighty are the deeds of his arm!'),
(994266,34,42,1,52,'he has cast down the mighty from their thrones,'),
(994267,34,42,1,53,'he has filled the hungry with good things,'),
(994268,34,42,1,54,'‘He has stretched out his hand to his servant Israel,'),
(994269,34,42,1,55,'as he promised to our ancestors'),
(994270,34,42,1,56,'Mary stayed with Elizabeth about three months, and then returned to her home.'),
(994271,34,42,1,57,'When Elizabeth’s time came, she gave birth to a son;'),
(994272,34,42,1,58,'and her neighbours and relatives, hearing of the great goodness of the Lord to her, came to share her joy.'),
(994273,34,42,1,59,'A week later they met to circumcise the child, and were about to call him Zechariah after his father,'),
(994274,34,42,1,60,'when his mother spoke up, ‘No, he is to be called John.’'),
(994275,34,42,1,61,'‘You have no relation of that name!’ they exclaimed;'),
(994276,34,42,1,62,'and they made signs to the child’s father, to find out what he wished the child to be called.'),
(994277,34,42,1,63,'Asking for a writing-tablet, he wrote the words – “His name is John.” Everyone was surprised'),
(994278,34,42,1,64,'and immediately Zechariah recovered his voice and the use of his tongue, and began to bless God.'),
(994279,34,42,1,65,'All their neighbours were awe-struck at this, and throughout the hill-country of Judea the whole story was much talked about.'),
(994280,34,42,1,66,'All who heard it kept it in mind, asking one another – ‘What can this child be destined to become?’ For the Power of the Lord was with him.'),
(994281,34,42,1,67,'Then his father Zechariah was filled with the Holy Spirit, and, speaking under inspiration, said:'),
(994282,34,42,1,68,'‘Blessed is the Lord, the God of Israel,'),
(994283,34,42,1,69,'and has raised up for us the strength of our salvation'),
(994284,34,42,1,70,'as he promised by the lips of his holy prophets of old –'),
(994285,34,42,1,71,'salvation from our enemies and from the hands of all who hate us,'),
(994286,34,42,1,72,'showing mercy to our ancestors,'),
(994287,34,42,1,73,'This was the oath which he swore to our ancestor Abraham –'),
(994288,34,42,1,74,'that we should be rescued from the hands of our enemies,'),
(994289,34,42,1,75,'and should serve him without fear in holiness and righteousness,'),
(994290,34,42,1,76,'And you, child, will be called prophet of the Most High,'),
(994291,34,42,1,77,'to give his people the knowledge of salvation'),
(994292,34,42,1,78,'through the tender mercy of our God,'),
(994293,34,42,1,79,'to give light to those who live in darkness and the shadow of death,'),
(994294,34,42,1,80,'The child grew and became strong in spirit, and he lived in the wilds until the time came for his appearance before Israel.'),
(994295,34,42,2,1,'About that time an edict was issued by the Emperor Augustus that a census should be taken of the whole Empire.'),
(994296,34,42,2,2,'(This was the first census taken while Quirinius was Governor of Syria).'),
(994297,34,42,2,3,'And everyone went to his own town to be registered.'),
(994298,34,42,2,4,'Among others Joseph went up from the town of Nazareth in Galilee to Bethlehem, the town of David, in Judea – because he belonged to the family and house of David –'),
(994299,34,42,2,5,'To be registered with Mary, his engaged wife, who was about to become a mother.'),
(994300,34,42,2,6,'While they were there her time came,'),
(994301,34,42,2,7,'and she gave birth to her first child, a son. And because there was no room for them in the inn, she swathed him round and laid him in a manger.'),
(994302,34,42,2,8,'In that same country-side were shepherds out in the open fields, watching their flocks that night,'),
(994303,34,42,2,9,'when an angel of the Lord suddenly stood by them, and the glory of the Lord shone around them; and they were seized with fear.'),
(994304,34,42,2,10,'‘Have no fear,’ the angel said. ‘For I bring you good news of a great joy in store for all the nation.'),
(994305,34,42,2,11,'This day there has been born to you, in the town of David, a Saviour, who is Christ and Lord.'),
(994306,34,42,2,12,'And this will be the sign for you. You will find the infant swathed, and lying in a manger.’'),
(994307,34,42,2,13,'Then suddenly there appeared with the angel a multitude of the heavenly Host, praising God, and singing –'),
(994308,34,42,2,14,'‘glory to God on high,'),
(994309,34,42,2,15,'Now, when the angels had left them and gone back to heaven, the shepherds said to one another, ‘Let us go at once to Bethlehem, and see this thing that has happened, of which the Lord has told us.’'),
(994310,34,42,2,16,'So they went quickly, and found Mary and Joseph, and the infant lying in a manger;'),
(994311,34,42,2,17,'and, when they saw it, they told of all that had been said to them about this child.'),
(994312,34,42,2,18,'All who heard the shepherds were astonished at their story,'),
(994313,34,42,2,19,'while Mary treasured up all that they said, and thought about it often in her thoughts.'),
(994314,34,42,2,20,'And the shepherds went back, giving glory and praise to God for all that they had heard and seen. It had all happened as they had been told.'),
(994315,34,42,2,21,'Eight days after the birth of the child, when it was time to circumcise him, he received the name Jesus – the name given him by the angel before his conception.'),
(994316,34,42,2,22,'When the period of purification of mother and child, required by the Law of Moses, came to an end, his parents took the child up to Jerusalem to present him to the Lord,'),
(994317,34,42,2,23,'in compliance with the Law of the Lord that every first-born male will be dedicated to the Lord,'),
(994318,34,42,2,24,'and also to offer the sacrifice required by the Law of the Lord – a pair of turtle-doves or two young pigeons.'),
(994319,34,42,2,25,'There was at that time in Jerusalem a man named Simeon, a righteous and devout man, who lived in constant expectation of the Consolation of Israel, and under the guidance of the Holy Spirit.'),
(994320,34,42,2,26,'It had been revealed to him by the Holy Spirit that he should not die until he had seen the Lord’s Christ.'),
(994321,34,42,2,27,'Moved by the Spirit, Simeon came into the Temple Courts, and, when the parents brought in the child Jesus, to do for him what was customary under the Law,'),
(994322,34,42,2,28,'Simeon himself took the child in his arms, and blessed God, and said:'),
(994323,34,42,2,29,'‘Now, Lord, you will let your servant go,'),
(994324,34,42,2,30,'for my eyes have seen the salvation'),
(994325,34,42,2,31,'which you have prepared in the sight of all nations –'),
(994326,34,42,2,32,'a light to bring light to the Gentiles,'),
(994327,34,42,2,33,'While the child’s father and mother were wondering at what was said about him,'),
(994328,34,42,2,34,'Simeon gave them his blessing, and said to Mary, the child’s mother, ‘This child is appointed to be the cause of the fall and rise of many in Israel, and to be a sign much spoken against –'),
(994329,34,42,2,35,'Yes, the sword will pierce your own heart – and so the thoughts in many minds will be disclosed.’'),
(994330,34,42,2,36,'There was also a prophet named Hannah, a daughter of Phanuel and of the tribe of Asher. She was far advanced in years, having lived with her husband for seven years after marriage,'),
(994331,34,42,2,37,'and then a widow, until she had reached the age of eighty-four. She never left the Temple Courts, but, fasting and praying, worshiped God night and day.'),
(994332,34,42,2,38,'At that moment she came up, and began publicly to thank God and to speak about the child to all who were looking for the deliverance of Jerusalem.'),
(994333,34,42,2,39,'When the child’s parents had done everything required by the Law of the Lord, they returned to Galilee to their own town of Nazareth.'),
(994334,34,42,2,40,'The child grew and became strong and wise, and the blessing of God was on him.'),
(994335,34,42,2,41,'Every year the child’s parents used to go to Jerusalem at the Passover Festival.'),
(994336,34,42,2,42,'When Jesus was twelve years old, they went according to custom to Jerusalem,'),
(994337,34,42,2,43,'and had finished their visit; but, when they started to return, the boy Jesus remained behind in Jerusalem, without their knowing it.'),
(994338,34,42,2,44,'Thinking that he was with their fellow travellers, they went one day’s journey before searching for him among their relatives and acquaintances;'),
(994339,34,42,2,45,'and then, as they did not find him, they returned to Jerusalem, searching everywhere for him.'),
(994340,34,42,2,46,'It was not until the third day that they found him in the Temple Courts, sitting among the teachers, now listening to them, now asking them questions.'),
(994341,34,42,2,47,'All who listened to him marvelled at his intelligence and his answers.'),
(994342,34,42,2,48,'His parents were amazed when they saw him, and his mother said to him, ‘My child, why have you treated us like this? Your father and I have been searching for you in great distress.’'),
(994343,34,42,2,50,'His parents did not understand what he meant.'),
(994344,34,42,2,51,'However he went down with them to Nazareth, and submitted himself to their control; and his mother treasured all that was said in her heart.'),
(994345,34,42,2,52,'And Jesus grew in wisdom as he grew in years, and gained the blessing of God and people.'),
(994346,34,42,3,1,'In the fifteenth year of the reign of the Emperor Tiberius, when Pontius Pilate was Governor of Judea, Herod Ruler of Galilee, his brother Philip Ruler of the territory comprising Ituraea and Trachonitis, and Lysanias Ruler of Abilene,'),
(994347,34,42,3,2,'and when Annas and Caiaphas were high priests, a command from God came to John, the son of Zechariah, while he was in the wilderness.'),
(994348,34,42,3,3,'And John went through the whole district of the Jordan, proclaiming baptism on repentance, for the forgiveness of sins.'),
(994349,34,42,3,4,'This was in fulfilment of what is said in the writings of the prophet Isaiah –'),
(994350,34,42,3,5,'Every chasm will be filled,'),
(994351,34,42,3,6,'and everyone will see the salvation of God.’”'),
(994352,34,42,3,7,'And John said to the crowds that went to be baptized by him, ‘You children of snakes! Who has prompted you to seek refuge from the coming judgment?'),
(994353,34,42,3,8,'Let your lives, then, prove your repentance; and do not begin to say among yourselves “Abraham is our ancestor,” for I tell you that out of these stones God is able to raise descendants for Abraham!'),
(994354,34,42,3,9,'Already, indeed, the axe is lying at the root of the trees. Therefore every tree that fails to bear good fruit will be cut down and thrown into the fire.’'),
(994355,34,42,3,10,'‘What are we to do then?’ the people asked.'),
(994356,34,42,3,11,'‘Let anyone who has two coats,’ answered John, ‘share with the person who has none; and anyone who has food do the same.’'),
(994357,34,42,3,12,'Even tax-gatherers came to be baptized, and said to John, ‘Teacher, what are we to do?’'),
(994358,34,42,3,13,'‘Do not collect more than you have authority to demand,’ John answered.'),
(994359,34,42,3,14,'And when some soldiers on active service asked ‘And we – what are we to do?’ he said, ‘Never use violence, or exact anything by false accusation; and be content with your pay.’'),
(994360,34,42,3,15,'Then, while the people were in suspense, and were all debating with themselves whether John could be the Christ,'),
(994361,34,42,3,16,'John, addressing them all, said, ‘I, indeed, baptize you with water; but there is coming one more powerful than I, and I am not fit even to unfasten his sandals. He will baptize you with the Holy Spirit and with fire.'),
(994362,34,42,3,17,'His winnowing-fan is in his hand so that he may clear his threshing-floor, and store the grain in his barn, but the chaff he will burn with a fire that cannot be put out.’'),
(994363,34,42,3,18,'And so with many different appeals John told his good news to the people.'),
(994364,34,42,3,19,'But Prince Herod, being rebuked by John respecting Herodias, the wife of Herod’s brother, and for all the evil things that he had done,'),
(994365,34,42,3,20,'crowned them all by shutting John up in prison.'),
(994366,34,42,3,21,'Now after the baptism of all the people, and when Jesus had been baptized and was still praying, the heavens opened,'),
(994367,34,42,3,22,'and the Holy Spirit came down on him in the form of a dove, and from the heavens came a voice – ‘You are my dearly loved son; you bring me great joy.’'),
(994368,34,42,3,23,'When beginning his work, Jesus was about thirty years old. He was regarded as the son of Joseph, whose ancestors were –'),
(994369,34,42,3,24,'Mattith, Levi, Melchiah, Janna, Joseph,'),
(994370,34,42,3,25,'Mattithiah, Amos, Nahum, Azaliah, Nogah,'),
(994371,34,42,3,26,'Mattith, Mattithiah, Shimei, Joseph, Josheh,'),
(994372,34,42,3,27,'Johanan, Rhesa, Zerubbabel, Salathiel, Neriah,'),
(994373,34,42,3,28,'Melchiah, Addi, Cosam, Elmodam, Er,'),
(994374,34,42,3,29,'Joshua, Eliezer, Joram, Mattith, Levi,'),
(994375,34,42,3,30,'Simeon, Judah, Joseph, Jonam, Eliakim,'),
(994376,34,42,3,31,'Meleah, Menan, Mattithiah, Nathan, David,'),
(994377,34,42,3,32,'Jesse, Obed, Boaz, Salah, Nahshon,'),
(994378,34,42,3,33,'Aminadab, Arni, Hezron, Perez, Judah,'),
(994379,34,42,3,34,'Jacob, Isaac, Abraham, Terah, Nahor,'),
(994380,34,42,3,35,'Serug, Reu, Peleg, Eber, Shelah,'),
(994381,34,42,3,36,'Kenan, Arpachshad, Shem, Noah, Lamech,'),
(994382,34,42,3,37,'Methuselah, Enoch, Jared, Mahalalel, Kenan,'),
(994383,34,42,3,38,'Enosh, Seth and Adam the son of God.'),
(994384,34,42,4,1,'On returning from the Jordan, full of the Holy Spirit, Jesus was led by the power of the Spirit through the wilderness for forty days, tempted by the devil.'),
(994385,34,42,4,2,'All that time he ate nothing; and, when it was over, he became hungry.'),
(994386,34,42,4,3,'So the devil said to him, ‘If you are God’s Son, tell this stone to become a loaf of bread.’'),
(994387,34,42,4,4,'And Jesus answered him,'),
(994388,34,42,4,5,'And the devil led Jesus up, and showing him in a single moment all the kingdoms of the earth, said to him,'),
(994389,34,42,4,6,'‘I will give you all this power, and the splendour of them; for it has been given into my hands and I give it to whom I wish.'),
(994390,34,42,4,7,'If you worship me, it will all be yours.’'),
(994391,34,42,4,8,'And Jesus answered him,'),
(994392,34,42,4,9,'The devil next led him into Jerusalem, and, placing him on the parapet of the Temple, said, ‘If you are God’s Son throw yourself down from here,'),
(994393,34,42,4,10,'for scripture says – “He will give his angels commands about you, to guard you safely,”'),
(994394,34,42,4,11,'And “On their hands they will lift you up, otherwise you might strike your foot against a stone.”’'),
(994395,34,42,4,12,'But Jesus answered him,'),
(994396,34,42,4,13,'When he had tried every kind of temptation, the devil left Jesus, until another opportunity.'),
(994397,34,42,4,14,'Moved by the power of the Spirit, Jesus returned to Galilee. Reports about him spread through all that region;'),
(994398,34,42,4,15,'and he began to teach in their synagogues, and was honoured by everyone.'),
(994399,34,42,4,16,'Coming to Nazareth, where he had been brought up, Jesus, as was his custom, went on the Sabbath into the synagogue, and stood up to read the scriptures.'),
(994400,34,42,4,17,'He was given the book of the prophet Isaiah; and Jesus opened the book and found the place where it says –'),
(994401,34,42,4,20,'Then, closing the book and returning it to the attendant, he sat down. The eyes of all in the synagogue were fixed on him,'),
(994402,34,42,4,21,'and Jesus began,'),
(994403,34,42,4,22,'All who were present spoke well of him, and were astonished at the beautiful words that fell from his lips. ‘Isn’t Joseph’s son?’ they asked.'),
(994404,34,42,4,28,'All the people in the synagogue, as they listened to this, became enraged.'),
(994405,34,42,4,29,'Starting up, they drove Jesus out of the town, and led him to the brow of the hill on which their town stood, intending to hurl him down.'),
(994406,34,42,4,30,'But he passed through the middle of the crowd and went on his way.'),
(994407,34,42,4,31,'Then Jesus went down to Capernaum, a city in Galilee. On the Sabbath he taught the people.'),
(994408,34,42,4,32,'They were amazed at his teaching, because his words were spoken with authority.'),
(994409,34,42,4,33,'In the synagogue there was a man with the spirit of a foul demon in him, who called out loudly,'),
(994410,34,42,4,34,'‘Stop! What do you want with us, Jesus of Nazareth? Have you come to destroy us? I know who you are – the Holy One of God!’'),
(994411,34,42,4,35,'But Jesus rebuked the demon.'),
(994412,34,42,4,36,'And they were all lost in amazement, and kept saying to one another, ‘What words are these? For he gives his commands to the foul spirits with a marvellous authority, and they come out.’'),
(994413,34,42,4,37,'And rumours about Jesus traveled through every place in the region.'),
(994414,34,42,4,38,'On leaving the synagogue, Jesus went into Simon’s house. Now Simon’s mother-in-law was suffering from a severe attack of fever, and they asked Jesus to cure her.'),
(994415,34,42,4,39,'Bending over her, he rebuked the fever; the fever left her, and she immediately got up and began to take care of them.'),
(994416,34,42,4,40,'At sunset, all who had friends suffering from various diseases took them to Jesus; and he placed his hands on everyone of them and cured them.'),
(994417,34,42,4,41,'And even demons came out from many people, screaming “You are the Son of God.” Jesus rebuked them, and would not allow them to speak, because they knew that he was the Christ.'),
(994418,34,42,4,42,'At daybreak, Jesus went out and walked to a lonely spot. But crowds of people began to look for him; and they came to where he was and tried to detain him and prevent his leaving them.'),
(994419,34,42,4,43,'Jesus, however, said to them,'),
(994420,34,42,4,44,'And he continued to make his proclamation in the synagogues of Judea.'),
(994421,34,42,5,1,'Once, when the people were pressing round Jesus as they listened to God’s message, he happened to be standing by the shore of the Lake of Gennesaret, and saw two boats close to the shore.'),
(994422,34,42,5,2,'The fishermen had gone away from them and were washing the nets.'),
(994423,34,42,5,3,'So, getting into one of the boats, which belonged to Simon, Jesus asked him to push off a little way from the shore, and then sat down and taught the people from the boat.'),
(994424,34,42,5,4,'When he had finished speaking, he said to Simon,'),
(994425,34,42,5,5,'‘We have been hard at work all night, Sir,’ answered Simon, ‘and have not caught anything, but, at your bidding, I will throw out the nets.’'),
(994426,34,42,5,6,'They did so, and enclosed such a great shoal of fish that their nets began to break.'),
(994427,34,42,5,7,'So they signalled to their partners in the other boat to come and help them; and they came and filled both the boats so full of fish that they were almost sinking.'),
(994428,34,42,5,8,'When Simon Peter saw this, he threw himself down at Jesus’ knees, exclaiming, ‘Master, leave me, for I am a sinful man!’'),
(994429,34,42,5,9,'For he and all who were with him were lost in amazement at the haul of fish which they had made;'),
(994430,34,42,5,10,'and so, too, were James and John, Zebedee’s sons, who were Simon’s partners.'),
(994431,34,42,5,11,'And, when they had brought their boats to shore, they left everything, and followed him.'),
(994432,34,42,5,12,'On one occasion Jesus was staying in a town, when he saw a man who was covered with leprosy. When the leper saw Jesus, he threw himself on his face and implored his help, ‘Master, if only you are willing, you are able to make me clean.’'),
(994433,34,42,5,13,'Stretching out his hand, Jesus touched him, saying as he did so,'),
(994434,34,42,5,14,'and then Jesus impressed on him that he was not to say a word to anyone,'),
(994435,34,42,5,15,'However, the story about Jesus spread all the more, and great crowds came together to listen to him, and to be cured of their illnesses;'),
(994436,34,42,5,16,'but Jesus used to withdraw to lonely places and pray.'),
(994437,34,42,5,17,'On one of those days, when Jesus was teaching, some Pharisees and Doctors of the Law were sitting near by. (They had come from all the villages in Galilee and Judea, and from Jerusalem; and the power of the Lord was on Jesus, so that he could work cures.)'),
(994438,34,42,5,18,'And there some men brought on a bed a man who was paralysed. They tried to get him in and lay him before Jesus;'),
(994439,34,42,5,19,'but, finding no way of getting him in owing to the crowd, they went up on the roof and lowered him through the tiles, with his pallet, into the middle of the people and in front of Jesus.'),
(994440,34,42,5,20,'When he saw their faith, Jesus said,'),
(994441,34,42,5,21,'The teachers of the Law and the Pharisees began debating about this. ‘Who is this man who speaks so blasphemously?’ they asked. ‘Who can forgive sins except God?’'),
(994442,34,42,5,22,'When Jesus became aware of the way in which they were debating, he turned to them and exclaimed,'),
(994443,34,42,5,25,'Instantly the man stood up before their eyes, took up what he had been lying on, and went to his home, praising God.'),
(994444,34,42,5,26,'The people, one and all, were lost in amazement, and praised God; and in great awe they said, ‘We have seen marvellous things today!’'),
(994445,34,42,5,27,'After this, Jesus went out; and he noticed a tax-gatherer, named Levi, sitting in the tax office, and said to him,'),
(994446,34,42,5,28,'Levi left everything and got up and followed him.'),
(994447,34,42,5,29,'And Levi gave a great entertainment at his house, in honour of Jesus; and a large number of tax-gatherers and others were having dinner with them.'),
(994448,34,42,5,30,'The Pharisees and the teachers of the Law belonging to their party complained of this to the disciples of Jesus.'),
(994449,34,42,5,31,'In answer Jesus said,'),
(994450,34,42,5,33,'‘John’s disciples,’ they said to Jesus, ‘Often fast and say prayers, and so do the disciples of the Pharisees, while yours are eating and drinking!’'),
(994451,34,42,5,34,'But Jesus answered them,'),
(994452,34,42,5,36,'Then, as an illustration, Jesus said to them,'),
(994453,34,42,6,1,'One Sabbath Jesus was walking through cornfields, and his disciples were picking the ears of wheat, and rubbing them in their hands, and eating them.'),
(994454,34,42,6,2,'‘Why are you doing what it is not allowable to do on the Sabbath?’ asked some of the Pharisees.'),
(994455,34,42,6,3,'Jesus’ answer was,'),
(994456,34,42,6,5,'Then Jesus added,'),
(994457,34,42,6,6,'On another Sabbath Jesus went into the synagogue and taught; and there was a man there whose right hand was withered.'),
(994458,34,42,6,7,'The teachers of the Law and the Pharisees watched Jesus closely, to see if he would work cures on the Sabbath, so that they might find a charge to bring against him.'),
(994459,34,42,6,8,'Jesus, however, knew what was in the their minds, and said to the man whose hand was withered,'),
(994460,34,42,6,9,'and Jesus said to them,'),
(994461,34,42,6,10,'Then, looking round at them all, he said to the man,'),
(994462,34,42,6,11,'But the teachers of the Law and the Pharisees were mad with rage, and consulted together what they could do to Jesus.'),
(994463,34,42,6,12,'Now about that time, Jesus went out, up the hill, to pray, and spent the whole night in prayer to God.'),
(994464,34,42,6,13,'When day came, he summoned his disciples, and chose twelve of them, whom he also named “apostles.”'),
(994465,34,42,6,14,'They were Simon (whom Jesus also named Peter), and his brother Andrew, James, John, Philip, Bartholomew,'),
(994466,34,42,6,15,'Matthew, Thomas, James son of Alphaeus, Simon known as the Zealot,'),
(994467,34,42,6,16,'Judas son of James, and Judas Iscariot, who proved a traitor.'),
(994468,34,42,6,17,'Afterwards Jesus came down the hill with them and took his stand on a level place. With him were a large crowd of his disciples, and great numbers of people from the whole of Judea, Jerusalem, and the coast district of Tyre and Sidon,'),
(994469,34,42,6,18,'who had come to hear him and to be restored to health. Those, too, who were troubled with foul spirits were cured;'),
(994470,34,42,6,19,'and everyone in the crowd was trying to touch him, because a power went out from him which restored them all.'),
(994471,34,42,6,20,'Then, raising his eyes and looking at his disciples, Jesus said:'),
(994472,34,42,7,1,'When Jesus had brought to a conclusion all that he had then had to say to the people, he entered Capernaum.'),
(994473,34,42,7,2,'A captain in the Roman army had a slave whom he valued, and who was seriously ill – almost at the point of death.'),
(994474,34,42,7,3,'And, hearing about Jesus, he sent some Jewish elders to him, with the request that he would come and save his slave’s life.'),
(994475,34,42,7,4,'When they found Jesus, they earnestly implored him to do so. ‘He deserves the favour from you,’ they said,'),
(994476,34,42,7,5,'‘For he is devoted to our nation, and himself built our synagogue for us.’'),
(994477,34,42,7,6,'So Jesus went with them. But, when he was no great distance from the house, the captain sent some friends with the message – ‘Do not trouble yourself, Sir; for I am unworthy to receive you under my roof.'),
(994478,34,42,7,7,'That was why I did not even venture to come to you myself; but speak, and let my manservant be cured.'),
(994479,34,42,7,8,'For I myself am a man under the orders of others, with soldiers under me; and if I say to one of them “Go,” he goes, and to another “Come,” he comes, and to my slave “Do this,” he does it.’'),
(994480,34,42,7,9,'Jesus was surprised to hear these words from him; and, turning to the crowd which was following him, he said,'),
(994481,34,42,7,10,'And, when the messengers returned to the house, they found the slave recovered.'),
(994482,34,42,7,11,'Shortly after, Jesus went to a town called Nain, his disciples and a great crowd going with him.'),
(994483,34,42,7,12,'Just as he approached the gate of the town, there was a dead man being carried out for burial – an only son, and his mother was a widow. A large number of the people of the town were with her.'),
(994484,34,42,7,13,'When he saw her, the Master was moved with compassion for her, and he said to her,'),
(994485,34,42,7,14,'Then he went up and touched the bier, and the bearers stopped; and Jesus said,'),
(994486,34,42,7,15,'The dead man sat up and began to talk, and Jesus restored him to his mother.'),
(994487,34,42,7,16,'Everyone was awe-struck and began praising God. ‘A great prophet has arisen among us,’ they said. ‘God has visited his people.’'),
(994488,34,42,7,17,'And this story about Jesus spread all through Judea, and in the neighbouring countries as well.'),
(994489,34,42,7,18,'All these events were reported to John by his disciples.'),
(994490,34,42,7,19,'So he summoned two of them, and sent them to the Master to ask – ‘Are you “the coming one,” or are we to look for someone else?’'),
(994491,34,42,7,20,'When these men found Jesus, they said, ‘John the Baptist has sent us to you to ask – Are you “the coming one,” or are we to look for somebody else?’'),
(994492,34,42,7,21,'At that very time Jesus had cured many people of diseases, afflictions, and wicked spirits, and had given many blind people their sight.'),
(994493,34,42,7,22,'So his answer to the question was,'),
(994494,34,42,7,24,'When John’s messengers had left, Jesus, speaking to the crowds, began to say with reference to John,'),
(994495,34,42,7,29,'(All the people, when they heard this, and even the tax-gatherers, having accepted John’s baptism, acknowledged the justice of God.'),
(994496,34,42,7,30,'But the Pharisees and the students of the Law, having rejected John’s baptism, frustrated God’s purpose in regard to them.)'),
(994497,34,42,7,36,'One of the Pharisees asked Jesus to dine with him, so Jesus went to his house and took his place at the table.'),
(994498,34,42,7,37,'Just then a woman, who was an outcast in the town, having heard that Jesus was eating in the Pharisee’s house, brought an alabaster jar of perfume,'),
(994499,34,42,7,38,'and placed herself behind Jesus, near his feet, weeping. Then she began to make his feet wet with her tears, and she dried them with the hair of her head, repeatedly kissing his feet and anointing them with the perfume.'),
(994500,34,42,7,39,'When the Pharisee who had invited Jesus saw this, he said to himself, ‘Had this man been “the prophet,” he would have known who, and what sort of woman, this is who is touching him, and that she is an outcast.’');
INSERT INTO verses (id, version_id, book_id, chapter, verse, text) VALUES
(994501,34,42,7,40,'But, addressing him, Jesus said,'),
(994502,34,42,7,43,'‘I suppose,’ answered Simon, ‘it will be the man to whom he forgave the greater debt.’'),
(994503,34,42,7,44,'and then, turning to the woman, he said to Simon,'),
(994504,34,42,7,48,'Then he said to the woman,'),
(994505,34,42,7,49,'The other guests began to say to one another, ‘Who is this man who even pardons sins?’'),
(994506,34,42,7,50,'But Jesus said to the woman,'),
(994507,34,42,8,1,'Shortly afterwards, Jesus went on a journey through the towns and villages, proclaiming the good news of the kingdom of God. With him went the Twelve,'),
(994508,34,42,8,2,'as well as some women who had been cured of wicked spirits and of infirmities. They were Mary, known as Mary of Magdala (from whom seven demons had been expelled),'),
(994509,34,42,8,3,'and Joanna (the wife of Herod’s steward, Chuza), and Susannah, and many others – all of whom provided for Jesus and his apostles out of their own resources.'),
(994510,34,42,8,4,'Once, when a great crowd was collecting, and, when the people of town after town were flocking to Jesus, he spoke to them in the form of a parable,'),
(994511,34,42,8,9,'His disciples asked Jesus the meaning of this parable.'),
(994512,34,42,8,19,'Presently Jesus’ mother and brothers came where he was, but they were not able to join him because of the crowd.'),
(994513,34,42,8,20,'So word was brought to him – “Your mother and your brothers are standing outside, wanting to see you.”'),
(994514,34,42,8,21,'His reply, spoken to them all, was,'),
(994515,34,42,8,22,'One day about that time, Jesus got into a boat with his disciples and said to them,'),
(994516,34,42,8,23,'So they put off. While they were sailing, Jesus fell asleep. A squall swept down on the lake, and their boat was filling and they were in danger.'),
(994517,34,42,8,24,'So the disciples came and roused him. ‘Sir, Sir,’ they cried, ‘we are lost!’ Jesus rose and rebuked the wind and the rushing waves, and they fell, and a calm followed.'),
(994518,34,42,8,26,'And they reached the region of the Gerasenes, which is on the opposite side to Galilee;'),
(994519,34,42,8,27,'and, on getting ashore, Jesus met a man, who had demons in him, coming out of the town. For a long time this man had worn no clothing, and he had not lived in a house, but in the tombs.'),
(994520,34,42,8,28,'Catching sight of Jesus, he shrieked out and threw himself down before him, and in a loud voice exclaimed, ‘What do you want with me, Jesus, Son of the Most High God? I beg you not to torment me.’'),
(994521,34,42,8,29,'For Jesus was commanding the foul spirit to come out of the man. On many occasions it had seized him, and, even when secured with chains and fetters, and watched, he would break through anything that bound him, and be driven by the demon into the Wilds.'),
(994522,34,42,8,31,'and the demons begged Jesus not to order them away into the bottomless pit.'),
(994523,34,42,8,32,'There was a drove of many pigs close by feeding on the hill-side; and the demons begged Jesus to give them leave to enter into them. Jesus gave them leave.'),
(994524,34,42,8,33,'They came out from the man and took possession of the pigs; and the drove rushed down the steep slope into the lake and were drowned.'),
(994525,34,42,8,34,'When the men who tended them saw what had happened, they ran away, and carried the news to the town, and to the country round.'),
(994526,34,42,8,35,'The people went out to see what had happened, and, when they came to Jesus, they found the man from whom the demons had gone out, sitting, clothed and in his right mind, at Jesus’ feet; and they were awe-struck.'),
(994527,34,42,8,36,'Those who had seen it told them how the possessed man had been delivered.'),
(994528,34,42,8,37,'Then all the people in the region of the Gerasenes asked Jesus to leave them, for they were terrified. Jesus got into a boat and returned.'),
(994529,34,42,8,38,'The man from whom the demons had gone out begged Jesus to let him be with him; but Jesus sent him away.'),
(994530,34,42,8,40,'On his return, Jesus was welcomed by the people; for everyone was looking out for him.'),
(994531,34,42,8,41,'And a man named Jairus, who was a synagogue leader, came to Jesus, and threw himself at Jesus’ feet, with entreaties that he would come to his house,'),
(994532,34,42,8,42,'because his only daughter, who was about twelve years old, was dying. As Jesus was going, the people were pressing closely round him.'),
(994533,34,42,8,43,'And a woman, who had suffered from haemorrhage for twelve years, and whom no one could cure,'),
(994534,34,42,8,44,'came up behind and touched the tassel of his cloak. Instantly the haemorrhage ceased.'),
(994535,34,42,8,47,'Then the woman, when she saw that she was discovered, came forward trembling, and threw herself down before him; and, in the presence of all the people, she told him her reason for touching him, and that she had been cured instantly.'),
(994536,34,42,8,49,'Before he had finished speaking, someone came from the house of the synagogue leader and said, ‘Your daughter is dead! Do not trouble the teacher further.’'),
(994537,34,42,8,50,'But Jesus, hearing this, spoke to the leader,'),
(994538,34,42,8,51,'When he reached the house, he did not allow anyone to go in with him, except Peter, John, and James, and the child’s father and mother.'),
(994539,34,42,8,52,'And everyone was weeping and mourning for her.'),
(994540,34,42,8,53,'They began to laugh at him, for they knew that she was dead.'),
(994541,34,42,8,54,'But, taking her by the hand, Jesus said in a loud voice,'),
(994542,34,42,8,55,'The child’s spirit returned to her, and she instantly stood up; and Jesus ordered them to give her something to eat.'),
(994543,34,42,8,56,'Her parents were amazed, but Jesus impressed on them that they were not to tell anyone what had happened.'),
(994544,34,42,9,1,'Jesus called the Twelve together, and gave them power and authority over all demons, as well as to cure diseases.'),
(994545,34,42,9,2,'He sent them out as his messengers, to proclaim the kingdom of God, and to work cures.'),
(994546,34,42,9,6,'Then they set out and went from village to village, telling the good news and curing people everywhere.'),
(994547,34,42,9,7,'Prince Herod heard of all that was happening, and was perplexed, because it was said by some that John must be risen from the dead.'),
(994548,34,42,9,8,'Some again said that Elijah had appeared, and others that one of the old prophets had risen again.'),
(994549,34,42,9,9,'But Herod himself said, ‘John I beheaded; but who is this of whom I hear such things?’ And he endeavoured to see him.'),
(994550,34,42,9,10,'When the apostles returned, they related to Jesus all that they had done. Then Jesus went privately to a town called Bethsaida, taking the apostles with him.'),
(994551,34,42,9,11,'But the people recognised him and followed him in crowds; and Jesus welcomed them and spoke to them about the kingdom of God, while he cured those who were in need of help.'),
(994552,34,42,9,12,'The day was drawing to a close, when the twelve came up to him, and said, ‘Send the crowd away, so that they may make their way to the villages and farms round about, and find themselves lodgings and provisions, for we are in a lonely spot here.’'),
(994553,34,42,9,13,'But Jesus said,'),
(994554,34,42,9,14,'(For the men among them were about five thousand.)'),
(994555,34,42,9,15,'This they did, and got all the people seated.'),
(994556,34,42,9,16,'Taking the five loaves and the two fish, Jesus looked up to heaven and said the blessing over them. Then he broke them in pieces, and gave them to his disciples to set before the people.'),
(994557,34,42,9,17,'Everyone had sufficient to eat, and what was left of the broken pieces was picked up – twelve baskets.'),
(994558,34,42,9,18,'Afterwards, when Jesus was alone, praying, his disciples joined him, and he asked them this question –'),
(994559,34,42,9,19,'‘John the Baptist,’ was their answer. ‘Others, however, say that you are Elijah, while others say that one of the old prophets has risen again.’'),
(994560,34,42,9,21,'Jesus, however, strictly charged them not to say this to anyone;'),
(994561,34,42,9,22,'he told them that the Son of Man must undergo much suffering, and be rejected by the elders, and chief priests, and teachers of the Law, and be put to death, and rise on the third day.'),
(994562,34,42,9,23,'And to all present he said,'),
(994563,34,42,9,28,'About eight days after speaking these words, Jesus went up the mountain to pray, taking with him Peter, John, and James.'),
(994564,34,42,9,29,'As he was praying, the aspect of his face was changed, and his clothing became of a glittering whiteness.'),
(994565,34,42,9,30,'And all at once two men were talking with Jesus; they were Moses and Elijah,'),
(994566,34,42,9,31,'who appeared in a glorified state, and spoke of his departure, which was destined to take place at Jerusalem.'),
(994567,34,42,9,32,'Peter and his companions had been overpowered by sleep but, suddenly becoming wide awake, they saw Jesus glorified and the two men who were standing beside him.'),
(994568,34,42,9,33,'And, as Moses and Elijah were passing away from Jesus, Peter exclaimed, ‘Sir, it is good to be here; let us make three tents, one for you, and one for Moses, and one for Elijah.’ He did not know what he was saying;'),
(994569,34,42,9,34,'and, while he was speaking, a cloud came down and enveloped them; and they were afraid, as they passed into the cloud;'),
(994570,34,42,9,35,'and from the cloud came a voice which said – ‘This is my Son, the Chosen One; him you must hear.’'),
(994571,34,42,9,36,'And, as the voice ceased, Jesus was found alone. The apostles kept silence, and told no one about any of the things that they had seen.'),
(994572,34,42,9,37,'The next day, when they had come down from the mountain, a great crowd met Jesus.'),
(994573,34,42,9,38,'And just then a man in the crowd shouted out, ‘Teacher, I entreat you to look at my son, for he is my only child;'),
(994574,34,42,9,39,'all at once a spirit will seize him, suddenly shriek out, and throw him into convulsions until he foams, and will leave him only when he is utterly exhausted.'),
(994575,34,42,9,40,'I entreated your disciples to drive the spirit out, but they could not.’'),
(994576,34,42,9,42,'While the boy was coming up to Jesus, the demon dashed him down and threw him into convulsions. But Jesus rebuked the foul spirit, and cured the boy, and gave him back to his father.'),
(994577,34,42,9,43,'And all present were struck with awe at the majesty of God.'),
(994578,34,42,9,45,'But the disciples did not understand the meaning of this; it had been concealed from them so that they did not see it, and they were afraid to question him as to what he meant.'),
(994579,34,42,9,46,'A discussion arose among the disciples as to which of them was the greatest;'),
(994580,34,42,9,47,'and Jesus, knowing of the discussion that was occupying their thoughts, took hold of a little child, and placed it beside him,'),
(994581,34,42,9,48,'and then said to them,'),
(994582,34,42,9,49,'John said, ‘Sir, we saw a man driving out demons by using your name, and we tried to prevent him, because he does not follow you with us.’'),
(994583,34,42,9,51,'As the days before his being taken up to heaven were growing few, Jesus set his face resolutely in the direction of Jerusalem; and he sent on messengers in advance.'),
(994584,34,42,9,52,'On their way, they went into a Samaritan village to make preparations for him,'),
(994585,34,42,9,53,'but the people there did not welcome him, because his face was set in the direction of Jerusalem.'),
(994586,34,42,9,54,'When James and John saw this, they said, ‘Master, do you wish us to call for fire to come down from the heavens and consume them?’'),
(994587,34,42,9,55,'But Jesus turned and rebuked them.'),
(994588,34,42,9,57,'And, while they were on their way, a man said to Jesus, ‘I will follow you wherever you go.’'),
(994589,34,42,9,59,'To another man Jesus said,'),
(994590,34,42,9,60,'But Jesus said,'),
(994591,34,42,9,61,'‘Master,’ said another, ‘I will follow you; but first let me say goodbye to my family.’'),
(994592,34,42,9,62,'But Jesus answered,'),
(994593,34,42,10,1,'After this, the Master appointed seventy-two other disciples, and sent them on as his messengers, two and two, in advance, to every town and place that he was himself intending to visit.'),
(994594,34,42,10,17,'When the seventy-two returned, they exclaimed joyfully, ‘Master, even the demons submit to us when we use your name.’'),
(994595,34,42,10,18,'And Jesus replied,'),
(994596,34,42,10,21,'At that same time, moved to exultation by the Holy Spirit, Jesus said:'),
(994597,34,42,10,23,'Then, turning to his disciples, Jesus said to them alone,'),
(994598,34,42,10,25,'Just then a Student of the Law came forward to test Jesus further. ‘Teacher,’ he said, ‘what must I do if I am to gain eternal life?’'),
(994599,34,42,10,27,'His reply was –'),
(994600,34,42,10,29,'But the man, wanting to justify himself, said to Jesus, ‘And who is my neighbour?’'),
(994601,34,42,10,30,'To which Jesus replied,'),
(994602,34,42,10,37,'‘The one that took pity on him,’ was the answer; at which Jesus said,'),
(994603,34,42,10,38,'As they continued their journey, Jesus came to a village, where a woman named Martha welcomed him to her house.'),
(994604,34,42,10,39,'She had a sister called Mary, who seated herself at the Master’s feet, and listened to his teaching;'),
(994605,34,42,10,40,'but Martha was distracted by the many preparations that she was making. So she went up to Jesus and said, ‘Master, do you approve of my sister’s leaving me to make preparations alone? Tell her to help me.’'),
(994606,34,42,11,1,'One day Jesus was at a certain place praying, and, when he had finished, one of his disciples said to him, ‘Master, teach us to pray, as John taught his disciples.’'),
(994607,34,42,11,5,'Jesus also said to them,'),
(994608,34,42,11,14,'Once Jesus was driving out a dumb demon, and, when the demon had gone out, the dumb man spoke. The people were amazed at this;'),
(994609,34,42,11,15,'but some of them said, ‘He drives out demons by the help of Beelzebul, the chief of the demons’;'),
(994610,34,42,11,16,'while others, to test him, asked him for some sign from the heavens.'),
(994611,34,42,11,17,'Jesus himself, however, was aware of what they were thinking, and said to them,'),
(994612,34,42,11,27,'As Jesus was saying this, a woman in the crowd, raising her voice, exclaimed, ‘Happy was the mother who bore you and nursed you!’'),
(994613,34,42,11,28,'But Jesus replied,'),
(994614,34,42,11,29,'As the crowds increased, Jesus began to speak,'),
(994615,34,42,11,37,'As Jesus finished speaking, a Pharisee asked him to breakfast with him, and Jesus went in and took his place at the table.'),
(994616,34,42,11,38,'The Pharisee noticed, to his astonishment, that Jesus omitted the ceremonial washing before breakfast.'),
(994617,34,42,11,39,'But the Master said to him,'),
(994618,34,42,11,45,'Here one of the students of the Law interrupted him by saying, ‘Teacher, when you say this, you are insulting us also.’'),
(994619,34,42,11,46,'But Jesus went on,'),
(994620,34,42,11,53,'When Jesus left the house, the teachers of the Law and the Pharisees began to press him hard and question him closely on many subjects,'),
(994621,34,42,11,54,'laying traps for him, so as to seize on anything that he might say.'),
(994622,34,42,12,1,'Meanwhile the people had gathered in thousands, so that they trod on one another, when Jesus, addressing himself to his disciples, began by saying to them,'),
(994623,34,42,12,13,'‘Teacher,’ a man in the crowd said to Jesus, ‘tell my brother to share the property with me.’'),
(994624,34,42,12,14,'But Jesus said to him,'),
(994625,34,42,12,15,'And then he added,'),
(994626,34,42,12,16,'Then Jesus told them this parable –'),
(994627,34,42,12,22,'And Jesus said to his disciples,'),
(994628,34,42,12,41,'‘Master,’ said Peter, ‘are you telling this parable with reference to us or to everyone?’'),
(994629,34,42,12,54,'And to the people Jesus said,'),
(994630,34,42,13,1,'Just at that time some people had come to tell Jesus about the Galileans, whose blood Pilate had mingled with the blood of their sacrifices.'),
(994631,34,42,13,6,'And Jesus told them this parable –'),
(994632,34,42,13,10,'Jesus was teaching on a Sabbath in one of the synagogues,'),
(994633,34,42,13,11,'and he saw before him a woman who for eighteen years had suffered from weakness owing to her having an evil spirit in her. She was bent double, and was wholly unable to raise herself.'),
(994634,34,42,13,12,'When Jesus saw her, he called her to him, and said,'),
(994635,34,42,13,13,'He placed his hands on her, and she was instantly made straight, and began to praise God.'),
(994636,34,42,13,14,'But the synagogue leader, indignant that Jesus had worked the cure on the Sabbath, intervened and said to the people, ‘There are six days on which work ought to be done; come to be cured on one of those, and not on the Sabbath.’'),
(994637,34,42,13,17,'As he said this, his opponents all felt ashamed; but all the people rejoiced to see all the wonderful things that he was doing.'),
(994638,34,42,13,18,'So Jesus said,'),
(994639,34,42,13,20,'And again Jesus said,'),
(994640,34,42,13,22,'Jesus went through towns and villages, teaching as he went, and making his way towards Jerusalem.'),
(994641,34,42,13,23,'‘Master,’ someone asked, ‘are there but few in the path of salvation?’ And Jesus answered,'),
(994642,34,42,13,31,'Just then some Pharisees came up to Jesus and said, ‘Go away and leave this place, for Herod wants to kill you.’'),
(994643,34,42,13,32,'But Jesus answered,'),
(994644,34,42,14,1,'On one occasion, as Jesus was going, on a Sabbath into the house of one of the leading Pharisees to dine, they were watching him closely.'),
(994645,34,42,14,2,'There he saw before him a man who was suffering from dropsy.'),
(994646,34,42,14,4,'They remained silent. Jesus took hold of the man and cured him, and sent him away.'),
(994647,34,42,14,5,'And he said to them,'),
(994648,34,42,14,6,'And they could not make any answer to that.'),
(994649,34,42,14,7,'Observing that the guests were choosing the best places for themselves, Jesus told them this parable –'),
(994650,34,42,14,12,'Then Jesus went on to say to the man who had invited him,'),
(994651,34,42,14,15,'One of the guests heard what he said and exclaimed, ‘Happy will be the person who will eat bread in the kingdom of God!’'),
(994652,34,42,14,16,'But Jesus said to him,'),
(994653,34,42,14,25,'One day, when great crowds of people were walking with Jesus, he turned and said to them,'),
(994654,34,42,15,1,'The tax-gatherers and the outcasts were all drawing near to Jesus to listen to him;'),
(994655,34,42,15,2,'but the Pharisees and the teachers of the Law found fault.'),
(994656,34,42,15,3,'So Jesus told them this parable –'),
(994657,34,42,15,11,'Then Jesus continued,'),
(994658,34,42,16,1,'Jesus said to his disciples,'),
(994659,34,42,16,14,'All this was said within hearing of the Pharisees, who were lovers of money, and they began to sneer at Jesus.'),
(994660,34,42,17,1,'Jesus said to his disciples,'),
(994661,34,42,17,5,'‘Give us more faith,’ said the apostles to the Master;'),
(994662,34,42,17,6,'but the Master said,'),
(994663,34,42,17,11,'On the way to Jerusalem Jesus passed between Samaria and Galilee.'),
(994664,34,42,17,12,'As he was entering a village, ten lepers met him.'),
(994665,34,42,17,13,'Standing still, some distance off, they called out loudly, ‘Jesus! Sir! Pity us!’'),
(994666,34,42,17,14,'When Jesus saw them, he said,'),
(994667,34,42,17,15,'One of them, finding he was cured, came back, praising God loudly,'),
(994668,34,42,17,16,'and threw himself on his face at Jesus’ feet, thanking him for what he had done; and this man was a Samaritan.'),
(994669,34,42,17,20,'Being once asked by the Pharisees when the kingdom of God was to come, Jesus answered,'),
(994670,34,42,17,37,'‘Where will it be, Master?’ asked the disciples.'),
(994671,34,42,18,1,'Jesus told his disciples a parable to show them that they should always pray and never despair.'),
(994672,34,42,18,6,'Then the Master added,'),
(994673,34,42,18,9,'Another time, speaking to people who were satisfied that they were religious, and who regarded everyone else with scorn, Jesus told this parable –'),
(994674,34,42,18,15,'Some of the people were bringing even their babies to Jesus, for him to touch them; but, when the disciples saw it, they began to find fault with those who had brought them.'),
(994675,34,42,18,16,'Jesus, however, called the little children to him.'),
(994676,34,42,18,18,'And one of the leaders asked Jesus this question – ‘Good teacher, what must I do if I am to gain eternal life?’'),
(994677,34,42,18,21,'‘I have observed all these,’ he replied, ‘from childhood.’'),
(994678,34,42,18,22,'Hearing this, Jesus said to him,'),
(994679,34,42,18,23,'But the man became greatly distressed on hearing this, for he was extremely rich.'),
(994680,34,42,18,24,'Seeing this, Jesus said to his disciples,'),
(994681,34,42,18,26,'‘Then who can be saved?’ asked those who heard this.'),
(994682,34,42,18,27,'But Jesus said,'),
(994683,34,42,18,28,'‘But we,’ said Peter, ‘we left what belonged to us and followed you.’'),
(994684,34,42,18,31,'Gathering the Twelve round him, Jesus said to them,'),
(994685,34,42,18,34,'The apostles did not comprehend any of this. His meaning was unintelligible to them and they did not understand what he was saying.'),
(994686,34,42,18,35,'As Jesus was getting near Jericho, a blind man was sitting by the roadside, begging.'),
(994687,34,42,18,36,'Hearing a crowd going by, the man asked what was the matter;'),
(994688,34,42,18,37,'and, when people told him that Jesus of Nazareth was passing,'),
(994689,34,42,18,38,'he shouted out, ‘Jesus, Son of David, take pity on me!’'),
(994690,34,42,18,39,'Those who were in front kept telling him to be quiet, but he continued to call out the louder, ‘Son of David, take pity on me!’'),
(994691,34,42,18,40,'Then Jesus stopped and ordered the man to be brought to him. And, when he had come close up to him, Jesus asked him,'),
(994692,34,42,18,42,'And Jesus said,'),
(994693,34,42,18,43,'Instantly he recovered his sight, and began to follow Jesus, praising God. And all the people, on seeing it, gave glory to God.'),
(994694,34,42,19,1,'Jesus entered Jericho and made his way through the town.'),
(994695,34,42,19,2,'There was a man there, known by the name of Zacchaeus, who was a commissioner of taxes and a rich man.'),
(994696,34,42,19,3,'He tried to see what Jesus was like; but, being short, he was unable to do so because of the crowd.'),
(994697,34,42,19,4,'So he ran on ahead and climbed into a mulberry tree, to see Jesus, for he knew that he must pass that way.'),
(994698,34,42,19,5,'When Jesus came to the place, he looked up and said to him,'),
(994699,34,42,19,6,'So Zacchaeus got down quickly, and joyfully welcomed him.'),
(994700,34,42,19,7,'On seeing this, everyone began to complain, ‘He has gone to stay with a man who is an outcast.’'),
(994701,34,42,19,8,'But Zacchaeus stood forward and said to the Master, ‘Listen, Master! I will give half my property to the poor, and, if I have defrauded anyone of anything, I will give him back four times as much.’'),
(994702,34,42,19,11,'As the people were listening to this, Jesus went on to tell them a parable. He did so because he was near Jerusalem, and because they thought that the kingdom of God was going to be proclaimed at once.'),
(994703,34,42,19,12,'He said,'),
(994704,34,42,19,28,'After saying this, Jesus went on in front, going up to Jerusalem.'),
(994705,34,42,19,29,'It was when Jesus had almost reached Bethphage and Bethany, near the Mount of Olives, that he sent on two of the disciples.'),
(994706,34,42,19,32,'So the two who were sent went and found it as Jesus had told them.'),
(994707,34,42,19,33,'While they were untying the foal, the owners asked them – ‘Why are you untying the foal?’'),
(994708,34,42,19,34,'And the two disciples answered – ‘The Master wants it.’'),
(994709,34,42,19,35,'Then they led it back to Jesus, and threw their cloaks on the foal and put Jesus on it.'),
(994710,34,42,19,36,'As he went along, the people kept spreading their cloaks in the road.'),
(994711,34,42,19,37,'When he had almost reached the place where the road led down the Mount of Olives, everyone of the many disciples began in their joy to praise God loudly for all the miracles that they had seen:'),
(994712,34,42,19,38,'‘Blessed is He who comes – our king – in the name of the Lord!'),
(994713,34,42,19,39,'Some of the Pharisees in the crowd said to him, ‘Teacher, restrain your disciples.’'),
(994714,34,42,19,40,'But Jesus answered,'),
(994715,34,42,19,41,'When he drew near, on seeing the city, he wept over it, and said,'),
(994716,34,42,19,45,'Jesus went into the Temple Courts and began to drive out those who were selling,'),
(994717,34,42,19,46,'saying as he did so,'),
(994718,34,42,19,47,'Jesus continued to teach each day in the Temple Courts; but the chief priests and teachers of the Law were eager to take his life, and so also were the leaders of the people.'),
(994719,34,42,19,48,'Yet they could not see what to do, for the people all hung on his words.'),
(994720,34,42,20,1,'On one of these days, when Jesus was teaching the people in the Temple Courts and telling the good news, the chief priests and the teachers of the Law, joined by the elders, confronted him,'),
(994721,34,42,20,2,'and addressing him, said, ‘Tell us what authority you have to do these things. Who is it who has given you this authority?’'),
(994722,34,42,20,5,'But they began arguing together, ‘If we say “divine,” he will say “Why didn’t you believe him?”'),
(994723,34,42,20,6,'But, if we say “human,” the people will all stone us, for they are persuaded that John was a prophet.’'),
(994724,34,42,20,7,'So they answered that they did not know its origin.'),
(994725,34,42,20,9,'But Jesus began to tell the people this parable –'),
(994726,34,42,20,17,'But Jesus looked at them and said,'),
(994727,34,42,20,19,'After this the teachers of the Law and the chief priest were eager to lay hands on Jesus then and there, but they were afraid of the people; for they saw that it was at them that he had aimed this parable.'),
(994728,34,42,20,20,'Having watched their opportunity, they afterwards sent some spies, who pretended to be good men, to catch Jesus in the course of conversation, and so enable them to give him up to the Governor’s jurisdiction and authority.'),
(994729,34,42,20,21,'These spies asked Jesus a question. They said, ‘Teacher, we know that you are right in what you say and teach, and that you do not take any account of a person’s position, but teach the way of God honestly;'),
(994730,34,42,20,22,'are we right in paying tribute to the Emperor or not?’'),
(994731,34,42,20,23,'Seeing through their deceitfulness, Jesus said to them,'),
(994732,34,42,20,25,'‘The Emperor’s,’ they said; and Jesus replied,'),
(994733,34,42,20,26,'They could not lay hold of this answer before the people; and, in their wonder at his reply, they held their tongues.'),
(994734,34,42,20,27,'Presently there came up some Sadducees, who maintain that there is no resurrection. Their question was this –'),
(994735,34,42,20,28,'‘Teacher, Moses laid down for us in his writings that –'),
(994736,34,42,20,29,'Well, there were once seven brothers; of whom the eldest, after taking a wife, died childless.'),
(994737,34,42,20,30,'The second and third brothers both took her as their wife;'),
(994738,34,42,20,31,'and so, too, did all seven – dying without children.'),
(994739,34,42,20,32,'The woman herself was the last to die.'),
(994740,34,42,20,33,'About the woman, then – at the resurrection, whose wife is she to be, all seven brothers having had her as their wife?’'),
(994741,34,42,20,39,'‘Well said, teacher!’ exclaimed some of the teachers of the Law,'),
(994742,34,42,20,40,'for they did not venture to question him any further.'),
(994743,34,42,20,41,'But Jesus said to them,'),
(994744,34,42,20,45,'While all the people were listening, Jesus said to the disciples,'),
(994745,34,42,21,1,'Looking up, Jesus saw the rich people putting their gifts into the chests for the Temple offerings.'),
(994746,34,42,21,2,'He saw, too, a widow in poor circumstances putting two small coins into them.'),
(994747,34,42,21,5,'When some of them spoke about the Temple being decorated with beautiful stones and offerings, Jesus said,'),
(994748,34,42,21,7,'So the disciples questioned Jesus, ‘But, teacher, when will this happen? And what sign will there be when this is near?’'),
(994749,34,42,21,8,'And Jesus said,'),
(994750,34,42,21,10,'Then he said to them,'),
(994751,34,42,21,29,'Then he taught them a lesson, saying –'),
(994752,34,42,21,37,'During the days, Jesus continued to teach in the Temple Courts, but he went out and spent the nights on the hill called the “Mount of Olives.”'),
(994753,34,42,21,38,'And all the people would get up early in the morning and come to listen to him in the Temple Courts.'),
(994754,34,42,22,1,'The feast of the unleavened bread, known as the Passover, was near.'),
(994755,34,42,22,2,'The chief priest and the teachers of the Law were looking for an opportunity of destroying Jesus, for they were afraid of the people.'),
(994756,34,42,22,3,'Now Satan took possession of Judas, who was known as Iscariot, and who belonged to the Twelve;'),
(994757,34,42,22,4,'and he went and discussed with the chief priests and officers in charge at the Temple the best way of betraying Jesus to them.'),
(994758,34,42,22,5,'They were glad of this, and agreed to pay him.'),
(994759,34,42,22,6,'So Judas assented, and looked for an opportunity to betray Jesus to them, in the absence of a crowd.'),
(994760,34,42,22,7,'When the day of the Festival of the unleavened bread came, on which the Passover lambs had to be killed,'),
(994761,34,42,22,8,'Jesus sent forward Peter and John, saying to them,'),
(994762,34,42,22,9,'‘Where do you wish us to make preparations?’ they asked.'),
(994763,34,42,22,13,'So Peter and John went on, and found everything just as Jesus had told them, and they prepared the Passover.'),
(994764,34,42,22,14,'When the time came, Jesus took his place at the table, and the apostles with him.'),
(994765,34,42,22,17,'Then, on receiving a cup, after saying the thanksgiving, he said,'),
(994766,34,42,22,19,'Then Jesus took some bread, and, after saying the thanksgiving, broke it and gave to them, with the words,'),
(994767,34,42,22,23,'Then they began questioning one another which of them it could be who was going to do this.'),
(994768,34,42,22,24,'And a dispute arose among them as to which of them was to be regarded as the greatest.'),
(994769,34,42,22,25,'Jesus, however, said,'),
(994770,34,42,22,33,'‘Master,’ said Peter, ‘with you I am ready to go both to prison and to death.’'),
(994771,34,42,22,35,'Then he said to them all,'),
(994772,34,42,22,38,'‘Master,’ they exclaimed, ‘look, here are two swords!’'),
(994773,34,42,22,39,'Jesus then went out, and made his way as usual to the Mount of Olives, followed by his disciples.'),
(994774,34,42,22,40,'And, when he reached the spot, he said to them,'),
(994775,34,42,22,41,'Then he withdrew about a stone’s throw, and knelt down and began to pray.'),
(994776,34,42,22,43,'Presently there appeared to him an angel from heaven, who strengthened him.'),
(994777,34,42,22,44,'And, as his anguish became intense, he prayed still more earnestly, while his sweat was like great drops of blood falling on the ground.'),
(994778,34,42,22,45,'Then he rose from praying, and came to the disciples and found them sleeping for sorrow.'),
(994779,34,42,22,47,'While he was still speaking, a crowd appeared in sight, led by the man called Judas, who was one of the Twelve. Judas approached Jesus, to kiss him;'),
(994780,34,42,22,48,'at which Jesus said to him,'),
(994781,34,42,22,49,'But when those who were round Jesus saw what was going to happen, they exclaimed, ‘Master, should we use our swords?’'),
(994782,34,42,22,50,'And one of them struck the high priest’s servant and cut off his right ear;'),
(994783,34,42,22,51,'at which Jesus said,'),
(994784,34,42,22,52,'Then, turning to the chief priests and officers in charge at the Temple and the elders, who had come for him, he said,'),
(994785,34,42,22,54,'Those who had taken Jesus prisoner took him away into the house of the high priest. Peter followed at a distance.'),
(994786,34,42,22,55,'But, when they had lit a fire in the centre of the courtyard and had all sat down there, Peter seated himself in the middle of them.'),
(994787,34,42,22,56,'Presently a maidservant saw him sitting near the blaze of the fire. She looked carefully at him and said, ‘Why, this man was one of his companions!’'),
(994788,34,42,22,57,'But Peter denied it. ‘I do not know him,’ he replied.'),
(994789,34,42,22,58,'A little while afterwards someone else – a man – saw him and said, ‘Why, you are one of them!’'),
(994790,34,42,22,59,'About an hour later another man declared positively, ‘This man also was certainly with him. Why, he is a Galilean!’'),
(994791,34,42,22,60,'But Peter said, ‘I do not know what you are speaking about.’ Instantly, while he was still speaking, a cock crowed.'),
(994792,34,42,22,61,'And the Master turned and looked at Peter; and Peter remembered the words that the Master had said to him –'),
(994793,34,42,22,62,'and he went outside and wept bitterly.'),
(994794,34,42,22,63,'The men who held Jesus kept making sport of him and beating him.'),
(994795,34,42,22,64,'They blindfolded him and then questioned him. ‘Now play the prophet,’ they said. ‘Who was it that struck you?’'),
(994796,34,42,22,65,'And they heaped many other insults on him.'),
(994797,34,42,22,66,'At daybreak the assembly of the elders of the people met – both the chief priests and the teachers of the Law – and took Jesus before their High Council.'),
(994798,34,42,22,67,'‘If you are the Christ,’ they said, ‘tell us so.’'),
(994799,34,42,22,70,'‘Are you, then, the Son of God?’ they all asked.'),
(994800,34,42,22,71,'At this they exclaimed, ‘Why do we want any more evidence? We have heard it ourselves from his own lips!’'),
(994801,34,42,23,1,'Then they all rose in a body and led Jesus before Pilate.'),
(994802,34,42,23,2,'And they began to accuse him, ‘This is a man whom we found misleading our people, preventing them from paying taxes to the Emperor, and giving out that he himself is “Christ, a king.”’'),
(994803,34,42,23,3,'‘Are you the king of the Jews?’ Pilate asked him.'),
(994804,34,42,23,4,'But Pilate, turning to the chief priests and the people, said, ‘I do not see anything to find fault with in this man.’'),
(994805,34,42,23,5,'But they insisted, ‘He is stirring up the people by his teaching all through Judea; he began with Galilee and has now come here.’'),
(994806,34,42,23,6,'Hearing this, Pilate asked if the man was a Galilean;'),
(994807,34,42,23,7,'and, having satisfied himself that Jesus came under Herod’s jurisdiction, he sent him to Herod, who also was at Jerusalem at the time.'),
(994808,34,42,23,8,'When Herod saw Jesus, he was exceedingly pleased, for he had been wanting to see him for a long time, having heard a great deal about him; and he was hoping to see some sign given by him.'),
(994809,34,42,23,9,'So he questioned him at some length, but Jesus made no reply.'),
(994810,34,42,23,10,'Meanwhile the chief priests and the teachers of the Law stood by and vehemently accused him.'),
(994811,34,42,23,11,'And Herod, with his soldiers, treated Jesus with scorn; he mocked him by throwing a gorgeous robe round him, and then sent him back to Pilate.'),
(994812,34,42,23,12,'And Herod and Pilate became friends that very day, for before that there had been ill-will between them.'),
(994813,34,42,23,13,'So Pilate summoned the chief priests, and the leading men, and the people,'),
(994814,34,42,23,14,'and said to them, ‘You brought this man before me charged with misleading the people; and yet, for my part, though I examined him before you, I did not find this man to blame for any of the things of which you accuse him;'),
(994815,34,42,23,15,'nor did Herod either; for he has sent him back to us. And, as a fact, he has not done anything deserving death;'),
(994816,34,42,23,16,'so I will have him scourged, and then release him.’'),
(994817,34,42,23,18,'But they began to shout as one man, ‘Kill this fellow, but release Barabbas for us.’'),
(994818,34,42,23,19,'(Barabbas was a man who had been put in prison for a riot that had broken out in the city and for murder.)'),
(994819,34,42,23,20,'Pilate, however, wanting to release Jesus, called to them again;'),
(994820,34,42,23,21,'but they kept calling out, ‘Crucify, crucify him!’'),
(994821,34,42,23,22,'‘Why, what harm has this man done?’ Pilate said to them for the third time. ‘I have found nothing in him for which he could be condemned to death. So I will have him scourged, and then release him.’'),
(994822,34,42,23,23,'But they persisted in loudly demanding his crucifixion; and their clamour gained the day.'),
(994823,34,42,23,24,'Pilate decided that their demand should be granted.'),
(994824,34,42,23,25,'He released the man who had been put in prison for riot and murder, as they demanded, and gave Jesus up to be dealt with as they pleased.'),
(994825,34,42,23,26,'And, as they were leading Jesus away, they laid hold of Simon from Cyrene, who was on his way in from the country, and they put the cross on his shoulders, for him to carry it behind Jesus.'),
(994826,34,42,23,27,'There was a great crowd of people following him, many being women who were beating their breasts and wailing for him.'),
(994827,34,42,23,28,'So Jesus turned and said to them,'),
(994828,34,42,23,32,'There were two others also, criminals, led out to be executed with Jesus.'),
(994829,34,42,23,33,'When they had reached the place called “The Skull,” there they crucified Jesus and the criminals, one on the right, and one on the left.'),
(994830,34,42,23,34,'Then Jesus said,'),
(994831,34,42,23,35,'Meanwhile the people stood looking on. Even the leading men said with a sneer, ‘He saved others, let him save himself, if he is God’s Christ, his chosen one.’'),
(994832,34,42,23,36,'The soldiers, too, came up in mockery, bringing him common wine,'),
(994833,34,42,23,37,'and saying as they did so, ‘If you are the king of the Jews, save yourself.’'),
(994834,34,42,23,38,'Above him were the words –'),
(994835,34,42,23,39,'One of the criminals who were hanging beside Jesus railed at him. ‘Aren’t you the Christ? Save yourself and us,’ he said.'),
(994836,34,42,23,40,'But the other rebuked him. ‘Haven’t you,’ he said, ‘any fear of God, now that you are under the same sentence?'),
(994837,34,42,23,41,'And we justly so, for we are only reaping our deserts, but this man has not done anything wrong.'),
(994838,34,42,23,42,'Jesus,’ he went on, ‘do not forget me when you have come to your kingdom.’'),
(994839,34,42,23,43,'And Jesus answered,'),
(994840,34,42,23,44,'It was nearly midday, when a darkness came over the whole country, lasting until three in the afternoon,'),
(994841,34,42,23,45,'the sun being eclipsed; and the Temple curtain was torn down the middle.'),
(994842,34,42,23,46,'Then Jesus, with a loud cry, said,'),
(994843,34,42,23,47,'The Roman captain, on seeing what had happened, praised God, exclaiming, ‘This must have been a good man!’'),
(994844,34,42,23,48,'All the people who had collected to see the sight watched what occurred, and then went home beating their breasts.'),
(994845,34,42,23,49,'All the friends of Jesus had been standing at a distance, with the women who accompanied him from Galilee, watching all this.'),
(994846,34,42,23,50,'Now there was a man of the name of Joseph, who was a member of the Council, and who bore a good and upright character.'),
(994847,34,42,23,51,'(This man had not assented to the decision and action of the Council.) He belonged to Ramah, a town in Judea, and lived in expectation of the kingdom of God.'),
(994848,34,42,23,52,'He now went to see Pilate, and asked for the body of Jesus;'),
(994849,34,42,23,53,'and, when he had taken it down, he wrapped it in a linen sheet, and laid him in a tomb cut out of stone, in which no one had yet been buried.'),
(994850,34,42,23,54,'It was the Preparation day, and just before the Sabbath began.'),
(994851,34,42,23,55,'The women who had accompanied Jesus from Galilee followed, and saw the tomb and how the body of Jesus was laid,'),
(994852,34,42,23,56,'and then went home, and prepared spices and perfumes.'),
(994853,34,42,24,1,'But very early on the first day of the week they went to the tomb, taking with them the spices that they had prepared.'),
(994854,34,42,24,2,'They found that the stone had been rolled away from the tomb;'),
(994855,34,42,24,3,'and, on going into it, they could not find the body'),
(994856,34,42,24,4,'While they were at a loss to account for this, all at once two men stood beside them, in dazzling clothing.'),
(994857,34,42,24,5,'But, when in their fear the women bowed their faces to the ground, the men said to them, ‘Why are you looking among the dead for him who is living?'),
(994858,34,42,24,7,'How he said that the Son of Man must be betrayed into the hands of wicked men, and be crucified, and rise again on the third day.’'),
(994859,34,42,24,8,'Then they remembered the words of Jesus,'),
(994860,34,42,24,9,'and, on returning from the tomb, they told all this to the Eleven and to all the rest.'),
(994861,34,42,24,10,'There were Mary of Magdala, and Joanna, and Mary, the mother of James. The other women, too, spoke about this to the apostles.'),
(994862,34,42,24,11,'What they said seemed to the apostles mere nonsense, and they did not believe them.'),
(994863,34,42,24,13,'It happened that very day that two of the disciples were going to a village called Emmaus, which was about seven miles from Jerusalem,'),
(994864,34,42,24,14,'talking together, as they went, about all that had just taken place.'),
(994865,34,42,24,15,'While they were talking about these things and discussing them, Jesus himself came up and went on their way with them;'),
(994866,34,42,24,16,'but their eyes were blinded so that they could not recognise him.'),
(994867,34,42,24,18,'and then one of them, whose name was Cleopas, said to Jesus, ‘Are you staying by yourself at Jerusalem, that you have not heard of the things that have happened there within the last few days?’'),
(994868,34,42,24,20,'and how the chief priests and our leading men gave him up to be sentenced to death, and afterwards crucified him.'),
(994869,34,42,24,21,'But we were hoping that he was the Destined Deliverer of Israel; yes, and besides all this, it is now three days since these things occurred.'),
(994870,34,42,24,22,'And what is more, some of the women among us have greatly astonished us. They went to the tomb at daybreak'),
(994871,34,42,24,23,'And, not finding the body of Jesus there, came and told us that they had seen a vision of angels who told them that he was alive.'),
(994872,34,42,24,24,'So some of our number went to the tomb and found everything just as the women had said, but they did not see Jesus.’'),
(994873,34,42,24,25,'Then Jesus said to them,'),
(994874,34,42,24,27,'Then, beginning with Moses and all the prophets, he explained to them all through the scriptures the passages that referred to himself.'),
(994875,34,42,24,28,'When they got near the village to which they were walking, Jesus appeared to be going further;'),
(994876,34,42,24,29,'but they pressed him not to do so. ‘Stay with us,’ they said, ‘for it is getting towards evening, and the sun in already low.’ So Jesus went in to stay with them.'),
(994877,34,42,24,30,'After he had taken his place at the table with them, he took the bread and said the blessing, and broke it, and gave it to them.'),
(994878,34,42,24,31,'Then their eyes were opened and they recognised him; but he disappeared from their sight.'),
(994879,34,42,24,32,'‘How our hearts glowed,’ the disciples said to each other, ‘while he was talking to us on the road, and when he explained the scriptures to us!’'),
(994880,34,42,24,33,'Then they immediately got up and returned to Jerusalem, where they found the Eleven and their companions all together,'),
(994881,34,42,24,34,'who told them that the Master had really risen, and had appeared to Simon.'),
(994882,34,42,24,35,'So they also related what had happened during their walk, and how they had recognised Jesus at the breaking of the bread.'),
(994883,34,42,24,36,'While they were still talking about these things, Jesus himself stood among them.'),
(994884,34,42,24,37,'In their terror and alarm they thought they saw a ghost,'),
(994885,34,42,24,38,'but Jesus said to them,'),
(994886,34,42,24,41,'While they were still unable to believe it all, overcome with joy, and were wondering if it were true, Jesus said to them,'),
(994887,34,42,24,42,'They handed him a piece of broiled fish,'),
(994888,34,42,24,43,'and he took it and ate it before their eyes.'),
(994889,34,42,24,45,'Then he enabled them to understand the meaning of the scriptures, saying to them,'),
(994890,34,42,24,50,'After this, Jesus led them out as far as Bethany, and there raised his hands and blessed them.'),
(994891,34,42,24,51,'As he was in the act of blessing them, he left them.'),
(994892,34,42,24,52,'They returned'),
(994893,34,42,24,53,'and they were constantly in the Temple Courts, blessing God.'),
(994894,34,43,1,1,'In the beginning the Word was;'),
(994895,34,43,1,2,'He was in the beginning with God;'),
(994896,34,43,1,3,'through him all things came into being,'),
(994897,34,43,1,4,'That which came into being in him was life;'),
(994898,34,43,1,5,'and the light shines in the darkness,'),
(994899,34,43,1,6,'There appeared a man sent from God, whose name was John;'),
(994900,34,43,1,7,'he came as a witness – to bear witness to the light'),
(994901,34,43,1,8,'He was not the light,'),
(994902,34,43,1,9,'That was the true light which enlightens everyone coming into the world.'),
(994903,34,43,1,10,'He was in the world;'),
(994904,34,43,1,11,'He came to his own –'),
(994905,34,43,1,12,'But to all who did receive him he gave power to become children of God –'),
(994906,34,43,1,13,'For not to natural conception, nor to human instincts, nor to human will did they owe the new life,'),
(994907,34,43,1,14,'And the Word became human, and lived among us,'),
(994908,34,43,1,15,'(John bears witness to him; he cried aloud – for it was he who spoke –'),
(994909,34,43,1,16,'out of his fullness we have all received some gift,'),
(994910,34,43,1,17,'for the Law was given through Moses,'),
(994911,34,43,1,18,'No one has ever yet seen God;'),
(994912,34,43,1,19,'When the religious authorities in Jerusalem sent some Priests and Levites to ask John – ‘Who are you?’,'),
(994913,34,43,1,20,'he told them clearly and simply, ‘I am not the Christ.’'),
(994914,34,43,1,21,'‘What then?’ they asked. ‘Are you Elijah?’'),
(994915,34,43,1,22,'‘Who then are you?’ they continued. ‘Tell us so that we have an answer to give to those who have sent us. What do you say about yourself?’'),
(994916,34,43,1,23,'‘I,’ he answered, ‘am –'),
(994917,34,43,1,24,'These men had been sent from the Pharisees;'),
(994918,34,43,1,25,'and their next question was, ‘Why then do you baptize, if you are not the Christ or Elijah or “the prophet”?’'),
(994919,34,43,1,26,'John’s answer was – ‘I baptize with water, but among you stands one whom you do not know;'),
(994920,34,43,1,27,'he is coming after me, yet I am not worthy even to unfasten his sandal.’'),
(994921,34,43,1,28,'This happened at Bethany, across the Jordan, where John was baptizing.'),
(994922,34,43,1,29,'The next day John saw Jesus coming towards him, and exclaimed, ‘Here is the Lamb of God, who takes away the sin of the world!'),
(994923,34,43,1,30,'I was talking about him when I said “After me there is coming a man who ranks ahead of me, because before I was born he already was.”'),
(994924,34,43,1,31,'I did not know who he was, but I have come baptizing with water to make him known to Israel.’'),
(994925,34,43,1,32,'John also said:'),
(994926,34,43,1,33,'I myself did not know him, but he who sent me to baptize with water, he said to me “He on whom you see the Spirit descending, and remaining on him – he it is who baptizes with the Holy Spirit.”'),
(994927,34,43,1,34,'This I have seen myself, and I have declared my belief that he is the Son of God.’'),
(994928,34,43,1,35,'The next day, when John was standing with two of his disciples,'),
(994929,34,43,1,36,'he looked at Jesus as he passed and exclaimed, ‘There is the Lamb of God!’'),
(994930,34,43,1,37,'The two disciples heard him say this, and followed Jesus.'),
(994931,34,43,1,38,'But Jesus turned round, and saw them following.'),
(994932,34,43,1,40,'One of the two, who heard what John said and followed Jesus, was Andrew, Simon Peter’s brother.'),
(994933,34,43,1,41,'He first found his own brother Simon, and said to him, ‘We have found the Messiah!’ (a word which means “Christ,” or “Consecrated”.)'),
(994934,34,43,1,42,'Then he brought him to Jesus. Looking straight at him, Jesus said,'),
(994935,34,43,1,43,'The following day Jesus decided to leave for Galilee. He found Philip, and said to him,'),
(994936,34,43,1,44,'Philip was from Bethsaida, the same town as Andrew and Peter.'),
(994937,34,43,1,45,'He found Nathanael and said to him, ‘We have found him of whom Moses wrote in the Law, and of whom the prophets also wrote – Jesus of Nazareth, Joseph’s son!’'),
(994938,34,43,1,46,'‘Can anything good come out of Nazareth?’ asked Nathanael. ‘Come and see,’ replied Philip.'),
(994939,34,43,1,47,'When Jesus saw Nathanael coming towards him, he said,'),
(994940,34,43,1,48,'‘How do you know me?’ asked Nathanael.'),
(994941,34,43,1,49,'‘Rabbi,’ Nathanael exclaimed, ‘you are the Son of God, you are king of Israel!’'),
(994942,34,43,2,1,'Two days after this there was a wedding at Cana in Galilee, and Jesus’ mother was there.'),
(994943,34,43,2,2,'Jesus himself, too, with his disciples, was invited to the wedding.'),
(994944,34,43,2,3,'And, when the wine ran short, his mother said to him, ‘They have no wine left.’'),
(994945,34,43,2,5,'His mother said to the servants, ‘Do whatever he tells you.’'),
(994946,34,43,2,6,'There were standing there six stone water-jars, in accordance with the Jewish rule of purification, each holding twenty or thirty gallons.'),
(994947,34,43,2,7,'Jesus said to the servants,'),
(994948,34,43,2,8,'And, when they had filled them to the brim, he added,'),
(994949,34,43,2,9,'And, when the Master of the feast had tasted the water which had now become wine, not knowing where it had come from – although the servants who had taken out the water knew –'),
(994950,34,43,2,10,'He called the groom and said to him, ‘Everyone puts good wine on the table first, and inferior wine afterwards, when his guests have drunk freely; but you have kept back the good wine till now!’'),
(994951,34,43,2,11,'This, the first sign of his mission, Jesus gave at Cana in Galilee, and by it revealed his glory; and his disciples believed in him.'),
(994952,34,43,2,12,'After this, Jesus went down to Capernaum – he, his mother, his brothers, and his disciples; but they stayed there only a few days.'),
(994953,34,43,2,13,'Then, as the Jewish Passover was near, Jesus went up to Jerusalem.'),
(994954,34,43,2,14,'In the Temple Courts he found people who were selling bullocks, sheep, and pigeons, and the money changers at their counters.'),
(994955,34,43,2,15,'So he made a whip of cords, and drove them all out of the Temple Courts, and the sheep and bullocks as well; he scattered the money of the money changers, and overturned their tables,'),
(994956,34,43,2,16,'and said to the pigeon-dealers,'),
(994957,34,43,2,17,'His disciples remembered that scripture said – “Passion for your house will consume me.”'),
(994958,34,43,2,18,'Then some of the religious authorities asked Jesus, ‘What sign are you going to show us, since you act in this way?’'),
(994959,34,43,2,20,'‘This Temple,’ the authorities replied, ‘has been forty-six years in building, and are you going to “raise it in three days”?’'),
(994960,34,43,2,21,'But Jesus was speaking of his body as a temple.'),
(994961,34,43,2,22,'Afterwards, when he had risen from the dead, his disciples remembered that he had said this; and they believed the passage of scripture, and the words which Jesus had spoken.'),
(994962,34,43,2,23,'While Jesus was in Jerusalem, during the Passover Festival, many came to trust in him, when they saw the signs of his mission that he was giving.'),
(994963,34,43,2,24,'But Jesus did not put himself in their power because he knew what was in their hearts.'),
(994964,34,43,2,25,'He did not need anyone to tell him about people because he could read what was in them.'),
(994965,34,43,3,1,'Now there was a Pharisee named Nicodemus, who was a leading man among his people.'),
(994966,34,43,3,2,'This man came to Jesus by night, and said to him, ‘Rabbi, we know that you are a teacher come from God; for no one could give such signs as you are giving, unless God were with him.’'),
(994967,34,43,3,4,'‘How can a person,’ asked Nicodemus, ‘be born when they are old? Can they be born a second time?’'),
(994968,34,43,3,9,'‘How can that be?’ asked Nicodemus.'),
(994969,34,43,3,22,'After this, Jesus went with his disciples into the country parts of Judea; and there he stayed with them, and baptized.'),
(994970,34,43,3,23,'John, also, was baptizing at Aenon near Salim, because there were many streams there; and people were constantly coming and being baptized.'),
(994971,34,43,3,24,'(For John had not yet been imprisoned).'),
(994972,34,43,3,25,'Now a discussion arose between some of John’s disciples and a fellow Jew on the subject of purification;'),
(994973,34,43,3,26,'and the disciples came to John and said, ‘Rabbi, the man who was with you on the other side of the Jordan, and to whom you have yourself borne testimony – he, also, is baptizing, and everybody is going to him.’'),
(994974,34,43,3,27,'John’s answer was – ‘A person can gain nothing but what is given them from heaven.'),
(994975,34,43,3,28,'You are yourselves witnesses that I said “I am not the Christ,” but “I have been sent before him as a messenger.”'),
(994976,34,43,3,29,'It is the groom who has the bride; but the groom’s friend, who stands by and listens to him, is filled with joy when he hears the groom’s voice. This joy I have felt to the full.'),
(994977,34,43,3,30,'He must become greater, and I less.’'),
(994978,34,43,3,31,'He who comes from above is above all others; but a child of earth is earthly, and his teaching is earthly, too. He who comes from heaven is above all others.'),
(994979,34,43,3,32,'He states what he has seen and what he heard, and yet no one accepts his statement.'),
(994980,34,43,3,33,'They who did accept his statement confirm the fact that God is true.'),
(994981,34,43,3,34,'For he whom God sent as his messenger gives us God’s own teaching, for God does not limit the gift of the Spirit.'),
(994982,34,43,3,35,'The Father loves his Son, and has put everything in his hands.'),
(994983,34,43,3,36,'The person who believes in the Son has eternal life, while a person who rejects the Son will not even see that life, but remains under God’s displeasure.'),
(994984,34,43,4,1,'Now, when the Master heard that the Pharisees had been told that he was making and baptizing more disciples than John'),
(994985,34,43,4,2,'(Though it was not Jesus himself, but his disciples, who baptized),'),
(994986,34,43,4,3,'he left Judea, and set out again for Galilee.'),
(994987,34,43,4,4,'He had to pass through Samaria,'),
(994988,34,43,4,5,'and, on his way, he came to a Samaritan town called Shechem, near the plot of land that Jacob gave to his son Joseph.'),
(994989,34,43,4,6,'Jacob’s Spring was there, and Jesus, being tired after his journey, sat down beside the spring, just as he was. It was then about midday.'),
(994990,34,43,4,7,'A woman of Samaria came to draw water; and Jesus said to her –'),
(994991,34,43,4,8,'For his disciples had gone into the town to buy food.'),
(994992,34,43,4,9,'‘How is it,’ replied the Samaritan woman, ‘that you who are a Jew ask for water from a Samaritan woman like me?’ (For Jews do not associate with Samaritans).'),
(994993,34,43,4,11,'‘You have no bucket, Sir, and the well is deep,’ she said. ‘Where did you get that “living water?”'),
(994994,34,43,4,12,'Surely you are not greater than our ancestor Jacob who gave us the well, and used to drink from it himself, and his sons, and his cattle!’'),
(994995,34,43,4,15,'‘Give me this water, Sir,’ said the woman, ‘so that I may not be thirsty, nor have to come all the way here to draw water.’'),
(994996,34,43,4,17,'‘I have no husband,’ answered the woman.'),
(994997,34,43,4,19,'‘I see, Sir, that you are a prophet!’ exclaimed the woman.'),
(994998,34,43,4,20,'‘It was on this mountain that our ancestors worshiped; and yet you Jews say that the proper place for worship is in Jerusalem.’'),
(994999,34,43,4,25,'‘I know,’ answered the woman, ‘that the Messiah, who is called the Christ, is coming; when once he has come, he will tell us everything.’'),
(995000,34,43,4,27,'At this moment his disciples came up, and were surprised to find him talking with a woman; but none of them asked “What do you want?” or “Why are you talking with her?”'),
(995001,34,43,4,28,'So the woman, leaving her pitcher, went back to the town, and said to the people,'),
(995002,34,43,4,29,'‘Come and see someone who has told me everything that I have done. Can he be the Christ?’'),
(995003,34,43,4,30,'And the people left the town and went to see Jesus.'),
(995004,34,43,4,31,'Meanwhile the disciples kept saying to him, ‘Take something to eat, Rabbi.’'),
(995005,34,43,4,33,'‘Can anyone have brought him anything to eat?’ the disciples said to one another.'),
(995006,34,43,4,39,'Many from that town came to believe in Jesus – Samaritans though they were – because the woman had said, “He has told me everything that I have done.”'),
(995007,34,43,4,40,'And, when these Samaritans had come to Jesus, they begged him to stay with them, and he stayed there two days.'),
(995008,34,43,4,41,'But far more came to believe in him because of what he said himself,'),
(995009,34,43,4,42,'and they said to the woman, ‘It is no longer because of what you say that we believe in him, for we have heard him ourselves and know that he really is the Saviour of the world.’'),
(995010,34,43,4,43,'After these two days Jesus went on to Galilee;'),
(995011,34,43,4,44,'for he himself declared that “a prophet is not honoured in his own country.”'),
(995012,34,43,4,45,'When he entered Galilee, the Galileans welcomed him, for they had seen all that he did at Jerusalem during the Festival, at which they also had been present.'),
(995013,34,43,4,46,'So Jesus came again to Cana in Galilee, where he had turned the water into wine. Now there was one of the king’s officers whose son was lying ill at Capernaum.'),
(995014,34,43,4,47,'When this man heard that Jesus had returned from Judea to Galilee, he went to him, and begged him to come down and cure his son; for he was at the point of death.'),
(995015,34,43,4,48,'Jesus answered,'),
(995016,34,43,4,49,'‘Sir,’ said the officer, ‘come down before my child dies.’ And Jesus answered, ‘Go, your son is living.’'),
(995017,34,43,4,50,'The man believed what Jesus said to him, and went;'),
(995018,34,43,4,51,'and, while he was on his way down, his servants met him, and told him that his child was living.'),
(995019,34,43,4,52,'So he asked them at what time the boy began to get better. ‘It was yesterday, about one o’clock,’ they said, ‘that the fever left him.’'),
(995020,34,43,4,53,'By this the father knew that it was at the very time when Jesus had said to him'),
(995021,34,43,4,54,'This was the second occasion on which Jesus gave a sign of his mission on coming from Judea to Galilee.'),
(995022,34,43,5,1,'Sometime after this there was a Jewish Festival; and Jesus went up to Jerusalem.'),
(995023,34,43,5,2,'There is in Jerusalem, near the sheep-gate, a bath with five colonnades round it. It is called in Hebrew “Bethesda.”'),
(995024,34,43,5,3,'In these colonnades a large number of sick people were lying – blind, lame, and crippled.'),
(995025,34,43,5,5,'One man who was there had been crippled for thirty-eight years.'),
(995026,34,43,5,6,'Jesus saw the man lying there, and, finding that he had been in this state a long time, said to him,'),
(995027,34,43,5,7,'‘I have no one, Sir,’ the sick man answered, ‘to put me into the bath when there is a troubling of the water, and, while I am getting to it, someone else steps down before me.’'),
(995028,34,43,5,9,'The man was cured immediately, and took up his mat and began walking.'),
(995029,34,43,5,10,'Now it was the Sabbath. So the religious authorities said to the man who had been cured, ‘This is the Sabbath; you must not carry your mat.’'),
(995030,34,43,5,11,'‘The man who cured me,’ he answered, ‘said to me'),
(995031,34,43,5,12,'‘Who was it,’ they asked, ‘that said to you'),
(995032,34,43,5,13,'But the man who had been restored did not know who it was; for Jesus had moved away, because there was a crowd there.'),
(995033,34,43,5,14,'Afterwards Jesus found the man in the Temple Courts, and said to him,'),
(995034,34,43,5,15,'The man went away, and told the authorities that it was Jesus who had cured him.'),
(995035,34,43,5,16,'And that was why they began to persecute Jesus – because he did things of this kind on the Sabbath.'),
(995036,34,43,5,17,'But Jesus replied,'),
(995037,34,43,5,18,'This made the authorities all the more eager to kill him, because not only was he doing away with the Sabbath, but he actually called God his own Father – putting himself on an equality with God.'),
(995038,34,43,5,19,'So Jesus made this further reply,'),
(995039,34,43,6,1,'After this, Jesus crossed the Sea of Galilee – otherwise called the Lake of Tiberias.'),
(995040,34,43,6,2,'A great crowd of people, however, followed him, because they saw the signs of his mission in his work among those who were sick.'),
(995041,34,43,6,3,'Jesus went up the hill, and sat down there with his disciples.'),
(995042,34,43,6,4,'It was near the time of the Jewish Festival of the Passover.'),
(995043,34,43,6,5,'Looking up, and noticing that a great crowd was coming towards him, Jesus said to Philip,'),
(995044,34,43,6,6,'He said this to test him, for he himself knew what he meant to do.'),
(995045,34,43,6,7,'‘Even if we spent a years’ wages on bread,’ answered Philip, ‘it would not be enough for each of them to have a little.’'),
(995046,34,43,6,8,'‘There is a boy here,’ said Andrew, another of his disciples, Simon Peter’s brother,'),
(995047,34,43,6,9,'‘Who has five barley loaves and two fish; but what is that for so many?’'),
(995048,34,43,6,11,'and then Jesus took the loaves, and, after saying the thanksgiving, distributed them to those who were sitting down; and the same with the fish, giving the people as much as they wanted.'),
(995049,34,43,6,12,'When they were satisfied, Jesus said to his disciples,'),
(995050,34,43,6,13,'The disciples did so, and filled twelve baskets with the pieces of the five barley loaves, which were left after all had eaten.'),
(995051,34,43,6,14,'When the people saw the signs which Jesus gave, they said, ‘This is certainly the prophet who was to come into the world.’'),
(995052,34,43,6,15,'But Jesus, having discovered that they were intending to come and carry him off to make him king, went again up the hill, quite alone.'),
(995053,34,43,6,16,'When evening fell, his disciples went down to the sea,'),
(995054,34,43,6,17,'and, getting into a boat, began to cross to Capernaum. By this time darkness had set in, and Jesus had not yet come back to them;'),
(995055,34,43,6,18,'the sea, too, was getting rough, for a strong wind was blowing.'),
(995056,34,43,6,19,'When they had rowed three or four miles, they caught sight of him walking on the water and approaching the boat, and they were frightened.'),
(995057,34,43,6,20,'But Jesus said to them,'),
(995058,34,43,6,21,'And after this they were glad to take him into the boat; and the boat at once arrived off the shore, for which they had been making.'),
(995059,34,43,6,22,'The people who remained on the further side of the sea had seen that only one boat had been there, and that Jesus had not gone into it with his disciples, but that they had left without him.'),
(995060,34,43,6,23,'Some boats, however, had come from Tiberias, from near the spot where they had eaten the bread after the Master had said the thanksgiving.'),
(995061,34,43,6,24,'So, on the next day, when the people saw that Jesus was not there, or his disciples either, they themselves got into the boats, and went to Capernaum to look for him.'),
(995062,34,43,6,25,'And, when they found him on the other side of the sea, they said, ‘When did you get here, Rabbi?’'),
(995063,34,43,6,28,'‘How,’ they asked, ‘are we to do the work that God wants us to do?’'),
(995064,34,43,6,30,'‘What sign, then,’ they asked, ‘are you giving, which we may see, and so believe you? What is the work that you are doing?'),
(995065,34,43,6,31,'Our ancestors had the manna to eat in the desert; as scripture says – “He gave them bread from heaven to eat.”’'),
(995066,34,43,6,34,'‘Master,’ they exclaimed, ‘give us that bread always!’'),
(995067,34,43,6,41,'The people began murmuring against Jesus for saying –'),
(995068,34,43,6,42,'‘Is not this Jesus, Joseph’s son,’ they asked, ‘whose father and mother we know? How is it that he now says that he has come down from heaven?’'),
(995069,34,43,6,52,'They began disputing with one another, ‘How is it possible for this man to give us his flesh to eat?’'),
(995070,34,43,6,59,'All this Jesus said in a synagogue, when he was teaching in Capernaum.'),
(995071,34,43,6,60,'On hearing it, many of his disciples said, ‘This is harsh doctrine! Who can bear to listen to it?’'),
(995072,34,43,6,61,'But Jesus, aware that his disciples were murmuring about it, said to them,'),
(995073,34,43,6,65,'and he added,'),
(995074,34,43,6,66,'After this many of his disciples drew back, and did not go about with him any longer.'),
(995075,34,43,6,67,'So Jesus said to the Twelve,'),
(995076,34,43,6,68,'But Simon Peter answered, ‘Master, to whom would we go? Eternal life is in your teaching;'),
(995077,34,43,6,69,'and we have learned to believe and to know that you are the Holy One of God.’'),
(995078,34,43,6,71,'He meant Judas, the son of Simon Iscariot, who was about to betray him, though he was one of the Twelve.'),
(995079,34,43,7,1,'After this, Jesus went about in Galilee, for he would not do so in Judea, because the religious authorities (in Jerusalem) were eager to put him to death.'),
(995080,34,43,7,2,'When the Jewish Festival of Tabernacles was near,'),
(995081,34,43,7,3,'his brothers said to him, ‘Leave this part of the country, and go into Judea, so that your disciples, as well as we, may see the work that you are doing.'),
(995082,34,43,7,4,'For no one does a thing privately, if they are seeking to be widely known. Since you do these things, you should show yourself publicly to the world.’'),
(995083,34,43,7,5,'For even his brothers did not believe in him.'),
(995084,34,43,7,9,'After telling them this, he stayed on in Galilee.'),
(995085,34,43,7,10,'But, when his brothers had gone up to the Festival, Jesus also went up – not publicly, but privately.'),
(995086,34,43,7,11,'The authorities were looking for him at the Festival and asking “Where is he?”;'),
(995087,34,43,7,12,'and there were many whispers about him among the people, some saying “He is a good man;” others, “No! He is leading the people astray.”'),
(995088,34,43,7,13,'No one, however, spoke freely about him, because they were afraid of the authorities.'),
(995089,34,43,7,14,'About the middle of the Festival week, Jesus went up into the Temple Courts, and began teaching.'),
(995090,34,43,7,15,'The authorities were astonished. ‘How has this man got his learning,’ they asked, ‘when he has never studied?’'),
(995091,34,43,7,16,'So, in reply, Jesus said,'),
(995092,34,43,7,20,'‘You must be possessed by a demon!’ the people exclaimed. ‘Who is seeking to put you to death?’'),
(995093,34,43,7,25,'At this some of the people of Jerusalem exclaimed, ‘Is not this the man who they are seeking to put to death?'),
(995094,34,43,7,26,'Yet here he is, speaking out boldly, and they say nothing to him! Is it possible that our leading men have really discovered that he is the Christ?'),
(995095,34,43,7,27,'Yet we know where this man is from; but, when the Christ comes, no one will be able to tell where he is from.’'),
(995096,34,43,7,28,'Therefore, Jesus, as he was teaching in the Temple Courts, raised his voice and said,'),
(995097,34,43,7,30,'So they sought to arrest him; but no one touched him, for his time was not come yet.'),
(995098,34,43,7,31,'Many of the people, however, believed in him. ‘When the Christ comes,’ they said, ‘will he give more signs of his mission than this man has given?’'),
(995099,34,43,7,32,'The Pharisees heard the people whispering about him in this way, and so the chief priests and the Pharisees sent officers to arrest him;'),
(995100,34,43,7,33,'at which Jesus said,'),
(995101,34,43,7,35,'‘Where is this man going,’ the people asked one another, ‘that we would not find him? Will he go to our countrymen abroad, and teach foreigners?'),
(995102,34,43,7,36,'What does he mean by saying'),
(995103,34,43,7,37,'On the last and greatest day of the Festival, Jesus, who was standing by, exclaimed,'),
(995104,34,43,7,39,'(By this he meant the Spirit, which those who had believed in him were to receive; for the Spirit had not yet come, because Jesus had not yet been exalted.)'),
(995105,34,43,7,40,'Some of the people, when they heard these words, said, ‘This is certainly the Prophet!’;'),
(995106,34,43,7,41,'others said, ‘the Christ!’; but some asked, ‘What! Does the Christ come from Galilee?'),
(995107,34,43,7,42,'Is not it said in scripture that it is of the descendants of David, and from Bethlehem, the village to which David belonged, that the Christ is to come?’'),
(995108,34,43,7,43,'So there was a sharp division among the people because of Jesus.'),
(995109,34,43,7,44,'Some of them wanted to arrest him, and yet no one touched him.'),
(995110,34,43,7,45,'When the officers returned to the chief priests and Pharisees, they were asked, ‘Why have you not brought him?’'),
(995111,34,43,7,46,'‘No one ever spoke as he speaks!’ they answered.'),
(995112,34,43,7,47,'‘What! Have you been led astray too?’ the Pharisees replied.'),
(995113,34,43,7,48,'‘Have any of our leading men believed in him, or any of the Pharisees?'),
(995114,34,43,7,49,'As for these people who do not know the Law – they are cursed!’'),
(995115,34,43,7,50,'But one of their number, Nicodemus, who before this had been to see Jesus, said to them,'),
(995116,34,43,7,51,'‘Does our Law pass judgment on a person without first giving them a hearing, and finding out what they have been doing?’'),
(995117,34,43,7,52,'‘Are you also from Galilee?’ they retorted. ‘Search, and you will find that no prophet is to arise in Galilee!’'),
(995118,34,43,7,53,'And everyone went home'),
(995119,34,43,8,1,'except Jesus, who went to the Mount of Olives'),
(995120,34,43,8,2,'But he went again into the Temple Courts early in the morning, and all the people came to him; and he sat down and taught them.'),
(995121,34,43,8,3,'Presently, however, the Teachers of the Law and the Pharisees brought a woman who had been caught in adultery, and placed her in the middle of the Court,'),
(995122,34,43,8,4,'and said to Jesus, ‘Teacher, this woman was found in the act of adultery.'),
(995123,34,43,8,5,'Now Moses, in the Law, commanded us to stone such women to death; what do you say?’'),
(995124,34,43,8,6,'They said this to test him, in order to have a charge to bring against him. But Jesus stooped down, and wrote on the ground with his finger.'),
(995125,34,43,8,7,'However, as they continued asking him, he raised himself, and said, ‘Let the person among you who has never done wrong throw the first stone at her.’'),
(995126,34,43,8,8,'And again he stooped down, and wrote on the ground.'),
(995127,34,43,8,9,'When they heard that, they went out one by one, beginning with the eldest; and Jesus was left alone with the woman in the middle of the Court.'),
(995128,34,43,8,10,'Raising himself, Jesus said to her, ‘Woman, where are they? Did no one condemn you?’'),
(995129,34,43,8,11,'‘No one, Sir,’ she answered.'),
(995130,34,43,8,12,'Jesus again addressed the people.'),
(995131,34,43,8,13,'‘You are bearing testimony to yourself!’ exclaimed the Pharisees, ‘your testimony is not trustworthy.’'),
(995132,34,43,8,20,'These statements Jesus made in the Treasury, while teaching in the Temple Courts. Yet no one arrested him, for his time had not then come.'),
(995133,34,43,8,21,'Jesus again spoke to the people.'),
(995134,34,43,8,22,'‘Is he going to kill himself,’ the people exclaimed, ‘that he says –'),
(995135,34,43,8,25,'‘Who are you?’ they asked.'),
(995136,34,43,8,27,'They did not understand that he meant the Father.'),
(995137,34,43,8,28,'So Jesus added,'),
(995138,34,43,8,30,'While he was speaking in this way, many came to believe in him.'),
(995139,34,43,8,31,'So Jesus went on to say to those who had believed him,'),
(995140,34,43,8,33,'‘We are descendants of Abraham,’ was their answer, ‘and have never yet been in slavery to anyone. What do you mean by saying'),
(995141,34,43,8,39,'‘Our father is Abraham,’ was their answer.'),
(995142,34,43,8,48,'‘Aren’t we right, after all,’ replied the people, ‘in saying that you are a Samaritan, and are possessed by a demon?’'),
(995143,34,43,8,52,'‘Now we are sure that you are possessed by a demon,’ the people replied. ‘Abraham died, and so did the prophets; and yet you say'),
(995144,34,43,8,53,'Are you greater than our ancestor Abraham, who died? And the prophets died too. Whom do you make yourself out to be?’'),
(995145,34,43,8,57,'‘You are not fifty years old yet,’ the people exclaimed, ‘and have you seen Abraham?’'),
(995146,34,43,8,59,'At this they took up stones to throw at him; but Jesus hid himself, and left the Temple Courts.'),
(995147,34,43,9,1,'As Jesus passed by, he saw a man who had been blind from his birth.'),
(995148,34,43,9,2,'‘Rabbi,’ asked his disciples, ‘who was it that sinned, this man or his parents, that he was born blind?’'),
(995149,34,43,9,6,'Saying this, Jesus spat on the ground, made clay with the saliva, and put it on the man’s eyes.'),
(995150,34,43,9,8,'His neighbours, and those who had formerly known him by sight as a beggar, exclaimed, ‘Is not this the man who used to sit and beg?’'),
(995151,34,43,9,9,'‘Yes,’ some said, ‘it is’; while others said, ‘No, but he is like him.’ The man himself said, ‘I am he.’'),
(995152,34,43,9,10,'‘How did you get your sight, then?’ they asked.'),
(995153,34,43,9,11,'‘The man whom they call Jesus,’ he answered, ‘made clay, and anointed my eyes, and said to me'),
(995154,34,43,9,12,'‘Where is he?’ they asked. ‘I do not know,’ he answered.'),
(995155,34,43,9,13,'They took the man, who had been blind, to the Pharisees.'),
(995156,34,43,9,14,'Now it was a Sabbath when Jesus made the clay and gave him his sight.'),
(995157,34,43,9,15,'So the Pharisees also questioned the man as to how he had gained his sight. ‘He put clay on my eyes,’ he answered, ‘and I washed them, and I can see.’'),
(995158,34,43,9,16,'‘The man cannot be from God,’ said some of the Pharisees, ‘for he does not keep the Sabbath.’'),
(995159,34,43,9,17,'So there was a difference of opinion among them, and they again questioned the man. ‘What do you yourself say about him, for it is to you that he has given sight?’'),
(995160,34,43,9,18,'The religious authorities, however, refused to believe that he had been blind and had gained his sight, until they had called his parents and questioned them.'),
(995161,34,43,9,19,'‘Is this your son,’ they asked, ‘who you say was born blind? If so, how is it that he can see now?’'),
(995162,34,43,9,20,'‘We know that this is our son,’ answered the parents, ‘and that he was born blind;'),
(995163,34,43,9,21,'but how it is that he can see now we do not know; nor do we know who it was that gave him his sight. Ask him – he is old enough – he will tell you about himself.’'),
(995164,34,43,9,22,'His parents spoke in this way because they were afraid of the authorities; for the authorities had already agreed that, if anyone should acknowledge Jesus as the Christ, he should be expelled from their synagogues.'),
(995165,34,43,9,23,'This was why his parents said “He is old enough; ask him.”'),
(995166,34,43,9,24,'So the authorities again called the man who had been blind, and said to him, ‘Give God the praise; we know that this is a bad man.’'),
(995167,34,43,9,25,'‘I know nothing about his being a bad man,’ he replied. ‘One thing I do know, that although I was blind, now I can see.’'),
(995168,34,43,9,26,'‘What did he do to you?’ they asked. ‘How did he give you your sight?’'),
(995169,34,43,9,27,'‘I told you just now,’ he answered, ‘and you did not listen. Why do you want to hear it again? Surely you also do not want to become his disciples?’'),
(995170,34,43,9,28,'‘You are his disciple,’ they retorted scornfully. ‘But we are disciples of Moses.'),
(995171,34,43,9,29,'We know that God spoke to Moses; but, as for this man, we do not know where he comes from.’'),
(995172,34,43,9,30,'‘Well,’ the man replied, ‘this is very strange; you do not know where he comes from, and yet he has given me my sight!'),
(995173,34,43,9,31,'We know that God never listens to bad people, but, when a person is god-fearing and does God’s will, God listens to them.'),
(995174,34,43,9,32,'Since the world began, such a thing was never heard of as anyone’s giving sight to a person born blind.'),
(995175,34,43,9,33,'If this man had not been from God, he could not have done anything at all.’'),
(995176,34,43,9,34,'‘You,’ they retorted, ‘were born totally depraved; and are you trying to teach us?’ So they expelled him.'),
(995177,34,43,9,35,'Jesus heard of their having put him out; and, when he had found the man, he asked,'),
(995178,34,43,9,36,'‘Tell me who he is, Sir,’ he replied, ‘so that I may believe in him.’'),
(995179,34,43,9,38,'‘Then, Sir, I do believe,’ said the man, bowing to the ground before him;'),
(995180,34,43,9,39,'and Jesus added,'),
(995181,34,43,9,40,'Hearing this, some of the Pharisees who were with him said, ‘Then are we blind too?’'),
(995182,34,43,10,6,'This was the allegory that Jesus told them, but they did not understand of what he was speaking.'),
(995183,34,43,10,7,'So he continued,'),
(995184,34,43,10,19,'In consequence of these words a difference of opinion again arose among the people.'),
(995185,34,43,10,20,'Many of them said, ‘He is possessed by a demon and is mad; why do you listen to him?’'),
(995186,34,43,10,21,'Others said, ‘This is not the teaching of one who is possessed by a demon. Can a demon give sight to the blind?’'),
(995187,34,43,10,22,'Soon after this the Festival of the Rededication was held at Jerusalem.'),
(995188,34,43,10,23,'It was winter; and Jesus was walking in the Temple Courts, in the Colonnade of Solomon,'),
(995189,34,43,10,24,'when the people gathered round him, and said, ‘How long are you going to keep us in suspense? If you are the Christ, tell us so frankly.’'),
(995190,34,43,10,31,'Some of the people again brought stones to throw at him;'),
(995191,34,43,10,32,'and seeing this, Jesus said,'),
(995192,34,43,10,33,'‘It is not for any good action that we would stone you,’ they answered, ‘but for blasphemy; and because you, who are only a man, make yourself out to be God.’'),
(995193,34,43,10,39,'The authorities again sought to arrest him; but he escaped their hands.'),
(995194,34,43,10,40,'Then Jesus again crossed the Jordan to the place where John used to baptize at first, and stayed there some time, during which many people came to see him.'),
(995195,34,43,10,41,'‘John gave no sign of his mission,’ they said. ‘But everything that he said about this man was true.’'),
(995196,34,43,10,42,'And many learned to believe in Jesus there.'),
(995197,34,43,11,1,'Now a man named Lazarus, of Bethany, was lying ill; he belonged to the same village as Mary and her sister Martha.'),
(995198,34,43,11,2,'This Mary, whose brother Lazarus was ill, was the Mary who anointed the Master with perfume, and wiped his feet with her hair.'),
(995199,34,43,11,3,'The sisters, therefore, sent this message to Jesus – “Master, your friend is ill”;'),
(995200,34,43,11,4,'and, when Jesus heard it, he said,'),
(995201,34,43,11,5,'Jesus loved Martha and her sister, and Lazarus.'),
(995202,34,43,11,6,'Yet, when he heard of the illness of Lazarus, he still stayed two days in the place where he was.'),
(995203,34,43,11,7,'Then, after that, he said to his disciples,'),
(995204,34,43,11,8,'‘Rabbi,’ they replied, ‘the authorities there were but just now seeking to stone you; and are you going there again?’'),
(995205,34,43,11,11,'And, when he had said this, he added,'),
(995206,34,43,11,12,'‘If he has fallen asleep, Master, he will get well,’ said the disciples.'),
(995207,34,43,11,13,'But Jesus meant that he was dead; they, however, supposed that he was speaking of natural sleep.'),
(995208,34,43,11,14,'Then he said to them plainly,'),
(995209,34,43,11,16,'At this, Thomas, who was called “The Twin,” said to his fellow disciples, ‘Let us go too, so that we may die with him.’'),
(995210,34,43,11,17,'When Jesus reached the place, he found that Lazarus had been four days in the tomb already.'),
(995211,34,43,11,18,'Bethany being only about two miles from Jerusalem,'),
(995212,34,43,11,19,'a number of the people had come there to comfort Martha and Mary because of brother’s death.'),
(995213,34,43,11,20,'When Martha heard that Jesus was coming, she went to meet him; but Mary sat quietly at home.'),
(995214,34,43,11,21,'‘Master,’ Martha said to Jesus, ‘if you had been here, my brother would not have died.'),
(995215,34,43,11,22,'Even now, I know that God will grant you whatever you ask him.’'),
(995216,34,43,11,24,'‘I know that he will,’ replied Martha, ‘in the resurrection at the Last day.’'),
(995217,34,43,11,27,'‘Yes Master,’ she answered. ‘I have learned to believe that you are the Christ, the Son of God, who was to come into the world.’'),
(995218,34,43,11,28,'After saying this, Martha went and called her sister Mary, and whispered, ‘The teacher is here, and is asking for you.’'),
(995219,34,43,11,29,'As soon as Mary heard that, she got up quickly, and went to meet him.'),
(995220,34,43,11,30,'Jesus had not then come into the village, but was still at the place where Martha had met him.'),
(995221,34,43,11,31,'So the people, who were in the house with Mary, comforting her, when they saw her get up quickly and go out, followed her, thinking that she was going to the tomb to weep there.'),
(995222,34,43,11,32,'When Mary came where Jesus was and saw him, she threw herself at his feet. ‘Master,’ she exclaimed, ‘if you had been here, my brother would not have died!’'),
(995223,34,43,11,33,'When Jesus saw her weeping, and the people who had come with her weeping also, he groaned deeply, and was greatly distressed.'),
(995224,34,43,11,35,'Jesus burst into tears.'),
(995225,34,43,11,36,'‘How he must have loved him!’ the people exclaimed;'),
(995226,34,43,11,37,'but some of them said, ‘Could not this man, who gave sight to the blind man, have also prevented Lazarus from dying?’'),
(995227,34,43,11,38,'Again groaning inwardly, Jesus came to the tomb. It was a cave, and a stone lay against the mouth of it.'),
(995228,34,43,11,41,'So they moved the stone away; and Jesus, with uplifted eyes, said,'),
(995229,34,43,11,43,'Then, after saying this, Jesus called in a loud voice,'),
(995230,34,43,11,44,'The dead man came out, wrapped hand and foot in a winding-sheet; his face, too, had been wrapped in a cloth.'),
(995231,34,43,11,45,'In consequence of this, many of the people, who had come to visit Mary and had seen what Jesus did, learned to believe in him.'),
(995232,34,43,11,46,'Some of them, however, went to the Pharisees, and told them what he had done.'),
(995233,34,43,11,47,'The chief priests and the Pharisees called a meeting of the High Council, and said, ‘What are we to do, now that this man is giving so many signs?'),
(995234,34,43,11,48,'If we allow him to continue as we are doing, everyone will believe in him; and the Romans will come and will take from us both our city and our Nationality.’'),
(995235,34,43,11,49,'One of them, however, Caiaphas, who was high priest that year, said to them,'),
(995236,34,43,11,50,'‘You are utterly mistaken. You do not consider that it is better for you that one person should die for the people, rather than the whole nation should be destroyed.’'),
(995237,34,43,11,51,'Now he did not say this of his own accord; but, as high priest that year, he prophesied that Jesus was to die for the nation –'),
(995238,34,43,11,52,'And not for the nation only, but also that he might unite in one body the children of God now scattered far and wide.'),
(995239,34,43,11,53,'So from that day they plotted to put Jesus to death.'),
(995240,34,43,11,54,'In consequence of this, Jesus did not go about publicly among the people any more, but left and went into the country bordering on the wilderness, to a town called Ephraim, where he stayed with his disciples.'),
(995241,34,43,11,55,'But the Jewish Festival of the Passover was near; and many people had gone up from the country to Jerusalem, for their purification, before the Festival began.'),
(995242,34,43,11,56,'So they looked for Jesus there, and said to one another, as they stood in the Temple Courts, ‘What do you think? Do you think he will come to the Festival?’'),
(995243,34,43,11,57,'The chief priests and the Pharisees had already issued orders that, if anyone learned where Jesus was, he should give information, so that they might arrest him.'),
(995244,34,43,12,1,'Six days before the Passover Jesus came to Bethany, where Lazarus, whom he had raised from the dead, was living.'),
(995245,34,43,12,2,'There a supper was given in honour at which Martha waited, while Lazarus was one of those present at the table.'),
(995246,34,43,12,3,'So Mary took a pound of choice spikenard perfume of great value, and anointed the feet of Jesus with it, and then wiped them with her hair. The whole house was filled with the scent of the perfume.'),
(995247,34,43,12,4,'One of the disciples, Judas Iscariot, who was about to betray Jesus, asked,'),
(995248,34,43,12,5,'‘Why was not this perfume sold for a year’s wages, and the money given to poor people?’'),
(995249,34,43,12,6,'He said this, not because he cared for the poor, but because he was a thief, and, being in charge of the purse, used to take what was put in it.'),
(995250,34,43,12,9,'Now great numbers of people found out that Jesus was at Bethany; and they came there, not only because of him, but also to see Lazarus, whom he had raised from the dead.'),
(995251,34,43,12,10,'The chief priests, however, plotted to put Lazarus, as well as Jesus, to death,'),
(995252,34,43,12,11,'because it was owing to him that many of the people had left them, and were becoming believers in Jesus.'),
(995253,34,43,12,12,'On the following day great numbers of people who had come to the Festival, hearing that Jesus was on his way to Jerusalem, took palm branches,'),
(995254,34,43,12,13,'and went out to meet him, shouting as they went, ‘God save Him! Blessed is He who Comes in the name of the Lord – The king of Israel!’'),
(995255,34,43,12,14,'Having found a young ass, Jesus seated himself on it, in accordance with the passage of scripture –'),
(995256,34,43,12,15,'“Fear not, people of Zion; Your king is coming to you, Sitting on the foal of an ass.”'),
(995257,34,43,12,16,'His disciples did not understand all this at first; but, when Jesus had been exalted, then they remembered that these things had been said of him in scripture, and that they had done these things for him.'),
(995258,34,43,12,17,'Meanwhile the people who were with him, when he called Lazarus out of the tomb and raised him from the dead, were telling what they had seen.'),
(995259,34,43,12,18,'This, indeed, was why the crowd met him – because people had heard that he had given this sign of his mission.'),
(995260,34,43,12,19,'So the Pharisees said to one another, ‘You see that you are gaining nothing! Why, all the world has run after him!’'),
(995261,34,43,12,20,'Among those who were going up to worship at the Festival were some Greeks,'),
(995262,34,43,12,21,'who went to Philip of Bethsaida in Galilee, and said, ‘Sir, we wish to see Jesus.’'),
(995263,34,43,12,22,'Philip went and told Andrew, and then together they went and told Jesus.'),
(995264,34,43,12,23,'This was his reply –'),
(995265,34,43,12,29,'The crowd of bystanders, who heard the sound, said that it was thundering. Others said, ‘An angel has been speaking to him.’'),
(995266,34,43,12,33,'By these words he indicated what death he was destined to die.'),
(995267,34,43,12,34,'‘We,’ replied the people, ‘have learned from the Law that the Christ is to remain for ever; how is it, then, that you say that the Son of Man must be'),
(995268,34,43,12,37,'But, though Jesus had given so many signs of his mission before their eyes, they still did not believe in him,'),
(995269,34,43,12,38,'in fulfilment of the words of the prophet Isaiah, where he says – “Lord, who has believed our teaching? And to whom has the might of the Lord been revealed?”'),
(995270,34,43,12,39,'The reason why they were unable to believe is given by Isaiah elsewhere, in these words –'),
(995271,34,43,12,40,'“He has blinded their eyes, and blunted their mind, so that they should not see with their eyes, and perceive with their mind, and turn – And I should heal them.”'),
(995272,34,43,12,41,'Isaiah said this, because he saw Christ’s glory; and it was of him that he spoke.'),
(995273,34,43,12,42,'Yet for all this, even among the leading men there were many who came to believe in Jesus; but, because of the Pharisees, they did not acknowledge it, because they were afraid that they should be expelled from their synagogues;'),
(995274,34,43,12,43,'for they valued honour from people more than honour from God.'),
(995275,34,43,12,44,'But Jesus had proclaimed,'),
(995276,34,43,13,1,'Before the Passover Festival began, Jesus knew that the time had come for him to leave the world and go to the Father. He had loved those who were his own in the world, and he loved them to the last.'),
(995277,34,43,13,2,'The devil had already put the thought of betraying Jesus into the mind of Judas Iscariot, the son of Simon;'),
(995278,34,43,13,3,'and at supper, Jesus – although knowing that the Father had put everything into his hands, and that he had come from God, and was to return to God –'),
(995279,34,43,13,4,'Rose from his place, and, taking off his upper garments, tied a towel round his waist.'),
(995280,34,43,13,5,'He then poured some water into the basin, and began to wash the disciples’ feet, and to wipe them with the towel which was tied round him.'),
(995281,34,43,13,6,'When he came to Simon Peter, Peter said, ‘You, Master! Are you going to wash my feet?’'),
(995282,34,43,13,8,'‘You will never wash my feet!’ exclaimed Peter.'),
(995283,34,43,13,9,'‘Then, Master, not my feet only,’ exclaimed Simon Peter, ‘but also my hands and my head.’'),
(995284,34,43,13,11,'For he knew who was going to betray him, and that was why he said'),
(995285,34,43,13,12,'When he had washed their feet, and had put on his upper garments and taken his place, he spoke to them again.'),
(995286,34,43,13,21,'After saying this, Jesus was much troubled, and said solemnly,'),
(995287,34,43,13,22,'The disciples looked at one another, wondering whom he meant.'),
(995288,34,43,13,23,'Next to Jesus, in the place on his right hand, was one of his disciples, whom he loved.'),
(995289,34,43,13,24,'So Simon Peter made signs to that disciple, and whispered, ‘Tell me who it is that he means.’'),
(995290,34,43,13,25,'Being in this position, that disciple leant back on Jesus’ shoulder, and asked him, ‘Who is it, Master?’'),
(995291,34,43,13,27,'and it was then, after he had received it, that Satan took possession of him. So Jesus said to him,'),
(995292,34,43,13,28,'But no one at the table understood why he said this to Judas.'),
(995293,34,43,13,29,'Some thought that, as Judas kept the purse, Jesus meant that he was to buy some things needed for the Festival, or to give something to the poor.'),
(995294,34,43,13,30,'After taking the piece of bread, Judas went out immediately; and it was night.'),
(995295,34,43,13,31,'When Judas had gone out, Jesus said,'),
(995296,34,43,13,36,'‘Where are you going, Master?’ asked Peter.'),
(995297,34,43,13,37,'‘Why cannot I follow you now, Master?’ asked Peter. ‘I will lay down my life for you.’'),
(995298,34,43,14,5,'‘We do not know where you are going, Master,’ said Thomas. ‘So how can we know the way?’'),
(995299,34,43,14,6,'Jesus answered,'),
(995300,34,43,14,8,'‘Master, show us the Father,’ said Philip, ‘and we will be satisfied.’'),
(995301,34,43,14,22,'‘What has happened, Master,’ said Judas (not Judas Iscariot), ‘that you are going to reveal yourself to us, and not to the world?’'),
(995302,34,43,16,1,'‘I have spoken to you in this way so that you may not falter.'),
(995303,34,43,16,17,'At this some of his disciples said to one another, ‘What does he mean by saying to us'),
(995304,34,43,16,18,'What does he mean by'),
(995305,34,43,16,19,'Jesus saw that they were wanting to ask him a question, and said,'),
(995306,34,43,16,29,'‘At last,’ exclaimed the disciples, ‘you are using plain words and not speaking in figures at all.'),
(995307,34,43,16,30,'Now we are sure that you know everything, and need not wait for anyone to question you. This makes us believe that you did come from God.’'),
(995308,34,43,17,1,'After saying this, Jesus raised his eyes heaven-wards, and said:'),
(995309,34,43,18,1,'When Jesus had said this, he went out with his disciples and crossed the brook Kedron to a place where there was a garden, into which he and his disciples went.'),
(995310,34,43,18,2,'The place was well known to Judas, the betrayer, for Jesus and his disciples had often met there.'),
(995311,34,43,18,3,'So Judas, who had obtained the soldiers of the Roman garrison, and some police officers from the chief priests and the Pharisees, came there with lanterns, torches, and weapons.'),
(995312,34,43,18,4,'Jesus, aware of all that was coming upon him, went to meet them, and said to them,'),
(995313,34,43,18,5,'‘Jesus of Nazareth,’ was their answer.'),
(995314,34,43,18,6,'When Jesus said'),
(995315,34,43,18,7,'So he again asked for whom they were looking, and they answered, ‘Jesus of Nazareth.’'),
(995316,34,43,18,9,'This was in fulfilment of his words –'),
(995317,34,43,18,10,'At this, Simon Peter, who had a sword with him, drew it, and struck the high priest’s servant, and cut off his right ear. The servant’s name was Malchus.'),
(995318,34,43,18,11,'But Jesus said to Peter,'),
(995319,34,43,18,12,'So the soldiers of the garrison, with their commanding officer and the Jewish police, arrested Jesus and bound him,'),
(995320,34,43,18,13,'and took him first of all to Annas. Annas was the father-in-law of Caiaphas, who was high priest that year.'),
(995321,34,43,18,14,'It was Caiaphas who had counselled the religious authorities, that it was best that one person should die for the people.'),
(995322,34,43,18,15,'Meanwhile Simon Peter followed Jesus, and so did another disciple. That disciple, being well-known to the high priest, went with Jesus into the high priest’s courtyard,'),
(995323,34,43,18,16,'while Peter stood outside by the door. Presently the other disciple – the one well-known to the high priest – went out and spoke to the portress, and brought Peter in.'),
(995324,34,43,18,17,'So the maidservant said to Peter, ‘Aren’t you also one of this man’s disciples?’'),
(995325,34,43,18,18,'The servants and police officers were standing round a charcoal fire (which they had made because it was cold), and were warming themselves. Peter, too, was with them, standing and warming himself.'),
(995326,34,43,18,19,'The high priest questioned Jesus about his disciples and about his teaching.'),
(995327,34,43,18,22,'When Jesus said this, one of the police officers, who was standing near, gave him a blow with his hand. ‘Do you answer the high priest like that?’ he exclaimed.'),
(995328,34,43,18,24,'Annas sent him bound to Caiaphas the high priest.'),
(995329,34,43,18,25,'Meanwhile Simon Peter was standing there, warming himself; so they said to him, ‘Aren’t you also one of his disciples?’ Peter denied it. ‘No, I am not,’ he said.'),
(995330,34,43,18,26,'One of the high priest’s servants, a relation of the man whose ear Peter had cut off, exclaimed, ‘Didn’t I myself see you with him in the garden?’'),
(995331,34,43,18,27,'Peter again denied it; and at that moment a cock crowed.'),
(995332,34,43,18,28,'From Caiaphas they took Jesus to the Government house. It was early in the morning. But they did not enter the Government house themselves, otherwise they might become defiled, and so be unable to eat the Passover.'),
(995333,34,43,18,29,'Therefore Pilate came outside to speak to them. ‘What charge do you bring against this man?’ he asked.'),
(995334,34,43,18,30,'‘If he had not been a criminal, we should not have given him up to you,’ they answered.'),
(995335,34,43,18,31,'‘Take him yourselves,’ said Pilate, ‘and try him by your own Law.’'),
(995336,34,43,18,32,'In fulfilment of what Jesus had said when indicating the death that he was destined to die.'),
(995337,34,43,18,33,'After that, Pilate went into the Government house again, and calling Jesus up, asked him, ‘Are you the king of the Jews?’'),
(995338,34,43,18,35,'‘Do you take me for a Jew?’ was Pilate’s answer. ‘It is your own nation and the chief priests who have given you up to me. What have you done?’'),
(995339,34,43,18,37,'‘So you are a king after all!’ exclaimed Pilate.'),
(995340,34,43,18,38,'‘What is truth?’ exclaimed Pilate. After saying this, he went out to the crowd again, and said, ‘For my part, I find nothing with which he can be charged.'),
(995341,34,43,18,39,'It is, however, the custom for me to grant you the release of one man at the Passover Festival. Do you wish for the release of the king of the Jews?’'),
(995342,34,43,18,40,'‘No, not this man,’ they shouted again, ‘but Barabbas!’ This Barabbas was a robber.'),
(995343,34,43,19,1,'After that, Pilate had Jesus scourged.'),
(995344,34,43,19,2,'The soldiers made a crown with some thorns and put it on his head and threw a purple robe round him.'),
(995345,34,43,19,3,'They kept coming up to him and saying, ‘Long live the king of the Jews!’ and they gave him blow after blow with their hands.'),
(995346,34,43,19,4,'Pilate again came outside, and said to the people, ‘Look! I am bringing him out to you, so that you may know that I find nothing with which he can be charged.’'),
(995347,34,43,19,5,'Then Jesus came outside, wearing the crown of thorns and the purple robe; and Pilate said to them, ‘Here is the man!’'),
(995348,34,43,19,6,'When the chief priests and the police officers saw him, they shouted, ‘Crucify him! Crucify him!’'),
(995349,34,43,19,7,'‘But we,’ replied the crowd, ‘have a Law, under which he deserves death for making himself out to be the Son of God.’'),
(995350,34,43,19,8,'When Pilate heard what they said, he became still more alarmed;'),
(995351,34,43,19,9,'and, going into the Government house again, he said to Jesus, ‘Where do you come from?’'),
(995352,34,43,19,10,'But Jesus made no reply. So Pilate said to him, ‘Do you refuse to speak to me? Don’t you know that I have power to release you, and have power to crucify you?’'),
(995353,34,43,19,12,'This made Pilate anxious to release him; but the crowd shouted, ‘If you release that man, you are no friend of the Emperor! Anyone who makes himself out to be a king is setting himself against the Emperor!’'),
(995354,34,43,19,13,'On hearing what they said, Pilate brought Jesus out, and took his seat on the Bench at a place called “The Stone Pavement” – in Hebrew “Gabbatha.”'),
(995355,34,43,19,14,'It was the Passover Preparation day, and about noon. Then he said to the crowd, ‘Here is your king!’'),
(995356,34,43,19,15,'At that the people shouted, ‘Kill him! Kill him! Crucify him!’'),
(995357,34,43,19,16,'so Pilate gave Jesus up to them to be crucified.'),
(995358,34,43,19,17,'and he went out, carrying his cross himself, to the place which is named from a scull, or, in Hebrew, Golgotha.'),
(995359,34,43,19,18,'There they crucified him, and two others with him – one on each side, and Jesus between them.'),
(995360,34,43,19,19,'Pilate also had these words written and put up over the cross – “JESUS OF NAZARETH, THE KING OF THE JEWS.”'),
(995361,34,43,19,20,'These words were read by many people, because the place where Jesus was crucified was near the city; and they were written in Hebrew, Latin and Greek.'),
(995362,34,43,19,21,'The chief priests said to Pilate, ‘Do not write “The king of the Jews”, but write what the man said – “I am the king of the Jews.”’'),
(995363,34,43,19,22,'But Pilate answered, ‘What I have written, I have written.’'),
(995364,34,43,19,23,'When the soldiers had crucified Jesus, they took his clothes and divided them into four shares – a share for each soldier – and they took the coat also. The coat had no seam, being woven in one piece from top to bottom.'),
(995365,34,43,19,24,'So they said to one another, ‘Do not let us tear it, but let us cast lots for it, to see who will have it.’ This was in fulfilment of the words of scripture –'),
(995366,34,43,19,25,'Meanwhile near the cross of Jesus were standing his mother and his mother’s sister, as well as Mary the wife of Clopas and Mary of Magdala.'),
(995367,34,43,19,26,'When Jesus saw his mother, and the disciple whom he loved, standing near, he said to his mother,'),
(995368,34,43,19,27,'Then he said to that disciple,'),
(995369,34,43,19,28,'Afterwards, knowing that everything was now finished, Jesus said, in fulfilment of the words of scripture,'),
(995370,34,43,19,29,'There was a bowl standing there full of common wine; so they put a sponge soaked in the wine on the end of a hyssop-stalk, and held it up to his mouth.'),
(995371,34,43,19,30,'When Jesus had received the wine, he exclaimed,'),
(995372,34,43,19,31,'It was the Preparation day, and so, to prevent the bodies from remaining on the crosses during the Sabbath (for that Sabbath was a great day), the Jews asked Pilate to have the legs broken and the bodies removed.'),
(995373,34,43,19,32,'Accordingly the soldiers came and broke the legs of the first man, and then those of the other who had been crucified with Jesus;'),
(995374,34,43,19,33,'but, on coming to him, when they saw that he was already dead, they did not break his legs.'),
(995375,34,43,19,34,'One of the soldiers, however, pierced his side with a spear, and blood and water immediately flowed from it.'),
(995376,34,43,19,35,'This is the statement of one who actually saw it – and his statement may be relied on, and he knows that he is speaking the truth – and it is given in order that you also may be convinced.'),
(995377,34,43,19,36,'For all this happened in fulfilment of the words of scripture – “Not one of its bones will be broken.”'),
(995378,34,43,19,37,'And there is another passage which says – “They will look on him whom they pierced.”'),
(995379,34,43,19,38,'After this, Joseph of Ramah, a disciple of Jesus – but a secret one, owing to his fear of the religious authorities – begged Pilate’s permission to remove the body of Jesus. Pilate gave him leave; so Joseph went and removed the body.'),
(995380,34,43,19,39,'Nicodemus, too – the man who had formerly visited Jesus by night – came with a roll of myrrh and aloes, weighing nearly a hundred pounds.'),
(995381,34,43,19,40,'They took the body of Jesus, and wound it in linen with the spices, according to the Jewish mode of burial.'),
(995382,34,43,19,41,'At the place where Jesus had been crucified there was a garden, and in the garden a newly made tomb in which no one had ever been laid.'),
(995383,34,43,19,42,'And so, because of its being the Preparation day, and as the tomb was close at hand, they laid Jesus there.'),
(995384,34,43,20,1,'On the first day of the week, early in the morning, while it was still dark, Mary of Magdala went to the tomb, and saw that the stone had been removed.'),
(995385,34,43,20,2,'So she came running to Simon Peter, and to that other disciple who was Jesus’ friend, and said to them, ‘They have taken away the Master out of the tomb, and we do not know where they have laid him!’'),
(995386,34,43,20,3,'So, Peter started off with that other disciple, and they went to the tomb.'),
(995387,34,43,20,4,'The two began running together; but the other disciple ran faster than Peter, and reached the tomb first.'),
(995388,34,43,20,5,'Stooping down, he saw the linen wrappings lying there, but did not go in.'),
(995389,34,43,20,6,'Presently Simon Peter came following behind him, and went into the tomb; and he looked at the linen wrappings lying there,'),
(995390,34,43,20,7,'and the cloth which had been on Jesus’ head, not lying with the wrappings, but rolled up on one side, separately.'),
(995391,34,43,20,8,'Then the other disciple, who had reached the tomb first, went inside too, and he saw for himself and was convinced.'),
(995392,34,43,20,9,'For they did not then understand the passage of scripture which says that Jesus must rise again from the dead.'),
(995393,34,43,20,10,'The disciples then returned to their companions.'),
(995394,34,43,20,11,'Meanwhile Mary was standing close outside the tomb, weeping. Still weeping, she leant forward into the tomb,'),
(995395,34,43,20,12,'and perceived two angels clothed in white sitting there, where the body of Jesus had been lying, one where the head and the other where the feet had been.'),
(995396,34,43,20,13,'‘Why are you weeping?’ asked the angels. ‘They have taken my Master away,’ she answered, ‘and I do not know where they have laid him.’'),
(995397,34,43,20,14,'After saying this, she turned round, and looked at Jesus standing there, but she did not know that it was Jesus.'),
(995398,34,43,20,18,'Mary of Magdala went and told the disciples that she had seen the Master, and that he had said this to her.'),
(995399,34,43,20,19,'In the evening of the same day – the first day of the week – after the doors of the room, in which the disciples were, had been shut because they were afraid of the religious authorities, Jesus came and stood among them and said,'),
(995400,34,43,20,20,'after which he showed them his hands and his side. The disciples were filled with joy when they saw the Master.'),
(995401,34,43,20,21,'Again Jesus said to them,'),
(995402,34,43,20,22,'After saying this, he breathed on them, and said,'),
(995403,34,43,20,24,'But Thomas, one of the Twelve, called “The Twin,” was not with them when Jesus came;'),
(995404,34,43,20,25,'so the rest of the disciples said to him, ‘We have seen the Master!’'),
(995405,34,43,20,26,'A week later the disciples were again in the house, and Thomas with them. After the doors had been shut, Jesus came and stood among them, and said,'),
(995406,34,43,20,27,'Then he said to Thomas,'),
(995407,34,43,20,28,'And Thomas exclaimed, ‘My Master, and my God!’'),
(995408,34,43,20,30,'There were many other signs of his mission that Jesus gave in presence of the disciples, which are not recorded in this book;'),
(995409,34,43,20,31,'but these have been recorded so that you may believe that Jesus is the Christ, the Son of God – and that, through your belief in his name, you may have life.'),
(995410,34,43,21,1,'Later on, Jesus showed himself again to the disciples by the Sea of Tiberias.'),
(995411,34,43,21,2,'It was in this way, – Simon Peter, Thomas, who was called “The Twin,” Nathanael of Cana in Galilee, Zebedee’s sons, and two other disciples of Jesus, were together, when Simon Peter said,'),
(995412,34,43,21,3,'‘I am going fishing.’'),
(995413,34,43,21,4,'Just as day was breaking, Jesus came and stood on the beach; but the disciples did not know that it was he.'),
(995414,34,43,21,7,'The disciple whom Jesus loved said to Peter, ‘It is the Master!’ When Simon Peter heard that it was the Master, he fastened his coat round him (for he had taken it off), and threw himself into the sea.'),
(995415,34,43,21,8,'But the rest of the disciples came in the boat (for they were only about a hundred yards from shore), dragging the net full of fish.'),
(995416,34,43,21,9,'When they had come ashore, they found a charcoal fire ready, with some fish already on it, and some bread as well.'),
(995417,34,43,21,11,'So Simon Peter got into the boat and hauled the net ashore full of large fish, a hundred and fifty-three of them; and yet, although there were so many, the net had not been torn.'),
(995418,34,43,21,13,'Jesus went and took the bread and gave it to them, and the fish too.'),
(995419,34,43,21,14,'This was the third time that Jesus showed himself to the disciples after he had risen from the dead.'),
(995420,34,43,21,15,'When breakfast was over, Jesus said to Simon Peter,'),
(995421,34,43,21,16,'Then, a second time, Jesus asked,'),
(995422,34,43,21,17,'The third time, Jesus said to him,'),
(995423,34,43,21,19,'Jesus said this to show the death by which Peter was to honour God, and then he added,'),
(995424,34,43,21,20,'Peter turned round, and saw the disciple whom Jesus loved following – the one who at the supper leant back on the Master’s shoulder, and asked him who it was who would betray him.'),
(995425,34,43,21,21,'Seeing him, Peter said to Jesus, ‘Master, what about this man?’'),
(995426,34,43,21,23,'So the report spread among his followers that that disciple was not to die; yet Jesus did not say that he was not to die, but said'),
(995427,34,43,21,24,'It is this disciple who states these things, and who recorded them; and we know that his statement is true.'),
(995428,34,43,21,25,'There are many other things which Jesus did; but, if every one of them were to be recorded in detail, I suppose that even the world itself would not hold the books that would be written.'),
(995429,34,44,1,2,'down to that day on which he was taken up to heaven, after he had, by the help of the Holy Spirit, given instructions to the apostles whom he had chosen.'),
(995430,34,44,1,3,'With abundant proofs, he showed himself to them, still living, after his death; appearing to them from time to time during forty days, and speaking of all that related to the kingdom of God.'),
(995431,34,44,1,4,'And once, when he had gathered them together, he charged them not to leave Jerusalem, but to wait there for the fulfilment of the Father’s promise –'),
(995432,34,44,1,6,'So, when the apostles had met together, they asked Jesus this question – ‘Master, is this the time when you intend to re-establish the kingdom for Israel?’'),
(995433,34,44,1,7,'His answer was,'),
(995434,34,44,1,9,'No sooner had Jesus said this than he was caught up before their eyes, and a cloud received him from their sight.'),
(995435,34,44,1,10,'While they were still gazing up into the heavens, as he went, suddenly two men, clothed in white, stood beside them,'),
(995436,34,44,1,11,'and said, ‘People of Galilee, why are you standing here looking up into the heavens? This same Jesus, who has been taken from you into the heavens, will come in the same way in which you have seen him go into the heavens.’'),
(995437,34,44,1,12,'Then the apostles returned to Jerusalem from the hill called Olivet, which is about three quarters of a mile from the city.'),
(995438,34,44,1,13,'When they reached Jerusalem, they went to the upstairs room, where they were staying. There were there Peter, John, James, and Andrew, Philip and Thomas, Bartholomew and Matthew, James the son of Alphaeus, Simon the Zealot, and Judas the son of James.'),
(995439,34,44,1,14,'They all united in devoting themselves to prayer, and so did some women, and Mary, the mother of Jesus, and his brothers.'),
(995440,34,44,1,15,'About this time, at a meeting of the Lord’s followers, when there were about a hundred and twenty present, Peter rose to speak.'),
(995441,34,44,1,16,'‘Friends,’ he said, ‘it was necessary that the prediction of scripture should be fulfilled, which the Holy Spirit made by the lips of David about Judas, who acted as guide to the men who arrested Jesus,'),
(995442,34,44,1,17,'for he was one of our number and had his part allotted him in this work of ours.’'),
(995443,34,44,1,18,'(This man had bought a piece of land with the price of his treachery; and, falling heavily, his body had burst open, and all his bowels protruded.'),
(995444,34,44,1,19,'This became known to everyone living in Jerusalem, so that the field came to be called, in their language, “Akeldama,” which means the “Field of Blood.”)'),
(995445,34,44,1,20,'‘For in the book of Psalms,’ Peter continued, ‘it is said –'),
(995446,34,44,1,21,'Therefore, from among the men who have been with us all the time that Jesus, our Master, went in and out among us –'),
(995447,34,44,1,22,'from his baptism by John down to that day on which he was taken from us – someone must be found to join us as a witness of his resurrection.’'),
(995448,34,44,1,23,'So they put forward two men, Joseph called Barsabbas, whose other name was Justus, and Matthias;'),
(995449,34,44,1,24,'and they offered this prayer –'),
(995450,34,44,1,25,'to take the place in this apostolic work, which Judas has abandoned, to go to his proper place.’'),
(995451,34,44,1,26,'Then they drew lots between them; and, the lot having fallen to Matthias, he was added to the number of the eleven apostles.'),
(995452,34,44,2,1,'In the course of the Festival at the close of the Harvest the disciples had all met together,'),
(995453,34,44,2,2,'when suddenly there came from the heavens a noise like a strong wind rushing by; it filled the whole house in which they were sitting.'),
(995454,34,44,2,3,'Then there appeared tongues of what seemed to be flame, separating, so that one settled on each of them;'),
(995455,34,44,2,4,'and they were all filled with the Holy Spirit, and began to speak in different languages as the Spirit prompted their utterances.'),
(995456,34,44,2,5,'Now there were then staying in Jerusalem religious Jews from every country in the world;'),
(995457,34,44,2,6,'and, when this sound was heard, numbers of people collected, in the greatest excitement, because each of them heard the disciples speaking in his own language.'),
(995458,34,44,2,7,'They were utterly amazed, and kept asking in astonishment, ‘What! Are not all these people who are speaking Galileans?'),
(995459,34,44,2,8,'Then how is it that we each of us hear them in our own language?'),
(995460,34,44,2,9,'Some of us are Parthians, some Medes, some Elamites; and some of us live in Mesopotamia, in Judea and Cappadocia, in Pontus and Roman Asia,'),
(995461,34,44,2,10,'in Phrygia and Pamphylia, in Egypt and the districts of Libya adjoining Cyrene; some of us are visitors from Rome,'),
(995462,34,44,2,11,'either Jews by birth or converts, and some are Cretans and Arabians – yet we all alike hear them speaking in our own languages of the great things that God has done.’'),
(995463,34,44,2,12,'They were all utterly amazed and bewildered.'),
(995464,34,44,2,13,'But there were some who said with a sneer, ‘They have had too much new wine.’'),
(995465,34,44,2,14,'Then Peter, surrounded by the eleven other apostles, stood up, and, raising his voice, addressed the crowd. ‘People of Judea,’ he began, ‘and all you who are staying in Jerusalem, let me tell you what this means. Mark well my words.'),
(995466,34,44,2,15,'These people are not drunk, as you suppose; for it is only now nine in the morning! No!'),
(995467,34,44,2,16,'This is what is spoken of in the prophet Joel –'),
(995468,34,44,2,17,'“It will come about in the last days,” God says,'),
(995469,34,44,2,18,'yes, even on the slaves – for they are mine – both men and women,'),
(995470,34,44,2,19,'and I will show wonders in the heavens above,'),
(995471,34,44,2,20,'the sun will become darkness,'),
(995472,34,44,2,21,'Then will everyone who invokes the name of the Lord be saved.”'),
(995473,34,44,2,22,'People of Israel, listen to what I am saying. Jesus of Nazareth, a man whose mission from God to you was proved by miracles, wonders, and signs, which God showed among you through him, as you know full well –'),
(995474,34,44,2,23,'He, I say, in accordance with God’s definite plan and with his previous knowledge, was betrayed, and you, by the hands of lawless men, nailed him to a cross and put him to death.'),
(995475,34,44,2,24,'But God released him from the pangs of death and raised him to life, it being impossible for death to retain its hold on him.'),
(995476,34,44,2,25,'Indeed he was the one David was referring to when he said –'),
(995477,34,44,2,26,'Therefore my heart was cheered, and my tongue told its delight;'),
(995478,34,44,2,27,'For you will not abandon my soul to Hades,'),
(995479,34,44,2,28,'You have shown me the path to life,'),
(995480,34,44,2,29,'Friends, I can speak to you the more confidently about the patriarch David, because he is dead and buried, and his tomb is here among us to this very day.'),
(995481,34,44,2,30,'David, then, prophet as he was, knowing that God had solemnly sworn to him to set one of his descendants on his throne, looked into the future,'),
(995482,34,44,2,31,'and referred to the resurrection of the Christ when he said that he had not been abandoned to Hades, nor had his body undergone corruption.'),
(995483,34,44,2,32,'It was this Jesus, whom God raised to life; and of that we are ourselves all witnesses.'),
(995484,34,44,2,33,'And now that he has been exalted to the right hand of God, and has received from the Father the promised gift of the Holy Spirit, he has begun to pour out that gift, as you yourselves now see and hear.'),
(995485,34,44,2,34,'It was not David who went up into heaven; for he himself says –'),
(995486,34,44,2,35,'Until I put your enemies as a footstool under your feet.’”'),
(995487,34,44,2,36,'So let the whole nation of Israel know beyond all doubt, that God has made him both Lord and Christ – this Jesus whom you crucified.’'),
(995488,34,44,2,37,'When the people heard this, they were conscience-smitten, and said to Peter and the rest of the apostles, ‘Friends, what can we do?’'),
(995489,34,44,2,38,'‘Repent,’ answered Peter, ‘and be baptized every one of you in the name of Jesus Christ for the forgiveness of your sins; and then you will receive the gift of the Holy Spirit.'),
(995490,34,44,2,39,'For the promise is for you and for your children, and also for all those now far away, who may be called by the Lord our God.’'),
(995491,34,44,2,40,'Peter spoke to them for a long time using many other arguments and pleaded with them – ‘Save yourselves from the perverse spirit of this age.’'),
(995492,34,44,2,41,'So those who accepted his teaching were baptized, and about three thousand people joined the disciples on that day alone.'),
(995493,34,44,2,42,'They devoted themselves to the teaching of the apostles and to the Common life of the church, to the breaking of the bread and to the Prayers.'),
(995494,34,44,2,43,'A deep impression was made on everyone, and many wonders and signs were done at the hands of the apostles.'),
(995495,34,44,2,44,'All who became believers in Christ held everything for the common use;'),
(995496,34,44,2,45,'they sold their property and their goods, and shared the proceeds among them all, according to their individual needs.'),
(995497,34,44,2,46,'Every day they devoted themselves to meeting together in the Temple Courts, and to the breaking of bread at their homes, while they partook of their food in simple-hearted gladness, praising God, and winning the goodwill of all the people.'),
(995498,34,44,2,47,'And the Lord daily added to their company those who were in the path of salvation.'),
(995499,34,44,3,1,'One day, as Peter and John were going up into the Temple Courts for the three o’clock Prayers, a man, who had been lame from his birth, was being carried by.'),
(995500,34,44,3,2,'This man used to be set down every day at the gate of the Temple called “the Beautiful Gate,” to beg of those who went in.');
INSERT INTO verses (id, version_id, book_id, chapter, verse, text) VALUES
(995501,34,44,3,3,'Seeing Peter and John on the point of entering, he asked them to give him something.'),
(995502,34,44,3,4,'Peter fixed his eyes on him, and so did John, and then Peter said, ‘Look at us.’'),
(995503,34,44,3,5,'The man was all attention, expecting to get something from them;'),
(995504,34,44,3,6,'but Peter added, ‘I have no gold or silver, but I give you what I have. In the name of Jesus Christ of Nazareth, get up and walk.’'),
(995505,34,44,3,7,'Grasping the lame man by the right hand, Peter lifted him up. Instantly the man’s feet and ankles became strong,'),
(995506,34,44,3,8,'and, leaping up, he stood and began to walk about, and then went with them into the Temple Courts, walking, and leaping, and praising God.'),
(995507,34,44,3,9,'All the people saw him walking about and praising God;'),
(995508,34,44,3,10,'and, when they recognised him as the man who used to sit begging at the Beautiful Gate of the Temple, they were utterly astonished and amazed at what had happened to him.'),
(995509,34,44,3,11,'While the man still clung to Peter and John, the people all quickly gathered round them in the Colonnade named after Solomon, in the greatest astonishment.'),
(995510,34,44,3,12,'On seeing this, Peter said to the people, ‘People of Israel, why are you surprised at this? And why do you stare at us, as though we, by any power or piety of our own, had enabled this man to walk?'),
(995511,34,44,3,13,'The God of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, the God of our ancestors, has done honour to his servant Jesus – him whom you gave up and disowned before Pilate, when he had decided to set him free.'),
(995512,34,44,3,14,'You, I say, disowned the holy and righteous one, and asked for the release of a murderer!'),
(995513,34,44,3,15,'The guide to life you put to death! But God raised him from the dead – and of that we are ourselves witnesses.'),
(995514,34,44,3,16,'And it is by faith in the name of Jesus, that this man, whom you all see and know, has – by his name – been made strong. Yes, it is the faith inspired by Jesus that has made this complete cure of the man, before the eyes of you all.'),
(995515,34,44,3,17,'And yet, my friends, I know that you acted as you did from ignorance, and your rulers also.'),
(995516,34,44,3,18,'But it was in this way that God fulfilled all that he had long ago foretold, as to the sufferings of his Christ, by the lips of all the prophets.'),
(995517,34,44,3,19,'Therefore, repent and turn so that your sins may be wiped away; so that happier times may come from the Lord himself,'),
(995518,34,44,3,20,'and so that he may send you, in Jesus, your long-appointed Christ.'),
(995519,34,44,3,21,'But heaven must be his home, until the days of the Universal Restoration, of which God has spoken by the lips of his holy prophets from the very first.'),
(995520,34,44,3,22,'Moses himself said –'),
(995521,34,44,3,23,'And it will be that should anyone among the people not listen to that prophet, he will be utterly destroyed.”'),
(995522,34,44,3,24,'Yes, and all the prophets from Samuel onwards, and all their successors who had a message to deliver, told of these days.'),
(995523,34,44,3,25,'You yourselves are the heirs of the prophets, and heirs, too, of the covenant which God made with your ancestors, when he said to Abraham –'),
(995524,34,44,3,26,'For you, first, God raised up his servant, and sent him to bless you, by turning each one of you from his wicked ways.’'),
(995525,34,44,4,1,'While Peter and John were still speaking to the people, the chief priest, with the officer in charge at the Temple and the Sadducees, came up to them,'),
(995526,34,44,4,2,'much annoyed because they were teaching the people, and because, through Jesus, they were preaching the resurrection from the dead.'),
(995527,34,44,4,3,'They arrested the apostles and, as it was already evening, had them placed in custody until the next day.'),
(995528,34,44,4,4,'Many, however, of those who had heard the apostles’ message became believers in Christ, the number of the men alone amounting to about five thousand.'),
(995529,34,44,4,5,'The next day, a meeting of the leaders of the people, the elders, and the teachers of the Law was held in Jerusalem.'),
(995530,34,44,4,6,'There were present Annas the high priest, Caiaphas, John, Alexander, and all who were of High-Priestly rank.'),
(995531,34,44,4,7,'They had Peter and John brought before them, and questioned them.'),
(995532,34,44,4,8,'Then, Peter, filled with the Holy Spirit, said, ‘Leaders of the people and elders,'),
(995533,34,44,4,9,'since we are on our trial today for a kind act done to a helpless man, and are asked in what way the man here before you has been cured,'),
(995534,34,44,4,10,'let me tell you all and all the people of Israel, that it is by the name of Jesus Christ of Nazareth, whom you crucified and whom God raised from the dead – it is, I say, by his name that this man stands here before you lame no longer.'),
(995535,34,44,4,11,'Jesus is “the stone which, scorned by you the builders, has yet become the corner stone.”'),
(995536,34,44,4,12,'And salvation is in him alone; for there is no other name in the whole world, given to people, to which we must look for our salvation.’'),
(995537,34,44,4,13,'When the Council saw how boldly Peter and John spoke, and found that they were uneducated men of humble station, they were surprised, and realised that they had been companions of Jesus.'),
(995538,34,44,4,14,'But, when they looked at the man who had been healed, standing there with them, they had nothing to say.'),
(995539,34,44,4,15,'So they ordered them out of court, and then began consulting together.'),
(995540,34,44,4,16,'‘What are we to do to these men?’ they asked one another. ‘That a remarkable sign has been given through them is obvious to everyone living in Jerusalem, and we cannot deny it.'),
(995541,34,44,4,17,'But, to prevent this thing from spreading further among the people, let us warn them not to speak in this name any more to anyone whatever.’'),
(995542,34,44,4,18,'So they called the apostles in, and ordered them not to speak or teach in the name of Jesus.'),
(995543,34,44,4,19,'But Peter and John replied, ‘Whether it is right, in the sight of God, to listen to you rather than to him –'),
(995544,34,44,4,20,'judge for yourselves, for we cannot help speaking of what we have seen and heard.’'),
(995545,34,44,4,21,'However, after further warnings, the Council set them at liberty, not seeing any safe way of punishing them, because of the people, for they were all praising God for what had occurred;'),
(995546,34,44,4,22,'for the man who was the subject of this miraculous cure was more than forty years old.'),
(995547,34,44,4,23,'After they had been set at liberty, the apostles went to their friends and told them what the chief priests and the elders had said to them.'),
(995548,34,44,4,24,'All who heard their story, moved by a common impulse, raised their voices to God in prayer:'),
(995549,34,44,4,25,'and who, by the lips of our ancestor, your servant David, who spoke under the influence of the Holy Spirit, have said –'),
(995550,34,44,4,26,'The kings of the earth set their array,'),
(995551,34,44,4,27,'There have indeed gathered together in this city against your holy servant Jesus, whom you has consecrated the Christ, not Herod and Pontius Pilate only, but the nations and the people of Israel besides –'),
(995552,34,44,4,28,'Yet only to do what you, by your power and of your own will, did long ago destine to be done.'),
(995553,34,44,4,29,'Now, therefore, Lord, mark their threats, and enable your servants, with all fearlessness, to tell your message,'),
(995554,34,44,4,30,'while you stretch out your hand to heal, and cause signs and wonders to take place through the name of your holy servant Jesus.’'),
(995555,34,44,4,31,'When their prayer was ended, the place in which they were assembled was shaken; and they were all filled with the Holy Spirit, and began to tell God’s message fearlessly.'),
(995556,34,44,4,32,'The whole body of those who had become believers in Christ were of one heart and mind. Not one of them claimed any of his goods as his own, but everything was held for the common use.'),
(995557,34,44,4,33,'The apostles continued with great power to bear their testimony to the resurrection of the Lord Jesus, and God’s blessing rested on them all abundantly.'),
(995558,34,44,4,34,'Nor was there anyone in need among them, for all who were owners of land or houses sold them, and brought the proceeds of the sales'),
(995559,34,44,4,35,'And laid them at the apostles’ feet; and then everyone received a share in proportion to his wants.'),
(995560,34,44,4,36,'A Levite of Cyprian birth, named Joseph, (who had received from the apostles the additional name of “Barnabas” – which means “The Consoler,”)'),
(995561,34,44,4,37,'Sold a farm that belonged to him, and brought the money and laid it at the apostles’ feet.'),
(995562,34,44,5,1,'There was, however, a man named Ananias, who, with his wife Sapphira, sold some property,'),
(995563,34,44,5,2,'and, with her connivance, kept back some of the proceeds. He brought only a part and laid it at the apostles’ feet.'),
(995564,34,44,5,3,'‘Ananias,’ Peter exclaimed, ‘how is it that Satan has so taken possession of your heart that you have lied to the Holy Spirit, and kept back a part of the money paid for the land?'),
(995565,34,44,5,4,'While it was unsold, was not it your own? And after it was sold, was not the money at your own disposal? How did you come to think of such a thing? You have lied, not to people, but to God!’'),
(995566,34,44,5,5,'As Ananias heard these words, he fell down and expired; and everyone who heard of it was appalled.'),
(995567,34,44,5,6,'The young men got up, and, winding the body in a sheet, carried it out and buried it.'),
(995568,34,44,5,7,'After an interval of about three hours his wife came in, not knowing what had happened.'),
(995569,34,44,5,8,'‘Is it true,’ Peter asked, addressing her, ‘that you sold your land for such a sum?’'),
(995570,34,44,5,9,'Then Peter said, ‘How did you come to agree to provoke the Spirit of the Lord? Listen! The footsteps of those who have buried your husband are at the door; and they will carry you out too.’'),
(995571,34,44,5,10,'Instantly Sapphira fell down at Peter’s feet and expired. On coming in, the young men found her dead; so they carried her out and buried her by her husband’s side.'),
(995572,34,44,5,11,'The whole church and all who heard of these events were appalled.'),
(995573,34,44,5,12,'Many signs and wonders continued to occur among the people, through the instrumentality of the apostles, whose custom it was to meet all together in the Colonnade of Solomon;'),
(995574,34,44,5,13,'but of the rest no one ventured to join them. On the other hand, the people were full of their praise,'),
(995575,34,44,5,14,'and still larger numbers, both of men and women, as they became believers in the Lord, were added to their number.'),
(995576,34,44,5,15,'The consequence was that people would bring out their sick even into the streets, and lay them on mattresses and mats, in the hope that, as Peter came by, at least his shadow might fall on someone of them.'),
(995577,34,44,5,16,'Besides this, the inhabitants of the towns round Jerusalem flocked into the city, bringing with them their sick and those who were troubled by foul spirits; and they were cured everyone.'),
(995578,34,44,5,17,'At this the high priest was roused to action, and he and all his supporters (who formed the party of the Sadducees), moved by jealousy,'),
(995579,34,44,5,18,'arrested the apostles, and had them placed in custody.'),
(995580,34,44,5,19,'An angel of the Lord, however, opened the prison doors at night and led them out.'),
(995581,34,44,5,20,'‘Go,’ he said, ‘and stand in the Temple Courts, and tell the people the whole message of this new life.’'),
(995582,34,44,5,21,'When they heard this, they went at daybreak into the Temple Courts, and began to teach. The high priest and his party, on their arrival, summoned the High Council, including all the leaders of the people among the Israelites, and sent to the jail to fetch the apostles.'),
(995583,34,44,5,22,'But, when the officers got there, they did not find them in the prison; so they returned and reported that,'),
(995584,34,44,5,23,'while they had found the goal barred securely and the guards posted at the doors, yet, on opening them, they had not found anyone inside.'),
(995585,34,44,5,24,'When the officer in charge at the Temple and the chief priests heard their story, they were perplexed about the apostles and as to what all this would lead to.'),
(995586,34,44,5,25,'Presently, however, someone came and told them, that the men whom they had put in prison were actually standing in the Temple Courts, teaching the people.'),
(995587,34,44,5,26,'Then, the officer went with his men and fetched the apostles – without using violence, for they were afraid of being stoned by the people –'),
(995588,34,44,5,27,'And then brought them before the Council. The high priest demanded an explanation from them.'),
(995589,34,44,5,28,'‘We gave you strict orders,’ he said, ‘not to teach in this name. Yet you have actually flooded Jerusalem with your teaching, and you want to make us responsible for the death of this man.’'),
(995590,34,44,5,29,'To this Peter and the apostles replied, ‘We must obey God rather than people.'),
(995591,34,44,5,30,'The God of our ancestors raised Jesus, whom you put to death by hanging him on a cross.'),
(995592,34,44,5,31,'It is this Jesus whom God has exalted to his right hand, to be a guide and a Saviour, to give Israel repentance and forgiveness of sins.'),
(995593,34,44,5,32,'And we are witness to the truth of this, and so is the Holy Spirit – the gift of God to those who obey him.’'),
(995594,34,44,5,33,'The members of the Council became frantic with rage on hearing this, and were for putting the apostles to death.'),
(995595,34,44,5,34,'But Gamaliel, a Pharisee, who was a Doctor of the Law and who was held in universal respect, rose in the Council, and directed that the men should be taken out of court for a little while.'),
(995596,34,44,5,35,'He then said, ‘People of Israel, take care as to what you intend to do with these men.'),
(995597,34,44,5,36,'For not long ago Theudas appeared, professing to be somebody, and was joined by a body of some four hundred men. But he was killed; and all his followers scattered and dwindled away.'),
(995598,34,44,5,37,'After him, Judas the Galilean appeared at the time of the census, and induced people to follow him; Yet he, too, perished and all his followers were dispersed.'),
(995599,34,44,5,38,'And, in this present case, my advice to you is not to interfere with these men, but to leave them alone, for, if their designs and their work are merely of human origin, they will come to an end;'),
(995600,34,44,5,39,'but, if they are of divine origin, you will be powerless to put an end to them – or else you may find yourselves fighting against God!’'),
(995601,34,44,5,40,'The Council followed his advice, and, calling the apostles in, had them flogged, and then, after cautioning them not to speak in the name of Jesus, set them free.'),
(995602,34,44,5,41,'But the apostles left the Council, rejoicing that they had been thought worthy to suffer disgrace for that name;'),
(995603,34,44,5,42,'and never for a single day, either in the Temple Courts or in private houses, did they cease to teach, or to tell the good news of Jesus, the Christ.'),
(995604,34,44,6,1,'About this time, when the number of the disciples was constantly increasing, complaints were made by the Greek speaking Jews against the Aramaic speaking Jews, that their widows were being overlooked in the daily distribution.'),
(995605,34,44,6,2,'The Twelve, therefore, called together the general body of the disciples and said to them, ‘It is not well for us to see to the distribution at the tables and neglect God’s message.'),
(995606,34,44,6,3,'Therefore, friends, look for seven men of reputation among yourselves, wise and spiritually-minded men, and we will appoint them to attend to this matter;'),
(995607,34,44,6,4,'while we, for our part, will devote ourselves to prayer, and to the delivery of the message.’'),
(995608,34,44,6,5,'This proposal was unanimously agreed to; and the disciples chose Stephen – a man full of faith and of the Holy Spirit – and Philip, Prochorus, Nicanor, Timon, Parmenas, and Nicholas of Antioch, a former convert to Judaism;'),
(995609,34,44,6,6,'and they brought these men to the apostles, who, after praying, placed their hands on them.'),
(995610,34,44,6,7,'So God’s message spread, and the number of the disciples continued to increase rapidly in Jerusalem, and a large body of the priests accepted the faith.'),
(995611,34,44,6,8,'Meanwhile Stephen, divinely helped and strengthened, was showing great wonders and signs among the people.'),
(995612,34,44,6,9,'But some members of the Synagogue of the Freed Slaves (as it was called), Cyrenians, Alexandrians, and Visitors from Cilicia and Roman Asia, were roused to action and began disputing with Stephen;'),
(995613,34,44,6,10,'yet they were quite unable to withstand the wisdom and the inspiration with which he spoke.'),
(995614,34,44,6,11,'Then they induced some men to assert that they had heard Stephen saying blasphemous things against Moses, and against God;'),
(995615,34,44,6,12,'and they stirred up the people, as well as the elders and the teachers of the Law, and set on Stephen, and arrested him, and brought him before the High Council.'),
(995616,34,44,6,13,'There they produced witnesses who gave false evidence.'),
(995617,34,44,6,14,'indeed, we have heard him declare that this Jesus of Nazareth will destroy this place, and change the customs handed down to us by Moses.’'),
(995618,34,44,6,15,'The eyes of all the members of the Council were riveted on Stephen, and they saw his face looking like the face of an angel.'),
(995619,34,44,7,1,'Then the high priest asked, ‘Is this true?’'),
(995620,34,44,7,2,'Stephen replied, ‘Brothers and fathers, hear what I have to say. God, who manifests himself in the glory, appeared to our ancestor Abraham when he was in Mesopotamia, and before he settled in Haran, and said to him –'),
(995621,34,44,7,3,'“Leave your country and your people, and come into the country that I will show you.”'),
(995622,34,44,7,4,'And so Abraham left the country of the Chaldaeans and settled in Haran; and from there, after his father’s death, God caused him to migrate into this country, in which you are now living.'),
(995623,34,44,7,5,'God did not at that time give him any part of it, not even a foot of ground. But he promised to give him possession of it and his descendants after him, though at that time he had no child.'),
(995624,34,44,7,6,'God’s words were these – “Abraham’s descendants will live in a foreign country, where they will be enslaved and ill-treated for four hundred years.'),
(995625,34,44,7,7,'But I myself will judge the nation, to which they will be enslaved,” God said, “and after that they will leave the country and worship me in this place.”'),
(995626,34,44,7,8,'Then God made with Abraham the covenant of circumcision; and under it Abraham became the father of Isaac, and circumcised him when he was eight days old; and Isaac became the father of Jacob; and Jacob of the Twelve Patriarchs.'),
(995627,34,44,7,9,'The Patriarchs, out of jealousy, sold Joseph into slavery in Egypt; but God was with him,'),
(995628,34,44,7,10,'and delivered him out of all his troubles, and enabled him to win favour and show wisdom before Pharaoh, king of Egypt, who appointed him Governor of Egypt and of his whole household.'),
(995629,34,44,7,11,'Then a famine spread over the whole of Egypt and Canaan, causing great distress, and our ancestors could find no food.'),
(995630,34,44,7,12,'Hearing, however, that there was corn in Egypt, Jacob sent our ancestors there on their first visit.'),
(995631,34,44,7,13,'In the course of their second visit, Joseph revealed himself to his brothers, and his family became known to Pharaoh.'),
(995632,34,44,7,14,'Then Joseph sent an urgent invitation to his father Jacob and to his relatives, seventy-five persons in all;'),
(995633,34,44,7,15,'and so Jacob went down into Egypt. There he died, and our ancestors also,'),
(995634,34,44,7,16,'and their bodies were removed to Shechem, and laid in the tomb which Abraham had bought for a sum of money from the sons of Hamor in Shechem.'),
(995635,34,44,7,17,'As the time drew near for the fulfilment of the promise which God had made to Abraham, the people increased largely in numbers in Egypt,'),
(995636,34,44,7,18,'until a new king, who knew nothing of Joseph, came to the throne.'),
(995637,34,44,7,19,'This king acted deceitfully towards our people and ill-treated our ancestors, making them abandon their own infants, so that they should not be reared.'),
(995638,34,44,7,20,'It was just at this time that Moses was born. He was an exceedingly beautiful child, and for three months was brought up in his own father’s house;'),
(995639,34,44,7,21,'and, when he was abandoned, the daughter of Pharaoh found him and brought him up as her own son.'),
(995640,34,44,7,22,'So Moses was educated in all the learning of the Egyptians, and proved his ability both by his words and actions.'),
(995641,34,44,7,23,'When he was in his fortieth year, he resolved to visit his fellow Israelites;'),
(995642,34,44,7,24,'and, seeing an Israelite ill-treated, he defended him, and avenged the man, who was being wronged, by striking down the Egyptian.'),
(995643,34,44,7,25,'He thought his own people would understand that God was using him to save them; but they failed to do so.'),
(995644,34,44,7,26,'The next day he again appeared on the scene, when some of them were fighting, and tried to make peace between them. “Men,” he said, “you are brothers; how is it that you are ill-treating one another?”'),
(995645,34,44,7,27,'But the man who was ill-treating his fellow workman pushed Moses aside saying – “Who made you a ruler and judge over us?'),
(995646,34,44,7,28,'Do you mean to make away with me as you did yesterday with that Egyptian?”'),
(995647,34,44,7,29,'At these words Moses took to flight, and became an exile in Midian; and there he had two sons born to him.'),
(995648,34,44,7,30,'Forty years had passed when there appeared to him, in the desert of Mount Sinai, an angel in a flame of fire in a bush.'),
(995649,34,44,7,31,'When Moses saw it, he was astonished at the vision; but on his going nearer to look at it more closely, the voice of the Lord was heard to say –'),
(995650,34,44,7,32,'“I am the God of your ancestors, the God of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob.” Moses trembled, and did not dare to look.'),
(995651,34,44,7,33,'Then the Lord said to him – “Take your sandals off your feet, for the spot where you are standing is holy ground.'),
(995652,34,44,7,34,'I have seen the oppression of my people who are in Egypt, and heard their groans, and I have come down to deliver them. Come now and I will send you into Egypt.”'),
(995653,34,44,7,35,'This same Moses, whom they had disowned with the words – “Who made you a ruler and a judge?” was the man whom God sent to be both a ruler and a deliverer, under the guidance of the angel that had appeared to him in the bush.'),
(995654,34,44,7,36,'He it was who led them out, after he had shown wonders and signs in Egypt, in the Red Sea, and in the desert during forty years.'),
(995655,34,44,7,37,'This was the Moses who said to the people of Israel – “God will raise up for you, from among yourselves, a prophet, as he raised up me.”'),
(995656,34,44,7,38,'He, too, it was who was present at the assembly in the desert, with the angel who talked to him on Mount Sinai, and with our ancestors, and who received living truths to impart to you.'),
(995657,34,44,7,39,'Yet our ancestors refused him obedience; more than that, they rejected him, and in their hearts turned back to Egypt,'),
(995658,34,44,7,40,'while they said to Aaron – “Make us Gods who will lead the way for us, since, as for this Moses who has brought us out of Egypt, we do not know what has become of him.”'),
(995659,34,44,7,41,'That was the time when they made the calf and offered sacrifice to their idol, and held festivities in honour of their own handiwork!'),
(995660,34,44,7,42,'So God turned from them and left them to the worship of the Starry Host, as is written in the book of the prophets –'),
(995661,34,44,7,43,'You took with you the tent where Moloch is worshipped'),
(995662,34,44,7,44,'Our ancestors had the tent where they worshipped God in the desert, constructed, just as he who spoke to Moses had directed him to make it, after the model which he had seen.'),
(995663,34,44,7,45,'This tent, which was handed down to them, was brought into this country by our ancestors who accompanied Joshua (at the conquest of the nations that God drove out before their advance), and remained here until the time of David.'),
(995664,34,44,7,46,'David found favour with God, and prayed that he might provide the God of Jacob with a place to reside.'),
(995665,34,44,7,47,'But it was Solomon who built a house for God.'),
(995666,34,44,7,48,'Yet it is not in buildings made by hands that the Most High dwells. As the prophet says –'),
(995667,34,44,7,49,'“The heavens are a throne for me,'),
(995668,34,44,7,50,'Was it not my hand that made all these things?”'),
(995669,34,44,7,51,'Stubborn people, heathen in heart and ears, you are for ever resisting the Holy Spirit; your ancestors did it, and you are doing it still.'),
(995670,34,44,7,52,'Which of the prophets escaped persecution at their hands? They killed those who foretold the coming of the righteous one; of whom you, in your turn, have now become the betrayers and murderers –'),
(995671,34,44,7,53,'You who received the Law as transmitted by angels and yet failed to keep it.’'),
(995672,34,44,7,54,'As they listened to this, the Council grew frantic with rage, and gnashed their teeth at Stephen.'),
(995673,34,44,7,55,'He, filled as he was with the Holy Spirit, fixed his eyes intently on the heavens, and saw the glory of God and Jesus standing at God’s right hand.'),
(995674,34,44,7,56,'‘Look,’ he exclaimed, ‘I see heaven open and the Son of Man standing at God’s right hand!’'),
(995675,34,44,7,57,'At this, with a loud shout, they stopped their ears and all rushed on him, forced him outside the city,'),
(995676,34,44,7,58,'and began to stone him, the witnesses laying their clothes at the feet of a young man named Saul.'),
(995677,34,44,7,59,'And they stoned Stephen, while he cried to the Lord, ‘Lord Jesus! Receive my spirit!’'),
(995678,34,44,7,60,'Falling on his knees, he called out loudly, ‘Lord! Do not charge them with this sin;’ and with these words he fell asleep.'),
(995679,34,44,8,1,'Saul approved of his being put to death.'),
(995680,34,44,8,2,'Some religious men buried Stephen, with loud lamentations for him.'),
(995681,34,44,8,3,'But Saul began to devastate the church; he entered house after house, dragged out men and women alike, and threw them into prison.'),
(995682,34,44,8,4,'Now those who were scattered in different directions went from place to place proclaiming the good news.'),
(995683,34,44,8,5,'Philip went down to the city of Samaria, and there began to preach the Christ.'),
(995684,34,44,8,6,'The people, one and all, listened attentively to what Philip told them, when they heard of, and saw, the miracles which he was working.'),
(995685,34,44,8,7,'For there were many instances of people with foul spirits, where the spirits, with loud screams, came out of them;'),
(995686,34,44,8,8,'and many who were paralysed or lame were cured, so that there was great rejoicing throughout that city.'),
(995687,34,44,8,9,'There was staying in the city a man named Simon, who had been practicing magic there and mystifying the Samaritan people, giving himself out to be some great being.'),
(995688,34,44,8,10,'Everyone, high and low, paid attention to him. “This man,” they used to say, “must be that power of God which people call ‘The Great Power.’”'),
(995689,34,44,8,11,'And they paid attention to him because they had for a long time been mystified by his magic arts.'),
(995690,34,44,8,12,'However, when they came to believe Philip, as he told them the good news about the kingdom of God and the name of Jesus Christ, they were baptized, both men and women.'),
(995691,34,44,8,13,'Even Simon believed, and after his baptism attached himself to Philip, and was in his turn mystified at seeing signs and great miracles constantly occurring.'),
(995692,34,44,8,14,'When the apostles at Jerusalem heard that the Samaritans had welcomed God’s message, they sent Peter and John to them;'),
(995693,34,44,8,15,'and they, on their arrival, prayed that the Samaritans might receive the Holy Spirit.'),
(995694,34,44,8,16,'(As yet the Spirit had not descended on any of them; they had only been baptized in the name of the Lord Jesus).'),
(995695,34,44,8,17,'Then Peter and John placed their hands on them, and they received the Holy Spirit.'),
(995696,34,44,8,18,'When Simon saw that it was through the placing of the apostles’ hands on them that the Spirit was given, he brought them a sum of money and said,'),
(995697,34,44,8,19,'‘Give me also this power of yours, so that, if I place my hands on anyone, he may receive the Holy Spirit.’'),
(995698,34,44,8,20,'‘A curse on you and on your money,’ Peter exclaimed, ‘for thinking that God’s free gift can be bought with gold!'),
(995699,34,44,8,21,'You have no share or part in our message, for your heart is not right with God.'),
(995700,34,44,8,22,'Therefore repent of this wickedness of yours, and pray to the Lord, that, if possible, you may be forgiven for such a thought;'),
(995701,34,44,8,23,'for I see that you have fallen into the bitterness of envy and the fetters of sin.’'),
(995702,34,44,8,24,'‘Pray to the Lord for me, all of you,’ Simon answered, ‘so that none of the things you have spoken of may happen to me.’'),
(995703,34,44,8,25,'Peter and John, having borne their testimony and delivered the Lord’s message, returned to Jerusalem, telling the good news, as they went, in many Samaritan villages.'),
(995704,34,44,8,26,'Meanwhile an angel of the Lord had said to Philip, ‘Set out on a journey southwards, along the road that runs down from Jerusalem to Gaza.’ (It is now deserted).'),
(995705,34,44,8,27,'So Philip set out on a journey; and on his way he came on an official of high rank, in the service of Candace, Queen of the Abyssinians. He was her treasurer, and had been to Jerusalem to worship,'),
(995706,34,44,8,28,'and was now on his way home, sitting in his carriage and reading the prophet Isaiah.'),
(995707,34,44,8,29,'The Spirit said to Philip, ‘Go up to the carriage over there and keep close to it.’'),
(995708,34,44,8,30,'So Philip ran up, and he heard the Abyssinian reading the prophet Isaiah.'),
(995709,34,44,8,31,'‘How can I,’ the other answered, ‘unless someone will explain it to me?’ and he invited Philip to get up and sit by his side.'),
(995710,34,44,8,32,'The passage of scripture which he was reading was this –'),
(995711,34,44,8,33,'He was humiliated and justice was denied him.'),
(995712,34,44,8,34,'‘Now,’ said the Treasurer, addressing Philip, ‘tell me, of whom is the prophet speaking? Of himself, or of someone else?’'),
(995713,34,44,8,35,'Then Philip began, and, taking this passage as his text, told him the good news about Jesus.'),
(995714,34,44,8,36,'Presently, as they were going along the road, they came to some water, and the Treasurer exclaimed, ‘Look! Here is water; what is to prevent my being baptized?’'),
(995715,34,44,8,38,'So he ordered the carriage to stop, and they went down into the water – both Philip and the Treasurer – and Philip baptized him.'),
(995716,34,44,8,39,'But, when they came up out of the water, the Spirit of the Lord caught Philip away, and the Treasurer saw no more of him; for he continued his journey with a joyful heart.'),
(995717,34,44,8,40,'But Philip was found at Ashdod, and, as he went on his way, he told the good news in all the towns through which he passed, until he came to Caesarea.'),
(995718,34,44,9,1,'Meanwhile Saul, still breathing murderous threats against the disciples of the Lord, went to the high priest,'),
(995719,34,44,9,2,'and asked him to give him letters to the Jewish congregations at Damascus, authorising him, if he found there any supporters of the Way, whether men or women, to have them put in chains and brought to Jerusalem.'),
(995720,34,44,9,3,'While on his journey, as he was nearing Damascus, suddenly a light from the heavens flashed around him.'),
(995721,34,44,9,4,'He fell to the ground and heard a voice saying to him –'),
(995722,34,44,9,5,'‘Who are you, Lord?’ he asked.'),
(995723,34,44,9,7,'The men traveling with Saul were meanwhile standing speechless; they heard the sound of the voice, but saw no one.'),
(995724,34,44,9,8,'When Saul got up from the ground, though his eyes were open, he could see nothing. So his men led him by the hand, and brought him into Damascus;'),
(995725,34,44,9,9,'and for three days he was unable to see, and took nothing either to eat or to drink.'),
(995726,34,44,9,10,'Now there was at Damascus a disciple named Ananias, to whom, in a vision, the Lord said,'),
(995727,34,44,9,13,'‘Lord,’ exclaimed Ananias, ‘I have heard from many people about this man – how much harm he has done at Jerusalem to your people there.'),
(995728,34,44,9,14,'And, here, too, he holds authority from the chief priests to put in chains all those who invoke your name.’'),
(995729,34,44,9,15,'But the Lord said to him,'),
(995730,34,44,9,17,'So Ananias went, entered the house, and, placing his hands on Saul, said, ‘Saul, my brother, I have been sent by the Lord – by Jesus, who appeared to you on your way here – so that you may recover your sight and be filled with the Holy Spirit.’'),
(995731,34,44,9,18,'Instantly it seemed as if a film fell from Saul’s eyes, and his sight was restored. Then he got up and was baptized,'),
(995732,34,44,9,19,'and, after he had taken food, he felt his strength return.'),
(995733,34,44,9,20,'and at once began in the synagogues to proclaim Jesus as the Son of God.'),
(995734,34,44,9,21,'All who heard him were amazed.'),
(995735,34,44,9,22,'Saul’s influence, however, kept steadily increasing, and he confounded the Jewish people who lived in Damascus by the proofs that he gave that Jesus was the Christ.'),
(995736,34,44,9,23,'After some time some of them laid a plot to kill Saul,'),
(995737,34,44,9,24,'but it became known to him. They even watched the gates day and night, to kill him;'),
(995738,34,44,9,25,'but his disciples let him down by night through an opening in the wall, lowering him in a basket.'),
(995739,34,44,9,26,'On his arrival in Jerusalem, Saul attempted to join the disciples, but they were all afraid of him, as they did not believe that he was really a disciple.'),
(995740,34,44,9,27,'Barnabas, however, taking him by the hand, brought him to the apostles, and told them the whole story of how Saul on his journey had seen the Lord, and how the Lord had talked to him, and how in Damascus he had spoken out fearlessly in the name of Jesus.'),
(995741,34,44,9,28,'After that, Saul remained in Jerusalem, in close contact with the apostles; and he spoke fearlessly in the name of the Lord,'),
(995742,34,44,9,29,'talking and arguing with the Jews of foreign birth, who, however, made attempts to kill him.'),
(995743,34,44,9,30,'But, when the followers found this out, they took him down to Caesarea, and sent him on his way to Tarsus.'),
(995744,34,44,9,31,'And so it came about that the church, throughout Judea, Galilee, and Samaria, enjoyed peace and became firmly established; and, ordering its life by respect for the Lord and the help of the Holy Spirit, it increased in numbers.'),
(995745,34,44,9,32,'Peter, while traveling from place to place throughout the country, went down to visit the people of Christ living at Lydda.'),
(995746,34,44,9,33,'There he found a man named Aeneas, who had been bedridden for eight years with paralysis.'),
(995747,34,44,9,34,'‘Aeneas,’ Peter said to him, ‘Jesus Christ cures you. Get up, and make your bed.’ Aeneas got up at once;'),
(995748,34,44,9,35,'and all the inhabitants of Lydda and of the Plain of Sharon saw him, and came over to the Lord’s side.'),
(995749,34,44,9,36,'At Jaffa there lived a disciple whose name was Tabitha, which is in Greek “Dorcas” – a Gazelle. Her life was spent in doing kind and charitable actions.'),
(995750,34,44,9,37,'Just at that time she was taken ill, and died; and they had washed her body and laid it out in an upstairs room.'),
(995751,34,44,9,38,'Jaffa was near Lydda, and the disciples, having heard that Peter was at Lydda, sent two men with the request that he come to them without delay.'),
(995752,34,44,9,39,'Peter returned with them at once. On his arrival, he was taken upstairs, and all the widows came round him in tears, showing the coats and other clothing which Dorcas had made while she was among them.'),
(995753,34,44,9,40,'But Peter sent everybody out of the room, and knelt down and prayed. Then, turning to the body, he said, ‘Tabitha! Stand up.’'),
(995754,34,44,9,41,'Giving her his hand, Peter raised her up, and, calling in the widows and others of Christ’s people, presented her to them alive.'),
(995755,34,44,9,42,'This became known all through Jaffa, and numbers of people came to believe in the Lord.'),
(995756,34,44,9,43,'And Peter stayed some days at Jaffa with a tanner named Simon.'),
(995757,34,44,10,1,'At Caesarea there was a man named Cornelius, a captain in the regiment known as the “Italian Regiment,”'),
(995758,34,44,10,2,'A religious man and one who reverenced God, with all his household. He was liberal in his charities to the people, and prayed to God constantly.'),
(995759,34,44,10,3,'One afternoon, about three o’clock, he distinctly saw in a vision an angel from God come to him, and call him by name.'),
(995760,34,44,10,4,'Cornelius fixed his eyes on him and, in great alarm, said, ‘What is it, Lord?’'),
(995761,34,44,10,5,'And now, send messengers to Jaffa and fetch a man called Simon, who is also known as Peter.'),
(995762,34,44,10,6,'He is lodging with a tanner named Simon, who has a house near the sea.’'),
(995763,34,44,10,7,'When the angel, who had spoken to him, had gone, Cornelius called two servants and a religious soldier, who was one of his constant attendants,'),
(995764,34,44,10,8,'and, after telling them the whole story, sent them to Jaffa.'),
(995765,34,44,10,9,'On the next day, while these men were on their way, just as they were nearing the town, Peter went up on the housetop about midday to pray.'),
(995766,34,44,10,10,'He became hungry and wanted something to eat; but while it was being prepared, he fell into a trance,'),
(995767,34,44,10,11,'and saw that the heavens were open, and that something like a great sail was descending, let down by its four corners towards the earth.'),
(995768,34,44,10,12,'In it were all kinds of quadrupeds, reptiles, and birds.'),
(995769,34,44,10,13,'Then he was aware of a voice which said –'),
(995770,34,44,10,14,'‘No, Lord, I cannot,’ answered Peter, ‘for I have never eaten anything defiled and unclean.’'),
(995771,34,44,10,15,'Again he was aware of a voice which said –'),
(995772,34,44,10,16,'This happened three times, and then suddenly it was all taken up into the heavens.'),
(995773,34,44,10,17,'While Peter was still perplexed as to the meaning of the vision that he had seen, the men sent by Cornelius, having enquired the way to Simon’s house, came up to the gate,'),
(995774,34,44,10,18,'and called out and asked if the Simon, who was also known as Peter, was lodging there.'),
(995775,34,44,10,19,'Peter was still pondering over the vision, when the Spirit said to him, ‘There are two men looking for you at this moment.'),
(995776,34,44,10,20,'Go down at once and do not hesitate to go with them, for I have sent them.’'),
(995777,34,44,10,21,'Peter went down to the men and said, ‘I am the person you are looking for. What is your reason for coming?’'),
(995778,34,44,10,22,'The men replied, ‘Our captain, Cornelius, a pious man who reverences God and is well spoken of by the whole Jewish nation, has been instructed by a holy angel to send for you to his house, and to listen to what you have to say.’'),
(995779,34,44,10,23,'So Peter invited them in and entertained them.'),
(995780,34,44,10,24,'and the day following he entered Caesarea. Cornelius was expecting them, and had invited his relatives and intimate friends to meet them.'),
(995781,34,44,10,25,'So, when Peter entered the city, Cornelius met him, and, throwing himself at Peter’s feet, bowed to the ground.'),
(995782,34,44,10,26,'Peter, however, lifted him up, saying as he did so, ‘Stand up, I am only human like yourself.’'),
(995783,34,44,10,27,'Talking with him as he went, Peter entered the house, where he found a large gathering of people, to whom he said,'),
(995784,34,44,10,28,'‘You are doubtless aware that it is forbidden for a Jew to be intimate with a foreigner, or even to enter his house; and yet God has shown me that I ought not to call anyone defiled or unclean.'),
(995785,34,44,10,29,'That was why I came, when I was sent for, without raising any objection. And now I ask your reason for sending for me.’'),
(995786,34,44,10,30,'‘Just three days ago this very hour,’ Cornelius said, ‘I was in my house, saying the Afternoon Prayers, when a man in dazzling clothing suddenly stood before me.'),
(995787,34,44,10,31,'“Cornelius,” he said, “your prayer has been heard, and your charities have been accepted, by God.'),
(995788,34,44,10,32,'Therefore send to Jaffa, and invite the Simon, who is also known as Peter, to come here. He is lodging in the house of Simon the tanner, near the sea.”'),
(995789,34,44,10,33,'Accordingly I sent to you at once, and you have been so good as to come. And now we are all here in the presence of God, to listen to all that you have been instructed by the Lord to say.’'),
(995790,34,44,10,34,'Then Peter began.'),
(995791,34,44,10,35,'but that in every nation he who reverences him and does what is right is acceptable to him.'),
(995792,34,44,10,36,'God has sent his message to the Israelites and told them, through Jesus Christ, the good news of peace – and Jesus is Lord of all!'),
(995793,34,44,10,37,'You yourselves know the story which spread through all Judea, how, beginning form Galilee, after the baptism which John proclaimed –'),
(995794,34,44,10,38,'The story, I mean, of Jesus of Nazareth, and how God consecrated him his Christ by enduing him with the Holy Spirit and with power; and how he went about doing good and curing all who were under the power of the devil, because God was with him.'),
(995795,34,44,10,39,'We are ourselves, too, witnesses to all that he did in Judea and in Jerusalem; yet they put him to death by hanging him on a cross!'),
(995796,34,44,10,40,'This Jesus God raised on the third day, and enabled him to appear,'),
(995797,34,44,10,41,'not indeed to everyone, but to witnesses chosen beforehand by God – to us, who ate and drank with him after his resurrection from the dead.'),
(995798,34,44,10,42,'Further, God charged us to proclaim to the people, and solemnly affirm, that it is Jesus who has been appointed by God judge of the living and the dead.'),
(995799,34,44,10,43,'To him it is that all the prophets bear witness, when they say that everyone who believes in him receives through his name forgiveness of sins.’'),
(995800,34,44,10,44,'Before Peter had finished saying these words, the Holy Spirit fell on all who were listening to the message.'),
(995801,34,44,10,45,'Those converts from Judaism, who had come with Peter, were amazed that the gift of the Holy Spirit had been bestowed even on the Gentiles;'),
(995802,34,44,10,46,'for they heard them speaking in different languages and extolling God. At this Peter asked,'),
(995803,34,44,10,47,'‘Can anyone refuse the water for the baptism of these people, now that they have received the Holy Spirit as we did ourselves?’'),
(995804,34,44,10,48,'And he directed that they should be baptized in the name of Jesus Christ; after which they asked him to stay there a few days longer.'),
(995805,34,44,11,1,'The apostles and the followers throughout Judea heard that even the Gentiles had welcomed God’s message.'),
(995806,34,44,11,2,'But, when Peter went up to Jerusalem, those who were converts from Judaism began to attack him,'),
(995807,34,44,11,3,'on the ground that he had visited people who were not circumcised, and had taken meals with them.'),
(995808,34,44,11,4,'So Peter began to relate the facts to them as they had occurred.'),
(995809,34,44,11,5,'‘I was in the town of Jaffa,’ he said, ‘and was praying; and, while in a trance, I saw a vision. There was something like a great sail descending, let down by its four corners out of the heavens; and it came right down to me.'),
(995810,34,44,11,6,'Looking intently at it, I began to distinguish quadrupeds, wild beasts, reptiles, and birds;'),
(995811,34,44,11,7,'and I also heard a voice saying to me –'),
(995812,34,44,11,8,'“No, Lord, I cannot,” I answered, “for nothing defiled or unclean has ever passed my lips.”'),
(995813,34,44,11,9,'Then a second time there came a voice from the heavens.'),
(995814,34,44,11,10,'This happened three times, and then all was drawn up again into the heavens.'),
(995815,34,44,11,11,'At that moment three men, who had been sent from Caesarea to see me, came up to the house in which we were.'),
(995816,34,44,11,12,'The Spirit told me to go with them without hesitation. These six companions also went with me. And, when we came into the man’s house,'),
(995817,34,44,11,13,'he told us how he had seen the angel standing in his house, and how the angel had said to him – “Send to Jaffa and fetch the Simon, who is also known as Peter;'),
(995818,34,44,11,14,'for he will tell you truths, which will prove the means of salvation to you and all your household.”'),
(995819,34,44,11,15,'I had but just begun to speak,’ continued Peter, ‘when the Holy Spirit fell on them, exactly as on us at the first;'),
(995820,34,44,11,16,'and I recalled the saying of the Master –'),
(995821,34,44,11,17,'Since then, God had given them the very same gift as he gave us when we became believers in Jesus Christ the Master – who was I that I could thwart God?’'),
(995822,34,44,11,18,'On hearing this statement, they said no more, but broke out into praise of God. ‘So even to the Gentiles,’ they exclaimed, ‘God has granted the repentance which leads to life!’'),
(995823,34,44,11,19,'Now those who had been scattered in different directions, in consequence of the persecution that followed the death of Stephen, went as far as Phoenicia, Cyprus, and Antioch, telling the message – but only to Jews.'),
(995824,34,44,11,20,'Some of them, however, who were men of Cyprus and Cyrene, on coming to Antioch, addressed themselves also to the Jews of foreign birth, telling them the good news about that Lord Jesus.'),
(995825,34,44,11,21,'The power of the Lord was with them, so that a great number who had learned to believe came over to the Lord’s side.'),
(995826,34,44,11,22,'The news about them reached the ears of the church at Jerusalem, and they sent Barnabas to Antioch.'),
(995827,34,44,11,23,'On coming there he saw to his great joy these tokens of the loving kindness of God, and encouraged them all to make up their minds to be faithful to the Lord –'),
(995828,34,44,11,24,'For Barnabas was a good man and full of the Holy Spirit and of faith – and a large number of people took their stand on the Lord’s side.'),
(995829,34,44,11,25,'Afterwards Barnabas left for Tarsus to look for Saul;'),
(995830,34,44,11,26,'and, when he had found him, he brought him to Antioch. And so it came about that, for a whole year, they attended the meetings of the church there, and taught a large number of people; and it was in Antioch that the disciples were first called “Christians.”'),
(995831,34,44,11,27,'During this time, some prophets came to Antioch from Jerusalem.'),
(995832,34,44,11,28,'One of them, named Agabus, came forward and, under the influence of the Spirit, foretold a great famine that was to spread over all the world – a famine which occurred in the reign of Claudius.'),
(995833,34,44,11,29,'So the disciples, without exception, determined, in proportion to their means, to send something to help the followers living in Judea.'),
(995834,34,44,11,30,'And this they did, sending it to the church elders by Barnabas and Saul.'),
(995835,34,44,12,1,'It was at that time that King Herod began to ill-treat some of the members of the church.'),
(995836,34,44,12,2,'He had James, the brother of John, beheaded;'),
(995837,34,44,12,3,'and, when he saw that the Jews were pleased with this, he proceeded to arrest Peter also. (This was during the Festival of the unleavened bread.)'),
(995838,34,44,12,4,'After seizing Peter, Herod put him in prison, and entrusted him to the keeping of four Guards of four soldiers each, intending, after the Passover, to bring him up before the people.'),
(995839,34,44,12,5,'So Peter was kept in prison, but meanwhile the prayers of the church were being earnestly offered to God on his behalf.'),
(995840,34,44,12,6,'Just when Herod was intending to bring him before the people, on that very night Peter was asleep between two soldiers, chained to them both, while there were sentries in front of the door, guarding the prison.'),
(995841,34,44,12,7,'Suddenly an angel of the Lord stood by him, and a light shone in the cell. The angel struck Peter on the side, and roused him with the words, ‘Get up quickly.’'),
(995842,34,44,12,8,'The chains dropped from his wrists, and then the angel said, ‘Put on your belt and sandals.’ When Peter had done so, the angel added, ‘Throw your cloak round you and follow me.’'),
(995843,34,44,12,9,'Peter followed him out, not knowing that what was happening under the angel’s guidance was real, but thinking that he was seeing a vision.'),
(995844,34,44,12,10,'Passing the first Guard, and then the second, they came to the iron gate leading into the city, which opened to them of itself; and, when they had passed through that, and had walked along one street, all at once the angel left him.'),
(995845,34,44,12,11,'Then Peter came to himself and said, ‘Now I know beyond all doubt that the Lord has sent his angel, and has rescued me from Herod’s hands and from all that the Jewish people have been expecting.’'),
(995846,34,44,12,12,'As soon as he realized what had happened, he went to the house of Mary, the mother of John who was also known as Mark, where a number of people were gathered together, praying.'),
(995847,34,44,12,13,'On his knocking at the door in the gate, a maidservant, named Rhoda, came to answer it.'),
(995848,34,44,12,14,'She recognized Peter’s voice, but in her joy left the gate unopened, and ran in, and told them that Peter was standing outside.'),
(995849,34,44,12,15,'‘You are mad!’ they exclaimed. But, when she persisted that it was so, they said, ‘It must be his spirit!’'),
(995850,34,44,12,16,'Meanwhile Peter went on knocking, and, when they opened the gate and saw him, they were amazed.'),
(995851,34,44,12,17,'Peter signed to them with his hand to be silent, and then told them how the Lord had brought him out of the prison, adding, ‘Tell James and the others all this.’ Then he left the house, and went away to another place.'),
(995852,34,44,12,18,'In the morning there was a great stir among the soldiers – what could have become of Peter!'),
(995853,34,44,12,19,'And, when Herod had made further search for him and failed to find him, he closely questioned the Guard, and ordered them away to execution. Then he went down from Judea to stay at Caesarea.'),
(995854,34,44,12,20,'It happened that Herod was deeply offended with the people of Tyre and Sidon, but they went in a body to him, and, having succeeded in winning over Blastus, the Chamberlain, they begged Herod for a reconciliation, because their country was dependent on the king’s for its food supply.'),
(995855,34,44,12,21,'On an appointed day Herod, wearing his state robes, seated himself on his throne, and delivered an oration.'),
(995856,34,44,12,22,'The people kept shouting, ‘It is the voice of God, and not of a person!’'),
(995857,34,44,12,23,'Instantly an angel of the Lord struck him, because he did not give God the glory; and he was attacked with worms, and died.'),
(995858,34,44,12,24,'Meanwhile the Lord’s message kept extending, and spreading far and wide.'),
(995859,34,44,12,25,'When Barnabas and Saul had carried out their mission, they returned to Jerusalem, and took with them John, who was also known as Mark.'),
(995860,34,44,13,2,'While they were engaged in the worship of the Lord and were fasting, the Holy Spirit said, ‘Set apart for me Barnabas and Saul, for the work to which I have called them.’'),
(995861,34,44,13,3,'Accordingly, after fasting and prayer, they placed their hands on them and dismissed them.'),
(995862,34,44,13,4,'Barnabas and Saul, sent on this mission, as they were, by the Holy Spirit, went down to Seleucia, and from there sailed to Cyprus.'),
(995863,34,44,13,5,'On reaching Salamis, they began to tell the message of God in the Jewish synagogues; and they had John with them as an assistant.'),
(995864,34,44,13,6,'After passing through the whole island, they reached Paphos, where they found an astrologer who pretended to be a prophet – a Jew by birth, whose name was Barjoshua.'),
(995865,34,44,13,7,'He was at the court of the Governor, Sergius Paulus, a man of intelligence, who sent for Barnabas and Saul and asked to be told God’s message.'),
(995866,34,44,13,8,'But Elymas, the astrologer (for that is the meaning of the word), opposed them, eager to divert the Governor’s attention from the faith.'),
(995867,34,44,13,9,'However, Saul (who is the same as Paul), full of the Holy Spirit, fixed his eyes on him and said,'),
(995868,34,44,13,10,'‘You incarnation of deceit and all fraud! You son of the devil! You opponent of all that is good! Will you never cease to divert the straight paths of the Lord? Listen!'),
(995869,34,44,13,11,'The hand of the Lord is on you even now, and you will be blind for a time and unable to see the sun.’ Immediately a mist and darkness fell on him, and he went feeling about for someone to guide him.'),
(995870,34,44,13,12,'When the Governor saw what had happened, he became a believer in Christ, being greatly impressed by the teaching about the Lord.'),
(995871,34,44,13,13,'After this, Paul and his companions set sail from Paphos and went to Perga in Pamphylia, where John left them and returned to Jerusalem.'),
(995872,34,44,13,14,'The others went on from Perga and arrived at Antioch in Pisidia. There they went into the synagogue on the Sabbath and took their seats.'),
(995873,34,44,13,15,'After the reading of the Law and the prophets, the synagogue leader sent them this message – ‘Friends, if you have any helpful words to address to the people, now is the time to speak.’'),
(995874,34,44,13,16,'So Paul rose and, motioning with his hand, said:'),
(995875,34,44,13,17,'The God of this people Israel chose our ancestors, and during their stay in Egypt increased the prosperity of the people, and then with uplifted arm brought them out from that land.'),
(995876,34,44,13,18,'For about forty years he bore with them in the desert;'),
(995877,34,44,13,19,'then, after destroying seven heathen nations in Canaan, he allotted their land to this people –'),
(995878,34,44,13,20,'For about four hundred and fifty years. In later times he gave them Judges, of whom the prophet Samuel was the last.'),
(995879,34,44,13,21,'And, when they demanded a king, God gave them Saul the son of Kish, a man of the tribe of Benjamin, who reigned for forty years.'),
(995880,34,44,13,22,'After removing him, he raised David to the throne, and bore this testimony to him – “In David, the son of Jesse, I have found a man after my own heart, who will carry out all my purposes.”'),
(995881,34,44,13,23,'It was from this man’s descendants that God, in accordance with his promise, gave Israel a Saviour – Jesus;'),
(995882,34,44,13,24,'John having first proclaimed, before the appearance of Jesus, a baptism on repentance for all the people of Israel.'),
(995883,34,44,13,25,'As John was drawing towards the end of his career, he said “What do you suppose that I am? I am not the Christ. But there is ‘one coming’ after me, whose sandal I am not worthy to untie.”'),
(995884,34,44,13,26,'Brothers and sisters, descendants of Abraham, and all those among you who worship God, it was to us that the message of this salvation was sent.'),
(995885,34,44,13,27,'The people of Jerusalem and their leaders, failing to recognise Jesus, and not understanding the utterances of the prophets that are read every Sabbath, fulfilled them by condemning him.'),
(995886,34,44,13,28,'They found no ground at all for putting him to death, and yet demanded his execution from Pilate;'),
(995887,34,44,13,29,'and, after carrying out everything written about him, they took Jesus down from the cross, and laid him in a tomb.'),
(995888,34,44,13,30,'But God raised him from the dead;'),
(995889,34,44,13,31,'and he appeared for many days to those who had gone up with him from Galilee to Jerusalem, and who are now witnesses for him to the people.'),
(995890,34,44,13,32,'We also have good news to tell you, about the promise made to our ancestors –'),
(995891,34,44,13,33,'That our children have had this promise completely fulfilled to them by God, by his raising Jesus. That is just what is said in the second Psalm –'),
(995892,34,44,13,34,'As to his raising Jesus from the dead, never again to return to corruption, this is what is said –'),
(995893,34,44,13,35,'And, therefore, in another Psalm it is said –'),
(995894,34,44,13,36,'David, after obediently doing God’s will in his own time, fell asleep and was laid by the side of his ancestors, and did undergo corruption;'),
(995895,34,44,13,37,'but Jesus, whom God raised from the dead, did not undergo corruption.'),
(995896,34,44,13,38,'I would, therefore, like you to know, friends, that through Jesus forgiveness of sins is being proclaimed to you,'),
(995897,34,44,13,39,'and that, in union with him, everyone who believes in him is absolved from every sin from which under the Law of Moses you could not be absolved.'),
(995898,34,44,13,40,'Beware, therefore, that what is said in the prophets does not come true of you –'),
(995899,34,44,13,41,'“Look, you despisers, and wonder, and perish;'),
(995900,34,44,13,42,'As Paul and Barnabas were leaving the synagogue, the people begged for a repetition of this teaching on the next Sabbath.'),
(995901,34,44,13,43,'After the congregation had dispersed, many of the Jews, and of the converts who joined in their worship, followed Paul and Barnabas, who talked with them and urged them to continue to rely on the loving kindness of God.'),
(995902,34,44,13,44,'On the following Sabbath, almost all the city gathered to hear God’s message.'),
(995903,34,44,13,45,'But the sight of the crowds of people filled the minds of the Jews with jealousy, and they kept contradicting Paul’s statements in violent language.'),
(995904,34,44,13,46,'Then Paul and Barnabas spoke out fearlessly, and said:'),
(995905,34,44,13,47,'For this is the Lord’s command to us –'),
(995906,34,44,13,48,'On hearing this, the Gentiles were glad and extolled God’s message; and all those who had been enrolled for eternal life became believers in Christ;'),
(995907,34,44,13,49,'and the Lord’s message was carried throughout that district.'),
(995908,34,44,13,50,'But the Jews incited the women of high social standing who worshiped with them, and the leading men of the town, and started a persecution against Paul and Barnabas, and drove them out of their region.'),
(995909,34,44,13,51,'They, however, shook the dust off their feet in protest,'),
(995910,34,44,13,52,'and went to Iconium, leaving the disciples full of joy and of the Holy Spirit.'),
(995911,34,44,14,1,'The same thing occurred in Iconium, where Paul and Barnabas went into the Jewish synagogue, and spoke in such a way that a great number of both Jews and Greeks believed in Christ.'),
(995912,34,44,14,2,'But the Jews who refused to believe stirred up the Gentiles, and poisoned their minds against the Lord’s followers.'),
(995913,34,44,14,3,'Therefore Paul and Barnabas spent a long time there, and spoke out fearlessly, relying on the Lord, who confirmed the message of his love by permitting signs and wonders to take place at their hands.'),
(995914,34,44,14,4,'But the townspeople were divided, some siding with the Jews, some with the apostles;'),
(995915,34,44,14,5,'and, when there was an attempt on the part of both Gentiles and Jews, with their leaders, to resort to violence and to stone them,'),
(995916,34,44,14,6,'the apostles heard of it, and took refuge in Lystra and Derbe, towns in Lycaonia, and in the district round,'),
(995917,34,44,14,7,'and there they continued to tell the good news.'),
(995918,34,44,14,8,'In the streets of Lystra there used to sit a man who had no power in his feet; he had been lame from his birth, and had never walked.'),
(995919,34,44,14,9,'This man was listening to Paul speaking, when Paul, looking intently at him, and seeing that he had the faith to be healed,'),
(995920,34,44,14,10,'said loudly, ‘Stand upright on your feet.’'),
(995921,34,44,14,11,'and the crowd, seeing what Paul had done, called out in the Lycaonian language, ‘The Gods have come down to us in human form.’'),
(995922,34,44,14,12,'So they called Barnabas “Zeus,” and Paul “Hermes,” because he took the lead in speaking;'),
(995923,34,44,14,13,'and the priest of Zeus-beyond-the-Walls, accompanied by the crowd, brought bullocks and garlands to the gates, with the intention of offering sacrifices.'),
(995924,34,44,14,14,'But, when the apostles Barnabas and Paul heard of it, they tore their clothes and rushed out into the crowd.'),
(995925,34,44,14,15,'‘We are only people like yourselves, and we have come with the good news that you should turn away from these follies to a living God, who made the heavens, the earth, the sea, and everything that is in them.'),
(995926,34,44,14,16,'In bygone times he permitted all the nations to go their own ways.'),
(995927,34,44,14,17,'Yet he has not failed to give you, in the good he does, some revelation of himself – sending you from heaven rain and fruitful seasons, and gladdening your hearts with plenty and good cheer.’'),
(995928,34,44,14,18,'Even with this appeal they could hardly restrain the people from offering sacrifice to them.'),
(995929,34,44,14,19,'Presently, however, there came some Jews from Antioch, and Iconium who, after they had won over the people, stoned Paul, and dragged him out of the town, thinking him to be dead.'),
(995930,34,44,14,20,'But, when the disciples had gathered round him, he got up and went back into the town; the next day he went with Barnabas to Derbe.'),
(995931,34,44,14,21,'After telling the good news throughout that town, and making a number of converts, they returned to Lystra, Iconium, and Antioch,'),
(995932,34,44,14,22,'reassuring the minds of the disciples, urging them to remain true to the faith, and showing that it is only through many troubles that we can enter the kingdom of God.'),
(995933,34,44,14,23,'They also appointed elders for them in every church, and, after prayer and fasting, commended them to the Lord in whom they had learned to believe.'),
(995934,34,44,14,24,'Paul and Barnabas then went through Pisidia, and came into Pamphylia,'),
(995935,34,44,14,25,'and, after telling the message at Perga, went down to Attaleia.'),
(995936,34,44,14,26,'From there they sailed to Antioch – the place where they had been committed to the gracious care of God for the work which they had now finished.'),
(995937,34,44,14,27,'After their arrival, they gathered the church together, and gave an account of all that God had helped them to do, and especially how he had opened to the Gentiles the door of faith;'),
(995938,34,44,14,28,'and at Antioch they stayed with the disciples for a considerable time.'),
(995939,34,44,15,1,'But certain persons came down from Judea, and began to teach the Lord’s followers that, unless they were circumcised, in accordance with the custom required by Moses, they could not be saved.'),
(995940,34,44,15,2,'This gave rise to a serious dispute, and much discussion, between Paul and Barnabas and these people, and it was therefore settled that Paul and Barnabas and others of their number should go up to Jerusalem, to consult the apostles and church elders about the matter under discussion.'),
(995941,34,44,15,3,'The church, therefore, sent them on their journey, and they made their way through Phoenicia and Samaria, telling the story of the conversion of the Gentiles, to the great joy of all the followers.'),
(995942,34,44,15,4,'On their arrival at Jerusalem, they were welcomed by the church, as well as by the apostles and the elders, and gave an account of all that God had helped them to do.'),
(995943,34,44,15,5,'Some of the Pharisees’ party, however, who had become believers in Christ, came forward and declared that they were bound to circumcise converts and to direct them to observe the Law of Moses.'),
(995944,34,44,15,6,'The apostles and the church elders held a meeting to consider this question.'),
(995945,34,44,15,7,'After much discussion, Peter rose and said:'),
(995946,34,44,15,8,'Now God, who reads all hearts, declared his acceptance of the Gentiles, by giving them the Holy Spirit, just as he did to us.'),
(995947,34,44,15,9,'He made no distinction between them and us, when he purified their hearts by their faith.'),
(995948,34,44,15,10,'Why, then, do you now provoke God, by putting on the necks of these disciples a yoke which neither our ancestors nor we were able to bear?'),
(995949,34,44,15,11,'No, it is through the loving kindness of the Lord Jesus that we, just as they do, believe that we have been saved.’'),
(995950,34,44,15,12,'Every voice in the assembly was hushed, as they listened to Barnabas and Paul, while they gave an account of all the signs and wonders which God had shown among the Gentiles through them.'),
(995951,34,44,15,13,'After they had finished speaking, James addressed the Council.'),
(995952,34,44,15,14,'Simon has described the manner in which God first visited the Gentiles, in order to take from among them a people to bear his name.'),
(995953,34,44,15,15,'And that is in harmony with the words of the prophets, where they say –'),
(995954,34,44,15,16,'“After this I will return;'),
(995955,34,44,15,17,'that so the rest of mankind may earnestly seek the Lord –'),
(995956,34,44,15,18,'says the Lord, as he does these things, known from long ago.”'),
(995957,34,44,15,19,'In my judgment, therefore, we should not add to the difficulties of those Gentiles who are turning to God,'),
(995958,34,44,15,20,'but we should write to them to abstain from food that has been polluted by being sacrificed to idols, from impurity, from eating the flesh of strangled animals, and from blood.'),
(995959,34,44,15,21,'For in every town, for generations past, there have been those who preach Moses, read as he is in the synagogues every Sabbath.’'),
(995960,34,44,15,22,'It was then decided by the apostles and the elders, with the assent of the whole church, to choose some of their number, and send them to Antioch with Paul and Barnabas. Those chosen were Judas (called Barsabas) and Silas, who were leaders among the community.'),
(995961,34,44,15,23,'They were bearers of the following letter –'),
(995962,34,44,15,24,'As we had heard that some of our number had upset you by their assertions, and unsettled your minds – without instructions from us –'),
(995963,34,44,15,25,'We met and decided to choose certain men and send them to you with our dear friends Barnabas and Paul,'),
(995964,34,44,15,26,'who have risked their lives for the name of our Lord, Jesus Christ.'),
(995965,34,44,15,27,'We are accordingly sending Judas and Silas, and they will tell you by word of mouth what we are now writing.'),
(995966,34,44,15,28,'We have, therefore, decided, under the guidance of the Holy Spirit, to lay no further burden on you beyond these necessary conditions –'),
(995967,34,44,15,29,'That you abstain from food offered to idols, from blood, from eating the flesh of strangled animals, and from impurity. If you guard yourselves against such things, it will be well with you. Farewell.”'),
(995968,34,44,15,30,'So the bearers of this letter were sent on their way, and went down to Antioch. There they called a meeting of all the followers,'),
(995969,34,44,15,31,'and delivered the letter, the reading of which caused great rejoicing by its encouraging contents.'),
(995970,34,44,15,32,'Judas and Silas, who were themselves prophets, further encouraged the them by many an address, and strengthened their faith.'),
(995971,34,44,15,33,'After some stay, they were dismissed with kind farewells from the followers, and returned to those who had sent them.'),
(995972,34,44,15,35,'Paul and Barnabas, however, remained in Antioch, where they taught and, with the help of many others, told the good news of the Lord’s message.'),
(995973,34,44,15,36,'Some time after this, Paul said to Barnabas, ‘Let us go back and visit the Lord’s followers in every town in which we have told the Lord’s message, and see how they are prospering.’'),
(995974,34,44,15,37,'Barnabas wished to take with them John, whose other name was Mark;'),
(995975,34,44,15,38,'but Paul felt that they ought not to take with them the man who had deserted them in Pamphylia, and had not gone on with them to their work.'),
(995976,34,44,15,39,'This caused such unpleasant feeling between them that they parted ways, Barnabas taking Mark and sailing for Cyprus,'),
(995977,34,44,15,40,'while Paul chose Silas for his companion and, after he had been committed by the followers to the gracious care of the Lord,'),
(995978,34,44,15,41,'started on his journey and went through Syria and Cilicia, strengthening the churches in the faith.'),
(995979,34,44,16,1,'Among other places Paul went to Derbe and Lystra. At the latter place they found a disciple, named Timothy, whose mother was a Jewish woman who was a believer, while his father was a Greek,'),
(995980,34,44,16,2,'and who was well spoken of by the followers of the Lord in Lystra and Iconium.'),
(995981,34,44,16,3,'Wishing to take this man with him on his journey, Paul caused him to be circumcised out of consideration for the Jews in that region, for they all knew that his father had been a Greek.'),
(995982,34,44,16,4,'As they traveled from town to town, they gave the followers the decisions which had been reached by the apostles and church elders at Jerusalem, for them to observe.'),
(995983,34,44,16,5,'So the churches grew stronger in the faith, and increased in numbers from day to day.'),
(995984,34,44,16,6,'They next went through the Phrygian district of Galatia, but were restrained by the Holy Spirit from delivering the message in Roman Asia.'),
(995985,34,44,16,7,'When they reached the borders of Mysia, they attempted to go into Bithynia, but the Spirit of Jesus did not permit them.'),
(995986,34,44,16,8,'Passing through Mysia, they went down to Troas;'),
(995987,34,44,16,9,'and there one night Paul saw a vision. A Macedonian was standing and appealing to him – “Come over to Macedonia and help us.”'),
(995988,34,44,16,10,'So, immediately after Paul had seen the vision, we looked for an opportunity to cross over to Macedonia, concluding that God had summoned us to tell the good news to the people there.'),
(995989,34,44,16,11,'Accordingly we set sail from Troas, and ran before the wind to Samothrace, reaching Neapolis the next day.'),
(995990,34,44,16,12,'From there we made our way to Philippi, which is the principal city of that part of Macedonia, and also a Roman Settlement.'),
(995991,34,44,16,13,'On the Sabbath we went outside the gate to the riverside, where we supposed there would be a place of prayer; and we sat down and talked to the women who were gathered there.'),
(995992,34,44,16,14,'Among them was a woman, named Lydia, belonging to Thyatira, a dealer in purple cloth, who was accustomed to join in the worship of God. The Lord touched this woman’s heart, so that she gave attention to the message delivered by Paul,'),
(995993,34,44,16,15,'and, when she and her household had been baptized, she urged us to become her guests.'),
(995994,34,44,16,16,'One day, as we were on our way to the place of prayer, we were met by a girl possessed by a divining spirit, who made large profits for her masters by fortune-telling.'),
(995995,34,44,16,17,'This girl followed Paul and the rest of us, calling, ‘These men are servants of the most high God, and they are bringing you news of a way to salvation.’'),
(995996,34,44,16,18,'She had been doing this for several days, when Paul, much vexed, turned and said to the spirit within her, ‘In the name of Jesus Christ I command you to leave her.’ That very moment the spirit left her.'),
(995997,34,44,16,19,'When her masters saw that there was no hope of further profit from her, they seized Paul and Silas, dragged them into the public square to the authorities,'),
(995998,34,44,16,20,'and took them before the Magistrates.'),
(995999,34,44,16,21,'‘They are Jews, and they are teaching customs which it is not right for us, as Romans, to sanction or adopt.’'),
(996000,34,44,16,22,'The mob rose as one person against them, and the Magistrates stripped them of their clothing and ordered them to be beaten with rods.'),
(996001,34,44,16,23,'After beating them severely, the Magistrates put them in prison, with orders to the jailer to keep them in safe custody.'),
(996002,34,44,16,24,'On receiving so strict an order, the Governor put them into the inner cell, and secured their feet in the stocks.'),
(996003,34,44,16,25,'About midnight, while Paul and Silas were praying and singing hymns to God, and while the prisoners were listening to them,'),
(996004,34,44,16,26,'suddenly there was an earthquake of such violence that the jail was shaken to its foundations; all the doors flew open, and all the prisoners’ chains were loosened.'),
(996005,34,44,16,27,'Roused from his sleep, and seeing the prison doors open, the Governor drew his sword intending to kill himself, in the belief that the prisoners had escaped.'),
(996006,34,44,16,28,'But Paul called our loudly, ‘Do not harm yourself; we are all here.’'),
(996007,34,44,16,29,'Calling for a light, the Governor rushed in, and flung himself trembling at the feet of Paul and Silas.'),
(996008,34,44,16,30,'Then he led them out, and said, ‘What must I do to be saved?’'),
(996009,34,44,16,31,'‘Believe in Jesus, our Lord,’ they replied, ‘and you will be saved, you and your household too.’'),
(996010,34,44,16,32,'Then they spoke to him of God’s message, and to all his household as well.'),
(996011,34,44,16,33,'And that very hour of the night he took them and washed their wounds, and he himself and everyone belonging to him were baptized without delay.'),
(996012,34,44,16,34,'Afterwards he took them up to his house and set before them something to eat, rejoicing that he, with all his household, had come to believe in God.'),
(996013,34,44,16,35,'In the morning the Magistrates sent the police with an order for the men to be discharged.'),
(996014,34,44,16,36,'The jailer told Paul of his instructions. ‘The Magistrates have sent an order for your discharge,’ he said, ‘so you had better leave the place at once and go quietly away.’'),
(996015,34,44,16,37,'But Paul’s answer to them was, ‘They have flogged us in public without trial, though we are Roman citizens, and they have put us in prison, and now they are for sending us out secretly! No, indeed! Let them come and take us out themselves.’'),
(996016,34,44,16,38,'The police reported his words to the Magistrates, who, on hearing that Paul and Silas were Roman citizens, were alarmed,'),
(996017,34,44,16,39,'and went to the prison, and did their best to conciliate them. Then they took them out, and begged them to leave the city.'),
(996018,34,44,16,40,'When Paul and Silas left the prison, they went to Lydia’s house, and, after they had seen the Lord’s followers, and encouraged them, they left the place.'),
(996019,34,44,17,1,'After passing through Amphipolis and Apollonia, Paul and Silas came to Thessalonica. Here the Jews had a synagogue;'),
(996020,34,44,17,2,'and, following his usual custom, Paul joined them, and for three Sabbaths addressed them, drawing his arguments from the scriptures.'),
(996021,34,44,17,3,'He laid before them and explained that the Christ must undergo suffering and rise from the dead; and ‘It is this man,’ he declared, ‘who is the Christ – this Jesus about whom I am telling you.’'),
(996022,34,44,17,4,'Some of the people were convinced, and threw in their lot with Paul and Silas, as did also a large body of Greeks who were accustomed to join in the Jewish services, and a great number of leading women.'),
(996023,34,44,17,5,'But the Jewish leaders, becoming jealous, engaged some worthless fellows from the streets, and, getting a mob together, kept the city in an uproar. They attacked Jason’s house, with the intention of bringing Paul and Silas before the Popular Assembly;'),
(996024,34,44,17,6,'and, not finding them there, they proceeded to drag Jason and some of the Lord’s followers before the city magistrates, shouting out,'),
(996025,34,44,17,7,'and have been harboured by Jason! They are all defying the decrees of the Emperor. They say that someone else is king – a man called Jesus!’'),
(996026,34,44,17,8,'On hearing this, the people and the city magistrates were much concerned;'),
(996027,34,44,17,9,'and, before letting them go, they took bail from Jason and the others.'),
(996028,34,44,17,10,'That very night the followers sent Paul and Silas off to Beroea; and on reaching that place, they went to the Jewish synagogue.'),
(996029,34,44,17,11,'These Jews of Beroea were better disposed than those in Thessalonica, for they welcomed the message with great readiness, and daily examined the scriptures to see if what was said was true.'),
(996030,34,44,17,12,'As a consequence, many of them became believers in Christ, besides a considerable number of Greek women of position, and of men also.'),
(996031,34,44,17,13,'But, when the Jewish leaders in Thessalonica found out that God’s message had been delivered by Paul at Beroea, they came there too, exciting and disturbing the minds of the people.'),
(996032,34,44,17,14,'The followers immediately arranged for Paul to go away to the coast, but both Silas and Timothy stayed behind in Beroea.'),
(996033,34,44,17,15,'The friends who escorted Paul took him as far as Athens, and, after receiving a message for Silas and Timothy to join him as quickly as possible, they started on their return.'),
(996034,34,44,17,16,'While Paul was waiting for them at Athens, his heart was stirred at seeing the whole city full of idols.'),
(996035,34,44,17,17,'So he argued in the synagogue with the Jews and with those who joined in their worship, as well as daily in the public Square with those who happened to be there.'),
(996036,34,44,17,18,'Among others, some Epicurean and Stoic Philosophers joined issue with him. Some asked ‘What is this prater wanting to make out?’, while others said ‘He seems to be a preacher of foreign Deities.’ (This was because he was telling the good news about Jesus and the resurrection).'),
(996037,34,44,17,19,'So they laid hold of him and took him to the Court of Areopagus.'),
(996038,34,44,17,20,'For you are bringing some strange things to our notice, and we should like to know what they mean.’'),
(996039,34,44,17,21,'(All Athenians and the foreigners staying in the city found no time for anything else but telling, or listening to, the last new thing.)'),
(996040,34,44,17,22,'So Paul took his stand in the middle of the Court, and said – ‘People of Athens, on every hand I see signs of your being very devout.'),
(996041,34,44,17,23,'For as I was going about, looking at your sacred shrines, I came upon an altar with this inscription – “To an Unknown God.” What, therefore, you worship in ignorance, that I am now proclaiming to you.'),
(996042,34,44,17,24,'The God who made the world and all things that are in it – he, Lord as he is of heaven and earth, does not live in temples made by hands,'),
(996043,34,44,17,25,'neither do human hands minister to his wants, as though he needed anything, since he himself gives, to all, life, and breath, and all things.'),
(996044,34,44,17,26,'He made all races of the earth’s surface – fixing a time for their rise and fall, and the limits of their settlements –'),
(996045,34,44,17,27,'That they might search for God, if by any means they might feel their way to him and find him. And yet he is not really far from any one of us;'),
(996046,34,44,17,28,'for in him we live and move and are. To use the words of some of your own poets –'),
(996047,34,44,17,29,'Therefore, as the offspring of God, we must not think that the Deity has any resemblance to anything made of gold, or silver, or stone – a work of human art and imagination.'),
(996048,34,44,17,30,'True, God looked with indulgence on the days of people’s ignorance, but now he is announcing to everyone everywhere the need for repentance,'),
(996049,34,44,17,31,'because he has fixed a day on which he intends to judge the world with justice, by a man whom he has appointed – and of this he has given all people a pledge by raising this man from the dead.’'),
(996050,34,44,17,32,'On hearing of a resurrection of the dead, some began jeering, but others said that they wanted to hear what he had to say about that another time.'),
(996051,34,44,17,33,'And so Paul left the Court.'),
(996052,34,44,17,34,'There were, however, some people who joined him, and became believers in Christ. Among them were Dionysius, a member of the Court of Areopagus, a woman named Damaris, and several others.'),
(996053,34,44,18,1,'On leaving Athens, Paul next went to Corinth.'),
(996054,34,44,18,2,'There he met a Jew of the name of Aquila, from Pontus, who, with his wife Priscilla, had lately come from Italy, in consequence of the order which had been issued by the Emperor Claudius for all Jews to leave Rome. Paul paid them a visit,'),
(996055,34,44,18,3,'and, since their trade was the same as his, he stayed and worked with them – their trade was tent-making.'),
(996056,34,44,18,4,'Every Sabbath Paul gave addresses in the synagogue, trying to convince both Jews and Greeks.'),
(996057,34,44,18,5,'But, when Silas and Timothy had come down from Macedonia, Paul devoted himself entirely to delivering the message, earnestly maintaining before the Jews that Jesus was the Christ.'),
(996058,34,44,18,6,'However, as they set themselves against him and became abusive, Paul shook his clothes in protest and said to them, ‘Your blood be on your own heads. My conscience is clear. From this time forward I will go to the Gentiles.’'),
(996059,34,44,18,7,'So he left, and went to the house of a certain Titius Justus, who had been accustomed to join in the worship of God, and whose house was next door to the synagogue.'),
(996060,34,44,18,8,'Crispus, the synagogue leader, came to believe in the Lord, and so did all his household; and many of the Corinthians, as they listened to Paul, became believers in Christ and were baptized.'),
(996061,34,44,18,9,'One night the Lord said to Paul, in a vision,'),
(996062,34,44,18,11,'So he settled there for a year and a half, and taught God’s message among the people.'),
(996063,34,44,18,12,'While Gallio was governor of Greece, some of the Jewish leaders made a combined attack on Paul, and brought him before the Governor’s Bench,'),
(996064,34,44,18,13,'charging him with persuading people to worship God in a way forbidden by the Law.'),
(996065,34,44,18,14,'Just as Paul was on the point of speaking, Gallio said to them, ‘If this were a case of misdemeanour or some serious crime, there would be some reason for my listening patiently to you;'),
(996066,34,44,18,15,'but, since it is a dispute about words, and names, and your own Law, you must see to it yourselves. I do not choose to be a judge in such matters.’'),
(996067,34,44,18,16,'Saying this, he drove them back from the Bench.'),
(996068,34,44,18,17,'Then they all set on Sosthenes, the synagogue leader, and beat him in front of the Bench, but Gallio did not trouble himself about any of these things.'),
(996069,34,44,18,18,'Paul remained there some time after this, and then took leave of the followers, and sailed to Syria with Priscilla and Aquila, but not before his head had been shaved at Cenchreae, because he was under a vow.'),
(996070,34,44,18,19,'They put into Ephesus, and there Paul, leaving his companions, went into the synagogue and addressed the Jews.'),
(996071,34,44,18,20,'When they asked him to prolong his stay, he declined, saying however,'),
(996072,34,44,18,21,'as he took his leave, ‘I will come back again to you, please God,’ and then set sail from Ephesus.'),
(996073,34,44,18,22,'On reaching Caesarea, he went up to Jerusalem and exchanged greetings with the church, and then went down to Antioch.'),
(996074,34,44,18,23,'After making some stay in Antioch, he set out on a tour through the Phrygian district of Galatia, strengthening the faith of all the disciples as he went.'),
(996075,34,44,18,24,'Meanwhile there had come to Ephesus an Alexandrian Jew, named Apollos, an eloquent man, who was well-versed in the scriptures.'),
(996076,34,44,18,25,'He had been well-instructed in the Way of the Lord, and with burning zeal he spoke of, and taught carefully, the facts about Jesus, though he knew of no baptism but John’s.'),
(996077,34,44,18,26,'This man began to speak out fearlessly in the synagogue; and when Priscilla and Aquila heard him, they took him home and explained the Way of God to him more carefully still.'),
(996078,34,44,18,27,'When he wanted to cross to Greece, the followers furthered his plans, and wrote to the disciples there to welcome him. On his arrival he proved of great assistance to those who had, through the loving kindness of God, become believers in Christ,'),
(996079,34,44,18,28,'for he vigorously confuted the Jews, publicly proving by the scriptures that Jesus was the Christ.'),
(996080,34,44,19,1,'While Apollos was at Corinth, Paul passed through the inland districts of Roman Asia, and went to Ephesus. There he found some disciples, of whom he asked,'),
(996081,34,44,19,2,'‘Did you, when you became believers in Christ, receive the Holy Spirit?’'),
(996082,34,44,19,3,'‘What then was your baptism?’ Paul asked.'),
(996083,34,44,19,4,'‘John’s baptism was a baptism on repentance,’ rejoined Paul, ‘and John told the people (speaking of the “one coming” after him) that they should believe in him – that is in Jesus.’'),
(996084,34,44,19,5,'On hearing this, they were baptized in the name of the Lord Jesus,'),
(996085,34,44,19,6,'and, after Paul had placed his hands on them, the Holy Spirit descended on them, and they began to speak in other languages and to preach.'),
(996086,34,44,19,7,'There were about twelve of them in all.'),
(996087,34,44,19,8,'Paul went to the synagogue there, and for three months spoke out fearlessly, giving addresses and trying to convince his hearers, about the kingdom of God.'),
(996088,34,44,19,9,'Some of them, however, hardened their hearts and refused to believe, denouncing the Way before the people. So Paul left them and withdrew his disciples, and gave daily addresses in the lecture-hall of Tyrannus.'),
(996089,34,44,19,10,'This went on for two years, so that all who lived in Roman Asia, Jews and Greeks alike, heard the Lord’s message.'),
(996090,34,44,19,11,'God did miracles of no ordinary kind by Paul’s hands;'),
(996091,34,44,19,12,'so that people would carry home to the sick handkerchiefs or aprons that had touched his body, and their diseases would leave them and the wicked spirits go out of them.'),
(996092,34,44,19,13,'An attempt was made by some itinerant Jews, who were exorcists, to use the name of the Lord Jesus over those who had wicked spirits in them.'),
(996093,34,44,19,14,'The seven sons of Sceva, a Jewish chief priest, were doing this;'),
(996094,34,44,19,15,'but the wicked spirit answered them, ‘Jesus I acknowledge, and Paul I know, but you – who are you?’'),
(996095,34,44,19,16,'Then the man, in whom this wicked spirit was, sprang on them, mastered both of them, and so completely overpowered them, that they fled out of the house, stripped of their clothes, and wounded.'),
(996096,34,44,19,17,'This incident came to the knowledge of all the Jews and Greeks living at Ephesus; they were all awe-struck, and the name of the Lord Jesus was held in the highest honour.'),
(996097,34,44,19,18,'Many, too, of those who had become believers in Christ came with a full confession of their practices;'),
(996098,34,44,19,19,'while a number of people, who had practiced magic, collected their books and burnt them publicly; and on reckoning up the price of these, they found it amounted to fifty thousand silver coins.'),
(996099,34,44,19,20,'So irresistibly did the Lord’s message spread and prevail.'),
(996100,34,44,19,21,'Sometime after these events Paul resolved to go through Macedonia and Greece, and then make his way to Jerusalem. ‘And after I have been there,’ he said, ‘I must visit Rome also.’'),
(996101,34,44,19,22,'So he sent to Macedonia two of his helpers, Timothy and Erastus, while he himself stayed for some time longer in Roman Asia.'),
(996102,34,44,19,23,'Just about that time a great disturbance arose about the Way.'),
(996103,34,44,19,24,'A silversmith named Demetrius, who made silver models of the shrine of Artemis, and so gave a great deal of work to the artisans,'),
(996104,34,44,19,25,'got these men together, as well as the workmen engaged in similar occupations, and said:'),
(996105,34,44,19,26,'and you see and hear that not only at Ephesus, but in almost the whole of Roman Asia, this Paul has convinced and won over great numbers of people, by his assertion that those Gods which are made by hands are not Gods at all.'),
(996106,34,44,19,27,'So that not only is this business of ours likely to fall into discredit, but there is the further danger that the Temple of the great Goddess Artemis will be thought nothing of, and that she herself will be deprived of her splendour – though all Roman Asia and the whole world worship her.’'),
(996107,34,44,19,28,'When they heard this, the men were greatly enraged, and began shouting – ‘Great is Artemis of the Ephesians!’'),
(996108,34,44,19,29,'The commotion spread through the whole city, and the people rushed together into the amphitheater, dragging with them Gaius and Aristarchus, two Macedonians who were Paul’s traveling companions.'),
(996109,34,44,19,30,'Paul wished to go into the amphitheater and face the people, but the disciples would not let him,'),
(996110,34,44,19,31,'while some of the chief religious officials of the province, who were friendly to him, sent repeated entreaties to him not to trust himself inside.'),
(996111,34,44,19,32,'Meanwhile some were shouting one thing and some another, for the Assembly was all in confusion, most of those present not even knowing why they had met.'),
(996112,34,44,19,33,'But some of the crowd prompted Alexander, whom several of the Jewish leaders had pushed to the front, and he waved his hand to show that he wanted to speak in their defence to the people.'),
(996113,34,44,19,34,'However, when they recognised him as a Jew, one cry broke from them all, and they continued shouting for two hours – ‘Great is Artemis of the Ephesians!’'),
(996114,34,44,19,35,'When the Recorder had succeeded in quieting the crowd, he said, ‘People of Ephesus, who is there, I ask you, who needs to be told that this city of Ephesus is the Warden of the Temple of the great Artemis, and of the statue which fell down from Zeus?'),
(996115,34,44,19,36,'As these are undeniable facts, you ought to keep calm and do nothing rash;'),
(996116,34,44,19,37,'for you have brought these men here, though they are neither robbers of Temples nor blasphemers of our Goddess.'),
(996117,34,44,19,38,'If, however, Demetrius and the artisans who are acting with him have a charge to make against anyone, there are court days and there are Magistrates; let both parties take legal proceedings.'),
(996118,34,44,19,39,'But if you want anything more, it will have to be settled in the regular Assembly.'),
(996119,34,44,19,40,'For I tell you that we are in danger of being proceeded against for today’s riot, there being nothing to account for it; and in that case we will be at a loss to give any reason for this disorderly gathering.’'),
(996120,34,44,19,41,'With these words he dismissed the Assembly.'),
(996121,34,44,20,1,'When the uproar had ceased, Paul sent for the disciples, and, with encouraging words, bade them goodbye, and started on his journey to Macedonia.'),
(996122,34,44,20,2,'After going through those districts and speaking many encouraging words to the disciples, he went into Greece, where he stayed three months.'),
(996123,34,44,20,3,'He was about to sail to Syria, when he learned that a plot had been laid against him by several of the Jewish leaders; so he decided to return by way of Macedonia.'),
(996124,34,44,20,4,'He was accompanied by Sopater the son of Pyrrhus, of Beroea, Aristarchus and Secundus from Thessalonica, Gaius of Derbe, and Timothy, as well as by Tychicus and Trophimus of Roman Asia.'),
(996125,34,44,20,5,'These people went to Troas and waited for us there;'),
(996126,34,44,20,6,'while we ourselves sailed from Philippi after the Passover, and joined them five days later at Troas, where we stayed for a week.'),
(996127,34,44,20,7,'On the first day of the week, when we had met for the breaking of bread, Paul, who was intending to leave the next day, began to address those who were present, and prolonged his address until midnight.'),
(996128,34,44,20,8,'There were a good many lamps in the upstairs room, where we had met;'),
(996129,34,44,20,9,'and a young man named Eutychus, sitting at the window, was gradually overcome with great drowsiness, as Paul continued his address. At last, quite overpowered by his drowsiness, he fell from the third story to the ground, and was picked up for dead.'),
(996130,34,44,20,10,'But Paul went down, threw himself on him, and put his arms round him.'),
(996131,34,44,20,11,'Then he went upstairs; and, after breaking and partaking of the bread, he talked with them at great length until daybreak, and then left.'),
(996132,34,44,20,12,'Meanwhile they had taken the lad away alive, and were greatly comforted.'),
(996133,34,44,20,13,'We started first, went on board ship, and sailed for Assos, intending to take Paul on board there. This was by his own arrangement, as he intended to go by land himself.'),
(996134,34,44,20,14,'So, when he met us at Assos, we took him on board and went on to Mitylene.'),
(996135,34,44,20,15,'The day after we had sailed from there, we arrived off Chios, touched at Samos the following day, and the next day reached Miletus;'),
(996136,34,44,20,16,'for Paul had decided to sail past Ephesus, so as to avoid spending much time in Roman Asia. He was making haste to reach Jerusalem, if possible, by the Festival at the close of the Harvest.'),
(996137,34,44,20,17,'From Miletus, however, he sent to Ephesus and invited the church elders to meet him;'),
(996138,34,44,20,18,'and, when they came, he said to them, ‘You know well the life that I always led among you from the very first day that I set foot in Roman Asia,'),
(996139,34,44,20,19,'serving the Lord, as I did, in all humility, amid the tears and trials which fell to my lot through the plots of some of the Jewish leaders.'),
(996140,34,44,20,20,'I never shrank from telling you anything that could be helpful to you, or from teaching you both in public and in private.'),
(996141,34,44,20,21,'I earnestly pointed both Jews and Greeks to the repentance that leads to God, and to faith in Jesus, our Lord.'),
(996142,34,44,20,22,'And now, under spiritual constraint, I am here on my way to Jerusalem, not knowing what will happen to me there,'),
(996143,34,44,20,23,'except that in town after town the Holy Spirit plainly declares to me that imprisonment and troubles await me.'),
(996144,34,44,20,24,'But I count my life of no value to myself, if only I may complete the course marked out for me, and the task that was allotted me by the Lord Jesus – which was to declare the good news of the love of God.'),
(996145,34,44,20,25,'And now, I tell you, I know that none of you will ever see my face again – you among whom I have gone about proclaiming the kingdom.'),
(996146,34,44,20,26,'Therefore I declare to you this day, that my conscience is clear in regard to the fate of any of you,'),
(996147,34,44,20,27,'for I have not shrunk from announcing the whole purpose of God regarding you.'),
(996148,34,44,20,28,'Be watchful over yourselves, and over the whole flock, of which the Holy Spirit has placed you in charge, to shepherd the church of God, which he won for himself at the cost of his life.'),
(996149,34,44,20,29,'I know that, after my departure, merciless wolves will get in among you, who will not spare the flock;'),
(996150,34,44,20,30,'and from among yourselves, too, people will arise, who will teach perversions of truth, so as to draw away the disciples after them.'),
(996151,34,44,20,31,'Therefore, be on your guard, remembering how for three years, night and day, I never ceased, even with tears, to warn each one of you.'),
(996152,34,44,20,32,'And now I commend you to the Lord and to the message of his love – a message which has the power to build up your characters, and to give you your place among all those who have become Christ’s people.'),
(996153,34,44,20,33,'I have never coveted anyone’s gold or silver or clothing.'),
(996154,34,44,20,34,'You, yourselves, know that these hands of mine provided not only for my own wants, but for my companions also.'),
(996155,34,44,20,35,'I left nothing undone to show you that, labouring as I laboured, you ought to help the weak, and to remember the words of the Lord Jesus, how he said himself –'),
(996156,34,44,20,36,'When Paul had finished speaking, he knelt down and prayed with them all.'),
(996157,34,44,20,37,'All were in tears; and throwing their arms round Paul’s neck, they kissed him again and again,'),
(996158,34,44,20,38,'grieving most of all over what he had said – that they would never see his face again. Then they escorted him to the ship.'),
(996159,34,44,21,1,'When we had torn ourselves away and had set sail, we ran before the wind to Cos; the next day we came to Rhodes, and from there to Patara,'),
(996160,34,44,21,2,'where we found a ship crossing to Phoenicia, and went on board and set sail.'),
(996161,34,44,21,3,'After sighting Cyprus and leaving it on the left, we sailed to Syria, and put into Tyre, where the ship was to discharge her cargo.'),
(996162,34,44,21,4,'There we found the disciples and stayed a week with them. Speaking under the influence of the Spirit, they warned Paul not to set foot in Jerusalem.'),
(996163,34,44,21,5,'However, when we had come to the end of our visit, we went on our way, all the disciples with their wives and children escorting us out of the city. We knelt down on the beach, and prayed,'),
(996164,34,44,21,6,'and then said goodbye to one another; after which we went on board, and they returned home.'),
(996165,34,44,21,7,'After we had made the run from Tyre, we landed at Ptolemais, and exchanged greetings with the followers there, and spent a day with them.'),
(996166,34,44,21,8,'The next day we left, and reached Caesarea, where we went to the house of Philip, the missionary, who was one of the Seven, and stayed with him.'),
(996167,34,44,21,9,'He had four unmarried daughters, who had the gift of prophecy.'),
(996168,34,44,21,10,'During our visit, which lasted several days, a prophet, named Agabus, came down from Judea.'),
(996169,34,44,21,11,'He came to see us, and, taking Paul’s belt, and binding his own feet and hands with it, said, ‘This is what the Holy Spirit says – “The man to whom this belt belongs will be bound like this by the religious authorities in Jerusalem, and they will give him up to the Gentiles”.’'),
(996170,34,44,21,12,'When we heard that, we and the people of the place began to entreat Paul not to go up to Jerusalem.'),
(996171,34,44,21,13,'It was then that Paul made the reply, ‘Why are you weeping and breaking my heart like this? For my part, I am ready not only to be bound, but even to suffer death at Jerusalem for the name of the Lord Jesus.’'),
(996172,34,44,21,14,'So, as he would not be persuaded, we said no more to him, only adding – ‘The Lord’s will be done.’'),
(996173,34,44,21,15,'At the end of our visit, we made our preparations, and started on our way up to Jerusalem.'),
(996174,34,44,21,16,'Some of the disciples from Caesarea went with us, and brought Mnason with them, a Cypriot disciple of long standing, with whom we were to stay.'),
(996175,34,44,21,17,'On our arrival at Jerusalem, the followers of the Lord there gave us a hearty welcome;'),
(996176,34,44,21,18,'and the next day Paul went with us to see James, and all the church elders were present.'),
(996177,34,44,21,19,'After greeting them, Paul related in detail all that God had done among the Gentiles through his efforts;'),
(996178,34,44,21,20,'and, when they had heard it, they began praising God, and said to Paul:'),
(996179,34,44,21,21,'Now they have heard it said about you, that you teach all of our people in foreign countries to forsake Moses, for you tell them not to circumcise their children or even to observe Jewish customs.'),
(996180,34,44,21,22,'Well now, as they are certain to hear of your arrival, do what we are going to suggest.'),
(996181,34,44,21,23,'We have four men here, who have of their own accord put themselves under a vow.'),
(996182,34,44,21,24,'Join these men, share their purification, and bear their expenses, so that they may shave their heads; and then all will see that there is no truth in what they have been told about you, but that, on the contrary, you yourself rule your life in obedience to the Jewish Law.'),
(996183,34,44,21,25,'As to the Gentiles who have become believers in Christ, we have sent our decision that they should avoid food offered to idols, and blood, and the flesh of strangled animals, and impurity.’'),
(996184,34,44,21,26,'Paul joined the men, and the next day shared their purification, and went into the Temple, and gave notice of the expiration of the period of purification when the usual offering should have been made on behalf of each of them.'),
(996185,34,44,21,27,'But, just as the seven days were drawing to a close, some of the Jewish people from Roman Asia caught sight of Paul in the Temple, and caused great excitement among all the people present, by seizing Paul and shouting,'),
(996186,34,44,21,28,'‘People of Israel! Help! This is the man who teaches everyone everywhere against our people, our Law, and this place; and, what is more, he has actually brought Greeks into the Temple and defiled this sacred place.’'),
(996187,34,44,21,29,'(For they had previously seen Trophimus the Ephesian in Paul’s company in the city, and were under the belief that Paul had taken him into the Temple.)'),
(996188,34,44,21,30,'The whole city was stirred, and the people quickly collected, seized Paul, and dragged him out of the Temple, when the doors were immediately shut.'),
(996189,34,44,21,31,'They were bent on killing him, when it was reported to the officer commanding the garrison, that all Jerusalem was in commotion.'),
(996190,34,44,21,32,'He instantly got together some officers and soldiers, and charged down on the crowd, who, when they saw the commanding officer and his soldiers, stopped beating Paul.'),
(996191,34,44,21,33,'Then he went up to Paul, arrested him, ordered him to be doubly chained, and proceeded to inquire who he was, and what he had been doing.'),
(996192,34,44,21,34,'Some of the crowd said one thing, and some another; and, as he could get no definite reply because of the uproar, he ordered Paul to be taken into the barracks.'),
(996193,34,44,21,35,'When Paul reached the steps, he was actually being carried by the soldiers, owing to the violence of the mob;'),
(996194,34,44,21,36,'for the people were following in a mass, shouting out, ‘Kill him!’'),
(996195,34,44,21,37,'Just as he was about to be taken into the Fort, Paul said to the commanding officer, ‘May I speak to you?’'),
(996196,34,44,21,38,'‘Aren’t you, then, the Egyptian who some time ago raised an insurrection and led the four thousand Bandits out into the wilderness?’'),
(996197,34,44,21,39,'‘No,’ said Paul, ‘I am a Jew of Tarsus in Cilicia, a citizen of a city of some note. I beg you to give me permission to speak to the people.’'),
(996198,34,44,21,40,'The commanding officer gave his permission, and Paul, standing on the steps, made signs with his hand to the people, and, when comparative silence had been obtained, he said to them in Hebrew:'),
(996199,34,44,22,1,'‘Brothers and fathers, listen to the defence which I am about to make.’'),
(996200,34,44,22,2,'When they heard that he was speaking to them in Hebrew, they were still more quiet; and Paul went on:'),
(996201,34,44,22,3,'‘I am a Jew, from Tarsus in Cilicia, but I was brought up in this city under the teaching of Gamaliel, and educated in accordance with the strict system of our ancestral Law. I was as zealous in God’s service as any of you who are here today.'),
(996202,34,44,22,4,'In my persecution of this Way I did not stop even at the taking of life. I put in chains, and imprisoned, men and women alike –'),
(996203,34,44,22,5,'And to that the high priest himself and all the council of elders can testify. For I had letters of introduction from them to our fellow Jews at Damascus, and I was on my way to that place, to bring those whom I might find there prisoners to Jerusalem for punishment.'),
(996204,34,44,22,6,'While I was still on my way, just as I was getting close to Damascus, about midday, suddenly there flashed from the heavens a great light all round me.'),
(996205,34,44,22,7,'I fell to the ground, and heard a voice saying to me'),
(996206,34,44,22,8,'“Who are you, Lord?” I replied. Then the voice said'),
(996207,34,44,22,9,'The men with me saw the light, but did not hear the speaker’s voice.'),
(996208,34,44,22,10,'Then I said “What am I to do, Lord?”'),
(996209,34,44,22,11,'In consequence of that dazzling light I could not see, but my companions held me by the hand, until I reached Damascus.'),
(996210,34,44,22,12,'There a man named Ananias, a strict observer of our Law, well spoken of by all the Jewish inhabitants, came to see me.'),
(996211,34,44,22,13,'Standing close to me, he said “Saul, my brother, recover your sight.” And then and there I recovered my sight and looked up at him.'),
(996212,34,44,22,14,'Then he said “The God of our ancestors has appointed you to learn his will, and to see the righteous one, and to hear words from his lips;'),
(996213,34,44,22,15,'for you will be a witness for him to all the world of what you have just seen and heard.'),
(996214,34,44,22,16,'And now why wait any longer, Be baptized at once, wash away your sins, and invoke his name.”'),
(996215,34,44,22,17,'After my return to Jerusalem, while I was praying one day in the Temple, I fell into a trance,'),
(996216,34,44,22,18,'and saw Jesus saying to me'),
(996217,34,44,22,19,'“Lord,” I answered, “these people know that I used to imprison and scourge, in synagogue after synagogue, those who believed in you;'),
(996218,34,44,22,20,'and, when the blood of your martyr, Stephen, was being shed, I was myself standing by, approving of his death, and took charge of the clothes of those who were murdering him.”'),
(996219,34,44,22,21,'But Jesus said to me'),
(996220,34,44,22,22,'Up to this point the people had been listening to Paul, but at these words they called out, ‘Kill him! A fellow like this ought not to have been allowed to live!’'),
(996221,34,44,22,23,'As they were shouting, tearing off their clothes, and throwing dust in the air,'),
(996222,34,44,22,24,'the commanding officer ordered Paul to be taken into the Fort, and directed that he should be examined under the lash so that he might find out the reason for their outcry against him.'),
(996223,34,44,22,25,'But just as they had tied him up to be scourged, Paul said to the captain standing near, ‘Is it legal for you to scourge a Roman citizen, unconvicted?’'),
(996224,34,44,22,26,'On hearing this, the captain went and reported it to the commanding officer. ‘Do you know what you are doing?’ he said. ‘This man is a Roman citizen.’'),
(996225,34,44,22,27,'So the commanding officer went up to Paul and said, ‘Tell me, are you a Roman citizen?’'),
(996226,34,44,22,28,'‘I had to pay a heavy price for my position as citizen,’ said the officer. ‘I am one by birth,’ rejoined Paul.'),
(996227,34,44,22,29,'The men who were to have examined Paul immediately drew back, and the officer, finding that Paul was a Roman citizen, was alarmed at having put him in chains.'),
(996228,34,44,22,30,'On the next day the commanding officer, wishing to find out the real reason why Paul was denounced by the Jewish leaders, had his chains taken off, and directed the chief priests and the whole of the High Council to assemble, and then took Paul down and brought him before them.'),
(996229,34,44,23,1,'Paul fixed his eyes on the Council, and began:'),
(996230,34,44,23,2,'At this, the high priest Ananias ordered the men standing near to strike him on the mouth;'),
(996231,34,44,23,3,'Paul turned to him and said:'),
(996232,34,44,23,4,'The people standing near said to Paul, ‘Do you know that you are insulting God’s high priest?’'),
(996233,34,44,23,5,'‘I did not know, brothers, that it was the high priest,’ said Paul, ‘for scripture says –'),
(996234,34,44,23,6,'Noticing that some of those present were Sadducees and others Pharisees, Paul called out in the Council, ‘Brothers, I am a Pharisee and a son of Pharisees. It is on the question of hope for the dead and of their resurrection that I am on my trial.’'),
(996235,34,44,23,7,'As soon as he said this, a dispute arose between the Pharisees and the Sadducees; and there was a sharp division of opinion among those present.'),
(996236,34,44,23,8,'(For Sadducees say there is no such thing as a resurrection, and that there is neither angel nor spirit, while Pharisees believe in both.)'),
(996237,34,44,23,9,'So a great uproar ensued, and some of the Teachers of the Law belonging to the Pharisees’ party stood up and hotly protested, ‘We find nothing whatever wrong in this man. Suppose a spirit did speak to him, or an angel…’'),
(996238,34,44,23,10,'The dispute was becoming so violent, that the commanding officer, fearing that Paul would be torn in pieces between them, ordered the Guard to go down and rescue him from them, and take him into the Fort.'),
(996239,34,44,23,11,'That night the Lord came and stood by Paul, and said,'),
(996240,34,44,23,12,'In the morning some Jewish men combined together, and took an oath that they would not eat or drink until they had killed Paul.'),
(996241,34,44,23,13,'There were more than forty in the plot;'),
(996242,34,44,23,14,'and they went to the chief priests and the elders, and said, ‘We have taken a solemn oath not to touch food until we have killed Paul.'),
(996243,34,44,23,15,'So we want you now, with the consent of the Council, to suggest to the commanding officer that he should bring Paul down before you, as though you intended to go more fully into his case; but, before he comes here, we will be ready to make away with him.’'),
(996244,34,44,23,16,'However, the son of Paul’s sister, hearing of the plot, went to the Fort, and on being admitted, told Paul about it.'),
(996245,34,44,23,17,'Paul called one of the Captains of the garrison and asked him to take the lad to the commanding officer, as he had something to tell him.'),
(996246,34,44,23,18,'The captain went with the lad to the commanding officer, and said, ‘The prisoner Paul called me and asked me to bring this lad to you, as he has something to tell you.’'),
(996247,34,44,23,19,'The commanding officer took the lad by the hand, and, stepping aside, asked what it was he had to tell him.'),
(996248,34,44,23,20,'‘Some men have agreed,’ answered the lad, ‘to ask you to bring Paul down before the Council tomorrow, on the plea of your making further inquiry into his case.'),
(996249,34,44,23,21,'But do not let them persuade you, for more than forty of them are lying in wait for him, who have taken an oath that they will not eat or drink, until they have made away with him; and they are at this very moment in readiness, counting on your promise.’'),
(996250,34,44,23,22,'The commanding officer then dismissed the lad, cautioning him not to mention to anybody that he had given him that information.'),
(996251,34,44,23,23,'Then he called two Captains, and ordered them to have two hundred soldiers ready to go to Caesarea, as well as seventy troopers and two hundred lancers, by nine o’clock that night,'),
(996252,34,44,23,24,'and to have horses ready for Paul to ride, so that they might take him safely to Felix, the Governor.'),
(996253,34,44,23,25,'He also wrote a letter along these lines:'),
(996254,34,44,23,26,'“Claudius Lysias sends his compliments to His Excellency Felix the Governor.'),
(996255,34,44,23,27,'The man whom I send with this had been seized by some Jews, and was on the point of being killed by them, when I came upon them with the force under my command, and rescued him, as I learned that he was a Roman citizen.'),
(996256,34,44,23,28,'Wanting to know exactly the ground of the charges they made against him, I brought him before their Council,'),
(996257,34,44,23,29,'when I found that their charges were connected with questions of their own Law, and that there was nothing alleged involving either death or imprisonment.'),
(996258,34,44,23,30,'Having, however, information of a plot against the man, which was about to be put into execution, I am sending him to you at once, and I have also directed his accusers to prosecute him before you.”'),
(996259,34,44,23,31,'The soldiers, in accordance with their orders, took charge of Paul and conducted him by night to Antipatris;'),
(996260,34,44,23,32,'and on the next day, leaving the troopers to go on with him, they returned to the Fort.'),
(996261,34,44,23,33,'On arriving at Caesarea, the troopers delivered the letter to the Governor, and brought Paul before him.'),
(996262,34,44,23,34,'As soon as Felix had read the letter, he enquired to what province Paul belonged, and, learning that he came from Cilicia, he said,'),
(996263,34,44,23,35,'‘I will hear all you have to say as soon as your accusers have arrived.’ And he ordered Paul to be kept under guard in Herod’s Government house.'),
(996264,34,44,24,1,'Five days afterwards the high priest Ananias came down with some of the elders and a barrister named Tertullus. They laid an information with the Governor against Paul;'),
(996265,34,44,24,2,'and, when the hearing came on, Tertullus began his speech for the prosecution.'),
(996266,34,44,24,3,'‘We owe it to your Excellency,’ he said, ‘that we are enjoying profound peace, and we owe it to your foresight that this nation is constantly securing reforms – advantages which we very gratefully accept at all times and places.'),
(996267,34,44,24,4,'But – not to be tedious – I beg you, with your accustomed fairness, to listen to a brief statement of our case.'),
(996268,34,44,24,5,'We have found this man a public pest; he is one who stirs up disputes among our people all the world over, and is a ringleader of the Nazarene heretics.'),
(996269,34,44,24,6,'He even attempted to desecrate the Temple itself, but we caught him;'),
(996270,34,44,24,8,'and you will be able, by examining him on all these points, to satisfy yourself as to the charges which we are bringing against him.’'),
(996271,34,44,24,9,'The Jewish crowd also joined in the attack and bore out his statements.'),
(996272,34,44,24,10,'On a sign from the Governor, Paul made this reply:'),
(996273,34,44,24,11,'For you can easily verify that it is not more than twelve days ago that I went up to worship at Jerusalem,'),
(996274,34,44,24,12,'where my prosecutors never found me holding discussions with anyone, or causing a crowd to collect – either in the Temple, or in the synagogues, or about the city;'),
(996275,34,44,24,13,'and they cannot establish the charges which they are now making against me.'),
(996276,34,44,24,14,'This, however, I do acknowledge to you, that it is as a believer in the Way which they call heretical, that I worship the God of my ancestors. At the same time, I believe everything that is in accordance with the Law and that is written in the prophets;'),
(996277,34,44,24,15,'and I have a hope that rests in God – a hope which they also cherish – that there will one day be a resurrection of good and bad alike.'),
(996278,34,44,24,16,'This being so, I strive at all times to keep my conscience clear before both God and people.'),
(996279,34,44,24,17,'After some years’ absence I had come to bring charitable gifts to my nation, and to make offerings;'),
(996280,34,44,24,18,'and it was while engaged in this that they found me in the Temple, after completing a period of purification, but not with any crowd or disorder.'),
(996281,34,44,24,19,'There were, however, some Jews from Roman Asia who ought to have been here before you, and to have made any charge that they may have against me –'),
(996282,34,44,24,20,'Or else let my opponents here say what they found wrong in me when I was before the Council,'),
(996283,34,44,24,21,'except as to the one sentence that I shouted out as I stood among them – “It is about the resurrection of the dead that I am on my trial before you today”.’'),
(996284,34,44,24,22,'Felix, however, adjourned the case – though he had a fairly accurate knowledge of all that concerned the Way – with the promise, ‘When Lysias, the commanding officer, comes down, I will give my decision in your case.’'),
(996285,34,44,24,23,'So he gave orders to the captain in charge of Paul to keep him in custody, but to relax the regulations, and not to prevent any of his personal friends from attending to his wants.'),
(996286,34,44,24,24,'Some days later Felix came with his wife Drusilla, who was Jewish, and, sending for Paul, listened to what he had to say about faith in Christ Jesus.'),
(996287,34,44,24,25,'But, while Paul was speaking at length about righteousness, self-control, and the coming judgment, Felix became terrified, and interrupted him – ‘Go for the present, but, when I find an opportunity, I will send for you again.’'),
(996288,34,44,24,26,'He was hoping, too, for a bribe from Paul, and so he used to send for him frequently and talk with him.'),
(996289,34,44,24,27,'But, after the lapse of two years, Felix was succeeded by Porcius Festus; and, wishing to gain popularity with the Jewish leaders, he left Paul a prisoner.'),
(996290,34,44,25,1,'Three days after Festus had arrived in his province, he left Caesarea and went up to Jerusalem.'),
(996291,34,44,25,2,'There the chief priests and the leading men among the Jews laid an information before him against Paul,'),
(996292,34,44,25,3,'and asked a favour of him, to Paul’s injury – to have Paul brought to Jerusalem. All the while they were plotting to make away with him on the road.'),
(996293,34,44,25,4,'But Festus answered that Paul was in prison at Caesarea, and that he himself would be leaving for that place shortly.'),
(996294,34,44,25,5,'‘So let the influential men among you,’ he said, ‘go down with me, and if there is anything amiss in the man, charge him formally with it.’'),
(996295,34,44,25,6,'After staying among them some eight or ten days, Festus went down to Caesarea. The next day he took his seat on the Bench, and ordered Paul to be brought before him.'),
(996296,34,44,25,7,'On Paul’s appearance, the Jewish leaders who had come down from Jerusalem surrounded him, and made many serious charges, which they failed to establish.'),
(996297,34,44,25,8,'Paul’s answer to the charge was – “I have not committed any offence against the Jewish Law, or the Temple, or the Emperor.”'),
(996298,34,44,25,9,'But, as Festus wished to gain popularity with the Jews, he interrupted Paul with the question, ‘Are you willing to go up to Jerusalem and be tried on these charges before me there?’'),
(996299,34,44,25,10,'‘No,’ replied Paul, ‘I am standing at the Emperor’s court, where I ought to be tried. I have not wronged the Jews, as you yourself are well aware.'),
(996300,34,44,25,11,'If, however, I am breaking the law and have committed any offence deserving death, I do not ask to escape the penalty; but, if there is nothing in the accusations of these people, no one has the power to give me up to them. I appeal to the Emperor.’'),
(996301,34,44,25,12,'Festus, after conferring with his Council, answered, ‘You have appealed to the Emperor; to the Emperor you will go.’'),
(996302,34,44,25,13,'Some days later King Agrippa and Bernice came down to Caesarea, and paid a visit of congratulation to Festus;'),
(996303,34,44,25,14,'and, as they were staying there for several days, Festus laid Paul’s case before the king. ‘There is a man here,’ he said, ‘left a prisoner by Felix,'),
(996304,34,44,25,15,'about whom, when I came to Jerusalem, the Jewish chief priest and the elders laid an information, demanding judgment against him.'),
(996305,34,44,25,16,'My answer to them was, that it was not the practice of Romans to give up anyone to their accusers until the accused had met them face to face, and had also had an opportunity of answering the charges brought against them.'),
(996306,34,44,25,17,'So they met here, and without loss of time I took my seat on the Bench the very next day, and ordered the man to be brought before me.'),
(996307,34,44,25,18,'But, when his accusers came forward, they brought no charge of wrong-doing such as I had expected;'),
(996308,34,44,25,19,'but I found that there were certain questions in dispute between them about their own religion, and about some dead man called Jesus, whom Paul declared to be alive.'),
(996309,34,44,25,20,'And, as I was at a loss how to enquire into questions of this kind, I asked Paul if he were willing to go up to Jerusalem, and be put on trial there.'),
(996310,34,44,25,21,'Paul, however, appealed to have his case reserved for the consideration of his August Majesty, so I ordered him to be detained in custody, until I could send him to the Emperor.’'),
(996311,34,44,25,22,'‘I should like to hear this man myself,’ Agrippa said to Festus.'),
(996312,34,44,25,23,'So the next day, when Agrippa and Bernice had come in full state and had entered the Audience Chamber, with the superior officers and the principal people of the city, by the order of Festus Paul was brought before them.'),
(996313,34,44,25,24,'Then Festus said, ‘King Agrippa, and all here present, you see before you the man about whom the whole Jewish people have applied to me, both at Jerusalem and here, loudly asserting that he ought not to be allowed to live.'),
(996314,34,44,25,25,'I found, however, that he had not done anything deserving death; so, as he had himself appealed to his August Majesty, I decided to send him.'),
(996315,34,44,25,26,'But I have nothing definite to write about him to my Imperial Master; and for that reason I have brought him before you all, and especially before you, King Agrippa, that, after examining him, I may have something to write.'),
(996316,34,44,25,27,'For it seems to me absurd to send a prisoner, without at the same time stating the charges made against him.’'),
(996317,34,44,26,1,'Turning to Paul, Agrippa said, ‘You are at liberty to speak for yourself.’ Then Paul stretched out his hand and began his defence.'),
(996318,34,44,26,2,'‘I have been congratulating myself, King Agrippa,’ he said, ‘that it is before you that I have to make my defence today, with regard to all the charges brought against me by my own people,'),
(996319,34,44,26,3,'especially as you are so well-versed in all the customs and questions of the Jewish world. I beg you therefore to give me a patient hearing.'),
(996320,34,44,26,4,'My life, then, from youth upwards, was passed, from the very first, among my own nation, and in Jerusalem, and is within the knowledge of all Jews;'),
(996321,34,44,26,5,'and they have always known – if they choose to give evidence – that, in accordance with the very strictest form of our religion, I lived a true Pharisee.'),
(996322,34,44,26,6,'Even now, it is because of my hope in the promise given by God to our ancestors that I stand here on my trial –'),
(996323,34,44,26,7,'A promise which our twelve tribes, by earnest service night and day, hope to see fulfilled. It is for this hope, your Majesty, that I am accused – and by Jews themselves!'),
(996324,34,44,26,8,'Why do you all hold it incredible that God should raise the dead?'),
(996325,34,44,26,9,'I myself, it is true, once thought it my duty to oppose in every way the name of Jesus of Nazareth;'),
(996326,34,44,26,10,'and I actually did so at Jerusalem. Acting on the authority of the chief priests, I myself threw many of the people of Christ into prison, and, when it was proposed to put them to death, I gave my vote for it.'),
(996327,34,44,26,11,'Time after time, in every synagogue, I tried by punishments to force them to blaspheme. So frantic was I against them, that I pursued them even to towns beyond our borders.'),
(996328,34,44,26,12,'It was while I was traveling to Damascus on an errand of this kind, entrusted with full powers by the chief priests,'),
(996329,34,44,26,13,'that at midday, your Majesty, I saw right in my path, coming from the heavens, a light brighter than the glare of the sun, which shone all round me and those traveling with me.'),
(996330,34,44,26,14,'We all fell to the ground, and then I heard a voice saying to me in Hebrew –'),
(996331,34,44,26,15,'“Who are you, Lord?” I asked. And the Lord said,'),
(996332,34,44,26,19,'After that, King Agrippa, I did not fail to obey the heavenly vision;'),
(996333,34,44,26,20,'on the contrary, first to those at Damascus and Jerusalem, and then through the whole of Judea, and to the Gentiles as well, I began to preach repentance and conversion to God, and a life befitting that repentance.'),
(996334,34,44,26,21,'This is why some men seized me in the Temple, and made attempts on my life.'),
(996335,34,44,26,22,'However I have received help from God to this very day, and so stand here, and bear my testimony to high and low alike – without adding a word to what the prophets, as well as Moses, declared should happen –'),
(996336,34,44,26,23,'That the Christ must suffer, and that, by rising from the dead, he was destined to be the first to bring news of light, not only to our nation, but also to the Gentiles.’'),
(996337,34,44,26,24,'While Paul was making this defence, Festus called out loudly, ‘You are mad, Paul; your great learning is driving you mad.’'),
(996338,34,44,26,25,'‘I am not mad, your Excellency,’ he replied. ‘On the contrary, the statements that I am making are true and sober.'),
(996339,34,44,26,26,'Indeed, the king knows about these matters, so I speak before him without constraint. I am sure that there is nothing whatever of what I have been telling him that has escaped his attention; for all this has not been done in a corner.'),
(996340,34,44,26,27,'King Agrippa, do you believe the prophets? I know you do.’'),
(996341,34,44,26,28,'But Agrippa said to Paul, ‘You are soon trying to make a Christian of me!’'),
(996342,34,44,26,29,'‘Whether it is soon or late,’ answered Paul, ‘I pray to God that not only you, but all who are listening to me, might today become just what I am myself – except for these chains!’'),
(996343,34,44,26,30,'Then the king rose, with the Governor and Bernice and those who had been sitting with them,'),
(996344,34,44,26,31,'and, after retiring, discussed the case among themselves. ‘There is nothing,’ they said, ‘deserving death or imprisonment in this man’s conduct’;'),
(996345,34,44,26,32,'and, speaking to Festus, Agrippa added, ‘The man might have been discharged, if he had not appealed to the Emperor.’'),
(996346,34,44,27,1,'As it was decided that we were to sail to Italy, Paul and some other prisoners were put in charge of a captain of the Augustan Guard, named Julius.'),
(996347,34,44,27,2,'We went on board a ship from Adramyttium, which was on the point of sailing to the ports along the coast of Roman Asia, and put to sea. Aristarchus, a Macedonian from Thessalonica, went with us.'),
(996348,34,44,27,3,'The next day we put in to Sidon, where Julius treated Paul in a friendly manner, and allowed him to go to see his friends and receive their hospitality.'),
(996349,34,44,27,4,'Putting to sea again, we sailed under the lee of Cyprus, because the wind was against us;'),
(996350,34,44,27,5,'and, after crossing the sea of Cilicia and Pamphylia, we reached Myra in Lycia.'),
(996351,34,44,27,6,'There the Roman officer found an Alexandrian ship on her way to Italy, and put us on board of her.'),
(996352,34,44,27,7,'For several days our progress was slow, and it was only with difficulty that we arrived off Cnidus. As the wind was still unfavourable when we came off Cape Salmone, we sailed under the lee of Crete,'),
(996353,34,44,27,8,'and with difficulty, by keeping close in shore, we reached a place called “Fair Havens,” near which was the town of Lasea.'),
(996354,34,44,27,9,'This had taken a considerable time, and sailing was already dangerous, for the Fast was already over; and so Paul gave this warning.'),
(996355,34,44,27,10,'‘My friends,’ he said, ‘I see that this voyage will be attended with injury and much damage, not only to the cargo and the ship, but to our own lives also.’'),
(996356,34,44,27,11,'The Roman officer, however, was more influenced by the captain and the owner than by what was said by Paul.'),
(996357,34,44,27,12,'And, as the harbour was not a suitable one to winter in, the majority were in favour of continuing the voyage, in hope of being able to reach Phoenix, and winter there. Phoenix was a Cretan harbour, open to the north-east and south-east.'),
(996358,34,44,27,13,'So, when a light wind sprang up from the south, thinking that they had found their opportunity, they weighed anchor and kept along the coast of Crete, close in shore.'),
(996359,34,44,27,14,'But shortly afterwards a hurricane came down on us off the land – a north-easter, as it is called.'),
(996360,34,44,27,15,'The ship was caught by it and was unable to keep her head to the wind, so we had to give way and let her drive before it.'),
(996361,34,44,27,16,'Running under the lee of a small island called Cauda, we only just managed to secure the ship’s boat,'),
(996362,34,44,27,17,'and, after hoisting it on board, the men frapped the ship. But, afraid of being driven on to the Syrtis Sands, they lowered the yard, and then drifted.'),
(996363,34,44,27,18,'So violently were we tossed about by the storm, that the next day they began throwing the cargo overboard,'),
(996364,34,44,27,19,'and, on the following day, threw out the ship’s tackle with their own hands.'),
(996365,34,44,27,20,'As neither sun nor stars were visible for several days, and, as the gale still continued severe, all hope of our being saved was at last abandoned.'),
(996366,34,44,27,21,'It was then, when they had gone a long time without food, that Paul came forward, and said, ‘My friends, you should have listened to me, and not have sailed from Crete and so incurred this injury and damage.'),
(996367,34,44,27,22,'Yet, even as things are, I beg you not to lose courage, for there will not be a single life lost among you – only the ship.'),
(996368,34,44,27,23,'For last night an angel of the God to whom I belong, and whom I serve, stood by me, and said –'),
(996369,34,44,27,24,'“Have no fear, Paul; you must appear before the Emperor, and God himself has given you the lives of all your fellow voyagers.”'),
(996370,34,44,27,25,'Therefore, courage, my friends! For I believe God, that everything will happen exactly as I have been told.'),
(996371,34,44,27,26,'We will, however, have to be driven on some island.’'),
(996372,34,44,27,27,'It was now the fourteenth night of the storm, and we were drifting about in the Adriatic Sea, when, about midnight, the sailors began to suspect that they were drawing near land.'),
(996373,34,44,27,28,'So they took soundings, and found twenty fathoms of water. After waiting a little, they took soundings again, and found fifteen fathoms.'),
(996374,34,44,27,29,'Then, as they were afraid of our being driven on some rocky coast, they let go four anchors from the stern, and longed for daylight.'),
(996375,34,44,27,30,'The sailors wanted to leave the ship, and had lowered the boat, on pretence of running out anchors from the bows,'),
(996376,34,44,27,31,'when Paul said to the Roman officer and his men, ‘Unless the sailors remain on board, you cannot be saved.’'),
(996377,34,44,27,32,'So the soldiers cut the ropes which held the boat, and let her drift away.'),
(996378,34,44,27,33,'In the interval before daybreak Paul kept urging them all to take something to eat.'),
(996379,34,44,27,34,'So I beg you to take something to eat; your safety depends on it, for not one of you will lose even a hair of his head.’'),
(996380,34,44,27,35,'With these words he took some bread, and, after saying the thanksgiving to God before them all, broke it in pieces, and began to eat;'),
(996381,34,44,27,36,'and the men all felt cheered and had something to eat themselves.'),
(996382,34,44,27,37,'There were about seventy-six of us on board, all told.'),
(996383,34,44,27,38,'After satisfying their hunger, they further lightened the ship by throwing the grain into the sea.'),
(996384,34,44,27,39,'When daylight came, they could not make out what land it was, but, observing a creek in which there was a beach, they consulted as to whether they could run the ship safely into it.'),
(996385,34,44,27,40,'Then they cast off, and abandoned the anchors, and at the same time unlashed the gear of the steering oars, hoisted the foresail to the wind, and made for the beach.'),
(996386,34,44,27,41,'They got, however, into a kind of channel, and there ran the ship aground. The bows stuck fast and could not be moved, while the stern began breaking up under the strain.'),
(996387,34,44,27,42,'The advice of the soldiers was that the prisoners should be killed, so that none of them could swim away and make their escape.'),
(996388,34,44,27,43,'But the Roman officer, anxious to save Paul, prevented their carrying out their intention, and ordered that those who could swim should be the first to jump into the sea and try to reach the shore;'),
(996389,34,44,27,44,'and that the rest should follow, some on planks, and others on different pieces of the ship. In these various ways everyone managed to get safely ashore.'),
(996390,34,44,28,1,'When we were all safe, we found that the island was called Malta.'),
(996391,34,44,28,2,'The island’s people showed us marked kindness, for they lit a fire and took us all under shelter, because it had come on to rain and was cold.'),
(996392,34,44,28,3,'Paul had gathered a quantity of dry sticks and laid them on the fire, when a poisonous snake, driven out by the heat, fastened on his hand.'),
(996393,34,44,28,4,'When the islanders saw the creature hanging from his hand, they said to one another, ‘Evidently this man is a murderer, for though he has been saved from the sea, Justice has not allowed him to live.’'),
(996394,34,44,28,5,'However, Paul shook the creature off into the fire and took no harm.'),
(996395,34,44,28,6,'The islanders were expecting inflammation to set in, or that he would suddenly fall dead; but, after waiting for a long time, and seeing that there was nothing amiss with him, they changed their minds and said that he was a God.'),
(996396,34,44,28,7,'In that region there was an estate belonging to the Governor of the island, whose name was Publius. He took us up to his house, and for three days entertained us most courteously.'),
(996397,34,44,28,8,'It happened that the father of Publius was lying ill of fever and dysentery. So Paul went to see him; and, after praying, he placed his hands on him and cured him.'),
(996398,34,44,28,9,'After this, all the people in the island who had any illness came to Paul, and were cured.'),
(996399,34,44,28,10,'They also presented us with many gifts, and when we set sail they put supplies of necessaries on board.'),
(996400,34,44,28,11,'After three months, we set sail in a ship that had wintered in the island. She was an Alexandrian vessel, and had the Twin sons of Zeus for her figure-head.'),
(996401,34,44,28,12,'We put in at Syracuse and stayed there three days,'),
(996402,34,44,28,13,'and from there we worked to windward and so got to Rhegium. A day later a south wind sprang up and took us to Puteoli in two days.'),
(996403,34,44,28,14,'There we found some of the Lord’s followers, and were urged to stay a week with them; after which we went on to Rome.'),
(996404,34,44,28,15,'The followers there had heard about us, and came out as far as the Market of Appius and the Three Taverns to meet us. At sight of them Paul thanked God and was much cheered.'),
(996405,34,44,28,16,'On our reaching Rome, Paul was allowed to live by himself, except for the soldier who was in charge of him.'),
(996406,34,44,28,17,'Three days after our arrival, Paul invited the leading Jews to meet him; and, when they came, he said, ‘Brothers, although I had done nothing hostile to the interests of our nation or to our ancestral customs, yet I was sent from Jerusalem as a prisoner, and handed over to the Romans.'),
(996407,34,44,28,18,'The Romans, when they had examined me, were ready to release me, because there was nothing in my conduct deserving death.'),
(996408,34,44,28,19,'But, as the Jewish leaders opposed my release, I was compelled to appeal to the Emperor – not, indeed, that I had any charge to make against my own nation.'),
(996409,34,44,28,20,'This, then, is my reason for urging you to come to see me and talk with me; because it is for the sake of the hope of Israel that I am here in chains.’'),
(996410,34,44,28,21,'‘We,’ was their reply, ‘have not had any letter about you from Judea, nor have any of our fellow Jews come and reported or said anything bad about you.'),
(996411,34,44,28,22,'But we will be glad to hear from you what your views are, for, with regard to this sect, we are well aware that it is spoken against on all sides.’'),
(996412,34,44,28,23,'They then fixed a day with him, and came to the place where he was staying, in even larger numbers, when Paul proceeded to lay the subject before them. He bore his testimony to the kingdom of God, and tried to convince them about Jesus, by arguments drawn from the Law of Moses and from the prophets – speaking from morning until evening.'),
(996413,34,44,28,24,'Some were inclined to accept what he said; others, however, rejected it.'),
(996414,34,44,28,25,'So, as they disagreed among themselves, they began to disperse, Paul adding only –'),
(996415,34,44,28,26,'Go to this nation and say:'),
(996416,34,44,28,27,'For the mind of this nation has grown dense,'),
(996417,34,44,28,28,'Understand, then, that this salvation of God was sent for the Gentiles; and they will listen.’'),
(996418,34,44,28,30,'For two whole years Paul stayed in a house which he rented for himself, welcoming all who came to see him,'),
(996419,34,44,28,31,'proclaiming the kingdom of God, and teaching about the Lord Jesus Christ, with perfect fearlessness, unhindered.'),
(996420,34,45,1,1,'From Paul, a servant of Jesus Christ, who has been called to become an apostle, and has been set apart to tell God’s good news.'),
(996421,34,45,1,2,'This good news God promised long ago through his prophets in the sacred scriptures,'),
(996422,34,45,1,3,'concerning his Son, Jesus Christ, our Lord; who, as to his human nature, was descended from David,'),
(996423,34,45,1,4,'but, as to the spirit of holiness within him, was miraculously designated Son of God by his resurrection from the dead.'),
(996424,34,45,1,5,'Through him we received the gift of the apostolic office, to win submission to the faith among all nations for the glory of his name.'),
(996425,34,45,1,6,'And among these nations are you – you who have been called to belong to Jesus Christ.'),
(996426,34,45,1,7,'To all in Rome who are dear to God and have been called to become Christ’s people, may God, our Father, and the Lord Jesus Christ bless you and give you peace.'),
(996427,34,45,1,8,'First, I thank my God through Jesus Christ for you all, because the report of your faith is spreading throughout the world.'),
(996428,34,45,1,9,'God, to whom I offer the worship of my soul as I tell the goodness of his Son, is my witness how constantly I mention you when I pray,'),
(996429,34,45,1,10,'asking that, if he be willing, I may some day at last find the way open to visit you.'),
(996430,34,45,1,11,'For I long to see you, in order to impart to you some spiritual gift and so give you fresh strength –'),
(996431,34,45,1,12,'or rather that both you and I may find encouragement in each other’s faith.'),
(996432,34,45,1,13,'I want you to know, my friends, that I have many times intended coming to see you – but until now I have been prevented – that I might find among you some fruit of my labours, as I have already among the other nations.'),
(996433,34,45,1,14,'I have a duty to both the Greek and the barbarian, to both the cultured and the ignorant.'),
(996434,34,45,1,15,'And so, for my part, I am ready to tell the good news to you also who are in Rome.'),
(996435,34,45,1,16,'For I am not ashamed of the good news; it is the power of God which brings salvation to everyone who believes, to the Jew first, but also to the Greek.'),
(996436,34,45,1,17,'For in it there is a revelation of the divine righteousness resulting from faith and leading on to faith; as scripture says – “Through faith the righteous will find life.”'),
(996437,34,45,1,18,'So, too, there is a revelation from heaven of the divine wrath against every form of ungodliness and wickedness on the part of those people who, by their wicked lives, are stifling the truth.'),
(996438,34,45,1,19,'This is so, because what can be known about God is plain to them; for God himself has made it plain.'),
(996439,34,45,1,20,'For ever since the creation of the universe God’s invisible attributes – his everlasting power and divinity – are to be seen and studied in his works, so that people have no excuse;'),
(996440,34,45,1,21,'because, although they learned to know God, yet they did not offer him as God either praise or thanksgiving. Their speculations about him proved futile, and their undiscerning minds were darkened.'),
(996441,34,45,1,22,'Professing to be wise, they showed themselves fools;'),
(996442,34,45,1,23,'and they transformed the glory of the immortal God into the likeness of mortal humans, and of birds, and beasts, and reptiles.'),
(996443,34,45,1,24,'Therefore God abandoned them to impurity, letting them follow the cravings of their hearts, until they dishonoured their own bodies;'),
(996444,34,45,1,25,'for they had substituted a lie for the truth about God, and had reverenced and worshiped created things more than the Creator, who is to be praised for ever. Amen.'),
(996445,34,45,1,26,'That, I say, is why God abandoned them to degrading passions. Even the women among them perverted the natural use of their bodies to the unnatural;'),
(996446,34,45,1,27,'while the men, disregarding that for which women were intended by nature, were consumed with passion for one another. Men indulged in vile practices with men, and incurred in their own persons the inevitable penalty for their perverseness.'),
(996447,34,45,1,28,'Then, as they would not keep God before their minds, God abandoned them to depraved thoughts, so that they did all kinds of shameful things.'),
(996448,34,45,1,29,'They revelled in every form of wickedness, evil, greed, vice. Their lives were full of envy, murder, quarrelling, treachery, malice.'),
(996449,34,45,1,30,'They became back-biters, slanderers, impious, insolent, boastful. They devised new sins. They disobeyed their parents.'),
(996450,34,45,1,31,'They were undiscerning, untrustworthy, without natural affection or pity.'),
(996451,34,45,1,32,'Well aware of God’s decree, that those who do such things deserve to die, not only are they guilty of them themselves, but they even applaud those who do them.'),
(996452,34,45,2,1,'Therefore you have nothing to say in your own defence, whoever you are who set yourself up as a judge. In judging others you condemn yourself, for you who set yourself up as a judge do the very same things.'),
(996453,34,45,2,2,'And we know that God’s judgment falls unerringly on those who do them.'),
(996454,34,45,2,3,'You who judge those that do such things and yet are yourself guilty of them – do you suppose that you of all people will escape God’s judgment?'),
(996455,34,45,2,4,'Or do you think lightly of his abundant kindness, patience, and forbearance, not realising that his kindness is meant to lead you to repentance?'),
(996456,34,45,2,5,'Hard-hearted and impenitent as you are, you are storing up for yourself wrath on the day of wrath, when God’s justice as a judge will be revealed;'),
(996457,34,45,2,6,'for he will give to everyone what their actions deserve.'),
(996458,34,45,2,7,'To those who, by perseverance in doing good, aim at glory, honour, and all that is imperishable, he will give immortal life;'),
(996459,34,45,2,8,'while as to those who are factious, and disobedient to truth but obedient to evil, wrath and anger, distress and despair,'),
(996460,34,45,2,9,'will fall on every human being who persists in wrong-doing – on the Jew first, but also on the Greek.'),
(996461,34,45,2,10,'But there will be glory, honour, and peace for everyone who does right – for the Jew first, but also for the Greek,'),
(996462,34,45,2,11,'since God shows no partiality.'),
(996463,34,45,2,12,'All who, when they sin, are without Law will also perish without Law; while all who, when they sin, are under Law, will be judged as being under Law.'),
(996464,34,45,2,13,'It is not those who hear the words of a Law that are righteous before God, but it is those who obey it that will be pronounced righteous.'),
(996465,34,45,2,14,'When Gentiles, who have no Law, do instinctively what the Law requires, they, though they have no Law, are a Law to themselves;'),
(996466,34,45,2,15,'for they show the demands of the Law written on their hearts; their consciences corroborating it, while in their thoughts they argue either in self-accusation or, it may be, in self-defence –'),
(996467,34,45,2,16,'on the day when God passes judgment on people’s inmost lives, as the good news that I tell declares that he will do through Christ Jesus.'),
(996468,34,45,2,17,'But, perhaps, you bear the name of “Jew,” and are relying on Law, and boast of belonging to God, and understand his will,'),
(996469,34,45,2,18,'and, having been carefully instructed from the Law, have learned to appreciate the finer moral distinctions.'),
(996470,34,45,2,19,'Perhaps you are confident that you are a guide to the blind, a light to those who are in the dark, an instructor of the unintelligent,'),
(996471,34,45,2,20,'and a teacher of the childish, because in the Law you possess the outline of all knowledge and truth.'),
(996472,34,45,2,21,'Why, then, you teacher of others, don’t you teach yourself? Do you preach against stealing, and yet steal?'),
(996473,34,45,2,22,'Do you forbid adultery, and yet commit adultery? Do you loathe idols, and yet plunder temples?'),
(996474,34,45,2,23,'Boasting, as you do, of your Law, do you dishonour God by breaking the Law?'),
(996475,34,45,2,24,'For, as scripture says – “The Gentiles insult God’s name because of you”!'),
(996476,34,45,2,25,'Circumcision has its value, if you are obeying the Law. But, if you are a breaker of the Law, your circumcision is no better than uncircumcision.'),
(996477,34,45,2,26,'If, then, an uncircumcised man pays regard to the requirements of the Law, won’t he, although not circumcised, be regarded by God as if he were?'),
(996478,34,45,2,27,'Indeed, the person who, owing to his birth, remains uncircumcised, and yet scrupulously obeys the Law, will condemn you, who, for all your written Law and your circumcision, are yet a breaker of the Law.'),
(996479,34,45,2,28,'For a man who is only a Jew outwardly is not a real Jew; nor is outward bodily circumcision real circumcision. The real Jew is the person who is a Jew in soul;'),
(996480,34,45,2,29,'and the real circumcision is the circumcision of the heart, a spiritual and not a literal thing. Such a person wins praise from God, though not from people.'),
(996481,34,45,3,1,'What is the advantage, then, of being a Jew? Or what is the good of circumcision?'),
(996482,34,45,3,2,'Great in every way. First of all, because the Jews were entrusted with God’s utterances.'),
(996483,34,45,3,3,'What follows then? Some, no doubt, showed a want of faith; but will their want of faith make God break faith? Heaven forbid!'),
(996484,34,45,3,4,'God must prove true, though everyone prove a liar! As scripture says of God – “That you may be pronounced righteous in what you say, and gain your cause when people would judge you.”'),
(996485,34,45,3,5,'But what if our wrong-doing makes God’s righteousness all the clearer? Will God be wrong in inflicting punishment? (I can but speak as a person.) Heaven forbid!'),
(996486,34,45,3,6,'Otherwise how can God judge the world?'),
(996487,34,45,3,7,'But, if my falsehood redounds to the glory of God, by making his truthfulness more apparent, why am I like others, still condemned as a sinner?'),
(996488,34,45,3,8,'Why should we not say – as some people slanderously assert that we do say – “Let us do evil that good may come”? The condemnation of such people is indeed just!'),
(996489,34,45,3,9,'What follows, then? Are we Jews in any way superior to others? Not at all. Our indictment against both Jews and Greeks was that all alike were in subjection to sin.'),
(996490,34,45,3,10,'As scripture says –'),
(996491,34,45,3,11,'not one who understands,'),
(996492,34,45,3,12,'They have all gone astray;'),
(996493,34,45,3,13,'“Their throats are like opened graves;'),
(996494,34,45,3,14,'“And their mouths are full of bitter curses.”'),
(996495,34,45,3,15,'“Swift are their feet to shed blood.'),
(996496,34,45,3,16,'Distress and trouble dog their steps,'),
(996497,34,45,3,17,'and the path of peace they do not know.”'),
(996498,34,45,3,18,'“The fear of God is not before their eyes.”'),
(996499,34,45,3,19,'Now we know that everything said in the Law is addressed to those who are under its authority, in order that every mouth may be closed, and to bring the whole world under God’s judgment.'),
(996500,34,45,3,20,'For no human being will be pronounced righteous before God as the result of obedience to Law; for it is Law that shows what sin is.');
INSERT INTO verses (id, version_id, book_id, chapter, verse, text) VALUES
(996501,34,45,3,21,'But now, quite apart from Law, the divine righteousness stands revealed, and to it the Law and the prophets bear witness –'),
(996502,34,45,3,22,'the divine righteousness which is bestowed, through faith in Jesus Christ, on all, without distinction, who believe in him.'),
(996503,34,45,3,23,'For all have sinned, and all fall short of God’s glorious ideal,'),
(996504,34,45,3,24,'but, in his loving kindness, are being freely pronounced righteous through the deliverance found in Christ Jesus.'),
(996505,34,45,3,25,'For God set him before the world, to be, by the shedding of his blood, a means of reconciliation through faith. And this God did to prove his righteousness, and because, in his forbearance, he had passed over the sins that people had previously committed;'),
(996506,34,45,3,26,'as a proof, I repeat, at the present time, of his own righteousness, that he might be righteous in our eyes, and might pronounce righteous the person who takes their stand on faith in Jesus.'),
(996507,34,45,3,27,'What, then, becomes of our boasting? It is excluded. By what sort of Law? A Law requiring obedience? No, a Law requiring faith.'),
(996508,34,45,3,28,'For we conclude that a person is pronounced righteous on the ground of faith, quite apart from obedience to Law.'),
(996509,34,45,3,29,'Or can it be that God is the God only of the Jews? Isn’t he also the God of the Gentiles?'),
(996510,34,45,3,30,'Yes, of the Gentiles also, since there is only one God, and he will pronounce those who are circumcised righteous as the result of faith, and also those who are uncircumcised on their showing the same faith.'),
(996511,34,45,3,31,'Do we, then, use this faith to abolish Law? Heaven forbid! No, we establish Law.'),
(996512,34,45,4,1,'What then, it may be asked, are we to say about Abraham, the ancestor of our nation?'),
(996513,34,45,4,2,'If he was pronounced righteous as the result of obedience, then he has something to boast of. Yes, but not before God.'),
(996514,34,45,4,3,'For what are the words of scripture? “Abraham had faith in God, and his faith was regarded by God as righteousness.”'),
(996515,34,45,4,4,'Now wages are regarded as due to the person who works, not as a favour, but as a debt;'),
(996516,34,45,4,5,'while, as for the person who does not rely on their obedience, but has faith in him who can pronounce the godless righteous, their faith is regarded by God as righteousness.'),
(996517,34,45,4,6,'In precisely the same way David speaks of the blessing pronounced on the person who is regarded by God as righteous apart from actions –'),
(996518,34,45,4,7,'“Blessed are those whose wrong-doings have been forgiven and over whose sins a veil has been drawn!'),
(996519,34,45,4,8,'Blessed the man whom the Lord will never regard as sinful!”'),
(996520,34,45,4,9,'Is this blessing, then, pronounced on the circumcised only or on the uncircumcised as well? We say that – “Abraham’s faith was regarded by God as righteousness.”'),
(996521,34,45,4,10,'Under what circumstances, then, did this take place? After his circumcision or before it?'),
(996522,34,45,4,11,'Not after, but before. And it was as a sign of this that he received the rite of circumcision – to show the righteousness due to the faith of an uncircumcised man – in order that he might be the father of all who have faith in God even when uncircumcised, so that they also may be regarded by God as righteous;'),
(996523,34,45,4,12,'as well as father of the circumcised – to those who are not only circumcised, but who also follow our father Abraham in that faith which he had while still uncircumcised.'),
(996524,34,45,4,13,'For the promise that he should inherit the world did not come to Abraham or his descendants through Law, but through the righteousness due to faith.'),
(996525,34,45,4,14,'If those who take their stand on Law are to inherit the world, then faith is robbed of its meaning and the promise comes to nothing!'),
(996526,34,45,4,15,'Law entails punishment; but, where no Law exists, no breach of it is possible.'),
(996527,34,45,4,16,'That is why everything is made to depend on faith: so that everything may be God’s gift, and in order that the fulfilment of the promise may be made certain for all Abraham’s descendants – not only for those who take their stand on the Law, but also for those who take their stand on the faith of Abraham. (He is the Father of us all;'),
(996528,34,45,4,17,'as scripture says – “I have made you the Father of many nations.”) And this they do in the sight of that God in whom Abraham had faith, and who gives life to the dead, and speaks of what does not yet exist as if it did.'),
(996529,34,45,4,18,'With no ground for hope, Abraham, sustained by hope, put faith in God; in order that, in fulfilment of the words – “So many will your descendants be,” he might become “the Father of many nations.”'),
(996530,34,45,4,19,'Though he was nearly a hundred years old, yet his faith did not fail him, even when he thought of his own body, then utterly worn out, and remembered that Sarah was past bearing children.'),
(996531,34,45,4,20,'He was not led by want of faith to doubt God’s promise.'),
(996532,34,45,4,21,'On the contrary, his faith gave him strength; and he praised God, in the firm conviction that what God has promised he is also able to carry out.'),
(996533,34,45,4,22,'And therefore his faith “was regarded as righteousness.”'),
(996534,34,45,4,23,'Now these words – “it was regarded as righteousness” – were not written with reference to Abraham only;'),
(996535,34,45,4,24,'but also with reference to us. Our faith, too, will be regarded by God in the same light, if we have faith in him who raised Jesus, our Lord, from the dead;'),
(996536,34,45,4,25,'for Jesus was given up to death to atone for our offences, and was raised to life that we might be pronounced righteous.'),
(996537,34,45,5,1,'Therefore, having been pronounced righteous as the result of faith, let us enjoy peace with God through Jesus Christ, our Lord.'),
(996538,34,45,5,2,'It is through him that, by reason of our faith, we have obtained admission to that place in God’s favour in which we now stand. So let us exult in our hope of attaining God’s glorious ideal.'),
(996539,34,45,5,3,'And not only that, but let us also exult in our troubles;'),
(996540,34,45,5,4,'for we know that trouble develops endurance, and endurance strength of character, and strength of character hope,'),
(996541,34,45,5,5,'and that hope never disappoints. For the love of God has filled our hearts through the Holy Spirit which was given us;'),
(996542,34,45,5,6,'seeing that, while we were still powerless, Christ, in God’s good time, died on behalf of the godless.'),
(996543,34,45,5,7,'Even for an upright person scarcely anyone will die. For a really good person perhaps someone might even dare to die.'),
(996544,34,45,5,8,'But God puts his love for us beyond all doubt by the fact that Christ died on our behalf while we were still sinners.'),
(996545,34,45,5,9,'Much more, then, now that we have been pronounced righteous by virtue of the shedding of his blood, will we be saved through him from the wrath of God.'),
(996546,34,45,5,10,'For if, when we were God’s enemies, we were reconciled to him through the death of his Son, much more, now that we have become reconciled, will we be saved by virtue of Christ’s life.'),
(996547,34,45,5,11,'And not only that, but we exult in God, through Jesus Christ, our Lord, through whom we have now obtained this reconciliation.'),
(996548,34,45,5,12,'Therefore, just as sin came into the world through one man, and through sin came death; so, also, death spread to all humanity, because every person has sinned.'),
(996549,34,45,5,13,'Even before the time of the Law there was sin in the world; but sin cannot be charged against someone where no Law exists.'),
(996550,34,45,5,14,'Yet, from Adam to Moses, death reigned even over those whose sin was not a breach of a law, as Adam’s was. And Adam foreshadows the One to come.'),
(996551,34,45,5,15,'But there is a contrast between Adam’s offence and God’s gracious gift. For, if by reason of the offence of the one man the whole human race died, far more were the loving kindness of God, and the gift given in the loving kindness of the one man, Jesus Christ, lavished on the whole human race.'),
(996552,34,45,5,16,'There is a contrast, too, between the gift and the results of the one man’s sin. The judgment, which followed on the one man’s sin, resulted in condemnation, but God’s gracious gift, which followed on many offences, resulted in a decree of righteousness.'),
(996553,34,45,5,17,'For if, by reason of the offence of the one man, death reigned through that one man, far more will those, on whom God’s loving kindness and his gift of righteousness are lavished, find life, and reign through the one man, Jesus Christ.'),
(996554,34,45,5,18,'Briefly then, just as a single offence resulted for all humanity in condemnation, so, too, a single decree of righteousness resulted for all humanity in that declaration of righteousness which brings life.'),
(996555,34,45,5,19,'For, as through the disobedience of the one man the whole human race was rendered sinful, so, too, through the obedience of the one, the whole human race will be rendered righteous.'),
(996556,34,45,5,20,'Law was introduced in order that offences might be multiplied. But, where sins were multiplied, the loving kindness of God was lavished the more,'),
(996557,34,45,5,21,'in order than, just as sin had reigned in the realm of death, so, too, might Loving-kindness reign through righteousness, and result in eternal life, through Jesus Christ, our Lord.'),
(996558,34,45,6,1,'What are we to say, then? Are we to continue to sin, in order that God’s loving kindness may be multiplied?'),
(996559,34,45,6,2,'Heaven forbid! We became dead to sin, and how can we go on living in it?'),
(996560,34,45,6,3,'Or can it be that you do not know that all of us, who were baptized into union with Christ Jesus, in our baptism shared his death?'),
(996561,34,45,6,4,'Consequently, through sharing his death in our baptism, we were buried with him; so that, just as Christ was raised from the dead by a manifestation of the Father’s power, so we also may live a new life.'),
(996562,34,45,6,5,'If we have become united with him by the act symbolic of his death, surely we will also become united with him by the act symbolic of his resurrection.'),
(996563,34,45,6,6,'We recognise the truth that our old self was crucified with Christ, in order that the body, the stronghold of sin, might be rendered powerless, so that we should no longer be slaves to sin.'),
(996564,34,45,6,7,'For the man who has so died has been pronounced righteous and released from sin.'),
(996565,34,45,6,8,'And our belief is, that, as we have shared Christ’s death, we will also share his life.'),
(996566,34,45,6,9,'We know, indeed, that Christ, having once risen from the dead, will not die again. Death has power over him no longer.'),
(996567,34,45,6,10,'For the death that he died was a death to sin, once and for all. But the life that he now lives, he lives for God.'),
(996568,34,45,6,11,'So let it be with you – regard yourselves as dead to sin, but as living for God, through union with Christ Jesus.'),
(996569,34,45,6,12,'Therefore do not let sin reign in your mortal bodies and compel you to obey its cravings.'),
(996570,34,45,6,13,'Do not offer any part of your bodies to sin, in the cause of unrighteousness, but once for all offer yourselves to God (as those who, though once dead, now have life), and devote every part of your bodies to the cause of righteousness.'),
(996571,34,45,6,14,'For sin will not lord it over you. You are living under the reign, not of Law, but of love.'),
(996572,34,45,6,15,'What follows, then? Are we to sin because we are living under the reign of love and not of Law? Heaven forbid!'),
(996573,34,45,6,16,'Surely you know that, when you offer yourselves as servants, to obey anyone, you are the servants of the person whom you obey, whether the service be a service sin which leads to death, or a service Duty which leads to righteousness.'),
(996574,34,45,6,17,'God be thanked that, though you were once servants of sin, yet you learned to give hearty obedience to that form of doctrine under which you were placed.'),
(996575,34,45,6,18,'Set free from the control of sin, you became servants to righteousness.'),
(996576,34,45,6,19,'I can but speak as people do because of the weakness of your earthly nature. Once you offered every part of your bodies to the service of impurity, and of wickedness, which leads to further wickedness. Now, in the same way, offer them to the service of righteousness, which leads to holiness.'),
(996577,34,45,6,20,'While you were still servants of sin, you were free as regards righteousness.'),
(996578,34,45,6,21,'But what were the fruits that you reaped from those things of which you are now ashamed? For the end of such things is death.'),
(996579,34,45,6,22,'But now that you have been set free from the control of sin, and have become servants to God, the fruit that you reap is an ever increasing holiness, and the end eternal life.'),
(996580,34,45,6,23,'The wages of sin are death, but the gift of God is eternal life, through union with Christ Jesus, our Lord.'),
(996581,34,45,7,1,'Surely, friends, you know (for I am speaking to people who know what Law means) that Law has power over a person only as long as they lives.'),
(996582,34,45,7,2,'For example, by law a married woman is bound to her husband while he is living; but, if her husband dies, she is set free from the law that bound her to him.'),
(996583,34,45,7,3,'If, then, during her husband’s lifetime, she unites herself to another man, she will be called an adulteress; but, if her husband dies, the law has no further hold on her, nor, if she unites herself to another man, is she an adulteress.'),
(996584,34,45,7,4,'And so with you, my friends; as far as the Law was concerned, you underwent death in the crucified body of the Christ, so that you might be united to another, to him who was raised from the dead, in order that our lives might bear fruit for God.'),
(996585,34,45,7,5,'When we were living merely earthly lives, our sinful passions, aroused by the Law, were active in every part of our bodies, with the result that our lives bore fruit for death.'),
(996586,34,45,7,6,'But now we are set free from the Law, because we are dead to that which once kept us under restraint; and so we serve under new, spiritual conditions, and not under old, written regulations.'),
(996587,34,45,7,7,'What are we to say, then? That Law and sin are the same thing? Heaven forbid! On the contrary, I should not have learned what sin is, had not it been for Law. If the Law did not say “You must not covet,” I should not know what it is to covet.'),
(996588,34,45,7,8,'But sin took advantage of the Commandment to arouse in me every form of covetousness, for where there is no consciousness of Law sin shows no sign of life.'),
(996589,34,45,7,9,'There was a time when I myself, unconscious of Law, was alive; but when the Commandment was brought home to me, sin sprang into life, while I died!'),
(996590,34,45,7,10,'The Commandment that should have meant life I found to result in death!'),
(996591,34,45,7,11,'sin took advantage of the Commandment to deceive me, and used it to bring about my death.'),
(996592,34,45,7,12,'And so the Law is holy, and each Commandment is also holy, and just, and good.'),
(996593,34,45,7,13,'Did, then, a thing, which in itself was good, involve death in my case? Heaven forbid! It was sin that involved death; so that, by its use of what I regarded as good to bring about my death, its true nature might appear; and in this way the Commandment showed how intensely sinful sin is.'),
(996594,34,45,7,14,'We know that the Law is spiritual, but I am earthly – sold into slavery to sin.'),
(996595,34,45,7,15,'I do not understand my own actions. For I am so far from habitually doing what I want to do, that I find myself doing the thing that I hate.'),
(996596,34,45,7,16,'But when I do what I want not to do, I am admitting that the Law is right.'),
(996597,34,45,7,17,'This being so, the action is no longer my own, but is done by the sin which is within me.'),
(996598,34,45,7,18,'I know that there is nothing good in me – I mean in my earthly nature. For, although it is easy for me to want to do right, to act rightly is not easy.'),
(996599,34,45,7,19,'I fail to do the good thing that I want to do, but the bad thing that I want not to do – that I habitually do.'),
(996600,34,45,7,20,'But, when I do the thing that I want not to do, the action is no longer my own, but is done by the sin which is within me.'),
(996601,34,45,7,21,'This, then, is the law that I find – when I want to do right, wrong presents itself!'),
(996602,34,45,7,22,'At heart I delight in the Law of God;'),
(996603,34,45,7,23,'but throughout my body I see a different law, one which is in conflict with the law accepted by my reason, and which endeavours to make me a prisoner to that law of sin which exists throughout my body.'),
(996604,34,45,7,24,'Miserable man that I am! Who will deliver me from the body that is bringing me to this death?'),
(996605,34,45,7,25,'Thank God, there is deliverance through Jesus Christ, our Lord! Well then, for myself, with my reason I serve the Law of God, but with my earthly nature the Law of sin.'),
(996606,34,45,8,1,'There is, therefore, now no condemnation for those who are in union with Christ Jesus;'),
(996607,34,45,8,2,'for through your union with Christ Jesus, the Law of the life-giving Spirit has set you free from the Law of sin and death.'),
(996608,34,45,8,3,'What Law could not do, in so far as our earthly nature weakened its action, God did, by sending his own Son, with a nature resembling our sinful nature, to atone for sin. He condemned sin in that earthly nature,'),
(996609,34,45,8,4,'so that the requirements of the Law might be satisfied in us who live now in obedience, not to our earthly nature, but to the Spirit.'),
(996610,34,45,8,5,'They who follow their earthly nature are earthly-minded, while they who follow the Spirit are spiritually minded.'),
(996611,34,45,8,6,'To be earthly-minded means death, to be spiritually minded means life and peace;'),
(996612,34,45,8,7,'because to be earthly-minded is to be an enemy to God, for such a mind does not submit to the Law of God, nor indeed can it do so.'),
(996613,34,45,8,8,'They who are earthly cannot please God.'),
(996614,34,45,8,9,'You, however, are not earthly but spiritual, since the Spirit of God lives within you. Unless a person has the Spirit of Christ, they do not belong to Christ;'),
(996615,34,45,8,10,'but, if Christ is within you, then, though the body is dead as a consequence of sin, the spirit is life as a consequence of righteousness.'),
(996616,34,45,8,11,'And, if the Spirit of him who raised Jesus from the dead lives within you, he who raised Christ Jesus from the dead will give life even to your mortal bodies, through his Spirit living within you.'),
(996617,34,45,8,12,'So then, friends, we owe nothing to our earthly nature, that we should live in obedience to it.'),
(996618,34,45,8,13,'If you live in obedience to your earthly nature, you will inevitably die; but if, by the power of the Spirit, you put an end to the evil habits of the body, you will live.'),
(996619,34,45,8,14,'All who are guided by the Spirit of God are sons of God.'),
(996620,34,45,8,15,'For you did not receive the spirit of a slave, to fill you once more with fear, but the spirit of a son which leads us to cry “Abba, Our Father.”'),
(996621,34,45,8,16,'The Spirit himself unites with our spirits in bearing witness to our being God’s children,'),
(996622,34,45,8,17,'and if children, then heirs – heirs of God, and joint heirs with Christ, since we share Christ’s sufferings in order that we may also share his glory.'),
(996623,34,45,8,18,'I do not count the sufferings of our present life worthy of mention when compared with the glory that is to be revealed and bestowed on us.'),
(996624,34,45,8,19,'All Nature awaits with eager expectation the appearing of the sons of God.'),
(996625,34,45,8,20,'For Nature was made subject to imperfection – not by its own choice, but owing to him who made it so –'),
(996626,34,45,8,21,'yet not without the hope that some day Nature, also, will be set free from enslavement to decay, and will attain to the freedom which will mark the glory of the children of God.'),
(996627,34,45,8,22,'We know, indeed, that all Nature alike has been groaning in the pains of labour to this very hour.'),
(996628,34,45,8,23,'And not Nature only; but we ourselves also, though we have already a first gift of the Spirit – we ourselves are inwardly groaning, while we eagerly await our full adoption as sons – the redemption of our bodies.'),
(996629,34,45,8,24,'By our hope we were saved. But the thing hoped for is no longer an object of hope when it is before our eyes; for who hopes for what is before his eyes?'),
(996630,34,45,8,25,'But when we hope for what is not before our eyes, then we wait for it with patience.'),
(996631,34,45,8,26,'So, also, the Spirit supports us in our weakness. We do not even know how to pray as we should; but the Spirit himself pleads for us in sighs that can find no utterance.'),
(996632,34,45,8,27,'Yet he who searches all our hearts knows what the Spirit’s meaning is, because the pleadings of the Spirit for Christ’s people are in accordance with his will.'),
(996633,34,45,8,28,'But we do know that God causes all things to work together for the good of those who love him – those who have received the call in accordance with his purpose.'),
(996634,34,45,8,29,'For those whom God chose from the first he also destined from the first to be transformed into likeness to his Son, so that his Son might be the eldest among many brothers and sisters.'),
(996635,34,45,8,30,'And those whom God destined for this he also called; and those whom he called he also pronounced righteous; and those whom he pronounced righteous he also brought to glory.'),
(996636,34,45,8,31,'What are we to say, then, in the light of all this?'),
(996637,34,45,8,32,'God did not withhold his own Son, but gave him up on behalf of us all; will he not, then, with him, freely give us all things?'),
(996638,34,45,8,33,'Who will bring a charge against any of God’s people? He who pronounces them righteous is God!'),
(996639,34,45,8,34,'Who is there to condemn them? He who died for us is Christ Jesus! – or, rather, it was he who was raised from the dead, and who is now at God’s right hand and is even pleading on our behalf!'),
(996640,34,45,8,35,'Who is there to separate us from the love of the Christ? Will trouble, or difficulty, or persecution, or hunger, or nakedness, or danger, or the sword?'),
(996641,34,45,8,36,'Scripture says – “For your sake we are being killed all the day long, We are regarded as sheep to be slaughtered.”'),
(996642,34,45,8,37,'Yet amid all these things we more than conquer through him who loved us!'),
(996643,34,45,8,38,'For I am persuaded that neither death, nor life, nor angels, nor archangels, nor the present, nor the future, nor any powers,'),
(996644,34,45,8,39,'nor height, nor depth, nor any other created thing, will be able to separate us from the love of God revealed in Christ Jesus, our Lord!'),
(996645,34,45,9,1,'I am speaking the truth as one in union with Christ; it is no lie; and my conscience, enlightened by the Holy Spirit,'),
(996646,34,45,9,2,'bears me out when I say that there is a great weight of sorrow on me and that my heart is never free from pain.'),
(996647,34,45,9,3,'I could wish that I were myself accursed and severed from the Christ, for the sake of my people – my own flesh and blood.'),
(996648,34,45,9,4,'For they are Israelites, and theirs are the adoption as sons, the visible presence, the Covenants, the revealed Law, the Temple worship, and the Promises.'),
(996649,34,45,9,5,'They are descended from the Patriarchs; and, as far as his human nature was concerned, from them came the Christ – he who is supreme over all things, God for ever blessed. Amen.'),
(996650,34,45,9,6,'Not that God’s Word has failed. For it is not all who are descended from Israel who are true Israelites;'),
(996651,34,45,9,7,'nor, because they are Abraham’s descendants, are they all his children; but – “It is Isaac’s children who will be called your descendants.”'),
(996652,34,45,9,8,'This means that it is not the children born in the course of nature who are God’s children, but it is the children born in fulfilment of the Promise who are to be regarded as Abraham’s descendants.'),
(996653,34,45,9,9,'For these words are the words of a promise – “About this time I will come, and Sarah will have a son.”'),
(996654,34,45,9,10,'Nor is that all. There is also the case of Rebecca, when she was about to bear children to our ancestor Isaac.'),
(996655,34,45,9,11,'For in order that the purpose of God, working through selection, might not fail – a selection depending, not on obedience, but on his call – Rebecca was told, before her children were born and before they had done anything either right or wrong,'),
(996656,34,45,9,12,'that the elder would be a servant to the younger.'),
(996657,34,45,9,13,'The words of scripture are – “I loved Jacob, but I hated Esau.”'),
(996658,34,45,9,14,'What are we to say, then? Is God guilty of injustice? Heaven forbid!'),
(996659,34,45,9,15,'For his words to Moses are – “I will take pity on whom I take pity, and be merciful to whom I am merciful.”'),
(996660,34,45,9,16,'So, then, all depends, not on human wishes or human efforts, but on God’s mercy.'),
(996661,34,45,9,17,'In scripture, again, it is said to Pharaoh – “It was for this purpose that I raised you to the throne, to show my power by my dealings with you, and to make my name known throughout the world.”'),
(996662,34,45,9,18,'So, then, where God wills, he takes pity, and where he wills, he hardens the heart.'),
(996663,34,45,9,19,'Perhaps you will say to me – “How can anyone still be blamed? For who withstands his purpose?”'),
(996664,34,45,9,20,'I might rather ask “Who are you who are arguing with God?” Does a thing which a person has moulded say to the person who has moulded it “Why did you make me like this?”'),
(996665,34,45,9,21,'Has not the potter absolute power over their clay, so that out of the same lump they make one thing for better, and another for common, use?'),
(996666,34,45,9,22,'And what if God, intending to reveal his displeasure and make his power known, bore most patiently with the objects of his displeasure, though they were fit only to be destroyed,'),
(996667,34,45,9,23,'so as to make known his surpassing glory in dealing with the objects of his mercy, whom he prepared beforehand for glory,'),
(996668,34,45,9,24,'and whom he called – even us – Not only from among the Jews but from among the Gentiles also!'),
(996669,34,45,9,25,'This, indeed, is what he says in the book of Hosea – “Those who were not my people, I will call my people, and those who were unloved I will love.'),
(996670,34,45,9,26,'And in the place where it was said to them – ‘You are not my people’, they will be called sons of the living God.”'),
(996671,34,45,9,27,'And Isaiah cries aloud over Israel – “Though the sons of Israel are like the sand of the sea in number, only a remnant of them will escape!'),
(996672,34,45,9,28,'For the Lord will execute his sentence on the world, fully and without delay.”'),
(996673,34,45,9,29,'It is as Isaiah foretold – “Had not the Lord of Hosts spared some few of our people to us, we should have become like Sodom and been made to resemble Gomorrah.”'),
(996674,34,45,9,30,'What are we to say, then? Why, that Gentiles, who were not in search of righteousness, secured it – a righteousness which was the result of faith;'),
(996675,34,45,9,31,'while Israel, which was in search of a Law which would ensure righteousness, failed to discover one.'),
(996676,34,45,9,32,'And why? Because they looked to obedience, and not to faith, to secure it. They stumbled over the stumbling-block.'),
(996677,34,45,9,33,'As scripture says – “See, I place a stumbling-block in Zion – a rock which will prove a hindrance; and he who believes in him will have no cause for shame.”'),
(996678,34,45,10,1,'My friends, my heart’s desire and prayer to God for my people is for their salvation.'),
(996679,34,45,10,2,'I can testify that they are zealous for the honour of God; but they are not guided by true insight,'),
(996680,34,45,10,3,'for, in their ignorance of the divine righteousness, and in their eagerness to set up a righteousness of their own, they refused to accept with submission the divine righteousness.'),
(996681,34,45,10,4,'For Christ has brought Law to an end, so that righteousness may be obtained by everyone who believes in him.'),
(996682,34,45,10,5,'For Moses writes that, as for the righteousness which results from Law, those who practice it will find life through it.'),
(996683,34,45,10,6,'But the righteousness which results from faith finds expression in these words: “Do not say to yourself ‘Who will go up into heaven?’” (which means to bring Christ down)'),
(996684,34,45,10,7,'“or ‘Who will go down into the depths below?’” (which means to bring Christ up from the dead).'),
(996685,34,45,10,8,'No, but what does it say? “The message is near you, on your lips and in your heart” (which means “The Message of faith” which we proclaim).'),
(996686,34,45,10,9,'For, if with your lips you acknowledge the truth of the message that JESUS IS LORD, and believe in your heart that God raised him from the dead, you will be saved.'),
(996687,34,45,10,10,'For with their hearts people believe and so attain to righteousness, while with their lips they make their Profession of faith and so find salvation.'),
(996688,34,45,10,11,'As the passage of scripture says – “No one who believes in him will have any cause for shame.”'),
(996689,34,45,10,12,'For no distinction is made between the Jew and the Greek, for all have the same Lord, and he is bountiful to all who invoke him.'),
(996690,34,45,10,13,'For everyone who invokes the name of the Lord will be saved.'),
(996691,34,45,10,14,'But how, it may be asked, are they to invoke one in whom they have not learned to believe? And how are they to believe in one whose words they have not heard? And how are they to hear his words unless someone proclaims him?'),
(996692,34,45,10,15,'And how is anyone to proclaim him unless they are sent as his messengers? As scripture says – “How beautiful are the feet of those who bring good news!”'),
(996693,34,45,10,16,'Still, it may be said, everyone did not give heed to the good news. No, for Isaiah asks – “Lord, who has believed our teaching?”'),
(996694,34,45,10,17,'And so we gather, faith is a result of teaching, and the teaching comes in the message of Christ.'),
(996695,34,45,10,18,'But I ask “Is it possible that people have never heard?” No, indeed, for – “Their voices spread through all the earth, and their message to the ends of the world.”'),
(996696,34,45,10,19,'But again I ask “Did not the people of Israel understand?” First there is Moses, who says – “I, the Lord, will stir you to rivalry with a nation which is no nation; Against an undiscerning nation I will arouse your anger.”'),
(996697,34,45,10,20,'And Isaiah says boldly – “I was found by those who were not seeking me; I made myself known to those who were not inquiring of me.”'),
(996698,34,45,10,21,'But of the people of Israel he says – “All day long I have stretched out my hands to a people who disobey and contradict.”'),
(996699,34,45,11,1,'I ask, then, “Has God rejected his people?” Heaven forbid! For I myself am an Israelite, a descendant of Abraham, of the tribe of Benjamin.'),
(996700,34,45,11,2,'God has not rejected his people, whom he chose from the first. Have you forgotten the words of scripture in the story of Elijah – how he appeals to God against Israel?'),
(996701,34,45,11,3,'“Lord, they have killed your prophets, they have pulled down your altars, and I only am left; and now they are eager to take my life.”'),
(996702,34,45,11,4,'But what was the divine response? “I have kept for myself seven thousand who have never bowed the knee to Baal.”'),
(996703,34,45,11,5,'And so in our own time, too, there is to be found a remnant of our nation selected by God in love.'),
(996704,34,45,11,6,'But if in love, then it is not as a result of obedience. Otherwise love would cease to be love.'),
(996705,34,45,11,7,'What follows from this? Why, that Israel as a nation failed to secure what it was seeking, while those whom God selected did secure it.'),
(996706,34,45,11,8,'The rest grew callous; as scripture says – “God has given them a deadness of mind – eyes that are not to see and ears that are not to hear – and it is so to this very day.”'),
(996707,34,45,11,9,'David, too, says – “May their feasts prove a snare and a trap to them – a hindrance and a retribution;'),
(996708,34,45,11,10,'may their eyes be darkened, so that they cannot see; and do you always make their backs to bend.”'),
(996709,34,45,11,11,'I ask then – “Was their stumbling to result in their fall?” Heaven forbid! On the contrary, through their falling away salvation has reached the Gentiles, to stir the rivalry of Israel.'),
(996710,34,45,11,12,'And, if their falling away has enriched the world, and their failure has enriched the Gentiles, how much more will result from their full restoration!'),
(996711,34,45,11,13,'But I am speaking to you who were Gentiles.'),
(996712,34,45,11,14,'Being myself an apostle to the Gentiles, I exalt my office, in the hope that I may stir my countrymen to rivalry, and so save some of them.'),
(996713,34,45,11,15,'For, if their being cast aside has meant the reconciliation of the world, what will their reception mean, but life from the dead?'),
(996714,34,45,11,16,'If the first handful of dough in holy, so is the whole mass; and if the root is holy, so are the branches.'),
(996715,34,45,11,17,'Some, however, of the branches were broken off, and you, who were only a wild olive, were grafted in among them, and came to share with them the root which is the source of the richness of the cultivated olive.'),
(996716,34,45,11,18,'Yet do not exult over the other branches. But, if you do exult over them, remember that you do not support the root, but that the root supports you.'),
(996717,34,45,11,19,'But branches, you will say, were broken off, so that I might be grafted in.'),
(996718,34,45,11,20,'True; it was because of their want of faith that they were broken off, and it is because of your faith that you are standing. Do not think too highly of yourself, but beware.'),
(996719,34,45,11,21,'For, if God did not spare the natural branches, neither will he spare you.'),
(996720,34,45,11,22,'See, then, both the goodness and the severity of God – his severity towards those who fell, and his goodness towards you, provided that you continue to confide in that goodness; otherwise you, also, will be cut off.'),
(996721,34,45,11,23,'And they, too, if they do not continue in their unbelief, will be grafted in; for God has it in his power to graft them in again.'),
(996722,34,45,11,24,'If you were cut off from your natural stock – a wild olive – and were grafted, contrary to the course of nature, on a good olive, much more will they – the natural branches – be grafted back into their parent tree.'),
(996723,34,45,11,25,'My friends, so that you don’t think too highly of yourselves, I want you to recognise the truth, hitherto hidden, that the callousness which has come over Israel is only partial, and will continue only until the whole Gentile world has been gathered in.'),
(996724,34,45,11,26,'And then all Israel will be saved. As scripture says – “From Zion will come the Deliverer; he will banish ungodliness from Jacob.'),
(996725,34,45,11,27,'And they will see the fulfilment of my covenant, when I have taken away their sins.”'),
(996726,34,45,11,28,'From the standpoint of the good news, the Jews are God’s enemies for your sake; but from the standpoint of God’s selection, they are dear to him for the sake of the Patriarchs.'),
(996727,34,45,11,29,'For God never regrets his gifts or his call.'),
(996728,34,45,11,30,'Just as you at one time were disobedient to him, but have now found mercy in the day of their disobedience;'),
(996729,34,45,11,31,'so, too, they have now become disobedient in your day of mercy, in order that they also in their turn may now find mercy.'),
(996730,34,45,11,32,'For God has given all alike over to disobedience, that to all alike he may show mercy.'),
(996731,34,45,11,33,'Oh! The unfathomable wisdom and knowledge of God! How inscrutable are his judgments, how untraceable his ways! Yes –'),
(996732,34,45,11,34,'Who has ever comprehended the mind of the Lord? Who has ever become his counsellor?'),
(996733,34,45,11,35,'Or who has first given to him, so that he may claim a reward?'),
(996734,34,45,11,36,'For all things are from him, through him, and for him. And to him be all glory for ever and ever! Amen.'),
(996735,34,45,12,1,'I entreat you, then, friends, by the mercies of God, to offer your bodies as a living and holy sacrifice, acceptable to God, for this is your rational worship.'),
(996736,34,45,12,2,'Do not conform to the fashion of this world; but be transformed by the complete change that has come over your minds, so that you may discern what God’s will is – all that is good, acceptable, and perfect.'),
(996737,34,45,12,3,'In fulfilment of the charge with which I have been entrusted, I tell every one of you not to think more highly of himself than he ought to think, but to think until he learns to think soberly – in accordance with the measure of faith that God has allotted to each.'),
(996738,34,45,12,4,'For, just as in the human body there is a union of many parts, and each part has its own function,'),
(996739,34,45,12,5,'so we, by our union in Christ, many though we are, form but one body, and individually we are related one to another as its parts.'),
(996740,34,45,12,6,'Since our gifts differ in accordance with the particular charge entrusted to us, if our gift is to preach, let our preaching correspond to our faith;'),
(996741,34,45,12,7,'if it is to minister to others, let us devote ourselves to our ministry; the teacher to their teaching,'),
(996742,34,45,12,8,'the counselor to their counsel. Let the person who gives in charity do so with a generous heart; let the person who is in authority exercise due diligence; let the person who shows kindness do so in a cheerful spirit.'),
(996743,34,45,12,9,'Let your love be sincere. Hate the wrong; cling to the right.'),
(996744,34,45,12,10,'In the love of the community of the Lord’s followers, be affectionate to one another; in showing respect, set an example of deference to one another;'),
(996745,34,45,12,11,'never flagging in zeal; fervent in spirit; serving the Master;'),
(996746,34,45,12,12,'rejoicing in your hope; steadfast under persecution; persevering in prayer;'),
(996747,34,45,12,13,'relieving the wants of Christ’s people; devoted to hospitality.'),
(996748,34,45,12,14,'Bless your persecutors – bless and never curse.'),
(996749,34,45,12,15,'Rejoice with those who are rejoicing, and weep with those who are weeping.'),
(996750,34,45,12,16,'Let the same spirit of sympathy animate you all, not a spirit of pride; enjoy the company of ordinary people. Do not think too highly of yourselves.'),
(996751,34,45,12,17,'Never return injury for injury. Aim at doing what everyone will recognise as honourable.'),
(996752,34,45,12,18,'If it is possible, as far as rests with you, live peaceably with everyone.'),
(996753,34,45,12,19,'Never avenge yourselves, dear friends, but make way for the wrath of God; for scripture declares – “‘It is for me to avenge, I will requite,’ says the Lord.”'),
(996754,34,45,12,20,'Rather – “If your enemy is hungry, feed him; if he is thirsty, give him to drink. By doing this you will heap coals of fire on his head.”'),
(996755,34,45,12,21,'Never be conquered by evil, but conquer evil with good.'),
(996756,34,45,13,1,'Let everyone obey the supreme Authorities. For no Authority exists except by the will of God, and the existing Authorities have been appointed by God.'),
(996757,34,45,13,2,'Therefore he who sets himself against the authorities is resisting God’s appointment, and those who resist will bring a judgment on themselves.'),
(996758,34,45,13,3,'A good action has nothing to fear from Rulers; a bad action has. Do you want to have no reason to fear the Authorities? Then do what is good, and you will win their praise.'),
(996759,34,45,13,4,'For they are God’s servants appointed for your good. But, if you do what is wrong, you may well be afraid; for the sword they carry is not without meaning! They are God’s servants to inflict his punishments on those who do wrong.'),
(996760,34,45,13,5,'You are bound, therefore, to obey, not only through fear of God’s punishments, but also as a matter of conscience.'),
(996761,34,45,13,6,'This, too, is the reason for your paying taxes; for the officials are God’s officers, devoting themselves to this special work.'),
(996762,34,45,13,7,'In all cases pay what is due from you – tribute where tribute is due, taxes where taxes are due, respect where respect is due, and honour where honour is due.'),
(996763,34,45,13,8,'Owe nothing to anyone except love; for they who love their neighbour have satisfied the Law.'),
(996764,34,45,13,9,'The commandments, “You must not commit adultery, You must not kill, You must not steal, You must not covet,” and whatever other commandment there is, are all summed up in the words – “You must love your neighbour as you love yourself.”'),
(996765,34,45,13,10,'Love never wrongs a neighbour. Therefore love fully satisfies the Law.'),
(996766,34,45,13,11,'This I say, because you know the crisis that we have reached, for the time has already come for you to rouse yourselves from sleep; our salvation is nearer now than when we accepted the faith.'),
(996767,34,45,13,12,'The night is almost gone; the day is near. Therefore let us have done with the deeds of darkness, and arm ourselves with the weapons of light.'),
(996768,34,45,13,13,'Being in the light of day, let us live becomingly, not in revelry and drunkenness, not in lust and licentiousness, not in quarrelling and jealousy.'),
(996769,34,45,13,14,'No! Arm yourselves with the spirit of the Lord Jesus Christ, and spend no thought on your earthly nature, to satisfy its cravings.'),
(996770,34,45,14,1,'As for those whose faith is weak, always receive them as friends, but not for the purpose of passing judgment on their scruples.'),
(996771,34,45,14,2,'One person’s faith permits of their eating food of all kinds, while another whose faith is weak eats only vegetable food.'),
(996772,34,45,14,3,'The person who eats meat must not despise the person who abstains from it; nor must the person who abstains from eating meat pass judgment on the one who eats it, for God himself has received them.'),
(996773,34,45,14,4,'Who are you, that you should pass judgment on the servant of another? Their standing or falling concerns their own master. And stand they will, for their Master can enable them to stand.'),
(996774,34,45,14,5,'Again, one person considers some days to be more sacred than others, while another considers all days to be alike. Everyone ought to be fully convinced in their own mind.'),
(996775,34,45,14,6,'The person who observes a day, observes it to the Master’s honour. They, again, who eat meat eat it to the Master’s honour, for they give thanks to God; while the person who abstains from it abstains from it to the Master’s honour, and also gives thanks to God.'),
(996776,34,45,14,7,'There is not one of us whose life concerns ourselves alone, and not one of us whose death concerns ourself alone;'),
(996777,34,45,14,8,'for, if we live, our life is for the Master, and, if we die, our death is for the Master. Whether, then, we live or die we belong to the Master.'),
(996778,34,45,14,9,'The purpose for which Christ died and came back to life was this – that he might be Lord over both the dead and the living.'),
(996779,34,45,14,10,'I would ask the one “Why do you judge other followers of the Lord?” And I would ask the other “Why do you despise them?” For we will all stand before the court of God.'),
(996780,34,45,14,11,'For scripture says – “‘As surely as I live,’ says the Lord, ‘every knee will bend before me and every tongue will praise God.’”'),
(996781,34,45,14,12,'So, then, each one of us will have to render account of himself to God.'),
(996782,34,45,14,13,'Let us, then, cease to judge one another. Rather let this be your resolve – never to place a stumbling-block or an obstacle in the way of a fellow follower of the Lord.'),
(996783,34,45,14,14,'Through my union with the Lord Jesus, I know and am persuaded that nothing is defiling in itself. A thing is “defiling” only to the person who holds it to be so.'),
(996784,34,45,14,15,'If, for the sake of what you eat, you wound your fellow follower’s feelings, your life has ceased to be ruled by love. Do not, by what you eat, ruin someone for whom Christ died!'),
(996785,34,45,14,16,'Do not let what is right for you become a matter of reproach.'),
(996786,34,45,14,17,'For the kingdom of God does not consist of eating and drinking, but of righteousness and peace and gladness through the presence of the Holy Spirit.'),
(996787,34,45,14,18,'The person who serves the Christ in this way pleases God, and wins the approval of their fellows.'),
(996788,34,45,14,19,'Therefore our efforts should be directed towards all that makes for peace and the mutual building up of character.'),
(996789,34,45,14,20,'Do not undo God’s work for the sake of what you eat. Though everything is “clean,” yet, if a person eats so as to put a stumbling-block in the way of others, they do wrong.'),
(996790,34,45,14,21,'The right course is to abstain from meat or wine or, indeed, anything that is a stumbling-block to your fellow follower of the Lord.'),
(996791,34,45,14,22,'As for yourself – keep this conviction of yours to yourself, as in the presence of God. Happy the person who never has to condemn themselves in regard to something they think right!'),
(996792,34,45,14,23,'The person, however, who has misgivings stands condemned if they still eat, because their doing so is not the result of faith. And anything not done as the result of faith is a sin.'),
(996793,34,45,15,1,'We, the strong, ought to take on our own shoulders the weaknesses of those who are not strong, and not merely to please ourselves.'),
(996794,34,45,15,2,'Let each of us please our neighbour for our neighbour’s good, to help in the building up of their character.'),
(996795,34,45,15,3,'Even the Christ did not please himself! On the contrary, as scripture says of him – “The reproaches of those who were reproaching you fell upon me.”'),
(996796,34,45,15,4,'Whatever was written in the scriptures in days gone by was written for our instruction, so that, through patient endurance, and through the encouragement drawn from the scriptures, we might hold fast to our hope.'),
(996797,34,45,15,5,'And may God, the giver of this patience and this encouragement, grant you to be united in sympathy in Christ,'),
(996798,34,45,15,6,'so that with one heart and one voice you may praise the God and Father of Jesus Christ, our Lord.'),
(996799,34,45,15,7,'Therefore always receive one another as friends, just as the Christ himself received us, to the glory of God.'),
(996800,34,45,15,8,'For I tell you that Christ, in vindication of God’s truthfulness, has become a minister of the covenant of circumcision, so that he may fulfil the promises made to our ancestors,'),
(996801,34,45,15,9,'and that the Gentiles also may praise God for his mercy. As scripture says – “Therefore will I make acknowledgment to you among the Gentiles and sing in honour of your name.”'),
(996802,34,45,15,10,'And again it says – “Rejoice, you Gentiles, with God’s people.”'),
(996803,34,45,15,11,'And yet again – “Praise the Lord, all you Gentiles, and let all Peoples sing his praises.”'),
(996804,34,45,15,12,'Again, Isaiah says – “There will be a Scion of the house of Jesse, One who is to arise to rule the Gentiles; on him will the Gentiles rest their hopes.”'),
(996805,34,45,15,13,'May God, who inspires our hope, grant you perfect happiness and peace in your faith, until you are filled with this hope by the power of the Holy Spirit.'),
(996806,34,45,15,14,'I am persuaded, my friends – yes, I Paul, with regard to you – that you are yourselves full of kindness, furnished with all Christian learning, and well able to give advice to one another.'),
(996807,34,45,15,15,'But in parts of this letter I have expressed myself somewhat boldly – by way of refreshing your memories –'),
(996808,34,45,15,16,'because of the charge with which God has entrusted me, that I should be an assistant of Christ Jesus to go to the Gentiles – that I should act as a priest of God’s good news, so that the offering up of the Gentiles may be an acceptable sacrifice, consecrated by the Holy Spirit.'),
(996809,34,45,15,17,'It is, then, through my union with Christ Jesus that I have a proud confidence in my work for God.'),
(996810,34,45,15,18,'For I will not dare to speak of anything but what Christ has done through me to win the obedience of the Gentiles –'),
(996811,34,45,15,19,'by my words and actions, through the power displayed in signs and marvels, and through the power of the Holy Spirit. And so, starting from Jerusalem and going as far as Illyria, I have told in full the good news of the Christ;'),
(996812,34,45,15,20,'yet always with the ambition to tell the good news where Christ’s name had not previously been heard, so as to avoid building on another’s foundations.'),
(996813,34,45,15,21,'But as scripture says – “They to whom he had never been proclaimed will see; and they who have never heard will understand!”'),
(996814,34,45,15,22,'That is why I have so often been prevented from coming to you.'),
(996815,34,45,15,23,'But now there are no further openings for me in these parts, and I have for several years been longing to come to you whenever I may be going to Spain.'),
(996816,34,45,15,24,'For my hope is to visit you on my journey, and then to be sent on my way by you, after I have first partly satisfied myself by seeing something of you.'),
(996817,34,45,15,25,'Just now, however, I am on my way to Jerusalem, to take help to Christ’s people there.'),
(996818,34,45,15,26,'For Macedonia and Greece have been glad to make a collection for the poor among Christ’s people at Jerusalem.'),
(996819,34,45,15,27,'Yes, they were glad to do so; and indeed it is a duty which they owe to them. For the Gentile converts who have shared their spiritual blessings are in duty bound to minister to them in the things of this world.'),
(996820,34,45,15,28,'When I have settled this matter, and have secured to the poor at Jerusalem the enjoyment of these benefits, I will go, by way of you, to Spain.'),
(996821,34,45,15,29,'And I know that, when I come to you, it will be with a full measure of blessing from Christ.'),
(996822,34,45,15,30,'I beg you, then, friends, by Jesus Christ, our Lord, and by the love inspired by the Spirit, to join me in earnest prayer to God on my behalf.'),
(996823,34,45,15,31,'Pray that I may be rescued from those in Judea who reject the faith, and that the help which I am taking to Jerusalem may prove acceptable to Christ’s people;'),
(996824,34,45,15,32,'so that, God willing, I may be able to come to you with a joyful heart, and enjoy some rest among you.'),
(996825,34,45,15,33,'May God, the giver of peace, be with you all. Amen.'),
(996826,34,45,16,1,'I commend to your care our sister, Phoebe, who is an assistant of the church at Cenchreae;'),
(996827,34,45,16,2,'and I ask you to give her a Christian welcome – one worthy of Christ’s people – and to aid her in any matter in which she may need your assistance. She has proved herself a staunch friend and protector and to many others.'),
(996828,34,45,16,3,'Give my greeting to Prisca and Aquila, my fellow workers in the cause of Christ Jesus,'),
(996829,34,45,16,4,'who risked their own lives to save mine. It is not I alone who thank them, but all the churches among the Gentiles thank them also.'),
(996830,34,45,16,5,'Give my greeting, also, to the church that meets at their house, as well as to my dear friend Epaenetus, one of the first in Roman Asia to believe in Christ;'),
(996831,34,45,16,6,'to Mary, who worked hard for you;'),
(996832,34,45,16,7,'to Andronicus and Junia, fellow Jews and once my fellow prisoners, who are people of note among the apostles, and who became Christians before I did;'),
(996833,34,45,16,8,'to my dear Christian friend Ampliatus;'),
(996834,34,45,16,9,'to Urban, our fellow worker in the cause of Christ, and to my dear friend Stachys;'),
(996835,34,45,16,10,'to that proved Christian Apelles; to the household of Aristobulus;'),
(996836,34,45,16,11,'to my countryman Herodion; to the Christians in the household of Narcissus;'),
(996837,34,45,16,12,'to Tryphaena and Tryphosa, who have worked hard for the Master; to my dear friend Persis, for she has done much hard work for the Master;'),
(996838,34,45,16,13,'to that eminent Christian, Rufus, and to his mother, who has been a mother to me also;'),
(996839,34,45,16,14,'to Asyncritus, Phlegon, Hermes, Patrobas, Hermas, and our friends with them;'),
(996840,34,45,16,15,'also to Philologus and Julia, Nereus and his sister, and Olympas, and to all Christ’s people who are with them.'),
(996841,34,45,16,16,'Greet one another with a sacred kiss. All the churches of the Christ send you greetings.'),
(996842,34,45,16,17,'I beg you, friends, to be on your guard against people who, by disregarding the teaching which you received, cause divisions and create difficulties; dissociate yourselves from them.'),
(996843,34,45,16,18,'For such persons are not serving Christ, our Master, but are slaves to their own appetites; and, by their smooth words and flattery, they deceive simple-minded people.'),
(996844,34,45,16,19,'Everyone has heard of your ready obedience. It is true that I am very happy about you, but I want you to be well versed in all that is good, and innocent of all that is bad.'),
(996845,34,45,16,20,'And God, the giver of peace, will before long crush Satan under your feet.'),
(996846,34,45,16,21,'Timothy, my fellow worker, sends you his greetings, and Lucius, Jason, and Sosipater, my countrymen, send theirs.'),
(996847,34,45,16,22,'I Tertius, who am writing this letter, send you my Christian greeting.'),
(996848,34,45,16,23,'My host Gaius, who extends his hospitality to the whole church, sends you his greeting; and Erastus, the city treasurer, and Quartus, our dear friend, add theirs.'),
(996849,34,45,16,25,'Now to him who is able to strengthen you, as promised in the good news entrusted to me and in the proclamation of Jesus Christ, in accordance with the revelation of that hidden purpose, which in past ages was kept secret but now has been revealed'),
(996850,34,45,16,26,'and, in obedience to the command of the immortal God, made known through the writings of the prophets to all nations, to secure submission to the faith –'),
(996851,34,45,16,27,'to him, I say, the wise and only God, be ascribed, through Jesus Christ, all glory for ever and ever. Amen.'),
(996852,34,46,1,1,'To the church of God in Corinth, to those who have been consecrated by union with Christ Jesus and called to become his people, and also to all, wherever they may be, who invoke the name of our Lord Jesus Christ – their Master and ours,'),
(996853,34,46,1,2,'from Paul, who has been called to be an apostle of Jesus Christ by the will of God, and from Sosthenes, our fellow follower of the Lord.'),
(996854,34,46,1,3,'May God, our Father, and the Lord Jesus Christ bless you and give you peace.'),
(996855,34,46,1,4,'I always thank God about you for the blessing bestowed on you in Christ Jesus.'),
(996856,34,46,1,5,'For through union with him you were enriched in every way – in your power to preach, and in your knowledge of the truth;'),
(996857,34,46,1,6,'and so became yourselves a confirmation of my testimony to the Christ.'),
(996858,34,46,1,7,'There is no gift in which you are deficient, while waiting for the appearing of our Lord Jesus Christ.'),
(996859,34,46,1,8,'And God himself will strengthen you to the end, so that at the day of our Lord Jesus Christ you may be found blameless.'),
(996860,34,46,1,9,'God will not fail you, and it is he who called you into communion with his Son, Jesus Christ, our Lord.'),
(996861,34,46,1,10,'But I appeal to you, my friends, by the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, to agree in what you profess, and not to allow divisions to exist among you, but to be united – of one mind and of one opinion.'),
(996862,34,46,1,11,'For I have been informed, my friends, by the members of Chloe’s household, that party feeling exists among you.'),
(996863,34,46,1,12,'I mean this: that every one of you says either “I follow Paul,” or “I Apollos,” or “I Cephas,” or “I Christ.”'),
(996864,34,46,1,13,'You have torn the Christ in pieces! Was it Paul who was crucified for you? Or were you baptized in the name of Paul?'),
(996865,34,46,1,14,'I am thankful that I did not baptize any of you except Crispus and Gaius,'),
(996866,34,46,1,15,'so that no one can say that you were baptized in my name.'),
(996867,34,46,1,16,'I baptized also the household of Stephanas. I do not know that I baptized anyone else.'),
(996868,34,46,1,17,'My mission from Christ was not to baptize, but to tell the good news; not, however, in the language of philosophy, in case the cross of the Christ should be robbed of its meaning.'),
(996869,34,46,1,18,'The message of the cross is indeed mere folly to those who are in the path to ruin, but to us who are in the path of salvation it is the power of God.'),
(996870,34,46,1,19,'For scripture says –'),
(996871,34,46,1,20,'Where is the philosopher? Where the teacher of the Law? Where the disputant of today? Has not God shown the world’s philosophy to be folly?'),
(996872,34,46,1,21,'For since the world, in God’s wisdom, did not by its philosophy learn to know God, God saw fit, by the “folly” of our proclamation, to save those who believe in Christ!'),
(996873,34,46,1,22,'While Jews ask for miraculous signs, and Greeks study philosophy,'),
(996874,34,46,1,23,'we are proclaiming Christ crucified! – to the Jews an obstacle, to the Gentiles mere folly,'),
(996875,34,46,1,24,'but to those who have received the call, whether Jews or Greeks, Christ, the power of God and the wisdom of God!'),
(996876,34,46,1,25,'For God’s “folly” is wiser than people, and God’s “weakness” is stronger than people.'),
(996877,34,46,1,26,'Look at the facts of your call, friends. There are not many among you who are wise, as people reckon wisdom, not many who are influential, not many who are high-born;'),
(996878,34,46,1,27,'but God chose what the world counts foolish to put its wise to shame, and God chose what the world counts weak to put its strong to shame,'),
(996879,34,46,1,28,'and God chose what the world counts poor and insignificant – things that to it are unreal – to bring its “realities” to nothing,'),
(996880,34,46,1,29,'so that in his presence no one should boast.'),
(996881,34,46,1,30,'But you, by your union with Christ Jesus, belong to God; and Christ, by God’s will, became not only our wisdom, but also our righteousness, holiness, and deliverance,'),
(996882,34,46,1,31,'so that – in the words of scripture –'),
(996883,34,46,2,1,'For my own part, friends, when I came to you, it was with no display of eloquence or philosophy that I came to tell the hidden purpose of God;'),
(996884,34,46,2,2,'for I had determined that, while with you, I would forget everything Jesus Christ – and him crucified!'),
(996885,34,46,2,3,'Indeed, when I came among you, I was weak, and full of fears, and in great anxiety.'),
(996886,34,46,2,4,'My message and my proclamation were not delivered in the persuasive language of philosophy, but were accompanied by the manifestation of spiritual power,'),
(996887,34,46,2,5,'so that your faith should be based, not on the human wisdom, but on the power of God.'),
(996888,34,46,2,6,'Yet there is a philosophy that we teach to those whose faith is matured, but it is not the philosophy of today, or of the leaders of today – whose downfall is at hand.'),
(996889,34,46,2,7,'No, it is a divine philosophy that we teach, one concerned with the hidden purpose of God – that long hidden philosophy which God, before time began, destined for our glory.'),
(996890,34,46,2,8,'This philosophy is not known to any of the leaders of today; for, had they known it, they would not have crucified our glorified Lord.'),
(996891,34,46,2,9,'It is what scripture speaks of as –'),
(996892,34,46,2,10,'Yet to us God revealed it through his Spirit; for the Spirit fathoms all things, even the inmost depths of God’s being.'),
(996893,34,46,2,11,'For what person is there who knows what a person is, except the person’s own spirit within them? So, also, no one comprehends what God is, except the Spirit of God.'),
(996894,34,46,2,12,'And as for us, it is not the spirit of the world that we have received, but the Spirit that comes from God, so that we may realize the blessings given to us by him.'),
(996895,34,46,2,13,'And we speak of these gifts, not in language taught by human philosophy, but in language taught by the Spirit, explaining spiritual things in spiritual words.'),
(996896,34,46,2,14,'The merely intellectual person rejects the teaching of the Spirit of God; for to them it is mere folly; they cannot grasp it, because it is to be understood only by spiritual insight.'),
(996897,34,46,2,15,'But the person with spiritual insight is able to understand everything, although they themselves are understood by no one.'),
(996898,34,46,2,16,'For who has so comprehended the mind of the Lord as to be able to instruct him? We, however, have the mind of Christ.'),
(996899,34,46,3,1,'But I, my friends, could not speak to you as people with spiritual insight, but only as worldly-minded – mere infants in the faith of Christ.'),
(996900,34,46,3,2,'I fed you with milk, not with solid food, for you were not then able to take it.'),
(996901,34,46,3,3,'While there exist among you jealousy and party feeling, is it not true that you are worldly, and are acting merely as other people do?'),
(996902,34,46,3,4,'When one says “I follow Paul,” and another “I follow Apollos,” aren’t you like other people?'),
(996903,34,46,3,5,'What, I ask, is Apollos? Or what is Paul? Servants through whom you were led to accept the faith; and that only as the Lord helped each of you.'),
(996904,34,46,3,6,'I planted, and Apollos watered, but it was God who caused the growth.'),
(996905,34,46,3,7,'Therefore neither the one who plants, nor the one who waters, counts for anything, but only God who causes the growth.'),
(996906,34,46,3,8,'In this the person who plants and the person who waters are one; yet each will receive their own reward in proportion to their own labour.'),
(996907,34,46,3,9,'For we are God’s fellow workers; you are God’s harvest field, God’s building.'),
(996908,34,46,3,10,'In fulfilment of the charge which God had entrusted to me, I laid the foundation like a skilful master; but someone else is now building on it. Let everyone take care how they build;'),
(996909,34,46,3,11,'for no one can lay any other foundation than the one already laid – Jesus Christ.'),
(996910,34,46,3,12,'Whatever is used by those who build on this foundation, whether gold, silver, costly stones, wood, hay, or straw,'),
(996911,34,46,3,13,'the quality of each man’s work will become known, for the day will make it plain; because that day is to be ushered in with fire, and the fire itself will test the quality of every man’s work.'),
(996912,34,46,3,14,'If anyone’s work, which they have built on that foundation, still remains, they will gain a reward.'),
(996913,34,46,3,15,'If anyone’s work is burnt up, they will suffer loss; though they themselves will escape, but only as one who has passed through fire.'),
(996914,34,46,3,16,'Don’t you know that you are God’s Temple, and that God’s Spirit has his home in you?'),
(996915,34,46,3,17,'If any one destroys the Temple of God, God will destroy them; for the Temple of God is sacred, and so also are you.'),
(996916,34,46,3,18,'Let no one deceive himself. If any one among you imagines that, as regards this world, they are wise, they should become a “fool,” that they may become wise.'),
(996917,34,46,3,19,'For in God’s sight this world’s wisdom is folly. Scripture tells of –'),
(996918,34,46,3,20,'And it says again –'),
(996919,34,46,3,21,'Therefore let no one boast about people; for all things are yours –'),
(996920,34,46,3,22,'Whether Paul, or Apollos, or Cephas, or the world, or life, or death, or the present, or the future – all things are yours!'),
(996921,34,46,3,23,'But you are Christ’s and Christ is God’s.'),
(996922,34,46,4,1,'Let people look on us as Christ’s servants, and as stewards of the hidden truths of God.'),
(996923,34,46,4,2,'Now what we look for in stewards is that they should be trustworthy.'),
(996924,34,46,4,3,'But it weighs very little with me that I am judged by you or by any human tribunal. No, I do not even judge myself;'),
(996925,34,46,4,4,'for, though I am conscious of nothing against myself, that does not prove me innocent. It is the Lord who is my judge.'),
(996926,34,46,4,5,'Therefore do not pass judgment before the time, but wait until the Lord comes. He will throw light on what is now dark and obscure, and will reveal the motives in people’s minds; and then everyone will receive due praise from God.'),
(996927,34,46,4,6,'All this, friends, I have, for your sakes, applied to Apollos and myself, so that, from our example, you may learn to observe the precept – “Keep to what is written,” that none of you may speak boastfully of one teacher to the disparagement of another.'),
(996928,34,46,4,7,'For who makes any one of you superior to others? And what have you that was not given you? But if you received it as a gift, why do you boast as if you had not?'),
(996929,34,46,4,8,'Are you all so soon satisfied? Are you so soon rich? Have you begun to reign without us? Would indeed that you had, so that we also might reign with you!'),
(996930,34,46,4,9,'For, as it seems to me, God has exhibited us, the apostles, last of all, as people doomed to death. We are made a spectacle to the universe, both to angels and to people!'),
(996931,34,46,4,10,'We, for Christ’s sake, are fools, but you, by your union with Christ, are people of discernment. We are weak, but you are strong. You are honoured, but we are despised.'),
(996932,34,46,4,11,'To this very hour we go hungry, thirsty, and naked; we are beaten; we are homeless;'),
(996933,34,46,4,12,'we work hard, toiling with our own hands. We meet abuse with blessings, we meet persecution with endurance,'),
(996934,34,46,4,13,'we meet slander with gentle appeals. We have been treated as the scum of the earth, the vilest of the vile, to this very hour.'),
(996935,34,46,4,14,'It is with no wish to shame you that I am writing like this; but to warn you as my own dear children.'),
(996936,34,46,4,15,'Though you may have thousands of instructors in the faith of Christ, yet you have not many fathers. It was I who, through union with Christ Jesus, became your father by means of the good news.'),
(996937,34,46,4,16,'Therefore I entreat you – Follow my example.'),
(996938,34,46,4,17,'This is my reason for sending Timothy to you. He is my own dear faithful child in the Master’s service, and he will remind you of my methods of teaching the faith of Christ Jesus – methods which I follow everywhere in every church.'),
(996939,34,46,4,18,'Some, I hear, are puffed up with pride, thinking that I am not coming to you.'),
(996940,34,46,4,19,'But come to you I will, and that soon, if it please the Lord; and then I will find out, not what words these people use who are so puffed up, but what power they possess;'),
(996941,34,46,4,20,'for the kingdom of God is based, not on words, but on power.'),
(996942,34,46,4,21,'What do you wish? Am I to come to you with a rod, or in a loving and gentle spirit?'),
(996943,34,46,5,1,'There is a wide-spread report respecting a case of immorality among you, and that, too, of a kind that does not occur even among the Gentiles – a man, I hear, is living with his father’s wife!'),
(996944,34,46,5,2,'Instead of grieving over it and taking steps for the expulsion of the man who has done this thing, is it possible that you are still puffed up?'),
(996945,34,46,5,3,'For I myself, though absent in body, have been present with you in spirit, and in the name of our Lord Jesus I have already passed judgment, just as if I had been present, on the man who has acted in this way.'),
(996946,34,46,5,4,'I have decided – having been present in spirit at your meetings, when the power of the Lord Jesus was with us –'),
(996947,34,46,5,5,'to deliver such a man as this over to Satan, that what is sensual in him may be destroyed, so that his spirit may be saved at the day of the Lord.'),
(996948,34,46,5,6,'Your boasting is unseemly. Don’t you know that even a little leaven leavens all the dough?'),
(996949,34,46,5,7,'Get rid entirely of the old leaven, so that you may be like new dough – free from leaven, as in truth you are. For our passover lamb is already sacrificed – Christ himself;'),
(996950,34,46,5,8,'therefore let us keep our festival, not with the leaven of former days, nor with the leaven of vice and wickedness, but with the unleavened bread of sincerity and truth.'),
(996951,34,46,5,9,'I told you, in my letter, not to associate with immoral people –'),
(996952,34,46,5,10,'not, of course, meaning people of the world who are in immoral, or who are covetous and grasping, or who worship idols; for then you would have to leave the world altogether.'),
(996953,34,46,5,11,'But, as things are, I say that you are not to associate with anyone who, although a follower of Christ in name, is immoral, or covetous, or an idolater, or abusive, or a drunkard, or grasping – no, not even to sit down to eat with such people.'),
(996954,34,46,5,12,'What have I to do with judging those outside the church? Is it not for you to judge those who are within the church,'),
(996955,34,46,5,13,'while God judges those who are outside? Put away the wicked from among you.'),
(996956,34,46,6,1,'Can it be that, when one of you has a dispute with another, they dare to have their case tried before the heathen, instead of before Christ’s people?'),
(996957,34,46,6,2,'Don’t you know that Christ’s people will try the world? And if the world is to be tried by you, are you unfit to try the most trivial cases?'),
(996958,34,46,6,3,'Don’t you know that we are to try angels – to say nothing of the affairs of this life?'),
(996959,34,46,6,4,'Why, then, if you have cases relating to the affairs of this life, do you set to try them those who carry no weight with the church? To your shame I ask it.'),
(996960,34,46,6,5,'Can it be that there is not one among you wise enough to decide between two of their fellow followers?'),
(996961,34,46,6,6,'Must a follower sue a fellow follower? In front of unbelievers?'),
(996962,34,46,6,7,'To begin with, it is undoubtedly a loss to you to have lawsuits with one another. Why not rather let yourselves be wronged? Why not rather let yourselves be cheated?'),
(996963,34,46,6,8,'Instead of this, you wrong and cheat others yourselves – yes, even other followers!'),
(996964,34,46,6,9,'Don’t you know that wrong-doers will have no share in God’s kingdom? Do not be deceived. No one who is immoral, or an idolater, or an adulterer, or licentious, or a sexual pervert,'),
(996965,34,46,6,10,'or a thief, or covetous, or a drunkard, or abusive, or grasping, will have any share in God’s kingdom.'),
(996966,34,46,6,11,'Such some of you used to be; but you washed yourselves clean. You became Christ’s people! You were pronounced righteous through the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, and through the Spirit of our God!'),
(996967,34,46,6,12,'Everything is allowable for me! Yes, but everything is not profitable. Everything is allowable for me! Yes, but for my part, I will not let myself be enslaved by anything.'),
(996968,34,46,6,13,'Food exists for the stomach, and the stomach for food; but God will put an end to both the one and the other. The body, however, exists, not for immorality, but for the Lord, and the Lord for the body;'),
(996969,34,46,6,14,'and, as God has raised the Lord, so he will raise up us also by the exercise of his power.'),
(996970,34,46,6,15,'Don’t you know that your bodies are Christ’s members? Am I, then, to take the members that belong to the Christ and make them the members of a prostitute? Heaven forbid!'),
(996971,34,46,6,16,'Or don’t you know that a man who unites himself with a prostitute is one with her in body (for “the two,” it is said, “will become one”);'),
(996972,34,46,6,17,'while a man who is united with the Lord is one with him in spirit?'),
(996973,34,46,6,18,'Shun all immorality. Every other sin that people commit is something outside the body; but an immoral person sins against their own body.'),
(996974,34,46,6,19,'Again, don’t you know that your body is a shrine of the Holy Spirit that is within you – the Spirit which you have from God?'),
(996975,34,46,6,20,'Moreover, you are not your own masters; you were bought, and the price was paid. Therefore, honour God in your bodies.'),
(996976,34,46,7,1,'With reference to the subjects about which you wrote to me: It is good for a man to remain single.'),
(996977,34,46,7,2,'But, owing to the prevalence of immorality, I advise every man to have his own wife, and every woman her husband.'),
(996978,34,46,7,3,'A husband should give his wife her due, and a wife her husband.'),
(996979,34,46,7,4,'It is not the wife, but the husband, who exercises power over her body; and so, too, it is not the husband, but the wife, who exercises power over his body.'),
(996980,34,46,7,5,'Do not deprive each other of what is due – unless it is only for a time and by mutual consent, so that your minds may be free for prayer until you again live as man and wife – otherwise Satan might take advantage of your want of self-control and tempt you.'),
(996981,34,46,7,6,'I say this, however, as a concession, not as a command.'),
(996982,34,46,7,7,'I should wish everyone to be just what I am myself. But everyone has his own gift from God – one in one way, and one in another.'),
(996983,34,46,7,8,'My advice, then, to those who are not married, and to widows, is this: It would be good for them to remain as I am myself.'),
(996984,34,46,7,9,'But, if they cannot control themselves, they should marry, for it is better to marry than to be consumed with passion.'),
(996985,34,46,7,10,'To those who are married my direction is – yet it is not mine, but the Master’s – that a woman is not to leave her husband'),
(996986,34,46,7,11,'(If she has done so, she should remain as she is, or else be reconciled to her husband) and also that a man is not to divorce his wife.'),
(996987,34,46,7,12,'To all others I say – I, not the Master – If a follower of the Lord is married to a woman, who is an unbeliever but willing to live with him, he should not divorce her;'),
(996988,34,46,7,13,'and a woman who is married to a man, who is an unbeliever but willing to live with her, should not divorce her husband.'),
(996989,34,46,7,14,'For, through his wife, the husband who is an unbeliever has become associated with Christ’s people; and the wife who is an unbeliever has become associated with Christ’s people through the Lord’s follower whom she has married. Otherwise your children would be “defiled,” but, as it is, they belong to Christ’s people.'),
(996990,34,46,7,15,'However, if the unbeliever wishes to be separated, let them be so. Under such circumstances neither is bound; God has called you to live in peace.'),
(996991,34,46,7,16,'How can you tell, wife, whether you may not save your husband? And how can you tell, husband, whether you may not save your wife?'),
(996992,34,46,7,17,'In any case, a person should continue to live in the condition which the Lord has allotted to them, and in which they were when God called them. This is the rule that I lay down in every church.'),
(996993,34,46,7,18,'Was a man already circumcised when he was called? Then he should not efface his circumcision. Has a man been called when uncircumcised? Then he should not be circumcised.'),
(996994,34,46,7,19,'Circumcision is nothing; the want of it is nothing; but to keep the commands of God is everything.'),
(996995,34,46,7,20,'Let everyone remain in that condition of life in which they were when the call came to them.'),
(996996,34,46,7,21,'Were you a slave when you were called? Do not let that trouble you. No, even if you are able to gain your freedom, still do your best.'),
(996997,34,46,7,22,'For the person who was a slave when they were called to the master’s service is the Master’s freedman; so, too, the person who was free when called is Christ’s slave.'),
(996998,34,46,7,23,'You were bought, and the price was paid. Do not let yourselves become slaves to people.'),
(996999,34,46,7,24,'Friends, let everyone remain in the condition in which they were when they were called, in close communion with God.'),
(997000,34,46,7,25,'With regard to unmarried women, I have no command from the Master to give you, but I tell you my opinion, and the Master in his mercy has made me worthy to be trusted.'),
(997001,34,46,7,26,'I think, then, that, in view of the time of suffering that has now come upon us, what I have already said is best – that a man should remain as he is.'),
(997002,34,46,7,27,'Are you married to a wife? Then do not seek to be separated. Are you separated from a wife? Then do not seek for a wife.'),
(997003,34,46,7,28,'Still, if you should marry, that is not wrong; nor, if a young woman marries, is that wrong. But those who marry will have much trouble to bear, and my wish is to spare you.'),
(997004,34,46,7,29,'What I mean, friends, is this – the time is short. Meanwhile, let those who have wives live as if they had none,'),
(997005,34,46,7,30,'those who are weeping as if not weeping, those who are rejoicing as if not rejoicing, those who buy as if not possessing,'),
(997006,34,46,7,31,'and those who use the good things of the world as using them sparingly; for this world as we see it is passing away.'),
(997007,34,46,7,32,'I want you to be free from anxiety. The unmarried man is anxious about the Master’s cause, desiring to please him;'),
(997008,34,46,7,33,'while the married man is anxious about worldly matters, desiring to please his wife;'),
(997009,34,46,7,34,'and so his interests are divided. Again, the unmarried woman, whether she is old or young, is anxious about the Master’s cause, striving to be pure both in body and in spirit, while the married woman is anxious about worldly matters, desiring to please her husband.'),
(997010,34,46,7,35,'I say this for your own benefit, not with any intention of putting a halter round your necks, but in order to secure for the Master seemly and constant devotion, free from all distraction.'),
(997011,34,46,7,36,'If, however, a father thinks that he is not acting fairly by his unmarried daughter, when she is past her youth, and if under these circumstances her marriage ought to take place, he should act as he thinks right. He is doing nothing wrong – let the marriage take place.'),
(997012,34,46,7,37,'On the other hand, a father, who has definitely made up his mind, and is under no compulsion, but is free to carry out his own wishes, and who has come to the decision, in his own mind, to keep his unmarried daughter at home will be doing right.'),
(997013,34,46,7,38,'In short, the one who consents to his daughter’s marriage is doing right, and yet the other will be doing better.'),
(997014,34,46,7,39,'A wife is bound to her husband as long as he lives; but, if the husband should pass to his rest, the widow is free to marry anyone she wishes, provided he is a believer.'),
(997015,34,46,7,40,'Yet she will be happier if she remains as she is – in my opinion, for I think that I also have the Spirit of God.'),
(997016,34,46,8,1,'With reference to food that has been offered in sacrifice to idols – We are aware that all of us have knowledge! Knowledge breeds conceit, while love builds up character.'),
(997017,34,46,8,2,'If someone thinks that they know anything, they have not yet reached that knowledge which they ought to have reached.'),
(997018,34,46,8,3,'On the other hand, if a person loves God, they are known by God.'),
(997019,34,46,8,4,'With reference, then, to eating food that has been offered to idols – we are aware that an idol is nothing in the world, and that there is no God but one.'),
(997020,34,46,8,5,'Even supposing that there are so-called “gods” either in heaven or on earth – and there are many such “gods” and “lords” –'),
(997021,34,46,8,6,'Yet for us there is only one God, the Father, from whom all things come (and for him we live), and one Lord, Jesus Christ, through whom all things come (and through him we live).'),
(997022,34,46,8,7,'Still, it is not everyone that has this knowledge. Some people, because of their association with idols, continued down to the present time, eat the food as food offered to an idol; and their consciences, while still weak, are dulled.'),
(997023,34,46,8,8,'What we eat, however, will not bring us nearer to God. We lose nothing by not eating this food, and we gain nothing by eating it.'),
(997024,34,46,8,9,'But take care that this right of yours does not become in any way a stumbling-block to the weak.'),
(997025,34,46,8,10,'For if someone should see you who possess this knowledge, feasting in an idol’s temple, will not their conscience, if they are weak, become so hardened that they, too, will eat food offered to idols?'),
(997026,34,46,8,11,'And so, through this knowledge of yours, the weak person is ruined – someone for whose sake Christ died!'),
(997027,34,46,8,12,'In this way, by sinning against your fellow followers of the Lord and injuring their consciences, while still weak, you sin against Christ.'),
(997028,34,46,8,13,'Therefore, if what I eat makes a follower of the Lord fall, rather than make them fall, I will never eat meat again.'),
(997029,34,46,9,1,'Am I not free? Am I not an apostle? Have I not seen our Lord Jesus? Aren’t you yourselves my work achieved in union with the Lord?'),
(997030,34,46,9,2,'If I am not an apostle to others, yet at least I am to you; for you are the seal that stamps me as an apostle in union with the Lord.'),
(997031,34,46,9,3,'The defence that I make to my critics is this:'),
(997032,34,46,9,4,'Haven’t we a right to food and drink?'),
(997033,34,46,9,5,'Haven’t we a right to take a wife with us, if she is a Christian, as the other apostles and the Master’s brothers and Cephas all do?'),
(997034,34,46,9,6,'Or is it only Barnabas and I who have no right to give up working for our bread?'),
(997035,34,46,9,7,'Does anyone ever serve as a soldier at his own expense? Does anyone plant a vineyard and not eat its produce? Or does anyone look after a herd and not drink the milk?'),
(997036,34,46,9,8,'Am I, in all this, speaking only from the human standpoint? Does not the Law also say the same?'),
(997037,34,46,9,9,'For in the Law of Moses it is said –'),
(997038,34,46,9,10,'Or is not is said entirely for our sakes? Surely it was written for our sakes, for the ploughman ought not to plough, nor the thrasher to thrash, without expecting a share of the grain.'),
(997039,34,46,9,11,'Since we, then, sowed spiritual seed for you, is it too much that we should reap from you an earthly harvest?'),
(997040,34,46,9,12,'If others share in this right over you, don’t we even more? Still we did not avail ourselves of this right. No, we endure anything rather than impede the progress of the good news of the Christ.'),
(997041,34,46,9,13,'Don’t you know that those who do the work of the Temple live on what comes from the Temple, and that those who serve at the altar share the offerings with the altar?'),
(997042,34,46,9,14,'So, too, the Master has appointed that those who tell the good news should get their living from the good news.'),
(997043,34,46,9,15,'I, however, have not availed myself of any of these rights. I am not saying this to secure such an arrangement for myself; indeed, I would far rather die – Nobody will make my boast a vain one!'),
(997044,34,46,9,16,'If I tell the good news, I have nothing to boast of, for I am compelled to do so. Woe is me if I do not tell it!'),
(997045,34,46,9,17,'If I do this work willingly, I have a reward; but, if unwillingly, I have been charged to perform a duty.'),
(997046,34,46,9,18,'What is my reward, then? To present the good news free of all cost, and so make but a sparing use of the rights which it gives me.'),
(997047,34,46,9,19,'Although I was entirely free, yet, to win as many converts as possible, I made myself everyone’s slave.'),
(997048,34,46,9,20,'To the Jews I became like a Jew, to win Jews. To those who are subject to Law I became like a man subject to Law – though I was not myself subject to Law – to win those who are subject to Law.'),
(997049,34,46,9,21,'To those who have no Law I became like a man who has no Law – not that I am free from God’s Law; no, for I am under Christ’s Law – to win those who have no law.'),
(997050,34,46,9,22,'To the weak I became weak, to win the weak. I have become all things to all people, so as at all costs to save some.'),
(997051,34,46,9,23,'And I do everything for the sake of the good news, so that with them I may share in its blessings.'),
(997052,34,46,9,24,'Don’t you know that on a racecourse, though all run, yet only one wins the prize? Run in such a way that you may win.'),
(997053,34,46,9,25,'Every athlete exercises self-restraint in everything; they, indeed, for a crown that fades, we for one that is unfading.'),
(997054,34,46,9,26,'I, therefore, run with no uncertain aim. I box – not like a man hitting the air.'),
(997055,34,46,9,27,'No, I bruise my body and make it my slave, so that I, who have called others to the contest, will not myself be rejected.'),
(997056,34,46,10,1,'I want you to bear in mind, friends, that all our ancestors were beneath the cloud, and all passed through the sea;'),
(997057,34,46,10,2,'that in the cloud and in the sea they all underwent baptism as followers of Moses;'),
(997058,34,46,10,3,'and that they all ate the same supernatural food,'),
(997059,34,46,10,4,'and all drank the same supernatural water, for they used to drink from a supernatural rock which followed them, and that rock was the Christ.'),
(997060,34,46,10,5,'Yet with most of them God was displeased; for they were struck down in the desert.'),
(997061,34,46,10,6,'Now these things happened as warnings to us, to teach us not to long for evil things as our ancestors longed.'),
(997062,34,46,10,7,'Do not become idolaters, as some of them became. Scripture says –'),
(997063,34,46,10,8,'Nor let us act immorally, as some of them acted, with the result that twenty-three thousand of them fell dead in a single day.'),
(997064,34,46,10,9,'Nor let us try the patience of the Lord too far, as some of them tried it, with the result that they were, one after another, destroyed by the snakes.'),
(997065,34,46,10,10,'And do not murmur, as some of them murmured, and so were destroyed by the angel of death.'),
(997066,34,46,10,11,'These things happened to them by way of warning, and were recorded to serve as a caution to us, in whose days the close of the ages has come.'),
(997067,34,46,10,12,'Therefore let the person who thinks that they stand take care that they do not fall.'),
(997068,34,46,10,13,'No temptation has come upon you that is not common to all humanity. God will not fail you, and he will not allow you to be tempted beyond your strength; but, when he sends the temptation, he will also provide the way of escape, so that you may have strength to endure.'),
(997069,34,46,10,14,'Therefore, my dear friends, shun the worship of idols.'),
(997070,34,46,10,15,'I speak to you as man of discernment; form your own judgment about what I am saying.'),
(997071,34,46,10,16,'In the cup of blessing which we bless, is not there a sharing in the blood of the Christ? And in the bread which we break, is not there a sharing in the body of the Christ?'),
(997072,34,46,10,17,'The bread is one, and we, though many, are one body; for we all partake of that one bread.'),
(997073,34,46,10,18,'Look at the people of Israel. Do not those who eat the sacrifices share with the altar?'),
(997074,34,46,10,19,'What do I mean? That an offering made to an idol, or the idol itself, is anything?'),
(997075,34,46,10,20,'No; what I say is that the sacrifices offered by the Gentiles are offered to demons and to a being who is no God, and I do not want you to share with demons.'),
(997076,34,46,10,21,'You cannot drink both the Cup of the Lord and the cup of demons. You cannot partake at the Table of the Lord and at the table of demons.'),
(997077,34,46,10,22,'Or are we to rouse the jealousy of the Lord? Are we stronger than he?'),
(997078,34,46,10,23,'Everything is allowable! Yes, but everything is not profitable. Everything is allowable! Yes, but everything does not build up character.'),
(997079,34,46,10,24,'A person must not study their own interests, but the interests of others.'),
(997080,34,46,10,25,'Eat anything that is sold in the market, without making inquiries to satisfy your scruples;'),
(997081,34,46,10,26,'for the earth, with all that is in it, belongs to the Lord.'),
(997082,34,46,10,27,'If an unbeliever invites you to his house and you consent to go, eat anything that is put before you, without making inquiries to satisfy your scruples.'),
(997083,34,46,10,28,'But, if anyone should say to you “This has been offered in sacrifice to an idol,” then, for the sake of the speaker and his scruples, do not eat it.'),
(997084,34,46,10,29,'I do not say your scruples, but his. For why should the freedom that I claim be condemned by the scruples of another?'),
(997085,34,46,10,30,'If, for my part, I take the food thankfully, why should I be abused for eating that for which I give thanks?'),
(997086,34,46,10,31,'Whether, then, you eat or drink or whatever you do, do everything to the honour of God.'),
(997087,34,46,10,32,'Do not cause offence either to Jews or Greeks or to the church of God;'),
(997088,34,46,10,33,'for I, also, try to please everybody in everything, not seeking my own advantage, but do what is best for others, so that they may be saved.'),
(997089,34,46,11,1,'Imitate me, as I myself imitate Christ.'),
(997090,34,46,11,2,'I praise you, indeed, because you never forget me, and are keeping my injunctions in mind, exactly as I laid them on you.'),
(997091,34,46,11,3,'But I am anxious that you should understand that the Christ is the head of every man, that man is the head of woman, and that God is the head of the Christ.'),
(997092,34,46,11,4,'Any man who keeps his head covered, when praying or preaching in public, dishonours him who is his head;'),
(997093,34,46,11,5,'while any woman, who prays or preaches in public bare-headed, dishonours him who is her head; for that is to make herself like one of the shameless women who shave their heads.'),
(997094,34,46,11,6,'Indeed, if a woman does not keep her head covered, she may as well cut her hair short. But, since to cut her hair short, or shave it off, marks her as one of the shameless women, she should keep her head covered.'),
(997095,34,46,11,7,'A man ought not to have his head covered, for he has been from the beginning the likeness of God and the reflection of his glory, but woman is the reflection of man’s glory.'),
(997096,34,46,11,8,'For it was not man who was taken from woman, but woman who was taken from man.'),
(997097,34,46,11,9,'Besides, man was not created for the sake of woman, but woman for the sake of man.'),
(997098,34,46,11,10,'And, therefore, a woman ought to wear on her head a symbol of her subjection, because of the presence of the angels.'),
(997099,34,46,11,11,'Still, when in union with the Lord, woman is not independent of man, or man of woman;'),
(997100,34,46,11,12,'for just as woman came from man, so man comes by means of woman; and all things come from God.'),
(997101,34,46,11,13,'Judge for yourselves. Is it fitting that a woman should pray to God in public with her head uncovered?'),
(997102,34,46,11,14,'Does not nature herself teach us that, while for a man to wear his hair long is degrading to him,'),
(997103,34,46,11,15,'a woman’s long hair is her glory? Her hair has been given her to serve as a covering.'),
(997104,34,46,11,16,'If, however, anyone still thinks it right to contest the point – well, we have no such custom, nor have the churches of God.'),
(997105,34,46,11,17,'In giving directions on the next subject, I cannot praise you; because your meetings do more harm than good.'),
(997106,34,46,11,18,'To begin with, I am told that when you meet together as a church there are divisions among you. In part I believe this,'),
(997107,34,46,11,19,'indeed, there must be parties among you, so that the people of real worth become known.'),
(997108,34,46,11,20,'When you meet together, as I understand, it is not possible to eat the Lord’s Supper;'),
(997109,34,46,11,21,'for, as you eat, each of you tries to secure his own supper first, with the result that one has too little to eat, and another has too much to drink!'),
(997110,34,46,11,22,'Have you no houses in which you can eat and drink? Or are you trying to show your contempt for the church of God, and to humiliate the poor? What can I say to you? Should I praise you? In this matter I cannot praise you.'),
(997111,34,46,11,23,'For I myself received from the Lord the account which I have in turn given to you – how the Lord Jesus, on the very night of his betrayal, took some bread,'),
(997112,34,46,11,24,'and, after saying the thanksgiving, broke it and said'),
(997113,34,46,11,25,'And in the same way with the cup, after supper, saying'),
(997114,34,46,11,26,'For whenever you eat this bread and drink the cup, you proclaim the Lord’s death – until he comes.'),
(997115,34,46,11,27,'Therefore, whoever eats the bread, or drinks the Lord’s cup, in an irreverent spirit, will have to answer for an offence against the Lord’s body and blood.'),
(997116,34,46,11,28,'Let everyone look into their own heart, and only then eat of the bread and drink from the cup.'),
(997117,34,46,11,29,'For the person who eats and drinks brings a judgment on themselves by their eating and drinking, when they do not discern the body.'),
(997118,34,46,11,30,'That is why so many among you are weak and ill, and why some are sleeping.'),
(997119,34,46,11,31,'But, if we judged ourselves rightly, we should not be judged.'),
(997120,34,46,11,32,'Yet, in being judged by the Lord, we are undergoing discipline, so that we may not have judgment passed on us with the rest of the world.'),
(997121,34,46,11,33,'Therefore, my friends, when you meet together to eat the Supper, wait for one another.'),
(997122,34,46,11,34,'If anyone is hungry, they should eat at home, so that your meetings may not bring a judgment on you. The other details I will settle when I come.'),
(997123,34,46,12,1,'In the next place, friends, I do not want you to be ignorant about spiritual gifts.'),
(997124,34,46,12,2,'You know that there was a time when you were Gentiles, going astray after idols that could not speak, just as you happened to be led.'),
(997125,34,46,12,3,'Therefore I tell you plainly that no one who speaks under the influence of the Spirit of God says “JESUS IS ACCURSED,” and that no one can say “JESUS IS LORD,” except under the influence of the Holy Spirit.'),
(997126,34,46,12,4,'Gifts differ, but the Spirit is the same;'),
(997127,34,46,12,5,'ways of serving differ, yet the Master is the same;'),
(997128,34,46,12,6,'results differ, yet the God who brings about every result is in every case the same.'),
(997129,34,46,12,7,'To each of us there is given spiritual illumination for the general good.'),
(997130,34,46,12,8,'To one is given the power to speak with wisdom through the Spirit; to another the power to speak with knowledge, due to the same Spirit;'),
(997131,34,46,12,9,'to another faith by the same Spirit; to another power to cure diseases by the one Spirit; to another supernatural powers;'),
(997132,34,46,12,10,'to another the gift of preaching; to another the gift of distinguishing between true and false inspiration; to another varieties of the gift of “tongues”; to another the power to interpret “tongues.”'),
(997133,34,46,12,11,'All these result from one and the same Spirit, who distributes his gifts to each individually as he wills.'),
(997134,34,46,12,12,'For just as the human body is one whole, and yet has many parts, and all its parts, many though they are, form but one body, so it is with the Christ;'),
(997135,34,46,12,13,'for it was by one Spirit that we were all baptized to form one body, whether Jews or Greeks, slaves or free, and were all imbued with one Spirit.'),
(997136,34,46,12,14,'The human body, I repeat, consists not of one part, but of many.'),
(997137,34,46,12,15,'If the foot says “Since I am not a hand, I do not belong to the body,” it does not because of that cease to belong to the body.'),
(997138,34,46,12,16,'Or if the ear says “Since I am not an eye, I do not belong to the body,” it does not because of that cease to belong to the body.'),
(997139,34,46,12,17,'If all the body were an eye, where would the hearing be? If it were all hearing, where would the sense of smell be?'),
(997140,34,46,12,18,'But in fact God has placed each individual part just where he thought fit in the body.'),
(997141,34,46,12,19,'If, however, they all made up only one part, where would the body be?'),
(997142,34,46,12,20,'But in fact, although it has many parts, there is only one body.'),
(997143,34,46,12,21,'The eye cannot say to the hand “I do not need you,” nor, again, the head to the feet “I do not need you.”'),
(997144,34,46,12,22,'No! Those parts of the body that seem naturally the weaker are indispensable;'),
(997145,34,46,12,23,'and those parts which we deem less honourable we surround with special honour; and our ungraceful parts receive a special grace which our graceful parts do not require.'),
(997146,34,46,12,24,'Yes, God has so constructed the body – by giving a special honour to the part that lacks it –'),
(997147,34,46,12,25,'As to secure that there should be no disunion in the body, but that the parts should show the same care for one another.'),
(997148,34,46,12,26,'If one part suffers, all the others suffer with it, and if one part has honour done it, all the others share its joy.'),
(997149,34,46,12,27,'Together you are the body of Christ, and individually its parts.'),
(997150,34,46,12,28,'In the church God has appointed, first, apostles, secondly preachers, thirdly teachers; then he has given supernatural powers, then power to cure diseases, aptness for helping others, capacity to govern, varieties of the gift of “tongues.”'),
(997151,34,46,12,29,'Can everyone be an apostle? Can everyone be a preacher? Can everyone be a teacher? Can everyone have supernatural powers?'),
(997152,34,46,12,30,'Can everyone have power to cure diseases? Can everyone speak in “tongues”? Can everyone interpret them?'),
(997153,34,46,12,31,'Strive for the greater gifts.'),
(997154,34,46,13,1,'Though I speak in the “tongues” of people, or even of angels, yet have not love, I have become mere echoing brass, or a clanging cymbal!'),
(997155,34,46,13,2,'Even though I have the gift of preaching, and fathom all hidden truths and all the depths of knowledge; even though I have such faith as might move mountains, yet have not love, I am nothing!'),
(997156,34,46,13,3,'Even though I dole my substance to the poor, even though I sacrifice my body in order to boast, yet have not love, it avails me nothing!'),
(997157,34,46,13,4,'Love is long-suffering, and kind; love is never envious, never boastful, never conceited, never behaves unbecomingly;'),
(997158,34,46,13,5,'love is never self-seeking, never provoked, never reckons up her wrongs;'),
(997159,34,46,13,6,'love never rejoices at evil, but rejoices in the triumph of truth;'),
(997160,34,46,13,7,'love bears with all things, ever trustful, ever hopeful, ever patient.'),
(997161,34,46,13,8,'Love never fails. But, whether it be the gift of preaching, it will be done with; whether it be the gift of “tongues,” it will cease; whether it be knowledge, it, too, will be done with.'),
(997162,34,46,13,9,'For our knowledge is incomplete, and our preaching is incomplete,'),
(997163,34,46,13,10,'but, when the perfect has come, that which is incomplete will be done with.'),
(997164,34,46,13,11,'When I was a child, I talked as a child, I felt as a child, I reasoned as a child; now that I am a man, I have done with childish ways.'),
(997165,34,46,13,12,'As yet we see, in a mirror, dimly, but then – face to face! As yet my knowledge is incomplete, but then I will know in full, as I have been fully known.'),
(997166,34,46,13,13,'Meanwhile faith, hope, and love endure – these three, but the greatest of these is love.'),
(997167,34,46,14,1,'Seek this love earnestly, and strive for spiritual gifts, above all for the gift of preaching.'),
(997168,34,46,14,2,'The person who, when speaking, uses the gift of “tongues” is speaking, not to people, but to God, for no one understands them; yet in spirit they are speaking of hidden truths.'),
(997169,34,46,14,3,'But those who preach are speaking to their fellow men and women words that will build up faith, and give them comfort and encouragement.'),
(997170,34,46,14,4,'Those who, when speaking, use the gift of “tongues” builds up their own faith, while those who preach build up the faith of the church.'),
(997171,34,46,14,5,'Now I want you all to speak in “tongues,” but much more I wish that you should preach. A preacher is worth more than one who speaks in “tongues,” unless they interprets their words, so that the faith of the church may be built up.'),
(997172,34,46,14,6,'This being so, friends, what good will I do you, if I come to you and speak in “tongues,” unless my words convey some revelation, or knowledge, or take the form of preaching or teaching?'),
(997173,34,46,14,7,'Even with inanimate things, such as a flute or a harp, though they produce sounds, yet unless the notes are quite distinct, how can the tune played on the flute or the harp be recognised?'),
(997174,34,46,14,8,'If the bugle sounds a doubtful call, who will prepare for battle?'),
(997175,34,46,14,9,'And so with you; unless, in using the gift of “tongues,” you utter intelligible words, how can what you say be understood? You will be speaking to the winds!'),
(997176,34,46,14,10,'There is, for instance, a certain number of different languages in the world, and not one of them fails to convey meaning.'),
(997177,34,46,14,11,'If, however, I do not happen to know the language, I will be a foreigner to those who speak it, and they will be foreigners to me.'),
(997178,34,46,14,12,'And so with you; since your are striving for spiritual gifts, be eager to excel in such as will build up the faith of the church.'),
(997179,34,46,14,13,'Therefore anyone who, when speaking, uses the gift of “tongues” should pray for ability to interpret them.'),
(997180,34,46,14,14,'If, when praying, I use the gift of “tongues,” my spirit indeed prays, but my mind is a blank.'),
(997181,34,46,14,15,'What, then, is my conclusion? Simply this – I will pray with my spirit, but with my mind as well; I will sing with my spirit, but with my mind as well.'),
(997182,34,46,14,16,'If you bless God with your spirit only, how can people in the congregation who are without your gift say “Amen” to your thanksgiving? They do not know what you are saying!'),
(997183,34,46,14,17,'Your thanksgiving may be excellent, but the other is not helped by it.'),
(997184,34,46,14,18,'Thank God, I use the gift of “tongues” more than any of you.'),
(997185,34,46,14,19,'But at a meeting of the church I would rather speak five words with my mind, and so teach others, than ten thousand words when using the gift of “tongues.”'),
(997186,34,46,14,20,'My friends, do not show yourselves children in understanding. In wickedness be infants, but in understanding show yourselves adults.'),
(997187,34,46,14,21,'It is said in the Law –'),
(997188,34,46,14,22,'Therefore the gift of the “tongues” is intended as a sign, not for those who believe in Christ, but for those who do not, while the gift of preaching is intended as a sign, not for those who do not believe in Christ, but for those who do.'),
(997189,34,46,14,23,'So, when the whole church meets, if all present use the gift of “tongues,” and some people who are without the gift, or who are unbelievers, come in, will not they say that you are mad?'),
(997190,34,46,14,24,'While, if all those present use the gift of preaching, and an unbeliever, or someone without the gift, comes in, they are convinced of their sinfulness by them all, they are called to account by them all;'),
(997191,34,46,14,25,'the secrets of their heart are revealed, and then, throwing themselves on their face, they will worship God, and declare “God is indeed among you!”'),
(997192,34,46,14,26,'What do I suggest, then, friends? Whenever you meet for worship, each of you comes, either with a hymn, or a lesson, or a revelation, or the gift of “tongues,” or the interpretation of them; let everything be directed to the building up of faith.'),
(997193,34,46,14,27,'If any of you use the gift of “tongues,” not more than two, or at the most three, should do so – each speaking in his turn – and someone should interpret them.'),
(997194,34,46,14,28,'If there is no one able to interpret what is said, they should remain silent at the meeting of the church, and speak to themselves and to God.'),
(997195,34,46,14,29,'Of preachers two or three should speak, and the rest should weigh well what is said.'),
(997196,34,46,14,30,'But, if some revelation is made to another person as he sits there, the first speaker should stop.'),
(997197,34,46,14,31,'For you can all preach in turn, so that all may learn some lesson and all receive encouragement.'),
(997198,34,46,14,32,'(The spirit that moves the preachers is within the preachers’ control;'),
(997199,34,46,14,33,'for God is not a God of disorder, but of peace.) This custom prevails in all the churches of Christ’s people.'),
(997200,34,46,14,34,'At the meetings of the church married women should remain silent, for they are not allowed to speak in public; they should take a subordinate place, as the Law itself directs.'),
(997201,34,46,14,35,'If they want information on any point, they should ask their husbands about it at home; for it is unbecoming for a married woman to speak at a meeting of the church.'),
(997202,34,46,14,36,'What! Did God’s message to the world originate with you? Or did it find its way to none but you?'),
(997203,34,46,14,37,'If anyone thinks that he has the gift of preaching or any other spiritual gift, he should recognise that what I am now saying to you is a command from the Lord.'),
(997204,34,46,14,38,'Anyone who ignores it may be ignored.'),
(997205,34,46,14,39,'Therefore, my friends, strive for the gift of preaching, and yet do not forbid speaking in “tongues.”'),
(997206,34,46,14,40,'Let everything be done in a proper and orderly manner.'),
(997207,34,46,15,1,'Next, friends, I would like to remind you of the good news which I told you, and which you received – the good news on which you have taken your stand,'),
(997208,34,46,15,2,'and by means of which you are being saved. I would like to remind you of the words that I used in telling it to you, since you are still holding fast to it, and since it was not in vain that you became believers in Christ.'),
(997209,34,46,15,3,'For at the very beginning of my teaching I gave you the account which I had myself received – that Christ died for our sins (as the scriptures had foretold),'),
(997210,34,46,15,4,'that he was buried, that on the third day he was raised (as the scriptures had foretold),'),
(997211,34,46,15,5,'and that he appeared to Cephas, and then to the Twelve.'),
(997212,34,46,15,6,'After that, he appeared to more than five hundred of his followers at one time, most of whom are still alive, though some have gone to their rest.'),
(997213,34,46,15,7,'After that, he appeared to James, and then to all the apostles.'),
(997214,34,46,15,8,'Last of all, he appeared even to me, who am, as it were, the abortion.'),
(997215,34,46,15,9,'For I am the meanest of the apostles, I who am unworthy of the name of “apostle,” because I persecuted the church of God.'),
(997216,34,46,15,10,'But it is through the love of God that I am what I am, and the love that he showed me has not been wasted. No, I have toiled harder than any of them, and yet it was not I, but the love of God working with me.'),
(997217,34,46,15,11,'Whether, then, it was I or whether it was they, this we proclaim, and this you believed.'),
(997218,34,46,15,12,'Now, if it is proclaimed of Christ that he has been raised from the dead, how is it that some of you say that there is no such thing as a resurrection of the dead?'),
(997219,34,46,15,13,'But, if there is no such thing as a resurrection of the dead, then even Christ has not been raised;'),
(997220,34,46,15,14,'and, if Christ has not been raised, then our proclamation is without meaning, and our faith without meaning also!'),
(997221,34,46,15,15,'Yes, and we are being proved to have borne false testimony about God; for we testified of God that he raised the Christ, whom he did not raise, if, indeed, the dead do not rise!'),
(997222,34,46,15,16,'For, if the dead do not rise, then even Christ himself has not been raised,'),
(997223,34,46,15,17,'and, if Christ has not been raised, your faith is folly – your sins are on you still!'),
(997224,34,46,15,18,'Yes, and they, who have passed to their rest in union with Christ, perished!'),
(997225,34,46,15,19,'If all that we have done has been to place our hope in Christ for this life, then we of all people are the most to be pitied.'),
(997226,34,46,15,20,'But, in truth, Christ has been raised from the dead, the first-fruits of those who are at rest.'),
(997227,34,46,15,21,'For, since through a man there is death, so, too, through a man there is a resurrection of the dead.'),
(997228,34,46,15,22,'For, as through union with Adam all die, so through union with the Christ will all be made to live.'),
(997229,34,46,15,23,'But each in their proper order – Christ the first-fruits; afterwards, at his coming, those who belong to the Christ.'),
(997230,34,46,15,24,'Then will come the end – when he surrenders the kingdom to his God and Father, having overthrown all other rule and all other authority and power.'),
(997231,34,46,15,25,'For he must reign until God “has put all his enemies under his feet.”'),
(997232,34,46,15,26,'The last enemy to be overthrown is death;'),
(997233,34,46,15,27,'for God has placed all things under Christ’s feet. (But, when it is said that all things have been placed under Christ, it is plain that God is excepted who placed everything under him.)'),
(997234,34,46,15,28,'And, when everything has been placed under him, the Son will place himself under God who placed everything under him, so that God may be all in all!'),
(997235,34,46,15,29,'Again, what good will they be doing who are baptized on behalf of the dead? If it is true that the dead do not rise, why are people baptized on their behalf?'),
(997236,34,46,15,30,'Why, too, do we risk our lives every hour?'),
(997237,34,46,15,31,'Daily I face death – I swear it, friends, by the pride in you that I feel through my union with Christ Jesus, our Lord.'),
(997238,34,46,15,32,'If with only human hopes I had fought in the arena at Ephesus, what should I have gained by it? If the dead do not rise, then let us eat and drink, for tomorrow we will die!'),
(997239,34,46,15,33,'Do not be deceived.'),
(997240,34,46,15,34,'Wake up to a righteous life, and cease to sin. There are some who have no true knowledge of God. I speak in this way to shame you.'),
(997241,34,46,15,35,'Someone, however, may ask “How do the dead rise? And in what body will they come?”'),
(997242,34,46,15,36,'You foolish person! The seed you yourself sow does not come to life, unless it dies!'),
(997243,34,46,15,37,'And when you sow, you sow not the body that will be, but a mere grain – perhaps of wheat, or something else.'),
(997244,34,46,15,38,'God gives it the body that he pleases – to each seed its special body.'),
(997245,34,46,15,39,'All forms of life are not the same; there is one for people, another for beasts, another for birds, and another for fish.'),
(997246,34,46,15,40,'There are heavenly bodies, and earthly bodies; but the beauty of the heavenly bodies is not the beauty of the earthly.'),
(997247,34,46,15,41,'There is a beauty of the sun, and a beauty of the moon, and a beauty of the stars; for even star differs from star in beauty.'),
(997248,34,46,15,42,'It is the same with the resurrection of the dead. Sown a mortal body, it rises immortal; sown disfigured, it rises beautiful;'),
(997249,34,46,15,43,'sown weak, it rises strong; sown a human body, it rises a spiritual body.'),
(997250,34,46,15,44,'As surely as there is a human body, there is also a spiritual body.'),
(997251,34,46,15,45,'That is what is meant by the words – “Adam, the first man, became a human being”; the last Adam became a life-giving spirit.'),
(997252,34,46,15,46,'That which comes first is not the spiritual, but the human; afterwards comes the spiritual;'),
(997253,34,46,15,47,'the first man was from the dust of the earth; the second man from heaven.'),
(997254,34,46,15,48,'Those who are of the dust are like him who came from the dust; and those who are of heaven are like him who came from heaven.'),
(997255,34,46,15,49,'And as we have borne the likeness of him who came from the dust, so let us bear the likeness of him who came from heaven.'),
(997256,34,46,15,50,'This I say, friends – Flesh and blood can have no share in the kingdom of God, nor can the perishable share the imperishable.'),
(997257,34,46,15,51,'Listen, I will tell you God’s hidden purpose! We will not all have passed to our rest, but we will all be transformed – in a moment, in the twinkling of an eye,'),
(997258,34,46,15,52,'at the last trumpet-call; for the trumpet will sound, and the dead will rise immortal, and we, also, will be transformed.'),
(997259,34,46,15,53,'For this perishable body of ours must put on an imperishable form, and this dying body a deathless form.'),
(997260,34,46,15,54,'And, when this dying body has put on its deathless form, then indeed will the words of scripture come true –'),
(997261,34,46,15,55,'“death has been swallowed up in victory! Where, Death, is your victory? Where, death, is your sting?”'),
(997262,34,46,15,56,'It is sin that gives death its sting, and it is the Law that gives sin its power.'),
(997263,34,46,15,57,'But thanks be to God, who gives us the victory, through Jesus Christ, our Lord.'),
(997264,34,46,15,58,'Therefore, my dear friends, stand firm, unshaken, always diligent in the Lord’s work, for you know that, in union with him, your toil is not in vain.'),
(997265,34,46,16,1,'With reference to the collection for Christ’s people, I want you to follow the instructions that I gave to the churches in Galatia.'),
(997266,34,46,16,2,'On the first day of every week each of you should put by what he can afford, so that no collections need be made after I have come.'),
(997267,34,46,16,3,'On my arrival, I will send any persons, whom you may authorise by letter, to carry your gift to Jerusalem;'),
(997268,34,46,16,4,'and, if it appears to be worth while for me to go also, they will go with me.'),
(997269,34,46,16,5,'I will come to you as soon as I have been through Macedonia – for I am going through Macedonia –'),
(997270,34,46,16,6,'And I will probably make some stay with you or, perhaps, remain for the winter, so that you may yourselves send me on my way, wherever I may be going.'),
(997271,34,46,16,7,'I do not propose to pay you a visit in passing now, for I hope to stay with you for some time, if the Lord permits.'),
(997272,34,46,16,8,'I intend, however, staying at Ephesus until the Festival at the close of the Harvest;'),
(997273,34,46,16,9,'for a great opening for active work has presented itself, and there are many opponents.'),
(997274,34,46,16,10,'If Timothy comes, take care that he has no cause for feeling anxious while he is with you. He is doing the Master’s work no less than I am.'),
(997275,34,46,16,11,'No one, therefore, should slight him. See him safely on his way to me, for I am expecting him with some of our friends.'),
(997276,34,46,16,12,'As for our friend Apollos, I have often urged him to go to you with the others. He has, however, been very unwilling to do so as yet; but he will go as soon as he finds a good opportunity.'),
(997277,34,46,16,13,'Be watchful; stand firm in your faith; be brave; be strong.'),
(997278,34,46,16,14,'Let everything you do be done in a loving spirit.'),
(997279,34,46,16,15,'I have another request to make of you, friends. You remember Stephanas and his household, and that they were the first-fruits gathered in from Greece, and set themselves to serve Christ’s people.'),
(997280,34,46,16,16,'I want you, on your part, to show deference to such people as these, as well as to every fellow labourer and earnest worker.'),
(997281,34,46,16,17,'I am glad Stephanas and Fortunatus and Achaicus have come, for they have made up for your absence;'),
(997282,34,46,16,18,'they have cheered my heart, and your hearts also. Recognise the worth of such people as these.'),
(997283,34,46,16,19,'The churches in Roman Asia send you their greetings. Aquila and Prisca and the church that meets at their house send you many Christian greetings.'),
(997284,34,46,16,20,'All of the Lord’s followers send you greetings. Greet one another with a sacred kiss.'),
(997285,34,46,16,21,'I, Paul, add this greeting in my own handwriting.'),
(997286,34,46,16,22,'Accursed be anyone who has no love for the Lord. THE LORD IS COMING.'),
(997287,34,46,16,23,'May the blessing of the Lord Jesus be with you.'),
(997288,34,46,16,24,'My love to all of you who are in union with Christ Jesus.'),
(997289,34,47,1,1,'To the church of God in Corinth, and to all Christ’s people throughout Greece, from Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus, by the will of God, and from Timothy, who is also a follower.'),
(997290,34,47,1,2,'May God, our Father, and the Lord Jesus Christ bless you and give you peace.'),
(997291,34,47,1,3,'Blessed is the God and Father of Jesus Christ our Lord, the all-merciful Father, the God ever ready to console,'),
(997292,34,47,1,4,'who consoles us in all our troubles, so that we may be able to console those who are in any trouble with the consolation that we ourselves receive from him.'),
(997293,34,47,1,5,'It is true that we have our full share of the sufferings of the Christ, but through the Christ we have also our full share of consolation.'),
(997294,34,47,1,6,'If we meet with trouble, it is for the sake of your consolation and salvation; and, if we find consolation, it is for the sake of the consolation that you will experience when you are called to endure the sufferings that we ourselves are enduring;'),
(997295,34,47,1,7,'and our hope for you remains unshaken. We know that, as you are sharing our sufferings, you will also share our consolation.'),
(997296,34,47,1,8,'We want you, friends, to know that, in the troubles which befell us in Roman Asia, we were burdened altogether beyond our strength, so much so that we even despaired of life.'),
(997297,34,47,1,9,'Indeed, we had the presentiment that we must die, so that we might rely, not on ourselves, but on God who raises the dead.'),
(997298,34,47,1,10,'And from so imminent a death God delivered us, and will deliver us again; for in him we have placed our hopes of future deliverance, while you, also, help us by your prayers.'),
(997299,34,47,1,11,'And then many lips will give thanks on our behalf for the blessing granted us in answer to many prayers.'),
(997300,34,47,1,12,'Indeed, our main ground for satisfaction is this – Our conscience tells us that our conduct in the world, and still more in our relations with you, was marked by a purity of motive and a sincerity that were inspired by God, and was based, not on worldly policy, but on the help of God.'),
(997301,34,47,1,13,'We never write anything to you other than what you will acknowledge to the very end –'),
(997302,34,47,1,14,'And, indeed, you have already partly acknowledged it about us – that you have a right to be proud of us, as we will be proud of you, on the day of our Lord Jesus.'),
(997303,34,47,1,15,'With this conviction in my mind, I planned to come to see you first, so that your pleasure might be doubled –'),
(997304,34,47,1,16,'To visit you both on my way to Macedonia, and to come to you again on my return from Macedonia, and then to get you to send me on my way into Judea.'),
(997305,34,47,1,17,'As this was my plan, where, pray, did I show any fickleness of purpose? Or do you think that my plans are formed on mere impulse, so that in the same breath I say “Yes” and “No”?'),
(997306,34,47,1,18,'As God is true, the message that we brought you does not waver between “Yes” and “No”!'),
(997307,34,47,1,19,'The Son of God, Christ Jesus, whom we – Silas, Timothy, and I – proclaimed among you, never wavered between “Yes” and “No.” With him it has always been “Yes.”'),
(997308,34,47,1,20,'For, many as were the promises of God, in Christ is the “Yes” that fulfils them. Therefore, through Christ again, let the “Amen” rise, through us, to the glory of God.'),
(997309,34,47,1,21,'God who brings us, with you, into close union with Christ, and who consecrated us,'),
(997310,34,47,1,22,'also set his seal on us, and gave us his Spirit in our hearts as a pledge of future blessings.'),
(997311,34,47,1,23,'But, as my life will answer for it, I call God to witness that it was to spare you that I deferred my visit to Corinth.'),
(997312,34,47,1,24,'I do not mean that we are to dictate to you with regard to your faith; on the contrary, we work with you for your true happiness; indeed, it is through your faith that you are standing firm.'),
(997313,34,47,2,1,'For my own sake, as well, I decided not to pay you another painful visit.'),
(997314,34,47,2,2,'If it is I who cause you pain, why, who is there to cheer me, except the person whom I am paining?'),
(997315,34,47,2,3,'So I wrote as I did because I was afraid that if I had come, I should have been pained by those who ought to have made me glad; for I felt sure that it was true of you all that my joy was in every case yours also.'),
(997316,34,47,2,4,'I wrote to you in sore trouble and distress of heart and with many tears, not to give you pain, but to let you see how intense a love I have for you.'),
(997317,34,47,2,5,'Now whoever has caused the pain has not so much pained me, as he has, to some extent – not to be too severe – pained every one of you.'),
(997318,34,47,2,6,'The man to whom I refer has been sufficiently punished by the penalty inflicted by the majority of you;'),
(997319,34,47,2,7,'so that now you must take the opposite course, and forgive and encourage him, or else he may be overwhelmed by the intensity of his pain.'),
(997320,34,47,2,8,'So I entreat you to assure him of your love.'),
(997321,34,47,2,9,'I had this further object, also, in what I wrote – to find out whether you might be relied on to be obedient in everything.'),
(997322,34,47,2,10,'Anyone you forgive, I forgive them, too. Indeed, for my part, whatever I have forgiven (if I have had to forgive anything), I have forgiven for your sakes, in the presence of Christ,'),
(997323,34,47,2,11,'so as to prevent Satan from taking advantage of us; for we are not ignorant of his devices.'),
(997324,34,47,2,12,'When I went to the district round Troas to tell the good news of the Christ, even though there was an opening for serving the Master,'),
(997325,34,47,2,13,'I could get no peace of mind because I failed to find Titus, my friend; so I took leave of the people there, and went on to Macedonia.'),
(997326,34,47,2,14,'All thanks to God, who, through our union with the Christ, leads us in one continual triumph, and uses us to spread the sweet perfume of the knowledge of him in every place.'),
(997327,34,47,2,15,'For we are the fragrance of Christ ascending to God – both among those who are in the path of salvation and among those who are in the path to ruin.'),
(997328,34,47,2,16,'To the latter we are a stench which arises from death and tells of death; to the former a fragrance which arises from life and tells of life. But who is equal to such a task?'),
(997329,34,47,2,17,'Unlike many people, we are not in the habit of making profit out of God’s message; but in all sincerity, and bearing God’s commission, we speak before him in union with Christ.'),
(997330,34,47,3,1,'Are we beginning to commend ourselves again? Or are we like some who need letters of commendation to you, or from you?'),
(997331,34,47,3,2,'You yourselves are our letter – a letter written on our hearts, and one which everybody can read and understand.'),
(997332,34,47,3,3,'All can see that you are a letter from Christ delivered by us, a letter written, not with ink, but with the Spirit of the living God, not on tablets of stone, but on tablets of human hearts.'),
(997333,34,47,3,4,'This, then, is the confidence in regard to God that we have gained through the Christ.'),
(997334,34,47,3,5,'I do not mean that we are fit to form any judgment by ourselves, as if on our own authority;'),
(997335,34,47,3,6,'our fitness comes from God, who himself made us fit to be assistants of a new covenant, of which the substance is, not a written Law, but a Spirit. For the written Law means death, but the Spirit gives life.'),
(997336,34,47,3,7,'If the system of religion which involved death, embodied in a written Law and engraved on stones, began amid such glory, that the Israelites were unable to gaze at the face of Moses because of its glory, though it was but a passing glory,'),
(997337,34,47,3,8,'will not the religion that confers the Spirit have still greater glory?'),
(997338,34,47,3,9,'For, if there was a glory in the religion that involved condemnation, far greater is the glory of the religion that confers righteousness!'),
(997339,34,47,3,10,'Indeed, that which then had glory has lost its glory, because of the glory which surpasses it.'),
(997340,34,47,3,11,'And, if that which was to pass away was attended with glory, far more will that which is to endure be surrounded with glory!'),
(997341,34,47,3,12,'With such a hope as this, we speak with all plainness;'),
(997342,34,47,3,13,'unlike Moses, who covered his face with a veil, to prevent the Israelites from gazing at the disappearance of what was passing away.'),
(997343,34,47,3,14,'But their minds were slow to learn. Indeed, to this very day, at the public reading of the old covenant, the same veil remains; only for those who are in union with Christ does it pass away.'),
(997344,34,47,3,15,'But, even to this day, whenever Moses is read, a veil lies on their hearts.'),
(997345,34,47,3,16,'Yet, whenever someone turns to the Lord, the veil is removed.'),
(997346,34,47,3,17,'And the Lord is the Spirit, and, where the Spirit of the Lord is, there is freedom.'),
(997347,34,47,3,18,'And all of us, with faces from which the veil is lifted, seeing, as if reflected in a mirror, the glory of the Lord, are being transformed into his likeness, from glory to glory, as it is given by the Lord, the Spirit.'),
(997348,34,47,4,1,'Therefore, since it is by God’s mercy that we are engaged in this ministry, we do not lose heart.'),
(997349,34,47,4,2,'No, we have renounced the secrecy prompted by shame, refusing to adopt crafty ways, or to tamper with God’s message, and commending ourselves to everyone’s conscience, in the sight of God, by our exhibition of the truth.'),
(997350,34,47,4,3,'And, even if the good news that we bring is veiled, it is veiled only in the case of those who are on the path to ruin –'),
(997351,34,47,4,4,'people whose minds have been blinded by the God of this age, unbelievers as they are, so that the light from the good news of the glory of the Christ, who is the incarnation of God, should not shine for them.'),
(997352,34,47,4,5,'(For it is not ourselves that we proclaim, but Christ Jesus, as Lord, and ourselves as your servants for Jesus’ sake.)'),
(997353,34,47,4,6,'Indeed, the same God who said “Out of darkness light will shine,” has shone in on our hearts, so that we should bring out into the light the knowledge of the glory of God, seen in the face of Christ.'),
(997354,34,47,4,7,'This treasure we have in these earthen vessels, so that its all-prevailing power may be seen to come from God, and not to be our own.'),
(997355,34,47,4,8,'Though hard pressed on every side, we are never hemmed in; though perplexed, never driven to despair;'),
(997356,34,47,4,9,'though pursued, never abandoned; though struck down, never killed!'),
(997357,34,47,4,10,'We always bear on our bodies the marks of the death that Jesus died, so that the life also of Jesus may be exhibited in our bodies.'),
(997358,34,47,4,11,'Indeed, we who still live are continually being given over to death for Jesus’ sake, so that the life also of Jesus may be exhibited in our mortal nature.'),
(997359,34,47,4,12,'And so, while death is at work within us, life is at work within you.'),
(997360,34,47,4,13,'But, in the same spirit of faith as that expressed in the words – “I believed, and therefore I spoke,” we, also believe, and therefore speak.'),
(997361,34,47,4,14,'For we know that he who raised the Lord Jesus will raise us also with him, and will bring us, with you, into his presence.'),
(997362,34,47,4,15,'For all this is for your sakes, so that the loving kindness of God, spreading from heart to heart, may cause yet more hearts to overflow with thanksgiving, to his glory.'),
(997363,34,47,4,16,'Therefore, as I said, we do not lose heart. No, even though outwardly we are wasting away, yet inwardly we are being renewed day by day.'),
(997364,34,47,4,17,'The light burden of our momentary trouble is preparing for us, in measure transcending thought, a weight of imperishable glory;'),
(997365,34,47,4,18,'we, all the while, gazing not on what is seen, but on what is unseen; for what is seen is transient, but what is unseen is imperishable.'),
(997366,34,47,5,1,'For we know that if our tent – that earthly body which is now our home – is taken down, we have a house of God’s building, a home not made by hands, imperishable, in heaven.'),
(997367,34,47,5,2,'Even while in our present body we sigh, longing to put over it our heavenly house,'),
(997368,34,47,5,3,'sure that, when we have put it on, we will never be found discarnate.'),
(997369,34,47,5,4,'For we who are in this tent sigh under our burden, unwilling to take it off, yet wishing to put our heavenly body over it, so that all that is mortal may be absorbed in life.'),
(997370,34,47,5,5,'And he who has prepared us for this change is God, who has also given us his Spirit as a pledge.'),
(997371,34,47,5,6,'Therefore we are always confident, knowing that, while our home is in the body, we are absent from our home with the Lord.'),
(997372,34,47,5,7,'For we guide our lives by faith, and not by what we see.'),
(997373,34,47,5,8,'And in this confidence we would gladly leave our home in the body, and make our home with the Lord.'),
(997374,34,47,5,9,'Therefore, whether in our home or absent from our home, our one ambition is to please him.'),
(997375,34,47,5,10,'For at the court of the Christ we must all appear in our true characters, so that each may reap the results of the life which he has lived in the body, in accordance with his actions – whether good or worthless.'),
(997376,34,47,5,11,'Therefore, because we know the fear inspired by the Lord, it is true that we are trying to win people over, but our motives are plain to God; and I hope that in your inmost hearts they are plain to you also.'),
(997377,34,47,5,12,'We are not ‘commending ourselves’ again to you, but rather are giving you cause for pride in us, so that you may have an answer ready for those who pride themselves on appearances and not on character.'),
(997378,34,47,5,13,'For, if we were ‘beside ourselves,’ it was in God’s service! If we are not in our senses, it is in yours!'),
(997379,34,47,5,14,'It is the love of the Christ which compels us, when we reflect that, as one died for all, therefore all died;'),
(997380,34,47,5,15,'and that he died for all, so that the living should no longer live for themselves, but for him who died and rose for them.'),
(997381,34,47,5,16,'For ourselves, then, from this time forward, we refuse to regard anyone from the world’s standpoint. Even if we once thought of Christ from the standpoint of the world, yet now we do so no longer.'),
(997382,34,47,5,17,'Therefore, if anyone is in union with Christ, he is a new being! His old life has passed away; a new life has begun!'),
(997383,34,47,5,18,'But all this is the work of God, who reconciled us to himself through Christ, and gave us the Ministry of Reconciliation –'),
(997384,34,47,5,19,'To proclaim that God, in Christ, was reconciling the world to himself, not reckoning people’s offences against them, and that he had entrusted us with the message of this reconciliation.'),
(997385,34,47,5,20,'It is, then, on Christ’s behalf that we are acting as ambassadors, God, as it were, appealing to you through us. We implore you on Christ’s behalf – Be reconciled to God.'),
(997386,34,47,5,21,'For our sake God made Christ, who was innocent of sin, one with our sinfulness, so that in him we might be made one with the righteousness of God.'),
(997387,34,47,6,1,'Therefore, as God’s fellow workers, we also appeal to you not to receive his loving kindness in vain.'),
(997388,34,47,6,2,'For he says –'),
(997389,34,47,6,3,'Never do we put an obstacle in anyone’s way, so that no fault may be found with our ministry.'),
(997390,34,47,6,4,'No, we are trying to commend ourselves under all circumstances, as God’s assistants should – in many an hour of endurance, in troubles, in hardships, in difficulties,'),
(997391,34,47,6,5,'in floggings, in imprisonments, in riots, in toils, in sleepless nights, in fastings;'),
(997392,34,47,6,6,'by purity, by knowledge, by patience, by kindliness, by holiness of spirit, by unfeigned love;'),
(997393,34,47,6,7,'by the message of truth, and by the power of God; by the weapons of righteousness in the right hand and in the left;'),
(997394,34,47,6,8,'amid honour and disrepute, amid slander and praise; regarded as deceivers, yet proved to be true;'),
(997395,34,47,6,9,'as unknown, yet well-known; as at death’s door, yet, see, we are living; as chastised, yet not killed;'),
(997396,34,47,6,10,'as saddened, yet always rejoicing; as poor, yet enriching many; as having nothing, and yet possessing all things!'),
(997397,34,47,6,11,'We have been speaking freely to you, dear friends in Corinth; we have opened our heart;'),
(997398,34,47,6,12,'there is room there for you, yet there is not room, in your love, for us.'),
(997399,34,47,6,13,'Can you not in return – I appeal to you as I should to children – open your hearts to us?'),
(997400,34,47,6,14,'Do not enter into inconsistent relations with those who reject the faith. For what partnership can there be between righteousness and lawlessness? Or what has light to do with darkness?'),
(997401,34,47,6,15,'What harmony can there be between Christ and Belial? Or what can those who accept the faith have in common with those who reject it?'),
(997402,34,47,6,16,'What agreement can you be between a temple of God and idols? And we are a temple of the living God. That is what God meant when he said –'),
(997403,34,47,6,17,'Therefore ‘Come out from among the nations, and separate yourselves from them,’ says the Lord,'),
(997404,34,47,6,18,'and I will be a father to you, and you will be my sons and daughters,’'),
(997405,34,47,7,1,'With these promises, dear friends, let us purify ourselves from everything that pollutes either body or spirit, and, in deepest respect for God, aim at perfect holiness.'),
(997406,34,47,7,2,'Make room for us in your hearts. In no instance have we ever wronged, or harmed, or taken advantage of, anyone.'),
(997407,34,47,7,3,'I am not saying this to condemn you. Indeed, I have already said that you are in our heart, to live and die together.'),
(997408,34,47,7,4,'I have the utmost confidence in you; I am always boasting about you. I am full of encouragement and, in spite of all our troubles, my heart is overflowing with happiness.'),
(997409,34,47,7,5,'Ever since we reached Macedonia, we have had no rest in body or mind; on every side there have been troubles – conflicts without, anxieties within.'),
(997410,34,47,7,6,'But God, who encourages the downcast, has encouraged us by the arrival of Titus.'),
(997411,34,47,7,7,'And it is not only by his arrival that we are encouraged, but also by the encouragement which he received from you; for he tells us of your strong affection, your penitence, and your zeal on my behalf – so that I am happier still.'),
(997412,34,47,7,8,'For, though I caused you sorrow by my letter, I do not regret it. Even if I were inclined to regret it – for I see that my letter did cause you sorrow though only for a time –'),
(997413,34,47,7,9,'I am glad now; not because of the sorrow it caused you, but because your sorrow brought you to repentance. For it was God’s will that you should feel sorrow, in order that you should not suffer loss in any way at our hands.'),
(997414,34,47,7,10,'For, when sorrow is in accordance with God’s will, it results in a repentance leading to salvation, and which will never be regretted. The sure result of the sorrow that the world knows is death.'),
(997415,34,47,7,11,'For see what results that other sorrow – sorrow in accordance with God’s will – has had in your case. What earnestness it produced! What explanations! What strong feeling! What alarm! What longing! What eagerness! What readiness to punish! You have proved yourselves altogether free from guilt in that matter.'),
(997416,34,47,7,12,'So, then, even though I did write to you, it was not for the sake of the wrong-doer, or of the man who was wronged, but to make you conscious, in the sight of God, of your own earnest care for us. And it is this that has encouraged us.'),
(997417,34,47,7,13,'In addition to the encouragement that this gave us, we were made far happier still by the happiness of Titus for his heart has been cheered by you all.'),
(997418,34,47,7,14,'Although I have been boasting a little to him about you, you did not put me to shame; but, just as every thing we had said to you was true, so our boasting to Titus about you has also proved to be the truth.'),
(997419,34,47,7,15,'And his affection for you is all the greater, as he remembers the deference that you all showed him, and recalls how you received him with anxious care.'),
(997420,34,47,7,16,'I am glad that I can feel perfect confidence in you.'),
(997421,34,47,8,1,'We want to remind you, friends, of the love that God has shown to the churches in Macedonia –'),
(997422,34,47,8,2,'How, tired though they were by many a trouble, their overflowing happiness, and even their deep poverty, resulted in a flood of generosity.'),
(997423,34,47,8,3,'I can bear witness that to the full extent of their power, and even beyond their power, spontaneously,'),
(997424,34,47,8,4,'and with many an appeal to us for permission, they showed their love, and contributed their share towards the fund for their fellow Christians.'),
(997425,34,47,8,5,'And that, not only in the way we had expected; but first they gave themselves to the Lord, and to us also, in accordance with God’s will.'),
(997426,34,47,8,6,'And this led us beg Titus, since he had started the work for you, he should also see to the completion of this expression of your love.'),
(997427,34,47,8,7,'And, remembering how you excel in everything – in faith, in teaching, in knowledge, in unfailing earnestness, and in the affection that we have awakened in you – I ask you to excel also in this expression of your love.'),
(997428,34,47,8,8,'I am not laying a command on you, but I am making use of the earnestness shown by others to test the genuineness of your affection.'),
(997429,34,47,8,9,'For you do not forget the loving kindness of our Lord Jesus Christ – how that for your sakes, although he was rich, he became poor, so that you also might become rich through his poverty.'),
(997430,34,47,8,10,'I am only making suggestions on this matter; for this is the best course for you, since you were a year before others, not only in taking action, but also in showing your readiness to do so.'),
(997431,34,47,8,11,'And now I want you to complete the work, so that its completion may correspond with your willing readiness – in proportion, of course, to your means.'),
(997432,34,47,8,12,'For, where there is willingness, a person’s gift is valued by its comparison with what they have, and not with what they do not have.'),
(997433,34,47,8,13,'For our object is not to give relief to others and bring distress on you. It is a matter of a fair balance.'),
(997434,34,47,8,14,'On this occasion what you can spare will supply what they need, at another time what they can spare may supply your need, and so things will be equal.'),
(997435,34,47,8,15,'As scripture says –'),
(997436,34,47,8,16,'I thank God for inspiring Titus with the same keen interest in your welfare that I have;'),
(997437,34,47,8,17,'for Titus has responded to my appeals and, in his great earnestness, is starting to go to you of his own accord.'),
(997438,34,47,8,18,'We are sending with him one of the Lord’s followers whose fame in the service of the good news has spread through all the churches;'),
(997439,34,47,8,19,'and not only that, but he has been elected by the churches to accompany us on our journey, in connexion with this expression of your love, which we are personally administering to the honour of the Lord, and to show our deep interest.'),
(997440,34,47,8,20,'What we are specially guarding against is that any fault should be found with us in regard to our administration of this charitable fund;'),
(997441,34,47,8,21,'for we are trying to make arrangements which will be right, not only in the eyes of the Lord, but also in the eyes of people.'),
(997442,34,47,8,22,'We are also sending with them another of our friends, whose earnestness we have many a time proved in many ways, and whom we now find made even more earnest by his great confidence in you.'),
(997443,34,47,8,23,'If I must say anything about Titus, he is my intimate companion, and he shares my work for you; if it is our friends, they are delegates of the churches, an honour to Christ.'),
(997444,34,47,8,24,'Show them, therefore – so that the churches may see it – the proof of your affection, and the ground for our boasting to them about you.'),
(997445,34,47,9,1,'With reference, indeed, to the Fund for your fellow Christians, it is quite superfluous for me to say anything to you.'),
(997446,34,47,9,2,'I know, of course, your willingness to help, and I am always boasting of it to the Macedonians. I tell them that you in Greece have been ready for a year past; and it was really your zeal that stimulated most of them.'),
(997447,34,47,9,3,'So my reason for sending our friends is to prevent what we said about you from proving, in this particular matter, an empty boast, and to enable you to be as well prepared as I have been saying that you are.'),
(997448,34,47,9,4,'Otherwise, if any Macedonians were to come with me, and find you unprepared, we – to say nothing of you – should feel ashamed of our present confidence.'),
(997449,34,47,9,5,'Therefore I think it necessary to beg the friends to go to you in advance, and to complete the arrangements for the gift, which you have already promised, so that it may be ready, as a gift, before I come, and not look as if it were being given under pressure.'),
(997450,34,47,9,6,'Remember the saying – “Scanty sowing, scanty harvest; plentiful sowing, plentiful harvest.”'),
(997451,34,47,9,7,'Let everyone give as he has determined before hand, not grudgingly or under compulsion; for God loves a cheerful giver.'),
(997452,34,47,9,8,'God has power to shower all kinds of blessings on you, so that, having, under all circumstances and on all occasions, all that you can need, you may be able to shower all kinds of benefits on others.'),
(997453,34,47,9,9,'(As scripture says –'),
(997454,34,47,9,10,'And he who supplies seed to the sower, and bread for eating, will supply you with seed, and cause it to increase, and will multiply the fruits of your righteousness).'),
(997455,34,47,9,11,'Rich in all things yourselves, you will be able to show liberality to all, which, with our help, will cause thanksgiving to be offered to God.'),
(997456,34,47,9,12,'For the rendering of a public service such as this, not only relieves the needs of your fellow Christians, but also results in the offering to God of many a thanksgiving.'),
(997457,34,47,9,13,'Through the evidence afforded by the service rendered, you cause people to praise God for your fidelity to your profession of faith in the good news of the Christ, as well as for the liberality of your contributions for them and for all others.'),
(997458,34,47,9,14,'And they also, in their prayers for you, express their longing to see you, because of the surpassing love of God displayed toward you.'),
(997459,34,47,9,15,'All thanks to God for his inestimable gift!'),
(997460,34,47,10,1,'Now, I, Paul, make a personal appeal to you by the meekness and gentleness of the Christ – I who, ‘in your presence, am humble in my bearing towards you, but, when absent, am bold in my language to you’ –'),
(997461,34,47,10,2,'I implore you not to drive me to ‘show my boldness,’ when I do come, by the confident tone which I expect to have to adopt towards some of you, who are expecting to find us influenced in our conduct by earthly motives.'),
(997462,34,47,10,3,'For, though we live an earthly life, we do not wage an earthly war.'),
(997463,34,47,10,4,'The weapons for our warfare are not earthly, but, under God, are powerful enough to pull down strongholds.'),
(997464,34,47,10,5,'We are engaged in confuting arguments and pulling down every barrier raised against the knowledge of God. We are taking captive every hostile thought, to bring it into submission to the Christ,'),
(997465,34,47,10,6,'and are fully prepared to punish every act of rebellion, when once your submission is complete.'),
(997466,34,47,10,7,'You look at the outward appearance of things! Let anyone, who is confident that he belongs to Christ, reflect, for himself, again on the fact – that we belong to Christ no less than he does.'),
(997467,34,47,10,8,'Even if I boast extravagantly about our authority – which the Lord gave us for building up your faith and not for overthrowing it – still I have no reason to be ashamed.'),
(997468,34,47,10,9,'I say this so that it doesn’t seem as if I am trying to overawe you by my letters.'),
(997469,34,47,10,10,'For people say ‘His letters are impressive and vigorous, but his personal appearance is insignificant and his speaking contemptible.’'),
(997470,34,47,10,11,'Let such a person be assured of this – that our words in our letters show us to be, when absent, just what our deeds will show us to be, when present.'),
(997471,34,47,10,12,'We have not indeed the audacity to class or compare ourselves with some of those who indulge in self-commendation! But, when such persons measure themselves by themselves, and compare themselves with themselves, they show a want of wisdom.'),
(997472,34,47,10,13,'We, however, will not give way to unlimited boasting, but will confine ourselves to the limits of the sphere to which God limited us, when he permitted us to come as far as Corinth.'),
(997473,34,47,10,14,'For it is not the case, as it would be if we were not in the habit of coming to you, that we are exceeding our bounds! Why, we were the very first to reach you with the good news of the Christ!'),
(997474,34,47,10,15,'Our boasting, therefore, is not unlimited, nor does it extend to the labours of others; but our hope is that, as your faith grows, our influence among you may be very greatly increased – though still confined to our sphere –'),
(997475,34,47,10,16,'So that we will be able to tell the good news in the districts beyond you, without trespassing on the sphere assigned to others, or boasting of what has been already done.'),
(997476,34,47,10,17,'Let anyone who boasts make their boast of the Lord.'),
(997477,34,47,10,18,'For it is not those who commend themselves that stand the test, but those who are commended by the Lord.'),
(997478,34,47,11,1,'I could wish that you would tolerate a little folly in me! But indeed you do tolerate me.'),
(997479,34,47,11,2,'I am jealous over you with the jealousy of God. For I engaged you to one husband so that I might present you to the Christ a pure bride.'),
(997480,34,47,11,3,'Yet I fear that it may turn out that, just as the snake by his craftiness deceived Eve, so your minds may have lost the loyalty and purity due from you to the Christ.'),
(997481,34,47,11,4,'For, if some newcomer is proclaiming a Jesus other than him whom we proclaimed, or if you are receiving a Spirit different from the Spirit which you received, or a good news different from that which you welcomed, then you are marvellously tolerant!'),
(997482,34,47,11,5,'I do not regard myself as in any way inferior to the most eminent apostles!'),
(997483,34,47,11,6,'Though I am no trained orator, yet I am not without knowledge; indeed we made this perfectly clear to you in every way.'),
(997484,34,47,11,7,'Perhaps you say that I did wrong in humbling myself that you might be exalted – I mean because I told you God’s good news without payment.'),
(997485,34,47,11,8,'I robbed other churches by taking pay from them, so that I might serve you!'),
(997486,34,47,11,9,'And, when I was with you in need, I did not become a burden to any of you; for our friends, on coming from Macedonia, supplied my needs. I kept myself, and will keep myself from being an expense to you in any way.'),
(997487,34,47,11,10,'As surely as I know anything of the truth of Christ, this boast, as far as I am concerned, will not be stopped in any part of Greece.'),
(997488,34,47,11,11,'Why? Because I do not love you? God knows that I do!'),
(997489,34,47,11,12,'What I am doing now I will continue to do in order to cut away the ground from under those who are wishing for some ground for attacking me, so that as regards the thing of which they boast they may appear in their true characters, just as we do.'),
(997490,34,47,11,13,'Such people are false apostles, treacherous workers, disguising themselves as apostles of Christ!'),
(997491,34,47,11,14,'And no wonder; for even Satan disguises himself as an angel of light.'),
(997492,34,47,11,15,'It is not surprising, therefore, if his servants also disguise themselves as servants of righteousness. But their end will be in accordance with their actions.'),
(997493,34,47,11,16,'I say again – Let no one think me a fool! Yet, if you do, at least welcome me as you would a fool, so that I, too may indulge in a little boasting.'),
(997494,34,47,11,17,'When I speak like this, I am not speaking as the Master would, but as a fool might, in boasting so confidently.'),
(997495,34,47,11,18,'As so many are boasting of earthly things, I, too, will boast.'),
(997496,34,47,11,19,'For all your cleverness, you tolerate fools willingly enough!'),
(997497,34,47,11,20,'You tolerate a person even when they enslave you, when they plunder you, when they get you into their power, when they put on airs of superiority, when they strike you in the face!'),
(997498,34,47,11,21,'I admit, to my shame, that we have been weak. But whatever the subject on which others are not afraid to boast – though it is foolish to say so – I am not afraid either!'),
(997499,34,47,11,22,'Are they Hebrews? So am I! Are they Israelites? So am I! Are they descendants of Abraham? So am I!'),
(997500,34,47,11,23,'Are they “Servants of Christ”? Though it is madness to talk like this, I am more so than they! I have had more of toil, more of imprisonment! I have been flogged times without number. I have been often at death’s door.');
INSERT INTO verses (id, version_id, book_id, chapter, verse, text) VALUES
(997501,34,47,11,24,'Five times I received at the hands of my own people forty lashes, all but one.'),
(997502,34,47,11,25,'Three times I was beaten with rods. Once I was stoned. Three times I was shipwrecked. I have spent a whole day and night in the deep.'),
(997503,34,47,11,26,'My journeys have been many. I have been through dangers from rivers, dangers from robbers, dangers from my own people, dangers from the Gentiles, dangers in towns, dangers in the country, dangers on the sea, dangers among people pretending to be followers of the Lord.'),
(997504,34,47,11,27,'I have been through toil and hardship. I have passed many a sleepless night; I have endured hunger and thirst; I have often been without food; I have known cold and nakedness.'),
(997505,34,47,11,28,'And, not to speak of other things, there is my daily burden of anxiety about all the churches.'),
(997506,34,47,11,29,'Who is weak without my being weak? Who is led astray without my burning with indignation?'),
(997507,34,47,11,30,'If I must boast, I will boast of things which show my weakness!'),
(997508,34,47,11,31,'The God and Father of the Lord Jesus – he who is for ever blessed – knows that I am speaking the truth.'),
(997509,34,47,11,32,'When I was in Damascus, the Governor under King Aretas had the gates of that city guarded, so as to arrest me,'),
(997510,34,47,11,33,'but I was let down in a basket through a window in the wall, and so escaped his hands.'),
(997511,34,47,12,1,'I must boast! It is unprofitable; but I will pass to visions and revelations given by the Lord.'),
(997512,34,47,12,2,'I know a man in union with Christ, who, fourteen years ago – whether in the body or out of the body I do not know; God knows – was caught up (this man of whom I am speaking) to the third heaven.'),
(997513,34,47,12,3,'And I know that this man – whether in the body or separated from the body I do not know; God knows –'),
(997514,34,47,12,4,'Was caught up into Paradise, and heard unspeakable things of which no human being may tell.'),
(997515,34,47,12,5,'About such a man I will boast, but about myself I will not boast except as regards my weaknesses.'),
(997516,34,47,12,6,'Yet if I choose to boast, I will not be a fool; for I will be speaking no more than the truth. But I refrain, in case anyone should credit me with more than he can see in me or hear from me, and because of the marvellous character of the revelations.'),
(997517,34,47,12,7,'It was for this reason, and to prevent my thinking too highly of myself, that a thorn was sent to pierce my flesh – an instrument of Satan to discipline me – so that I should not think too highly of myself.'),
(997518,34,47,12,8,'About this I three times entreated the Lord, praying that it might leave me.'),
(997519,34,47,12,9,'But his reply has been –'),
(997520,34,47,12,10,'That is why I delight in weakness, ill treatment, hardship, persecution, and difficulties, when borne for Christ. For, when I am weak, then it is that I am strong!'),
(997521,34,47,12,11,'I have been ‘playing the fool!’ It is you who drove me to it. For it is you who ought to have been commending me! Although I am nobody, in no respect did I prove inferior to the most eminent apostles.'),
(997522,34,47,12,12,'The marks of the true apostle were exhibited among you in constant endurance, as well as by signs, by marvels, and by miracles.'),
(997523,34,47,12,13,'In what respect, I ask, were you treated worse than the other churches, unless it was that, for my part, I refused to become a burden to you? Forgive me the wrong I did to you!'),
(997524,34,47,12,14,'Remember, this is the third time that I have made every preparation to come to see you, and I will refuse to be a burden to you; I want, not your money, but you. It is not the duty of children to put by for their parents, but of parents to put by for their children.'),
(997525,34,47,12,15,'For my part, I will most gladly spend, and be spent, for your welfare. Can it be that the more intensely I love you the less I am to be loved?'),
(997526,34,47,12,16,'You will admit that I was not a burden to you but you say that I was ‘crafty’ and caught you ‘by a trick’!'),
(997527,34,47,12,17,'Do you assert that I took advantage of you through any of those whom I have sent to you?'),
(997528,34,47,12,18,'I urged Titus to go, and I sent another follower with him. Did Titus take any advantage of you? Didn’t we live in the same Spirit, and tread in the same footsteps?'),
(997529,34,47,12,19,'Have you all this time been fancying that it is to you that we are making our defence? No, it is in the sight of God, and in union with Christ, that we are speaking. And all this, dear friends, is to build up your characters;'),
(997530,34,47,12,20,'for I am afraid that perhaps, when I come, I may find that you are not what I want you to be, and, on the other hand, that you may find that I am what you do not want me to be. I am afraid that I may find quarrelling, jealousy, ill feeling, rivalry, slandering, backbiting, self-assertion, and disorder.'),
(997531,34,47,12,21,'I am afraid that, on my next visit, my God may humble me in regard to you, and that I may have to mourn over many who have long been sinning, and have not repented of the impurity, immorality, and sensuality, in which they have indulged.'),
(997532,34,47,13,1,'For the third time I am coming to see you. By the word of two or three witnesses each statement will be established.'),
(997533,34,47,13,2,'I have said it, and I say it again before I come, just as if I were with you on my second visit, though for the moment absent, I say to those who have been long sinning, as well as to all others – that if I come again, I will spare no one.'),
(997534,34,47,13,3,'And that will be the proof, which you are looking for, that the Christ speaks through me. There is no weakness in his dealings with you. No, he shows his power among you.'),
(997535,34,47,13,4,'For though his crucifixion was due to weakness, his life is due to the power of God. And we, also, are weak in his weakness, but with him we will live for you through the power of God.'),
(997536,34,47,13,5,'Put yourselves to the proof, to see whether you are holding to the faith. Test yourselves. Surely you recognise this fact about yourselves – that Jesus Christ is in you! Unless indeed you cannot stand the test!'),
(997537,34,47,13,6,'But I hope that you will recognise that we can stand the test.'),
(997538,34,47,13,7,'We pray God that you may do nothing wrong, not that we may be seen to stand the test, but that you may do what is right, even though we may seem not to stand the test.'),
(997539,34,47,13,8,'We have no power at all against the truth, but we have power in the service of the truth.'),
(997540,34,47,13,9,'We are glad when we are weak, if you are strong. And what we pray for is that you may become perfect.'),
(997541,34,47,13,10,'This is my reason for writing as I am now doing, while I am away from you, so that, when I am with you, I may not act harshly in the exercise of the authority which the Lord gave me – and gave me for building up and not for pulling down.'),
(997542,34,47,13,11,'And now, friends, goodbye. Aim at perfection; take courage; agree together; live in peace. And then God, the source of all love and peace, will be with you.'),
(997543,34,47,13,12,'Greet one another with a sacred kiss.'),
(997544,34,47,13,13,'All Christ’s people here send you their greetings.'),
(997545,34,47,13,14,'May the blessing of the Lord Jesus Christ, and the love of God, and the communion with the Holy Spirit, be with you all.'),
(997546,34,48,1,1,'To the churches in Galatia, from Paul, an apostle whose commission is not from any human authority and is given, not by human beings, but by Jesus Christ and God the Father who raised him from the dead;'),
(997547,34,48,1,2,'and from all the followers of the Lord here.'),
(997548,34,48,1,3,'May God, our Father, and the Lord Jesus Christ, bless you and give you peace. For Christ, to rescue us from this present wicked age,'),
(997549,34,48,1,4,'gave himself for our sins, in accordance with the will of God and Father,'),
(997550,34,48,1,5,'to whom be ascribed all glory for ever and ever. Amen.'),
(997551,34,48,1,6,'I am astonished at your so soon deserting him, who called you through the love of Christ, for a different “good news,”'),
(997552,34,48,1,7,'which is really no good news at all. But then, I know that there are people who are harassing you, and who want to pervert the good news of the Christ.'),
(997553,34,48,1,8,'Yet even if we – or if an angel from heaven were to tell you any other “good news” than that which we told you, may he be accursed!'),
(997554,34,48,1,9,'We have said it before, and I repeat it now – If anyone tells you a “good news” other than that which you received, may he be accursed!'),
(997555,34,48,1,10,'Is this, I ask, trying to conciliate people, or God? Am I seeking to please people? If I were still trying to please people, I should not be a servant of Christ.'),
(997556,34,48,1,11,'I remind you, friends, that the good news which I told is no mere human invention.'),
(997557,34,48,1,12,'I, at least, did not receive it from any human being, nor was I taught it, but it came to me through a revelation made by Jesus Christ.'),
(997558,34,48,1,13,'You heard, no doubt, of my conduct when I was devoted to Judaism – how I persecuted the church of God to an extent beyond belief, and made havoc of it,'),
(997559,34,48,1,14,'and how, in my devotion to Judaism, I surpassed many of my contemporaries among my own people in my intense earnestness in upholding the traditions of my ancestors.'),
(997560,34,48,1,15,'But when God, who had set me apart even before my birth, and who called me by his love,'),
(997561,34,48,1,16,'saw fit to reveal his Son in me, so that I might tell the good news of him among the Gentiles, then at once, instead of consulting any human being,'),
(997562,34,48,1,17,'or even going up to Jerusalem to see those who were apostles before me, I went to Arabia, and came back again to Damascus.'),
(997563,34,48,1,18,'Three years afterwards I went up to Jerusalem to make the acquaintance of Peter, and I stayed a fortnight with him.'),
(997564,34,48,1,19,'I did not, however, see any other apostle, except James, the Master’s brother.'),
(997565,34,48,1,20,'(As to what I am now writing to you, I call God to witness that I am speaking the truth).'),
(997566,34,48,1,21,'Afterwards I went to the districts of Syria and Cilicia.'),
(997567,34,48,1,22,'But I was still unknown even by sight to the Christian churches in Judea;'),
(997568,34,48,1,23,'all that they had heard was – “The man who once persecuted us is now telling the good news of the faith of which he once made havoc.”'),
(997569,34,48,1,24,'And they praised God for my sake.'),
(997570,34,48,2,1,'Fourteen years afterwards I went up to Jerusalem again with Barnabas, and I took Titus also with me.'),
(997571,34,48,2,2,'It was in obedience to a revelation that I went; and I laid before the apostles the good news that I am proclaiming among the Gentiles. I did this privately before those who are thought highly of because I was afraid that I might possibly be taking, or might have already taken, a course which would prove useless.'),
(997572,34,48,2,3,'Yet even my companion, Titus, though a Greek, was not compelled to be circumcised.'),
(997573,34,48,2,4,'But, because of those who pretended to be followers who had stolen in, the intruders who had crept in to spy on the liberty which we have through union with Christ Jesus, in order to bring us back to slavery –'),
(997574,34,48,2,5,'Why, we did not for a moment yield submission to them, so that the truth of the good news might be yours always!'),
(997575,34,48,2,6,'Of those who are thought somewhat highly of – what they once were makes no difference to me; God does not recognise human distinctions – those, I say, who are thought highly of added nothing to my message.'),
(997576,34,48,2,7,'On the contrary, they saw that I had been entrusted with the good news for the Gentiles, just as Peter had been for the Jews.'),
(997577,34,48,2,8,'For he who gave Peter power for his mission to the Jews gave me, also, power to go to the Gentiles.'),
(997578,34,48,2,9,'Recognising the charge entrusted to me, James, Peter, and John, who were regarded as pillars of the church, openly acknowledged Barnabas and me as fellow workers, agreeing that we should go to the Gentiles, and they to the Jews.'),
(997579,34,48,2,10,'Only we were to remember the poor – the thing I was myself anxious to do.'),
(997580,34,48,2,11,'But, when Peter came to Antioch, I opposed him to his face; for he stood self-condemned.'),
(997581,34,48,2,12,'Before certain persons came from James, he had been in the habit of eating with the Gentile converts; but, when they came, he began to withdraw and hold aloof, because he was afraid of offending those who still held to circumcision.'),
(997582,34,48,2,13,'The rest of the Jewish converts were guilty of the same hypocrisy, so that even Barnabas was led away by it.'),
(997583,34,48,2,14,'But, when I saw that they were not dealing straightforwardly with the truth of the good news, I said to Peter, before them all, ‘If you, who were born a Jew, adopt Gentile customs, instead of Jewish, why are you trying to compel the Gentile converts to adopt Jewish customs?’'),
(997584,34,48,2,15,'We, though we are Jews by birth and not outcasts of Gentile origin, know that no one is pronounced righteous as the result of obedience to Law, but only through faith in Christ Jesus.'),
(997585,34,48,2,16,'So we placed our faith in Christ Jesus, in order that we might be pronounced righteous, as the result of faith in Christ, and not of obedience to Law; for such obedience will not result in even one soul’s being pronounced righteous.'),
(997586,34,48,2,17,'If, while seeking to be pronounced righteous through union with Christ, we were ourselves seen to be outcasts, would that make Christ an agent of sin? Heaven forbid!'),
(997587,34,48,2,18,'For, if I rebuild the things that I pulled down, I prove myself to have done wrong.'),
(997588,34,48,2,19,'I, indeed, through Law became dead to Law, in order to live for God.'),
(997589,34,48,2,20,'I have been crucified with Christ. So it is no longer I that live, but it is Christ who lives in me; and, as for my present earthly life, I am living it by faith in the Son of God, who loved me and gave himself for me.'),
(997590,34,48,2,21,'I do not reject the love of God. If righteousness comes through Law, then there was no need for Christ to die!'),
(997591,34,48,3,1,'Foolish Galatians! Who has been fascinating you – you before whose eyes Jesus Christ was depicted on the cross?'),
(997592,34,48,3,2,'Here is the one thing that I want to find out from you – Did you receive the Spirit as the result of obedience to Law, or of your having listened with faith?'),
(997593,34,48,3,3,'Can you be so foolish? After beginning with what is spiritual, do you now end with what is external?'),
(997594,34,48,3,4,'Did you go through so much to no purpose? – if indeed it really was to no purpose!'),
(997595,34,48,3,5,'He who supplies you abundantly with his Spirit and endows you with such powers – does he do this as the result of obedience to Law? Or as the result of your having listened with faith?'),
(997596,34,48,3,6,'It is just as it was with Abraham –'),
(997597,34,48,3,7,'You see, then, that those whose lives are based on faith are the sons of Abraham.'),
(997598,34,48,3,8,'And scripture, foreseeing that God would pronounce the Gentiles righteous as the result of faith, foretold the good news to Abraham in the words –'),
(997599,34,48,3,9,'And, therefore, those whose lives are based on faith share the blessings bestowed on the faith of Abraham.'),
(997600,34,48,3,10,'All who rely on obedience to Law are under a curse, for scripture says –'),
(997601,34,48,3,11,'Again, it is evident that no one is pronounced righteous before God through Law, for we read –'),
(997602,34,48,3,12,'But the Law is not based on faith; no, its words are –'),
(997603,34,48,3,13,'Christ ransomed us from the curse pronounced in the Law, by taking the curse on himself for us, for scripture says –'),
(997604,34,48,3,14,'And this he did that the blessing given to Abraham might be extended to the Gentiles through their union with Jesus Christ; that so, through our faith, we also might receive the promised gift of the Spirit.'),
(997605,34,48,3,15,'To take an illustration, friends, from daily life – No one sets aside even an agreement between two people, when once it has been confirmed, nor do they add conditions to it.'),
(997606,34,48,3,16,'Now it was to Abraham that the promises were made, “and to his offspring.” It was not said “to his offsprings,” as if many persons were meant, but the words were “to your offspring,” showing that one person was meant – and that was Christ.'),
(997607,34,48,3,17,'My point is this – An agreement already confirmed by God cannot be canceled by the Law, which came four hundred and thirty years later, so as to cause the promise to be set aside.'),
(997608,34,48,3,18,'If our heritage is the result of Law, then it has ceased to be the result of a promise. Yet God conferred it on Abraham by a promise.'),
(997609,34,48,3,19,'What, then, you ask, was the use of the Law? It was a later addition, to make people conscious of their wrong-doings, and intended to last only until the coming of that offspring to whom the promise had been made; and it was delivered through angels by a mediator.'),
(997610,34,48,3,20,'Now mediation implies more than one person, but God is one only.'),
(997611,34,48,3,21,'Does that set the Law in opposition to God’s promises? Heaven forbid! For, if a Law had been given capable of bestowing life, then righteousness would have actually owed its existence to Law.'),
(997612,34,48,3,22,'But the words of scripture represent the whole world as being in bondage to sin, so that the promised blessing, dependent, as it is, on faith in Jesus Christ, may be given to those who have faith in him.'),
(997613,34,48,3,23,'Before the coming of faith, we were kept under the guard of the Law, in bondage, awaiting the faith that was destined to be revealed.'),
(997614,34,48,3,24,'Thus the Law has proved a guide to lead us to Christ, in order that we may be pronounced righteous as the result of faith.'),
(997615,34,48,3,25,'But now that faith has come we no longer need a guide.'),
(997616,34,48,3,26,'For you are all sons of God, through your faith in Christ Jesus.'),
(997617,34,48,3,27,'For all of you who were baptized into union with Christ clothed yourselves with Christ.'),
(997618,34,48,3,28,'All distinctions between Jew and Greek, slave and free, male and female, have vanished; for in union with Christ Jesus you are all one.'),
(997619,34,48,3,29,'And, since you belong to Christ, it follows that you are Abraham’s offspring and, under the promise, sharers in the inheritance.'),
(997620,34,48,4,1,'My point is this – As long as the heir is under age, there is no difference between him and a slave, though he is master of the whole estate.'),
(997621,34,48,4,2,'He is subject to the control of guardians and stewards, during the period for which his father has power to appoint them.'),
(997622,34,48,4,3,'And so is it with us; when we were under age, as it were, we were slaves to the puerile teaching of this world;'),
(997623,34,48,4,4,'but, when the full time came, God sent his Son – born a woman’s child, born subject to Law –'),
(997624,34,48,4,5,'To ransom those who were subject to Law, so that we might take our position as sons.'),
(997625,34,48,4,6,'And it is because you are sons that God sent into our hearts the Spirit of his Son, with the cry – “Abba, our Father.”'),
(997626,34,48,4,7,'You, therefore, are no longer a slave, but a son; and, if a son, then an heir also, by God’s appointment.'),
(997627,34,48,4,8,'Yet formerly, in your ignorance of God, you became slaves to “gods” which were no gods.'),
(997628,34,48,4,9,'But now that you have found God – or, rather, have been found by him – how is it that you are turning back to that poor and feeble puerile teaching, to which yet once again you are wanting to become slaves?'),
(997629,34,48,4,10,'You are scrupulous in keeping days and months and seasons and years!'),
(997630,34,48,4,11,'You make me fear that the labour which I have spent on you may have been wasted.'),
(997631,34,48,4,12,'I entreat you, friends, to become like me, as I became like you. You have never done me any wrong.'),
(997632,34,48,4,13,'You remember that it was owing to bodily infirmity that on the first occasion I told you the good news.'),
(997633,34,48,4,14,'And as for what must have tried you in my condition, it did not inspire you with scorn or disgust, but you welcomed me as if I had been an angel of God – or Christ Jesus himself!'),
(997634,34,48,4,15,'What has become then, of your blessings? For I can bear witness that, had it been possible, you would have torn out your eyes and given them to me!'),
(997635,34,48,4,16,'Am I to think, then, that I have become your enemy by telling you the truth?'),
(997636,34,48,4,17,'Certain people are seeking your favour, but with no honourable object. No, indeed, they want to isolate you, so that you will have to seek their favour.'),
(997637,34,48,4,18,'It is always honourable to have your favour sought in an honourable cause, and not only when I am with you, my dear children –'),
(997638,34,48,4,19,'you for whom I am again enduring a mother’s pains, until a likeness to Christ will have been formed in you.'),
(997639,34,48,4,20,'But I could wish to be with you now and speak in a different tone, for I am perplexed about you.'),
(997640,34,48,4,21,'Tell me, you who want to be still subject to Law – Why don’t you listen to the Law?'),
(997641,34,48,4,22,'Scripture says that Abraham had two sons, one the child of the slave-woman and the other the child of the free woman.'),
(997642,34,48,4,23,'But the child of the slave-woman was born in the course of nature, while the child of the free woman was born in fulfilment of a promise.'),
(997643,34,48,4,24,'This story may be taken as an allegory. The women stand for two Covenants. One covenant, given from Mount Sinai, produces a race of slaves and is represented by Hagar'),
(997644,34,48,4,25,'(The word Hagar meaning in Arabia Mount Sinai) and it ranks with the Jerusalem of today, for she and her children are in slavery.'),
(997645,34,48,4,26,'But the Jerusalem above is free, and she it is who is our mother.'),
(997646,34,48,4,27,'For scripture says –'),
(997647,34,48,4,28,'As for ourselves, friends, we, like Isaac, are children born in fulfilment of a promise.'),
(997648,34,48,4,29,'Yet at that time the child born in the course of nature persecuted the child born by the power of the Spirit; and it is the same now.'),
(997649,34,48,4,30,'But what does the passage of scripture say?'),
(997650,34,48,4,31,'And so, friends, we are not children of a slave, but of her who is free.'),
(997651,34,48,5,1,'It is for freedom that Christ set us free; stand firm therefore, and do not again be held under the yoke of slavery.'),
(997652,34,48,5,2,'Understand that I, Paul, myself tell you that if you allow yourselves to be circumcised, Christ will avail you nothing.'),
(997653,34,48,5,3,'I again declare to everyone who receives circumcision, that he binds himself to obey the whole Law.'),
(997654,34,48,5,4,'You have severed yourselves from Christ – you who are seeking to be pronounced righteous through Law; you have fallen away from love.'),
(997655,34,48,5,5,'For we, by the help of the Spirit, are eagerly waiting for the fulfilment of our hope – that we may be pronounced righteous as the result of faith.'),
(997656,34,48,5,6,'If we are in union with Christ Jesus, neither is circumcision nor the omission of it anything, but faith, working through love, is everything.'),
(997657,34,48,5,7,'You were once making good progress! Who has hindered you from obeying the truth?'),
(997658,34,48,5,8,'The persuasion brought to bear on you does not come from him who calls you.'),
(997659,34,48,5,9,'A little leaven leavens all the dough.'),
(997660,34,48,5,10,'I, through my union with the Lord, am persuaded that you will learn to think with me. But the man who is disturbing your minds will have to bear his punishment, whoever he may be.'),
(997661,34,48,5,11,'If I, friends, am still proclaiming circumcision, why am I still persecuted? It seems that the cross has ceased to be an obstacle!'),
(997662,34,48,5,12,'I could even wish that the people who are unsettling you would go further still and mutilate themselves.'),
(997663,34,48,5,13,'Remember, friends, to you the call came to give you freedom. Only do not make your freedom an opportunity for self-indulgence, but serve one another in a loving spirit.'),
(997664,34,48,5,14,'Indeed, the whole Law has been summed up in this one precept –'),
(997665,34,48,5,15,'But, if you are continually wounding and preying on one another, take care that you are not destroyed by one another.'),
(997666,34,48,5,16,'This is what I have to say – Let your steps be guided by the Spirit, and then you will never gratify the cravings of your earthly nature.'),
(997667,34,48,5,17,'For these cravings of our earthly nature conflict with the Spirit, and the Spirit with our earthly nature – they are two contrary principles – so that you cannot do what you wish.'),
(997668,34,48,5,18,'But, if you follow the guidance of the Spirit, you are not subject to Law.'),
(997669,34,48,5,19,'The sins of our earthly nature are unmistakable. They are sins like these – sexual immorality, impurity, indecency,'),
(997670,34,48,5,20,'idolatry, sorcery, quarrels, strife, jealousy, outbursts of passion, rivalries, dissensions, divisions,'),
(997671,34,48,5,21,'feelings of envy, drunkenness, revelry, and the like. And I warn you, as I warned you before, that those who indulge in such things will have no place in the kingdom of God.'),
(997672,34,48,5,22,'But the fruit produced by the Spirit is love, joy, peace, forbearance, kindliness, generosity, trustfulness, gentleness, self-control.'),
(997673,34,48,5,23,'Against such things there is no law!'),
(997674,34,48,5,24,'And those who belong to Jesus, the Christ, have already crucified their earthly nature, with its passions and its cravings.'),
(997675,34,48,5,25,'Since our life is due to the Spirit, let us rule our conduct also by the Spirit.'),
(997676,34,48,5,26,'Do not let us grow vain, and provoke or envy one another.'),
(997677,34,48,6,1,'My friends, even if someone should be caught committing a sin, you who are spiritually minded should, in a gentle spirit, help them to recover themselves, taking care that you yourselves are not tempted.'),
(997678,34,48,6,2,'Bear one another’s burdens, and so carry out the Law of the Christ.'),
(997679,34,48,6,3,'If a person imagines themselves to be somebody, when they are really nobody, they deceive themselves.'),
(997680,34,48,6,4,'Let everyone test their own work, and then their cause for satisfaction will be in themselves and not in a comparison with their neighbour;'),
(997681,34,48,6,5,'for everyone must bear their own load.'),
(997682,34,48,6,6,'The person, however, who is being instructed in the message ought always to share their blessings with their teacher.'),
(997683,34,48,6,7,'Do not be deceived. God cannot be mocked. What a person sows that they will reap.'),
(997684,34,48,6,8,'For the person who sows the field of their earthly nature will from that earthly nature reap corruption; while the one who sows the field of the spirit will from that spirit reap eternal life.'),
(997685,34,48,6,9,'Let us never tire of doing right, for at the proper season we will reap our harvest, if we do not grow weary.'),
(997686,34,48,6,10,'Therefore, I say, as the opportunity occurs, let us treat everyone with kindness, and especially members of the Household of the faith.'),
(997687,34,48,6,11,'See in what large letters I am writing with my own hand.'),
(997688,34,48,6,12,'Those who wish to appear to advantage in regard to outward observances are the people who are trying to compel you to be circumcised; and they do it only to avoid being persecuted for the cross of Jesus, the Christ.'),
(997689,34,48,6,13,'Even these men who are circumcised do not themselves keep the Law; yet they want you to be circumcised, so that they may boast of your observance of the rite.'),
(997690,34,48,6,14,'But, for my part, may I never boast of anything except the cross of Jesus Christ, our Master, through whom the world has been crucified to me, and I to the world.'),
(997691,34,48,6,15,'For neither is circumcision nor the omission of it anything; but a new nature is everything.'),
(997692,34,48,6,16,'May all who rule their conduct by this principle find peace and mercy – they who are the Israel of God.'),
(997693,34,48,6,17,'For the future let no one trouble me; for I bear the marks of Jesus branded on my body.'),
(997694,34,48,6,18,'May the blessing of Jesus Christ, our Lord, rest on your souls, friends. Amen.'),
(997695,34,49,1,1,'To Christ’s people at Ephesus who are faithful to him, from Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus, by the will of God.'),
(997696,34,49,1,2,'May God, our Father, and the Lord Jesus Christ bless you and give you peace.'),
(997697,34,49,1,3,'Blessed is the God and Father of Jesus Christ, our Lord, who has blessed us on high with every spiritual blessing, in Christ.'),
(997698,34,49,1,4,'For he chose us in our union with Christ before the creation of the universe, so that we might be holy and blameless in his sight, living in the spirit of love.'),
(997699,34,49,1,5,'From the first he destined us, in his goodwill towards us, to be adopted as sons through Jesus Christ,'),
(997700,34,49,1,6,'and so to enhance that glorious manifestation of his loving kindness which he gave us in the one he loves;'),
(997701,34,49,1,7,'for in him, and through the shedding of his blood, we have found redemption in the pardon of our offences.'),
(997702,34,49,1,8,'All this accords with the loving kindness which God lavished on us, accompanied by countless gifts of wisdom and discernment,'),
(997703,34,49,1,9,'when he made known to us his hidden purpose. And it also accords with the goodwill which God purposed to exhibit in Christ,'),
(997704,34,49,1,10,'in view of that divine order which was to mark the completion of the ages, when he should make everything, both in heaven and on earth, centre in him.'),
(997705,34,49,1,11,'In him, I say, for by our union with him we became God’s heritage, having from the first been destined for this in the intention of him who, in all that happens, is carrying out his own fixed purpose;'),
(997706,34,49,1,12,'that we should enhance his glory – we who have been the first to rest our hopes on the Christ.'),
(997707,34,49,1,13,'And you, too, by your union with him, after you had heard the message of the truth, the good news of your salvation – you believed in him and were sealed as his by receiving the holy Spirit, which he had promised.'),
(997708,34,49,1,14,'And the Spirit is a pledge of our future heritage, foreshadowing the full redemption of God’s own people – to enhance his glory.'),
(997709,34,49,1,15,'And therefore I, ever since I heard of the faith in the Lord Jesus which prevails among you, and of your confidence in all Christ’s people,'),
(997710,34,49,1,16,'have never omitted to thank God on your behalf, whenever I make mention of you in my prayers.'),
(997711,34,49,1,17,'My prayer is that the God of Jesus Christ our Lord, the all-glorious Father, may inspire you with wisdom and true insight through a fuller knowledge of himself;'),
(997712,34,49,1,18,'that your minds may be so enlightened that you may realise the hope given by God’s call, the wealth of the glory of his heritage among Christ’s people,'),
(997713,34,49,1,19,'and the transcendent greatness of the power which he is able to exercise in dealing with us who believe in him.'),
(997714,34,49,1,20,'The same mighty power was exerted on the Christ, when he raised the Christ from the dead and “caused him to sit at his right hand” on high, exalting him above all angels and archangels of every rank,'),
(997715,34,49,1,21,'and above every name that can be named, whether in the present age, or in the age to come.'),
(997716,34,49,1,22,'And God placed all things under Christ’s feet, and gave him to the church as its supreme head;'),
(997717,34,49,1,23,'for the church is Christ’s body, and is filled by him who fills all things everywhere with his presence.'),
(997718,34,49,2,1,'You yourselves were once dead because of your offences and sins.'),
(997719,34,49,2,2,'For at one time you lived in sin, following the ways of the world, in subjection to the Ruler of the powers of the air – the Spirit who is still at work among the disobedient.'),
(997720,34,49,2,3,'And it was among them that we all once lived our lives, indulging the cravings of our earthly nature, and carrying out the desires prompted by that earthly nature and by our own thoughts. Our nature exposed us to the divine wrath, like the rest of humanity.'),
(997721,34,49,2,4,'Yet God, in his abundant compassion, and because of the great love with which he loved us,'),
(997722,34,49,2,5,'even though we were dead because of our offences, gave life to us in giving life to the Christ. (By God’s loving kindness you have been saved.)'),
(997723,34,49,2,6,'And, through our union with Christ Jesus, God raised us with him, and caused us to sit with him on high,'),
(997724,34,49,2,7,'in order that, by his goodness to us in Christ Jesus, he might display in the ages to come the boundless wealth of his loving kindness.'),
(997725,34,49,2,8,'For it is by God’s loving kindness that you have been saved, through your faith. It is not due to yourselves; the gift is God’s.'),
(997726,34,49,2,9,'It is not due to obedience to Law, so that no one can boast.'),
(997727,34,49,2,10,'For we are God’s handiwork, created, by our union with Christ Jesus, for the good actions in doing which God had pre-arranged that we should spend our lives.'),
(997728,34,49,2,11,'Remember, therefore, that you were once Gentiles yourselves, as your bodies showed; you were called “the Uncircumcised” by those who were called “the Circumcised” – circumcised only by human hands!'),
(997729,34,49,2,12,'Remember that you were at that time far from Christ; you were shut out from the citizenship of Israel; you were strangers to the Covenants founded on God’s Promise; you were in the world without hope and without God.'),
(997730,34,49,2,13,'But now, through your union with Christ Jesus, you who once were far off have, by the shedding of the blood of the Christ, been brought near.'),
(997731,34,49,2,14,'He it is who is our peace. He made the two divisions of humanity one, broke down the barrier that separated them,'),
(997732,34,49,2,15,'and in his human nature put an end to the cause of enmity between them – the Law with its injunctions and ordinances – in order to create, through union with himself, from Jew and Gentile, one new humanity and so make peace.'),
(997733,34,49,2,16,'And when, on the cross, he had destroyed their mutual enmity, he sought by means of his cross to reconcile them both to God, united in one body.'),
(997734,34,49,2,17,'He came with the good news of peace for you who were far off, and of peace for those who were near;'),
(997735,34,49,2,18,'for it is through him that we, the Jews and the Gentiles, united in the one Spirit, are now able to approach the Father.'),
(997736,34,49,2,19,'It follows, then, that you are no longer strangers and aliens, but are fellow citizens with Christ’s people and members of God’s Household.'),
(997737,34,49,2,20,'You have been built up on the foundation laid by the apostles and prophets, Christ Jesus himself being the corner-stone.'),
(997738,34,49,2,21,'United in him, every part of the building, closely joined together, will grow into a Temple, consecrated by its union with the Lord.'),
(997739,34,49,2,22,'And, through union in him, you also are being built up together, to be a place where God lives through the Spirit.'),
(997740,34,49,3,1,'For this reason I, Paul, the prisoner of Jesus, the Christ, for the sake of you Gentiles –'),
(997741,34,49,3,2,'For you have heard, I suppose, of the responsible charge with which God entrusted me for your benefit,'),
(997742,34,49,3,3,'and also that it was by direct revelation that the hidden purpose of God was made known to me, as I have already briefly told you.'),
(997743,34,49,3,4,'And, by reading what I have written, you will be able to judge how far I understand this hidden purpose of God in Christ.'),
(997744,34,49,3,5,'In former generations it was not made known to humanity, as fully as it has now been revealed by the Spirit to the apostles and prophets among Christ’s people –'),
(997745,34,49,3,6,'That, by union with Christ Jesus and through the good news, the Gentiles are coheirs with us and members of one body, and that they share with us in God’s Promise.'),
(997746,34,49,3,7,'Of this good news I become an assistant, in virtue of the charge with which God entrusted me in the exercise of his power –'),
(997747,34,49,3,8,'Yes, to me, who am less than the least of all Christ’s people, was this charge entrusted! – to tell the Gentiles the good news of the boundless wealth to be found in the Christ,'),
(997748,34,49,3,9,'and to make clear what is God’s way of working out that hidden purpose which from the first has been concealed in the mind of the Creator of all things;'),
(997749,34,49,3,10,'so that now to the archangels and to all the powers on high should be made known, through the church, the all-embracing wisdom of God,'),
(997750,34,49,3,11,'in accordance with that purpose which runs through all the ages and which he has now accomplished in Jesus, the Christ, our Master.'),
(997751,34,49,3,12,'And in union with him, and through our trust in him, we find courage to approach God with confidence.'),
(997752,34,49,3,13,'Therefore I beg you not to be disheartened at the sufferings that I am undergoing for your sakes; for they redound to your honour.'),
(997753,34,49,3,14,'For this reason, then, I kneel before the Father –'),
(997754,34,49,3,15,'from whom all “fatherhood” in heaven and on earth derives its name –'),
(997755,34,49,3,16,'And pray that, in proportion to the wealth of his glory, he will strengthen you with his power by breathing his Spirit into your inmost soul,'),
(997756,34,49,3,17,'so that the Christ, through your faith, may make his home within your hearts in love; And I pray that you, now firmly rooted and established, may, with all Christ’s people,'),
(997757,34,49,3,18,'have the power to comprehend in all its width and length and height and depth,'),
(997758,34,49,3,19,'and to understand – though it surpasses all understanding – the love of the Christ; and so be filled to the full with God himself.'),
(997759,34,49,3,20,'To him who, through his power which is at work within us, is able to do far more than anything that we can ask or conceive –'),
(997760,34,49,3,21,'To him be all glory through the church and through Christ Jesus, for all generations, age after age. Amen.'),
(997761,34,49,4,1,'I beg you, then – I who am a prisoner in the Master’s cause – to live lives worthy of the call that you have received;'),
(997762,34,49,4,2,'always humble and gentle, patient, bearing lovingly with one another,'),
(997763,34,49,4,3,'and striving to maintain in the bond of peace the unity given by the Spirit.'),
(997764,34,49,4,4,'There is but one body and one Spirit, just as there was but one hope set before you when you received your call.'),
(997765,34,49,4,5,'There is but one Lord, one faith, one baptism.'),
(997766,34,49,4,6,'There is but one God and Father of all – the God who is over all, pervades all, and is in all.'),
(997767,34,49,4,7,'Everyone of us, however, has been entrusted with some charge, each in accordance with the extent of the gift of the Christ.'),
(997768,34,49,4,8,'That is why it is said –'),
(997769,34,49,4,9,'Now surely this “going up” must imply that he had already gone down into the world beneath.'),
(997770,34,49,4,10,'He who went down is the same as he who went up – up beyond the highest heaven, so that he might fill all things with his presence.'),
(997771,34,49,4,11,'And he it is who gave to the church apostles, prophets, missionaries, pastors, and teachers,'),
(997772,34,49,4,12,'to fit his people for the work of the ministry, for the building up of the body of the Christ.'),
(997773,34,49,4,13,'And this will continue, until we all attain to that unity which is given by faith and by a fuller knowledge of the Son of God; until we reach maturity – the full standard of the perfection of the Christ.'),
(997774,34,49,4,14,'Then we will no longer be like infants, tossed backward and forward, blown about by every breath of human teaching and by people’s trickery and craftiness;'),
(997775,34,49,4,15,'but holding the truth in a spirit of love, we will grow into complete union with him who is our head – Christ himself.'),
(997776,34,49,4,16,'For from him the whole body, closely joined and knit together by the contact of every part with the source of its life, derives its power to grow, in proportion to the vigour of each individual part; and so is being built up in a spirit of love.'),
(997777,34,49,4,17,'This, then, as one in union with the Lord, I implore: Do not continue to live such purposeless lives as the Gentiles live,'),
(997778,34,49,4,18,'with their powers of discernment darkened, cut off from the life of God, owing to the ignorance that prevails among them and to the hardness of their hearts.'),
(997779,34,49,4,19,'Lost to all sense of shame, they have abandoned themselves to licentiousness, in order to practice every kind of impurity without restraint.'),
(997780,34,49,4,20,'But far different is the lesson you learned from the Christ – if, that is, you really listened to him,'),
(997781,34,49,4,21,'and through union with him were taught the truth, as it is to be found in Jesus.'),
(997782,34,49,4,22,'For you learned with regard to your former way of living that you must cast off your old nature, which, yielding to deluding passions, grows corrupt;'),
(997783,34,49,4,23,'that the spirit of your minds must be constantly renewed;'),
(997784,34,49,4,24,'and that you must clothe yourselves in that new nature which was created to resemble God, with the righteousness and holiness springing from the truth.'),
(997785,34,49,4,25,'Since, therefore, you have cast off what is false, you must every one of you speak the truth to your neighbours. For we are united to one another like the parts of a body.'),
(997786,34,49,4,26,'Be angry, yet do not sin. Do not let the sun go down on your anger;'),
(997787,34,49,4,27,'and give no opportunity to the devil.'),
(997788,34,49,4,28,'Let the person who steals steal no longer, but rather they should toil with their hands at honest work, so that they may have something to share with anyone in need.'),
(997789,34,49,4,29,'Never let any foul word pass your lips, but only such good words as the occasion demands, so that they may be a help to those who hear them.'),
(997790,34,49,4,30,'And do not grieve God’s Holy Spirit; for it was through that Spirit that God sealed you as his, against the day of redemption.'),
(997791,34,49,4,31,'Let all bitterness, passion, anger, brawling, and abusive language be banished from among you, as well as all malice.'),
(997792,34,49,4,32,'Be kind to one another, tenderhearted, ready to forgive one another, just as God, in Christ, forgave you.'),
(997793,34,49,5,1,'Therefore imitate God, as his dear children,'),
(997794,34,49,5,2,'and live a life of love, following the example of the Christ, who loved you and gave himself for you as an offering and a sacrifice to God, that should be fragrant and acceptable.'),
(997795,34,49,5,3,'As for sexual immorality and every kind of impurity, or greed, do not let them even be mentioned among you, as befits Christ’s people,'),
(997796,34,49,5,4,'nor shameful conduct, nor foolish talk or jesting, for they are wholly out of place among you; but rather thanksgiving.'),
(997797,34,49,5,5,'For of this you may be sure – that no one who is unchaste or impure or greedy of gain (for to be greedy of gain is idolatry) has any place awaiting him in the kingdom of the Christ and God.'),
(997798,34,49,5,6,'Do not let anyone deceive you with specious arguments. Those are the sins that bring down the wrath of God on the disobedient.'),
(997799,34,49,5,7,'Therefore have nothing to do with such people.'),
(997800,34,49,5,8,'For, although you were once in darkness, now, by your union with the Lord, you are in the light. Live as children of light –'),
(997801,34,49,5,9,'for the outcome of life in the light may be seen in every form of goodness, righteousness, and sincerity –'),
(997802,34,49,5,10,'always trying to find out what is pleasing to the Lord.'),
(997803,34,49,5,11,'Take no part in deeds of darkness, from which no good can come; on the contrary, expose them.'),
(997804,34,49,5,12,'It is degrading even to speak of the things continually done by them in secret.'),
(997805,34,49,5,13,'All such actions, when exposed, have their true character made manifest by the light.'),
(997806,34,49,5,14,'For everything that has its true character made manifest is clear as light. And that is why it is said –'),
(997807,34,49,5,15,'Take great care, then, how you live – not unwisely but wisely,'),
(997808,34,49,5,16,'making the most of every opportunity; for these are evil days.'),
(997809,34,49,5,17,'Therefore do not grow thoughtless, but try to understand what the Lord’s will is.'),
(997810,34,49,5,18,'Do not drink wine to excess, for that leads to profligacy; but seek to be filled with the Spirit of God, and speak to one another in psalms and hymns and sacred songs.'),
(997811,34,49,5,19,'Sing and make music in your hearts to the Lord.'),
(997812,34,49,5,20,'Always give thanks for everything to our God and Father, in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ.'),
(997813,34,49,5,21,'Submit to one another because you honour and respect Christ.'),
(997814,34,49,5,22,'Wives should submit to their husbands as submitting to the Lord.'),
(997815,34,49,5,23,'For a man is the head of his wife, as the Christ is the head of the church – being indeed himself the Saviour of his body.'),
(997816,34,49,5,24,'But as the church submits to the Christ, so also should wives submit to their husbands in everything.'),
(997817,34,49,5,25,'Husbands, love your wives, just as the Christ loved the church, and gave himself for her,'),
(997818,34,49,5,26,'to make her holy, after purifying her by the washing with the water, according to his promise;'),
(997819,34,49,5,27,'so that he might himself bring the church, in all her beauty, into his own presence, with no spot or wrinkle or blemish of any kind, but that she might be holy and faultless.'),
(997820,34,49,5,28,'That is how husbands ought to love their wives – as if they were their own bodies. A man who loves his wife is really loving himself;'),
(997821,34,49,5,29,'for no one ever yet hated his own body. But everyone feeds his body and cares for it, just as the Christ for the church;'),
(997822,34,49,5,30,'for we are members of his body.'),
(997823,34,49,5,31,'For this cause a man will leave his father and mother, and be united to his wife; and the man and his wife will become one.'),
(997824,34,49,5,32,'In this there is a profound truth – I am speaking of Christ and his church.'),
(997825,34,49,5,33,'However, for you individually, let each love his wife as if she were himself; and the wife be careful to respect her husband.'),
(997826,34,49,6,1,'Children, obey your parents, as children of the Lord; for that is but right.'),
(997827,34,49,6,2,'“Honour your father and mother” – this is the first Commandment with a promise –'),
(997828,34,49,6,3,'“so that you may prosper and have a long life on earth.”'),
(997829,34,49,6,4,'And fathers, do not irritate your children, but bring them up with Christian discipline and instruction.'),
(997830,34,49,6,5,'Slaves, obey your earthly masters, with anxious care, giving them ungrudging service, as if obeying the Christ;'),
(997831,34,49,6,6,'not only when their eyes are on you, as if you had merely to please people, but as slaves of Christ, who are trying to carry out the will of God.'),
(997832,34,49,6,7,'Give your service heartily and cheerfully, as working for the Master and not for people;'),
(997833,34,49,6,8,'for you know that everyone will be rewarded by the Master for any honest work that he has done, whether he is a slave or free.'),
(997834,34,49,6,9,'And masters, treat your slaves in the same spirit. Give up threatening them; for you know that he who is both their Master and yours is in heaven, and that before him there is no distinction of rank.'),
(997835,34,49,6,10,'For the future, find strength in your union with the Lord, and in the power which comes from his might.'),
(997836,34,49,6,11,'Put on the full armour of God, so that you may be able to stand your ground against the stratagems of the devil.'),
(997837,34,49,6,12,'For ours is no struggle against enemies of flesh and blood, but against all the various powers of evil that hold sway in the darkness around us, against the spirits of wickedness on high.'),
(997838,34,49,6,13,'Therefore take up the full armour of God, so that when the evil day comes, you may be able to withstand the attack, and, having fought to the end, still to stand your ground.'),
(997839,34,49,6,14,'Stand your ground, then, with truth for your belt, and with righteousness for your breast-plate,'),
(997840,34,49,6,15,'and with the readiness to serve the good news of peace as shoes for your feet.'),
(997841,34,49,6,16,'At every onslaught take up faith for your shield; for with it you will be able to extinguish all the flaming darts of the evil one.'),
(997842,34,49,6,17,'And receive the helmet of salvation, and the sword of the Spirit – which is the message of God – always with prayer and supplication.'),
(997843,34,49,6,18,'Pray in spirit at all times. Be intent on this, with unwearying perseverance and supplication for all Christ’s people –'),
(997844,34,49,6,19,'and on my behalf also, so that when I begin to speak, words may be given me, so that I may fearlessly make known the inmost truth of the good news,'),
(997845,34,49,6,20,'on behalf of which I am an ambassador – in chains! Pray that, in telling it, I may speak fearlessly as I ought.'),
(997846,34,49,6,21,'To enable you, as well as others, to know all that concerns me and what I am doing, Tychicus, our dear friend and faithful helper in the Master’s cause, will tell you everything.'),
(997847,34,49,6,22,'I am sending him to you on purpose that you may learn all about us, and that he may cheer your hearts.'),
(997848,34,49,6,23,'May God, the Father, and the Lord Jesus Christ give every follower peace, and love linked with faith.'),
(997849,34,49,6,24,'May God’s blessing be with all who love our Lord Jesus Christ with an undying love.'),
(997850,34,50,1,1,'To all Christ’s people at Philippi, with the supervisors and assistants, from Paul and Timothy, servants of Christ Jesus.'),
(997851,34,50,1,2,'May God, our Father, and the Lord Jesus Christ bless you, and give you peace.'),
(997852,34,50,1,3,'Every recollection that I have of you is a cause of thankfulness to God,'),
(997853,34,50,1,4,'always, in every prayer that I offer for you all – my prayers are full of joy –'),
(997854,34,50,1,5,'Because of the share that you have had in spreading the good news, from the first day that you received it until now.'),
(997855,34,50,1,6,'For of this I am confident, that he who began a good work in you will complete it in readiness for the day of Jesus Christ.'),
(997856,34,50,1,7,'And, indeed, I am justified in feeling like this about you all; because you have a warm place in my heart – you who all, both in my imprisonment and in the work of defending and establishing the good news, shared my privilege with me.'),
(997857,34,50,1,8,'God will bear me witness how I yearn over you all with the tenderness of Christ Jesus.'),
(997858,34,50,1,9,'And what I pray for is this – that your love may grow yet stronger and stronger, with increasing knowledge and all discernment,'),
(997859,34,50,1,10,'until you are able to appreciate all moral distinctions. And I pray, too, that you may be kept pure and blameless against the day of Christ,'),
(997860,34,50,1,11,'bearing a rich harvest of that righteousness which comes through Jesus Christ, to the glory and praise of God.'),
(997861,34,50,1,12,'Friends, I want you to realise that what has happened to me has actually served to forward the good news.'),
(997862,34,50,1,13,'It has even become evident, not only to all the imperial guard, but to everyone else, that it is for Christ’s sake that I am in chains.'),
(997863,34,50,1,14,'And besides this, most of our fellow followers have gained confidence in the Lord through my chains, and now venture with far greater freedom to speak of God’s message fearlessly.'),
(997864,34,50,1,15,'It is true that some do proclaim the Christ out of Jealousy and opposition; but there are others who proclaim him from goodwill.'),
(997865,34,50,1,16,'The latter do it from love for me, knowing that I have been appointed to plead the cause of the good news.'),
(997866,34,50,1,17,'The former spread the news of the Christ in a factious spirit, and not sincerely, thinking to add to the pain of my chains.'),
(997867,34,50,1,18,'But what of that? Only that in some way or other, either with assumed or with real earnestness, Christ is being made known; and at that I rejoice.'),
(997868,34,50,1,19,'Yes, and I will rejoice, for I know that, through your prayers and through a rich supply of the Spirit of Jesus Christ, all this will make for my salvation.'),
(997869,34,50,1,20,'And this will fulfil my earnest expectation and hope that I will have no cause for shame, but that, with unfailing courage, now as hitherto, Christ will be honoured in my body, whether by my life or by my death,'),
(997870,34,50,1,21,'for to me life is Christ, and death is gain.'),
(997871,34,50,1,22,'But what if the life here in the body – if this brings me fruit from my labours? Then which to choose I cannot tell! I am sorely perplexed either way!'),
(997872,34,50,1,23,'My own desire is to depart and be with Christ, for this would be far better.'),
(997873,34,50,1,24,'But, for your sakes, it may be more needful that I should still remain here in the body.'),
(997874,34,50,1,25,'Yes, I am confident that this is so, and therefore I am sure that I will stay, and stay near you all, to promote your progress and joy in the faith;'),
(997875,34,50,1,26,'so that, when you once more have me among you, you, in your union with Christ Jesus, may find in me fresh cause for exultation.'),
(997876,34,50,1,27,'Under all circumstances let your lives be worthy of the good news of the Christ: so that, whether I come and see you, or whether I hear of your affairs at a distance, I may know that you are standing firm, animated by one spirit, and joining with one heart in a common struggle for the faith taught by the good news,'),
(997877,34,50,1,28,'without ever shrinking from your opponents. To them this will be a sign of their destruction and of your salvation – a sign from God.'),
(997878,34,50,1,29,'For, on behalf of Christ, you have had the privilege granted you, not only of trusting in him, but also of suffering on his behalf.'),
(997879,34,50,1,30,'You will be engaged in the same hard struggle as that which you once saw me waging, and which you hear that I am waging still.'),
(997880,34,50,2,1,'If, then, any encouragement comes through union with Christ, if there is any persuasive power in love, if there is any communion with the Spirit, if there is any tenderness or pity,'),
(997881,34,50,2,2,'I entreat you to make my happiness complete – Live together animated by the same spirit and in mutual love, one in heart, animated by one Spirit.'),
(997882,34,50,2,3,'Nothing should be done out of selfish ambition or vain conceit. Rather, in humility lift others up above yourselves,'),
(997883,34,50,2,4,'considering not only your own interests but also the interests of others.'),
(997884,34,50,2,5,'Let the spirit of Christ Jesus be yours also.'),
(997885,34,50,2,6,'Though the divine nature was his from the beginning, yet he did not look on equality with God as above all things to be clung to,'),
(997886,34,50,2,7,'but impoverished himself by taking the nature of a servant and becoming like one of us;'),
(997887,34,50,2,8,'he appeared among us as a man, and still further humbled himself by submitting even to death – to death on a cross!'),
(997888,34,50,2,9,'And that is why God raised him to the very highest place, and gave him the name which stands above all other names,'),
(997889,34,50,2,10,'so that in adoration of the name of Jesus every knee should bend, in heaven, on earth, and under the earth,'),
(997890,34,50,2,11,'and that every tongue should acknowledge JESUS CHRIST as LORD – to the glory of God the Father.'),
(997891,34,50,2,12,'Therefore, my dear friends, as you have always been obedient in the past, so now work out your own salvation with anxious care, not only when I am with you, but all the more now that I am absent.'),
(997892,34,50,2,13,'Remember it is God who, in his kindness, is at work within you, enabling you both to will and to work.'),
(997893,34,50,2,14,'In all that you do, avoid murmuring and dissension,'),
(997894,34,50,2,15,'so as to prove yourselves blameless and innocent – faultless children of God, in the midst of an evil-disposed and perverse generation, in which you are seen shining like stars in a dark world,'),
(997895,34,50,2,16,'offering to them the message of life; and then I will be able at the day of Christ to boast that I did not run my course for nothing, or toil for nothing.'),
(997896,34,50,2,17,'And yet, even if, when your faith is offered as a sacrifice to God, my lifeblood must be poured out in addition, still I will rejoice and share the joy of you all;'),
(997897,34,50,2,18,'and you must also rejoice and share my joy.'),
(997898,34,50,2,19,'I hope, however, as one who trusts in the Lord Jesus, to send Timothy to you before long, so that I may myself be cheered by receiving news of you.'),
(997899,34,50,2,20,'For I have no one but him to send – no one of kindred spirit who would take the same genuine interest in your welfare.'),
(997900,34,50,2,21,'They are all pursuing their own aims and not those of Christ Jesus.'),
(997901,34,50,2,22,'But you know what Timothy has proved himself to be, and how, like a child working for his father, he worked hard with me in spreading the good news.'),
(997902,34,50,2,23,'It is Timothy, then, whom I hope to send, as soon as ever I can foresee how it will go with me.'),
(997903,34,50,2,24,'And I am confident, as one who trusts in the Lord Jesus, that before long I myself will follow.'),
(997904,34,50,2,25,'Still I think it necessary to send Epaphroditus to you now, for he is my dear friend, fellow worker, and fellow soldier, and he was also your messenger to help me in my need.'),
(997905,34,50,2,26,'For he has been longing to see you all, and has been distressed because you heard of his illness.'),
(997906,34,50,2,27,'And I can assure you that his illness very nearly proved fatal. But God had pity on him, and not on him only but also on me, so that I might not have sorrow on sorrow.'),
(997907,34,50,2,28,'I am all the more ready, therefore, to send him, so that the sight of him may revive your spirits and my own sorrow be lightened.'),
(997908,34,50,2,29,'Give him, then, the heartiest of Christian welcomes, and hold such people in great honour.'),
(997909,34,50,2,30,'For it was owing to his devotion to the Master’s work that he was at the point of death, having risked his own life in the effort to supply what was wanting in the help that you sent me.'),
(997910,34,50,3,1,'In conclusion, my friends, all joy be yours in your union with the Lord. To repeat what I have already written does not weary me, and is the safe course for you.'),
(997911,34,50,3,2,'Beware of those dogs! Beware of those mischievous workers! Beware of the men who mutilate themselves!'),
(997912,34,50,3,3,'For it is we who are the circumcised – we whose worship is prompted by the Spirit of God, who exult in Christ Jesus, and who do not rely on external privileges;'),
(997913,34,50,3,4,'though I, if anyone, have cause to rely even on them. If anyone thinks he can rely on external privileges, far more can I!'),
(997914,34,50,3,5,'I was circumcised when eight days old; I am an Israelite by birth, and of the tribe of Benjamin; I am a Hebrew, and the child of Hebrews. As to the Law, I was a Pharisee;'),
(997915,34,50,3,6,'as to zeal, I was a persecutor of the church; as to such righteousness as is due to Law, I proved myself blameless.'),
(997916,34,50,3,7,'But all the things which I once held to be gains I have now, for the Christ’s sake, come to count as loss.'),
(997917,34,50,3,8,'More than that, I count everything as loss, for the sake of the exceeding value of the knowledge of Christ Jesus my Lord. And for his sake I have lost everything, and count it as refuse, if I may but gain Christ and be found in union with him;'),
(997918,34,50,3,9,'any righteousness that I have being, not the righteousness that results from Law, but the righteousness which comes through faith in Christ – the righteousness which is derived from God and is founded on faith.'),
(997919,34,50,3,10,'Then indeed I will know Christ, and the power of his resurrection, and all that it means to share his sufferings,'),
(997920,34,50,3,11,'in the hope that, if I become like him in death, I may possibly attain to the resurrection from the dead.'),
(997921,34,50,3,12,'Not that I have already laid hold of it, or that I am already made perfect. But I press on, in the hope of actually laying hold of that for which indeed I was laid hold of by Christ Jesus.'),
(997922,34,50,3,13,'For I, friends, do not regard myself as having yet laid hold of it. But this one thing I do – forgetting what lies behind, and straining every nerve for that which lies in front,'),
(997923,34,50,3,14,'I press on to the goal, to gain the prize of that heavenward call which God gave me through Christ Jesus.'),
(997924,34,50,3,15,'Let all of us, then, whose faith is mature, think this way. Then, if on any matter you think otherwise, God will make that also plain to you.'),
(997925,34,50,3,16,'Only we are bound to order our lives by what we have already attained.'),
(997926,34,50,3,17,'My friends, unite in following my example, and fix your eyes on those who are living by the pattern which we have set you.'),
(997927,34,50,3,18,'For there are many – of whom I have often told you, and now tell you even with tears – who are living in enmity to the cross of the Christ.'),
(997928,34,50,3,19,'The end of such people is ruin; for their appetites are their God, and they glory in their shame; their minds are given up to earthly things.'),
(997929,34,50,3,20,'But we are citizens of heaven, and from heaven we expect a saviour to come, the Lord Jesus Christ.'),
(997930,34,50,3,21,'By the exercise of his power to bring everything into subjection to himself, he will make our humble bodies like his glorious body.'),
(997931,34,50,4,1,'So then, my dear friends, whom I am longing to see – you who are my joy and my crown, stand fast in union with the Lord, dear friends.'),
(997932,34,50,4,2,'I entreat Euodia, and I entreat Syntyche, to live in harmony, in union with the Lord;'),
(997933,34,50,4,3,'yes, and I ask you, my true comrade, to help them, remembering that they toiled by my side in spreading the good news; and so, too, did Clement and my other fellow workers, whose names are in the book of life.'),
(997934,34,50,4,4,'All joy be yours at all times in your union with the Lord. Again I repeat – All joy be yours.'),
(997935,34,50,4,5,'Let your forbearing spirit be plain to everyone. The Lord is near.'),
(997936,34,50,4,6,'Do not be anxious about anything; but under all circumstances, by prayer and entreaty joined with thanksgiving, make your needs known to God.'),
(997937,34,50,4,7,'Then the peace of God, which is beyond all human understanding, will stand guard over your hearts and thoughts, through your union with Christ Jesus.'),
(997938,34,50,4,8,'In conclusion, friends, whenever you find things that are true or honourable, righteous or pure, loveable or praiseworthy, or if virtue and honour have any meaning, let them fill your thoughts.'),
(997939,34,50,4,9,'All that you learned and received and heard and saw in me put into practice continually; and then God, the giver of peace, will be with you.'),
(997940,34,50,4,10,'It was a matter of great joy to me, as one in union with the Lord, that at length your interest in me had revived. The interest indeed you had, but not the opportunity.'),
(997941,34,50,4,11,'Do not think that I am saying this under the pressure of want. For I, however I am placed, have learned to be independent of circumstances.'),
(997942,34,50,4,12,'I know how to face humble circumstances, and I know how to face prosperity. Into all and every human experience I have been initiated – into plenty and hunger, into prosperity and want.'),
(997943,34,50,4,13,'I can do everything in the strength of him who makes me strong!'),
(997944,34,50,4,14,'Yet you have acted nobly in sharing my troubles.'),
(997945,34,50,4,15,'And you at Philippi know, as well as I, that in the early days of the good news – at the time when I had just left Macedonia – no church, with the one exception of yourselves, had anything to do with me as far as giving and receiving are concerned.'),
(997946,34,50,4,16,'Indeed, even while I was still in Thessalonica, you sent more than once to relieve my wants.'),
(997947,34,50,4,17,'It is not that I am anxious for your gifts, but I am anxious to see the abundant return that will be placed to your account. I have enough of everything, and to spare.'),
(997948,34,50,4,18,'My wants are fully satisfied, now that I have received from Epaphroditus the gifts which you sent me – the sweet fragrance of a sacrifice acceptable and pleasing to God.'),
(997949,34,50,4,19,'And my God, out of the greatness of his wealth, will, in glory, fully satisfy your every need, through your union with Christ Jesus.'),
(997950,34,50,4,20,'To him, our God and Father, be ascribed all glory for every and ever. Amen.'),
(997951,34,50,4,21,'Give my greeting to everyone of the people of Christ Jesus. The Lord’s followers who are with me send your their greetings.'),
(997952,34,50,4,22,'All Christ’s people here, and especially those who belong to the Emperor’s household, send theirs.'),
(997953,34,50,4,23,'May the blessing of the Lord Jesus Christ rest on your souls.'),
(997954,34,51,1,1,'From Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus, by the will of God, and from Timothy, also a follower of the Lord.'),
(997955,34,51,1,2,'To Christ’s people at Colossae – the followers who are faithful to him: May God, our Father, bless you and give you peace.'),
(997956,34,51,1,3,'Whenever we pray we never fail to thank God, the Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, for you,'),
(997957,34,51,1,4,'now that we have heard of your faith in Christ Jesus and of the love that you have for all his people,'),
(997958,34,51,1,5,'because of the hope which is kept safe for you in heaven. Of this hope you heard long ago in the true message of the good news which reached you,'),
(997959,34,51,1,6,'bearing fruit and growing, as it does, through all the world, just as it did among you from the very day that you heard of God’s loving kindness, and understood what that loving kindness really is.'),
(997960,34,51,1,7,'It is just what you learned from Epaphras, our dear fellow servant, who, as a minister of the Christ, faithfully represents us,'),
(997961,34,51,1,8,'and who told us of the love with which the Spirit has inspired you.'),
(997962,34,51,1,9,'And therefore we, from the very day that we heard this, have never ceased praying for you, or asking that you may be filled with the knowledge of the will of God, which comes through all true spiritual wisdom and insight.'),
(997963,34,51,1,10,'Then you will live lives worthy of the Master, and so please God in every way. Your lives will be fruitful in every kind of good action, and grow into a fuller knowledge of God;'),
(997964,34,51,1,11,'you will be made strong at all points with a strength worthy of the power manifested in his glory – strong to endure with patience, and even with gladness, whatever may happen to you;'),
(997965,34,51,1,12,'and you will give thanks to the Father who made you fit to share the lot which awaits Christ’s people in the realms of light.'),
(997966,34,51,1,13,'For God has rescued us from the tyranny of darkness, and has removed us into the kingdom of his Son, who is the embodiment of his love,'),
(997967,34,51,1,14,'and through whom we have found deliverance in the forgiveness of our sins.'),
(997968,34,51,1,15,'For Christ is the incarnation of the invisible God – first-born and head of all creation;'),
(997969,34,51,1,16,'for in him was created all that is in heaven and on earth, the visible and the invisible – angels and archangels and all the powers of heaven.'),
(997970,34,51,1,17,'All has been created through him and for him. He was before all things, and all things unite in him;'),
(997971,34,51,1,18,'and he is the head of the church, which is his body. The first-born from the dead, he is to the church the Source of its life, that he, in all things, may stand first.'),
(997972,34,51,1,19,'For it pleased the Father that in him the divine nature in all its fulness should live,'),
(997973,34,51,1,20,'and through him to reconcile all things to himself (making peace by the shedding of Christ’s blood offered on the cross) – whether on earth or in heaven.'),
(997974,34,51,1,21,'And it pleased God that you, once estranged from him and hostile towards him in your thoughts, intent only on wickedness –'),
(997975,34,51,1,22,'But now he has reconciled you to himself by the sacrifice of Christ’s earthly body in death – it has pleased God that you should stand in his presence holy, pure, and blameless,'),
(997976,34,51,1,23,'if only you remain true to your faith, firm and immovable, never abandoning the hope held out in the good news to which you listened, which has been proclaimed among all created things under heaven, and of which I, Paul, was made an assistant.'),
(997977,34,51,1,24,'Now at last I can rejoice in my sufferings on your behalf, and in my own person I supplement the afflictions endured by the Christ, for the sake of his body, the church;'),
(997978,34,51,1,25,'of which I myself became a minister in virtue of the office with which God entrusted me for your benefit, to declare the message of God in all its fulness –'),
(997979,34,51,1,26,'That truth which has been hidden from former ages and generations. But now it has been revealed to God’s people,'),
(997980,34,51,1,27,'to whom it was his pleasure to make known the surpassing glory of that hidden truth when proclaimed among the Gentiles – “Christ among you! Your hope of glory!”'),
(997981,34,51,1,28,'This is the Christ whom we proclaim, warning everyone, and instructing everyone, with all the wisdom that we possess, in the hope of bringing everyone into God’s presence perfected by union with Christ.'),
(997982,34,51,1,29,'It is for that I toil, struggling with all the energy which he inspires and which works powerfully within me.'),
(997983,34,51,2,1,'I want you to know in how great a struggle I am engaged for you and for Christ’s people at Laodicea, and for all who have not yet seen me;'),
(997984,34,51,2,2,'in the hope that they, being bound to one another by love, and keeping in view the full blessedness of a firm conviction, may be encouraged to strive for a perfect knowledge of God’s hidden truth,'),
(997985,34,51,2,3,'even Christ himself, in whom all treasures of wisdom and knowledge lie hidden.'),
(997986,34,51,2,4,'I say this to prevent anyone from deceiving you by plausible arguments.'),
(997987,34,51,2,5,'It is true that I am not with you in person, but I am with you in spirit, and am glad to see the good order and the unbroken front resulting from your faith in Christ.'),
(997988,34,51,2,6,'Since, therefore, you have received Jesus, the Christ, as your Lord, live your lives in union with him –'),
(997989,34,51,2,7,'rooted in him, building up your characters through union with him, growing stronger through your faith, as you were taught, overflowing with faith and thanksgiving.'),
(997990,34,51,2,8,'Take care there is not someone who will carry you away by his “philosophy” – a hollow sham! – following, as it does, mere human traditions, and dealing with puerile questions of this world, and not with Christ.'),
(997991,34,51,2,9,'For in Christ the Godhead in all its fulness dwells incarnate;'),
(997992,34,51,2,10,'and, by your union with him, you also are filled with it. He is the head of all archangels and powers of heaven.'),
(997993,34,51,2,11,'By your union with him you received a circumcision that was not performed by human hands, when you threw off the tyranny of the earthly body, and received the circumcision of the Christ.'),
(997994,34,51,2,12,'For in baptism you were buried with Christ; and in baptism you were also raised to life with him, through your faith in the omnipotence of God, who raised him from the dead.'),
(997995,34,51,2,13,'And to you, who once were dead, by reason of your sins and your uncircumcised nature – to you God gave life in giving life to Christ! He pardoned all our sins!'),
(997996,34,51,2,14,'He canceled the bond which stood against us – the bond that consisted of ordinances – and which was directly hostile to us! He has taken it out of our way by nailing it to the cross!'),
(997997,34,51,2,15,'He rid himself of all the powers of evil, and held them up to open contempt, when he celebrated his triumph over them on the cross!'),
(997998,34,51,2,16,'Do not, then, allow anyone to take you to task on questions of eating or drinking, or in the matter of annual or monthly or weekly festivals.'),
(997999,34,51,2,17,'These things are only the shadow of what is to come; the substance is in the Christ.'),
(998000,34,51,2,18,'Do not let anyone defraud you of the reality by affecting delight in so-called “humility” and angel-worship. Such a person busies themselves with their visions, and without reason are rendered conceited by their merely human intellect.'),
(998001,34,51,2,19,'They fail to maintain union with the head, to whom it is due that the whole body, nourished and knit together by the contact and connexion of every part, grows with a divine growth.'),
(998002,34,51,2,20,'Since, with Christ, you became dead to the puerile teaching of this world, why do you submit, as if you still belonged to the world,'),
(998003,34,51,2,21,'to such ordinances as “Do not handle, or taste, or touch”?'),
(998004,34,51,2,22,'For all the things referred to in them cease to exist when used. You are following mere human directions and instructions.'),
(998005,34,51,2,23,'Such prohibitions appear reasonable where there is a desire for self-imposed service, and so-called “humility,” and harsh treatment of the body, but are of no real value against the indulgence of our earthly nature.'),
(998006,34,51,3,1,'Since, therefore, you were raised to life with the Christ, seek for the things that are above; for it is there that the Christ is seated at the right hand of God.'),
(998007,34,51,3,2,'Fix your thoughts on the things that are above, not on those that are on earth.'),
(998008,34,51,3,3,'For you died, and your life now lies hidden, with the Christ, in God.'),
(998009,34,51,3,4,'When the Christ, who is our life, appears, then you also will appear with him in glory.'),
(998010,34,51,3,5,'Therefore destroy all that is earthly in you – immorality, uncleanness, passions, evil desires, and that greed which is idolatry.'),
(998011,34,51,3,6,'These are the things because of which the wrath of God comes,'),
(998012,34,51,3,7,'and to which you, like others, once devoted your lives, when you lived for them.'),
(998013,34,51,3,8,'You, however, must now lay aside all such things – anger, passion, malice, slander, abuse.'),
(998014,34,51,3,9,'Never lie to one another. Get rid of your old self and its habits,'),
(998015,34,51,3,10,'and clothe yourselves with that new self, which, as it gains in knowledge, is being constantly renewed in resemblance to him who made it.'),
(998016,34,51,3,11,'In that new life there is no distinction between Greek and Jew, circumcised and uncircumcised, barbarian, Scythian, slave, free; but Christ is all! – and in all!'),
(998017,34,51,3,12,'Therefore, as God’s people, consecrated and dear to him, clothe yourselves with tenderness of heart, kindliness, humility, gentleness, forbearance;'),
(998018,34,51,3,13,'bearing with one another, and, when there is any ground for complaint, forgiving one another freely. As the Master freely forgave you, so you must forgive one another.'),
(998019,34,51,3,14,'Over all these virtues put on love; for that is the belt which makes all complete.'),
(998020,34,51,3,15,'Let the peace that the Christ gives decide all doubts within your hearts; for you also were called to the enjoyment of peace as members of one body. And show yourselves thankful.'),
(998021,34,51,3,16,'Let the message of the Christ be alive in your minds in all its wealth, bringing all wisdom with it. Teach and admonish one another with psalms, and hymns, and sacred songs, full of the loving kindness of God, lifting your hearts in song to him.'),
(998022,34,51,3,17,'And, whatever you say or do, do everything in the name of the Lord Jesus; and through him offer thanksgiving to God the father.'),
(998023,34,51,3,18,'Wives, submit to your husbands, as befits those who belong to the Lord.'),
(998024,34,51,3,19,'Husbands, love your wives, and never treat them harshly.'),
(998025,34,51,3,20,'Children, always obey your parents; for that is pleasant to see in those who belong to the Lord.'),
(998026,34,51,3,21,'Fathers, never irritate your children, otherwise they might become disheartened.'),
(998027,34,51,3,22,'Slaves, always obey your earthly masters, not only when their eyes are on you, as if you had but to please people alone, but giving them ungrudging service, in your respect for the Master.'),
(998028,34,51,3,23,'Whatever you do, do it with all your heart, as if working for the Master and not for people,'),
(998029,34,51,3,24,'since you know that it is from the Master that you will receive the inheritance which will be your reward. You are serving Christ, the Master.'),
(998030,34,51,3,25,'Those who do wrong will reap the wrong they have done; and there will be no partiality.'),
(998031,34,51,4,1,'Masters, do what is right and fair by your slaves, for you know that you also have a Master – in heaven.'),
(998032,34,51,4,2,'Devote yourselves to prayer. Give your whole mind to it, and also offer thanksgiving;'),
(998033,34,51,4,3,'and at the same time pray for us, so that God may give us an opening for our message, so that we may speak of the truths hidden in the Christ – the truths for which I am in chains!'),
(998034,34,51,4,4,'Then I will make them known, as I ought to do.'),
(998035,34,51,4,5,'Show tact in your behaviour to the outside world, making the most of every opportunity.'),
(998036,34,51,4,6,'Let your conversation always be kindly, but not bland, season it, as it were, with salt; be aware in each case of the answer you should be giving.'),
(998037,34,51,4,7,'Our dear friend, Tychicus, will tell you all about me. He is a faithful minister, and a fellow servant in the Master’s cause.'),
(998038,34,51,4,8,'I send him to you expressly that you may learn our circumstances, and that he may give you encouragement.'),
(998039,34,51,4,9,'With him will be Onesimus, our dear faithful friend, who is one of yourselves. They will tell you all that is going on here.'),
(998040,34,51,4,10,'My fellow prisoner, Aristarchus, sends you his greeting, and Barnabas’s cousin, Mark, sends his. (You have received directions about him. If he comes to you, make him welcome.)'),
(998041,34,51,4,11,'Joshua, who is called Justus, also sends his greeting. These are the only converts from Judaism who have worked with me for the kingdom of God; I have found them a great comfort.'),
(998042,34,51,4,12,'Epaphras, who is one of yourselves, sends you his greeting. He is a servant of Christ Jesus, and is always most earnest in your behalf in his prayers, praying that you may stand firm, with a matured faith and with a sure conviction of all that is in accordance with God’s will.'),
(998043,34,51,4,13,'I can bear testimony to the deep interest he takes in you, as well as in the followers at Laodicea and at Hierapolis.'),
(998044,34,51,4,14,'Luke, our dear doctor, sends you his greeting, and Demas sends his.'),
(998045,34,51,4,15,'Give my greeting to the followers at Laodicea, and to Nymphe, and to the church that meets at her house.'),
(998046,34,51,4,16,'And when this letter has been read to you, see that it is also read before the church at Laodicea, and that you yourselves read the letter which will be forwarded from there.'),
(998047,34,51,4,17,'Give this message to Archippus – “Take care to discharge to the best of your ability the office to which you were appointed in the Master’s cause.”'),
(998048,34,51,4,18,'I, Paul, add this greeting in my own handwriting. Remember these chains of mine. God’s blessing be with you.'),
(998049,34,52,1,1,'To the Thessalonian church in union with God the Father and the Lord Jesus Christ, from Paul, Silas, and Timothy. May God bless you and give you peace.'),
(998050,34,52,1,2,'We always mention you in our prayers and thank God for you all;'),
(998051,34,52,1,3,'recalling continually before our God and Father the efforts that have resulted from your faith, the toil prompted by your love, and the patient endurance sustained by your hope in our Lord Jesus Christ.'),
(998052,34,52,1,4,'Friends, whom God loves, we know that he has chosen you,'),
(998053,34,52,1,5,'because the good news that we brought came home to you, not merely as so many words, but with a power and a fulness of conviction due to the Holy Spirit. For you know the life that we lived among you for your good.'),
(998054,34,52,1,6,'And you yourselves began to follow, not only our example, but the Master’s also; and, in spite of much suffering, you welcomed the message with a joy inspired by the Holy Spirit,'),
(998055,34,52,1,7,'and so became a pattern to all who believed in Christ throughout Macedonia and Greece.'),
(998056,34,52,1,8,'For it was from you that the Lord’s message resounded throughout Macedonia and Greece; and, more than that, your faith in God has become known far and wide; so that there is no need for us to say another word.'),
(998057,34,52,1,9,'Indeed, in speaking about us, the people themselves tell of the reception you gave us, and how, turning to God from your idols, you became servants of the true and living God,'),
(998058,34,52,1,10,'and are now awaiting the return from heaven of his Son whom he raised from the dead – Jesus, our deliverer from the coming wrath.'),
(998059,34,52,2,1,'Yes, friends, you yourselves know that your reception of us was not without result.'),
(998060,34,52,2,2,'For, although we had experienced suffering and ill treatment, as you know, at Philippi, we had the courage, by the help of our God, to tell you God’s good news in spite of great opposition.'),
(998061,34,52,2,3,'Our appeal to you was not based on a delusion, nor was it made from unworthy motives, or with any intention of misleading you.'),
(998062,34,52,2,4,'But, having been found worthy by God to be entrusted with the good news, therefore we tell it; with a view to please, not people, but God who proves our hearts.'),
(998063,34,52,2,5,'Never at any time, as you know, did we use the language of flattery, or make false professions in order to hide selfish aims. God will bear witness to that.'),
(998064,34,52,2,6,'Nor did we seek to win honour from people, whether from you or from others, although, as apostles of Christ, we might have burdened you with our support.'),
(998065,34,52,2,7,'But we lived among you with the simplicity of a child; we were like a woman nursing her own children.'),
(998066,34,52,2,8,'In our strong affection for you, that seemed to us the best way of sharing with you, not only God’s good news, but our lives as well – so dear had you become to us.'),
(998067,34,52,2,9,'You will not have forgotten, friends, our labour and toil. Night and day we used to work at our trades, so as not be a burden to any of you, while we proclaimed to you God’s good news.'),
(998068,34,52,2,10,'You will bear witness, and God also, that our relations with you who believed in Christ were pure, and upright, and beyond reproach.'),
(998069,34,52,2,11,'Indeed, you know that, like a father with his own children, we used to encourage and comfort every one of you, and solemnly plead with you;'),
(998070,34,52,2,12,'so that you should make your daily lives worthy of God who is calling you into the glory of his kingdom.'),
(998071,34,52,2,13,'This, too, is a reason why we, on our part, are continually thanking God – because, in receiving the teaching that you had from us, you accepted it, not as the teaching of humans, but as what it really is – the teaching of God, which is even now doing its work within you who believe in Christ.'),
(998072,34,52,2,14,'For you, friends, began to follow the example of the churches of God in Judea which are in union with Jesus Christ; you, in your turn, suffering at the hands of your fellow citizens, in the same way as those churches did at the hands of their people –'),
(998073,34,52,2,15,'who killed both the Lord Jesus and the prophets, and persecuted us also. They do not try to please God, and they are enemies to all humanity,'),
(998074,34,52,2,16,'for they try to prevent us from speaking to the Gentiles with a view to their salvation, and so are always filling up the measure of their iniquity. But the wrath of God has come upon them to the full!'),
(998075,34,52,2,17,'As for ourselves, friends, our having been bereaved of you even for a short time – though in body only, and not in spirit – made us all the more eager to see your faces again; and the longing to do so was strong on us.'),
(998076,34,52,2,18,'That was why we made up our minds to go and see you – at least I, Paul, did, more than once – but Satan put difficulties in our way.'),
(998077,34,52,2,19,'For what hope or joy will be ours, or what crown will we have to boast of, in the presence of our Lord Jesus, at his coming, if it isn’t you?'),
(998078,34,52,2,20,'You are our pride and our delight!'),
(998079,34,52,3,1,'And so, as we could bear it no longer, we made up our minds to remain behind alone at Athens,'),
(998080,34,52,3,2,'and sent Timothy, our dear friend and God’s minister of the good news of the Christ, to strengthen you, and to encourage you in your faith,'),
(998081,34,52,3,3,'so that none of you should be shaken by the troubles through which you are passing. You yourselves know that we are destined to meet with such things.'),
(998082,34,52,3,4,'For, even while we were with you, we warned you beforehand that we were certain to encounter trouble. And so it proved, as you know.'),
(998083,34,52,3,5,'Therefore, since I could no longer endure the uncertainty, I sent to make inquiries about your faith, fearing that the Tempter had tempted you, and that our toil might prove to have been in vain.'),
(998084,34,52,3,6,'But, when Timothy recently returned to us from you with good news of your faith and love, and told us how kindly you think of us – always longing, he said, to see us, just as we are longing to see you –'),
(998085,34,52,3,7,'on hearing this, we felt encouraged about you, friends, in the midst of all our difficulties and troubles, by your faith.'),
(998086,34,52,3,8,'For it is new life to us to know that you are holding fast to the Lord.'),
(998087,34,52,3,9,'How can we thank God enough for all the happiness that you are giving us in the sight of our God?'),
(998088,34,52,3,10,'Night and day we pray most earnestly that we may see you face to face, and make good any deficiency in your faith.'),
(998089,34,52,3,11,'May our God and Father himself, and Jesus, our Lord, make the way plain for us to come to you.'),
(998090,34,52,3,12,'And for you, may the Lord fill you to overflowing with love for one another and for everyone, just as we are filled with love for you;'),
(998091,34,52,3,13,'and so make your hearts strong, and your lives pure beyond reproach, in the sight of our God and Father, at the coming of our Lord Jesus, with all his Holy Ones.'),
(998092,34,52,4,1,'Further, friends, we beg and urge you in the name of our Lord Jesus to carry out more fully than ever – as indeed you are already doing – all that you have heard from us as to what your daily life must be, if it is to please God.'),
(998093,34,52,4,2,'For you have not forgotten the directions that we gave you on the authority of our Lord Jesus.'),
(998094,34,52,4,3,'For this is God’s purpose – that you should be pure; abstaining from all immorality;'),
(998095,34,52,4,4,'each of you learning to gain control over your own body, in a way that is holy and honourable,'),
(998096,34,52,4,5,'and not for the mere gratification of your passions, like the Gentiles who know nothing of God;'),
(998097,34,52,4,6,'none of you overreaching or taking advantage of their fellow follower of the Lord in such matters. The Lord takes vengeance on all who do such things, as we have already warned you and solemnly declared.'),
(998098,34,52,4,7,'For God’s call to us does not permit of an impure life, but demands purity.'),
(998099,34,52,4,8,'Therefore the person who disregards this warning disregards, not people, but God who gives you his Holy Spirit.'),
(998100,34,52,4,9,'As to love for each other there is no need to write to you; for you have yourselves been taught by God to love one another;'),
(998101,34,52,4,10,'and indeed you do act in this spirit towards all his people throughout Macedonia.'),
(998102,34,52,4,11,'Make it your ambition to live quietly, and to attend to your own business, and to work with your hands, as we directed you;'),
(998103,34,52,4,12,'so that your conduct may win respect from those outside the church, and that you may not want for anything.'),
(998104,34,52,4,13,'We don’t want you to be ignorant, friends, about those who have passed to their rest. We don’t want you to grieve like other people who have no hope.'),
(998105,34,52,4,14,'For, as we believe that Jesus died and rose again, so also we believe that God will bring, with Jesus, those who through him have passed to their rest.'),
(998106,34,52,4,15,'This we tell you on the authority of the Lord – that those of us who are still living at the coming of the Lord will not anticipate those who have passed to their rest.'),
(998107,34,52,4,16,'For, with a loud summons, with the shout of an archangel, and with the trumpet-call of God, the Lord himself will come down from heaven.'),
(998108,34,52,4,17,'Then those who died in union with Christ will rise first; and afterwards we who are still living will be caught up in the clouds, with them, to meet the Lord in the air; and so we will be for ever with the Lord.'),
(998109,34,52,4,18,'Therefore, comfort one another with what I have told you.'),
(998110,34,52,5,1,'But as to the times and the moments, there is no need, friends, for anyone to write to you.'),
(998111,34,52,5,2,'You yourselves know well that the day of the Lord will come just as a thief comes in the night.'),
(998112,34,52,5,3,'When people are saying “All is quiet and safe,” it is then that, like birth pains on a pregnant woman, ruin comes suddenly upon them, and there will be no escape!'),
(998113,34,52,5,4,'You, however, friends, are not in darkness, that the daylight should take you by surprise as if you were thieves.'),
(998114,34,52,5,5,'For you all are children of light and children of the day.'),
(998115,34,52,5,6,'Therefore let us not sleep as others do. No, let us be watchful and self-controlled.'),
(998116,34,52,5,7,'It is at night that people sleep, and at night that drunkards get drunk.'),
(998117,34,52,5,8,'But let us, who belong to the day, control ourselves, and put on faith and love as a breast plate, and the hope of salvation as a helmet.'),
(998118,34,52,5,9,'For God destined us, not for wrath, but to win salvation through our Lord Jesus Christ, who died for us,'),
(998119,34,52,5,10,'that, whether we are still watching or have fallen asleep, we may live with him.'),
(998120,34,52,5,11,'Therefore encourage one another, and try to build up one another’s characters, as indeed you are doing.'),
(998121,34,52,5,12,'We beg you, friends, to value those who toil among you, and are your leaders in the Lord’s service, and give you counsel.'),
(998122,34,52,5,13,'Hold them in the very greatest esteem and affection for the sake of their work. Live at peace with one another.'),
(998123,34,52,5,14,'We entreat you also, friends – warn the disorderly, comfort the faint-hearted, give a helping hand to the weak, and be patient with everyone.'),
(998124,34,52,5,15,'Take care that none of you ever pays back wrong for wrong, but always follow the kindest course with one another and with everyone.'),
(998125,34,52,5,16,'Always be joyful;'),
(998126,34,52,5,17,'never cease to pray;'),
(998127,34,52,5,18,'under all circumstances give thanks to God. For this is his will for you as made known in Christ Jesus.'),
(998128,34,52,5,19,'Do not quench the Spirit;'),
(998129,34,52,5,20,'do not make light of preaching.'),
(998130,34,52,5,21,'Bring everything to the test; cling to what is good;'),
(998131,34,52,5,22,'shun every form of evil.'),
(998132,34,52,5,23,'May God himself, the giver of peace, make you altogether holy; and may your spirits, souls, and bodies be kept altogether faultless until the coming of our Lord Jesus Christ.'),
(998133,34,52,5,24,'He who calls you will not fail you; he will complete his work.'),
(998134,34,52,5,25,'Friends, pray for us.'),
(998135,34,52,5,26,'Greet all the Lord’s followers with a sacred kiss.'),
(998136,34,52,5,27,'I order you in the Lord’s name to have this letter read to all the brethren.'),
(998137,34,52,5,28,'May the blessing of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you.'),
(998138,34,53,1,1,'To the Thessalonian church in union with God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ, From Paul, Silas, and Timothy.'),
(998139,34,53,1,2,'May God, the Father, and the Lord Jesus Christ bless you and give you peace.'),
(998140,34,53,1,3,'Friends, it is our duty always to thank God about you, as is but right, considering the wonderful growth of your faith, and because, without exception, your love for one another is continually increasing.'),
(998141,34,53,1,4,'So much is this the case that we ourselves speak with pride, before the churches of God, of the patience and faith which you have shown, in spite of all the persecutions and troubles that you are enduring.'),
(998142,34,53,1,5,'These persecutions will vindicate the justice of God’s judgment, and will result in your being reckoned worthy of God’s kingdom, for the sake of which you are now suffering;'),
(998143,34,53,1,6,'since God deems it just to inflict suffering on those who are now inflicting suffering on you,'),
(998144,34,53,1,7,'and to give relief to you who are suffering, as well as to us, at the appearing of the Lord Jesus from heaven with his mighty angels, in flaming fire.'),
(998145,34,53,1,8,'Then he will inflict punishment on those who refuse to know God, and on those who turn a deaf ear to the good news of Jesus, our Lord.'),
(998146,34,53,1,9,'They will pay the penalty of unutterable ruin – banished from the presence of the Lord and from the glorious manifestation of his might,'),
(998147,34,53,1,10,'when he comes to be honoured in his people, and to be revered in all who have learned to believe in him (for you also believed our testimony) – as he will be on that day.'),
(998148,34,53,1,11,'With this in view, our constant prayer for you is that our God may count you worthy of the call that you have received, and by his power make perfect your delight in all goodness and the efforts that have resulted from your faith.'),
(998149,34,53,1,12,'Then, in the loving kindness of our God and the Lord Jesus Christ, will the name of Jesus, our Lord, be honoured in you, and you in him.'),
(998150,34,53,2,1,'As to the coming of our Lord Jesus Christ, and our being gathered to meet him, we beg you, friends,'),
(998151,34,53,2,2,'not lightly to let your minds become unsettled, or disturbed by any revelation, or by any message, or by any letter, purporting to come from us, to the effect that the day of the Lord is come.'),
(998152,34,53,2,3,'Do not let anyone deceive you, whatever he may do. For it will not come until after the Great Apostasy, and the appearing of that Incarnation of Wickedness, that Lost Soul,'),
(998153,34,53,2,4,'who so opposes himself to everyone that is spoken of as a God or as an object of worship, and so exalts himself above them, that he seats himself in the Temple of God, and displays himself as God!'),
(998154,34,53,2,5,'Don’t you remember how, when I was with you, I used to speak to you of all this?'),
(998155,34,53,2,6,'And you know now what the restraining influence is which prevents his appearing before his appointed time.'),
(998156,34,53,2,7,'Wickedness, indeed, is already at work in secret; but only until he who at present restrains it is removed out of the way.'),
(998157,34,53,2,8,'Then will “Wickedness Incarnate” appear, but the Lord Jesus will destroy him with the breath of his lips, and annihilate him by the splendour of his coming.'),
(998158,34,53,2,9,'For at the coming of the Lord there will be great activity on the part of Satan, in the form of all kinds of deceptive miracles, signs, and marvels, as well as of wicked attempts to delude –'),
(998159,34,53,2,10,'to the ruin of those who are on the path to destruction, because they have never received and loved the truth to their own salvation.'),
(998160,34,53,2,11,'That is why God places them under the influence of a delusion, to cause them to believe a lie;'),
(998161,34,53,2,12,'so that sentence may be passed on all those who refuse to believe the truth, but delight in wickedness.'),
(998162,34,53,2,13,'But, friends, whom the Lord loves, it is our duty always to thank God about you, for, from the first, God chose you for salvation through the purifying influence of the Spirit, and your belief in the truth.'),
(998163,34,53,2,14,'To this you were called by the good news which we brought you, to attain to the glory of our Lord Jesus Christ.'),
(998164,34,53,2,15,'Stand firm then, friends, and hold fast to the truths that we taught you, whether by word or by letter.'),
(998165,34,53,2,16,'And may our Lord Jesus Christ himself, and God our Father, who loved us and, in his loving kindness, gave us unfailing consolation and good ground for hope,'),
(998166,34,53,2,17,'console your hearts, and strengthen you to do and to say all that is right.'),
(998167,34,53,3,1,'In conclusion, friends, pray for us – pray that the Lord’s message may spread rapidly, and be received everywhere with honour, as it was among you;'),
(998168,34,53,3,2,'and that we may be preserved from wrong-headed and wicked people – for it is not everyone who believes in Christ.'),
(998169,34,53,3,3,'But the Lord will not fail you. He will give you strength, and guard you from evil.'),
(998170,34,53,3,4,'Yes, and the confidence that our union with the Lord enables us to place in you leads us to believe that you are doing, and will do, what we direct you.'),
(998171,34,53,3,5,'May the Lord bring you to the love of God, and to the patience of the Christ.'),
(998172,34,53,3,6,'We beg you, friends, in the name of the Lord Jesus Christ, to avoid any follower who is living an ill-ordered life, which is not in agreement with the teaching that you received from us.'),
(998173,34,53,3,7,'For you know well that you ought to follow our example. When we were with you, our life was not ill-ordered,'),
(998174,34,53,3,8,'nor did we eat anyone’s bread without paying for it. Night and day, labouring and toiling, we used to work at our trades, so as not to be a burden on any of you.'),
(998175,34,53,3,9,'This was not because we had not a right to receive support, but our object was to give you a pattern for you to copy.'),
(998176,34,53,3,10,'Indeed, when we were with you, the rule we laid down was – “Whoever does not choose to work will not get to eat.”'),
(998177,34,53,3,11,'We hear that there are among you people who are living ill-ordered lives, and who, instead of attending to their own business, are mere busybodies.'),
(998178,34,53,3,12,'All such people we beg, and implore, in the name of the Lord Jesus Christ, to attend quietly to their business, and earn their own living.'),
(998179,34,53,3,13,'You, friends, must not grow weary of doing what is right.'),
(998180,34,53,3,14,'If anyone disregards what we have said in this letter, take note of them and avoid their company, so that they may feel ashamed.'),
(998181,34,53,3,15,'Yet do not think of them as an enemy, but caution them as you would a brother or sister.'),
(998182,34,53,3,16,'May the Lord, from whom all peace comes, himself give you his peace at all times and in all ways. May he be with you all.'),
(998183,34,53,3,17,'I, Paul, add this greeting in my own handwriting. It is my signature to every letter. This is how I write.'),
(998184,34,53,3,18,'May the blessing of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you all.'),
(998185,34,54,1,1,'From Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus by the appointment of God, our Saviour, and Christ Jesus, our hope.'),
(998186,34,54,1,2,'To Timothy, my true child in the faith: May God, the Father, and Christ Jesus, our Lord, bless you, and be merciful to you, and give you peace.'),
(998187,34,54,1,3,'I beg you, as I did when I was on my way into Macedonia, to remain at Ephesus; so that you may instruct certain people there not to teach new and strange doctrines,'),
(998188,34,54,1,4,'nor to devote their attention to legends and interminable genealogies, which tend to give rise to argument rather than to further that divine plan which is revealed in the faith.'),
(998189,34,54,1,5,'The object of all instruction is to call forth that love which comes from a pure heart, a clear conscience, and a sincere faith.'),
(998190,34,54,1,6,'And it is because they have not aimed at these things that the attention of certain people has been diverted to unprofitable subjects.'),
(998191,34,54,1,7,'They want to be teachers of the Law, and yet do not understand either the words they use, or the subjects on which they speak so confidently.'),
(998192,34,54,1,8,'We know, of course, that the Law is excellent, when used legitimately,'),
(998193,34,54,1,9,'by one who recognises that laws were not made for good people, but for the lawless and disorderly, for irreligious and wicked people, for those who are irreverent and profane, for those who ill-treat their fathers or mothers, for murderers,'),
(998194,34,54,1,10,'for the immoral, for perverts, for slave-dealers, for liars, for perjurers, and for whatever else is opposed to sound Christian teaching –'),
(998195,34,54,1,11,'as is taught in the glorious good news of the ever-blessed God, with which I was entrusted.'),
(998196,34,54,1,12,'I am thankful to Christ Jesus, our Lord, who has been my strength, for showing that he thought me worthy of trust by appointing me to his ministry,'),
(998197,34,54,1,13,'though I once used to blaspheme, and to persecute, and to insult. Yet mercy was shown me, because I acted in ignorance, while still an unbeliever;'),
(998198,34,54,1,14,'and the loving kindness of our Lord was boundless, and filled me with that faith and love which come from union with Christ Jesus.'),
(998199,34,54,1,15,'How true the saying is, and worthy of the fullest acceptance, that “Christ Jesus came into the world to save sinners”! And there is no greater sinner than I!'),
(998200,34,54,1,16,'Yet mercy was shown me for the express purpose that Christ Jesus might exhibit in my case, beyond all others, his exhaustless patience, as an example for those who were afterwards to believe on him and attain eternal life.'),
(998201,34,54,1,17,'To the eternal King, ever-living, invisible, the one God, be ascribed honour and glory for ever and ever. Amen.'),
(998202,34,54,1,18,'This, then, is the charge that I lay on you, Timothy, my child, in accordance with what was predicted of you – Fight the good fight in the spirit of those predictions,'),
(998203,34,54,1,19,'with faith, and with a clear conscience; and it is because they have thrust this aside, that, as regards the faith, some have wrecked their lives.'),
(998204,34,54,1,20,'Hymenaeus and Alexander are instances – the men whom I delivered over to Satan so that they might be taught not to blaspheme.'),
(998205,34,54,2,1,'First of all, then, I ask that petitions, prayers, intercessions, and thanksgivings should be offered for everyone,'),
(998206,34,54,2,2,'especially for kings and all who are in high positions, in order that we may lead a quiet and peaceful life in a deeply religious and reverent spirit.'),
(998207,34,54,2,3,'This will be good and acceptable in the eyes of God, our Saviour,'),
(998208,34,54,2,4,'whose will is that everyone should be saved, and attain to a full knowledge of the truth.'),
(998209,34,54,2,5,'There is but one God, and one mediator between God and humanity – the human, Christ Jesus,'),
(998210,34,54,2,6,'who gave himself as a ransom on behalf of all.'),
(998211,34,54,2,7,'and it was for this that I was myself appointed a herald and an apostle (I am telling the simple truth and no lie) – a teacher of the Gentiles in the faith and truth.'),
(998212,34,54,2,8,'My desire, then, is that it should be the custom everywhere for the men to lead the prayers, with hands reverently uplifted, avoiding heated controversy.'),
(998213,34,54,2,9,'I also desire that women should adorn themselves with appropriate dress, worn quietly and modestly, and not with wreaths or gold ornaments for the hair, or pearls, or costly clothing,'),
(998214,34,54,2,10,'but – as is proper for women who profess to be religious – with good actions.'),
(998215,34,54,2,11,'They must learn, listening quietly to their teachers and showing them all deference.'),
(998216,34,54,2,12,'I do not consent to them becoming teachers, or exercising authority over men; they ought to not make a fuss.'),
(998217,34,54,2,13,'Adam was formed first, not Eve.'),
(998218,34,54,2,14,'And it was not Adam who was deceived; it was the woman who was entirely deceived and fell into sin.'),
(998219,34,54,2,15,'But she will be saved by the birth of a child, if they never abandon faith, love, or holiness, and behave with modesty.'),
(998220,34,54,3,1,'How true is this saying: “To aspire to be to be a supervisor in the church is to be ambitious for a noble task.”'),
(998221,34,54,3,2,'The supervisor should be of blameless character; a faithful partner; living a temperate, discreet, and well-ordered life; hospitable, and a skilful teacher,'),
(998222,34,54,3,3,'not addicted to drink or brawling, but of a forbearing and peaceable disposition, and not a lover of money;'),
(998223,34,54,3,4,'they should provide for own household well, and their children should kept under control and be well-behaved.'),
(998224,34,54,3,5,'If someone does not know how to provide for their own household, how can they take charge of the church of God?'),
(998225,34,54,3,6,'The supervisor should not be a recent convert, or they might become blinded by pride and fall under the same judgement as the devil.'),
(998226,34,54,3,7,'They should also be well spoken of by outsiders, so that they may not incur censure and so fall into the devil’s trap.'),
(998227,34,54,3,8,'So, too, assistants should be serious and straightforward, not given to taking much drink or to questionable money-making,'),
(998228,34,54,3,9,'but people who hold the deep truths of the faith and have a clear conscience.'),
(998229,34,54,3,10,'They should be tested first, and only appointed to their office if no objection is raised against them.'),
(998230,34,54,3,11,'It should be the same with the women in this office. They should be serious, not gossips, sober, and trustworthy in all respects.'),
(998231,34,54,3,12,'Assistants should be faithful partners who manage their children and their households well.'),
(998232,34,54,3,13,'Those who have filled that post with honour gain for themselves an honourable position, as well as great confidence through the faith that they place in Christ Jesus.'),
(998233,34,54,3,14,'I am writing this to you, though I hope that I will come to see you before long;'),
(998234,34,54,3,15,'but in case I should be delayed, I want you to know what your conduct ought to be in the Household of God, which is the church of the living God – the pillar and stay of the truth.'),
(998235,34,54,3,16,'Yes, and confessedly wonderful are the deep truths of our religion; for –'),
(998236,34,54,4,1,'But the Spirit distinctly says that in later times there will be some who will fall away from the faith, and devote their attention to misleading spirits, and to the teaching of demons,'),
(998237,34,54,4,2,'who will make use of the hypocrisy of lying teachers. These people’s consciences are seared,'),
(998238,34,54,4,3,'and they discourage marriage and enjoin abstinence from certain kinds of food; though God created these foods to be enjoyed thankfully by those who hold the faith and have attained a full knowledge of the truth.'),
(998239,34,54,4,4,'Everything created by God is good, and there in nothing that need be rejected – provided only that it is received thankfully;'),
(998240,34,54,4,5,'for it is consecrated by God’s blessing and by prayer.'),
(998241,34,54,4,6,'Put all this before the followers, and you will be a good servant of Christ Jesus, sustained by the precepts of the faith and of that good teaching by which you have guided your life.'),
(998242,34,54,4,7,'As for profane legends and old wives’ tales, leave them alone. Train yourself to lead a religious life;'),
(998243,34,54,4,8,'for while the training of the body is of service in some respects, religion is of service in all, carrying with it, as it does, a promise of life both here and hereafter.'),
(998244,34,54,4,9,'How true that saying is and worthy of the fullest acceptance!'),
(998245,34,54,4,10,'With that aim we toil and struggle, for we have set our hopes on the living God, who is the Saviour of all, and especially of those who hold the faith.'),
(998246,34,54,4,11,'Remember these things in your teaching.'),
(998247,34,54,4,12,'Do not let anyone look down on you because you are young, but, by your conversation, your conduct, your love, your faith, and your purity, be an example to those who hold the faith.'),
(998248,34,54,4,13,'Until I come, apply yourself to public reading, preaching, and teaching.'),
(998249,34,54,4,14,'Do not neglect the divine gift within you, which was given you, amid many a prediction, when the hands of the church elders were laid on your head.'),
(998250,34,54,4,15,'Practice these things, devote yourself to them, so that your progress may be plain to everyone.'),
(998251,34,54,4,16,'Look to yourself as well as to your teaching. Persevere in this, for your doing so will mean salvation for yourself as well as for your hearers.'),
(998252,34,54,5,1,'Do not reprimand an older man, but plead with him as if he were your father. Treat the young men as brothers,'),
(998253,34,54,5,2,'the older women as mothers, and the younger women as sisters – with all purity.'),
(998254,34,54,5,3,'Show consideration for widows – I mean those who are really widowed.'),
(998255,34,54,5,4,'But, if a widow has children or grandchildren, they should learn to show proper regard for the members of their own family first, and to make some return to their parents; for that is pleasing in God’s sight.'),
(998256,34,54,5,5,'As for the woman who is really widowed and left quite alone, her hopes are fixed on God, and she devotes herself to prayers and supplications night and day.'),
(998257,34,54,5,6,'But the life of a widow who is devoted to pleasure is a living death.'),
(998258,34,54,5,7,'Those are the points you should teach, so that there may be no call for your censure.'),
(998259,34,54,5,8,'Anyone who fails to provide for their own relatives, and especially for those under their own roof, has disowned the faith, and is worse than an unbeliever.'),
(998260,34,54,5,9,'A widow, when her name is added to the list, should not be less than sixty years old; she should have been a faithful wife,'),
(998261,34,54,5,10,'and be well spoken of for her kind actions. She should have brought up children, have shown hospitality to strangers, have washed the feet of her fellow Christians, have relieved those who were in distress, and devoted herself to every kind of good action.'),
(998262,34,54,5,11,'But you should exclude the younger widows from the list; for, when they grow restive under the yoke of the Christ, they want to marry,'),
(998263,34,54,5,12,'and so they bring condemnation on themselves for having broken their previous promise.'),
(998264,34,54,5,13,'And not only that, but they learn to be idle as they go about from house to house. Nor are they merely idle, but they also become gossips and busybodies, and talk of what they ought not.'),
(998265,34,54,5,14,'Therefore I advise young widows to marry, bear children, and attend to their homes, and so avoid giving the enemy an opportunity for scandal.'),
(998266,34,54,5,15,'There are some who have already left us, to follow Satan.'),
(998267,34,54,5,16,'Any Christian woman, who has relatives who are widows, ought to relieve them and not allow them to become a burden to the church, so that the church may relieve those widows who are really widowed.'),
(998268,34,54,5,17,'Those church elders who fill their office well should be held deserving of especial consideration, particularly those whose work lies in preaching and teaching.'),
(998269,34,54,5,18,'The words of scripture are –'),
(998270,34,54,5,19,'Do not entertain a charge against an church elder, unless it is supported by two or three witnesses;'),
(998271,34,54,5,20,'but rebuke offenders publicly, so that others may take warning.'),
(998272,34,54,5,21,'I charge you solemnly, before God and Christ Jesus and the chosen angels, to carry out these directions, unswayed by prejudice, never acting with partiality.'),
(998273,34,54,5,22,'Never ordain anyone hastily, and take no part in the wrong-doing of others. Keep your life pure.'),
(998274,34,54,5,23,'Do not continue to drink water only, but take a little wine because of the weakness of your stomach, and your frequent ailments.'),
(998275,34,54,5,24,'There are some people whose sins are conspicuous and lead on to judgment, while there are others whose sins dog their steps.'),
(998276,34,54,5,25,'In the same way noble deeds become conspicuous, and those which are otherwise cannot be concealed.'),
(998277,34,54,6,1,'All who are in the position of slaves should regard their masters as deserving of the greatest respect, so that the name of God, and our teaching, may not be maligned.'),
(998278,34,54,6,2,'Those who have Christian masters should not think less of them because they are also followers of Christ, but on the contrary they should serve them all the better, because those who are to benefit by their good work are dear to them as their fellow Christians.'),
(998279,34,54,6,3,'Anyone who teaches otherwise, and refuses their assent to sound instruction – the instruction of our Lord Jesus Christ – and to the teaching of religion,'),
(998280,34,54,6,4,'is puffed up with conceit, not really knowing anything, but having a morbid craving for discussions and arguments. Such things only give rise to envy, quarrelling, recriminations, base suspicions,'),
(998281,34,54,6,5,'and incessant wrangling on the part of these corrupt-minded people who have lost all hold on the truth, and who think of religion only as a source of gain.'),
(998282,34,54,6,6,'Of course religion is a great source of gain – when combined with contentment!'),
(998283,34,54,6,7,'For we brought nothing into the world, because we cannot even carry anything out of it.'),
(998284,34,54,6,8,'So, with food and shelter, we will be content.'),
(998285,34,54,6,9,'Those who want to be rich fall into the net of temptation, and become the prey of many foolish and harmful ambitions, which plunge people into destruction and ruin.'),
(998286,34,54,6,10,'Love of money is a source of all kinds of evil; and in their eagerness to be rich some have wandered away from the faith, and have been pierced to the heart by many a regret.'),
(998287,34,54,6,11,'But you must, servant of God, avoid all this. Aim at righteousness, piety, faith, love, endurance, gentleness.'),
(998288,34,54,6,12,'Run the great race of the faith, and win the eternal life. It was for this that you received the call, and, in the presence of many witnesses, made the great profession of faith.'),
(998289,34,54,6,13,'I beg you, as in the sight of God, the source of all life, and of Christ Jesus who before Pontius Pilate made the great profession of faith –'),
(998290,34,54,6,14,'I implore you to keep his command free from stain or reproach, until the appearing of our Lord Jesus Christ.'),
(998291,34,54,6,15,'This will be brought about in his own time by the one ever-blessed Potentate, the king of all kings and Lord of all lords,'),
(998292,34,54,6,16,'who alone is possessed of immortality and dwells in unapproachable light, whom no one has ever seen or ever can see – to whom be ascribed honour and power for ever. Amen.'),
(998293,34,54,6,17,'Teach those who are wealthy in this life not to pride themselves, or fix their hopes, on so uncertain a thing as wealth, but on God, who gives us a wealth of enjoyment on every side.'),
(998294,34,54,6,18,'Teach them to show kindness, to exhibit a wealth of good actions, to be open-handed and generous,'),
(998295,34,54,6,19,'storing up for themselves what in the future will prove to be a good foundation, so that they may gain the only true life.'),
(998296,34,54,6,20,'Timothy, guard what has been entrusted to you. Avoid the profane prattle and contradictions of what some miscall “theology,”'),
(998297,34,54,6,21,'for there are those who, while asserting their proficiency in it, have yet, as regards the faith, gone altogether astray.'),
(998298,34,55,1,1,'From Paul who, by the will of God, is an apostle of Christ Jesus, charged to proclaim the life that comes from union with Christ Jesus,'),
(998299,34,55,1,2,'to Timothy, my dear child: may God, the Father, and Christ Jesus, our Lord, bless you, and be merciful to you, and give you peace.'),
(998300,34,55,1,3,'I am thankful to God, whom I serve, as my ancestors did, with a clear conscience, when I remember you, as I never fail to do, in my prayers – night and day alike,'),
(998301,34,55,1,4,'as I think of your tears, longing to see you, that my happiness may be completed,'),
(998302,34,55,1,5,'now that I have been reminded of the sincere faith that you have shown. That faith was seen first in your grandmother Lois and your mother Eunice, and is now, I am convinced, in you also.'),
(998303,34,55,1,6,'And that is my reason for reminding you to stir into flame that gift of God, which is yours through your ordination at my hands.'),
(998304,34,55,1,7,'For the Spirit which God gave us was not a spirit of cowardice, but a spirit of power, love, and self-control.'),
(998305,34,55,1,8,'Do not, therefore, be ashamed of the testimony which we have to bear to our Lord, or of me imprisoned for his sake; but join with me in suffering for the good news, as far as God enables you.'),
(998306,34,55,1,9,'It was God who saved us, and from him we received our solemn call – not as a reward for anything that we had done, but in fulfilment of his own loving purpose. For that love was extended to us, through Christ Jesus, before time began,'),
(998307,34,55,1,10,'and has now been made apparent through the appearing of our Saviour, Christ Jesus; who has made an end of death, and has brought life and Immortality to light by that good news,'),
(998308,34,55,1,11,'of which I was myself appointed a herald and apostle, and teacher.'),
(998309,34,55,1,12,'That is why I am undergoing these sufferings; yet I feel no shame, for I know in whom I have put my faith, and am convinced that he is able to guard what I have entrusted to him until that day.'),
(998310,34,55,1,13,'Keep before you, as an example of sound teaching, all that you learnt from me as you listened with that faith and love which come from union with Christ Jesus.'),
(998311,34,55,1,14,'Guard by the help of the Holy Spirit, who is within us, the glorious trust that has been committed to you.'),
(998312,34,55,1,15,'You know, of course, that all our friends in Roman Asia turned their backs on me, including Phygellus and Hermogenes.'),
(998313,34,55,1,16,'May the Lord show mercy to the household of Onesiphorus; for he often cheered me and was not ashamed of my chains.'),
(998314,34,55,1,17,'On the contrary, when he arrived in Rome, he sought eagerly for me until he found me.'),
(998315,34,55,1,18,'The Lord grant that he may find mercy at the hands of the Lord on that day. The many services that he rendered at Ephesus you have the best means of knowing.'),
(998316,34,55,2,1,'You must, then, my child, find strength in the help which comes from the union with Christ Jesus;'),
(998317,34,55,2,2,'and what you learnt from me, in the presence of many listeners, entrust to reliable people, who will be able in their turn to teach others.'),
(998318,34,55,2,3,'Share hardships with me, as a true soldier of Christ Jesus.'),
(998319,34,55,2,4,'A soldier on active service, to please his superior officer, always avoids entangling himself in the affairs of ordinary life.'),
(998320,34,55,2,5,'No athlete is ever awarded the wreath of victory unless they have kept the rules.'),
(998321,34,55,2,6,'The labourer who does the work should be the first to receive a share of the fruits of the earth.'),
(998322,34,55,2,7,'Reflect on what I say; the Lord will always help you to understand.'),
(998323,34,55,2,8,'Keep before your mind Jesus Christ, raised from the dead, a descendant of David, as told in the good news entrusted to me;'),
(998324,34,55,2,9,'in the service of which I am suffering hardships, even to being put in fetters as a criminal. But the message of God is not fettered;'),
(998325,34,55,2,10,'and that is why I submit to anything for the sake of God’s people: so that they also may obtain the salvation which comes from union with Christ Jesus, and imperishable glory.'),
(998326,34,55,2,11,'How true this saying is – “If we have shared his death, we will also share his life.'),
(998327,34,55,2,12,'If we continue to endure, we will also share his throne. If we should ever disown him, he, too, will disown us.'),
(998328,34,55,2,13,'If we lose our trust, he is still to be trusted, for he cannot be false to himself!”'),
(998329,34,55,2,14,'Remind people of all this; tell them solemnly, as in the sight of God, to avoid controversy, a useless thing and the ruin of those who listen to it.'),
(998330,34,55,2,15,'Do your utmost to show yourself true to God, a worker with no reason to be ashamed, accurate in delivering the message of the truth.'),
(998331,34,55,2,16,'Avoid profane prattle. Those who indulge in it only get deeper into irreligious ways,'),
(998332,34,55,2,17,'and their teaching will spread like a cancer. Hymenaeus and Philetus are instances of this.'),
(998333,34,55,2,18,'They have gone completely astray as regards the truth; they say that a resurrection has already taken place, and so upset some people’s faith.'),
(998334,34,55,2,19,'Yet God’s firm foundation still stands unmoved, and it bears this inscription –'),
(998335,34,55,2,20,'Now in a large house there are not only things of gold and silver, but also others of wood and earthenware, some for better and some for common use.'),
(998336,34,55,2,21,'If, then, a person has escaped from the pollution of such errors as I have mentioned, they will be like a thing kept for better use, set apart, serviceable to its owner, ready for any good purpose.'),
(998337,34,55,2,22,'Flee from the passions of youth, but pursue righteousness, faith, love, and peace, in the company of those who, with a pure heart, invoke the Lord.'),
(998338,34,55,2,23,'Shun foolish and ignorant discussions, for you know that they only breed quarrels;'),
(998339,34,55,2,24,'and a servant of the Lord should never quarrel. They ought, on the contrary, to be courteous to everyone, skilful teachers, and forbearing.'),
(998340,34,55,2,25,'They should instruct their opponents in a gentle spirit; for, possibly, God may give those opponents a repentance that will lead to a fuller knowledge of truth,'),
(998341,34,55,2,26,'and they may yet come to a sober mind, and escape from the devil’s net, when captured by the Lord’s servant to do the will of God.'),
(998342,34,55,3,1,'Be sure of this, that in the last days difficult times will come.'),
(998343,34,55,3,2,'People will be selfish, mercenary, boastful, haughty, and blasphemous; disobedient to their parents, ungrateful, impure,'),
(998344,34,55,3,3,'incapable of affection, merciless, slanderous, wanting in self-control, brutal, careless of the right,'),
(998345,34,55,3,4,'treacherous, reckless, and puffed up with pride; they will love pleasure more than they love God;'),
(998346,34,55,3,5,'and while they retain the outward form of religion, they will not allow it to influence them. Turn your back on such people as these.'),
(998347,34,55,3,6,'For among them are to be found those who creep into homes and captivate weak women – women who, loaded with sins, and slaves to all kinds of passions,'),
(998348,34,55,3,7,'are always learning, and yet never able to attain to a real knowledge of the truth.'),
(998349,34,55,3,8,'Just as Jannes and Jambres opposed Moses, so do these people, in their turn, oppose the truth. Their minds are corrupted, and, as regards the faith, they are utterly worthless.'),
(998350,34,55,3,9,'They will not, however, make further progress; for their wicked folly will be plain to everyone, just as the folly Jannes and Jambres was.'),
(998351,34,55,3,10,'But you, Timothy, were a close observer of my teaching, my conduct, my purposes, my faith, my forbearance, my love, and my patient endurance,'),
(998352,34,55,3,11,'as well as of my persecutions, and of the sufferings which I met with at Antioch, Iconium, and Lystra. You know what persecutions I underwent; and yet the Lord brought me safe out of all!'),
(998353,34,55,3,12,'Yes, and all who aim at living a religious life in union with Christ Jesus will have to suffer persecution;'),
(998354,34,55,3,13,'but wicked people and impostors will go from bad to worse, deceiving others and deceived themselves.'),
(998355,34,55,3,14,'You, however, must stand by what you learnt and accepted as true. You know who they were from whom you learnt it;'),
(998356,34,55,3,15,'and that, from your childhood, you have known the sacred writings, which can give you the wisdom that, through belief in Christ Jesus, leads to salvation.'),
(998357,34,55,3,16,'All scripture is God-breathed: helpful for teaching, for refuting error, for giving guidance, and for training others in righteousness;'),
(998358,34,55,3,17,'so that God’s people may be capable and equipped for good work of every kind.'),
(998359,34,55,4,1,'I solemnly charge you – in the sight of God and of Christ Jesus, who will one day judge the living and the dead – I charge you by his appearing and by his kingdom:'),
(998360,34,55,4,2,'Proclaim the message, be ready in season and out of season, convince, rebuke, encourage, never failing to instruct with forbearance.'),
(998361,34,55,4,3,'For a time will come when people will not tolerate sound teaching. They will follow their own wishes, and, in their itching for novelty, procure themselves a crowd of teachers.'),
(998362,34,55,4,4,'They will turn a deaf ear to the truth, and give their attention to legends instead.'),
(998363,34,55,4,5,'But you, Timothy, must always be temperate. Face hardships; do the work of a missionary; discharge all the duties of your office.'),
(998364,34,55,4,6,'As for me, my life blood is already being poured out; the time of my departure is close at hand.'),
(998365,34,55,4,7,'I have run the great race; I have finished the course; I have kept the faith.'),
(998366,34,55,4,8,'And now the crown of righteousness awaits me, which the Lord, the just judge, will give me on that day – and not only to me, but to all who have loved his appearing.'),
(998367,34,55,4,9,'Do your utmost to come to me soon;'),
(998368,34,55,4,10,'for Demas, in his love for the world, has deserted me. He has gone to Thessalonica, Crescens to Galatia, and Titus to Dalmatia.'),
(998369,34,55,4,11,'There is no one but Luke with me. Pick up Mark on your way, and bring him with you, for he is useful to me in my work.'),
(998370,34,55,4,12,'I have sent Tychicus to Ephesus.'),
(998371,34,55,4,13,'Bring with you, when you come, the cloak which I left at Troas with Carpus, and the books, especially the parchments.'),
(998372,34,55,4,14,'Alexander, the coppersmith, showed much ill feeling towards me. The Lord will give him what his actions deserve.'),
(998373,34,55,4,15,'You must also on your guard against him, for he is strongly opposed to our teaching.'),
(998374,34,55,4,16,'At my first trial no one stood by me. They all deserted me. May it never be counted against them!'),
(998375,34,55,4,17,'But the Lord came to my help and strengthened me, in order that, through me, the proclamation should be made so widely that all the Gentiles should hear it; and I was rescued out of the lion’s mouth.'),
(998376,34,55,4,18,'The Lord will rescue me from all evil, and bring me safe into his Heavenly kingdom. All glory to him for ever and ever! Amen.'),
(998377,34,55,4,19,'Give my greeting to Prisca and Aquila, and to the household of Onesiphorus.'),
(998378,34,55,4,20,'Erastus remained at Corinth, and I left Thophimus ill at Miletus.'),
(998379,34,55,4,21,'Do your utmost to come before winter. Eubulus, Pudens, Linus and Claudia send you their greetings, and so do the rest of the Lord’s followers.'),
(998380,34,55,4,22,'May the Lord be with your soul. God bless you all.'),
(998381,34,56,1,1,'From Paul, a servant of God, and an apostle of Jesus Christ, on behalf of the faith of God’s chosen people, and their knowledge of that truth which makes for godliness'),
(998382,34,56,1,2,'– and is based on the hope of eternal life, which God, who never lies, promised before the ages began,'),
(998383,34,56,1,3,'and has revealed at his own time in his message, with the preaching of which I was entrusted by the command of God our Saviour.'),
(998384,34,56,1,4,'To Titus, my true child in our shared faith: May God, the Father, and Christ Jesus, our Saviour, bless you and give you peace.'),
(998385,34,56,1,5,'My reason for leaving you in Crete was that you might put in order what had been left unfinished, and appoint church elders in the various towns, as I myself directed you.'),
(998386,34,56,1,6,'They are to be of irreproachable character, faithful to their partners, whose children are believers in Christ and have never been open to the charge of being wild or unruly.'),
(998387,34,56,1,7,'For a supervisor, as God’s steward, ought to be of blameless character – not arrogant or quick-tempered, not given to drunkeness, violence or shady money-making.'),
(998388,34,56,1,8,'Instead, they should be hospitable, love what is good, self-controlled, upright, people of holy life and disciplined,'),
(998389,34,56,1,9,'holding firmly to the trustworthy message as it has been taught – so that they may be able to encourage others by sound teaching, as well as to refute those who contradict it.'),
(998390,34,56,1,10,'For there are many undisciplined persons who lead others astray with their nonsense, especially those of the group advocating the necessity of circumcision.'),
(998391,34,56,1,11,'They need to be kept quiet as they disrupt whole households by teaching what they ought not to teach, simply to make shameful financial gain.'),
(998392,34,56,1,12,'It was a Cretan – one of their own prophets – who said: “Cretans are always liars, evil beasts, and lazy gluttons.” This statement is true.'),
(998393,34,56,1,13,'Therefore rebuke them sharply, so that they may be sound in the faith,'),
(998394,34,56,1,14,'and may pay no attention to Jewish legends, or to the directions of those who turn their backs on the truth.'),
(998395,34,56,1,15,'To those whose minds are pure, all things are ritually pure, but to those whose minds are tainted and unbelieving nothing is pure, as their minds and consciences are alike polluted.'),
(998396,34,56,1,16,'They claim to know God, but by their actions they deny him. They are detestable and disobedient and useless for any good work.'),
(998397,34,56,2,1,'You however, should speak of such subjects as properly have a place in sound teaching.'),
(998398,34,56,2,2,'Teach that the older men should be soberly clear minded, dignified and self-controlled – sound in faith, love, and patient endurance.'),
(998399,34,56,2,3,'So, too, that the older women should live reverent lives, not slanderers, not slaves to excessive drinking.'),
(998400,34,56,2,4,'They should teach what is good, so as to train the younger women to love their husbands and children,'),
(998401,34,56,2,5,'and to be self-controlled, pure-minded, to be watching over their home, to be kind, respecting the authority of their husbands, so that no one will speak badly of God’s message.'),
(998402,34,56,2,6,'In the same way with the younger men – encourage them to be self-controlled.'),
(998403,34,56,2,7,'In all things, set an example of doing good. In your teaching, show integrity and seriousness –'),
(998404,34,56,2,8,'let the instruction that you give be sound and above reproach, so that those who oppose you may be ashamed when they fail to find anything bad to say about us.'),
(998405,34,56,2,9,'Tell slaves to respect their owner’s authority in all circumstances, and to try their best to please them.'),
(998406,34,56,2,10,'Teach them not to contradict or to pilfer, but to show such praiseworthy fidelity in everything, as to recommend the teaching about God our Saviour by all that they do.'),
(998407,34,56,2,11,'For the loving kindness of God has been revealed, bringing salvation for all,'),
(998408,34,56,2,12,'leading us to renounce ungodliness and worldly desires, and to live self-controlled, upright, and godly lives here in this present age,'),
(998409,34,56,2,13,'while awaiting our blessed hope – the appearing in glory of our great God and Saviour, Christ Jesus.'),
(998410,34,56,2,14,'For he gave himself on our behalf, to deliver us from all wickedness, and to purify for himself a people who should be truly his own and eager to do good.'),
(998411,34,56,2,15,'Tell them of all this, and encourage and rebuke with all authority. Do not let anyone belittle you.'),
(998412,34,56,3,1,'Remind them to respect and obey the rulers and authorities, to be ready for every kind of good work, to slander no one, to avoid quarrelling,'),
(998413,34,56,3,2,'to be reasonable, and under all circumstances to show a gentle spirit with all.'),
(998414,34,56,3,3,'There was a time when we ourselves were foolish, disobedient, misled, enslaved to all kinds of desires and pleasures, living in malice and envy, hating ourselves and hating one another.'),
(998415,34,56,3,4,'But, when the kindness of God our Saviour and his love for humanity appeared, he saved us,'),
(998416,34,56,3,5,'not as the result of any righteous actions that we had done, but due to his mercy. He saved us though the washing of rebirth and renewal by the power of the Holy Spirit,'),
(998417,34,56,3,6,'which he poured out on us abundantly through Jesus Christ our Saviour –'),
(998418,34,56,3,7,'so that, having been put right with God through his grace, we become heirs to the hope of eternal life.'),
(998419,34,56,3,8,'This saying is trustworthy! And it is on these subjects that I want you to lay special emphasis, so that those who have learned to trust in God may be careful to devote themselves to doing good. Such subjects are excellent in themselves, and of benefit to all.'),
(998420,34,56,3,9,'But have nothing to do with foolish controversies, or with genealogies, or with quarrels, or fights about the Law. They are useless and futile.'),
(998421,34,56,3,10,'If someone is causing divisions among you then, after giving them a second warning, excuse yourself from them.'),
(998422,34,56,3,11,'You can be sure that such a person has forsaken the truth and is in the wrong. They stand self-condemned.'),
(998423,34,56,3,12,'As soon as I send Artemas or Tychicus to you, join me as quickly as possible at Nicopolis, for I have arranged to spend the winter there.'),
(998424,34,56,3,13,'Do your best to help Zenas, the teacher of the Law, and Apollos, on their way, and see that they want for nothing.'),
(998425,34,56,3,14,'Let all our people learn to devote themselves to doing good, so as to meet the most pressing needs, and that their lives may not be unfruitful.'),
(998426,34,56,3,15,'All who are with me here send you their greeting. Give my greeting to our friends in the faith.'),
(998427,34,57,1,1,'From Paul, now a prisoner for Christ Jesus, and from Timothy, a fellow follower of the Lord.'),
(998428,34,57,1,2,'To our dear friend and fellow worker Philemon, to our sister Apphia, to our fellow soldier Archippus; and to the church that meets at Philemon’s house;'),
(998429,34,57,1,3,'may God, our Father, and the Lord Jesus Christ bless you and give you peace.'),
(998430,34,57,1,4,'I always mention you in my prayers and thank God for you,'),
(998431,34,57,1,5,'because I hear of the love and the faith which you show, not only to the Lord Jesus, but also to all his people;'),
(998432,34,57,1,6,'and I pray that your participation in the faith may result in action, as you come to a fuller realisation of everything that is good and Christlike in us.'),
(998433,34,57,1,7,'I have indeed found great joy and encouragement in your love, knowing, as I do, how the hearts of Christ’s People have been cheered, friend, by you.'),
(998434,34,57,1,8,'And so, though my union with Christ enables me, with all confidence, to dictate the course that you should adopt,'),
(998435,34,57,1,9,'yet the claims of love make me prefer to plead with you – yes, even me, Paul, though I am an ambassador for Christ Jesus and, now a prisoner for him as well.'),
(998436,34,57,1,10,'I plead with you for this child of mine, Onesimus, to whom, in my prison, I have become a father.'),
(998437,34,57,1,11,'Once he was of little service to you, but now he has become of great service, not only to you, but to me as well;'),
(998438,34,57,1,12,'and I am sending him back to you with this letter – though it is like tearing out of my heart.'),
(998439,34,57,1,13,'For my own sake I should like to keep him with me, so that, while I am in prison for the good news, he might attend to my wants on your behalf.'),
(998440,34,57,1,14,'But I do not wish to do anything without your consent, because I want your generosity to be voluntary and not, as it were, compulsory.'),
(998441,34,57,1,15,'It may be that he was separated from you for an hour, for this reason, so that you might have him back for ever,'),
(998442,34,57,1,16,'no longer as a slave, but as something better – a dearly loved friend and follower of the Lord, especially dear to me, and how much more so to you, not only as a person, but as your fellow Christian!'),
(998443,34,57,1,17,'If, then, you count me your friend, receive him as you would me.'),
(998444,34,57,1,18,'If he has caused you any loss, or owes you anything, charge it to me.'),
(998445,34,57,1,19,'I, Paul, put my own hand to it – I will repay you myself. I say nothing about your owing me your self.'),
(998446,34,57,1,20,'Yes, friend, let me gain something from you because of your union with the Lord. Cheer my heart by your Christlike spirit.'),
(998447,34,57,1,21,'Even as I write, I have such confidence in your compliance with my wishes, that I am sure that you will do even more than I am asking.'),
(998448,34,57,1,22,'Please also get a lodging ready for me, for I hope that I will be given back to you all in answer to your prayers.'),
(998449,34,57,1,23,'Epaphras, who is my fellow prisoner for Christ Jesus, sends you his greeting;'),
(998450,34,57,1,24,'and Marcus, Aristarchus, Demas, and Luke, my fellow workers, send theirs.'),
(998451,34,57,1,25,'May the blessing of the Lord Jesus Christ rest on your souls.'),
(998452,34,58,1,1,'God, who, of old, at many times and in many ways, spoke to our ancestors, by the prophets,'),
(998453,34,58,1,2,'has in these latter days spoken to us by the Son, whom he appointed the heir of all things, and through whom he made the universe.'),
(998454,34,58,1,3,'For he is the radiance of the glory of God and the expression of his being, upholding all creation by the power of his word; and, when he had made an expiation for the sins of humanity, he took his seat at the right hand of God’s Majesty on high,'),
(998455,34,58,1,4,'having shown himself as much greater than the angels as the name that he has inherited surpasses theirs.'),
(998456,34,58,1,5,'For to which of the angels did God ever say –'),
(998457,34,58,1,6,'And again, when God brought the first-born into the world, he said –'),
(998458,34,58,1,7,'Speaking of the angels, he said –'),
(998459,34,58,1,8,'while of the Son he said –'),
(998460,34,58,1,9,'You love righteousness and hates iniquity;'),
(998461,34,58,1,10,'Again –'),
(998462,34,58,1,11,'They will perish, but you remain;'),
(998463,34,58,1,12,'As a mantle you will fold them up,'),
(998464,34,58,1,13,'To which of the angels has God ever said –'),
(998465,34,58,1,14,'Are not all the angels spirits in the service of God, sent out to minister for the sake of those who are destined to obtain salvation?'),
(998466,34,58,2,1,'Therefore we must give still more heed to what we were taught, so we do not drift away.'),
(998467,34,58,2,2,'For, if the message which was delivered by angels had its authority confirmed, so that every offence against it, or neglect of it, met with a fitting requital,'),
(998468,34,58,2,3,'how can we, of all people, expect to escape, if we disregard so great a salvation? It was the Master who at the outset spoke of this salvation, and its authority was confirmed for us by those who heard him,'),
(998469,34,58,2,4,'while God himself added his testimony to it by signs, and marvels, and many different miracles, as well as by imparting the Holy Spirit as he saw fit.'),
(998470,34,58,2,5,'God has not given to angels the control of that future world of which we are speaking!'),
(998471,34,58,2,6,'No; a writer has declared somewhere –'),
(998472,34,58,2,7,'You have made them, for a while, lower than angels;'),
(998473,34,58,2,8,'you have placed all things beneath their feet.”'),
(998474,34,58,2,9,'What our eyes do see is Jesus, who was made for a while lower than angels, now, because of his sufferings and death, crowned with glory and honour; so that his tasting the bitterness of death should, in God’s loving kindness, be on behalf of all humanity.'),
(998475,34,58,2,10,'It was, indeed, fitting that God, for whom and through whom all things exist, should, when leading many children to glory, make the author of their salvation perfect through suffering.'),
(998476,34,58,2,11,'For he who purifies, and those whom he purifies, all spring from One; and therefore he is not ashamed to call them his brothers and sisters.'),
(998477,34,58,2,12,'He says –'),
(998478,34,58,2,13,'And again –'),
(998479,34,58,2,14,'Therefore, since human nature is the common heritage of the children, Jesus also shared it, in order that by death he might render powerless him whose power lies in death – that is, the devil –'),
(998480,34,58,2,15,'and so might deliver all those who, from fear of death, had all their lives been living in slavery.'),
(998481,34,58,2,16,'It was not, surely, to the help of the angels that Jesus came, but to the help of the descendants of Abraham.'),
(998482,34,58,2,17,'And consequently it was necessary that he should in all points be made like his brothers and sisters, in order that he might prove a merciful as well as a faithful high priest in humanity’s relations with God, for the purpose of expiating the sins of his people.'),
(998483,34,58,2,18,'The fact that he himself suffered under temptation enables him to help those who are tempted.'),
(998484,34,58,3,1,'Therefore, my Christian friends, you who, all alike, have received the call from heaven, fix your attention on Jesus, the apostle and high priest of our religion.'),
(998485,34,58,3,2,'See how faithful he was to the God who appointed him, as Moses was in the whole house of God.'),
(998486,34,58,3,3,'He has been deemed worthy of far higher honour than Moses, just as the founder of the house is held in greater regard than the house itself.'),
(998487,34,58,3,4,'For every house has its founder, and the founder of the universe is God.'),
(998488,34,58,3,5,'While the faithful service of Moses in the whole house of God was that of a servant, whose duty was to bear testimony to a message still to come,'),
(998489,34,58,3,6,'the faithfulness of Christ was that of a son set over the house of God. And we are his house – if only we retain, unshaken to the end, the courage and confidence inspired by our hope.'),
(998490,34,58,3,7,'Therefore, as the Holy Spirit says –'),
(998491,34,58,3,8,'harden not your hearts, as when Israel provoked me'),
(998492,34,58,3,9,'Where your ancestors tried my forbearance,'),
(998493,34,58,3,10,'Therefore I was sorely vexed with that generation,'),
(998494,34,58,3,11,'While in my wrath I swore –'),
(998495,34,58,3,12,'Be careful, friends, that there is never found in anyone of you a wicked and faithless heart, shown by that person separating themselves from the living God.'),
(998496,34,58,3,13,'Rather encourage one another daily – while there is a today – to prevent anyone among you from being hardened by the deceitfulness of sin.'),
(998497,34,58,3,14,'For we now all share in the Christ, if indeed we retain, unshaken to the end, the confidence that we had at the first.'),
(998498,34,58,3,15,'To use the words of scripture –'),
(998499,34,58,3,16,'Who were they who heard God speak and yet provoked him? Were not they all those who left Egypt under the leadership of Moses?'),
(998500,34,58,3,17,'And with whom was it that God was sorely vexed for forty years? Was not it with those who had sinned, and who fell dead in the desert?');
INSERT INTO verses (id, version_id, book_id, chapter, verse, text) VALUES
(998501,34,58,3,18,'And who were they to whom God swore that they should not enter upon his rest, if not those who had proved faithless?'),
(998502,34,58,3,19,'We see, then, that they failed to enter upon it because of their want of faith.'),
(998503,34,58,4,1,'We must, therefore, be very careful, though there is a promise still standing that we will enter upon God’s rest, that none of you even appear to have missed it.'),
(998504,34,58,4,2,'For we have had the good news told us just as they had. But the message which they heard did them no good, since they did not share the faith of those who were attentive to it.'),
(998505,34,58,4,3,'Upon that rest we who have believed are now entering. As God has said –'),
(998506,34,58,4,4,'for, in a passage referring to the seventh day, you will find these words –'),
(998507,34,58,4,5,'On the other hand, we read in that passage –'),
(998508,34,58,4,6,'Since, then, there is still a promise that some will enter upon this rest, and since those who were first told the good news did not enter upon it, because of their disbelief,'),
(998509,34,58,4,7,'again God fixed a day. “Today,” he said, speaking after a long interval through the mouth of David, in the passage already quoted –'),
(998510,34,58,4,8,'Now if Joshua had given “rest” to the people, God would not have spoken of another and later day.'),
(998511,34,58,4,9,'There is, then, a Sabbath rest still awaiting God’s people.'),
(998512,34,58,4,10,'For the person who enters upon God’s rest do themselves rest after their work, just as God did.'),
(998513,34,58,4,11,'Let us, therefore, make every effort to enter upon that rest, so that none of us fall through such disbelief as that of which we have had an example.'),
(998514,34,58,4,12,'God’s message is a living and active power, sharper than any two-edged sword, piercing its way until it penetrates soul and spirit – not the joints only but the marrow – and detecting the inmost thoughts and purposes of the mind.'),
(998515,34,58,4,13,'There is no created thing that can hide itself from the sight of God. Everything is exposed and laid bare before the eyes of him to whom we have to give account.'),
(998516,34,58,4,14,'We have, then, in Jesus, the Son of God, a great high priest who has passed into the highest heaven; let us, therefore, hold fast to the faith which we have professed.'),
(998517,34,58,4,15,'Our high priest is not one unable to sympathise with our weaknesses, but one who has in every way been tempted, exactly as we have been, but without sinning.'),
(998518,34,58,4,16,'Therefore, let us draw near boldly to the throne of love, to find pity and love for the hour of need.'),
(998519,34,58,5,1,'Every high priest, taken from among the people, is appointed as their representative in their relations with God, to offer both gifts and sacrifices in expiation of sins.'),
(998520,34,58,5,2,'And he is able to sympathise with the ignorant and deluded, since he is himself subject to weakness,'),
(998521,34,58,5,3,'and is therefore bound to offer sacrifices for sins, not only for the people, but equally so for himself.'),
(998522,34,58,5,4,'Nor does anyone take that high office on themselves, until they have been called to do so by God, as Aaron was.'),
(998523,34,58,5,5,'In the same way, even the Christ did not take the honour of the high priesthood on himself, but he was appointed by him who said to him –'),
(998524,34,58,5,6,'and on another occasion also –'),
(998525,34,58,5,7,'Jesus, in the days of his earthly life, offered prayers and supplications, with earnest cries and with tears, to him who was able to save him from death; and he was heard because of his devout submission.'),
(998526,34,58,5,8,'Son though he was, he learned obedience from his sufferings;'),
(998527,34,58,5,9,'and, being made perfect, he became to all those who obey him the source of eternal salvation,'),
(998528,34,58,5,10,'while God himself pronounced him a high priest of the order of Melchizedek.'),
(998529,34,58,5,11,'Now on this subject I have much to say, but it is difficult to explain it to you, because you have shown yourselves so slow to learn.'),
(998530,34,58,5,12,'For whereas, considering the time that has elapsed, you ought to be teaching others, you still need someone to teach you the alphabet of the divine revelation, and need again to be fed with milk instead of with “solid food.”'),
(998531,34,58,5,13,'For everyone who still has to take milk knows nothing of the teaching of righteousness; they are a mere infant.'),
(998532,34,58,5,14,'But solid food is for Christians of mature faith – those whose faculties have been trained by practice to distinguish right from wrong.'),
(998533,34,58,6,1,'Therefore, let us leave behind the elementary teaching about the Christ and press on to perfection, not always laying over again a foundation of repentance for a lifeless formality, of faith in God –'),
(998534,34,58,6,2,'teaching concerning baptisms and the laying on of hands, the resurrection of the dead and a final judgment.'),
(998535,34,58,6,3,'Yes and, with God’s help, we will.'),
(998536,34,58,6,4,'For if those who were once for all brought into the light, and learned to appreciate the gift from heaven, and came to share in the Holy Spirit,'),
(998537,34,58,6,5,'and learned to appreciate the beauty of the divine message, and the new powers of the coming age –'),
(998538,34,58,6,6,'if those, I say, fell away, it would be impossible to bring them again to repentance; they would be crucifying the Son of God over again for themselves, and exposing him to open contempt.'),
(998539,34,58,6,7,'Ground that drinks in the showers that from time to time fall on it, and produces vegetation useful to those for whom it is tilled, receives a blessing from God;'),
(998540,34,58,6,8,'but, if it bears thorns and thistles, it is regarded as worthless, it is in danger of being cursed, and its end will be the fire.'),
(998541,34,58,6,9,'But about you, dear friends, even though we speak in this way, we are confident of better things – of things that point to your salvation.'),
(998542,34,58,6,10,'For God is not unjust; he will not forget the work that you did, and the love that you showed for his name, in sending help to your fellow Christians – as you are still doing.'),
(998543,34,58,6,11,'But our great desire is that every one of you should be equally earnest to attain to a full conviction that our hope will be fulfilled, and that you should keep that hope to the end.'),
(998544,34,58,6,12,'Then you will not show yourselves slow to learn, but you will copy those who, through faith and patience, are now entering upon the enjoyment of God’s promises.'),
(998545,34,58,6,13,'When God gave his promise to Abraham, since there was no one greater by whom he could swear, he swore by himself.'),
(998546,34,58,6,14,'His words were –'),
(998547,34,58,6,15,'And so, after patiently waiting, Abraham obtained the fulfilment of God’s promise.'),
(998548,34,58,6,16,'People, of course, swear by what is greater than themselves, and with them an oath is accepted as putting a matter beyond all dispute.'),
(998549,34,58,6,17,'And therefore God, in his desire to show, with unmistakable plainness, to those who were to enter on the enjoyment of what he had promised, the unchangeableness of his purpose, bound himself with an oath.'),
(998550,34,58,6,18,'For he intended us to find great encouragement in these two unchangeable things, which make it impossible for God to prove false – we, I mean, who fled for safety where we might lay hold on the hope set before us.'),
(998551,34,58,6,19,'This hope is an anchor for our souls, secure and strong, and it reaches into the sanctuary that lies behind the curtain,'),
(998552,34,58,6,20,'where Jesus, our forerunner, has entered on our behalf, after being made for all time a high priest of the order of Melchizedek.'),
(998553,34,58,7,1,'It was this Melchizedek, king of Salem and priest of the Most High God, who met Abraham returning from the slaughter of the kings, and gave him his blessing;'),
(998554,34,58,7,2,'and it was to him that Abraham allotted a tithe of all the spoil. The meaning of his name is “king of righteousness,” and besides that, he was also king of Salem, which means “king of peace.”'),
(998555,34,58,7,3,'There is no record of his father, or mother, or lineage, nor again of any beginning of his days, or end of his life. In this he resembles the Son of God, and stands before us as a priest whose priesthood is continuous.'),
(998556,34,58,7,4,'Consider, then the importance of this Melchizedek, to whom even the patriarch Abraham himself gave a tithe of the choicest spoils.'),
(998557,34,58,7,5,'Those descendants of Levi, who are from time to time appointed to the priesthood, are directed to collect tithes from the people in accordance with the Law – that is from their own kindred, although they also are descended from Abraham.'),
(998558,34,58,7,6,'But Melchizedek, although not of this lineage, received tithes from Abraham, and gave his blessing to the man who had God’s promises.'),
(998559,34,58,7,7,'Now no one can dispute that it is the superior who blesses the inferior.'),
(998560,34,58,7,8,'In the one case the tithes are received by people who are mortal; in the other case by one about whom there is the statement that his life still continues.'),
(998561,34,58,7,9,'Moreover, in a sense, even Levi, who is the receiver of the tithes, has, through Abraham, paid tithes;'),
(998562,34,58,7,10,'for Levi was still in the body of his ancestor when Melchizedek met Abraham.'),
(998563,34,58,7,11,'If, then, perfection had been attainable through the Levitical priesthood – and it was under this priesthood that the people received the Law – why was it still necessary that a priest of a different order should appear, a priest of the order of Melchizedek and not of the order of Aaron?'),
(998564,34,58,7,12,'With the change of the priesthood a change of the Law became a necessity.'),
(998565,34,58,7,13,'And he of whom all this is said belonged to quite a different tribe, no member of which has ever served at the altar.'),
(998566,34,58,7,14,'For it is plain that our Lord had sprung from the tribe of Judah, though of that tribe Moses said nothing about their being priests.'),
(998567,34,58,7,15,'All this becomes even yet plainer when we remember that a new priest has appeared, resembling Melchizedek,'),
(998568,34,58,7,16,'and that he was appointed, not under a Law regulating only earthly matters, but by virtue of a life beyond the reach of death;'),
(998569,34,58,7,17,'for that is the meaning of the declaration –'),
(998570,34,58,7,18,'On the one hand, we have the abolition of a previous regulation as being both inefficient and useless'),
(998571,34,58,7,19,'(for the Law never brought anything to perfection); and, on the other hand, we have the introduction of a better hope, which enables us to draw near to God.'),
(998572,34,58,7,20,'Then again, the appointment of this new priest was ratified by an oath, which is not so with the Levitical priests,'),
(998573,34,58,7,21,'but his appointment was ratified by an oath, when God said to him –'),
(998574,34,58,7,22,'And the oath shows the corresponding superiority of the covenant of which Jesus is appointed the surety.'),
(998575,34,58,7,23,'Again, new Levitical priests are continually being appointed, because death prevents their remaining in office;'),
(998576,34,58,7,24,'but Jesus remains for all time, and therefore the priesthood that he holds will never pass to another.'),
(998577,34,58,7,25,'And that is why he is able to save perfectly those who come to God through him, living for ever, as he does, to intercede of their behalf.'),
(998578,34,58,7,26,'This was the high priest that we needed – holy, innocent, spotless, withdrawn from sinners, exalted above the highest heaven,'),
(998579,34,58,7,27,'one who has no need to offer sacrifices daily as those high priests have, first for their own sins, and then for those of the people. For this he did once and for all, when he offered himself as the sacrifice.'),
(998580,34,58,7,28,'The Law appoints as high priests men who are weak, but the words of God’s oath, which was later than the Law, name the Son as, for all time, the perfect priest.'),
(998581,34,58,8,1,'To sum up what I have been saying: Such is the high priest that we have, one who has taken his seat at the right hand of the throne of God’s Majesty in heaven,'),
(998582,34,58,8,2,'where he serves in the sanctuary, in that true tent set up by the Lord and not by man.'),
(998583,34,58,8,3,'Every high priest is appointed for the purpose of offering gifts and sacrifices to God; it follows, therefore, that this high priest must have some offering to make.'),
(998584,34,58,8,4,'If he were, however, still on earth, he would not even be a priest, since there are already priests who offer the gifts as the Law directs.'),
(998585,34,58,8,5,'(These priests, it is true, are engaged in a service which is only a copy and shadow of the heavenly realities, as is shown by the directions given to Moses when he was about to construct the tent. “Look to it,” are the words, “that you make every part in accordance with the pattern shown you on the mountain.”)'),
(998586,34,58,8,6,'But Jesus, as we see, has obtained a ministry as far excelling theirs, as the covenant of which he is the intermediary, based, as it is, on better promises, excels the former covenant.'),
(998587,34,58,8,7,'If that first covenant had been faultless, there would have been no occasion for a second.'),
(998588,34,58,8,8,'But, finding fault with the people, God says –'),
(998589,34,58,8,9,'Not such a covenant as I made with their ancestors'),
(998590,34,58,8,10,'‘This is the covenant that I will make with the people of Israel'),
(998591,34,58,8,11,'There will be no need for anyone to instruct their fellow citizen,'),
(998592,34,58,8,12,'For I will be merciful to their wrong-doings,'),
(998593,34,58,8,13,'By speaking of a new covenant, God at once renders the former covenant obsolete; and whatever becomes obsolete and loses its force is virtually annulled.'),
(998594,34,58,9,1,'It is true that even the first covenant had its regulations for divine worship, and its sanctuary – though only a material one.'),
(998595,34,58,9,2,'For a tent was constructed, with an outer part which contained the stand for the lamps, and the table, and the consecrated bread. This is called the sanctuary.'),
(998596,34,58,9,3,'The part of the tent behind the second curtain is called the inner sanctuary.'),
(998597,34,58,9,4,'In it is the gold incense-altar, and the ark containing the covenant, completely covered with gold. In the ark is a gold casket containing the manna, Aaron’s rod that budded, and the tablets on which the covenant was written;'),
(998598,34,58,9,5,'while above it, and overshadowing the cover on which atonement was made, are the cherubim of the presence. Now is not the time to discuss these things in detail.'),
(998599,34,58,9,6,'Such, then, was the arrangement of the tent. Into the outer part priests are constantly going, in the discharge of their sacred duties;'),
(998600,34,58,9,7,'but into the inner only the high priest goes, and that but once a year, and never without taking the blood of a victim, which he offers on his own behalf, and on behalf of the errors of the people.'),
(998601,34,58,9,8,'By this the Holy Spirit is teaching that the way into the sanctuary was hidden, as long as the outer part of the tent still remained.'),
(998602,34,58,9,9,'For that was only a type, to continue down to the present time; and, in keeping with it, both gifts and sacrifices are offered, though incapable of satisfying the conscience of the worshiper;'),
(998603,34,58,9,10,'the whole system being concerned only with food and drink and various ablutions – external ceremonials imposed until the coming of the new order.'),
(998604,34,58,9,11,'But, when Christ came, he appeared as high priest of that better system which was established; and he entered through that nobler and more perfect tent, not made by human hands – that is to say, not a part of this present creation.'),
(998605,34,58,9,12,'Nor was it with the blood of goats and calves, but with his own blood, that he entered, once and for all, into the sanctuary, and obtained our eternal deliverance.'),
(998606,34,58,9,13,'For, if the blood of goats and bulls, and the sprinkling of the ashes of a heifer, purify those who have been defiled (as far as ceremonial purification goes),'),
(998607,34,58,9,14,'how much more will the blood of the Christ, who, through his eternal Spirit, offered himself up to God, as a victim without blemish, purify our consciences from a lifeless formality, and fit us for the service of the living God!'),
(998608,34,58,9,15,'And that is why he is the intermediary of a new covenant; in order that, as a death has taken place to effect a deliverance from the offences committed under the first covenant, those who have received the call may obtain the eternal inheritance promised to them.'),
(998609,34,58,9,16,'Whenever such a covenant as a will is in question, the death of the testator must of necessity be alleged.'),
(998610,34,58,9,17,'For such a covenant takes effect only on death, it does not come into force as long as the testator is alive.'),
(998611,34,58,9,18,'This explains why even the first covenant was not ratified without the shedding of blood.'),
(998612,34,58,9,19,'For, when every command had been announced to all the people by Moses in accordance with the Law, he took the blood of the calves and of the goats, with water, scarlet wool, and a bunch of hyssop, and sprinkled even the book of the Law, as well as all the people,'),
(998613,34,58,9,20,'saying, as he did so – ‘This is the blood that renders valid the covenant which God has commanded to be made with you.’'),
(998614,34,58,9,21,'And in the same way he also sprinkled with the blood the tent and all the things that were used in public worship.'),
(998615,34,58,9,22,'Indeed, under the Law, almost everything is purified with blood; and, unless blood is shed, no forgiveness is to be obtained.'),
(998616,34,58,9,23,'While, then, it was necessary for the copies of the heavenly realities to be purified by such means as these, the heavenly realities themselves required better sacrifices.'),
(998617,34,58,9,24,'For it was not into a sanctuary made by human hands, which merely foreshadowed the true one, that Christ entered, but into heaven itself, so that he might now appear in the presence of God on our behalf.'),
(998618,34,58,9,25,'Nor yet was it to offer himself may times, as year after year the high priest entered the sanctuary with an offering of blood – but not his own blood;'),
(998619,34,58,9,26,'for then Christ would have had to undergo death many times since the creation of the world. But now, once and for all, at the close of the age, he has appeared, in order to abolish sin by the sacrifice of himself.'),
(998620,34,58,9,27,'And, as it is ordained for people to die but once (death being followed by judgment),'),
(998621,34,58,9,28,'so it is with the Christ. He was offered up once and for all, to bear away the sins of many; and the second time he will appear – but without any burden of sin – to those who are waiting for him, to bring salvation.'),
(998622,34,58,10,1,'The Law, though able to foreshadow the better system which was coming, never had its actual substance. Its priests, with those sacrifices which they offer continuously year after year, can never make those who come to worship perfect.'),
(998623,34,58,10,2,'Otherwise, would not the offering of these sacrifices have been abandoned, as the worshipers, having been once purified, would have had their consciences clear from sins?'),
(998624,34,58,10,3,'But, on the contrary, these sacrifices recall their sins to mind year after year.'),
(998625,34,58,10,4,'For the blood of bulls and goats is powerless to remove sins.'),
(998626,34,58,10,5,'That is why, when he was coming into the world, the Christ declared –'),
(998627,34,58,10,6,'You take no pleasure in burnt offerings and sacrifices for sin.'),
(998628,34,58,10,7,'So I said, ‘See, I have come’ (as is written of me in the pages of the book),'),
(998629,34,58,10,8,'First come the words – “You do not desire, nor do you take pleasure in, sacrifices, offerings, burnt offerings, and sacrifices for sin” (offerings regularly made under the Law),'),
(998630,34,58,10,9,'and then there is added – “See, I have come to do your will.” The former sacrifices are set aside to be replaced by the latter.'),
(998631,34,58,10,10,'And it is in the fulfilment of the will of God that we have been purified by the sacrifice, once and for all, of the body of Jesus Christ.'),
(998632,34,58,10,11,'Every other priest stands day after day at his ministrations, and offers the same sacrifices over and over again – sacrifices that can never take sins away.'),
(998633,34,58,10,12,'But, this priest, after he had offered one sacrifice for sins, which should serve for all time, “took his seat at the right hand of God,”'),
(998634,34,58,10,13,'and has since then been waiting “for his enemies to be put as a stool for his feet.”'),
(998635,34,58,10,14,'By a single offering he has made perfect for all time those who are being purified.'),
(998636,34,58,10,15,'We have also the testimony of the Holy Spirit. For, after saying –'),
(998637,34,58,10,16,'“‘This is the covenant that I will make with them'),
(998638,34,58,10,17,'then we have –'),
(998639,34,58,10,18,'And, when these are forgiven, there is no further need of an offering for sin.'),
(998640,34,58,10,19,'Therefore, friends, since we may enter the sanctuary with confidence, in virtue of the blood of Jesus,'),
(998641,34,58,10,20,'by the way which he inaugurated for us – a new and living way, a way through the sanctuary curtain (that is, his human nature);'),
(998642,34,58,10,21,'and, since we have in him “a great priest set over the house of God,”'),
(998643,34,58,10,22,'let us draw near to God in all sincerity of heart and in perfect faith, with our hearts purified by the sprinkled blood from all consciousness of wrong, and with our bodies washed with pure water.'),
(998644,34,58,10,23,'Let us maintain the confession of our hope unshaken, for he who has given us his promise will not fail us.'),
(998645,34,58,10,24,'Let us vie with one another in a rivalry of love and noble actions.'),
(998646,34,58,10,25,'And let us not, as some do, cease to meet together; but, on the contrary, let us encourage one another, and all the more, now that you see the day drawing near.'),
(998647,34,58,10,26,'Remember, if we sin wilfully after we have gained a full knowledge of the truth, there can be no further sacrifice for sin;'),
(998648,34,58,10,27,'there is only a fearful anticipation of judgment, and a burning indignation which will destroy all opponents.'),
(998649,34,58,10,28,'When someone disregarded the Law of Moses, they were, on the evidence of two or three witnesses, put to death without pity.'),
(998650,34,58,10,29,'How much worse then, think you, will be the punishment deserved by those who have trampled underfoot the Son of God, who have treated the blood that rendered the covenant valid – the blood by which they were purified – as if it were not holy, and who have outraged the Spirit of love?'),
(998651,34,58,10,30,'We know who it was that said –'),
(998652,34,58,10,31,'It is a fearful thing to fall into the hands of the living God.'),
(998653,34,58,10,32,'Call to mind those early days in which, after you had received the light, you patiently underwent a long and painful conflict.'),
(998654,34,58,10,33,'Sometimes, in consequence of the taunts and injuries heaped on you, you became a public spectacle; and sometimes you suffered through having shown yourselves to be the friends of people who were in the same position in which you had been.'),
(998655,34,58,10,34,'For you not only sympathised with those who were in prison, but you even took the confiscation of your possessions joyfully, knowing, as you did, that you had in yourselves a greater possession and a lasting one.'),
(998656,34,58,10,35,'Do not, therefore, abandon the confidence that you have gained, for it has a great reward awaiting it.'),
(998657,34,58,10,36,'You still have need of patient endurance, in order that, when you have done God’s will, you may obtain the fulfilment of his promise.'),
(998658,34,58,10,37,'“For there is indeed but a very little while'),
(998659,34,58,10,38,'and through faith the righteous will find life,'),
(998660,34,58,10,39,'But we do not belong to those who draw back, to their ruin, but to those who have faith, to the saving of their souls.'),
(998661,34,58,11,1,'Faith is the realisation of things hoped for – the proof of things not seen.'),
(998662,34,58,11,2,'And it was for faith that the people of old were renowned.'),
(998663,34,58,11,3,'Faith enables us to perceive that the universe was created at the bidding of God – so that we know that what we see was not made out of visible things.'),
(998664,34,58,11,4,'Faith made the sacrifice which Abel offered to God a better sacrifice than Cain’s, and won him renown as a righteous man, God himself establishing his renown by accepting his gifts; and it is by the example of his faith that Abel, though dead, still speaks.'),
(998665,34,58,11,5,'Faith led to Enoch’s removal from earth, so that he might not experience death. “He could not be found because God had removed him.” For, before his removal, he was renowned as having pleased God;'),
(998666,34,58,11,6,'but without faith it is impossible to please him, for he who comes to God must believe that God exists, and that he rewards those who seek for him.'),
(998667,34,58,11,7,'It was faith that enabled Noah, after he had received the divine warning about what could not then be foreseen, to build, in reverent obedience, an ark in which to save his family. By his faith he condemned the world, and became possessed of that righteousness which follows on faith.'),
(998668,34,58,11,8,'It was faith that enabled Abraham to obey the call that he received, and to set out for the place which he was afterwards to obtain as his own; and he set out not knowing where he was going.'),
(998669,34,58,11,9,'It was faith that made him go to live as an emigrant in the promised land – as in a strange country – living there in tents with Isaac and Jacob, who shared the promise with him.'),
(998670,34,58,11,10,'For he was looking for the city with the sure foundations, whose architect and builder is God.'),
(998671,34,58,11,11,'Again, it was faith that enabled Sarah to conceive (though she was past the age for child-bearing), because she felt sure that he who had given her the promise would not fail her.'),
(998672,34,58,11,12,'And so from one man – and that when his powers were dead – there sprang a people as numerous “as the stars in the heavens or the countless grains of sand on the shore.”'),
(998673,34,58,11,13,'All these died sustained by faith. They did not obtain the promised blessings, but they saw them from a distance and welcomed the sight, and they acknowledged themselves to be only aliens and strangers on the earth.'),
(998674,34,58,11,14,'Those who speak like this show plainly that they are seeking their homeland.'),
(998675,34,58,11,15,'If they had been thinking of the land that they had left, they could have found opportunities to return.'),
(998676,34,58,11,16,'But no, they were longing for a better, a heavenly, land! And therefore God was not ashamed to be called their God; indeed he had already prepared them a city.'),
(998677,34,58,11,17,'It was faith that enabled Abraham, when put to the test, to offer Isaac as a sacrifice – he who had received the promises offering up his only son,'),
(998678,34,58,11,18,'of whom it had been said –'),
(998679,34,58,11,19,'For he argued that God was even able to raise a man from the dead – and indeed, figuratively speaking, Abraham did receive Isaac back from the dead.'),
(998680,34,58,11,20,'It was faith that enabled Isaac to bless Jacob and Esau, even with regard to the future.'),
(998681,34,58,11,21,'Faith enabled Jacob, when dying, to give his blessing to each of the sons of Joseph, and “to bow himself in worship as he leant on the top of his staff.”'),
(998682,34,58,11,22,'Faith caused Joseph, when his end was near, to speak of the future migration of the Israelites, and to give instructions with regard to his bones.'),
(998683,34,58,11,23,'Faith caused the parents of Moses to hide the child for three months after his birth, for they saw that he was a beautiful child; and they would not respect the king’s order.'),
(998684,34,58,11,24,'It was faith that caused Moses, when he was grown up, to refuse the title of “son of a daughter of Pharaoh.”'),
(998685,34,58,11,25,'He preferred sharing the hardships of God’s people to enjoying the short-lived pleasures of sin.'),
(998686,34,58,11,26,'For he counted “the reproaches that are heaped on the Christ” of greater value than the treasures of Egypt, looking forward, as he did, to the reward awaiting him.'),
(998687,34,58,11,27,'Faith caused him to leave Egypt, though undaunted by the king’s anger, for he was strengthened in his endurance by the vision of the invisible God.'),
(998688,34,58,11,28,'Faith led him to institute the Passover and the sprinkling of the blood, so that the Destroyer might not touch the eldest children of the Israelites.'),
(998689,34,58,11,29,'Faith enabled the people to cross the Red Sea, as if it had been dry land, while the Egyptians, when they attempted to do so, were drowned.'),
(998690,34,58,11,30,'Faith caused the walls of Jericho to fall after being encircled for seven days.'),
(998691,34,58,11,31,'Faith saved Rahab, the prostitute, from perishing with the unbelievers, after she had entertained the spies with friendliness.'),
(998692,34,58,11,32,'Need I add anything more? Time would fail me if I attempted to relate the stories of Gideon, Barak, Samson, and Jephthah, and those of David, Samuel, and the prophets.'),
(998693,34,58,11,33,'By their faith they subdued kingdoms, ruled righteously, gained the fulfilment of God’s promises, shut the mouths of lions,'),
(998694,34,58,11,34,'quelled the fury of the flames, escaped the edge of the sword, found strength in the hour of weakness, displayed their prowess in war, and routed hostile armies.'),
(998695,34,58,11,35,'Women received back their dead raised to life. Some were tortured on the wheel, and refused release in order that they might rise to a better life.'),
(998696,34,58,11,36,'Others had to face taunts and blows, and even chains and imprisonment.'),
(998697,34,58,11,37,'They were stoned to death, they were tortured, they were swan asunder, they were put to the sword; they wandered about clothed in the skins of sheep or goats, destitute, persecuted, ill-used –'),
(998698,34,58,11,38,'people of whom the world was not worthy – roaming in lonely places, and on the mountains, and in caves and holes in the ground.'),
(998699,34,58,11,39,'Yet, though they all won renown by their faith, they did not obtain the final fulfilment of God’s promise;'),
(998700,34,58,11,40,'since God had in view some better thing for us, so that they would only reach perfection together with us.'),
(998701,34,58,12,1,'Seeing, therefore, that there is on every side of us such a throng of witnesses, let us also lay aside everything that hinders us, and the sin that clings about us, and run with patient endurance the race that lies before us,'),
(998702,34,58,12,2,'our eyes fixed on Jesus, the leader and perfect example of our faith, who, for the joy that lay before him, endured the cross, heedless of its shame, and now “has taken his seat at the right hand” of the throne of God.'),
(998703,34,58,12,3,'Weigh well the example of him who had to endure such opposition from “people who were sinning against themselves,” so that you should not grow weary or faint-hearted.'),
(998704,34,58,12,4,'You have not yet, in your struggle with sin, resisted to the death;'),
(998705,34,58,12,5,'and you have forgotten the encouraging words which are addressed to you as God’s children –'),
(998706,34,58,12,6,'For it is him whom he loves that he disciplines,'),
(998707,34,58,12,7,'It is for your discipline that you have to endure all this. God is dealing with you as his children. For where is there a child whom his father does not discipline?'),
(998708,34,58,12,8,'If you are left without that discipline, in which all children share, it shows that you are bastards, and not true children.'),
(998709,34,58,12,9,'Further, when our earthly fathers disciplined us, we respected them. Should we not, then, much rather yield submission to the Father of souls, and live?'),
(998710,34,58,12,10,'Our fathers disciplined us for only a short time and as seemed best to them; but God disciplines us for our true good, to enable us to share his holiness.'),
(998711,34,58,12,11,'No discipline is pleasant at the time; on the contrary, it is painful. But afterwards its fruit is seen in the peacefulness of a righteous life which is the lot of those who have been trained under it.'),
(998712,34,58,12,12,'Therefore “lift again the down-dropped hands and straighten the weakened knees;'),
(998713,34,58,12,13,'make straight paths for your feet,” so that the lame limb may not be put out of joint, but rather be cured.'),
(998714,34,58,12,14,'Try earnestly to live at peace with everyone, and to attain to that purity without which no one will see the Lord.'),
(998715,34,58,12,15,'Take care that no one fails to use the loving help of God, “that no bitterness is allowed to take root and spring up, and cause trouble,” and so poison the whole community.'),
(998716,34,58,12,16,'Take care that no one becomes immoral, or irreligious like Esau, who sold his birthright for a single meal.'),
(998717,34,58,12,17,'For you know that even afterwards, when he wished to claim his father’s blessing, he was rejected – for he never found an opportunity to repair his error – though he begged for the blessing with tears.'),
(998718,34,58,12,18,'It is not to tangible “flaming fire” that you have drawn near, nor to “gloom, and darkness, and storm,'),
(998719,34,58,12,19,'and the blast of a trumpet, and an audible voice.” Those who heard that voice entreated that they might hear no more,'),
(998720,34,58,12,20,'for they could not bear to think of the command – “If even an animal touches the mountain, it is to be stoned to death;”'),
(998721,34,58,12,21,'and so fearful was the sight that Moses said – “I tremble with fear.”'),
(998722,34,58,12,22,'No, but it is to Mount Zion that you have drawn near, the city of the living God, the heavenly Jerusalem, to countless hosts of angels,'),
(998723,34,58,12,23,'to the festal gathering and assemblage of God’s firstborn whose names are enrolled in heaven, to God the judge of all people, to the spirits of the righteous who have attained perfection,'),
(998724,34,58,12,24,'to Jesus, the intermediary of a new covenant, and to the sprinkled blood that tells of better things than the blood of Abel.'),
(998725,34,58,12,25,'Beware how you refuse to hear him who is speaking. For, if the Israelites did not escape punishment, when they refused to listen to him who taught them on earth the divine will, far worse will it be for us, if we turn away from him who is teaching us from heaven.'),
(998726,34,58,12,26,'Then his voice shook the earth, but now his declaration is –'),
(998727,34,58,12,27,'And those words “still once more” indicate the passing away of all that is shaken – that is, of all created things – in order that only what is unshaken may remain.'),
(998728,34,58,12,28,'Therefore, let us, who have received a kingdom that cannot be shaken, be thankful, and so offer acceptable worship to God, with awe and the deepest respect.'),
(998729,34,58,12,29,'For our God is “a consuming fire.”'),
(998730,34,58,13,1,'Let your love for the Lord’s followers continue.'),
(998731,34,58,13,2,'Do not neglect to show hospitality; for, through being hospitable, people have all unawares entertained angels.'),
(998732,34,58,13,3,'Remember the prisoners, as if you were their fellow prisoners, and the oppressed, not forgetting that you also are still in the body.'),
(998733,34,58,13,4,'Let marriage be honoured by all and the married life be pure; for God will judge those who are immoral and those who commit adultery.'),
(998734,34,58,13,5,'Do not let your conduct be ruled by the love of money. Be content with what you have, for God himself has said –'),
(998735,34,58,13,6,'Therefore we may say with confidence –'),
(998736,34,58,13,7,'Do not forget your leaders, who told you God’s message. Recall the close of their lives, and imitate their faith.'),
(998737,34,58,13,8,'Jesus Christ is the same yesterday and today – yes, and for ever!'),
(998738,34,58,13,9,'Do not let yourselves be carried away by the various novel forms of teaching. It is better to rely for spiritual strength on the divine help, than on regulations regarding food; for those whose lives are guided by such regulations have not found them of service.'),
(998739,34,58,13,10,'We are not without an altar; but it is one at which those who still worship in the tent have no right to eat.'),
(998740,34,58,13,11,'The bodies of those animals whose blood is brought by the high priest into the sanctuary, as an offering for sin, are burnt outside the camp.'),
(998741,34,58,13,12,'And so Jesus, also, to purify the people by his own blood, suffered outside the gate.'),
(998742,34,58,13,13,'Therefore let us go out to him “outside the camp,” bearing the same reproaches as he;'),
(998743,34,58,13,14,'for here we have no permanent city, but are looking for the city that is to be.'),
(998744,34,58,13,15,'Through him let us offer, as our sacrifice, continual praise to God – an offering from lips that glorify his name.'),
(998745,34,58,13,16,'Never forget to do kindly acts and to share what you have with others, for such sacrifices are acceptable to God.'),
(998746,34,58,13,17,'Obey your leaders, and submit to their control, for they are watching over your souls, since they will have to render an account, so that they may do it with joy, and not in sorrow. That would not be to your advantage.'),
(998747,34,58,13,18,'Pray for us, for we are sure that our consciences are clear, since our wish is to be occupied with what is good.'),
(998748,34,58,13,19,'And I the more earnestly ask for your prayers, so that I may be restored to you the sooner.'),
(998749,34,58,13,20,'May God, the source of all peace, who brought back from the dead him who, “by virtue of the blood that rendered valid the unchangeable covenant, is the great shepherd of God’s Sheep,” Jesus, our Lord –'),
(998750,34,58,13,21,'may God make you perfect in everything that is good, so that you may be able to do his will. May he bring out in us all that is pleasing in his sight, through Jesus Christ, to whom be all glory for ever and ever. Amen.'),
(998751,34,58,13,22,'I beg you, friends, to bear with these words of advice. For I have written only very briefly to you.'),
(998752,34,58,13,23,'You will be glad to hear that our friend, Timothy, has been set free. If he comes here soon, we will visit you together.'),
(998753,34,58,13,24,'Give our greeting to all your leaders, and to all Christ’s people. Our friends from Italy send their greetings to you.'),
(998754,34,58,13,25,'May God bless you all.'),
(998755,34,59,1,1,'James, a servant of God and of the Lord Jesus Christ, greets the twelve tribes that are living abroad.'),
(998756,34,59,1,2,'My friends, whatever trials you may face from time to time, always regard them as a reason for rejoicing,'),
(998757,34,59,1,3,'knowing, as you do, that the testing of your faith develops endurance.'),
(998758,34,59,1,4,'And let endurance do its work perfectly, so that you may be altogether perfect, and in no respect lacking.'),
(998759,34,59,1,5,'If any one of you lacks wisdom, they should ask wisdom from the God who gives freely to everyone without reproach, and it will be given to them.'),
(998760,34,59,1,6,'But they should ask with confidence, never doubting; for the person who doubts is like a wave of the sea driven here and there at the mercy of the wind –'),
(998761,34,59,1,7,'Such a person must not expect that they will receive anything from the Lord,'),
(998762,34,59,1,8,'vacillating as they are, irresolute at every turn.'),
(998763,34,59,1,9,'Let a follower in humble circumstances be proud of their exalted position,'),
(998764,34,59,1,10,'but a rich follower of their humiliation; for the rich will pass away like a wild flower.'),
(998765,34,59,1,11,'As the sun rises, and the hot wind blows, the plant withers, its flower fades, and all its beauty is gone. So is it with the rich. In the midst of their pursuits they will wither away.'),
(998766,34,59,1,12,'Blessed is the person who remains firm under temptation, for, when they have stood the test, they will receive the crown of life, which the Lord has promised to those who love him.'),
(998767,34,59,1,13,'Let no one say, when they are tempted, ‘It is God who is tempting me!’ For God, who cannot be tempted to do wrong, does not himself tempt anyone.'),
(998768,34,59,1,14,'A man is in every case tempted by their own passions – allured and enticed by them.'),
(998769,34,59,1,15,'Then passion conceives and gives birth to sin, and sin, on reaching maturity, brings forth death.'),
(998770,34,59,1,16,'Do not be deceived, my dear friends.'),
(998771,34,59,1,17,'Every good thing given us, and every perfect gift, is from above, and comes down to us from the Father of the lights in the heavens, who is himself never subject to change or to eclipse.'),
(998772,34,59,1,18,'Because he so willed, he gave us life, through the message of the truth, so that we should be, as it were, a kind of first fruits of his creation.'),
(998773,34,59,1,19,'Mark this, my dear friends – Let everyone be quick to listen, slow to speak, and slow to get angry;'),
(998774,34,59,1,20,'for human anger does not forward the righteous purpose of God.'),
(998775,34,59,1,21,'Therefore, get rid of all filthiness and whatever wickedness still remains, and in a humble spirit receive that message which has been planted in your hearts and is able to save your souls.'),
(998776,34,59,1,22,'Put that message into practice, and do not merely listen to it – deceiving yourselves.'),
(998777,34,59,1,23,'For, when anyone listens to it and does not practice it, they are like a person looking at their own face in a mirror.'),
(998778,34,59,1,24,'They look at themselves, then go on their way,'),
(998779,34,59,1,25,'but the person who looks carefully into the perfect Law, the Law of freedom, and continues to do so, not listening to it and then forgetting it, but putting it into practice – that person will be blessed in what they do.'),
(998780,34,59,1,26,'When a person appears to be religious, yet does not bridle their tongue, but imposes on their own conscience, that person’s religious observances are valueless.'),
(998781,34,59,1,27,'That religious observance which is pure and spotless in the eyes of God our Father is this – to visit orphans and widows in their trouble, and to keep oneself uncontaminated by the world.'),
(998782,34,59,2,1,'My friends, are you really trying to combine faith in Jesus Christ, our glorified Lord, with discrimination?'),
(998783,34,59,2,2,'Suppose a visitor should enter your synagogue, with gold rings and in grand clothes, and suppose a poor man should come in also, in shabby clothes,'),
(998784,34,59,2,3,'and you show more respect to the visitor who is wearing grand clothes, and say – ‘There is a good seat for you here,’ but to the poor man – ‘You must stand; or sit down there by my footstool,’'),
(998785,34,59,2,4,'Haven’t you made distinctions among yourselves, and used evil standards of judgement?'),
(998786,34,59,2,5,'Listen, my dear friends. Has not God chosen those who are poor in the things of this world to be rich through their faith, and to possess the kingdom which he has promised to those who love him?'),
(998787,34,59,2,6,'But you – you insult the poor man! Isn’t it the rich who oppress you? Isn’t it they who drag you into law courts?'),
(998788,34,59,2,7,'Isn’t it they who malign that honourable name spoken over you at your baptism?'),
(998789,34,59,2,8,'If you keep the royal law which runs – “You must love your neighbour as you love yourself,” you are doing right;'),
(998790,34,59,2,9,'but, if you discriminate, you commit a sin, and stand convicted by that same law of being offenders against it.'),
(998791,34,59,2,10,'For a person who has laid the Law, as a whole, to heart, but has failed in one particular, is accountable for breaking all its provisions.'),
(998792,34,59,2,11,'He who said “You must not commit adultery” also said “You must not murder.” If, then, you commit murder but not adultery, you are still an offender against the Law.'),
(998793,34,59,2,12,'Therefore, speak and act as people who are to be judged by the “Law of freedom.”'),
(998794,34,59,2,13,'For there will be justice without mercy for the person who has not acted mercifully. Mercy triumphs over Justice.'),
(998795,34,59,2,14,'My friends, what good is it if someone claims that they have faith, but they do not prove it by actions? Can such faith save them?'),
(998796,34,59,2,15,'Suppose some brother or sister should be in need of clothes and of daily bread,'),
(998797,34,59,2,16,'and one of you says to them – ‘Go, and peace be with you; keep warm and eat well!’ and yet you do not actually give them the necessities of life, what good would it be to them?'),
(998798,34,59,2,17,'In just the same way faith, if not followed by actions, is, by itself, a lifeless thing.'),
(998799,34,59,2,18,'Someone, indeed, may say – ‘You are a man of faith, and I am a man of action.’'),
(998800,34,59,2,19,'It is a part of your faith, is it not, that there is one God? Good; yet even the demons have that faith, and tremble at the thought.'),
(998801,34,59,2,20,'Now do you really want to understand, fool, how it is that faith without actions leads to nothing?'),
(998802,34,59,2,21,'Look at our ancestor, Abraham. Was he not justified by his actions after he had offered his son, Isaac, on the altar?'),
(998803,34,59,2,22,'You see how, in his case, faith and actions went together; that his faith was perfected as the result of his actions;'),
(998804,34,59,2,23,'and that in this way the words of scripture came true – ‘Abraham believed God, and that was regarded by God as righteousness,’ and ‘He was called the friend of God.’'),
(998805,34,59,2,24,'You see, then, that a person is justified by actions, and not by faith alone.'),
(998806,34,59,2,25,'Wasn’t it the same with the prostitute, Rahab? Was she not justified by her actions, after she had welcomed the messengers and helped them escape by another road?'),
(998807,34,59,2,26,'Just as a body is dead without a spirit, so faith is dead without actions.'),
(998808,34,59,3,1,'Not many of you should become teachers, my friends, because you know that we who teach will be judged more strictly than others.'),
(998809,34,59,3,2,'We often make mistakes, every one of us. Anyone who does not make mistakes when speaking is indeed a perfect person, able to bridle their whole body as well.'),
(998810,34,59,3,3,'When we put bits into horses’ mouths to make them obey us, we change their course the rest of their bodies.'),
(998811,34,59,3,4,'Again, think of ships. Large as they are, and even when driven by fierce winds, they are guided by a very small rudder and steered in whatever direction the man at the helm may determine.'),
(998812,34,59,3,5,'So is it with the tongue. Small as it is, it is a great boaster. Think how a tiny spark may set the largest forest ablaze!'),
(998813,34,59,3,6,'And the tongue is like a spark. It is a world of unrighteousness among the parts of our body. It contaminates the whole body; it sets the whole course of our existence on fire, and is itself set on fire by the flames of Gehenna.'),
(998814,34,59,3,7,'For while all kinds of animals, birds and reptiles and sea creatures can be tamed and have been tamed by humans,'),
(998815,34,59,3,8,'no human being can tame the tongue. It is a restless plague! It is charged with deadly poison!'),
(998816,34,59,3,9,'With it we bless our Lord and Father, and with it we curse people who are made “in God’s likeness.”'),
(998817,34,59,3,10,'From the very same mouth come blessings and curses! My friends, it is not right that this should be so.'),
(998818,34,59,3,11,'Does a spring give both good and bad water from the same source?'),
(998819,34,59,3,12,'Can a fig tree, my friends, bear olives? Or a vine bear figs? No, nor can a brackish well give good water.'),
(998820,34,59,3,13,'Who among you claims to be wise and intelligent? They should show that their actions are the outcome of a good life lived in the humility of true wisdom.'),
(998821,34,59,3,14,'But if you harbour bitter envy and a spirit of rivalry in your hearts, do not boast or deny the truth.'),
(998822,34,59,3,15,'That is not the wisdom which comes from above; no, it is earthly, animalistic, demonic.'),
(998823,34,59,3,16,'For where envy and rivalry exist, there you will also find disorder and all kinds of bad, worthless actions.'),
(998824,34,59,3,17,'But the wisdom from above is, before everything else, pure; then peace-loving, gentle, open to conviction, rich in compassion and good deeds, and free from partiality and insincerity.'),
(998825,34,59,3,18,'Justice is the harvest peacemakers will reap from seeds sown in a spirit of peace.'),
(998826,34,59,4,1,'What is the cause of the fighting and quarrelling that goes on among you? Isn’t it to be found in the desires which are always at war within you?'),
(998827,34,59,4,2,'You crave, yet do not have, so you commit murder, so You covet, yet cannot gain your end. You quarrel and fight. You do not have, because you do not ask.'),
(998828,34,59,4,3,'You ask, yet do not receive, because you ask for a wrong purpose – to spend what you get on your pleasures.'),
(998829,34,59,4,4,'Unfaithful people! Don’t you know that to be friends with the world means to be at enmity with God? Therefore whoever chooses to be friends with the world makes himself an enemy to God.'),
(998830,34,59,4,5,'Do you suppose scripture means nothing when it says, “Envy results from the longings of the spirit which God has implanted within you?”'),
(998831,34,59,4,6,'But he gives us greater grace; and that is why it says, –'),
(998832,34,59,4,7,'Therefore submit to God. Stand up to the devil, and he will flee from you.'),
(998833,34,59,4,8,'Draw near to God, and he will draw near to you. Make your hands clean, you sinners; and your hearts pure, you vacillators!'),
(998834,34,59,4,9,'Grieve, mourn, and lament! Let your laughter be turned to mourning, and your happiness to gloom!'),
(998835,34,59,4,10,'Humble yourselves before the Lord, and he will exalt you.'),
(998836,34,59,4,11,'Do not disparage one another, friends. The person who disparages others, or passes judgment on them, disparages the Law and passes judgment on the Law. But, if you pass judgment on the Law, you are not obeying it, but judging it.'),
(998837,34,59,4,12,'There is only one lawgiver and judge – he who has the power both to save and to destroy. So then who are you to pass judgment on your neighbour?'),
(998838,34,59,4,13,'Listen to me, you who say “Today or tomorrow we will go to such and such a town and spend a year there, doing business and making money,”'),
(998839,34,59,4,14,'yet you do not know what your life will be like tomorrow! For you are but a puff of smoke that appears for a little while and then vanishes.'),
(998840,34,59,4,15,'Instead you should say “If the Lord wills, we will live and do this or that.”'),
(998841,34,59,4,16,'But as it is, you are boasting presumptuously! All such boasting is wicked.'),
(998842,34,59,4,17,'The person, then, who knows what is right but fails to do it – that is sin in them.'),
(998843,34,59,5,1,'Listen to me, you rich people, weep and wail for the miseries that are coming upon you!'),
(998844,34,59,5,2,'Your riches have wasted away, and your clothes have become moth-eaten.'),
(998845,34,59,5,3,'Your gold and silver are rusted; and the rust on them will be evidence against you, and will eat into your flesh. It was fire, so to speak, that you stored up for yourselves in these last days.'),
(998846,34,59,5,4,'Listen! The wages you have held back from the labourers who mowed your fields are crying out against you, and the outcries of your harvesters have reached the ears of the Lord of Hosts!'),
(998847,34,59,5,5,'You have lived on earth a life of extravagance and luxury; you have indulged your fancies in a time of bloodshed.'),
(998848,34,59,5,6,'You have condemned, you have murdered, the righteous one! Must not God be opposed to you?'),
(998849,34,59,5,7,'Be patient, then, friends, until the coming of the Lord. Even the farmer has to wait for the precious fruit of the earth, watching over it patiently, until it has had the spring and summer rains.'),
(998850,34,59,5,8,'And you must be patient also, and not be discouraged; for the Lord’s coming is near.'),
(998851,34,59,5,9,'Do not make complaints against one another, friends, or judgment will be passed on you. The judge is already standing at the door!'),
(998852,34,59,5,10,'Friends, as an example of the patient endurance of suffering, take the prophets who spoke in the name of the Lord.'),
(998853,34,59,5,11,'We count those who displayed such endurance blessed! You have heard, too, of Job’s endurance, and have seen what the Lord’s purpose was, for “the Lord is full of pity and compassion.”'),
(998854,34,59,5,12,'Above all things, my friends, never take an oath, either by heaven, or by earth, or by anything else. Let your “Yes” suffice for yes, and “No” for no, so that you may escape condemnation.'),
(998855,34,59,5,13,'If anyone of you is in trouble, they should pray; if anyone is happy, they should sing hymns.'),
(998856,34,59,5,14,'If anyone of you is ill, they should send for the church elders, and let them pray over them, anointing them with oil in the name of the Lord.'),
(998857,34,59,5,15,'The prayer offered in faith will save the person who is sick, and the Lord will raise them from their bed; and if they have committed sins, they will be forgiven.'),
(998858,34,59,5,16,'Therefore, confess your sins to one another and pray for one another, so that you may be cured. Great is the power of a good person’s fervent prayer.'),
(998859,34,59,5,17,'Elijah was only human like ourselves, but, when he prayed fervently that it might not rain, no rain fell on the land for three and a half years.'),
(998860,34,59,5,18,'And, when he prayed again, the clouds brought rain, and the land bore crops.'),
(998861,34,59,5,19,'My friends, should one of you be led astray from the truth, and someone bring them back again,'),
(998862,34,59,5,20,'be sure that the person who brings a sinner back from their mistaken ways will save that person’s soul from death, and will cover a multitude of sins.'),
(998863,34,60,1,1,'To the people of God who are living abroad, dispersed throughout Pontus, Galatia, Cappadocia, Roman Asia, and Bithynia,'),
(998864,34,60,1,2,'and who were chosen in accordance with the foreknowledge of God the Father, through the consecration of the Spirit, to learn obedience, and to be purified by the sprinkling of the blood of Jesus Christ, from Peter, an apostle of Jesus Christ. May blessing and peace be yours in ever increasing measure.'),
(998865,34,60,1,3,'Blessed is the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, who has, in his great mercy, through the resurrection of Jesus Christ from the dead,'),
(998866,34,60,1,4,'given us the new life of undying hope, that promises an inheritance, imperishable, stainless, unfading, which has been reserved for you in heaven –'),
(998867,34,60,1,5,'for you who, through faith, are being guarded by the power of God, awaiting a salvation that is ready to be revealed in the last days.'),
(998868,34,60,1,6,'At the thought of this you are full of exultation, though (if it has been necessary) you have suffered for the moment somewhat from various trials;'),
(998869,34,60,1,7,'that the genuineness of your faith – a thing far more precious than gold, which is perishable, yet has to be tested by fire – may win praise and glory and honour at the appearing of Jesus Christ.'),
(998870,34,60,1,8,'Though you have never seen him, yet you love him; though you do not even now see him, yet you believe in him, and exalt with a triumphant happiness too great for words,'),
(998871,34,60,1,9,'as you receive the reward of your faith in the salvation of your souls!'),
(998872,34,60,1,10,'It was this salvation that the prophets, who spoke long ago of the blessing intended for you, sought, and strove to comprehend;'),
(998873,34,60,1,11,'as they strove to discern what that time could be, to which the Spirit of Christ within them was pointing, when foretelling the sufferings that Christ would have to endure, and the glories that would follow.'),
(998874,34,60,1,12,'And it was revealed to them that it was not for themselves, but for you, that they were acting as Ministers of the truths which have now been told to you, by those who, with the help of the Holy Spirit sent from heaven, have brought you the good news – truths into which even angels long to look.'),
(998875,34,60,1,13,'Therefore concentrate your minds, with the strictest self-control, and fix your hopes on the blessing that is coming for you at the appearing of Jesus Christ.'),
(998876,34,60,1,14,'Be like obedient children; do not let your lives be shaped by the passions which once swayed you in the days of your ignorance,'),
(998877,34,60,1,15,'but in your whole life show yourselves to be holy, after the pattern of the Holy One from whom you received your call.'),
(998878,34,60,1,16,'For scripture says –'),
(998879,34,60,1,17,'And since you call on him as “Father,” who judges everyone impartially by what he has done, let respectful awe be the spirit of your lives during the time of your stay on earth.'),
(998880,34,60,1,18,'For you know that it was not by perishable things, such as silver and gold, that you were ransomed from the aimless way of living which was handed down to you from your ancestors,'),
(998881,34,60,1,19,'but by precious blood, as it were of a lamb, unblemished and spotless, the blood of Christ.'),
(998882,34,60,1,20,'Destined for this before the beginning of the world, he has been revealed in these last days for your sakes,'),
(998883,34,60,1,21,'who, through him, are faithful to God who raised him from the dead and gave him honour, so that your faith and hope are now in God.'),
(998884,34,60,1,22,'Now that, by your obedience to the truth, you have purified your lives, so that there is growing up among you a genuine affection, love one another earnestly with all your hearts;'),
(998885,34,60,1,23,'since your new life has come, not from perishable, but imperishable, seed, through the message of the Everliving God.'),
(998886,34,60,1,24,'For –'),
(998887,34,60,1,25,'but the teaching of the Lord remains for ever.”'),
(998888,34,60,2,1,'Now that you have done with all malice, all deceitfulness, insincerity, jealous feelings, and all backbiting,'),
(998889,34,60,2,2,'like newly born infants, crave pure spiritual milk, so that you may be enabled by it to grow until you attain salvation –'),
(998890,34,60,2,3,'since “you have found by experience that the Lord is kind.”'),
(998891,34,60,2,4,'Come to him, then, as to a living stone, rejected, indeed, by men, but in God’s eyes choice and precious;'),
(998892,34,60,2,5,'and, as living stones, form yourselves into a spiritual house, to be a consecrated priesthood, for the offering of spiritual sacrifices that will be acceptable to God through Jesus Christ.'),
(998893,34,60,2,6,'For there is a passage of scripture that runs –'),
(998894,34,60,2,7,'It is to you, then, who believe in him that he is precious, but to those who do not believe he is “a stone which, though rejected by the builders, has now itself become the corner-stone,”'),
(998895,34,60,2,8,'and “a stumbling-block, and a rock which will prove a hindrance.” They stumble because they do not accept the message. This was the fate destined for them.'),
(998896,34,60,2,9,'But you are “a chosen people, a royal priesthood, a consecrated nation, God’s own people,” entrusted with the proclamation of the goodness of him who called you out of darkness into his wonderful light.'),
(998897,34,60,2,10,'Once you were “not a people,” but now you are “God’s people”; once you “had not found mercy,” but now you “have found mercy.”'),
(998898,34,60,2,11,'Dear friends, I beg you, as pilgrims and strangers on earth, to refrain from indulging the cravings of your earthly nature, for they make war on the soul.'),
(998899,34,60,2,12,'Let your daily life among the Gentiles be so upright, that, whenever they malign you as evil-doers, they may learn, as they watch, from the uprightness of your conduct, to praise God “at the time when he will visit them.”'),
(998900,34,60,2,13,'Submit to all human institutions for the Lord’s sake, alike to the emperor as the supreme authority,'),
(998901,34,60,2,14,'and to governors as sent by him to punish evil-doers and to commend those who do right.'),
(998902,34,60,2,15,'For God’s will is this – that you should silence the ignorance of foolish people by doing what is right.'),
(998903,34,60,2,16,'Act as free people, yet not using your freedom as those do who make it a cloak for wickedness, but as Servants of God.'),
(998904,34,60,2,17,'Show honour to everyone, love the Lord’s followers, “revere God, honour the emperor.”'),
(998905,34,60,2,18,'Those of you who are domestic servants should always be submissive and respectful to their masters, not only to those who are good and considerate, but also to those who are arbitrary.'),
(998906,34,60,2,19,'For this wins God’s approval when, because conscious of God’s presence, a person who is suffering unjustly bears their troubles patiently.'),
(998907,34,60,2,20,'What credit can you claim when, after doing wrong, you take your punishment for it patiently? But, on the other hand, if, after doing right, you take your sufferings patiently, that does win the approval of God.'),
(998908,34,60,2,21,'For it was to this that you were called! For Christ, too, suffered – on your behalf – and left you an example, that you should follow in his steps.'),
(998909,34,60,2,22,'He “never sinned, nor was anything deceitful ever heard from his lips.”'),
(998910,34,60,2,23,'He was abused, but he did not answer with abuse; he suffered, but he did not threaten; he entrusted himself to him whose judgments are just.'),
(998911,34,60,2,24,'And he “himself carried our sins” in his own body to the cross, so that we might die to our sins, and live for righteousness. “His bruising was your healing.”'),
(998912,34,60,2,25,'Once you were straying like sheep, but now you have returned to the shepherd and guardian of your souls.'),
(998913,34,60,3,1,'Again, you married women should submit to your husbands, so that if any of them reject the message, they may, apart from the message, be won over, by the conduct of their wives,'),
(998914,34,60,3,2,'as they see your pure, reverent conduct.'),
(998915,34,60,3,3,'Yours should be, not the external adornment of the arrangement of the hair, the wearing of jewellery, or the putting on of dresses,'),
(998916,34,60,3,4,'but the inner life with the imperishable beauty of a quiet and gentle spirit; for this is very precious in God’s sight.'),
(998917,34,60,3,5,'It was by this that the holy women of old, who rested their hopes on God, adorned themselves; submitting to their husbands,'),
(998918,34,60,3,6,'as Sarah did, who obeyed Abraham, and called him master. And you are her true children, as long as you live good lives, and let nothing terrify you.'),
(998919,34,60,3,7,'Again, those of you who are married men should live considerately with their wives, showing due regard to their sex, as physically weaker than their own, and not forgetting that they share with you in the gift of life. Then you will be able to pray without hindrance.'),
(998920,34,60,3,8,'Lastly, you should all be united, sympathetic, full of love for each other, kind-hearted, humble-minded;'),
(998921,34,60,3,9,'never returning evil for evil, or abuse for abuse, but, on the contrary, blessing. It was to this that you were called – to obtain a blessing!'),
(998922,34,60,3,10,'“The person who wants to enjoy life'),
(998923,34,60,3,11,'they should turn from evil and do good,'),
(998924,34,60,3,12,'For the eyes of the Lord are on the righteous,'),
(998925,34,60,3,13,'Who, indeed, is there to harm you, if you prove yourselves to be eager for what is good?'),
(998926,34,60,3,14,'Even if you should suffer for righteousness, count yourselves blessed! “Do not let people terrify you, or allow yourselves to be dismayed.”'),
(998927,34,60,3,15,'Revere the Christ as Lord in your hearts; always ready to give an answer to anyone who asks your reason for the hope that you cherish, but giving it with courtesy and respect,'),
(998928,34,60,3,16,'and keeping your consciences clear, so that, whenever you are maligned, those who vilify your good and Christian conduct may be put to shame.'),
(998929,34,60,3,17,'It is better that you should suffer, if that should be God’s will, for doing right, than for doing wrong.'),
(998930,34,60,3,18,'For Christ himself died to atone for sins once for all – the good on behalf of the bad – that he might bring you to God; his body being put to death, but his spirit entering on new life.'),
(998931,34,60,3,19,'And it was then that he went and preached to the imprisoned spirits,'),
(998932,34,60,3,20,'who once were disobedient, at the time when God patiently waited, in the days of Noah, while the ark was being prepared; in which some few lives, eight in all, were saved by means of water.'),
(998933,34,60,3,21,'And baptism, which this foreshadowed, now saves you – not the mere cleansing of the body, but the search of a clear conscience after God – through the resurrection of Jesus Christ,'),
(998934,34,60,3,22,'who has gone into heaven, and is at God’s right hand, where angels and archangels and the powers of heaven now yield submission to him.'),
(998935,34,60,4,1,'Since, then, Christ suffered in body, arm yourselves with the same resolve as he; for he who has suffered in body has ceased to sin,'),
(998936,34,60,4,2,'and so will live the rest of his earthly life guided, not by human passions, but by the will of God.'),
(998937,34,60,4,3,'Surely in the past you have spent time enough living as the Gentiles delight to live. For your path has lain among scenes of debauchery, licentiousness, drunkenness, revelry, hard-drinking, and profane idolatry.'),
(998938,34,60,4,4,'And, because you do not run to the same extremes of profligacy as others, they are astonished, and malign you.'),
(998939,34,60,4,5,'But they will have to answer for their conduct to him who is ready to judge both the living and the dead.'),
(998940,34,60,4,6,'For that was why the good news was told to the dead also – that, after they have been judged in the body, as people are judged, they might live in the spirit, as God lives.'),
(998941,34,60,4,7,'But the end of all things is near. Therefore exercise self-restraint and be calm, so that you may be able to pray.'),
(998942,34,60,4,8,'Above all things, let your love for one another be earnest, for “Love throws a veil over countless sins.”'),
(998943,34,60,4,9,'Never grudge hospitality to one another.'),
(998944,34,60,4,10,'Whatever the gift that each has received, use it in the service of others, as good stewards of the varied bounty of God.'),
(998945,34,60,4,11,'When anyone speaks, they should speak as one who is delivering the oracles of God. When anyone is endeavouring to serve others, they should do so in reliance on the strength which God supplies; so that in everything God may be honoured through Jesus Christ – to whom be ascribed all honour and might for ever and ever. Amen.'),
(998946,34,60,4,12,'Dear friends, do not be astonished at the trial of fire that you are passing through, to test you, as though something strange were happening to you.'),
(998947,34,60,4,13,'No, the more you share the sufferings of the Christ, the more may you rejoice, that, when the time comes for the manifestation of his glory, you may rejoice and exult.'),
(998948,34,60,4,14,'If you are insulted for bearing the name of Christ, count yourselves blessed; because the divine glory and the Spirit of God are resting on you.'),
(998949,34,60,4,15,'I need hardly say that no one among you must suffer as a murderer, or a thief, or a criminal, or for interfering in matters which do not concern Christians.'),
(998950,34,60,4,16,'But, if someone suffers as a Christian, they should not be ashamed of it; they should bring honour to God even though they bear that name.'),
(998951,34,60,4,17,'For the time has come for judgment to begin with the house of God; and, if it begins with us, what will be the end of those who reject God’s good news?'),
(998952,34,60,4,18,'If “a good person is saved only with difficulty, what will become of the godless and the sinful?”'),
(998953,34,60,4,19,'Therefore, I say, let those who suffer, because God wills it so, commit their lives into the hands of a faithful Creator, and persevere in doing right.'),
(998954,34,60,5,1,'As for the older ones among you, who are elders in the church, I, their fellow elder, and a witness to the sufferings of the Christ, who will also share in the glory that is to be revealed –'),
(998955,34,60,5,2,'I beg you to be true shepherds of the flock of God among you, not because you are compelled, but of your own free will; not from a base love of gain, but with a ready spirit;'),
(998956,34,60,5,3,'not as lords of your charges, but as examples to your flock.'),
(998957,34,60,5,4,'Then, when the chief shepherd appears, you will win the crown of glory that never fades.'),
(998958,34,60,5,5,'Again, you younger ones should show deference to the older. And all of you should put on the badge of humility in mutual service, for “God is opposed to the proud, but gives his help to the humble.”'),
(998959,34,60,5,6,'Humble yourselves, therefore, under the mighty hand of God, so that he may exalt you in his good time,'),
(998960,34,60,5,7,'laying all your anxieties on him, for he makes you his care.'),
(998961,34,60,5,8,'Exercise self-control, be watchful. Your adversary, the devil, like a roaring lion, is prowling about, eager to devour you.'),
(998962,34,60,5,9,'Stand firm against him, strong in your faith; knowing, as you do, that the sufferings which you are undergoing are being endured to the full by the Lord’s followers throughout the world.'),
(998963,34,60,5,10,'God, from whom all help comes, and who called you, by your union with Christ, into his eternal glory, will, when you have suffered for a little while, himself perfect, establish, strengthen you.'),
(998964,34,60,5,11,'To him be ascribed dominion for ever. Amen.'),
(998965,34,60,5,12,'I have been writing to you briefly by the hand of Silas, our true-hearted friend (for so I regard him), to encourage you, and to bear my testimony that in what I have written is to be found the true love of God. On that take your stand.'),
(998966,34,60,5,13,'Your sister church in “Babylon” sends you greeting, and so does Mark, who is as a son to me.'),
(998967,34,60,5,14,'Greet one another with the kiss of love.'),
(998968,34,61,1,1,'To those to whom, through the justice of our God and Saviour Jesus Christ, there has been granted faith equally privileged with our own, from Simon Peter, a servant and an apostle of Jesus Christ.'),
(998969,34,61,1,2,'May blessing and peace be yours in ever increasing measure, as you advance in the knowledge of God and of Jesus, our Lord.'),
(998970,34,61,1,3,'For his divine power has given us everything that is needful for a life of piety, as we advance in the knowledge of him who called us by a glorious manifestation of his goodness.'),
(998971,34,61,1,4,'For it was through this that he gave us what we prize as the greatest of his promises, that through them you might participate in the divine nature, now that you have fled from the corruption in the world, resulting from human passions.'),
(998972,34,61,1,5,'Yes, and for this reason do your best to supplement your faith by goodness, goodness by knowledge,'),
(998973,34,61,1,6,'knowledge by self-control, self-control by endurance, endurance by piety,'),
(998974,34,61,1,7,'piety by mutual affection, and mutual affection by love.'),
(998975,34,61,1,8,'For, when these virtues are yours, in increasing measure, they prevent your being indifferent to, or destitute of, a fuller knowledge of our Lord Jesus Christ.'),
(998976,34,61,1,9,'Surely the person who has not these virtues is shortsighted even to blindness, and has chosen to forget that they have been purified from their sins of the past!'),
(998977,34,61,1,10,'Therefore, friends, do your best to put God’s call and selection of you beyond all doubt; for, if you do this, you will never fall.'),
(998978,34,61,1,11,'For in this way you will be given a triumphant admission into the eternal kingdom of our Lord and Saviour, Jesus Christ.'),
(998979,34,61,1,12,'I will, therefore, always be ready to remind you of all this, even though you know it and are firmly established in the truth that you now hold.'),
(998980,34,61,1,13,'But I think it my duty, as long as I live in this “tent,” to rouse you by awakening memories of the past;'),
(998981,34,61,1,14,'for I know that the time for this “tent” of mine to be put away is soon coming, as our Lord Jesus Christ himself assured me.'),
(998982,34,61,1,15,'So I will do my best to enable you, at any time after my departure, to call these truths to mind.'),
(998983,34,61,1,16,'For we were not following cleverly devised stories when we told you of the coming in power of our Lord Jesus Christ, but we had been eye-witnesses of his majesty.'),
(998984,34,61,1,17,'For he received honour and glory from God the Father, when from the glory of the Divine Majesty there were borne to his ears words such as these – “This is my dearly loved son, who brings me great joy.”'),
(998985,34,61,1,18,'These were the words that we heard, borne to our ears from heaven, when we were with him on that sacred mountain.'),
(998986,34,61,1,19,'And still stronger is the assurance that we have in the teaching of the prophets; to which you will do well to pay attention (as if it were a lamp shining in a gloomy place), until the day dawns and the morning star rises in your hearts.'),
(998987,34,61,1,20,'But first be assured of this: There is no prophetic teaching found in scripture that can be interpreted by a person’s unaided reason;'),
(998988,34,61,1,21,'for no prophetic teaching ever came in the old days at the mere wish of people, but people, moved by the Holy Spirit, spoke direct from God.'),
(998989,34,61,2,1,'But there were false prophets also in the nation, just as there will be false teachers among you, people who will secretly introduce ruinous divisions, disowning even the Lord who bought them, and bringing speedy ruin on themselves.'),
(998990,34,61,2,2,'There will be many, too, who will follow their licentious courses, and cause the way of the truth to be maligned.'),
(998991,34,61,2,3,'In their covetousness they will try to make you a source of profit by their fabrications; but for a long time past their sentence has not been standing idle, nor their ruin slumbering.'),
(998992,34,61,2,4,'Remember, God did not spare angels when they sinned, but sent them down to Tartarus, and consigned them to caverns of darkness, to be kept under guard for judgment.'),
(998993,34,61,2,5,'Nor did he spare the world of old; though he preserved Noah, the preacher of righteousness, and seven others, when he brought a flood on the godless world.'),
(998994,34,61,2,6,'He condemned the cities of Sodom and Gomorrah and reduced them to ashes, holding them up as a warning to the godless of what was in store for them;'),
(998995,34,61,2,7,'but he rescued righteous Lot, whose heart was vexed by the wanton licentiousness of his neighbours;'),
(998996,34,61,2,8,'for, seeing and hearing what he did, as he lived his righteous life among them, day after day, Lot’s righteous soul was tortured by their wicked doings.'),
(998997,34,61,2,9,'The Lord, therefore, knows how to deliver the pious from temptation, and to keep the wicked, who are even now suffering punishment, in readiness for “the day of judgment” –'),
(998998,34,61,2,10,'especially those who, following the promptings of their lower nature, indulge their polluting passions and despise all control. Audacious and self-willed, they feel no awe of the celestial beings, maligning them,'),
(998999,34,61,2,11,'even where angels, though excelling them in strength and power, do not bring against them a malignant charge before the Lord.'),
(999000,34,61,2,12,'These people, however, like animals without reason, intended by nature to be caught and killed – these people, I say, malign those of whom they know nothing, and will assuredly perish through their own corruption,'),
(999001,34,61,2,13,'suffering themselves, as the penalty for the suffering that they have inflicted. They think that pleasure consists in the self-indulgence of the moment. They are a stain and a disgrace, indulging, as they do, in their wanton revelry, even while joining you at your feasts.'),
(999002,34,61,2,14,'They have eyes only for adulteresses, eyes never tired of sin; they entice weak souls; their minds are trained to covet; they live under a curse.'),
(999003,34,61,2,15,'Leaving the straight road, they have gone astray and followed in the steps of Balaam, the son of Beor, who set his heart on the reward for wrong-doing,'),
(999004,34,61,2,16,'but was rebuked for his offence. A dumb animal spoke with a human voice, and checked the prophet’s madness.'),
(999005,34,61,2,17,'These people are like springs without water, or mists driven before a gale; and for them the blackest darkness has been reserved.'),
(999006,34,61,2,18,'With boastful and foolish talk, they appeal to the passions of people’s lower nature, and, by their profligacy, entice those who are just escaping from the people who live such misguided lives.'),
(999007,34,61,2,19,'They promise them freedom, while they themselves are slaves to corrupt habits; for a person is the slave of anything to which they give way.'),
(999008,34,61,2,20,'If, after having escaped the polluting influences of the world, through knowing our Lord and Saviour, Jesus Christ, people are again entangled in them, and give way to them, their last state has become worse than their first.'),
(999009,34,61,2,21,'It would, indeed, have been better for them not to have known the way of righteousness, than, after knowing it, to turn away from the holy command delivered to them.'),
(999010,34,61,2,22,'In their case is seen the truth of the proverb – “A dog returns to what it has vomited” and “A sow after washing to her wallowing-place in the mud.”'),
(999011,34,61,3,1,'This, dear friends, is my second letter to you. In both of them I have tried, by appealing to your remembrance, to arouse your better feelings.'),
(999012,34,61,3,2,'I want you to recall what was foretold by the holy prophets, as well as the command of our Lord and Saviour given to you through your apostles.'),
(999013,34,61,3,3,'First be assured of this, that, as the age draws to an end, scoffers, led by their own passions,'),
(999014,34,61,3,4,'will come and ask scoffingly – “Where is his promised coming? Ever since our ancestors passed to their rest, everything remains just as it was when the world was first created!”'),
(999015,34,61,3,5,'For they wilfully shut their eyes to the fact that long ago the heavens existed; and the earth, also – formed out of water and by the action of water, by the fiat of God;'),
(999016,34,61,3,6,'and that by the same means the world which then existed was destroyed in a deluge of water.'),
(999017,34,61,3,7,'But the present heavens and earth, by the same fiat, have been reserved for fire, and are being kept for the day of the judgment and destruction of the godless.'),
(999018,34,61,3,8,'But you, dear friends, must never shut your eyes to the fact that, to the Lord, one day is the same as a thousand years, and a thousand years as one day.'),
(999019,34,61,3,9,'The Lord is not slow to fulfil his promise, as some count slowness; but he is forbearing with you, as it is not his will that any of you should perish, but that all should be brought to repentance.'),
(999020,34,61,3,10,'The day of the Lord will come like a thief; and on that day the heavens will pass away with a crash, the elements will be burnt up and dissolved, and the earth and all that is in it will be disclosed.'),
(999021,34,61,3,11,'Now, since all these things are in the process of dissolution, think what you yourselves ought to be – what holy and pious lives you ought to lead,'),
(999022,34,61,3,12,'while you wait for the coming of the day of God and strive to make it come soon'),
(999023,34,61,3,13,'but we look for new heavens and a new earth, where righteousness will have its home, in fulfilment of the promise of God.'),
(999024,34,61,3,14,'Therefore, dear friends, in expectation of these things, make every effort to be found by him spotless, blameless, and at peace.'),
(999025,34,61,3,15,'Regard our Lord’s forbearance as your one hope of salvation. This is what our dear friend Paul wrote to you, with the wisdom that God gave him.'),
(999026,34,61,3,16,'It is the same in all his letters, when he speaks in them about these subjects. There are some things in them difficult to understand, which untaught and weak people distort, just as they do all other writings, to their own ruin.'),
(999027,34,61,3,17,'You must, therefore, dear friends, now that you know this beforehand, be on your guard against being led away by the errors of reckless people, and so lapsing from your present steadfastness;'),
(999028,34,61,3,18,'and advance in the love and knowledge of our Lord and Saviour, Jesus Christ. All glory be to him now and for ever.'),
(999029,34,62,1,1,'We write to you about the Word of life, which has been in existence from the beginning. We write of what we have heard, of what we have seen with our eyes, of what we watched reverently and touched with our hands.'),
(999030,34,62,1,2,'That life was made visible, and we have seen it. We bear our testimony to it, and tell you of that eternal life which was with the Father and was made visible to us.'),
(999031,34,62,1,3,'It is of what we have seen and heard that we now tell you, so that you may have fellowship with us. And our fellowship is with the Father and with his Son, Jesus Christ.'),
(999032,34,62,1,4,'We are writing all this to you that our joy may be complete.'),
(999033,34,62,1,5,'This is the message which we have heard from him and announce to you: God is light, and there is no darkness in him at all.'),
(999034,34,62,1,6,'If we say that we have fellowship with him and yet continue to walk in the darkness, our words and our lives are a lie.'),
(999035,34,62,1,7,'But if we walk in the light, as he is in the light, we have fellowship with one another, and the blood of Jesus, his Son, cleanses us from all sin.'),
(999036,34,62,1,8,'If we say, ‘we have no sin,’ then we are deceiving ourselves, and the truth is not in us.'),
(999037,34,62,1,9,'If we confess our sins, he is just and may be trusted to forgive our sins and cleanse us from all wrongdoing.'),
(999038,34,62,1,10,'If we say that we haven’t sinned, we make God a liar, and his Word is not in us.'),
(999039,34,62,2,1,'My children, I am writing to you to keep you from sinning. But if anyone does sin, we have an advocate with the Father – Jesus Christ, the righteous.'),
(999040,34,62,2,2,'He is the atoning sacrifice for our sins, and not for ours only, but the sins of the whole world.'),
(999041,34,62,2,3,'It is by keeping God’s commands that we can be sure we know him.'),
(999042,34,62,2,4,'Whoever says ‘I know him,’ but does not keep his commands, is a liar. The truth has no place in them.'),
(999043,34,62,2,5,'But the person who keeps God’s word, in them the love of God has indeed reached its perfection. This is how we can be sure we are in him:'),
(999044,34,62,2,6,'whoever claims to live in him should live just as Jesus did.'),
(999045,34,62,2,7,'Dear friends, it is no new command that I am writing to you, but an old command, which you have had from the beginning. That old command is the message you have already heard.'),
(999046,34,62,2,8,'Yet, in a way, it is a new command that I am writing to you – which is shown true in Christ’s life and in yours – for the darkness is passing away and the true light is already shining.'),
(999047,34,62,2,9,'The person who says that they are in the light, and yet hates others, is still in the darkness.'),
(999048,34,62,2,10,'The person who loves others is always in the light, and there is nothing within them to cause them to stumble.'),
(999049,34,62,2,11,'The person who hates is in the dark. They stumble along in the darkness; they do not know where they are going because the darkness blinds them.'),
(999050,34,62,2,12,'Little children, I am writing to you'),
(999051,34,62,2,13,'Parents, I am writing to you'),
(999052,34,62,2,14,'Parents, I write to you'),
(999053,34,62,2,15,'Do not love the world or what the world can offer. When anyone loves the world, there is no love for the Father in them.'),
(999054,34,62,2,16,'For all that the world can offer – the desires for physical pleasure, the enticements to the eye, the arrogance of wealth – belongs, not to the Father, but to the world.'),
(999055,34,62,2,17,'And the world, and all that it gratifies, is passing away, but they who do God’s will remain for ever.'),
(999056,34,62,2,18,'My children, it is the last hour. You were told that an antichrist was coming; and many antichrists have already arisen. This is why we know that this is the last hour.'),
(999057,34,62,2,19,'These people come from our ranks, but they were never truly part of us – if they had been then they would have stayed with us. They left so it would be clear that none of them really belonged to us.'),
(999058,34,62,2,20,'You, however, have been annointed by the Holy One. You all know the truth.'),
(999059,34,62,2,21,'I am not writing to you because you do not know the truth, but because you do know it, and because no lie can come from the truth.'),
(999060,34,62,2,22,'Who is a liar, if not the one who denies that Jesus is the Christ? That person is the antichrist – one who rejects the Father and the Son.'),
(999061,34,62,2,23,'No one who rejects the Son has the Father; to acknowledge the Son is to have the Father also.'),
(999062,34,62,2,24,'As for you, you must let what you have heard from the beginning continue to live in you. If what you heard from the beginning dwells in you, you will remain both in the Son and the Father.'),
(999063,34,62,2,25,'And this is what he himself promised us – eternal life!'),
(999064,34,62,2,26,'In writing this to you, I have in mind those who are trying to mislead you.'),
(999065,34,62,2,27,'As for you, the anointing which you received from him remains with you. You do not need anyone to teach you. His anointing teaches you about everything. What it teaches you is true, it is not a lie. Do what it has taught you: abide in him.'),
(999066,34,62,2,28,'Yes, my children, remain in him, so that when he appears our confidence doesn’t fail us, and we are not ashamed to meet him at his coming.'),
(999067,34,62,2,29,'Since you know he is righteous, you realise that everyone who does what is right is his child.'),
(999068,34,62,3,1,'See what great love the Father has lavished on us: he lets us be called God’s children! For that is what we are. The reason why the world does not know us is that it has not learned to know him.'),
(999069,34,62,3,2,'Dear friends, we are God’s children now, and what we will be has not yet been revealed. What we do know is that, when it is revealed, we will be like him, because we will see him as he is.'),
(999070,34,62,3,3,'And just as he is pure, everyone who has this hope, makes and keeps themselves pure.'),
(999071,34,62,3,4,'Everyone who lives sinfully is living in violation of God’s law. Sin is lawlessness.'),
(999072,34,62,3,5,'You know that Christ appeared to take away our sins and that there is no sin in him.'),
(999073,34,62,3,6,'No one who lives in him continues to sin; the sinner has not seen or known him.'),
(999074,34,62,3,7,'My children, don’t let anyone mislead you. The person who does what is right is righteous, just as Christ is righteous.'),
(999075,34,62,3,8,'The person who lives in sin is a child of the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the beginning. To undo the devil’s work is the reason the Son of God appeared.'),
(999076,34,62,3,9,'No child of God sins, because God’s nature dwells in them. They can’t live in sin, because they are God’s children.'),
(999077,34,62,3,10,'By this it is made clear who are the children of God and who are the devil’s: anyone who doesn’t do what is right or doesn’t love others is not a child of God.'),
(999078,34,62,3,11,'For this is the message we heard from the beginning: we are to love one another.'),
(999079,34,62,3,12,'We must not be like Cain, who belonged to the evil one and murdered his brother. Why did he kill him? Because his actions were evil, and his brother’s were righteous.'),
(999080,34,62,3,13,'Do not be suprised, friends, if the world hates you.'),
(999081,34,62,3,14,'We know that we have passed out of death into life, because we love each other. The person who does not love remains in a state of death.'),
(999082,34,62,3,15,'The person who hates another is a murderer, and you know that no murderer has eternal life dwelling within them.'),
(999083,34,62,3,16,'This is how we know that love is: Christ gave his life for us. So we should lay down our own lives for each other.'),
(999084,34,62,3,17,'If anyone has material possessions, and sees one of our own in need, but closes their heart against that person, how can it be said that the love of God is within them?'),
(999085,34,62,3,18,'My children, our love must not be mere words or talk. It must be true and show itself in actions.'),
(999086,34,62,3,19,'This is how we will know we belong to the truth and reassure ourselves in God’s presence:'),
(999087,34,62,3,20,'though our conscience condemns us, God is greater than our conscience and knows everything.'),
(999088,34,62,3,21,'Dear friends, if our conscience does not condemn us, then we approach God with confidence,'),
(999089,34,62,3,22,'and we receive from him whatever we ask, because we are keeping his commands, and are doing what pleases him.'),
(999090,34,62,3,23,'His command is that we should believe in his Son, Jesus Christ, and love one another, as Christ commanded us.'),
(999091,34,62,3,24,'The person who keeps his commands dwells in God and God dwells in them. And we are sure he lives in us because of the Spirit he has given us.'),
(999092,34,62,4,1,'Dear friends, do not trust every spirit, but test the spirits to see whether they are from God, because many false prophets have gone out into the world.'),
(999093,34,62,4,2,'This is the way to recognise the Spirit of God: those who acknowledge Jesus Christ as come in the flesh have God’s Spirit,'),
(999094,34,62,4,3,'while a spirit that doesn’t acknowledge Jesus isn’t from God. Instead it is the spirit of the antichrist; you have heard that it was coming, and it is now already in the world!'),
(999095,34,62,4,4,'You, my children, come from God, and you have successfully resisted such people as these, because he who is in you is greater than the one who is in the world.'),
(999096,34,62,4,5,'Those people belong to the world and therefore they speak as the world speaks, and the world listens to them.'),
(999097,34,62,4,6,'We come from God. Whoever knows God listens to us; the person who does not come from God does not listen to us. This is how we distinguish the spirit of truth and the spirit of deception.'),
(999098,34,62,4,7,'Dear friends, let us love one another, because love comes from God and everyone who loves is a child of God and knows God.'),
(999099,34,62,4,8,'Those who do not love know nothing of God, for God is love.'),
(999100,34,62,4,9,'This is how God showed his love among us: he sent his one and only Son into the world that we might live through him.'),
(999101,34,62,4,10,'This is what love is: it is not that we have loved God, but that he loved us and sent his Son to be an atoning sacrifice for our sins.'),
(999102,34,62,4,11,'Dear friends, since God loved us in this way, we should love one another.'),
(999103,34,62,4,12,'No one has ever seen God, but if we love one another, God lives in us and his love reaches perfection within us.'),
(999104,34,62,4,13,'We know that we live in him, and he lives in us, because he has given us a measure of his Spirit.'),
(999105,34,62,4,14,'Moreover, we have seen for ourselves and testify that the Father has sent the Son to be the Saviour of the world.'),
(999106,34,62,4,15,'Whoever acknowledges that Jesus Christ is the Son of God, God lives in them, and they live in God.'),
(999107,34,62,4,16,'And so we have come to know and believe the love which God has for us.'),
(999108,34,62,4,17,'This is the way love has reached its perfection among us, so that we may have confidence on the day of judgment, because in this world we are like Christ.'),
(999109,34,62,4,18,'There is no fear in love; perfect love drives out fear because fear has to do with punishment. So anyone who is afraid has not reached perfection in love.'),
(999110,34,62,4,19,'We love, because God first loved us.'),
(999111,34,62,4,20,'If someone says “I love God,” and yet hates others, they are a liar. For the person who does not love their brother or sister, whom they have seen, cannot love God, whom they have not seen.'),
(999112,34,62,4,21,'Indeed, we have this command from Christ: Those who love God must also love each other.'),
(999113,34,62,5,1,'Everyone who believes that Jesus is the Christ is a child of God, and everyone who loves a parent loves his child.'),
(999114,34,62,5,2,'By this we know that we love God’s children – when we love God and carry out his commands.'),
(999115,34,62,5,3,'For to love God is to do what he commands and his commands are not a burden,'),
(999116,34,62,5,4,'for whatever is born of God overcomes the world. What is the victory by which the world is overcome? Our faith!'),
(999117,34,62,5,5,'Who can overcome the world but the person who believes that Jesus is the Son of God?'),
(999118,34,62,5,6,'Jesus Christ, the one who came by water and blood – not by water only but by water and blood – and the Spirit testifies to this because the Spirit is truth.'),
(999119,34,62,5,7,'Indeed three testify:'),
(999120,34,62,5,8,'the Spirit, the water, and the blood, and these three agree.'),
(999121,34,62,5,9,'We accept human testimony, surely God’s testimony is even stronger! And God’s testimony is the testimony he has given about his Son.'),
(999122,34,62,5,10,'The person who believes in the Son of God has that testimony within them. The person who does not believe God has made God a liar, by not believing the testimony God has given about his Son.'),
(999123,34,62,5,11,'And this is that testimony: God gave us eternal life, and this life is in his Son.'),
(999124,34,62,5,12,'Whoever has the Son has life; whoever who doesn’t have God’s Son does not have life.'),
(999125,34,62,5,13,'I have written these things to you who believe in the name of God’s Son, so that you may know that you have eternal life.'),
(999126,34,62,5,14,'We can approach him with this confidence, that whenever we ask anything that is in accordance with his will, he listens to us.'),
(999127,34,62,5,15,'And if we know he hears us – whatever we ask – we know also that what we ask for is ours.'),
(999128,34,62,5,16,'If anyone sees one of our people committing some sin that is not a sin leading to death, they should ask, and God will give them life. I refer to those whose sin does not lead to death. There is a sin that leads to death. I am not saying that you should pray about that.'),
(999129,34,62,5,17,'All wrongdoing is sin, but there is sin that does not lead to death.'),
(999130,34,62,5,18,'We know that those who have been born of God do not keep sinning. God protects his children and the evil one cannot get hold of them.'),
(999131,34,62,5,19,'We know that we are God’s children, though the whole world lies in the power of the evil one.'),
(999132,34,62,5,20,'We also know that the Son of God has come and has given us understanding, so that we may know the true God – and we are in him who is true, by being in his Son Jesus Christ. He is the true God and eternal life.'),
(999133,34,62,5,21,'My children, guard yourselves against false ideas of God.'),
(999134,34,63,1,1,'From the elder, to the lady chosen by God and her children. I truly love you all, and I am not the only one but all who know the truth love you as well.'),
(999135,34,63,1,2,'We love you for the sake of the truth, which lives in us and will be with us forever.'),
(999136,34,63,1,3,'Grace, mercy, and peace will be ours – the gift of God, the Father, and of Jesus Christ, the Father’s Son – in truth and love.'),
(999137,34,63,1,4,'It was a great joy to me to find the lives of some of your children guided by the truth, in obedience to the command that we received from the Father.'),
(999138,34,63,1,5,'And now I implore you, dear lady, let us love one another This is not a new command I am writing to you. It is the command we have had from the beginning. – Let us love one another.'),
(999139,34,63,1,6,'And this is love – to live in obedience to the Father’s commands. This is the command as you learned from the beginning, to live a life of love.'),
(999140,34,63,1,7,'I say this because many deceivers have gone out into the world – men who do not acknowledge that Jesus Christ came in flesh and blood. Any such person is a deceiver and antichrist.'),
(999141,34,63,1,8,'Take care so that you do not what we have worked for but instead receive your full reward.'),
(999142,34,63,1,9,'Anyone who goes beyond and fails to live inside of the teaching of Christ does not have God. The person who lives inside that teaching – they have both the Father and the Son.'),
(999143,34,63,1,10,'If anyone comes to you and does not bring this teaching, do not receive them into your house or even welcome them;'),
(999144,34,63,1,11,'because the person who welcomes them is sharing with them in his evil work.'),
(999145,34,63,1,12,'Though I have many other things to tell you, I would rather not use paper and ink. Instead I hope to come and see you, and to speak with you face to face, so that our joy may be complete.'),
(999146,34,63,1,13,'The children of your sister, who is chosen by God, send you their greetings.'),
(999147,34,64,1,1,'From the elder to his dear friend Gaius, whom he sincerely loves.'),
(999148,34,64,1,2,'Dear friend, I pray that all may be well with you and that you may have good health – I know that all is well with your soul.'),
(999149,34,64,1,3,'For it was a great joy to me, when some followers of the Lord came and testified to your fidelity to the truth. I know that your own life is guided by the truth.'),
(999150,34,64,1,4,'Nothing gives me greater pleasure than to hear from time to time that the lives of my children are guided by the truth.'),
(999151,34,64,1,5,'Dear friend, you are faithful in all the things you do for other followers – even when they are strangers to you.'),
(999152,34,64,1,6,'They themselves have testified before the church to your love. You will do well to help them on their way in a manner worthy of the service of God.'),
(999153,34,64,1,7,'For it was on behalf of Christ’s name that they set out, not accepting even one thing from the Gentiles.'),
(999154,34,64,1,8,'Therefore, we should support people like them, and so take our share in their work for the truth.'),
(999155,34,64,1,9,'I wrote something to the church, but Diotrephes (who loves to be the leader among them) doesn’t welcome us.'),
(999156,34,64,1,10,'So if I come, I will bring up his actions in telling wicked nonsense about us. Not content with that, he not only refuses to personally welcome our friends who are followers, but actually stops those who would, and expels them from the church.'),
(999157,34,64,1,11,'Dear friend, do not follow a bad example, but a good one. The person who does what is good is from God; the person who does what is bad has never seen God.'),
(999158,34,64,1,12,'Everyone has always had a good word for Demetrius, and the truth itself speaks for him. Yes, and we also add our good word, and you know that what we say is true.'),
(999159,34,64,1,13,'I have many things to tell you, but I would rather not use pen and ink.'),
(999160,34,64,1,14,'I hope to see you soon, and then we will speak face to face.'),
(999161,34,64,1,15,'Peace be with you. The friends here send you their greetings. Greet each one of our friends.'),
(999162,34,65,1,1,'To those who, having received the call, have been loved by God the Father and protected by Jesus Christ, From Jude, a servant of Jesus Christ, and the brother of James.'),
(999163,34,65,1,2,'May mercy, peace, and love be yours in ever increasing measure.'),
(999164,34,65,1,3,'Dear friends, while I was making every effort to write to you about our common salvation, I felt that I must write to you at once to encourage you to fight in defence of the faith that has once for all been entrusted to the keeping of Christ’s people.'),
(999165,34,65,1,4,'For there have crept in among you certain godless people, whose sentence has long since been pronounced, and who make the mercy of God an excuse for profligacy, and disown our only lord and master, Jesus Christ.'),
(999166,34,65,1,5,'Now I want to remind you – but you already know it all – that, though the Lord delivered the people from Egypt, yet he afterwards destroyed those who refused to believe in him;'),
(999167,34,65,1,6,'and that even those angels, who did not keep to their appointed spheres, but left their proper homes, have been kept by him for the judgment of the great day in everlasting chains and black darkness.'),
(999168,34,65,1,7,'Like Sodom and Gomorrah and the towns near them, which gave themselves up to fornication, and fell into unnatural vice, these angels now stand out as a warning, undergoing, as they are, punishment in eternal fire.'),
(999169,34,65,1,8,'Yet in the same way these people, too, cherishing vain dreams, pollute our human nature, reject control, and malign the celestial beings.'),
(999170,34,65,1,9,'Yet even Michael, the archangel, when, in his dispute with the devil, he was arguing about the body of Moses, did not venture to charge him with maligning, but said merely “The Lord rebuke you!”'),
(999171,34,65,1,10,'But these people malign whatever they do not understand; while they use such things as they know by instinct (like the animals that have no reason) for their own corruption.'),
(999172,34,65,1,11,'Alas for them! They walk in the steps of Cain; led astray by Balaam’s love of gain, they plunge into sin, and meet their ruin through rebellion like Korah.'),
(999173,34,65,1,12,'These are the people who are blots on your “love-feasts,” when they feast together and provide without scruple for themselves alone. They are clouds without rain, driven before the winds; they are leafless trees without a vestige of fruit, dead through and through, torn up by the roots;'),
(999174,34,65,1,13,'they are wild sea waves, foaming with their own shame; they are “wandering stars,” for which the blackest darkness has been reserved for ever.'),
(999175,34,65,1,14,'To these people, as to others, Enoch, the seventh in descent from Adam, declared – “See! The Lord has come with his hosts of holy ones around him,'),
(999176,34,65,1,15,'to execute judgment on all people, and to convict all godless people of all their godless acts, which in their ungodliness they have committed, and of all the harsh words which they have spoken against him, godless sinners that they are!”'),
(999177,34,65,1,16,'These people are always murmuring, and complaining of their lot; they follow where their passions lead them; they have arrogant words on their lips; and they flatter others for the sake of what they can get from them.'),
(999178,34,65,1,17,'But you should, dear friends, recall what was foretold by the apostles of our Lord Jesus Christ;'),
(999179,34,65,1,18,'how they used to say to you – “As time draws to an end, there will be scoffers, who will be led by their godless passions.”'),
(999180,34,65,1,19,'These are the people – animal and unspiritual – who cause divisions.'),
(999181,34,65,1,20,'But you must, dear friends, build up your characters on the foundation of your most holy faith, pray under the guidance of the Holy Spirit,'),
(999182,34,65,1,21,'and keep within the love of God, while waiting for the mercy of our Lord Jesus Christ, to bring you to eternal life.'),
(999183,34,65,1,22,'To some show pity, because they are in doubt. “Drag them out of the fire,” and save them.'),
(999184,34,65,1,23,'To others show pity, but with caution, hating the clothing polluted by their touch.'),
(999185,34,65,1,24,'To him who is able to guard you from falling, and to bring you into his glorious presence, blameless and rejoicing –'),
(999186,34,65,1,25,'to the one God, our Saviour, be ascribed, through Jesus Christ, our Lord, glory, majesty, power, and dominion, as it was before time began, is now, and will be for all time to come. Amen.'),
(999187,34,66,1,1,'The Revelation of Jesus Christ, which God gave to him to make known to his servants, concerning what must shortly take place, and which he sent and revealed by his angel to his servant John,'),
(999188,34,66,1,2,'who testified to the message of God and to the testimony to Jesus Christ, omitting nothing of what he had seen.'),
(999189,34,66,1,3,'Blessed is the one who reads, and blessed are they who listen to, the words of this prophecy, and lay to heart what is here written; for the time is near.'),
(999190,34,66,1,4,'From John, to the seven churches which are in Roman Asia. Blessing and peace be yours from him who is, and who was, and who will be, and from the seven spirits that are before his throne,'),
(999191,34,66,1,5,'and from Jesus Christ, the faithful witness, the first-born from the dead, and the Ruler of all the kings of the earth. To him who loves us and freed us from our sins by his own blood –'),
(999192,34,66,1,6,'and he made us a kingdom of priests in the service of God, his Father! – to Him be ascribed glory and dominion for ever. Amen.'),
(999193,34,66,1,7,'He is coming among the clouds! Every eye will see him, even those who pierced him and all the nations of the earth will mourn over him. So will it be. Amen.'),
(999194,34,66,1,9,'I, John, who am your brother, and who share with you in the suffering and kingship and endurance of Jesus, found myself on the island called Patmos, for the sake of the message of God and the testimony to Jesus.'),
(999195,34,66,1,10,'I fell into a trance on the Lord’s day, and I heard behind me a loud voice, like the blast of a trumpet.'),
(999196,34,66,1,11,'It said –'),
(999197,34,66,1,12,'I turned to see what voice it was that spoke to me; and when I turned, I saw seven golden lamps,'),
(999198,34,66,1,13,'and in the midst of the lamps one like a man, in a robe reaching to his feet, and with a golden sash across his breast.'),
(999199,34,66,1,14,'The hair of his head was as white as wool, as white as snow; his eyes were like flaming fire;'),
(999200,34,66,1,15,'and his feet were like brass as when molten in a furnace; his voice was like the sound of many streams,'),
(999201,34,66,1,16,'in his right hand he held seven stars, from his mouth came a sharp two-edged sword, and his face was like the sun in the fulness of its power.'),
(999202,34,66,1,17,'And, when I saw him, I fell at his feet like one dead. He laid his hand on me and said –'),
(999203,34,66,4,1,'After this, in my vision, I saw an open door in the heavens, and the first voice that I heard was like the blast of a trumpet speaking to me. It said – “Come up here and I will show you what must take place.”'),
(999204,34,66,4,2,'Immediately after this I fell into a trance. There stood a throne in heaven, and on the throne was One seated.'),
(999205,34,66,4,3,'He who was seated on it was in appearance like a jasper and a sardius; and round the throne there was a rainbow of the colour of an emerald.'),
(999206,34,66,4,4,'And round the throne were twenty-four other thrones, and on these I saw twenty-four elders sitting clothed in white robes; and on their heads they had crowns of gold.'),
(999207,34,66,4,5,'Out from the throne come flashes of lightning, cries, and peals of thunder! There are seven torches burning in front of the throne, which are the seven spirits of God;'),
(999208,34,66,4,6,'and in front of the throne is what seemed to be a sea of glass, resembling crystal, while within the space before the throne and round the throne are four creatures full of eyes in front and behind.'),
(999209,34,66,4,7,'The first creature is like a lion, the second creature like a calf, the third creature has a face like a man’s, and the fourth creature is like an eagle on the wing.'),
(999210,34,66,4,8,'These four creatures have each of them six wings, and all round, and within, they are full of eyes; and day and night they never cease to say –'),
(999211,34,66,4,9,'And, whenever these creatures give praise and honour and thanks to him who is seated on the throne, to him who lives for ever and ever,'),
(999212,34,66,4,10,'the twenty-four elders prostrate themselves before him who is seated on the throne, and worship him who lives for ever and ever, and throw down their crowns before the throne, saying –'),
(999213,34,66,4,11,'“Worthy are you, our Lord and God, to receive all praise, and honour, and power, for you did create all things, and at your bidding they came into being and were created.”'),
(999214,34,66,5,1,'Then I saw at the right hand of him who was seated on the throne a book, with writing inside and out, and sealed with seven seals;'),
(999215,34,66,5,2,'and I saw a mighty angel who was proclaiming in a loud voice – “Who is worthy to open the book and break its seals?”'),
(999216,34,66,5,3,'But no one either in heaven or on earth or under the earth was able to open the book or look within it.'),
(999217,34,66,5,4,'At this I wept long, because no one could be found who was worthy to open the book or look within it.'),
(999218,34,66,5,5,'But one of the elders said to me – “Do not weep. The Lion conquered – the Lion of the tribe of Judah, the Scion of David – and can therefore open the book with its seven seals.”'),
(999219,34,66,5,6,'Then, within the space between the throne and the four creatures, and in the midst of the elders, I saw, standing, a Lamb, which seemed to have been sacrificed. It had seven horns and seven eyes. (These eyes are the seven spirits of God, and they are sent into all the world.)'),
(999220,34,66,5,7,'The Lamb came forward; and he has taken the book from the right hand of him who was seated on the throne.'),
(999221,34,66,5,8,'And, when he had taken the book, the four creatures and the twenty-four elders prostrated themselves before the Lamb, each of them holding a harp and golden bowls full of incense. (These are the prayers of Christ’s people.)'),
(999222,34,66,5,9,'And they are singing a new song –'),
(999223,34,66,5,10,'and did make them a kingdom of priests in the service of our God, and they are reigning on the earth.”'),
(999224,34,66,5,11,'Then, in my vision, I heard the voices of many angels round the throne, and of the creatures, and of the elders. In number they were ten thousand times ten thousand and thousands of thousands,'),
(999225,34,66,5,12,'and they cried in a loud voice –'),
(999226,34,66,5,13,'And I heard every created thing in the air, and on the earth, and under the earth, and on the sea, and all that is in them crying –'),
(999227,34,66,5,14,'And the four creatures said “Amen,” and the elders prostrated themselves and worshiped.'),
(999228,34,66,6,1,'Then I saw the Lamb break one of the seven seals, and I heard one of the four creatures crying with a voice like thunder – “Come.”'),
(999229,34,66,6,2,'And in my vision I saw a white horse. Its rider held a bow, and he was given a crown, and he went out conquering and to conquer.'),
(999230,34,66,6,3,'When the Lamb broke the second seal, I heard the second creature crying – “Come.”'),
(999231,34,66,6,4,'Then there went out another horse, a red horse, and to its rider was given the power to deprive the earth of peace, so that people should kill one another; and he was given a great sword.'),
(999232,34,66,6,5,'When the Lamb broke the third seal, I heard the third creature crying – “Come.” And in my vision I saw a black horse. Its rider held scales in his hand.'),
(999233,34,66,6,6,'And I heard what seemed to be a voice, coming from among the four creatures, crying – “A quart of wheat for a silver coin, and three quarts of barley for a silver coin! But do not harm the oil and the wine.”'),
(999234,34,66,6,7,'When the Lamb broke the fourth seal, I heard the voice of the fourth creature crying – “Come.”'),
(999235,34,66,6,8,'And in my vision I saw a grey horse. His rider’s name was Death, and Hades rode behind him; and power was given them over the fourth part of the earth, so that they might destroy with sword and famine and death, and by means of the wild Beasts of the earth.'),
(999236,34,66,6,9,'When the Lamb opened the fifth seal, I saw under the altar the souls of those who had been killed for the sake of God’s message and for the testimony which they had borne.'),
(999237,34,66,6,10,'They cried in a loud voice – “How long, Sovereign Lord, holy and true, before you will give judgment and avenge our blood on all who are living on the earth?”'),
(999238,34,66,6,11,'Then to each of them was given a white robe, and they were told to rest yet a little longer, until the number of their fellow servants and of their friends in Christ’s service who were about to be put to death, as they had been, should be complete.'),
(999239,34,66,6,12,'And I saw the Lamb break the sixth seal, and then there was a great earthquake. The sun became black, like sackcloth, and the moon, which was at its full, like blood.'),
(999240,34,66,6,13,'The stars of the heavens fell to the earth, as when a fig-tree, shaken by a strong wind, drops its unripe fruit.'),
(999241,34,66,6,14,'The heavens disappeared like a scroll when it is rolled up, and every mountain and island was moved from its place.'),
(999242,34,66,6,15,'Then all the kings of the earth, and the princes, and the generals, and the rich, and the powerful, and every slave and free person, hid themselves in the caves and under the rocks of the mountains;'),
(999243,34,66,6,16,'and they are crying to the mountains and the rocks – “Fall on us, and hide us from the eyes of him who is seated on the throne, and from the wrath of the Lamb,'),
(999244,34,66,6,17,'for the great day of their wrath is come, and who can stand to meet it?”'),
(999245,34,66,7,1,'After this, I saw four angels standing on the four corners of the earth, restraining the four winds of the earth, so that no wind should blow over the earth, or over the sea, or against any tree.'),
(999246,34,66,7,2,'And, in the east, I saw another angel, ascending, holding the seal of the living God; and he cried in a loud voice to the four angels, to whom there had been given power to harm the earth and the sea –'),
(999247,34,66,7,3,'“Do not harm the earth, or the sea, or the trees, until we have sealed the servants of our God on their foreheads.”'),
(999248,34,66,7,4,'I heard, too, the number of those who had been sealed. It was one hundred and forty-four thousand; and they were from every tribe of the Israelites.'),
(999249,34,66,7,5,'From the tribe of Judah twelve thousand were sealed,'),
(999250,34,66,7,6,'from the tribe of Asher twelve thousand,'),
(999251,34,66,7,7,'from the tribe of Simeon twelve thousand,'),
(999252,34,66,7,8,'from the tribe of Zebulon twelve thousand,'),
(999253,34,66,7,9,'After this, in my vision, I saw a vast throng which no one could number, of people from every nation and of all tribes, and peoples, and languages. They stood in front of the throne and in front of the Lamb, robed in white, holding palm branches in their hands.'),
(999254,34,66,7,10,'And they are crying in a loud voice –'),
(999255,34,66,7,11,'And all the angels were standing round the throne and the elders and the four creatures, and they prostrated themselves on their faces in front of the throne and worshiped God,'),
(999256,34,66,7,12,'saying –'),
(999257,34,66,7,13,'Then one of the elders turned to me and said “Who are these who are robed in white? And where did they come from?”'),
(999258,34,66,7,14,'“My Lord,” I answered, “it is you who know.”'),
(999259,34,66,7,15,'And therefore it is that they are before the throne of God, and are serving him day and night in his Temple; and he who is seated on the throne will shelter them.'),
(999260,34,66,7,16,'Never again will they be hungry, never again will they be thirsty, nor will the sun smite them, nor any scorching heat;'),
(999261,34,66,7,17,'for the Lamb that stands in the space before the throne will be their shepherd, and will lead them to life-giving springs of water; and God will wipe away all tears from their eyes.”'),
(999262,34,66,8,1,'As soon as the Lamb had broken the seventh seal, there was silence in heaven for, it might be, half an hour.'),
(999263,34,66,8,2,'Then I saw the seven angels who stand before God, and seven trumpets were given to them.'),
(999264,34,66,8,3,'Next, another angel came and stood at the altar with a golden censer in his hand; and a great quantity of incense was given to him, to mingle with the prayers of all Christ’s people on the golden altar before the throne.'),
(999265,34,66,8,4,'The smoke of the incense ascended, with the prayers of Christ’s people, from the hand of the angel before God.'),
(999266,34,66,8,5,'Then the angel took the censer, and filled it with fire from the altar, and threw it down on the earth; and there followed peals of thunder, cries, flashes of lightning, and an earthquake.'),
(999267,34,66,8,6,'Then the seven angels holding the seven trumpets prepared to blow their blasts.'),
(999268,34,66,8,7,'The first blew; and there came hail and fire mixed with blood, and it fell on the earth. A third part of the earth was burnt up, and a third of the trees, and every blade of grass.'),
(999269,34,66,8,8,'Then the second angel blew; and what appeared to be a great mountain, burning, was hurled into the sea. A third of the sea became blood,'),
(999270,34,66,8,9,'and a third part of all created things that are in the sea – that is, of all living things – died, and a third of the ships was destroyed.'),
(999271,34,66,8,10,'Then the third angel blew; and there fell from the heavens a great star, burning like a torch. It fell on a third of the rivers and on the springs.'),
(999272,34,66,8,11,'(The star is called “Wormwood.”) A third of the water became bitter as wormwood, and so bitter was the water that many died from drinking it.'),
(999273,34,66,8,12,'Then the fourth angel blew; and a third of the sun and a third of the moon and a third of the stars were blasted, so that a third of them was eclipsed, and for a third part of the day there was no light, and at night it was the same.'),
(999274,34,66,8,13,'And, in my vision, I heard an eagle flying in mid-heaven and crying in a loud voice – “Woe, woe, woe for all who live on the earth, at the other trumpet-blasts of the three angels who have yet to blow.”'),
(999275,34,66,9,1,'Then the fifth angel blew; and I saw a star that had fallen on the earth from the heavens, and to him was given the key of the bottomless pit.'),
(999276,34,66,9,2,'He opened the bottomless pit, and from the pit rose a smoke like the smoke of a great furnace. The sun and the air grew dark because of the smoke from the pit.'),
(999277,34,66,9,3,'Out of the smoke locusts descended on the earth, and they received the same power as that possessed by scorpions.'),
(999278,34,66,9,4,'They were told not to harm the grass, or any plant, or any tree, but only those who have not the seal of God on their foreheads.'),
(999279,34,66,9,5,'Yet they were not allowed to kill them, but it was ordered that those men should be tortured for five months. Their torture was like the torture caused by a scorpion when it stings a person.'),
(999280,34,66,9,6,'In those days people will seek Death and will not find it; They will long to die, but Death flees from them.'),
(999281,34,66,9,7,'In appearance the locusts were like horses equipped for battle. On their heads there were what appeared to be crowns that shone like gold, their faces resembled human faces,'),
(999282,34,66,9,8,'and they had hair like the hair of a woman, their teeth were like lions’ teeth,'),
(999283,34,66,9,9,'and they had what seemed to be iron breastplates, while the noise of their wings was like the noise of chariots drawn by many horses, galloping into battle.'),
(999284,34,66,9,10,'They have tails like scorpions, and stings, and in their tails lies their power to harm people for five months.'),
(999285,34,66,9,11,'They have as their king the angel of the bottomless pit, whose name, in Hebrew, is “Abaddon,” while, in Greek, his name is “Apollyon” (the Destroyer).'),
(999286,34,66,9,12,'The first Woe has passed; and still there are two Woes to follow!'),
(999287,34,66,9,13,'Then the sixth angel blew; and I heard a voice proceeding from the corners of the golden altar that stood before God.'),
(999288,34,66,9,14,'It spoke to the sixth angel – the angel with the trumpet – and said “Let loose the four angels that are in chains at the great river Euphrates.”'),
(999289,34,66,9,15,'Then the four angels, that were held in readiness for that hour and day and month and year, were let loose, to destroy a third of mankind.'),
(999290,34,66,9,16,'The number of the hosts of cavalry was ten thousand times ten thousand, twice told; I heard their number.'),
(999291,34,66,9,17,'And this is what the horses and their riders appeared to be like in my vision: They had breastplates of fire, blood-red and sulphurous, and the heads of the horses were like lions’ heads, while out of their mouths issue fire, and smoke, and sulphur.'),
(999292,34,66,9,18,'Through these three curses a third of humanity perished – because of the fire, and the smoke, and the sulphur that issued from their mouths;'),
(999293,34,66,9,19,'for the power of the horses lies in their mouths and in their tails. For their tails are like snakes, with heads, and it is with them that they do harm.'),
(999294,34,66,9,20,'But those who were left of humanity, who had not perished through these curses, did not repent and turn away from what their own hands had made; they would not abandon the worship of demons, and of idols made of gold or silver or brass or stone or wood, which can neither see, nor hear, nor walk;'),
(999295,34,66,9,21,'and they did not repent of their murders, or their sorceries, or their licentiousness, or their thefts.'),
(999296,34,66,10,1,'Then I saw another mighty angel, descending from heaven. His robe was a cloud; over his head was the rainbow; his face was like the sun, and his feet like pillars of fire;'),
(999297,34,66,10,2,'in his hand he held a little book open. He set his right foot on the sea, and his left on the land;'),
(999298,34,66,10,3,'and he cried in a loud voice like the roaring of a lion. At his cry the seven peals of thunder spoke, each with its own voice.'),
(999299,34,66,10,4,'And, when they spoke, I was about to write; but I heard a voice from heaven say – “Keep secret what the seven peals of thunder said, and do not write it down.”'),
(999300,34,66,10,5,'Then the angel, whom I had seen standing on the sea and on the land, raised his right hand to the heavens,'),
(999301,34,66,10,6,'and swore by him who lives for ever and ever, who created the heavens and all that is in them, and the earth and all that is in it, and the sea and all that is in it, that time should cease to be.'),
(999302,34,66,10,7,'Moreover at the time when the seventh angel will speak, when he is ready to blow his blast, then the hidden purposes of God, of which he told the good news to his servants, the prophets, are at once fulfilled.'),
(999303,34,66,10,8,'Then came the voice which I had heard from heaven. It spoke to me again, and said – “Go and take the book that is open in the hand of the angel who stands on the sea and on the land.”'),
(999304,34,66,10,9,'So I went to the angel and asked him to give me the little book. And he said “Take it, and eat it. It will be bitter to your stomach, but in your mouth it will be as sweet as honey.”'),
(999305,34,66,10,10,'I took the little book out of the angel’s hand and ate it, and, while in my mouth, it was like the sweetest honey; but, when I had eaten it, it was bitter to my stomach.'),
(999306,34,66,10,11,'And I was told – “You must prophesy again about men of many peoples, and nations, and languages, and about many kings.”'),
(999307,34,66,11,1,'Then I was given a measure like a rod, and a voice said to me – “Go and measure the Temple of God and the altar, and count the worshiper there.'),
(999308,34,66,11,2,'But omit the court outside the Temple, and do not measure that, for it has been given up to the nations; and the holy City will be under their heel for forty-two months.'),
(999309,34,66,11,3,'Then I will give permission to my Two Witnesses, and for those twelve hundred and sixty days they will continue teaching, clothed in sackcloth.”'),
(999310,34,66,11,4,'These men are represented by the two olive trees and the two lamps that stand before the Lord of the earth.'),
(999311,34,66,11,5,'When anyone wishes to harm them, fire comes from their mouths and consumes their enemies; and whoever wishes to harm them will, in this way, inevitably perish.'),
(999312,34,66,11,6,'These men have the power to close the heavens, so that no rain may fall during the time that they are teaching; and they have power to turn the streams into blood, and to smite the land with any curse, whenever they will.'),
(999313,34,66,11,7,'As soon as they have completed their testimony, the wild Beast that ascends from the bottomless pit will make war on them and conquer and kill them.'),
(999314,34,66,11,8,'Their dead bodies will lie in the streets of the great city, which is mystically spoken of as “Sodom” and “Egypt,” where their Master was crucified.'),
(999315,34,66,11,9,'People of all nations, and tribes, and languages, and races look at their dead bodies for three days and a half, and do not allow them to be laid in a grave.'),
(999316,34,66,11,10,'Those who live on the earth rejoice over them and are merry, and they will send presents to one another, because these two prophets brought torments on those who live on the earth.'),
(999317,34,66,11,11,'After three days and a half the life-giving breath of God entered these men, and they stood up on their feet, and a great terror took possession of those who were watching them.'),
(999318,34,66,11,12,'The two men heard a loud voice from heaven which said to them – “Come up here,” and they went up to heaven in the cloud, while their enemies watched them.'),
(999319,34,66,11,13,'At that very time a great earthquake occurred. A tenth part of the city fell, and seven thousand people perished in the earthquake. Those who escaped were much terrified, and praised the God of heaven.'),
(999320,34,66,11,14,'The second Woe has passed; and there is a third Woe soon to follow!'),
(999321,34,66,11,15,'Then the seventh angel blew; and loud voices were heard in heaven saying –'),
(999322,34,66,11,16,'At this the twenty-four elders, who were seated on their thrones before God, prostrated themselves on their faces and worshiped Him,'),
(999323,34,66,11,17,'saying –'),
(999324,34,66,11,18,'The nations were enraged, and your wrath fell on them; the time came for the dead to be judged, and for you to give the reward to your servants the prophets, and to the people of Christ, and to those who honour your name – the high and the low alike – and to destroy those who are destroying the earth.”'),
(999325,34,66,11,19,'Then the Temple of God in heaven was opened, and the ark containing his covenant was seen in his Temple; and there followed flashes of lightning, cries, peals of thunder, an earthquake, and a great storm of hail.'),
(999326,34,66,12,1,'Then a great portent was seen in the heavens – a woman whose robe was the sun, and who had the moon under her feet, and on her head a crown of twelve stars.'),
(999327,34,66,12,2,'She was pregnant; and she is crying out in the pain and agony of childbirth.'),
(999328,34,66,12,3,'Another portent also was seen in the heavens There was a great red Dragon, with seven heads and ten horns, and on his heads were seven diadems.'),
(999329,34,66,12,4,'His tail draws after it a third of the stars in the heavens, and it hurled them down on the earth. The Dragon is standing in front of the woman who is about to give birth to the child, so that he may devour it as soon as it is born.'),
(999330,34,66,12,5,'The woman gave birth to a son, a male child, who is destined to rule all the nations with an iron rod; and her child was at once caught up to God on his throne.'),
(999331,34,66,12,6,'But the woman fled into the wilderness, where there is a place prepared for her by God, to be tended there for twelve hundred and sixty days.'),
(999332,34,66,12,7,'Then a battle took place in the heavens. Michael and his angels fought with the Dragon. But though the Dragon, with his angels, fought,'),
(999333,34,66,12,8,'he did not prevail; and there was no place left for them any longer in the heavens.'),
(999334,34,66,12,9,'Then the great Dragon, the primeval snake, known as the “devil” and “Satan,” who deceives all the world, was hurled down to the earth, and his angels were hurled down with him.'),
(999335,34,66,12,10,'And I heard a loud voice in heaven which said –'),
(999336,34,66,12,11,'Their victory was due to the blood of the Lamb, and to the message to which they bore their testimony. In their love of life they shrank not from death.'),
(999337,34,66,12,12,'Therefore, be glad, heaven, and all who live in heaven! Alas for the earth and for the sea, for the devil has gone down to you in great fury, knowing that he has but little time.”'),
(999338,34,66,12,13,'When the Dragon saw that he was hurled down to the earth, he pursued the woman who had given birth to the male child.'),
(999339,34,66,12,14,'But to the woman were given the two wings of the great eagle, so that she might fly to her place in the wilderness, where she is being tended for one year, and for two years, and for half a year in safety from the snake.'),
(999340,34,66,12,15,'Then the snake poured water from its mouth after the woman, like a river, so that it might sweep her away.'),
(999341,34,66,12,16,'But Earth came to her help, and opened her mouth and drank up the river which the Dragon had poured out of its mouth.'),
(999342,34,66,12,17,'The Dragon was enraged at the woman, and went to fight with the rest of her offspring – those who lay to heart the commands of God and bear their testimony to Jesus;'),
(999343,34,66,12,18,'and he took his stand on the sea-shore.'),
(999344,34,66,13,1,'Then I saw, rising out of the sea, a wild Beast with ten horns and seven heads. On its horns were ten diadems, and on its heads were blasphemous names.'),
(999345,34,66,13,2,'The Beast that I saw was like a leopard; but its feet were like a bear’s, and its mouth like the mouth of a lion. The Dragon gave it his power and his throne, and wide dominion.'),
(999346,34,66,13,3,'One of its heads seemed to me to have been mortally wounded, but its deadly wound had been healed. The whole earth followed the Beast, wondering;'),
(999347,34,66,13,4,'and men worshiped the Dragon, because he had given his dominion to the Beast; while, as they worshiped the Beast, they said – “Who can compare with the Beast? And who can fight with it?”'),
(999348,34,66,13,5,'The Beast was given a mouth that spoke proudly and blasphemously, and it was empowered to work its will for forty-two months.'),
(999349,34,66,13,6,'It opened its mouth only to blaspheme God, to blaspheme his name and his tent – those who live in his tent in heaven.'),
(999350,34,66,13,7,'It had been permitted to fight with Christ’s people and to conquer them, and it had received power over men of every tribe, and people, and language, and nation.'),
(999351,34,66,13,8,'All who are living on earth will worship it – all whose names have not been written in the Lamb’s book of life, the Lamb that has been sacrificed from the foundation of the world.'),
(999352,34,66,13,9,'Let those who have ears hear.'),
(999353,34,66,13,10,'Whoever is destined for captivity goes into captivity. Whoever will kill with the sword must inevitably be killed with the sword. (Here there is need for endurance and faith on the part of Christ’s people.)'),
(999354,34,66,13,11,'Then I saw, rising out of the earth, another wild Beast. It had two horns like those of a lamb, and its voice was like a dragon’s.'),
(999355,34,66,13,12,'It exercises all the authority of the first Beast under its eyes; and it makes the earth and all who are living on it worship that first Beast, whose mortal wound was healed.'),
(999356,34,66,13,13,'It performs great marvels, even causing fire to fall from the heavens to the earth, before people’s eyes;'),
(999357,34,66,13,14,'and in consequence of the marvels which it was allowed to perform under the eyes of the Beast, it is able to deceive all who are living on the earth. It tells those who live on the earth to make a statue in honour of the Beast, who, despite the wound from the sword, yet lived.'),
(999358,34,66,13,15,'It was permitted to breathe life into the image of the Beast, so that the image of the Beast might speak; and it was also permitted to cause all who refused to worship the image of the Beast to be put to death.'),
(999359,34,66,13,16,'High and low, rich and poor, free and enslaved – it causes a brand to be put on the right hand or on the forehead of every one of them,'),
(999360,34,66,13,17,'so that no one is able to buy or sell, except those that bear this brand – either the name of the Beast or the number indicated by the letters of his name.'),
(999361,34,66,13,18,'(Here there is need for discernment.) The person with ability can compute the number of the Beast; for the number indicates a person’s name. Its number is six hundred and sixty-six.'),
(999362,34,66,14,1,'Then, in my vision, I saw the Lamb standing on Mount Zion. With him were a hundred and forty-four thousand, with his name and the name of his Father written on their foreheads.'),
(999363,34,66,14,2,'And I heard a sound from heaven, like the sound of many waters, and like the sound of a loud peal of thunder; the sound that I heard was like the music of harpers playing on their harps.'),
(999364,34,66,14,3,'They are singing what seems to be a new song, before the throne, and before the four creatures and the elders; and no one was able to learn that song except the hundred and forty-four thousand who had been redeemed from earth.'),
(999365,34,66,14,4,'These are the men who never defiled themselves in their intercourse with women; they are as pure as virgins. These are the men who follow the Lamb wherever he goes. They were redeemed as the first-fruits of mankind for God and for the Lamb.'),
(999366,34,66,14,5,'No lie was ever heard on their lips. They are beyond reach of blame.'),
(999367,34,66,14,6,'Then I saw another angel, flying in mid-heaven. He had the good news, decreed from eternity, to announce to those who live on the earth – to men of every nation, and tribe, and language, and people;'),
(999368,34,66,14,7,'and he cried in a loud voice – “Reverence God, and give him praise (for the hour of his judgment has come) and worship him who made the heaven and the earth and the sea and all springs of water.”'),
(999369,34,66,14,8,'Then a second angel followed, crying – “She has fallen! She has fallen – Babylon the Great, who has made all the nations drink the maddening wine of her licentiousness!”'),
(999370,34,66,14,9,'Then a third angel followed them, crying in a loud voice – “Whoever worships the Beast and its image, and receives its brand on his forehead or on his hand,'),
(999371,34,66,14,10,'that person will drink the maddening wine of God that has been poured unmixed into the cup of his wrath, and they will be tortured with fire and sulphur before the eyes of the holy angels and before the eyes of the Lamb.'),
(999372,34,66,14,11,'The smoke from their torture rises for ever and ever, and they have no rest day nor night – those who worship the Beast and its image, and all who are branded with its name.”'),
(999373,34,66,14,12,'(Here there is need for endurance on the part of Christ’s people – those who lay to heart the commands of God and the faith of Jesus.)'),
(999374,34,66,14,13,'Then I heard a voice from heaven saying “Write: ‘Blessed are the dead who from this hour die in union with the Lord.’”'),
(999375,34,66,14,14,'Then, in my vision, I saw a white cloud, and on the cloud there was sitting one like a man. On his head he had a crown of gold, and in his hand a sharp sickle.'),
(999376,34,66,14,15,'Then another angel came out from the Temple, crying in a loud voice to him who was sitting on the cloud – “Take your sickle and reap, for the time to reap has come; the Harvest of Earth is ready.”'),
(999377,34,66,14,16,'He who was sitting on the cloud brought his sickle down on the earth, and the Harvest of Earth was reaped.'),
(999378,34,66,14,17,'Then another angel came out of the Temple in heaven; he, also, had a sharp sickle.'),
(999379,34,66,14,18,'Then another angel came out of the altar; he had power over fire, and he called in a loud voice to the angel that had the sharp sickle – “Take your sharp sickle, and gather the bunches from the vine of Earth, for its grapes are ripe.”'),
(999380,34,66,14,19,'The angel brought his sickle down on the earth and gathered the fruit of the vine of Earth, and threw it into the great winepress of the wrath of God.'),
(999381,34,66,14,20,'The grapes were trodden in the press outside the city; and blood came out of the press, rising as high as the bridles of the horses for a distance of two hundred miles.'),
(999382,34,66,15,1,'Then I saw another portent in the heavens – a great and marvellous portent – seven angels with the seven last curses; because with them the wrath of God is ended.'),
(999383,34,66,15,2,'Then I saw what appeared to be a sea of glass mixed with fire; and, standing by this sea of glass, holding the harps of God, I saw those who had come victorious out of the conflict with the Beast and its image and the number that formed its name.'),
(999384,34,66,15,3,'They are singing the song of Moses, the servant of God, and the song of the Lamb –'),
(999385,34,66,15,4,'Who will not honour and praise your name, Lord? You alone are holy! All nations will come and worship before you, for your judgments have become manifest.”'),
(999386,34,66,15,5,'After this I saw that the inmost shrine of the tent of testimony in heaven was opened,'),
(999387,34,66,15,6,'and out of it came the seven angels with the seven curses. They were adorned with precious stones, pure and bright, and had golden girdles round their breasts.'),
(999388,34,66,15,7,'One of the four creatures gave the seven angels seven golden bowls, filled with the wrath of God who lives for ever and ever.'),
(999389,34,66,15,8,'The Temple was filled with smoke from the glory and majesty of God; and no one could enter the Temple, until the seven curses inflicted by the seven angels were at an end.'),
(999390,34,66,16,1,'Then I heard a loud voice, which came from the Temple, saying to the seven angels – “Go and empty the seven bowls of the wrath of God on the earth.”'),
(999391,34,66,16,2,'The first angel went and emptied his bowl on the earth; and it turned to loathsome and painful sores on all who bore the brand of the Beast and who worshiped its image.'),
(999392,34,66,16,3,'Then the second angel emptied his bowl on the sea; and it turned to blood like the blood of a corpse, and every living thing died – everything in the sea.'),
(999393,34,66,16,4,'Then the third angel emptied his bowl on the rivers and springs of water; and it turned to blood.'),
(999394,34,66,16,5,'And I heard the angel of the Waters saying – “Righteous are you, you who is and who is, the Holy One, in inflicting this judgment;'),
(999395,34,66,16,6,'for men shed the blood of Christ’s people and of the prophets, and you have given them blood to drink. It is what they deserve.”'),
(999396,34,66,16,7,'And I heard the response from the altar – “Yes, Lord, our God, the Almighty, true and righteous are they judgments.”'),
(999397,34,66,16,8,'Then the fourth angel emptied his bowl on the sun; and he was permitted to scorch men with fire;'),
(999398,34,66,16,9,'and men were scorched by the intense heat. They blasphemed the name of God who controlled these curses, yet they did not repent and give him praise.'),
(999399,34,66,16,10,'Then the fifth angel emptied his bowl on the throne of the Beast; and darkness fell on its kingdom. Men gnawed their tongues for pain,'),
(999400,34,66,16,11,'and blasphemed the God of heaven, because of their pains and because of their sores; yet they did not repent of what they had done.'),
(999401,34,66,16,12,'Then the sixth angel emptied his bowl on the great river Euphrates; and the water in the river was dried up, so that the road for the kings of the East might be made ready.'),
(999402,34,66,16,13,'And I saw three foul spirits, like frogs, come from the mouth of the Dragon and from the mouth of the Beast and from the mouth of the false prophet.'),
(999403,34,66,16,14,'They are the spirits of demons, and perform marvels; they go to kings all over the world, to collect them for the battle on the great day of Almighty God.'),
(999404,34,66,16,16,'And the spirits collected the kings at the place called in Hebrew “Har-Magedon.”'),
(999405,34,66,16,17,'Then the seventh angel emptied his bowl on the air. (A loud voice came from the throne in the Temple; it said “All is over.”)'),
(999406,34,66,16,18,'There followed flashes of lightning, cries, and peals of thunder; and there was a great earthquake, such as had not occurred since man began to be on the earth – none so great;'),
(999407,34,66,16,19,'and the great city was torn in three, and the cities of the nation fell, and God remembered Babylon the Great, and gave her the maddening wine-cup of his wrath;'),
(999408,34,66,16,20,'and every island vanished, and the mountains disappeared.'),
(999409,34,66,16,21,'Great hailstones, a pound in weight, are falling on men from the heavens. And men blasphemed God because of the curse of the hail, for it was a very terrible curse.'),
(999410,34,66,17,1,'Then one of the seven angels who held the seven bowls came and spoke to me. “Come here,” he said, “and I will show you the sentence passed on that Great Harlot who is seated at the meeting of many waters,'),
(999411,34,66,17,2,'and with whom all the kings of the earth have had licentious intercourse; while all who live on the earth have been make drunk by the wine of her licentiousness.”'),
(999412,34,66,17,3,'And he bore me away in a trance to a lonely place, and I saw a woman seated on a scarlet Beast, which was covered with blasphemous names; it had seven heads and ten horns.'),
(999413,34,66,17,4,'The woman was clothed in purple and scarlet, and glittering with gold ornaments, precious stones, and pearls. In her hand she held a gold cup, full of idolatrous abominations, and the unclean fruits of her licentiousness;'),
(999414,34,66,17,5,'while on her forehead there was written this mystic name – “BABYLON THE GREAT, THE MOTHER OF HARLOTS AND OF ALL IDOLATROUS ABOMINATIONS ON EARTH.”'),
(999415,34,66,17,6,'And I saw the woman drunk with the blood of Christ’s people and with the blood of the martyrs for Jesus. When I saw her, I was amazed beyond measure;'),
(999416,34,66,17,7,'but the angel said to me – “Why were you amazed? I will tell you the mystic meaning of the vision of this woman, and of the Beast, with the seven heads and ten horns, that carries her.'),
(999417,34,66,17,8,'The Beast that you saw was, but is not, and is about to rise out of the bottomless pit, and is on its way to destruction. Those who are living on earth will be amazed – those whose names have not been written in the book of life from the foundation of the world – when they see that the Beast was, but is not, and yet will come.”'),
(999418,34,66,17,9,'(Here there is need for the discerning mind.) The seven heads are seven mountains on which the woman is seated.'),
(999419,34,66,17,10,'They are also seven kings; of whom five have fallen and one remains, while one is not yet come. When he comes, he must stay for a little while.'),
(999420,34,66,17,11,'So must the Beast that was, but is not. He counts as an eighth king, although he is one of the seven, and is on his way to destruction.'),
(999421,34,66,17,12,'The ten horns that you saw are ten kings, who have not yet received their kingdoms, but for an hour they receive the authority of kings, together with the Beast.'),
(999422,34,66,17,13,'These kings are of one mind in surrendering their power and authority to the Beast.'),
(999423,34,66,17,14,'They will fight with the Lamb, but the Lamb will conquer them, for he is Lord of lords and King of kings; so, too, will those with him who have received the call and are chosen and faithful.'),
(999424,34,66,17,15,'And the angel said to me – “The waters that you saw, where the Harlot is seated, are throngs of people and men of all nations and languages.'),
(999425,34,66,17,16,'The ten horns that you saw, and the Beast – they will hate the Harlot, and cause her to become deserted and strip her bare; they will eat her flesh and utterly consume her with fire.'),
(999426,34,66,17,17,'For God has put it into their minds to carry out his purpose, in carrying out their common purpose and surrendering their kingdoms to the Beast, until God’s decrees will be executed.'),
(999427,34,66,17,18,'As for the woman whom you saw, she is the great city that holds sway over all the kings of the earth.”'),
(999428,34,66,18,1,'After this I saw another angel, descending from heaven, invested with great authority; and the earth was illuminated by his splendour.'),
(999429,34,66,18,2,'With a mighty voice he cried – ‘She has fallen! She has fallen – Babylon the Great! She has become an abode of demons, a stronghold of every wicked spirit, a stronghold of every foul and hateful bird.'),
(999430,34,66,18,3,'For, after drinking the maddening wine of her licentiousness, all the nations have fallen; while all the kings of the earth have had licentious intercourse with her, and the merchants of the earth have grown rich through the excess of her luxury.’'),
(999431,34,66,18,4,'Then I heard another voice from heaven saying – ‘Come out of her, my people, so that you may not participate in her sins, and that you may not suffer from the curses inflicted on her.'),
(999432,34,66,18,5,'For her sins are heaped up to the heavens, and God has not forgotten her misdeeds.'),
(999433,34,66,18,6,'Pay her back the treatment with which she has treated you; yes, repay twice over what her actions deserve; in the cup which she mixed for you, mix for her as much again;'),
(999434,34,66,18,7,'for her self-glorification and her luxury, give her now an equal measure of torture and misery. In her heart she says “I sit here a queen; no widow am I; I will never know misery.”'),
(999435,34,66,18,8,'Therefore in one day will these curses strike her – death, misery, and famine, and she will be utterly consumed by fire; for mighty is the Lord God who condemned her.’'),
(999436,34,66,18,9,'All the kings of the earth who had licentious intercourse with her and shared her luxury will weep and lament over her, when they see the smoke from the burning city,'),
(999437,34,66,18,10,'while they stand at a distance, horrified at her torture, and cry – ‘Alas! Alas! Great city! Mighty city of Babylon! In a single hour your judgment fell.’'),
(999438,34,66,18,11,'And the merchants of the earth weep and wail over her, because no longer does anyone buy their cargoes –'),
(999439,34,66,18,12,'their cargoes of gold, or silver, or precious stones, or pearls, or fine linen, or purple robes, or silk, or scarlet cloth; nor their many scented woods; nor their many articles of ivory; nor their many articles of choicest wood, or brass, or iron, or marble;'),
(999440,34,66,18,13,'nor their cinnamon, or spice, or incense, or perfumes, or frankincense, or wine, or oil, or fine flour, or wheat, or cattle, or sheep; nor their horses, or chariots, or slaves; nor the bodies and souls of people.'),
(999441,34,66,18,14,'The fruit that your soul craved is no longer within your reach, and all dainties and luxuries are lost to you, never to be found again.'),
(999442,34,66,18,15,'The merchants who sold these things, and grew rich by her, will stand at a distance weeping and wailing, horrified at her torture, and crying –'),
(999443,34,66,18,16,'‘Alas! Alas! Great city! City clothed in fine linen, and purple, and scarlet cloth! City adorned with gold ornaments, and precious stones, and pearls!'),
(999444,34,66,18,17,'In a single hour your vast wealth vanished.’ Every ship’s captain and all who sail to any port, and sailors, and all who get their living from the sea, stood at a distance,'),
(999445,34,66,18,18,'and seeing the smoke from the burning city, cried – ‘What city can compare with the Great city?’'),
(999446,34,66,18,19,'They threw dust on their heads, and, as they wept and wailed, they cried – ‘Alas! Alas! Great city! All who have ships on the sea grew rich through her magnificence. In a single hour it has vanished.’'),
(999447,34,66,18,20,'Rejoice over her, heaven, and people of Christ, and apostles, and prophets, for God has avenged you on her!'),
(999448,34,66,18,21,'Then a mighty angel took up a stone like a great millstone, and threw it into the sea, crying – ‘So will Babylon, the great city, be violently overthrown, never more to be seen.'),
(999449,34,66,18,22,'No more will the music of harpers, or minstrels, or flute players, or trumpeters be heard in you, no more will any worker, skilled in any art, be found in you; no more will the sound of a mill be heard in you;'),
(999450,34,66,18,23,'no more will the light of a lamp shine in you; no more will the voices of groom and bride be heard in you. Your merchants were the great men of the earth, for all the nations were deceived by your magical charms.’'),
(999451,34,66,18,24,'Yes, and in her was to be found the blood of the prophets and of Christ’s people, and of all who have been put to death on the earth.'),
(999452,34,66,19,1,'After this, I heard what seemed to be a great shout from a vast throng in heaven, crying –'),
(999453,34,66,19,2,'for true and righteous are his judgments. For he has passed judgment on the Great Harlot who was corrupting the earth by her licentiousness, and he has taken vengeance on her for the blood of his servants.”'),
(999454,34,66,19,3,'Again they cried – “Hallelujah!” And the smoke from her ruins rises for ever and ever.'),
(999455,34,66,19,4,'Then the twenty-four elders and the Four creatures prostrated themselves and worshiped God who was seated on the throne, crying – “Amen, Hallelujah!”;'),
(999456,34,66,19,5,'and from the throne there came a voice which said –'),
(999457,34,66,19,6,'Then I heard what seemed to be the shout of a vast throng, like the sound of many waters, and like the sound of loud peals of thunder, crying –'),
(999458,34,66,19,7,'Let us rejoice and exalt; and we will pay him honour, for the hour for the Marriage of the Lamb has come, and his Bride has made herself ready.'),
(999459,34,66,19,8,'And to her it has been granted to robe herself in fine linen, white and pure, for that linen is the good deeds of the people of Christ.”'),
(999460,34,66,19,9,'Then a voice said to me “Write – ‘Blessed are those who have been summoned to the marriage feast of the Lamb.’” And the voice said – “These words of God are true.”'),
(999461,34,66,19,10,'I prostrated myself at the feet of him who spoke to worship him, but he said to me – “No! I am your fellow servant, and the fellow servant of your brothers and sisters who bear their testimony to Jesus. Worship God. For to bear testimony to Jesus needs the inspiration of the prophets.”'),
(999462,34,66,19,11,'Then I saw that heaven lay open. There appears a white horse; its rider is called “Faithful” and “True”; righteously does he judge and make war.'),
(999463,34,66,19,12,'His eyes are flaming fires; on his head there are many diadems, and he bears a name, written, which no one knows but himself;'),
(999464,34,66,19,13,'he has been clothed in a garment sprinkled with blood; and the name by which he is called is “The Word of God.”'),
(999465,34,66,19,14,'The armies of heaven followed him, mounted on white horses and clothed in fine linen, white and pure.'),
(999466,34,66,19,15,'From his mouth comes a sharp sword, with which to smite the nations; and he will rule them with an iron rod. He treads the grapes in the press of the maddening wine of the wrath of Almighty God;'),
(999467,34,66,19,16,'and on his robe and on his thigh he has this name written – “KING OF KINGS AND LORD OF LORDS.”'),
(999468,34,66,19,17,'Then I saw an angel standing on the sun. He cried in a loud voice to all the birds that fly in mid-heaven – “Gather and come to the great feast of God,'),
(999469,34,66,19,18,'to eat the flesh of kings, and the flesh of commanders, and the flesh of mighty men, and the flesh of horses and their riders, and the flesh of all free and enslaved, and of high and low.”'),
(999470,34,66,19,19,'Then I saw the Beast and the kings of the earth and their armies, gathered together to fight with him who sat on the horse and with his army.'),
(999471,34,66,19,20,'The Beast was captured, and with him was taken the false prophet, who performed the marvels before the eyes of the Beast, with which he deceived those who had received the brand of the Beast and those who worshiped his image. Alive, they were thrown, both of them, into the lake of fire – of burning sulphur.'),
(999472,34,66,19,21,'The rest were killed by the sword which came out of the mouth of him who rode on the horse; and all the birds fed on their flesh.'),
(999473,34,66,20,1,'Then I saw an angel coming down from heaven, with the key of the bottomless pit and a great chain in his hand.'),
(999474,34,66,20,2,'He seized the Dragon, the primeval snake (who is the “devil” or “Satan”), and bound him in chains for a thousand years.'),
(999475,34,66,20,3,'He flung him into the bottomless pit and locked it, and set his seal on it; that he should not deceive the nations any more, until the thousand years were ended. After that he must be let loose for a while.'),
(999476,34,66,20,4,'Then I saw thrones, and to those who took their seats on them authority was given to act as judges. And I saw the souls of those who had been beheaded because of the testimony to Jesus and because of the message of God, for they had refused to worship the Beast or its image, and had not received the brand on their foreheads and on their hands. They were restored to life, and they reigned with the Christ for a thousand years.'),
(999477,34,66,20,5,'(The rest of the dead were not restored to life until the thousand years were ended.) This is the first resurrection.'),
(999478,34,66,20,6,'Blessed and holy will he be who shares in that first resurrection. The second Death has no power over them; but they will be priests of God, and the Christ, and they will reign with him for the thousand years.'),
(999479,34,66,20,7,'When the thousand years are ended, Satan will be let loose from his prison,'),
(999480,34,66,20,8,'and he will come out to deceive the nations that live in the four corners of the earth – Gog and Magog. He will come to gather them together for battle; and their number will be as great as the sand on the sea-shore.'),
(999481,34,66,20,9,'They went up over the breadth of the whole earth, and surrounded the camp of Christ’s people and the city that he loves. Then fire fell from the heavens and consumed them;'),
(999482,34,66,20,10,'and the devil, their deceiver, was hurled into the lake of fire and sulphur, where the Beast and the false prophet already were, and they will be tortured day and night for ever and ever.'),
(999483,34,66,20,11,'Then I saw a great white throne, and him who was seated on it. The earth and the heavens fled from his presence; no place was left for them.'),
(999484,34,66,20,12,'And I saw the dead, high and low, standing before the throne; and books were opened. Then another book was opened, the book of life; and the dead were judged, according to their actions, by what was written in the books.'),
(999485,34,66,20,13,'The sea gave up its dead, and Death and Hades gave up their dead; and they were judged, one by one, each according to his actions.'),
(999486,34,66,20,14,'Then Death and Hades were hurled into the lake of fire. This is the Second Death – the lake of fire;'),
(999487,34,66,20,15,'and all whose names were not found written in the book of life were hurled into the lake of fire.'),
(999488,34,66,21,1,'Then I saw new heavens and a new earth. The former heavens and the former earth had passed away; and the sea has ceased to be.'),
(999489,34,66,21,2,'And I saw the Holy City, Jerusalem, descending new out of heaven from God, like a bride adorned in readiness for her husband.'),
(999490,34,66,21,3,'And I heard a loud voice from the throne, which said – “See! The tent of God is set up among people. God will live among them, and they will be his Peoples, and God himself will be among them,'),
(999491,34,66,21,4,'and he will wipe away all tears from their eyes. There will be no more death, nor will there be any more grief or crying or pain. The old order has passed away.”'),
(999492,34,66,21,5,'And he who was seated on the throne said – “See, I make all things new!” And he said – “Write this, for these words may be trusted and are true.”'),
(999493,34,66,21,6,'And he said to me – “They are fulfilled. I am the Alpha and the Omega, the beginning and the End. To those who thirst I will give of the spring of the water of life, freely.'),
(999494,34,66,21,7,'Those who conquer will enter into possession of these things, and I will be their God, and they will be my children.'),
(999495,34,66,21,8,'But as for cowards, unbelievers, the degraded, murderers, the impure, sorcerers, idolaters, and all liars – their place will be in the burning lake of fire and sulphur. That is the Second Death.”'),
(999496,34,66,21,9,'Then one of the seven angels who had the seven bowls, and were laden with the seven last curses, came and spoke to me. “Come here,” he said, “and I will show you the Bride, the Wife of the Lamb.”'),
(999497,34,66,21,10,'He carried me away in a trance to a great high mountain, and showed me Jerusalem, the Holy City, descending out of heaven from God, filled with the glory of God.'),
(999498,34,66,21,11,'Its brilliance was like a precious stone, like a jasper, transparent as crystal.'),
(999499,34,66,21,12,'It had a great high wall, in which were twelve gates; and at these gates there were twelve angels, and there were names inscribed on the gates, the names of the twelve tribes of the Israelites.'),
(999500,34,66,21,13,'There were three gates on the east, three gates on the north, three gates on the south, and three gates on the west.');
INSERT INTO verses (id, version_id, book_id, chapter, verse, text) VALUES
(999501,34,66,21,14,'The wall of the city had twelve foundation stones, on which were the twelve names of the twelve apostles of the Lamb.'),
(999502,34,66,21,15,'And the angel who was speaking to me had as a measure a gold rod, with which to measure the city and its gates and its wall.'),
(999503,34,66,21,16,'The city is square; the length and the breadth are the same. The angel measured with his rod; it was twelve hundred miles; its length, and breadth, and height are equal.'),
(999504,34,66,21,17,'Then he measured the wall; it was two hundred and eighty-eight feet, as people measure, that is as the angel measured.'),
(999505,34,66,21,18,'The material of the wall of the city was jasper, and the city was built of pure gold, which shone like clear glass.'),
(999506,34,66,21,19,'The foundations of the wall of the city were ornamented with every kind of precious stone. The first foundation stone was a jasper; the second a sapphire; the third a chalcedony; the fourth an emerald;'),
(999507,34,66,21,20,'the fifth a sardonyx; the sixth a carnelian; the seventh a chrysolite; the eighth a beryl; the ninth a topaz; the tenth a chrysoprase; the eleventh a hyacinth; and the twelfth an amethyst.'),
(999508,34,66,21,21,'The twelve gates were made of twelve pearls, each gate of one pearl. The street of the city was of pure gold, transparent as glass.'),
(999509,34,66,21,22,'And I saw no Temple there, for the Lord, our God, the Almighty, and the Lamb are its Temple.'),
(999510,34,66,21,23,'The city has no need of the sun or the moon to shine on it, for the glory of God illuminated it, and its Lamp was the Lamb.'),
(999511,34,66,21,24,'The nations walk by the light of it; and the kings of the earth bring their glory into it.'),
(999512,34,66,21,25,'Its gates will never be shut by day, and there will be no night there.'),
(999513,34,66,21,26,'And people will bring the glory and honour of the nations into it.'),
(999514,34,66,21,27,'Never will any unhallowed thing enter it, nor they whose life is shameful and false, but only those whose names have been written in the Lamb’s book of life.'),
(999515,34,66,22,1,'And the angel showed me a river of the water of life, as clear as crystal, issuing from the throne of God and of the Lamb,'),
(999516,34,66,22,2,'in the middle of the street of the city. On each side of the river was a Tree of life which bore twelve kinds of fruit, yielding its fruit each month; and the leaves of the tree were for the healing of the nations.'),
(999517,34,66,22,3,'Every thing that is accursed will cease to be. The throne of God and of the Lamb will be within it, and his servants will worship him;'),
(999518,34,66,22,4,'they will see his face, and his name will be on their foreheads.'),
(999519,34,66,22,5,'Night will cease to be. They have no need of the light of a lamp, nor have they the light of the sun; for the Lord God will be their light, and they will reign for ever and ever.'),
(999520,34,66,22,6,'Then the angel said to me – ‘These words may be trusted and are true. The Lord, the God that inspires the prophets, sent his angel to show his servants what must quickly take place;'),
(999521,34,66,22,7,'and they said'),
(999522,34,66,22,8,'It was I, John, who heard and saw these things; and, when I heard and saw them, I prostrated myself in worship at the feet of the angel that showed them to me.'),
(999523,34,66,22,9,'But he said to me – ‘Forbear; I am your fellow servant, and the fellow servant of your fellow prophets, and of all who lay to heart the words in this book. Worship God.’'),
(999524,34,66,22,10,'Then the angel said to me – ‘Do not keep secret the words of the prophecy contained in this book; for the time is near.'),
(999525,34,66,22,11,'Let the wrong-doer continue to do wrong; the filthy-minded continue to be filthy; the righteous continue to act righteously; and the holy-minded continue to be holy.’'),
(999526,34,66,22,14,'Blessed will they be who wash their robes! They will have the right to approach the Tree of life, and may enter the city by the gates.'),
(999527,34,66,22,15,'Outside will be the filthy, the sorcerers, the impure, the murderers, the idolaters, and all who love the false and live it.'),
(999528,34,66,22,17,'“Come,” say the Spirit and the Bride; and all who hear, say “Come.” All who thirst, come; anyone who wants, take the water of life freely.'),
(999529,34,66,22,18,'I declare to all who hear the words of the prophecy contained in this book – “If anyone adds to it, God will add to his troubles the curses described in this book;'),
(999530,34,66,22,19,'and if anyone takes away any of the words in the book containing this prophecy, God will take away his share in the Tree of life, and in the Holy City – as described in this book.”'),
(999531,34,66,22,20,'He whose testimony this is says –'),
(999532,34,66,22,21,'May the blessing of the Lord Jesus Christ, be with his people.');
